          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "[{\"id\":840,\"name\":\"Olive Wreath + Ayu Mesi \",\"start_time\":\"1998-08-28T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"1998-08-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f3efddac8e1638a2e8ea8a8d5f4657ca.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38436/t4tunes-olive-wreath-ayu-mesi\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"Near Field Communication 2.0\",\"start_time\":\"2025-10-03T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2025-10-04T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b7083704e8c06878cfce0868c29a570f.webp\",\"background\":\"d074b0c95ceff8a5891bc5765752e815.webp\\n\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"Twin System\",\"start_time\":\"2025-10-17T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2025-10-18T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1fb31edd63c58065fec67b1f4d7c422f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Diversion\",\"start_time\":\"2025-10-26T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2025-10-26T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ed5e7ca045e7556f9119ae32504a3903.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Riiiiiiight then we’re back at Ormside with a special Sunday edition of Diversion powered by the Beatcrime Soundsystem to bring you some of our favourites from London and beyond.\\n\\nIf you like your music weird and eclectic, Grace Black has you covered with gorgeous selections which cover ground from mellow guitars, to left field dub, to dancehall, to industrial and beyond - at times infused with a touch of dark, twisted dread, all beautifully knitted together with care and precision.\\n\\nOur resident jester takes a brief pause from mastering ceremonies as Rex Dominos and jumps behind his mixing desk to treat us to his critically acclaimed live set as Elijah Minnelli taking inspiration from dub, folk and cumbia processed through fried synapses to bring you his own sonic soup designed to be enjoyed on big rigs.\\n\\nSouth London native Elle Andrews is a stalwart of the scene. Co-founder of MAL Recordings alongside Jon K and host of the bi-monthly BUͧS͛Y S͛IͥGN∀LS͛ which ran on French station LYL until May 2024, she draws from a sprawling, expansive collection which touches many corners of her influences including, dub, percussion, r\\u0026b, house, industrial, experimental, psych rock, punk and more. The care, thought and ingenuity that goes into her sets is always very evident and we can’t wait to hear what she brings to Diversion for you.\\n\\nComing all the way from Belgium, we’re very fortunate to be joined by Rudi J, fka Weird Dust and one half of Tav Exotic with Bear Bones, Lay Low. Rudi’s rare but extremely well developed live set encompasses most of the sound system music spectrum; playing fluidly and equally with dancehall’s syncopation, dubstep’s halftime squelch and steppers' pounding baselines. Having worked consistently with Meakusma and releasing on the likes of Sagat and Pretty Sneaky on his own Private Stress label, his taste in psychedelic lefty wonk and psych acid kraut synth while paying the proper tribute to Soundsystem culture’s sonic legacy shines through everything he does. An under appreciated hero of the European underground music scene, we cant wait to have him for his London debut.\\n\\nLast and by no means least, we have East London’s mighty Gary The Tall returning to take the reins and make you move with panache. If you were at the last event, you’ll know how much we loved his excursion into post-punk, synth, no wave, dub, sexy psychedelic rock and other left field cosmic delights. He can talk about his records endlessly and clearly has passion running through his veins so we’re very grateful he’s agreed to come back again and share that with you.\\n\\nOur trusty residents will be knocking about to start and end the event and see off your Sunday scaries. Diversion is designed to be a friendly space of self expression, but any bullshit will get you the boot. Please be accountable to each-other and talk to the bar staff, sinny, Charlie or the door staff if someone is acting up.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":9,\"name\":\"Dean Rodney Jr. \\u0026 The Cowboys\",\"start_time\":\"2026-01-28T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-01-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8fde8c52505fe23a0d68b0eb82d171b9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dean Rodney Jr. \\u0026 The Cowboys return to The Ivy House for a very special headline performance as part of Independent Venue Week. Support comes from Big World and Bog Band. Yee-haw!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/6dwoq3-dean-rodney-and-the-cowboys-28th-jan-the-ivy-house-london-tickets?dice_id=gbd325862ccf\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":12,\"name\":\"Accidental Meetings: John T. Gast presents Petrols\",\"start_time\":\"2026-01-30T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-01-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0352287ece99d1e6af4082b781ebb2e1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"John T. Gast Presents Petrols. \\nFlutes + FX form the core of a more improvisational framework.\\nDrawing on Gast’s Gossiwor material, with Aase Nielsen, Petrols moves into looser, more exploratory territory, balancing intimacy with sonic weight.\\n\\nWith support from Exlruth, Nervio Cosmico and I-Sha.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/accidental-meetings-jan-26/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":10,\"name\":\"Niche at MOT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-02-07T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-02-08T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"97f9fbd24aa2d81f45611dd0fc003192.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"2026, time to mutate: Niche becomes itinerant, migrating between like-minded venues and spreading weird sounds across both sides of the river.\\nSaturday 7th February our habitat will be MOT.\\nA 6am-finish exploration with a lineup of daring DJs, and a live debut by one of our favourites: welcome Amsterdam hero Tammo Hesselink, alongside our longtime collaborator Airali all the way from California, DJ ojo’s first ever live show, plus residents b2bs with Ikävä Pii \\u0026 Wordcolour and Queenie \\u0026 Ben.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://a-niche.org/events/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":19,\"name\":\"Club Commons: Book Launch Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-02-12T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-02-12T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e25f35207178e33b503b3815b56fe7d2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a Club Commons book launch with no talks, no panels, no speeches - just music, movement, and collective energy. Author Anjali Prashar-Savoie will be behind the decks alongside friends and collaborators, soundtracking an evening that reflects the spirit of the book: queer nightlife as a space of care, resistance, and possibility.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":4,\"name\":\"CNI 1: Ormside Projects, London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-02-20T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-02-21T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"97e53ee3b4c85369b52da9ace29d9b57.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SELN returns to Ormside for the debut show of it’s 2026 event series Celebrating New Industrial. A celebration in the PUREST SENSE - international artists, local talent, and everything in between performing strong music LIVE.\\n\\nSHXCXCHCXSH [live]\\n\\nWhile borderlining impractical terms such as techno or avantgarde, the Swedish duo has for the past decade built a reputation for their sonic finesse. Simply put their music embodies a primitive urge to BE ALIVE. Following renowned releases on labels including Avian, Northern Electronics and most recently MORD, SHXCXCHCXSH continually manage to create and destroy everything the consumer seeks and enjoys, all whilst keeping a true momentum within their techno sound. NOT TO BE MISSED!\\n\\nDJ Gonz [live]\\n\\nDJ Gonz is a producer, DJ and visual artist hailing from London. He co-runs SELN recordings where his releases perpetuate focused melodic riffs joint with heavy leading percussion. Drawing on influences taken from free-tekno, dub and kuduro, his sound is both pensive, driving whilst still rooted in a soundsystem tradition. Previous output include The Lamentation of Vern, and The Messenger on Wain Records. He has a solo EP on SELN due for release early 2026.\\n\\nSarah Wreath\\n\\nSarah Wreath is a German artist and DJ. With over two decades spent collecting electronic music alongside a DJ practice, her relationship with sound is the result of a long and patient craftsmanship rooted in vinyl, deep listening, and an intuitive understanding of atmosphere and flow.\\n\\nAlongside performing regularly at Tresor Berlin, Wreath recently collaborated on Sandwell District’s album End Beginnings, placing her within the current vanguard of experimental techno, while continuing to explore her sound as a tool for connection and TRANSFORMATION.\\n\\nLNR\\n\\nLNR plays in the shadows. A freetek enthusiast, their sets present their closely studied collection of high bpm and rave-esq music. Testament to their sound, LNR is a regular performer at free party collective V23 in Belgium alongside Amsterdam’s Garage Noord where their sets showcase the hardcore and psychedelic spectrums, integrating technological rawness with dissociative coilz.\\n\\nLNR is the author of Biodegradable Soundsystem, a series of essays, features, and interviews navigating microclimates of old school dance music culture within the sphere of free parties, raves, club culture, and experimental sonics.\\n\\nThere is a limited number of free tickets available for those who are unwaged / on UC. Please email info@selnrecordings.com to reserve one.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2340802\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":45,\"name\":\"KRAUTOCK KARAOKE vol.71— 13th Anniversary Special\",\"start_time\":\"2026-02-27T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-02-28T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6dfdb5297f99c3cac8bf0c74b1d501dd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"13th anniversary / Vol. 71 of Krautrock Karaoke\\n\\nA chaotic crazy night of improvisation of various artists various artforms various sounds. tickets out now, first 19 people to enter will receive a free CD with exclusive recordings from Kenichi Iwasa/ Krautrock Karaoke \\u0026 aloisius/ life is beautiful records.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2362667\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":11,\"name\":\"10 Years of Tanum Sound System\",\"start_time\":\"2026-02-28T22:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-01T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8ba22b4e547f46b07bb690228e790a7b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ten years strong, Tanum soundsystem take to Ormside to celebrate a decade since their first party. Rooted in community, Tanum have spent the past 10 years running fundraisers for marginalised groups, hosting speaker building workshops and throwing infamous all-dayers. This Saturday, they bring together a lineup stacked with significant faces from the system’s orbit: Keeves Bros \\u0026 Manchu, B.O.S.S. DJs, Front Left Life \\u0026 Drime, and the Tanum crew – Crease, Junior Loves, Klaus, L4E, Mellowdramatics, and Winsome.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2329337\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":43,\"name\":\"LIVE X Bolding\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-03T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-03T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"67d506cf4717b94e19f0b2b767bc9635.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Openperformancef x Bolding \\n\\nPerformances by Skjold Rambow with Fie Ljungmann, Zahra Van Nguyen with Sky Bebbs, Casper Dillen, Luisa D Rozo\\n\\n92 Cromer Street\\nWC1H 8DD\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.operformancef.com/rsvp\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":17,\"name\":\"Adventures In Dub #10\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-05T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-05T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"410651717ea800170d22411cba29a63b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SLICKnBOBBY's monthly Dub night in Brixton. DJs, special guests, food stalls, a warm friendly environment and full live sound system. Come down to Arch 555 to catch a vibe IRL.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2337377\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":8,\"name\":\"Diversion\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-06T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-07T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"842e21c24e557581a1f794315e244fb0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Once again, we're making use of the whopping Beatcrime Soundsystem to take over Ormside Projects for a night of our favourite DJs (and close friends).\\n\\nOnce again, we’re importing talent from the fertile underground scenes of Belgium and Bristol and are ecstatic to showcase another episode of experimental soundsystem indebted sonics to the people of London.\\n\\ni-sha manages to fit us into her plans for 2026, having spent 2025 scorching eardrums and singeing synapses all over the UK, Europe and NYC - we're very lucky to have her back since she played the first event we did at Ormside 3 years ago!\\n\\nShe's since been developing her craft into a sort of unspeakable sonic witchery that escapes description, prediction and races through all superlatives.\\n\\nA short list of her recent movements includes touring as part of 10 years of Timedance, Paris, Glasgow, New York, a new show on Tblisi tastemaker's Mutant Radio and a return to organising Bristol music events in the form of The Secret Shade (investigation essential).\\n\\n-\\n\\nojoo is a Moroccan polymath based in Brussels, where you can find her running workshops, facilitating organised activism and dancefloor status quo deconstruction whilst organising the community soundsystem project known as psst. \\n \\nHer DJ practice operates close to the source of her sound. A deadly kaleidoscope of dub, dancehall, and industrial, which orbits only the largest of speaker cabinets. She regularly plays alongside the very best in experimental dub in Europe and 2025 alone saw her support the likes of Shackleton, DJ Marcelle and Demdike Stare. Her credentials are bulletproof, and she’s very often fielded by our good friends at Accidental Meetings and (may she rest in peace) Bokeh Versions.\\n\\nCheck out her recent Kiosk show with NVST and archived show on London’s Kindred Radio.\\n\\n-\\n\\nMish is a hero of Bristol’s music scene, having operated on Noods since its start, working both on the station and behind the bar at Zoggs.\\n\\nA seemingly limitlessly well of dark and sludgy tunes that lie on a gnarly wayline of esotericism between genres such as kraut rock, post punk, industrial, metal and of course dub.\\n\\nThe dark prince’s sets represent a refined (yet extremely dextrous and fun) slice of music we rarely see elsewhere. We honestly couldn’t be more pleased to have him back to play on the rig. \\n\\nHe also produces music which would have slugs doing cartwheels. To get a flavour of Mish, you can check out his releases on grid and dummy hand and listen back to his closing set at Diversion in 2024.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":14,\"name\":\"Triskl w/ Wednesday B2B Richard Gregory, Kristina May (LIVE), B. McQueen and Hoggy\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-06T23:59:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-07T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"912f67e24ad76ba8005586e09553fa2b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A single ray wiggles between branches, beaming down upon wet, thawed earth.\\nStirring memory, an inkling of desire.\\nAs feet slip and slide on grubby park grass, they suddenly remember,\\nThe need to dance.\\n\\nOur fifth encounter will take place on the 6th March. We gather at our favourite spot, with a roster bearing London’s finest: Wednesday, Richard Gregory, B. McQueen, Kristina May, and Hoggy.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2312177\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":70,\"name\":\"Sore\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-07T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7444a579cd08cacd9f48a56add370d05.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An evening of readings, performance, and music featuring Adriana Lasheras Mabanta, Louis Mason, Inka Hilsenbek, Billy Morgan, Kate Tyndall, Moritz Tibes, and aloisius. The publication's latest issue, as well as a special limited poster print, will be available to purchase.\\n\\nSore is a serial literary anthology, initiated in November 2022, that explores the everyday manifestations of a divergent movement between body and mind. The project understands writing itself as a tool to navigate this gap, supporting authors in collectively developing new works in a multitude of genres – spanning prose fiction, poetry, and diary keeping. For our third issue, contributors were selected from an open call inviting authors to respond to the themes of Virgina Woolf's 1926 essay, \\\"On Being Ill.\\\"\\n\\nSore is the joint production of editors Mathilde Heuliez, Kristina Stallvik, and Lisa Lagova.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/sore-publication-launch-tickets-1983450864930?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\\u0026fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQMMjU2MjgxMDQwNTU4AAGnF9RwxlU6k1rrKxvxiT8IiH0GDqclujr4b4EFcrGxpyGtnpXtH9lxeZ03woc_aem_JID3JfZfKo4_RmX3cf3SMg\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":46,\"name\":\"Nebo Arts\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-07T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-08T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"29d91483d2d3e91725203c7c929e3491.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For their first dance of the year, Nebo Arts present a night of leftfield electronic and archival sounds from A Colder Consciousness, Oliver Kay and Lizzie Urquhart.\\n\\nFlora Pitrolo is the Palermo-based academic, archivist and DJ behind A Colder Consciousness. Her work investigates alternative European performance and music cultures of the 1980s, with a special focus on Italy and the Balkan region.\\n\\nLizzie Urquhart is a DJ, artist and co-founder of record label Somewhere Press. She has honed her sound over a series of radio shows and guest mixes, characterised by their reflective nature. Her DJ sets take on a hypnotic EBM sound, a low-tempo pulse across pitched-down chuggers and leftfield dub - intertwining the dark, emotional and psychedelic into a meandering narrative.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2356315\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":31,\"name\":\"Get Sexy\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-07T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-08T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2290d651ec7e5b99b81c06742a38436d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Get Sexy is all about sexy, sleazy, pumping house music - bringing together the heads and the queers and everyone in between for a night of pure dancefloor magic.\\n\\nExpect silliness and sexiness from some of the best in the underground. This one is not to be missed!\\n\\nHouse is a feeling, music is the answer.\\n\\nThis is a queer friendly event open to all. A night of good vibes, good energy and good people.\\n\\nSee you on the dancefloor x\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2358288\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":41,\"name\":\"KAVARI - Plague Music Release Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-07T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-08T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2dcf446354f55a21f4d4d552b754c7d9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kavari (DJ)\\n+ Special Guests\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2372367\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":44,\"name\":\"Everything Can Be Felt\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-10T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-10T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a27f6c862bc12a72cfc6cc8c4d2eba9b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Everything Can Be Felt - a radical improvised set by Olivia, Monchan \\u0026 Coby\\n\\nFields Become Sky - Monasunne live set\\n\\nOlivia, Monchan \\u0026 Coby (Members of GAISTER) come together through voice, percussion, and multi-instrumental composition, crafting a unique fusion shaped by improvisation, precision, and conceptual depth.\\n\\nMonasunne are Lara Agar and Louis d’Heudières. Their first album, Fields Become Sky, was released on Hyperdelia in June 2025, garnering praise from The Quietus and coverage on BBC Radio 3’s Late Junction.\\n\\nStarting from their shared experience of growing up in East Anglia in the UK, the duo dug into the history of the region, finding myths and poems written at a time when it was an independent kingdom. Rather than embalm a buried past, Monasunne re-imagine the historical geographies as a myth. The sonic worlding that results is a journeying across distanced times.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/nv97p3-everything-can-be-felt-a-radical-improvised-set-by-olivia-monchan-coby-monasunne-live-10th-mar-iklectik-london-tickets?dice_id=8465558\\u0026dice_channel=web\\u0026dice_tags=organic\\u0026dice_campaign=DICE\\u0026dice_feature=mio_marketing\\u0026_branch_match_id=1147658534976493535\\u0026utm_source=web\\u0026utm_campaign=DICE\\u0026utm_medium=mio_marketing\\u0026_branch_referrer=H4sIAAAAAAAAA8soKSkottLXz8nMy9ZLyUxO1UvL1c8wNzIySjFKNDUxMbKvK0pNSy0qysxLj08qyi8vTi2ydc4oys9NBQAIy6KQOwAAAA%3D%3D\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":55,\"name\":\"Cycles of Resistance – Community Iftar\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-11T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-11T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"481c83f2de3c25542f110cd17122b6f7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us to mark Women’s History Month with a community Iftar open to people of marginalised genders. Following a meal, there’ll be a short talk linking the personal and political struggles against period poverty and for bodily autonomy in Palestine, Sudan and Britain. The rest of the evening will involve performances, henna, zine-making and opportunities for collective discussion and the celebration of feminist resistance.\\n\\nThis Iftar is a fundraiser to support charities focused on period poverty and reproductive justice.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pelicanhouse.org/event/cycles-of-resistance-community-iftar/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":24,\"name\":\"GRAIN Presents: Ute Kanngiesser \\u0026 Theo Guttenplan (duo), Theodora Laird, Conal Blake, Caius Williams (trio), Emilie Škrijelj \\u0026 Tom Malmendier (duo)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-11T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"706cf481ffaac360509411db309e6872.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"GRAIN is a concert series and archiving project for experimental and improvised music, largely happening within South Bermondsey, and programmed / produced by Caius Williams \\u0026 Theodora Laird.\\n\\nThrough programming and documenting new and adventurous music through collaboration, archiving, workshops, and performances, the project explores the ongoing dialogue between the transience of DIY art spaces and the communities that inhabit them. \\n_____\\n\\nUte Kanngießer is a London based cellist and composer from Germany. Over the years, she has carefully deconstructed her classical roots and almost exclusively performs unscripted, improvised music. Much of her work has evolved in relationship with other art forms such as film, poetry, dance and site specific work. She is interested in the vast expressive possibilities of her instrument in relation to body, space, and others, always looking to rediscover or redefine what is musical/lyrical in this moment in time.\\nRecent releases include Blue Monday - a collaboration with writer Zara Joan Miller - on New York label Reading Group.\\n_____\\n\\nTheo Guttenplan is a drummer and percussionist from London, playing improvised and other musics. He is also interested in woodworking, crosswords, computers, and football.\\n_____\\n\\nTheodora Laird is a vocalist and multidisciplinary artist. Releases under her solo project ‘feeo’ have received critical acclaim. Theodora's practice has involved in tandem with an interest in situating narratives within freely improvised music, specifically through frequent involvement in the GRAIN residency.\\n_____\\n\\nConal Blake is a musician from Glasgow. He currently plays solo and improvises with Li Song and Regan Bowering, using electronics and percussion. He also runs the Feedback Moves label.\\n_____\\n\\nCaius Williams is a musician from London who plays the double bass, guitar, and bass guitar. He works in collaboration with others, alongside various solo projects, often working with improvisation and explorations of resonance, and perception.  \\n\\n\\n_____\\n\\nEmilie Skrijelj and Tom Malmendier began to work together in 2019, with the duo \\\"Les Marquises\\\", an electric and intense duo in which Emilie plays turntable, amplified accordion and electronics, and Tom plays the drums.\\n\\nTheir last cd Live in Nickelsdorf was just released on their own label eux sæm.\\n\\nIn parallel with this duo, they developed other projects in collaborations with international musicians, such as Michael Thieke, Otomo Yoshihide, Christine Abdelnour, Angelica Castello, Mike Ladd, a.o...\\n\\nLately they wanted to explore a more acoustic duo, with only snare drum for Tom, and a small portable turntable for Emilie, mostly played with objects..\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.thehorsehospital.com/events/grain-march11\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":60,\"name\":\"LISA / Relax Kevin \\u0026 IR / eastangliarecords / Ed Lehan (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-11T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"416dbee75d384418eeb19aa4d52b752e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lineup :\\n\\nLISA is three souls in a room erupting. \\n\\nTheir debut is conjured by Koichi Yamanoha and Anastasia Freygang using rhythmic samples, synthesizer percussion, guitar and vocals.\\n\\nLISA's first Album Yamaha Dog is being released by Bristol based Collapsing Drums.\\n\\nhttps://collapsingdrums.bandcamp.com/album/yamaha-dog\\n\\n-- \\n\\nRelax Kev \\u0026 IR // opened out guitar spills and freeform lullabies. For their live set they will move between improv, works in progress and full-blown ballads. Their debut EP 'All Over the Road' is out in March 2026\\n\\n--\\n\\neastangliarecords' hazel sticks started life in a Manor House and gardens in Norfolk and constructed as a tracking device for filming any potential scandal within the grounds. When rotated a beautiful voice emerged. Here it is presented with mc eastangliarecords. Due to seasonal change the sticks no longer have a voice, the throat is dry and the mc feeds new voices.\\n\\nhttp://www.eastangliarecords.com/\\n\\n--\\n\\nThe night will end with a DJ set of deep selections from Ed Lehan.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ticketlab.app/event/37831#/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":91,\"name\":\"Testing the Water presents: Melodie Blaison (live), Poole (live), Daksh (dj)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-11T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-11T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ff4666a89463a6ca01c5345c2328c2bd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Come see in the spring with us, as we ease into new, warmer waters...\\nFor our first gig of 2026, we’re thrilled to be bringing two artists from out of town to a space we think is perfectly suited to their work.\\n\\nWith soft furnishings, floor mats, and a custom‑built sound system (plus a BYOB policy!), it creates the ideal environment for music that rewards close attention, and punters who are up for getting comfy.\\n\\nMélodie Blaison is a Brussels-based flautist and experimental composer, whose work dissolves the boundaries between instrumental performance, sound art, and immersive listening. Trained at the Conservatoire before expanding into visual arts and sound creation, she has developed a distinctive language rooted in breath, texture, and the evocative potential of sonic memory.\\n\\nAcross installations, concerts, and radio performances - whether opening for Loraine James or playing in a 17th century church - Blaison explores hybrid environments where sound, sculpture, and narrative intersect. Approaching the flute as a vessel for storytelling rather than a fixed instrument, her performances weave together transverse and ceramic flutes, field recordings, and analogue electronics to create sound worlds that feel intimate yet otherworldly.\\n\\nPoole is a Glasgow‑based electronic sound artist working at the intersection of environmental music, post‑digital sound practices, and folk traditions. His live work is immersive and textural, moving between meditative resonance and fractured digital landscapes, inviting listeners to experience sound as a living ecology shaped by touch, weathering, and transformation.\\n\\nSince releasing his sophomore record Ben Beinn, he has deepened his engagement with the materiality of sound, crafting basalt sculptures inspired by Pinuccio Sciola that function as both instruments and geological archives. Alongside these sculptures, Poole has built a lithophone from slate gathered on the Scottish Slate Isles, merging fieldwork, craft, and composition. These stones, activated through physical gesture and electronic augmentation, form the basis of new material developed for this performance.\\n\\nSitting alongside these two performances will be Daksh. Having cut his teeth at Edinburgh's Sneaky Pete’s - where he still regularly programmes his own night Membrane - Daksh has since been busy opening for some of our favourite artists, including James K and feeo. His recent appearance at Ormside Projects (since captured in this highly-recommended mix for Kiosk Radio) took us on a drift through warm ambient textures and field recordings, unfolding through moments of stillness and tension. We’re looking forward to him bringing that same careful ear and steadied, atmospheric touch to Shai Space.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2377789\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":65,\"name\":\"Everybody to Kenmore Street + Q\\u0026A\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-12T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-12T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5037cfe13a8b64c41ab4d4b51024be34.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Anti-establishment struggles and activism run in the veins of Glasgow inhabitants. So when In May 2021, a U.K. Home Office raid is launched at dawn on the first day of Eid, it triggers one of the most spontaneous acts of civil resistance in recent memory. In Scotland’s most diverse neighbourhood, hundreds of residents rush to Kenmure Street to stop the deportation of their neighbours. \\n\\nHackney Anti-Raids was established in response to the action on Kenmure Street and will be joining us for a post-screening Q\\u0026A alongside director Felipe Bustos Sierra (NAE PASARAN), hosted by Sylvie Dumont.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://riocinema.org.uk/Rio.dll/WhatsOn?f=2274989\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":48,\"name\":\"happyhumans : AMBIENT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-12T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"68ae78c327ebfc02e8b0d7fbb65cb4db.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An evening of immersive electronic and experimental ambient at Shai Space.\\n\\nThe night brings together two distinct live approaches to texture and form. Hems performs a live set navigating extended drone, resonant metal and evolving electronic structures, unfolding through sustained tone, spatial depth and tactile detail. happyhappyface, echoing the nights theme, presents minimal analog compositions shaped through keyboard improvisation and modular synthesis, moving between restraint and rupture with a language informed by IDM, techno and classical.\\n\\nVisuals by Ralph Berryman will be created live using microscopic image processes, revealing shifting micro-textural landscapes that echo the sonic terrain of the evening.\\n*\\n*\\n*\\n*\\n*\\nHenrique Matias (Hems) is a London-based artist working between experimental electronics and contemporary sound practice. As co-founder of Titrate, he has developed a platform dedicated to exploratory electronic and drone music, fostering a collective commitment to pushing sonic boundaries. His most recent performance took place at Funkhaus Berlin for Spatial Festival by MONOM, presented across a 60-speaker, 12-sub immersive sound system.\\n\\nhappyhappyface merges keyboard and modular systems into dynamic, unpredictable sonic environments. A regular presence on the London scene, he has performed across Europe from Manchester to Hamburg.\\n\\nRalph Berryman is a London-based multidisciplinary artist whose practice spans Fine Art, Set Design and Architecture.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2376374\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":83,\"name\":\"Dirar Kalash: Orbits of Time - مدارات الزمن\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-12T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"61ff5b09a95d152a555b09709c4ea8cf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A four-channel electro-acoustic composition for double-bass and live electronics\\n\\nJoin us for the premiere of a new durational sonic composition by Dirar Kalash, an immersive live performance that traces the shifting, poetic resonances of the moon across time and space. Weaving together electronic sound, field recordings, and acoustic instrumentation, the work unfolds into a contemplative continuum of sound.\\n\\nMoving between silence and presence, the composition explores how we attune ourselves to the supposed distance of historical time. Orbits of Time engages the tension between distance and proximity to and from Palestine. Layers of texture and tone emerge and dissolve, inviting a listening to what is intimate, expansive and political. It reflects on the Palestinian experience - past and ongoing. \\n\\nPresented at Mosaic Rooms, the performance acts as a site-responsive sonic intervention, entering into dialogue with Dima Srouji’s permanent commission, Four Moons from Home.\\n\\nFree entry. Sign up via the link below to reserve a spot.\\n\\nDoors open: 7pm - a chance to visit Bouchra Khalili’s Circles and Storytellers and our bookshop.\\nPerformance start: 7.30pm\\nEnd: ~9pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/dirar-kalash-orbits-of-time--tickets-1984639543299\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":76,\"name\":\"One Jazz \\u0026 Audio Gold presents On The Corner at The Mildmay: SULA\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-12T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-12T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6dd7abaa87ba90248ebfc6cbb50bd430.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"One Jazz and Audio Gold are delighted to have another amazing, upcoming band SULA play our first date of 2026 this March. SULA is a new trio project made up of drummer Miranda Radford, bassist Aleks Dimitrova and pianist Kezia Abuoma. All currently studying jazz at Trinity Laban, these exciting young musicians have come up through hailed jazz organisation Tomorrow's Warriors.Taking inspiration from the likes of Kris Davis, Wayne Shorter and Orrin Evans, these three unique voices have come together to play both their original compositions and other music inspired by the energetic sounds of modern-day jazz.\\n\\nAfter glowing reviews at We Out Here this year, be sure to catch this trio LIVE at the historic Mildmay club on the Audio Gold, audiophile sound system.\\n\\nThursday 12th March,\\nSmall Hall, Doors 7.30pm\\nMembers £10, Non-Members £12\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/mildmayclubandinstituteltd/2041087\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":51,\"name\":\"Queer Ambient Sauna | o•rbyss w/ S3BA\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-13T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-13T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e546962aecd08472db9349df97490e5c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"o•rbyss presents the Queer Ambient Sauna Sessions at Sauna Social Club. Inviting queer DJs to reveal a softer side of their sound outside of a rave and offering alternative safe spaces to bask in the warmth of community, while nurturing our wellbeing.\\n\\nOn Friday and Saturday evenings, we curate a line up of DJ’s and live acts to soundtrack our listening lounge. The main sauna is equipped with a sound system for deep listening. Our upstairs sauna and yard offer a social setting, perfect for a catch up and meeting new friends.\\n\\nS3BA is a trans*disciplinary musician and artist whose individual practice spans DJing, live performance, flute, and vocals. She is a resident with Makaan, Blue Parti and Playbody, for whom they curate the collective’s ambient event Afterglow. \\n\\nThey hosts a monthly show on Netil Radio with collaborator Akis Ka, and recent highlights include playing Copenhagen’s Den Anden Side, a performance at The Mercury Prize with FKA Twigs, and live performance at the V\\u0026A Storehouse with trio SEMARĀ.\\n\\nEach ticket includes a 70-minute session to move between sauna and ice baths, before and after unwinding in the lounge. \\n\\nDoors open at 6pm and you're welcome to stay until close at 10:30pm. Arrive early to soak in the atmosphere and enjoy the music programme to the fullest.\\n\\nHow to book for a friend: You can only book one slot at a time. Book yourself onto the session and pay, then go to the same session again and select 'book for someone else'.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.saunasocialclub.co.uk/book#/class-detail/4340030/r/1383\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":58,\"name\":\"Free Practice 001\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-13T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-13T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b657be2ab9abdbada763fd544c10405f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"2 poets\\n1 mic\\nA conversation\\nJust words\\n\\n\\nFree Practice is a bi-monthly poetry night shaped by a conversation between two poets. In an ongoing exchange between the poets and their work, space is created for echoes, responses and interruptions.\\n\\nFREE PRACTICE 01 Features Brother Portrait + eve of poems\\n\\nWe’re starting Free Practice because we’ve noticed something missing in the poetry event landscape. While many nights spotlight a wide range of voices on a single bill, Free Practice makes room for something more focused: a duet. Two poets, one stage, and a shared space for dialogue that’s improvised, porous, and alive.\\n\\nAcross 45 minutes, two poets move in and out of each other’s work; riffing, responding, colliding, and letting their poems take on new forms in the presence of each other. Think of it like a back-to-back DJ set: two selectors weaving a shared sonic and emotional journey, guided not by a script but by energy, trust, and curiosity.\\n\\nAfter the poets have performed, the evening transforms into a conversation and Q+A hosted by Rohan Ayinde. Serving as interviewer and first responder, Ayinde guides a discussion that traces the threads that emerged during the performance.\\n\\nFree Practice is a site for overlap, for listening, and for spontaneous invention. It’s an invitation to witness two voices finding new rhythms together, and to learn in the spaces between them.\\n\\nBios:\\n\\nbrother portrait is a London-born Sierra Leonean artist \\u0026 writer often thinking on: memory and objects as vessels; how we're shaped by space and place; the limits of language; social living; map making and; freedom dreaming. His preoccupations find form in poetry, prose and song\\n\\nEve AKA Eve of Poems (she/they) is an award-winning spoken word artist, storyteller and creative community facilitator based in South-East London. A 2022 BBC Words First poet, Eve’s work has featured on BBC4, Radio 1Xtra, at BFI Flare Festival and film festivals worldwide. Her animated poem, After The After Party, won an RTS award for best short form in 2023. Her latest project, poetry film Holding An Island, is due to be released later this year.\\n\\nWith an immersive, trauma-informed and radically present praxis, Eve brings spoken word to schools, prisons, arts organisations such as Roundhouse and Southbank Centre and programmes such as Daniel Kaluuya’s Centre 59, helping to nurture the next generation of poets. She organises and hosts Special Guest, a monthly community open mic night where the audience are the special guests and anyone can take the mic for 60 seconds.\\n\\nEve’s happiest drinking tea, learning a new language, and listening to grime on TfL.\\n\\nRohan Ayinde (they/he) is a poet and artist from Tulse Hill Estate committed to dreaming new worlds through a Black feminist imagination\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2377786\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":49,\"name\":\"Les Disques Omnison presents: Orion Music Workshop, Shelter, Jeanne Gorisse, Oda Fiasco Bravo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-13T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-13T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2c6d7ca92aefd81103962047e2405efd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Big One ! Les Disques Omnison, Paris based label run by Tom Val AKA Orion Music Workshop since 2021 presents 4 lives by artists from the label roster : Orion Music Workshop's industrial fourth world, Shelter's acid ambient, Jeanne Gorisse's electric bass improvisations and Oda Fiasco Bravo's emo-IDM chants.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2356327\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":77,\"name\":\"Moin +++\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-13T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-14T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bf86daee9768c9faa15167ce5bb73a1a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2378443\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":82,\"name\":\"Dengue Dengue Dengue\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-13T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-14T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ea1aa2c37e933425f07ae746311c97a2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"From the heart of Lima, Perú, Dengue Dengue Dengue bring Tropical Bass to life like no one else. Behind the masks are Felipe Salmon and Rafael Pereira, producers, DJs, and graphic designers whose sound fuses the traditional with the futuristic.\\n\\nTheir musical explorations span psychedelic cumbia, dub, salsa, footwork, tribal, and techno  — a kaleidoscope of genres that constantly evolve.\\n\\nDengue Dengue Dengue mixes rhythms from Perú and beyond, blending old and new, analogue and digital, to create a hypnotic, audiovisual experience.\\n\\nAcross distorted kicks, warped reggaeton, and orchestral synths, the masked duo encapsulate everything from Singeli to Doble Paso Reggaeton, crafting a tripped-out, fully unhinged experience.\\n\\nIn 2024, the cutting-edge duo returned with AGITA2, their first EP in nearly two years, released via Florentino’s Club Romantico. Mixed entirely by themselves, this five-track odyssey pulses with Latin-rooted rhythms and boundary-breaking production, propelling the pair into a bold new sonic realm.\\n\\nTwelve years in the game, Dengue Dengue Dengue are still outdoing themselves and expanding the size of their sonic universe at every turn.\\n\\n\\nJoining them is prolific Chilean producer DJ Raff, who also counts DDD as regular collaborators, as well as Colombian sound artist, DJ, organiser, Patricia Doors to keep the Cheeky soundsystem fired up all night long!\\n\\n+ Opening the space with an immersive sound experience is Colombian sound artist Viviana Caro\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/avergv-dengue-dengue-dengue-13th-mar-club-cheek-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":57,\"name\":\"ORMSIDE presents: DJ Nigga Fox – Two Nights\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-13T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-14T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"94928d0481fb3fd25f7c528d054fbab3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"THURSDAY 12/03/26 [19:30-23:30]\\nDJ Nigga Fox (Live)\\nKareem Samara \\nOkaeri (Kenichi Iwasa \\u0026 Samara Langham )\\n\\nFRIDAY 13/03/26 [23:00-05:00]\\nDJ Nigga Fox (DJ)\\nCooly G\\nSaint Abdullah \\u0026 Eomac (Live)\\nXterea (Live)\\nMellowdramatics\\nShare\\n\\nORMSIDE presents DJ Nigga Fox for two nights.\\n\\nA pivotal figure in the evolution of contemporary batida emerging from Lisbon’s Angolan-Portuguese community, brought to worldwide acclaim via beloved label, collective and party series Príncipe Discos.\\n\\nThrough Thursday and Friday, we approach DJ Nigga Fox’s work as a lens – tracing parallels between fractured histories and approaches towards sonic construction, rhythm, and storytelling. Across the two nights, he is joined by Kareem Samara, Kenichi Iwasa \\u0026 Samara Langham, Xterea, Mellowdramatics, Saint Abdullah \\u0026 Eomac, and Cooly G.\\n\\nSupported by Carhartt WIP\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2358868\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":15,\"name\":\"Squares // Ekkel, Mia Cecille \\u0026 Patrick Rowe\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-13T23:59:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-14T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e99cc8c0fb27d526c96c0b2cbdb226c2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Diving into the new year with another long journey through the night. Powered by 3 exceptional artists and set in the ex-industrial emerging institution, Gaffe.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2315955\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":52,\"name\":\"West London Dub Club: Ital Power Meets Jah Messenjah\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-14T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-14T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c43537c92f85f7f52b081dba6959e963.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"West London Dub Club presents Chapter VI:\\nITAL POWER meets JAH MESSENJAH\\n\\nALL TRIBES WELCOME!\\n5PM-11PM\\nSaturday 14th March 2026\\n\\nThe Dominion Centre\\n112 The Green, Southall UB2 4BQ\\n\\nFood - Music - Merchandise\\n\\nItal Power Sound System\\n-Outta West London\\n-M.Ital, Ital Shash, Benji Roots \\u0026 full crew\\n\\nJah Messenjah Sound System\\n-Outta Swindon\\n\\nBoth playing on their own full sound systems\\nStrictly heavyweight business till done!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.skiddle.com/whats-on/Uxbridge/The-Dominion-Centre/Ital-Power-meet-Jah-Messenjah---West-London-Dub-Club/42129734/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":69,\"name\":\"Musical Overload : Earthquake Sound, Soul Energy Musiq, R.B.F. Sound System \",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-14T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-14T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8ea2a93cd390d05a2bcae8d7d91ee39e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"YES PEOPLE 💯\\nMUSICAL OVERLOAD IS BACK ONCE AGAIN 📣\\n\\nBIG SOUND SYSTEMS MUSICAL JUGGLE 🎛️\\nMUSIC FOR THE SOUL\\n\\nQUALITY ASSURED, TAKING IT BACK IN TIME TO WHEN SOUND USED TO RUN NICE 🔊 ORIGINAL STYLE\\n\\nMUSICAL DISC, PLAYED BY THE FLICK OF THE WRIST ⬆️🔔\\n\\n£10 OTD CASH ONLY\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":67,\"name\":\"Silkarmour, Nik Colk Void, MM'99\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-14T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-14T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"24a081481b58224be80e977940877943.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Silkarmour (Live)\\nNik Colk Void (Live)\\nMM'99 (Live)\\n\\nin the round\\n\\na night of multidisciplinary electronic acts\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2368290\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":63,\"name\":\"Queer House Party \\u0026 Friends: Emergency Fundraiser for Calais Appeal\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-14T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-15T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"74013914101a9ec4b3d0f177301f16c7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Over the past few months we've seen anti-migrant rhetoric and action escalate from an already very hostile place. From various wannabe crusaders and fascists making the journey to Northern France to harrass displaced people; destroying boats, life jackets, attacking them and stealing their belongings to blatantly racist policy proposals and messaging coming from the government. \\n\\n\\nWe've teamed up with Calais Appeal before, and we knew it was time we had to again. It's so necessary in this climate to reach beyond our community to support all those that are marginalised and at the sharp end of state oppression and violence. \\n\\nSo, we're supporting their winter fundraising drive by doing what we know best… \\n\\nGetting a together a bunch of our pals, packing out a club with some  of the most gorgeous queers and getting sweaty until the sun rises. \\n\\nSo that's exactly what we're going to do. 💋\\n\\n \\n\\nExpect our classic DIY energy from a select line up of some of our nearest and dearest- QHP family vibes all night long to keep it pumping start to finish. 🥵\\n\\n \\n\\nMarch 14th, 10pm-4am, Vespers Club, SE15\\n\\nFull line up released soon. \\n\\n \\n\\nTickets are cheap \\u0026 capacity is limited. So get yours in asap. \\n\\nArtwork by @lynne.on.paper\\n\\n\\n‘At Calais Appeal, we are working hard to provide dignified and human support to people on the move at the UK–France border, as they will once again be forced to sleep rough during the freezing winter months.\\n\\nWe treat people with respect, dignity and provide essential services - food, water, tents, specialist support for women and children…. the list goes on.. But these services are  only possible if we receive the support we need.​’\\n\\n \\n\\nFind out more about Calais Appeal here → https://www.calaisappeal.org/\\n\\nVENUE:\\nWe're gassed to be hosting this event at Vespers Club for the first time ever. One of London's few trans+ run clubs at 133a Rye Ln, London SE15 4BQ. \\n\\nACCESS + WELFARE:\\nVespers Club has step free access and the venue is partially wheelchair accessible. The wheelchair access is via a separate entrance and uses a lift to descend to the basement of the building where the club is located. The bar and accessible toilet have step free access. The dancefloor is sunken and is accessed via 5 steps down.\\n\\nAs this event has no performances, we'll have no BSL interpreters and no hearing induction loop will be installed. We have a welfare team, with one member trained in BSL. Free tickets are available for carers and personal assistants (PAs). If you have any questions, please email us at queerhouseparty@gmail.com.\\n \\n\\nTICKETS AND GUEST LIST:\\nQueer House Party is for everyone, but trans people to the front! We’ve worked hard to keep ticket prices affordable. Tickets are on a sliding scale from £7.50–£15. If cost is still a barrier for you, send us a message and we’ll add you to our free list.\\n\\nLow-income Tickets: These are for those receiving Universal Credit or equivalent, working-class students, and people earning minimum wage. They are limited, so please be mindful before purchasing.\\nGeneral Admission Tickets: These are for those on a salary, students, comfortable freelancers, or those who are “skint atm” but have some savings.\\nSolidarity Tickets: These tickets are for those financially stable enough that rent and bills aren’t a daily struggle (this could be you—take a moment to reflect!).\\nGuest List and Discount Codes: If none of these options work for you, our guest list is reserved for people who can’t afford ticket prices, particularly those with No Recourse to Public Funds. Email us at qhptickets@gmail.com, and we’ll sort it out—no need to disclose any personal details about your situation.\\nCarer and Support Worker Tickets: Your ticket is free if you are coming as a support worker for a ticket holder.\\nVIPS: If you consider yourself a VIP, this probably isn’t the party for you.\\nRefund Policy: To help keep our ticket prices affordable, we don’t offer any refunds. However, you’re welcome to sell your ticket on.\\nQueer House Party is all about celebrating everybody, no apologies, no filters. This is your space to be loud and 100% you. Mutual respect is a must, and consent isn’t up for debate. We’re here to build each other up and tear down anything that gets in the way of feeling safe and free. \\n\\nZero Tolerance Policy on Harassment and Discrimination\\nAt Queer House Party, we are committed to creating a safe and inclusive space for everyone. We have a zero-tolerance policy towards any form of harassment, discrimination, or abusive behaviour based on race, gender, sexual orientation, disability, religion, or any other personal characteristic. Anyone engaging in such behaviour will be asked to leave immediately. Consent is vital and non-negotiable. \\n\\nSubstance Policy\\nWe encourage responsible alcoholic drinking and plenty of hydration. Our bar serves a range of alcoholic and non-alcoholic options to suit all preferences. If you think you've had too much, reach out to our welfare team, who will be able to help. Aggressive or unsafe behaviour towards anyone will not be tolerated.\\n\\nEntry Policy\\nYou must bring your ID for entry. We also reserve the right to refuse entry to anyone whose actions or attitudes conflict with these values, ensuring that our event remains a welcoming environment for all.\\n \\n\\nGot a question? Email queerhouseparty@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/33934/queer-house-party-friends-emergency-fundraiser-for-calais-appeal\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":18,\"name\":\"Kool FM Brixton Takeover: Tim Reaper, Silva Snipa, Jolie P + more\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-14T22:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-15T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8ad2a6bae1184652498ec74328d8e7a3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kool FM heads to Brixton for an unmissable, high-energy night dedicated to jungle and drum \\u0026 bass 🔊🎛️\\n\\nRenowned for its commitment to the scene, one of the most influential platforms of UK underground music is taking over Hootananny Brixton to celebrate dnb culture. Expect a BIG bass-heavy night with a serious lineup of heavyweight selectors..\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/7dpm8v-kool-fm-brixton-takeover-tim-reaper-silva-snipa-jolie-p-more-14th-mar-hootananny-brixton-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":59,\"name\":\"Sunday Sequence: ddwy (live), Georgi☻ooOoO, Inner Totality\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-15T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-15T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a3e7173de11e1c6e931edf05024fd333.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sunday Dance @ Spanners\\n\\nddwy (live)\\nGeorgi☻ooOoO (Creatures)\\nInner Totality\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2381746\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":111,\"name\":\"Avalon Choir\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-16T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c63970998f86a7260805c2598711fd92.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A drop-in community choir singing a fruity blend of folk/pop/jazzy sounds in acapella harmony, including original compositions and songs of resistance. Meeting for fun, performing sometimes, everyone welcome! £8 a session (cash or card)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":74,\"name\":\"Maggie Nicols: The Gathering IX\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-16T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a08069778e332084c7d8afb35c16f3dc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Gathering is a monthly residency series from vocalist, dancer and performer Maggie Nicols. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.thehorsehospital.com/events/maggie-nicols-the-gathering-9\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":64,\"name\":\"PIEHOUSE PRESENTS: Atesami, HTMLJones, Noum, Trial Tapes\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"66778bc54d18ead4a91f9fb8ac3e6d1e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Piehouse presents 4 acts from our community, that we think you should know about! Come down and find your new favourite artist before they're famous. \\n\\n \\n\\nOn the lineup: \\n\\nAtesami\\n\\nHTMLJones\\n\\nNoum\\n\\nTrial Tapes\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/33795/piehouse-presents-atesami-htmljones-noum-trial-tapes\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":114,\"name\":\"Films4Freedom and The Learning Co-op Presents: The Battle Of Algiers\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"212e4dcea803cc1e645e50cbf7daa20e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Films4Freedom and The Learning Co-op invites you to join us for a special fundraising screening of Gillo Pontecorvo’s revolutionary masterpiece, “The Battle of Algiers”, to understand the tactics of the Algerian revolution and their relevance to global struggles today.\\n\\nJoin us to witness the steadfast courage and success of Algerian resistance against French colonial occupation. We will examine how imperialist exploitation inevitably leads to organised, popular resistance, and how the tactics of the Algerian National-Liberation Front, from clandestine organising to the battle for public opinion, continue to inspire global struggles against oppression today, from Western Sahara to Palestine and beyond.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://wegottickets.com/event/696239\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":32,\"name\":\"Conjuring #1 ft. Lucinda Chua, Ben Vince, Xiaoqiao, Saied Silbak\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-19T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1b05b02d93577335bab4a617a7f23fbd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Conjuring #1 features a live improvisation by Lucinda Chua, Ben Vince, Xiaoqiao and Saied Silbak.\\n\\nConjuring is a monthly live music event series curated by Studio Njoku, and presented by Club Cheek.\\n\\nConjuring brings together leading experimental musicians for collaborative, improvised performances. The project foregrounds musical dialogue, community building and spiritual expression.\\n\\nEach edition features a unique lineup of guest musicians performing a one-time live improvisation around a central motif developed by Tony Njoku.\\n\\nLucinda Chua is a composer, producer and artist with British, Malaysian and ancestral Chinese roots. Her elemental soundscapes embrace the hybridity of traditional instruments and electronic production, often combining voice, cello and effects to create music that is both intimate and expansive.\\n\\nBen Vince is a composer and performer, known for his improvised saxophone explorations and inventive techniques in creating new rhythms, textures and moods.\\n\\nXiaoqiao is a London-based harpist and singer-songwriter who fuses harp with a blend of electronic effects and ghostly vocals, crafting a hypnotic soundscape into the under river.\\n\\nSaied Silbak is a London-based Palestinian composer and oud virtuoso renowned for his evocative fusion of Arabic maqam, jazz, and Western classical traditions.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/wwrn8v-lucinda-chua-ben-vince-xiaoqiao-saied-silbak-19th-mar-club-cheek-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":66,\"name\":\"Dan Nicholls, Dudù Kouate, Seb Rochford \\u0026 guests + Iko Chérie (Dj set)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"278eef9df13eb4844ede4dd95bbf71f9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Keyboardist, producer and improviser Dan Nicholls––who has worked with Alabaster De Plume, Matthew Herbert, Dali De Saint Paul, Shabaka, Goldie, Saint Abdullah and many more––invites a group of friends for a one-off gig in the intimate space downstairs at Total Refreshment Centre.\\n\\nDan will be joined by one of the world's most dazzling and creative percussionists, Dudù Kouate (Moor Mother, Art Ensemble of Chicago) and Seb Rochford (Patti Smith, Brian Eno), Cypher Alexander plus secret guests.\\n\\nAs an versatile and boundary-pushing musician, Dan embraces sound as a tool for liberation, healing and joyful communion. Intricately crafting sound worlds which invite listeners to explore both other-worldly perceptions and the grounding and embodying nature of sound and movement, their work deeply considers how sonic (and other) gestures might facilitate forms of resistance, unity and deeper understanding. Dan co-curates the event series Free Movements.\\n\\n+Iko Chérie (dj set)\\n\\nIko Chérie's sets celebrate women in music, digging into laid-back disco, experimental bangers, leftfield indie gems and psychedelic grooves from around the world.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/k695pl-dan-nicholls-dud-kouate-seb-rochford-guests-19th-mar-downstairs-total-refreshment-centre-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":30,\"name\":\"Eavesdropping: A Festival of Experimental Musics\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-22T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3515584c720a03505aa6a670eeac6348.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"eavesdropping returns to Cafe OTO for another four-day festival, curated by Juliet Fraser, which includes four evening double-bill events and a weekend-long forum of provocations up the road at Vortex Jazz Club. We hope to stimulate your ears and your imagination by presenting new work by eight artists working at the experimental fringes of a variety of genres. The programming within each set is artist-led: repertoire is only announced on the night.\\n\\neavesdropping\\neavesdropping is a platform for the sharing of new music and new ways of thinking about music. Founded by soprano Juliet Fraser in 2017, our activity includes a festival, a forum, a podcast, outpost events around the UK and artist development opportunities. Our mission is to build community through an ethics of curiosity and care, in the belief that ripples do make waves.\\nhttps://www.eavesdropping.london\\n\\neavesdropping is a PRS Foundation Talent Development Network Partner supported by PPL. eavesdropping gratefully acknowledges the generous support of Arts Council England's National Lottery Project Grants \\u0026 the eavesdropping consortium patrons.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/eavesdropping-festival-2026/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"CNI 2.1: Spanners, London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-19T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-20T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"75860a3b49928d345d61410be2d70914.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SELN kicks off DJ Valentimes \\u0026 Truthspeakers UK tour in style - with a Thursday night in Brixton.\\n\\nDJ VALENTIMES\\n\\nDJ Valentimes is the alias of American musician Stefan Cvitanic. As label head of PUPPY he has fore-fronted the reemergence of Industrial hard tekno since 2018. Frequenting the EU \\u0026 US he has performed at Herrensauna Tresor Berlin, Enter Oslo, and Corsica Studios (UK) alongside countless freeparties across the world.\\n\\nValentimes’ own productions channel a razor sharp approach to acid tek and beyond. Imagine the feeling of a bullet train entering your mind and you might have something close to the experience of a Valentimes set. Come and bear witness!\\n\\nTRUTHSPEAKER\\n\\nAs an enigmatic figure in the European underground hard-dance scene, Berlin based German artist Truthspeaker presents a unique vision of bullet paced dance-music, delivering a transcending, occasionally unpredictable, yet consistently intense and immediate listening experience for the dance floor.\\n\\nTestament to his sonic output and artists commitment Truthspeaker has performed worldwide from warehouses in the USA to clubs across the EU. Having previously released with SELN, alongside co run's the label Post Hoc, he will be joining DJ Valentimes for a UK tour.\\n\\nThere is a limited number of free tickets available for those who are unwaged / on UC. Please email info@selnrecordings.com to reserve one.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2340804\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":73,\"name\":\"against the clock: LONDON COMMUNITY LAPTOP ORCHESTRA and BINT MBAREH\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-20T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ff3e6d9ee14b71ee1ee3be016f512187.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Against the Clock is the first of its kind. Here we share stories with no beginning middle or end. Our first AtC is at Vesper's. We love Vesper's. We invite you to watch Bint Mbareh and London Community Laptop Orchestra spiralling in doom-based hypnoses. all welcome \\u003c3\\n\\nTHE LONDON COMMUNITY LAPTOP ORCHESTRA IS A COMMUNITY RUN LAPTOP ORCHESTRA MAKING SOUNDS IN A VARIETY OF UNUSUAL PLACES. THE LCLO HOLDS A COMMUNITY ETHOS WHERE ANYONE CAN PARTICIPATE.\\n\\nINSPIRED BY GROUPS LIKE THE 1969-1974'S SCRATCH ORCHESTRA AND WITH A FOCUS ON GUERRILLA PERFORMANCES, WE BELIEVE IN THE POWER OF THE LAPTOP AS A TOOL FOR LOCALISED COLLECTIVE CREATIVE ENGAGEMENT AND PERFORMANCE.\\n\\nOUR POLITICS ARE EXPLICIT BECAUSE THEY NEED TO BE. SOUND ART SPACES CAN BE ISOLATING, ELITIST, EXCLUSIONARY AND BIGOTED. WE AIM TO BE ACTIVE IN BREAKING THOSE STEREOTYPES.\\n\\nFOUNDED AND (CURRENTLY) RUN BY KAT MACDONALD.\\n\\nBINT mbareh is a sound researcher with a focus on water in palestine. her interest in the physical parallel between the water wave and the sound wave leads her into questions of border dissolutions (between bodies, between states, between tenses), and into the possibility of being enveloped by the voice, by sounding communally similarly to being enveloped by a water body. she challenges settler colonial epistemology by taking seriously palestinian ways of knowing, from rain-summoning music to shrine pilgrimage as an instigator to political revolution.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":78,\"name\":\"fundraiser for migrants' rights networks\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-20T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0861ec0e3c73193d55b690854c368d0c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hoofbeats Pounding presents a night of conversation and performances to raise funds for Migrants' Rights Network. \\n\\nPlease join us on 20th March at Reference Point to raise funds in solidarity with the global anti-raids movement and to investigate: in an era of mass deportations and constant digital surveillance, how might live art, community and conversation disrupt the status quo? \\n\\nArtists:\\nCajm + Caius Williams\\nPoundshop + Xt1ana\\nTheodora Laird (feeo)\\nLagtime Seedling\\nEn Creux\\n+ more tba\\n\\nDiscussion and Q+A by Dr Alexandra Anikina and Elinor Arden.\\n\\nMigrants’ Rights Network is a London-based organisation who work alongside migrants in their fight for rights and justice. MRN partners with individuals and organisations to challenge policy and legislation; build leadership and campaigning capacity in migrant communities; and raise awareness of migrants’ rights.\\n\\nHoofbeats Pounding is a curatorial project exploring tech + surveillance and its effect on our shared humanity. Their book under the same name will be stocked at Reference Point.\\n\\nReserve your ticket with a donation via the Eventbrite!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/fundraiser-for-migrants-rights-network-at-reference-point-tickets-1984559005408\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":54,\"name\":\"flowers.06\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99e507a83bc5fab9609d2b1c1dad30a7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"flowers returns next month for our sixth germination…\\n\\nwe are truly excited to welcome Ifeoluwa and watcha as sonic gardeners for the night. both these creative practitioners are invested in understanding what makes dancefloors move deeply through a commitment to experimentation and an intentionality that we seek to cultivate with each gathering.\\n\\nwe can't wait to share sounds and space together again.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/33499/flowers06\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":28,\"name\":\"Pagan Sex Magick #002: Les Animaux Sauvages\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"90e0bb81ef1eca82ae5558b3eff7016f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"HENGE Live presents Pagan Sex Magick, a series of electronic music nights at Club Cheek in Brixton by Dash The Henge\\n\\nLes Animaux Sauvages (LIVE) Les Animaux Sauvages are three louche artistic soulmates who came together in 2014 as one electro/minimalwave/postpunk entity\\n\\nSibylla Seraphim (actress, singer \\u0026 pianist), Nasso (singer \\u0026 whirlwind frontman) and Charlie (producer, guitarist \\u0026 captain) hail from Sofia, BG, but the euphoric danceability and bipolar mood swings of their music were also partly formed in Paris, London and Berlin\\n\\nMadd Rod (DJ) Madd Rod is a Berlin-based artist forged in long nights and extended sets, where patience, risk, and instinct matter more than trends. Shaped by marathon residencies and years of experimentation, his sound cuts across raw electronics, punk energy, and forward-driven club music with total control\\n\\nC.A.R. (DJ) London residing, Franco-Canadian Chloé Raunet has been immersed in the world of post-punk, cold wave and her own brand of off-kilter synth-pop since the days fronting her band Battant. A fan of the weirder edges of electronic music, as well as composing as C.A.R., she also DJs and hosts the monthly 'On The Slip Road' show on NTS Radio\\n\\n33rd December (DJ) South London producers Matt Priory \\u0026 Miles Davies, working at dusk-tinted tempos with smoked synths and gently obsessive grooves. Their sets lean into slow-motion momentum, hypnotic patterns, bass weight and space, built for heads-down floors that like it woozy and warm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2348828\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":6,\"name\":\"CNI 2.2: Exit, Glasgow\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"30ba0f9ac90400dfd812f1cfbb7faa61.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SELN debuts in Glasgow for its 2026 event series Celebrating New Industrial.\\nThe 2nd stop of DJ Valentimes \\u0026 Truthspeakers UK tour, they are joined by SELN typists Conrad Pack \\u0026 DJ Gonz. DJ Eliot graces the show for full effect.\\n\\nDJ VALENTIMES\\n\\nDJ Valentimes is the alias of American musician Stefan Cvitanic. As label head of PUPPY he has fore-fronted the reemergence of Industrial hard tekno since 2018. Frequenting the EU \\u0026 US he has performed at Herrensauna Tresor Berlin, Enter Oslo, and Corsica Studios (UK) alongside countless freeparties across the world.\\n\\nValentimes’ own productions channel a razor sharp approach to acid tek and beyond. Imagine the feeling of a bullet train entering your mind and you might have something close to the experience of a Valentimes set. Come and bear witness!\\n\\nTRUTHSPEAKER\\n\\nAs an enigmatic figure in the European underground hard-dance scene, Berlin based German artist Truthspeaker presents a unique vision of bullet paced dance-music, delivering a transcending, occasionally unpredictable, yet consistently intense and immediate listening experience for the dance floor.\\n\\nTestament to his sonic output and artists commitment Truthspeaker has performed worldwide from warehouses in the USA to clubs across the EU. Having previously released with SELN, alongside co run's the label Post Hoc, he will be joining DJ Valentimes for a UK tour.\\n\\nCONRAD PACK [live]\\n\\nConrad Pack is one of the most exciting producers operating in London's underground. He runs the SELN Recordings label with DJ Gonz, and his productions there explore the fertile terrain between tuff, rooted soundsystem steppers and high-BPM techno, while his evolving productions for Lost Domain explore a distorted, hard-edged but deep and dub-enriched techno sound with echoes of Obscurum, early Downwards and Axis.\\n\\nDJ GONZ\\n\\nDJ Gonz is a producer, DJ and visual artist hailing from London. He co-runs SELN recordings where his releases perpetuate focused melodic riffs joint with heavy leading percussion. Drawing on influences taken from free-tekno, dub and kuduro, his sound is both pensive, driving whilst still rooted in a soundsystem tradition. Previous output include The Lamentation of Vern, and The Messenger on Wain Records. He has a solo EP on SELN due for release early 2026.\\n\\nDJ ELIOT\\n\\nUnconventional and enthusiastic about many kinds of frequencies, DJ Eliot is guided by curiosity rather than category. Drawing in equal measure from the old, the new, and the timeless. Her sets move fluidly across style and speed, creating spaces where borders blur and intensity unfolds.\\n\\nThere is a limited number of free tickets available for those who are unwaged / on UC. Please email info@selnrecordings.com to reserve one.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2340807\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":61,\"name\":\"depth charge inc. #01\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T22:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ac4d539a81cd2b6f12cf6a5d2b1f93a0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A new exploration series delving into the histories of dubstep and its adjacent sound worlds, with a focus on where ideas around the genre get stretched, fractured, break and fall apart.\\n\\nAn experimental point of departure rather than a sound brief, with an invitation for all participants to leave assumptions at the door.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2381674\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":68,\"name\":\"Kooky Ken 4th Birthday: Carl H \\u0026 Matthias (All Night Long)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"567f39189aa53d36571a24c2bb7ca2e3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Carl H \\u0026 Matthias all night long at Venue MOT.\\n\\nA debut b2b in the UK, seven hours together, open till close.\\n\\nThis will mark the celebration of our fourth year. We will also be bringing a new light installation into the venue.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2351980\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":80,\"name\":\"PLOY \\u0026 FINN\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bd27ea5aabbfaf7de789c7593ffc7c00.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ploy joins Finn under the arch!\\nHouse trax galore, all night long   \\n#HouseNation\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2355559\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":47,\"name\":\"thumbprint ❁ livwutang, Loidis \\u0026 Priori\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-20T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f4a7c72f1dbbf4e7577a46d878d1e2f8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"from across the atlantic,\\nour next chapter emerges.\\n\\nlivwutang\\nLoidis\\nPriori\\n\\nthree distinct minds trace a line through dub, progressive and minimal spheres.\\n\\nsee you where they intersect...\\n\\nw/ not so genius \\u0026 tom thumb\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2355000\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":150,\"name\":\"ChuntFM Presents: call-köl showroom turns 4\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-21T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2879db1495275731d116de610e038965.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"call-köl celebrates 4yrs of the 201 deptford high st showroom with a 8hr live stream straight from the atelier/studio to ChuntFM airwaves tune in or come enjoy in person\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":153,\"name\":\"Living Under Apartheid: Palestinian Stories from the West Bank and the ’48\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-21T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"310bba85c100c796045554abf92615b3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join photographer Denise Laura Baker for a powerful and unfiltered evening documenting Palestinian life under Israeli rule — across the occupied West Bank and within the borders of what Palestinians call the ’48.\\n\\nThrough intimate portraits and first-hand testimonies, Denise’s work explores the layered realities of life under apartheid: from physical violence and military intimidation to the quieter, systemic forms of economic restriction and cultural erasure. Her images move beyond headlines, grounding political realities in human experience — families, workers, children, elders — navigating a system designed to fragment and control.\\n\\nBut this is not only a story of oppression. It is also one of steadfastness, dignity, and resistance. Alongside accounts of hardship, Denise shares stories of everyday hope: community care, cultural preservation, humour, faith, and refusal.\\n\\nThis is a space to listen, to witness, and to engage with lived realities rarely seen in mainstream narratives. The evening will conclude with a Q\\u0026A and open discussion.\\n\\nAn essential event for anyone seeking deeper understanding through the lens of documentary photography.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/palestinehouse/2092943\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":104,\"name\":\"Złom w/ uh, Faebia, MUTE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-22T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ed0732916335b34df0432de386e15065.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"złom (Polish) noun. scrap [noun]; waste articles that are only valuable for the material they contain\\n\\nzłom returns to Spanners once again ♪˞͛◖₍ᐢ. ̫.ᐢ₎◗˞͛♪\\n\\nwith:\\n\\nuh\\nUH is the sibling duo of Dominic and Finn Kennedy, uniting bedroom-burbling hardware jams \\u0026 narrative vignettes. Over time, they’ve honed a cathartic, live, experimental acid-trancelike sonic world, touching on their heritage, pastoral idylls, and staple styles from breakbeat to broken beat to balladry\\n\\nfaebia \\nfaebia’s world-building practice encompasses immersive sound, performance and spatial design. Her world is grounded in flesh, the earth and technology, but is scattered with unreal elements that reveal themselves through glitches and tears in the fabric of ⊹₊⟡ ⋆reality ⋆.˚. It attempts to capture the abstractness of the brain/mind as something physical and finite, but ineffable and transcendent.\\n\\nleisure fm \\npolish twin electronica duo – leisure fm – utilise manipulated field recordings, stretched-out beats and basslines, and distorted, haunting vocals – to create experimental, murky soundscapes to disassociate to… their work explores repetition and rumination, with most tracks composed of loops – weaving a loose narrative about esoteric fables, cycles, and mercurial relationships\\n\\nAidan Hendrickse AKA MUTE\\nAidan Hendrickse is a producer and DJ from Lewisham. Cycling through various forms of hybrid club music, they knit together frictious rhythmic structures for you to dance to\\n\\nomoo \\nResident DJ \\n\\nan experimental sonic scrap yard\\n\\n7 - midnight ˚‧º·( 。ᗒ ‸ ◕✿)\\n\\nnotaflof (email us for a reduced cost ticket - zlom.zlom.3000@gmail.com)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2374119\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":125,\"name\":\"Dirar Kalash Presents: Q(٤)artet\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-21T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2eb079a9f26eb1276bc19004ff3e0527.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Roxanna AlBayati, Seán Being, Dirar Kalash, and Oliver Turvey convene together for the first time as a string quartet.\\n\\nThe evening will unfold across a series of movements. The past is the present and the present is the past. From here we will depart.\\n\\nRoxanna Albayati is an Iranian-Iraqi interdisciplinary artist, researcher and music educator. Driven by embodied artistic research, her transcultural practice centres around combining experimental music with multilingual art forms and audio-visuals, where her music merges cross-cultural improvisation with Persian traditional music and the physicality of performance.\\n\\nSeán Being is an Irish musician working across a range of modes of composition and performance. They work with site-specific solo performance through a variety of means—recently plainchant, feedback, pianos and car horns—thinking through spatial, social and historical bases of music performance.\\n\\nDirar Kalash is a musician and sound artist whose work spans a wide range of musical and sonic practices within a variety of instrumental, compositional and improvisational contexts.\\n\\nOliver Turvey is an artist working across sound and performance. A longtime member of the band Midlight, he also performs with Hilary Woods and Gabriel Ferrandini. `His practice sits at the intersection of site- and subject-specific improvisation and composition.\\n\\nUnwaged tickets available for those on no or low incomes. Please email oliver.turvey@icloud.com if you cannot afford the unwaged ticket price, NOTAFLOF.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/dirar-kalash-presents-qartet-tickets-1985157151479?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":81,\"name\":\"BERMONDSEY ROOTS SESSION\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-21T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-22T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0875442842f7a53c3a13cca62b84d095.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":50,\"name\":\"ToughLuv: Loefah (Jungle Set) / Peshay / RWKUS / Nancy June / Sumgii / NOLI\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-21T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-22T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c46c8cae3492c70066b83372118e88c4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"ToughLuv makes it’s debut edition with Jungle, Breakbeat \\u0026140 session\\n\\nThe dubstep godfather Loefah takes a look backward at the history of Breakbeat \\u0026 Jungle with an OG jungle set.\\n\\nPeshay follows that lineage as one of the true architects of the breakbeat continuum, carrying decades of innovation that helped shape the sound into what it is today.\\n\\nRWKUS off the back of theire Jazz Cafe headline bring things back to the early rave years with a live 91–94 review, reworking hardcore, jungle, and early breakbeat through live instrumentation and improvisation.\\n\\nNancy June, SUMGII, and NOLI represent the next movement forward, starting-off and rounding-off the night through breakbeat, jungle, footwork, halftime \\u0026 140\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/32984/#tribe-tickets__tickets-form\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":7,\"name\":\"CNI 2.3: The Lubberfiend, Newcastle\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-21T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-22T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"af32ffb7d6e91c83242fb38c9ca03746.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SELN arrives in Newcastle for its 2026 event series Celebrating New Industrial.\\nThe final stop of DJ Valentimes \\u0026 Truthspeakers UK tour, they are joined by Newcastle’s techno-de-force Jacklyn.\\n\\nDJ VALENTIMES\\n\\nDJ Valentimes is the alias of American musician Stefan Cvitanic. As label head of PUPPY he has fore-fronted the reemergence of Industrial hard tekno since 2018. Frequenting the EU \\u0026 US he has performed at Herrensauna Tresor Berlin, Enter Oslo, and Corsica Studios (UK) alongside countless freeparties across the world.\\n\\nValentimes’ own productions channel a razor sharp approach to acid tek and beyond. Imagine the feeling of a bullet train entering your mind and you might have something close to the experience of a Valentimes set. Come and bear witness!\\n\\nTRUTHSPEAKER\\n\\nAs an enigmatic figure in the European underground hard-dance scene, Berlin based German artist Truthspeaker presents a unique vision of bullet paced dance-music, delivering a transcending, occasionally unpredictable, yet consistently intense and immediate listening experience for the dance floor.\\n\\nTestament to his sonic output and artists commitment Truthspeaker has performed worldwide from warehouses in the USA to clubs across the EU. Having previously released with SELN, alongside co run's the label Post Hoc, he will be joining DJ Valentimes for a UK tour.\\n\\nJacklyn\\n\\nReigning in on clean oscillation Jacklyn is a DJ and techno producer navigating\\nthrough her collection of puristic techno styles, whether it be fusing atmospheric landscapes together with raw European styles or foreloading synth-loaded Detroit bombs.\\n\\nOften displaying heavy-hitting selections from her record collection, her mixes travel through the depths of techno foundations with reference to 303 acid, alongside the full wrath of the TR-909 (the classic sounds of techno).\\n\\nHaving supported heavyweight artists such as the wizard Jeff Mills, her talents have seen her frequent the EU club circuit including Tresor Berlin, World headquarters and Rote Sonne. Her self-released productions explore driving percussion across mesmeric spoken samples and atmospheres.\\n\\nThere is a limited number of free tickets available for those who are unwaged / on UC. Please email info@selnrecordings.com to reserve one.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2340810\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":152,\"name\":\"Antiuniversity anticonference\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-22T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-22T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"26fa2ab344a42fcd0d4076fa2a0ad3e6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hi!\\nＡｎｔｉｕｎｉｖｅｒｓｉｔｙ　Ａｎｔｉｃｏｎｆｅｒｅｎｃｅ　２２ｎｄ　Ｍａｒｃｈ　２０２６ 10am-5pm\\n１　Ｄａｙ　\\u003e\\u003e　１　Ｖｅｎｕｅ\\nAM and PM timetable created at breakfast and lunch by participants 30 minute slots with up 3 spaces available at the same time for each ‘event’.\\n\\n*If you’re interested in facilitating and have any questions get in touch! (Ig @antiuniversitynow / antiuniversity@gmail.com)\\nPrevious iterations of the week long festival can be found at www.antiuniversity.org and examples on our instagram\\nＤｏｎ’ｔ░ａｓｋ░ｆｏｒ░ｐｅｒｍｉｓｓｉｏｎ！\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":62,\"name\":\"free movements : Equinox\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-22T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-23T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"014b3cdaa0c494dfe75198ace450634d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"big big honours to host these incredible artists:\\n\\nDhangsha (live)\\nUpsammy (dj) \\nZoë Mc Pherson (hybrid) \\nSeb Rochford (drums) \\nEdward George (dj)\\nDan Nicholls (keyboards) \\n+ more\\n+ veg/vegan Indian street food by Hari\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/freemovements/2026079\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":35,\"name\":\"Deptford Dub Club feat. the legendary rocksteady teacher Duke Neville\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-22T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-22T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b65b1546cfa1ef59203a9dc085623b48.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We are pleased and proud to welcome Duke Neville back to the D.D.C.. The legendary Duke is known as “The Rocksteady Teacher”. The mighty Neville started out selecting on the General Soundsystem in the 70s. He selects to entertain and is also an entertaining raconteur on the mic.. Duke Neville remains a very well respected figure on the London Reggae Revive circuit and has wowed big events, such as the London Ska Festival. Neville’s record auctions at Peckings Shop are the stuff of legend and speak to the depth of his personal collection of rare tunes. He also ran his own vinyl imprint “Neville Sounds”. \\n\\nThroughout proceedings our resident Sing-jay, the mighty Doc Murdoc will be on hand to nice-up the dance. The inimitable Doctor will need no introduction to many, as he is a pillar of the London Reggae scene. He, and the club’s resident selector, Soft Wax, recently supported Black Uhuru and together they’ve grace many of the capital’s stages and far beyond. For this night they will be joined by the D.D.C.s recently amended live horn section including Club favourite Michael. We may well see some special guests too.\\n\\nThe evening will also include a selection from Duppy Sista Sound. We’re delighted to welcome the vibrant Jaz back to select for us, she is a stalwart of the Club; more broadly, she’s a well-established figure on the London Reggae scene. \\n\\nWe’re looking forward to another blinding evening of live mixes from the great Prince Fatty on the desk. An enhanced sound system is a feature of this popular night, held in a convivial boozer. We expect this session to be one of our most memorable. The palatial, discrete garden will have the evening sets piped out to it. It has developed into a firm favourite chill out zone for Club regulars. Put on your dancing shoes.\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/deptford-dub-club-22nd-march-2026/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":117,\"name\":\"Brixton Community Cinema : The Black and the Green \\u0026 The Ban\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-23T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4c300460fa2a63a52ae1dc5702411e0f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In the wake of St Patrick’s Day, our next screening is a double bill of documentaries exploring the Troubles, a protracted and bloody chapter in the longer anti-colonial fight for self-determination in Ireland, and how it maps onto other struggles across time and space. \\n\\n\\nIn The Black and the Green (1983), activist, documentarian and prolific chronicler of Black American life St. Clair Bourne accompanies five African American civil rights activists on a journey to Belfast, where they engage in a reflective exchange of organising strategies with Northern Irish Catholics involved in their own struggle for liberation from British rule. Through debate and immersion, they explore both the dissonances and resonances between the systems of oppression they confront, lingering on the fraught question of whether violence is necessary in the pursuit of radical change.\\n\\n\\nCollaging together revelatory archival material, Roisin Agnew’s The Ban (2024) examines the media censorship Margaret Thatcher imposed on the Irish Republican Army and its political wing Sinn Féin between 1988 and 1994. The film traces the incredulous dubbing techniques used to varying effect to circumvent the ban, while foregrounding the stakes of the tireless organising and conflict that continued to unfold. Though historically specific, the documentary draws parallels with the British government’s contemporary invocation of the threat of terrorism to justify restrictions on free speech and the right to protest.\\n\\n\\nFollowing the screening, filmmaker Roisin Agnew will be joined by author and academic Emma Dabiri, for a conversation with film curator and writer, Rógan Graham.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://bccspring26.eventive.org/schedule/69b837b2532dbf982414ccb6\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":122,\"name\":\"Sister Midnight: Skill-Sharing Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-23T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"15348f8165c087e2a669421ded02ab8a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Want to start a community, culture or co-op project in Lewisham?\\n\\nJoin us on Monday 23rd March at The Catford House for a skills sharing workshop!\\n\\nLearn more about legal structures for not-for-profits / Fundraising \\u0026 grants / Working with Lewisham Council.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYc4sqKC117V79cOP7zWmvDFrcXGqbji-fRaY3spydX6y4Qw/viewform\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":36,\"name\":\"Sense Ability with Zongamin and friends\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-23T19:15:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-23T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fd6afad80eb629916392571131e003f5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An improvisatory music session by local musicians and artists, curated by London based musician Susumu Mukai aka Zongamin. Abstract communications echoing the vibration, noise and reverberation of The Crypt Gallery, London.\\n\\nThe collaborators for this session are secret for now, expect a surprise 🙂\\n\\nZongamin is a composer, producer, and illustrator based in London. He has released records on Flesh Records, XL recordings, Ed Banger, Multi Culti, ESP Institute, and AD93, and has remixed for Air, John Cale, Trevor Jackson, Sandro Perri, and others.\\n\\nHis artworks have been exhibited around the world, and he has published art books with Nieves and Pam Books.\\n\\nHe has also provided designs for clothing labels PAM, Silas, Undercover, VIVA Strange Boutique, and record covers for George Issakidis, Amkarahoi, and Al Wootton.\\n\\nHe is a member of groups Vanishing Twin,\\nV/Z, Holy Tongue, Becker \\u0026 Mukai, and Stalactite.\\n\\nAll funds we receive go directly towards creating and maintaining opportunities for our collaborators - supporting their work, amplifying their voice, and building a platform that reflects what we stand for.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/senseability/2041743\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":86,\"name\":\"Corringham + Shiell, Pentu + Ward, Ansuman Biswas\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4bf093bbf3e6a9e2b641925f9b4805de.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Viv Corringham is a British vocalist and sound artist working with voice, electronics and field recordings. She has been described as “a vital force in improvised music since the late 1970s”. Her practice explores relations between voice, place and walking, responding with sung improvisations to natural and urban soundscapes.\\n\\nStephen Shiell is a London-based sound artist, improviser, composer and field recordist working across music, radiophonic art and site-responsive practice. His recorded works, live performances, sound walks, and workshops explore listening, gathering and performing.\\n\\nPentu is a London based producer, sound designer and guitarist, exploring experimental and ambient soundscapes, focusing on sounds that mirror the splintered reality of living in an online world.\\n\\n‘Feels like slipping into a delirious state of digital fatigue’ -- AQNB\\n\\nJoanna Ward is a London-based composer and performer. Her based practice revolves around experimental score-making methodologies, and exploring what happens when improvisation is situated alongside simple, repetitious musical ideas. She likes to work with other artists on projects which layer live sound with recorded sound, video, and other media.\\n\\nAnsuman Biswas has an interdisciplinary practice encompassing music, film, live art, installation, writing and theatre. He has worked as a composer and musician in a wide range of contexts from jazz to Indian Classical music, pop songs, to industrial noise.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/bb87ev-corringham-shiell-pentu-ward-ansuman-biswas-24th-mar-the-horse-hospital-london-tickets?lng=en\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":71,\"name\":\"Analogue Animation Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-24T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"410c7b42cc3cb6b72605393f2f8c1c75.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Miranda Peyton Jones leads an analogue animation workshop at SET Social.\\n\\nThis hands-on workshop offers an introduction to analogue and handmade animation techniques.\\n\\nLed by artist and animator, Miranda Peyton Jones, the workshop is designed as an open, supportive space to try new ideas, learn practical techniques, and meet others interested in experimental animation.Participants can expect to leave with a short piece of moving image, along with printed materials created during the session.\\n\\nNo previous animation or drawing experience is required. All materials are provided, and participants are welcome to bring their own materials if they wish.\\n\\nPlease note that you’ll need a smartphone with the free Stop Motion Studio app downloaded before attending.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/analogue-animation-workshop-tickets-1983086859179?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":56,\"name\":\"Lee Scratch Perry 'Black Ark' – Book Launch \",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-24T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bd4803e1bf888c6251e24e856fe48a92.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"OTO hosts the launch of Black Ark, presented with Edition Patrick Frey, centred on Lee Scratch Perry’s Black Ark Studios in Kingston, Jamaica. The evening features a panel conversation, a visual presentation, a curated listening session with commentary led by Perry biographer David Katz, plus sonic responses to Black Ark from invited contributors.\\n\\nThe 600-page book takes as its point of departure a visual inventory made in spring 2021 at the Black Ark in Kingston, Jamaica—where Perry produced his music from 1973 onwards. It documents the studio as both recording site and continuously evolving visual environment: mural paintings and drawings, and shape-shifting assemblages of records, instruments, often obsolete recording equipment and media devices, found objects, and collages including posters, newspaper and magazine clippings, and appropriated books—layers upon layers, rhizomatically entangled with the building, its furniture, and Perry’s life and persona. The premises have since been sold, and the book stands as a record of a world on the verge of disappearing.\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\nPublished by Edition Patrick Frey, Black Ark was conceived with Lee Scratch Perry (1936–2021) in its early stages. The book was designed by Maximage (David Keshavjee). Photographic documentation is by Marc Asekhame.\\n\\nThe evening will begin with a panel discussion featuring Martine Rose, Marc Asekhame, David Katz, and Chris Peckings, moderated by Canan Batur. Following the panel, Katz will guide a listening session that traces the book’s visual archive to music. This session will showcase significant Black Ark productions, elusive original vinyl from Lee Scratch Perry, and various archival materials. Highsteppers and Canan Batur will then present a sonic response to round out the night.\\n\\nExclusive copies of Black Ark will be available in the OTO bookshop\\n\\nOrganised by C-Studios and No Tax.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/lee-scratch-perry-black-ark-book-launch/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":110,\"name\":\"The Radical Library: Launch event\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-25T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-25T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"750d8809d2fbbb43ad5c8f375b0ca5ca.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us on Wednesday 25th March for the launch of the Radical Library!\\n\\nOpen 12 - 4pm, and then on a biweekly basis.\\n\\nBrowse a range of books available to borrow - whether you want to read something in the space or take a book home with you.\\n\\nThere will be comfy sofas to lounge on, and hot drinks and pies available to purchase!\\n\\nThe hope is for the library to grow through donations and the people who use it, so come in n chat with us about what you want to see on the shelves💛:)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":84,\"name\":\"all my thoughts with Yetsuby, Seb Wildblood, Blossom Hill\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7870cbece22a4c3a2d0951d6ad6bbd8f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"all my thoughts label night @ M.O.T\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2362611\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":75,\"name\":\"AMBIVERT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-25T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ccaaddc26662e369e289319104056ed5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Come to our debut evening of ambient atmosphere in the overwhelming city of London, where a night like this might just be what you need. Expect live performances, experimentations and DJs, surrounded by soft seating and a hazy aura to match.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2376853\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":168,\"name\":\"Lug Hole 007: Libretto of Lion \\u0026 Lamb\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-25T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-25T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"af324bc4a7672165dbe16975e33c7c16.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lug Hole is a zine launch (written by Frank Wasser!) alongside a DIY live performance art \\u0026 music event!\\n\\nThe Libretto of Lamb \\u0026 Lion sees us return to The Piehouse to welcome in the Spring Bleet!-style with our customary array of artistic talents, all united by their intrepid exploration of words, sounds and the inbetween.\\n\\nIt wouldn’t be a Lug Hole without a brand new Bleet! zine! (!) We are beyond thrilled to be presenting our ninth edition by the Irish artist and writer Frank Wasser! Frank’s work snags, stutters and interrupts... Be prepared to reassess how you read!\\n\\n@bleet_zine\\n\\n@nadeemdingabisi\\n@tobyevansjesra\\n@hannah_m_clarkson\\n@frankwasserartist\\n@theodunne.art\\n\\nFree tickets for Personal Assistants or Essential Companions - just email us at email: bleetzine@gmail.com to let us know!' \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/33595/lug-hole-007-the-libretto-of-lamb-lion\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":53,\"name\":\"Public preview: Noorani Metal Sound – Zahra Malkani and Syma Tariq\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-26T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-26T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"898859b2da026fd4c0d8f655e65fa948.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Auto Italia presents Noorani Metal Sound, the first major UK solo exhibition by Pakistani interdisciplinary artist and researcher Zahra Malkani. Featuring new sound work, sculpture, installation, and moving image, the exhibition draws on mysticism, ecological resistance movements and feminist aural practices to explore the intersections of the sonic and the sacred across Pakistan’s heavily exploited coastal and delta regions. Emerging from over five years of ongoing research, Noorani Metal Sound brings together Malkani’s field recordings and archival work tracing oral and sonic traditions of lament, devotion and resistance.\\n\\nSet against the ravaged aquatic landscape of Pakistan, Noorani Metal Sound unfolds through interwoven motifs of water and metal, rust, circling themes of revolt and remembrance. The recurring use of metal and rust gestures toward the materialities of infrastructural ruin and violence in the region, amidst which this body of work emerged. In both sound and form, metal also resonates with the rhythms and sonic intensities of ritual lament, as well as the hard-edged devotional spirit of South Asian shrines as sites of death, refuge and sacrifice.\\n\\nNew sound works weave together lullabies, war cries, stories of martyrdom and protest songs with devotional laments that reverberate across temporal and geographic thresholds – from the Battle of Karbala at the Euphrates River some 1,400 years ago, to the ongoing Baloch insurgency along Pakistan’s Makran Coast. The exhibition opens with Noorani Echo Sound, a three-part cassette box set documenting the artist’s expansive audio archive, collected between 2020 and 2025, alongside a publication of fieldnotes, conversations and translations.\\n\\nIn the back gallery, an audio-visual installation brings together sound, sculpture, and newly commissioned moving image work. The film presents footage of ceremonial footwork, a reference to Sur Purab, a Sindhi folk song about a woman who, entranced, is inexplicably drawn to walk along a mysterious path. An accompanying two-channel soundscape draws sounds of ritual ceremonial mourning into relation: songs, cries and laments that echo unspeakable massacres and brutalities. Woven together with recordings from Karachi’s oldest aquatic neighborhoods, the work is structured around sounds of joyous praise for the martyred and the missing.\\n\\nSitting in deliberate opposition to the secular conventions of the gallery, the exhibition takes the form of a sacralised environment or shrine. In doing so, it destabilises the colonial and touristic imagination through which such sites in Pakistan have often been rendered as quaint, colourful or merely festive. Here, the shrine emerges instead as a charged political and emotionally weighty space: a site of collective mourning and refuge, of death and entrancement, agitation and lament.\\n\\nThe exhibition will be accompanied by an expanded public programme of events curated by researcher, producer and Malkani’s long time collaborator, Dr Syma Tariq. Further details to be announced.\\n\\nNoorani Metal Sounds is curated by Milda Batakyte in collaboration with Mariam Elnozahy. The exhibition was realised with the generous support of Arts Council England and Cockayne Grants for the Arts.\\n\\nZahra Malkani is a multidisciplinary artist from Karachi, Pakistan. Collaboration, research, and pedagogy are at the heart of her practice. Working across multiple media she explores the politics of development and dispossession through the lens of dissident ecological knowledges and traditions of environmental resistance. She is a co-founder with Shahana Rajani of Karachi LaJamia: experimental and ecstatic ecopedagogies in collaboration with ongoing movements in defense of land and water in the city.\\n\\nZahra’s work has been supported by institutions such as the Sharjah Art Foundation, the Graham Foundation for Advanced Studies in the Fine Arts and the Rockbund Arts Museum. She has been awarded residencies at Academie Schloss Solitude, the Jan Van Eyck Academie, La Becque and the Rijksmuseum. Her work has circulated internationally, more recently in spaces such as KonsthallC (Stockholm), Nottingham Contemporary (UK), the V\\u0026A Museum (UK) and Colomboscope (Sri Lanka). She has published writings in journals like Perspecta: The Yale Architectural Journal, the Journal of Architectural Education and online publications such as Against Catastrophe and Decolonial Hacker. Zahra was nominated for the Jameel Art Prize from the V\\u0026A Museum and Jameel Arts Foundation (2023), and is a recipient of the Asia Arts Gamechanger Award (2024).\\n\\nDr Syma Tariq is a practice-based researcher, sound practitioner and writer based in London, UK. Drawing on feminist practices and theory, colonial a/temporality and audio archiving experiments, she is interested in the relationship listening has to time, violence and extractive and differentiating knowledge systems. Her pedagogical work encompasses teaching, workshops, and talks in public, artistic and academic settings.\\n\\nSyma’s artistic commissions include The Silent Ones (National Museum of Fine Arts Taiwan, forthcoming), Delay Lines (Tower Hamlets Local Library and Archives, 2023), and A Thousand Channels (Colomboscope festival, 2021–24). Partitioned Listening has been presented in The Contemporary Journal, World Records journal, BL79 Tunis gallery and the anthologies Pakistan Desires: Queer Futures Elsewhere (Duke University Press, 2023) and Bodies of Sound: Becoming a Feminist Ear (Silver Press, 2024). She has recently co-written her first piece for theatre Unheard: a live radio play, commissioned by Justice Project Pakistan and performed at the National Council of Arts, Islamabad in 2025.\\n\\nPublic preview: 26 March 6pm-8pm\\nExhibition runs: 27 March 2026 — 21 June 2026\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":178,\"name\":\"Camera As Gun: Anti-Colonial Film Units As Counter-Archives\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-26T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-26T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a8673b28e35ea7f7afebb351a3662a03.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An informal evening of film screenings, readings, and discussions on the power of African cinema in service of political cause.\\n\\nSession 1: Africa\\n\\nJoin us for informal evening of film screenings, discussions, readings, on the theme of Anti-Colonial Film Units, exploring their history and relevance to the Colonial Present that we continue to live in today.\\n\\nWe are excited to announce our film residency series titled Camera As Gun: Anti-Colonial Film Units As Counter-Archives hosted in Pelican House, a social centre in east London for worker organising, movement building, experimental arts \\u0026 culture.\\n\\nAnti-Colonial Film Units, shaped by the spirit of Third Cinema, emerged across the South as response to Colonial Film Units and as vital practices of counter-archives, seizing and subverting the colonial lens into mediums of political weapon, in service of liberation and revolution.\\n\\nHeld on the last Thursday evening of every month, we will be focusing on Anti-Colonial Film Units from geography to geography month by month. In our March session, we begin with the continent of Africa, followed by Latin America in April, and concluding with the continent of Asia in May.\\n\\nSession 1: Africa - Thursday 26 March 2026\\nSession 2: Latin America - Thursday 30 April 2026\\nSession 3: Asia - Thursday 28 May 2026\\n\\nThawra Archive is 100% unfunded and volunteer-run. Please consider making a solidarity ticket or donation if you are able to. If you are unable to afford a general admission ticket, please email thawrarchive@gmail.com or message on Instagram.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/camera-as-gun-anti-colonial-film-units-as-counter-archives-tickets-1985379997016\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":188,\"name\":\"Bludud + Special Guests\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-26T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-26T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"82230bd50e741b4d1697ff8678ba47d9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Witty experimental rockers Bludud play their first gig in London at the legendary Ivy House. For fans of Slint, caroline, Blake Mills, Radiohead, Eiafuawn.\\n\\nSupport from Avalon Cafe Choir and Olive Wreath.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2343570\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":37,\"name\":\"Church of Sound: Kahil El'Zabar And The New Ethnic Heritage Ensemble\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"af8204aae8f0359e3ee5423c6ca315fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"~~~ Friday sold out to mailing list - Thursday show added ~~~\\n\\nCome \\u0026 witness one of the great creatives performing at the peak of his powers. We have so much to thank Kahil for. In many ways, he is the quintessential Church of Sound performer. This appearance represents his sixth collaboration with us, and that is a fact that makes us incredibly proud. Anyone who has seen the man \\u0026 his band perform knows this truth - the music \\u0026 the spirit of a Kahil show has the capacity touch you immeasurably and to change your life for the better. If you let it.\\n\\nKahil El'Zabar – mbira, drumset, vox\\n\\nCorey Wilkes – trumpet\\n\\nAlex Harding – saxophone\\n\\nIshmael Ali – cello\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/ww6w8v-kahil-elzabar-the-new-ethnic-heritage-ensemble-26th-mar-st-james-the-great-church-of-sound-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":189,\"name\":\"Odda: Pume Orenge (live), Thea HD (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-26T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-26T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"34a24986e738fe1522faa692cd695b9f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pume Orenge's first live appearance, celebrating the release of their debut album Angel By Milo. Released on 27 March.\\n\\n\\\"It is a world that opens draped in ferric hiss. A fog of sound, dense and yet not quite there, catching the light in strange shades and ambient drifts. Looping and receding, looping and receding, as pucks of static burst like faraway fireworks on a cold winter’s night. Sound sources obscured, ambiguous, not quite what they seem.\\\"\\n\\nWith support from Thea HD.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2374283\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":191,\"name\":\"pwrSystm\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-26T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-27T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"18a06576111111081e158dd622348c0d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"pwrSystm is a collective based between London and Tokyo.\\nOur work is rooted in the themes of “liberation from systems” and experimentation.\\n\\nOn the night, we will present an electronic music journey centered around techno, incorporating a wide range of sonic elements. The set will begin with spatial, experimental sounds, gradually building in intensity as time progresses. In the later hours, more rave-oriented, danceable tracks will emerge, shaping a floor that moves beyond fixed genres and existing scene conventions.\\n\\nThe venue will also feature an interior design reflecting our worldview, creating an immersive environment for the night.\\n\\nTo learn more about the event and our activities, feel free to visit our Instagram (@pwrsystm_) or website (pwrsystm.com).\\n\\n\\n\\npwrSystmは、ロンドンと東京を拠点に活動するコレクティブです。\\n私たちは「システムからの解放」と「実験性」をテーマに活動しています。\\n\\n当日は、テクノを軸に様々な要素を取り入れたエレクトロニックミュージックを展開します。序盤は空間的で実験的なサウンドから始まり、時間が進むにつれて徐々にエネルギーが高まっていく流れを想定しています。後半にはレイヴ感のあるダンサブルなトラックも交えながら、ジャンルや既存のシーンの文脈にとらわれないフロアを目指します。\\n\\n当日は、私たちの世界観を反映した内装デザインにも要注目。イベントや私たちについてもっと知りたい方は、@pwrsystm_ (インスタグラム)や pwrsystm.com (ウェブサイト)を訪れていただけたら嬉しいです。\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2391735\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":129,\"name\":\"Dublife Edition 45: Roots Youths Sound System \\u0026 Vedic Roots Sound System\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-27T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-27T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99638c5df8def651554902ab62ca5614.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A very special heritage sound system night with Vedic Roots meets Roots Youths \\u0026 Rootsrev Sound System, featuring Ras Kayleb. \\n\\nFree parking, and ital food and vinyl stalls. Spread the word and link!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/dublife-edition-45-roots-youths-sound-system-vedic-roots-sound-system-tickets-1984179150251\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":195,\"name\":\"SONIDERA: La Unión es la Cumbia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-27T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-27T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fdae76bad1e7f39f7afb23342831adce.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SONIDERA is a social event that platforms music from the Global South,  articulating sonic discourse through carefully selected playlists and a safe environment for dancing and collective enjoyment.\\n\\nThe Horse Hospital opens its doors with a geographically rich playlist curated by record collector Tapacampeon all the way from Bolivia, focusing on cumbia as a unifying force of Latinamerican legacy\\n\\n4 hours of specially selected hits, including old cumbias found only on vinyl, cumbias colombianas,  cumbia mexicana poblana [distinct for its use of synths], as well as cumbia chicha from the Andes and the Amazon\\n\\nFREE ENTRY 6pm-10pm\\n\\nJuan Manuel Tapia aka Tapacampeon is a Bolivian DJ, vinyl collector and anthropologist whose work explores music as a form of cultural memory and identity. His selections are informed by ongoing archival research - especially on Bolivian music - and by a broad interest in sound from different parts of the world. He shares parts of his archive online and approaches contemporary and older recordings with the same curiosity.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":154,\"name\":\"Exhibition: Forget Me Not\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-27T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-27T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1bea9227f5783686c3c680a9090462e2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This exhibition brings together photography, film, and personal storytelling to reflect on South Lebanon - its land, its people, and the threads that continue to bind them across borders and generations.\\n\\nThrough a collection of photographs, the exhibition traces the layered history of the region: villages shaped by resilience, landscapes marked by occupation, and communities that have endured cycles of displacement while holding tightly to memory and identity. The images move between past and present; documenting everyday life, fragments of history, and the quiet persistence of culture.\\n\\nAlongside the photography, a short film explores the experience of the Lebanese diaspora and the journeys that have carried families far from their homeland. Centered on intergenerational migration, the film asks how culture survives distance: how language, food, music, stories, and traditions are passed from grandparents to parents to children who may have never walked the same soil. It is a reflection on inheritance; not of land, but of belonging.\\n\\nTogether, the exhibition and film consider what it means to remain rooted when geography changes. They explore the ways memory travels, how identity is shaped across generations, and how communities continue to keep their connection to South Lebanon alive, through storytelling, ritual, and the determination not to forget.\\n\\nThis is not only an exhibition about place. It is about continuity, about diaspora, and about the enduring relationship between people and the land they come from - even when they are far away from it.\\n\\nProceeds will be split between initiatives in Saida and Houla for displaced residents.\\n\\nOpening night: Friday 27th March 7pm-10pm\\nExhibition continues Saturday 28th March – Friday 3rd April, open daily 11am-8pm.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/palestinehouse/2123477\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":196,\"name\":\"Trio Explorations with Sheldon Agwu, Max Luthert and Dave Storey\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-27T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-28T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"71194b63ee8c381f24a460111d4d9d7a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Monthly Friday night jazz residency continues at SJQ.\\n\\nSheldon Agwu - Electric Guitar \\u0026 Effects\\nMax Luthert - Upright Bass \\u0026 Modular Synth\\nDave Storey - Drums\\n\\nDoors 8pm\\nMusic from 8.30pm\\nFree Entry\\n\\nDJ Set - Jack Foster 10.30pm - 2am\\n\\nSupported by Arts Council England\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":16,\"name\":\"Palestinian sound archive Invites Herb Diamanté\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-27T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-28T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c9ff6ebd8b1bd0cd5e63832d87dd444f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Palestinian sound archive Invites Herb Diamanté in the first of this year’s Local Angels archive sessions.\\n\\nPalestinian sound archive / Majazz project is the first Palestinian independent London-based research and re-issue music label. For the last 7 years Palestinan Sound Archive has brought to life 11 Palestinian albums, telling the stories of each album and bringing back forgotten memories and sounds from Palestine.\\n\\nThis year, Palestinian Sound Archive will be collaborating in a series of live events and performances with local musicians under the title Local Angels Archive, inviting homegrown bands and DJs to join their club nights, spinning rare sounds from 1970s and 1980s.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":119,\"name\":\"Doc 'N Roll: Rave Culture: A New Era + Q\\u0026A\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-27T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"50f7033f89478ede4229ff1d0f18bcfe.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"When Society Collapsed, Music Took Over.\\n \\nLate 80s. In an England suffocated by unemployment and Margaret Thatcher’s policies, a generation found refuge and a voice in music. In abandoned factories and secret fields, underground raves were born—explosions of light and sound where thousands of young people escaped social oppression to the rhythm of a new musical genre: breakbeat. \\n\\nFusing the raw intensity of Detroit techno, the warmth of Chicago house, and the energy of New York hip hop, breakbeat shattered all the rules. Syncopated rhythms, powerful bass lines, and limitless production fuelled by samplers and synthesisers gave birth to a sound that was not just danced to—it was an act of rebellion. \\n\\nRAVE CULTURE–A NEW ERA is an electrifying journey into the heart of the rave revolution, from the first illegal beats in England to its global explosion. Through never-before-seen archival footage, interviews with the most underground pioneers, and a soundtrack that still resonates today, this documentary unveils the story of a movement that transformed music, culture, and the very essence of nightlife.\\n\\nFollowed by a live Q\\u0026A with the filmmakers\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://riocinema.org.uk/Rio.dll/WhatsOn?f=1967545\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":190,\"name\":\"Studio Crumb 043: Haseeb Iqbal - All Night Long\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-27T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-28T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"92a431b523cf8059858940df63f02528.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Haseeb Iqbal All Night Long.\\nEclectic selections.\\nFresh with a bag of new wax from NYC.\\nStrictly vinyl.\\nBar - cash only.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2393529\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":187,\"name\":\"Hutte in the City - London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-28T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"18490c9fa374e56b99a2742661b6eb62.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"After a successful event in Berlin, Hutte in the city returns to London for a day event at Algha’s Plantroom, transforming the venue into an intimate, immersive space.\\n\\nRooted in connection and inclusivity, Hutte invites artists shaping underground scenes across the European Landscape. Expect a dance-driven journey curated to seamlessly flow from start to finish.\\n\\nOn Saturday 28th March, we bring the spirit of the forest to London’s iconic venue for a truly immersive experience. Step into a fairy-tale wonderland where melodies and playful grooves flutter and flow into deeper, darker marshes as earthy rhythms ground you to the dance floor. Join us for an unforgettable moment of magic.\\n\\nMore than a party, this is a gathering for those who seek intimacy, respect, and collective energy on the dancefloor.\\n\\nMusic: Techno / Progressive / Trance\\nVibe: Psychedelic • Intimate • Inclusive\\nDecor \\u0026 visuals: Forest-inspired transformation\\nCommunity: Safe space, conscious crowd\\n\\nAlgha’s Plantroom, Plantroom, Hackney, E3 2NR, London\\n28.03.2026\\nTime: 12:00–23:00\\n\\nCome early. Stay present. Dance together.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2381776\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":197,\"name\":\"If LOVE had Senses…\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-28T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-28T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"067d2eb66d8b8272e57425e9979d3d6f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We are delighted to invite you to If LOVE had Senses…, a day of embodied encounters consisting of a workshop, interactive soundscape performance, and participatory screening. Responding to Victoria Cantons’ autobiographical ruminations on selfhood and expressions of emotion through language, this public programme moves from the tactile to the sonic to the somatic. The day invites participants to rediscover personal narrative not as exposure, but as connection. \\n\\nAcross three acts, we ask: what if LOVE could touch? What if it could speak? What if it could move?\\n\\nThis is a celebration of the self, others, and things, a space for collective engagement across cultural differences, grounded in shared experience. It’s also an opportunity to experience Cantons’ exhibition ‘A Formula for How to Find Love’ through sensory exchange.\\n\\n13:00 – 15:45\\nAct I: If LOVE Could Touch\\n‘Automatic Poetry’ Workshop with Gem Bryant \\n\\n16:30 – 17:15\\nAct II: If LOVE Could Speak\\nInteractive Soundscape Performance with Anju M. Kasturiraj and F. Dobrota \\n\\n17:15 – 18:00\\nAct III: If LOVE Could Move\\nParticipatory Screening with Rhiana Bonterre \\n\\nThis event is free and open to all, however advanced booking is required for the workshop and recommended for the evening events.\\n\\nIf LOVE had Senses… is curated by Nishi Chodimella, Norah Tsai, Reaia Parkes in partnership with Mimosa House and Goldsmiths MFA Curating for the exhibition A Formula for How to Find Love by artist Victoria Cantons.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.mimosahouse.co.uk/upcoming-events\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":113,\"name\":\"M.O.B at REinsTATE Project\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-28T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f29ba88ab4bd12776b4081684df3b7e9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"M.O.B is back Saturday 28th of March for the next iteration of our multi-disciplinary arts events, celebrating creativity in its various forms.\\n\\nOur curation for this event focuses on the body, its movement(s), its response to (new) spaces. On the programme is:\\n\\n- Beatrice M. B2b Soa420 (DJ set)\\n\\n- FYI Robyn (Bodily workshop)\\n\\n- Neurotica Exotica (live) \\n\\n- Claudia Palazzo (Dance)\\n\\n- 27 Eggs (M.O.B residents live performance)\\n\\n+ Visuals by Max Burstyn\\n\\n+ Art/Lighting installation by Baos\\n\\n+ Food by Spring Garden London\\n\\nWe are hosting this gathering at the REinsTate for the first time - a recently refurbished, previously abandoned social club with deep roots in its local community. Central to M.O.B’s ethos is the importance of repurposing/reimagining disused space, creating platforms for creativity and community action from empty/under-utilised space. We are therefore super grateful to the great people at REinsTATE for kindly hosting us for what promises to be another mind (and body) bender.\\n\\nMain Event REinsTate from 3pm to 11pm\\n\\nAfters from Midnight to 7-8AM + ... HW Location, TBC on the day, you know the drill. Not to be missed.\\n\\nPoster by our amazing friend Domenico Gatto\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/mob/2108489\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":25,\"name\":\"Impulse Control: L.F.T., Timothy J. Fairplay, d.phylleia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-28T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-29T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"81cc4ec538989bd9deb91d9b5a922de6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"L.F.T. (live)\\n\\nBerlin-based DJ, producer, and live act who is rapidly carving out a place in contemporary electronic music. His sound blends new wave and breakbeat-influenced electro, shaped by the distorted drum machines of The Hague and the romantic synth melodies of 1980s San Francisco.\\n\\nTIMOTHY J. FAIRPLAY (live)\\n\\nA long-standing figure in UK underground electronic music, DJing and producing since the 1990s. Blending Detroit techno, minimal wave, Italo, Chicago house, and electro, his sound is hypnotic, synth-driven, and steeped in dystopian atmosphere.\\n\\nHARROWED (live)\\n\\nCrushing Metallic Hardcore fusing the intensity of bands like Integrity and Ringworm with the riffs of 90s Swedish Death metal.\\n\\nMONIKA BADLY (live)\\n\\nBristol’s dealer of industrial pain jazz noise techno. The Avon Terror Corps and Chewing Glass Collective member has spent the last few years refining their sound. In 2025, they released their sophomore full-length album Love Songs on Eggy Tapes.\\n\\nDIE VERLETZT (live)\\n\\nLondon based electronic post punk duo influenced by 80s new wave, 70s punk and Berlin electronica. They set about making music that both makes you want to dance hard and cry harder.\\n\\nD.PHYLLEIA (dj)\\n\\nBeing inspired by all things gritty, distorted, and bass-driven, she draws from the legacy of UK and Detroit’s electro and techno innovators, crafting a raw, industrial sound with a punkish drawl.\\n\\nGERST (live)\\n\\nLondon based noise / sound artist.\\n\\nNEW FLESH + IAMA\\n\\nResident DJs.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2357042\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":179,\"name\":\"Ill-3AB Presents: Arab Timing Vol.7\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-28T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-29T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bc5c59a93fe0ac4bedaf278befb612a2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"POP UP PARTY !! 28th of March 2026 The Orange Room 9pm-3am for the release of our second edition print only Magazine:\\n\\nRoom 1 Vendors: 🤝🏼 🎪\\n\\n@mehdi__studio\\n@fear2fuckup\\n@rimah.co\\n@love.hurts\\n@on_tick_\\n@angelswearnada\\n\\nRoom 2 Music:🕺🏼💃🏼\\n\\n@lanabaybie\\n@therealloai\\n@nora.abbs\\n@intibint\\n\\n+ SPECIAL GUEST 👽\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/l85anw-ill-3ab-presents-arab-timing-vol7-28th-mar-the-orange-room-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":26,\"name\":\"[CANCELLED] Fast \\u0026 Bi-Furious: A Very Buggery Birthday\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-28T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-29T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d4ea55ea2748a2b819f30178169f6983.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"If you like boys, girls \\u0026 bass then this premium bisexual rave situation is just what the doctor ordered\\n\\nExpect speedy Gs, UKFunky, 92 hardcore, jungle, bassline bangers and anything inbetween\\n\\nID required for entry.\\nThere’s some v cheap tickets up for those who are unwaged- if u still can’t afford drop us a msg on ve insta well sort u xxx\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2375798\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":163,\"name\":\"XOXA x Queer Future Club x Manual Smiles\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-28T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-29T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ca20b0b50c35e4279b4782f3a24b0e42.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Landing at Peckham’s beloved Carpet Shop, New York/London collective XOXA team up with the Brussels-based Queer Future Club and local record label + DJ Manual Smiles for seven hours of club indulgence. Iconic local duo FAFF lead the charge, known for elevating dance music spaces with genre-traversing sounds.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2364440\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":176,\"name\":\"House of Annetta: House Care Day\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-29T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-29T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"de2a6d647353d3f20fe7b12b1137c0d7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The house is still closed for hibernation but we will hold a couple drop-in Care Days to get ready for the reopening in the first weekend of May.\\n\\nSpitalfields City Farm will be collecting old bricks from the house to build new growing beds. We need helping hands to get them ready for collection! We’ll also be taking care of the garden at HoA too, tending to the planters and compost.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":131,\"name\":\"The Good The Bad And The Zugly / Dog Rotten / Heelplant\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-29T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-29T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0266cbeea01f6e95dbabaa81a119779a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nThe Good the Bad and the Zugly\\nThe bastard child of the 90s Oslo punk scene, reminding us of a time when punk rock was a promise of infantile nihilism and pure vicious fun! Now, after five studio albums and a decade of touring their infamous live shows, the once so virile Norwegians have hit the inevitable 18-wheeled semi-truck that is middle-age. But the pitch black satiric humor that has characterized GBZ throughout their career seems only to be fueled further on by the growing bitterness instilled in these five hemorrhoid infested critters.\\n\\n+ support from\\nDog Rotten\\nSE London Punk Rap\\n\\nHeelplant\\nSouth London noise punk\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£15\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/the-good-the-bad-and-the-zugly\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":216,\"name\":\"A Century In Sound: London Premiere Event at Jumbi\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-30T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-30T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d36d406106b372bdf838492b98994736.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A record that predicted the future. Some nights are for movement. This one is for meaning.\\n\\nMonday 30th March from 6PM at Jumbi - A Century in Sound lands for a special talk + listening session led by Dennis Bovell MBE, exploring Riot in Lagos by Ryuichi Sakamoto - a track released in 1980 that many credit as a blueprint for electro, years before the sound fully took hold in clubs across the world.\\n\\nRooted in Japan’s 100-year ongaku kissa tradition - spaces built for deep, intentional listening - this is about slowing things all the way down. About sound, as it’s meant to be felt.\\n\\nWith music on the night from Kay Suzuki and Anu.\\n\\nFor the heads who read liner notes.\\nFor those who stay behind after everyone’s gone, just to hear one more record.\\nFor anyone who knows the difference between hearing music and listening to it.\\n\\nA room. A system. No distractions. Just presence.\\n\\nIf that’s you - you already know.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2399745\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":132,\"name\":\"No Man / Supernova / Tethered / Scadenza / Sevy Verna\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-30T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-30T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"32be40c912d2b1bd89540836f46cbb57.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nNo Man\\nPunks for Palestine. Experimental hardcore fury.\\n\\n+ support from\\nSupernova\\nConscious hardcore for radical moshers, FFO Bane \\u0026 Time To Heal\\n\\nTethered\\nFrantic riffing Emo Punx, FFO Plaids \\u0026 Embrace\\n\\nScadenza\\nNew London screamo, FFO Ravachol \\u0026 Yaphet Kotto\\n\\nSevy Verna\\nNew London screamo, FFO Oathbreaker \\u0026 Circle Takes The Square\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£13\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/no-man\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":124,\"name\":\"COVID-26: Bad Bias in the Body\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-30T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5ebb89c9e6840b245ff5fdb9ce2758d3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"COVID-26: Bad Bias in the Body explores what remains in the body after COVID-era anti-Asian racism and how it might be released together.\\n\\nDuring the pandemic, East and Southeast Asian communities became highly visible targets of racism worldwide. While many of these experiences remained unaddressed and were treated as isolated incidents, they left traces that continue to shape how people perceive and move through the world.\\n\\nCOVID-26: Bad Bias in the Body begins from the recognition that these experiences continue to linger in the body as residues, and therefore explores them through a shared sensory and physical experience. \\n\\nBringing together artists from diverse East and Southeast Asian backgrounds, Bad Bias revisits these experiences through artistic experimentation in 2026, transforming what once felt scattered and individual into a collective moment of reflection and release.\\n______\\n\\nPROGRAMME\\n\\nThe evening unfolds across three acts. Audiences are encouraged to experience the full programme.\\n\\nACT 1 – Movement (Ming Chin Hsieh)\\n\\nThe Weight of a Word is a contemporary dance performance responding to anti-Asian racism during the COVID-19 pandemic. Through rope, spoken words and facemasks, the piece explores how language, fear and bias can restrain and dehumanise the body, while gradually opening a space for reflection and resilience.\\n\\nACT 2 – Short Film Programme\\n\\nA curated programme of four short films exploring pandemic memory and anti-Asian racism.\\nMoving from specific experiences to broader historical and social contexts, the films situate these stories within longer histories of racism while reframing ESEA identities through ESEA perspectives.\\n\\nACT 3 – Sound Performance (Angela Wai Nok Hui) \\n\\nThe Church Bell Cancels is a live sound performance centred around the resonance of a church bell. Through vibration, silence and the echo of the room, the work transforms the space into a shared sonic environment where personal and collective stories resonate through the body.\\n\\n______\\n\\nMing Chin Hsieh is a dance artist originally from Taipei, Taiwan, now based in London, United Kingdom. Trained in ballet, contemporary dance, and martial arts Taichi, she studied at the National Taiwan University of Arts in Taipei before continuing her training at London Contemporary Dance School, where she performed with James Cousins Dance Company.\\n\\nAngela Wai Nok Hui is a percussionist and sound artist based in London and Hong Kong. She uses sounds that are not meant to be, childhood-like sugarcoating to frame and tell the true story of the living, uses sonic elements to bring attention to the phenomena of activism and self-love with a bitter aftertaste.\\n\\n______\\n\\nSHORT FILMS\\n\\nCOVID Dystopia\\nThomas Thorspecken / USA / 2023 / 4’\\n\\n“We might be done with COVID, but COVID is not done with us.”\\nFast-paced animated short about humanity's inability to adapt to a virus.\\n\\nWuhan Driver\\nTiger Ji / USA, China / 2021 / 14’\\n\\nAt the onset of the pandemic, a Chinese Uber driver in New York struggles to make ends meet as he picks up various passengers on a long and dreary night.\\n\\nCenturies and Still\\nSally Tran / USA / 2021 / 4’\\n\\nA mixed media illustrated short film by a Vietnamese creative team telling the history of anti-Asian racism and violence in the U.S. The film seeks to unveil how history took part in the birth and perpetuation of today’s surge of anti-Asian discrimination and hate crimes.\\n\\nSunny\\nSky Yang / UK / 2020 / 7’\\n\\nAs a Chinese boy transitions from childhood to adolescence, he finds himself lost in a world that tells him he should hate where he comes from. SUNNY follows the story of a mixed race Chinese British boy who is ashamed of his ethnicity, and unsure of where he belongs.\\n\\n______\\n\\nBad Bias is a London-based organisation producing multidisciplinary events centred on East and Southeast Asian (ESEA) arts and culture. Through curated programmes and experimental formats, we collaborate with ESEA creatives to create safe and creative spaces where artists and audiences can engage with ESEA cultures and stories.\\n\\n@badbias.official\\n\\nbadbias.uk@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://wegottickets.com/event/696220\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":215,\"name\":\"Drainfly, My Bisexual Girlfriend, Rosemary Moss\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-30T19:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7c232bf8d08bd566e9642981014c30d5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"DRAINFLY London folk post-punk crawling with the debris of your drains\\n\\nMY BISEXUAL GIRLFRIEND loves me\\n\\nROSEMARY MOSS Singing for pleasure. Appearing here in duo form.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.windmillbrixton.co.uk/events/2026-03-30-drainfly-my-bisexual-girlfriend-rosemary-moss-the-windmill\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":217,\"name\":\"12 Acts of Shelter: Act III\",\"start_time\":\"2026-03-31T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-31T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"207a0b9ac177f5344e2e8595c7341ee8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nJoin us for Act III of Twelve Acts of Shelter, where poetry, music and guided writing gather around three small houses of light.\\n\\n12 Acts of Shelter is a year-long monthly performance series unfolding through object, text, and sound: a small house under light, poetry and music.\\n\\nAcross twelve months, the series becomes a visible archive of time. Each month, a new house. Each house, a new performance. These small hand-built structures will anchor each gathering.\\n\\nEach evening features a performance by Black Geographies, alongside invited readers whose work speaks to questions of shelter, inheritance, desire, and survival, as well as a short open mic. And together, the night will move between music, language, and ritual.\\n\\nA guided freewriting session, scored by Alex DT and led by Phoenix Yemi, will invite the audience into a quiet act of making. You’ll leave the evening with your own poem.\\n\\nAudience members will also receive small printed tokens designed specifically for each month.\\n\\n12 Acts of Shelter asks: What do we build to survive? What remains in the aftermath of ruin, and what is the body, if not another kind of house?\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/twelve-acts-of-shelter-act-iii-tickets-1984698514684/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":115,\"name\":\"SAMODIVA [Kissing choir]\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-01T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-02T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"edb55fa6a77aafee28b52433b71bc2f5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"01/04/26 - Chat’s Palace\\n\\n02/04/26 - Longfield Hall\\n\\nVOICING PROJECT is a collaborative project between filmmaker Tomislav Latinovic and choir facilitator Noa Costello. With pieces that explore folk origins of sin, queer intimacy and community, participants perform live scoring of film. Noa and Tomislav are informed by Irish and Slavic/Balkan folk cultures, stories, music and art.\\nThe films and scores are created simultaneously, with the choir scoring the film and the film scoring the choir. \\n\\nVoicing Choir projects run in two series, workshops and rehearsals. During workshops participants explore folk and experimental sound, and create the foundations that are developed into the final score. Voicing choir agrees to avoid formal music language in our spaces, only using language that every person in the room could understand. \\nThe Voicing choir agrees that no understanding of music is superior to another, and that each new person that joins the choir will shape our collective understanding of sound. We talk about music for the way it feels, for the atmosphere it creates, for tension it builds or bursts.\\nWe want to hear each participants contributions in all of our pieces. Voicing choir is completely free to attend.\\n\\nSAMODIVA [Kissing choir] will be our third large-scale screening and performance. Showing film work directed by Tomislav Latinovic and Matilda Harrison, the piece shows intimacy for it’s building, it’s moment, and it’s falling away. \\n\\nSometimes anticipation outshines the satisfaction of a kiss. I’m excited by the build-up and the tension, when my hairs stand on end and my body feels fizzy. Things that were gross ten minutes ago become beautiful and erotic. We reach this meditative state in our thoughts, sinking into our future satisfaction. Release is tainted by the knowledge that I’ve done this before, and I’ll need to do it again.\\n\\nWe will run over two nights.\\n\\n01/04/26 19:00 - Chat’s Palace\\n\\n02/04/26 19:00 - Longfield Hall\\n\\nDoors at 19:00\\n\\n20:00 \\n\\nLa Bise - Abby witchalls \\n\\n20:30\\n\\nWalking choir - Voicing Project \\n\\n21:00 \\n\\nSAMODIVA [Live performance]\\n\\nTickets available here or OTD \\n\\nGeneral Admission £10\\n\\nConcession Ticket £5\\n[Low income, older adult etc. Please note that these tickets are limited]\\n\\nFundraising Ticket £15\\n\\n\\n\\nProfit from these events allows us to continue to run our free community projects. \\nNo one turned away for lack of funds.\\n\\nPlease email voicingproject@gmail.com \\nOr find us on instagram @voicingproject\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":204,\"name\":\"Vanessa Amara + nil00 \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-01T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-01T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0b50075d9bd2048aed017ca57189418a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Vanessa Amara is a Danish duo consisting of Birk Gjerlufsen and Sebastián Santillana. Their music is purposely difficult to classify, working within a patchwork of playful absurdity and contemporary classical and experimental music.Through their distinct blend of analog instruments, ranging from the resonance of the pipe organ to the intricate warmth of strings, they forge a tapestry of sound.\\n\\n\\nnil00 is a scouse-Iranian multidisciplinary artist working across music, filmmaking and DIY fashion to materialise transmissions from the subconcious realm. soaring from lofty heights to cartoonish falls, nil00 develops and expands a slapstick but deeply felt mythology across multiple forms.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":109,\"name\":\"Cinema F'el Salon\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-02T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-02T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fad866b42b1186b2866adc895307f8c6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A new screening event is coming to London, baba. Brought to you by NAFS x Salt \\u0026 Sister Studio    Cinema f’el Salon is a soft landing of a film night. A safe, non-judgemental, non-shaming space to be authentic; sitting at home, together. If, like us, your experience of the salon growing up was that it was stiff and off-limits; you can rejoice in reclaiming the very space, in the name of comfort and connection.    We’ll gather around a film from the golden era of Cairo cinema, watching and noticing what was always there: queerness in the margins, in the looks and gestures, in the subtext. Y3ni مش جديد علينا,  it’s part of the archive, part of the language. We azz-azz on lib and za3tar popcorn, and gag on the timeless gorgeousness of our friends Faten, Shadia, So3ad, Omar and Hind, to name a few.     For our first event, we’ll be We’ll be screening the 1955 Sigarah wa Kas سيجارة وكاس by Niazi Mostafa, starring the exquisite Samia Gamal and Dalida. The drama! The tension! The shik-shak-shok of it all!  Post-screening, we farfesh, with space to discuss the film - and anything else. كلّه ماشي.    Your ticket includes a live music performance, screening and an arrival snack (if you want to be very 3ammo about it and bring more snacks with you in your jacket lining, feel free). Drinks will be available at the bar, and all you need to do is turn up.    Topline // من الآخر    What - Sigarah Wa Kas (1955 dir Niazi Mostafa)        When - 2 April from 6pm. Performance at 7pm, screening at 8pm.  Where - Close-Up Cinema, E1 6HR  Who - everybody is welcome. The film will be subtitled.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.zeffy.com/en-GB/ticketing/cinema-fel-salon\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":156,\"name\":\"Two Way Dreaming\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-02T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4fe109b83ee69efb5707454fa5f58eff.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Two Way Dreaming presents Small Talk Screening – An inferno of pleasure and madness: postcolonial cinema in 1980s London.\\n\\nWorking in collaboration with the independent film series Two Way Dreaming, we are delighted to announce that “Small Talk: On the Corners of London \\u0026 Paris” will be hosting a screening.\\n\\nBuilding on the themes of the Hanif Kureishi workshop, we shall be screening a classic of 1980s London postcolonial cinema. Once again, Sita Balani and Ashwani Sharma are our guests to share a post-screening discussion.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/two-way-dreaming-presents-small-talk-screening-tickets-1983615750106\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":88,\"name\":\"Unhappen\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-02T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-03T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8bf88b0d8b700675da00f709245ca484.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Unhappen is a new club series based at Cu, Dalston, focusing on soundsystem music untethered by genre, with an emphasis on affordability and creating a safe community space. Through it’s first few excursions, Maris \\u0026 Wandah have nurtured Unhappen as a space for guest DJs to dig deeper into their selections, while intentionally bringing different musical communities together in the dance.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2387018\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":107,\"name\":\"Buss with Bambi, Yushh \\u0026 Meku\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-02T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-03T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"39958f3837186abf4a1e6bfd035c1800.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We present to you, a new night called buss, illustrated by Edie Medley, curated by Cam Joon.\\n\\nJoin us on adventures with the bussdem as they interact with clubland, most notably their favourite club, The Carpet Shop in Peckham. It’s a London party, for the London heads.\\n\\nBussdem going through the ritual of shubz - it starts at home and ends on the lime bike home.\\n\\nReal spread of talent on this one, all artists crossing boundaries in their own ways.\\n\\nBambi, hailing from Paris, brings her unique blend of dub \\u0026 psychedelic infused Bass \\u0026 Tech. Deep, groovy \\u0026 trippy.\\n\\nBristols Yushh (Pressure Dome) with her signature Bristolian touch, left leaning Bass \\u0026 UK Techno. A refreshing take on the sounds we all know and love.\\n\\nLastly, fresh off his debut release with Off Beat, local favourite Meku. An artist with deep roots in bass music, textural house \\u0026 rhythmic pleasure.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2375640\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":133,\"name\":\"Bank Holiday Beatdowns | Headbussa / Negative Frame / Not Without Punishment \\u0026 More\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-03T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c45d1306b91884ab62a0dd72c309e811.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nHeadbussa\\nParis hardcore fight music\\n\\nPlus special guests:\\nNegative Frame\\nLondon metalcore maniacs\\n\\n+ support\\nNot Without Punishment\\nSouthampton hardcore\\n\\nRekrucify\\nEvilcore filth from the void\\n\\nWarden\\nDeathcore devastation\\n\\nSo Far So Good\\nLondon heavy hardcore\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£15\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/headbussa\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":172,\"name\":\"etsdts fundraiser - smallbig\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f1f93e9f051844bc07344b9b311c1545.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The first sonic event curated by angela wai nok hui, artistic director of an art cafe basement - Eat the Sunshine . Down the Sun, with guest curator Jonathan Higgins.    Two nights for curious ears and odd souls out there.  Bringing in a mad line up with artists and musicians in the London experimental, improvisation sonic and noise scene.\\n\\nsmallBig is a fundraiser gig to get a sound system for the etsdts basement. All ticket income will go into making a new intimate music and art space for London.\\n\\n---\\n\\nplease note - as this is a 2 day event your ticket will display Friday April 3rd as the date, but the 'tier' section will correctly display the specific day you purchased for.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":160,\"name\":\"TROUGH 05\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1113fb61494584305d326f31519f02c3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"🥚 TROUGH 05 🥚 Avalon Cafe 🥚 Friday 3rd April 🥚 7pm-4am 🥚\\n\\nSpring is here. And so is our fifth offering to you all. \\n\\nWe’re back at Avalon caf to inaugurate your bank holiday weekend, and it will be filled with treats and surprises. Think egg shaped choccy hunts, free soup as per, a duet of very important clowns, and the UK debut of hyperpop starlet Rikky Mandozza \\n\\n///////\\n\\nPLOWMAN AND CUMMINS are an experimental clown duo. Expect classical singing, falling over, mess, beauty, violence, and the feeling you get when you see someone running for the bus as it drives away 👽\\n\\nPlease note this act will have a limited capacity, and will be on a first-come first-served basis. Please arrive in good time! \\n\\n///////\\n\\nMOONDISC bring their oddball mix of medieval percussion, 3D printed recorders, horns, and bass to Avalon for their debut performance 🌀 John Cage eat your heart out 🌀\\n\\n///////\\n\\nAnjali’s sets are lil universes of their own - dank, sparkly, euphoric, murky, rawdy, saucy, and hard. Expect all the above and more ✨\\n\\n///////\\n\\nRikky Mandozza (live) - we are so very excited to host Berlin-based artist Rikky Mandozza for their UK debutttt. Their live set is somewhat unforgettable, sitting in the glittering ether between hyperpop and trance. Make sure you’ve done your stretches upon arrival. 💅\\n\\nWe’ll be fundraising for Sister Midnight - a collective grown from the fires of SE London’s political music world, who are on a mission to build a collectively owned venue in the heart of Catford. They’ve secured a site at the former Brookdale Club, and the proceeds of the night will go towards the ongoing renovation works at the space. Come shake a leg and contribute to more spaces for dance and play\\n\\nArtwork by the wonderful @t.twillis / @body_bits_ \\n\\nLove from Trough x\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34532/trough-05\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":121,\"name\":\"Small Car NRG\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b0e9c0f3abbbbcdb429ac98caa6700b7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Beep beep, Small Car NRG taxed and legal once again. Service now. Two warning lights. Stolen Velour, Grunt Govan and Mid Century Soundsystem inside the 5 cd changer, eject 2am. Rotherhithe tunnel open to 18 wheelers for one night only, you may be charged.\\n\\nFundraiser for the awesome Piehouse Coop in Deptford. Engines warming up from 7pm.\\n\\nWe’re starting the night off with Tweakers Welcome which is a supportive and low-pressure environment to practice DJing in a real club, on a real soundsystem! Practice mixing with active support and advice, have a go by yourself, or just play a few tunes and listen to them on a big system.\\n\\nPlease sign up for a slot using the form in our insta bio if you'd like a bit of time on the decks :)\\n\\n£10 Tickets on RA.\\n\\nNo one turned away for lack of funds. Get in touch with us on insta and we will sort you out. @smallcarnrg\\n\\nLet’s have it !\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2387833\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":198,\"name\":\"REGGAE AT THE RIVOLI \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-03T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4fdab0ad471476698fa7e57231ef0937.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us at the Rivoli Ballroom for a night of Ska, Rocksteady, Reggae,  classics all on vinyl. Expect to hear, Dennis Brown, Gregory Isaacs, Bob Marley, John Holt, Alton Ellis, Ken Boothe, Johnny Clarke, Marcia Griffiths, King Tubby, Keith \\u0026 Tex, Lee Perry, Skatalites-Legends of Reggae, Studio 1, Treasure Isle, Trojan, Joe Gibbs, Channel One-labels, Beres Hammond, Sanchez, Frankie Paul,Wailing Souls,Barrington Levy, Protoje.\\n\\nCash only on the door and at the bar!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://reggae-at-the-rivoli.designmynight.com/69a9bfe1ab5e27743c079cef/reggae-at-the-rivoli-3\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":108,\"name\":\"Germinal: Rojin Sharafi / Rhizocorp / leo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a901b0f74550acfa8fd9c4bce674f593.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Experimental electronic music from PTP label artist Rojin Sharafi, sci-fi dance punk from Rhizocorp, and mutant club sounds from leo. London Spanners, 3 April, 8pm, £15.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/germinal-rojin-sharafi-rhizocorp-leo-tickets-1861484\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":184,\"name\":\"CLUB PLEASURE Presents: Resurrection!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"30d136da11bb3c2fd318944bf2591add.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"HOT, new, queer club night coming to the iconic Bethnal Green Working Men's Club.\\n\\nClub Pleasure Presents: Resurrection!\\n\\nnew party, new pleasures.\\n\\nFriday 3rd April 2026 (Bank Holiday Friday) 9pm-3am \\n\\n@ Bethnal Green Working Men's Club, 42-46 Pollard Row, London E2 6NB.\\n\\nall-nite-dancing. with a selection of east london's finest DJ's spinning sexy sounds of house, disco, italo, hi-nrg + more. \\n\\nPerrin (Happy Endings, Wormhole)\\nRita Lin (UOKHUN)\\nStav B (No.11, Dyke March, This Is My Culture)\\nPUBLICTOILETDISCO (This Is My Culture, Locomotive Disco, Remix)\\n\\n \\n\\nBGWMC will be serving up their Bank Holiday Happy Hour too -\\n\\n*HAPPY HOUR 9PM UNTIL 10PM! MOST DRINKS A FIVER! *\\n*EARLY DOORS COCKTAILS!\\n\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n!! support this iconic east london venue !!\\n\\nCLUB PLEASURE will be raising money for different local/LGBTQ causes each event (TBA)\\n\\nWe're hosting this edition at Bethnal Green Working Men's Club to help support this iconic venue! Turning up for our beloved venues, buying tickets, spending money at the bar, all help to keep these places going and BGWMC is still going and still throwing great parties! So please show some love for BGWMC and their incredible team.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2389373\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":106,\"name\":\"Shady Sisters W/ Luisa, Gabriel Finch \\u0026 Dean Watton\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e9d6c34478929d63282cdae6162d0275.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Good Friday, better company.\\n\\nShady Sisters returns April 3rd to Low Profile Studio for our fourth rendezvous.\\n\\nJoining us, we have Luisa, one of Portugal's finest selectors, along sides Shady family favourites Dean Watton \\u0026 Gabriel Finch.\\n\\nThis one will be a journey, always take the road less travelled.\\n\\nWe cant wait to see you.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2370202\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":173,\"name\":\"Forever 02\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-03T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"593b5dc29a430db374b4c7ab9786359f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Forever 02 @ Venue MOT\\n\\nUnannounced line up, live music and DJs, 21+, no phones\\n\\nForever is Big Dyke Energy's sister party, for the dykes, dolls, t boys, faggots, friends \\u0026 family\\n\\nWe've invited some of our absolute favourite artists to showcase all the music we love. \\nExpect bass-led club sounds, deep \\u0026 dubby melodies,\\nrolling acid house, \\u0026 FAB live performances \\n\\n~ something for everyone ~\\n\\nAccessibility info on our Instagram highlights (@_4ever_4ever_4ever_)\\n\\nI'm gonna keep dancing forever, me x\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2370645\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":123,\"name\":\"Lebanon and Palestine Solidarity Market\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c4b7fa3ff6731982bca1e6301731a0ff.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Steadfast Solidarity Market\\n \\nSAT 4 APRIL\\nMARKET 2-11PM\\nW/ MUSIC 8-11PM\\n\\nTHE HORSE HOSPITAL, WC1N 1JD\\n \\nSelling clothing, books, artworks, jewellery, accessories, homeware, merch and more. \\nLebanese snacks served throughout the day.\\n \\nThis solidarity market is raising funds for vital initiatives that provide food, supplies, and medicine for those who remain steadfast on their land. These support networks include our friends: The Sanabel Team food bank in Gaza, and medicine drives in the south of Lebanon.\\n\\nSince our last solidarity market in November 2023, our government has continued to ignore the people’s support for Palestinian self-determination and Lebanese resistance. As they surveil and threaten the livelihoods of Muslim communities and stifle boycotts and protests against the genocide in Gaza that continues despite the pretence of a ceasefire.\\n\\nAs of today (16 March), over 14% of Lebanon’s population (830,000 people) have been forcibly displaced, with 500 people killed by the recently intensified Israeli invasion. Israel has ordered further blanket evacuations in South Lebanon and threatened to replicate the genocide in Gaza.\\n\\nIn violation of the ceasefire agreement, genocide in Gaza continues, abetted by the UK, EU, and US. Since 19 Jan 2025, Israel’s strikes and shelling alone have killed 650 people and wounded thousands more. The siege on Gaza continues to limit access to clean water, food, shelter, and vital medicine, leaving more people to die from preventable diseases and malnutrition.\\n\\nWe learn from the UK-EU-US-Israel Imperial Alliance’s attacks on Iran and Lebanon that this iteration of ongoing genocide in Palestine has set a renewed precedent for the expansion of the state of Israel. Instead of taking meaningful action, our elected leaders scramble to lend military, economic, diplomatic, and ideological support to the settler colonial project and to destabilise the region for their own agendas. The complicity of our state remains undeniable, yet we can continue to come together and support each other in grief, rage, and resistance to state violence, local and global.\\n\\nTo make it manageable and affordable for as many people as possible to contribute at the solidarity market, there will be guide prices for items but the majority will be “pay what you can.” If you can pay less or more than the guide prices, please do. All of your money will go directly to where it is most needed on the ground in Gaza and the South of Lebanon.\\n\\nAll Welcome. All budgets.\\n\\nThank you as ever to the Horse Hospital and to everyone who donated for their generosity.\\n\\nWith donations from (\\u0026 more TBA):\\n\\n5 gate temple\\nAlia Hamaoui\\nAlice Fraser\\nAmy Rodriguez\\nAnastasia Sosunova\\nArcadia Missa Publications\\nAugust Sklar\\nBog\\nBradley Harrington\\nCafe OTO\\nCatarina Moura\\nCC Steding\\nCecile Tulkens\\nChris Chapman\\nDivided Press\\nEleanor Arnold\\nEwa Poniaowska\\nDiogo Gama\\nGaby Sahhar\\nGala Colivet Dennison\\nHannah Black\\nHat \\u0026 Beard Press\\nHela Press\\nHeloise Chaise\\nHurtence\\nFirpal Jawanda\\nI.W. Payne\\nIshbel Lowther\\nJame St Findlay\\nJawara Alleyne\\nJ C McCormack\\nJess Maybury\\nJos Nyreen\\nKani Lent\\nKatie Shannon\\nKhalid Jauffer\\nLUEDER\\nMad Bad Tats\\nMainline RUS/Fr.CA/DE\\nMaria Giulia Casco\\nMica Levi\\nPaola V Rozo\\nParapraxis magazine\\nPerfect Lives\\nPhoebe Randall\\nRat Section\\nRacheal Crowther\\nRehana Zaman\\nRen Matsunaga Sogunro\\nRoland Knowlden\\nRuth Angel Edwards\\nSara Graça\\nSam Dolbear\\nShola von Reinhold\\nSophia Al-Maria\\nSteph Linn\\nStill House Plants\\nStanislav Iordinav\\nSusu Laroche\\nTabitha Weddell\\nTarmara Kalo\\nTwos\\nXenab Lone Jamil / Aune Collections\\nYalda Valizadeh\\nYiduo Cheng\\nZoe Williams\\nZoey Yang\\nZOMMER\\n\\u0026 Anonymous artists who face criminalisation for their solidarity\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":210,\"name\":\"Easter Party @ SET Social\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-05T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"dccae3d8bcd197f84229b5bd88e22262.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dust off your best spoon and gather your eggs ’cause Easter is coming to SET Social!\\n\\nExpect egg hunts, spring bunting, face painting and a few other things that felt right at the time.\\n\\nAt midnight, things get serious with a strictly regulated egg and spoon race. Bring your own spoon. Ladles will be disqualified without discussion. Chocolate prizes are at stake.\\n\\nFrom 10pm, SET Social favourite DJ Faddy takes over the Red Bar, carrying things through til the early hours.\\n\\nNo need to dress up, but it wouldn’t hurt 😉\\n\\n!!!Calling all tarot readers!!!\\n\\nWe’re on the look out for a tarot reader to join the night.\\n\\nIf you read cards, interpret signs or have a general sense of what’s coming up next, we’d love to hear from you.\\n\\nPlease get in touch at social@setspace.uk and include a bit about your experience.\\n\\nEvent details\\nDate: Saturday 4 April\\nTime: 6pm-3am\\nLocation: SET Social, 55a Nigel Road, Peckham, SE15 4NP\\n\\nTickets on the door:\\n\\nFree before 8pm\\n£3 for SET Social members\\n£5 for non-members (must be accompanied by a member)\\n\\nPoster design by Lola Hibberd \\u003c3\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://setspace.uk/event/easter-at-set-social/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":220,\"name\":\"FUNDRAISER FOR LEBANON - Music, Film Screening, Food \\u0026 Poetry\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T23:45:00Z\",\"poster\":\"194311c630b9eea682947cf175256017.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Show up for Lebanon through an evening of community, art, and collective care. Location: Forno - 322 Andrews Road, E8 4RP Date: 4 April\\n\\n🤍🇱🇧Lebanon Fundraiser🇱🇧🤍\\n\\nPlease join us on Sat, 04 April, for an evening of live music, short films and poetry.\\n\\n\\n\\n100% of funds raised are going to grassroots groups supporting the 1 million displaced in Lebanon.\\n\\n\\nNote: this event is not a party, but an evening to share, enjoy and reflect upon a variety of Lebanese, Palestinian and Arab artistry across different forms and themes\\n\\n📍Forno - 322 Andrews Road, E8 4\\n\\n\\n\\n⏰ Time: 6pm until late. Tickets: £11.\\n\\n\\n\\n🎤 We’ll hear live music from:\\n\\n\\n\\n- Kareem Samara (oud)\\n\\n- Dina (vocals)\\n\\n- and others\\n\\n\\n\\n🎬 Short films from:\\n\\n\\n\\n- Firas Itani\\n\\n- Tamara Kalo\\n\\n- Azkadinya\\n\\n- Nouf Alhimiary\\n\\n- Romy Matar\\n\\n\\n\\n📜 Poetry from:\\n\\n\\n\\n- BabyO\\n\\n- Abdullah Erikat\\n\\n- Riwa Saab\\n\\n- And others\\n\\n\\n\\n🍽️ We'll also have food, drinks and artwork to buy, including manaeesh from EDAMI bakery, wines from Osros Vinos x Salseo, and crochet from LAMSA.\\n\\n\\n\\n🙏🏼 Come and support\\n\\n💓 Stand in solidarity\\n\\n🗣️ Share\\n\\n🇱🇧 helps us raise much needed funds for those working on the ground in Lebanon\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/fundraiser-for-lebanon-music-film-screening-food-poetry-tickets-1985639576425?aff=erellivmlt\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":42,\"name\":\"Noctifer\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"08db8e9f3f2a905e5a5f516205ece111.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This Easter, Sunday School returns for its only full weekend of 2026. After a few years of running bi-annual festival instalments, we now converge for only one annual long-weekend gathering - bigger, more vulgar, and more brutally disgusting than ever.\\n\\nThe ultimate descent into sound, darkness, and doom - tickets are limited, so secure yours and make the most of the discounted two-day passes available now.\\n\\nw/\\nbela (presents Korean Love Sonnets)\\nKenichi Iwasa \\u0026 Maxwell Sterling\\nEye Measure\\nNoise Warfare\\nSvartvit\\n+ Wilma (dj)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://wegottickets.com/f/14865/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":177,\"name\":\"BOOK LAUNCH: ‘A Studious Use’ with Giovanni Marmont\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-04T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cd0019554b7262f2d7a077549ce8633b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for some radical thinking, some real radical autonomist thinking, with one of our favourite publishers, Minor Compositions. Come and celebrate the publication of another vital, alert and mind bending work of theory.\\n\\nA Studious Use invites readers to reconsider the habitual logics and material priorities at play in practices of both study and use. It examines their potential and actual interplay, unravelling the ways in which these are at once shaped by and reproductive of broader social, political, and cultural currents. Here Giovanni Marmont explores how a seemingly inoffensive commitment to the terms of individuation, as a manner of understanding and organising the world first and foremost as an aggregate of separate entities, carries with it profoundly harmful implications. With an eye toward the unseen possibilities of social life, he proposes an alternative mode of engagement with and through artefacts – studious use – predicated instead on our general, shared, practical indebtedness. Through a blend of theoretical critique, philosophical inquiry, and experimental design practices, A Studious Use offers a rethinking of sociality not as a coming together of independent, if interacting subjects and objects but, rather, as a primary, undirected, ongoing collective experiment.\\n\\nAuthor of For a Pragmatics of the Useless,Erin Manning says: “How do practices dispossess us? How does use reorient the very question of function and form? Where else can it take us beyond our-selves? In this compelling engagement with use-beyond-use-value, Marmont takes us on a journey to a non-binary account of use that refuses the limited account of any marketable claim. Instead, it moves use toward the surprise of constellations as experimental as they are quotidian.”\\n\\nAs always, tickets are priced on a sliding scale. If you are unable to pay for a ticket please do not hesitate to contact us at shop@housmans.com, and a free ticket will be made available.\\n\\nIf you choose ‘book +entry’ your copies of the book will be available to collect on the evening. If you would like to collect it earlier, or arrange for delivery, please contact us (postage is £2.95). Telephone 020 7837 4473 or email shop@housmans.com.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/book-launch-a-studious-use-with-giovanni-marmont/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":112,\"name\":\"Dawdle: Dance or Dream\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-05T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"142f7184e77aeee3f48b7600c3004cd7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An evening of dream… sound for dancing or drifting off – Saturday 4 April, 8pm-1am.\\n\\nour peculiar customs including ambient mosh / speechless hours / cloaks(byo) / imps / wool webbing\\n\\ndeep comfort zones.\\n\\nhigh exploratorial sounds for movement by Onya Dev, Shimble and Jung.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dandelion.events/e/daw\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":22,\"name\":\"SUGAR 003\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-05T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"670594f7b2959bd04908acc163ea8f09.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SUGAR slinks back into the smoke @ the intimate SPANNERS for the 3rd steamy edition of blissed out euphoria all night long - let the sophisticated yet DIY lights n sound hypnotise ur booty\\n\\n— dreamy trance, luscious breakbeats, deep house grooves, with a sweet n soft centre, served slow and hot by London DJ's Angel D’lite and Bethan \\u003c3\\n\\nIf you are low on funds and really want to join, we have some low income tickets available :)\\n\\n10pm - 4am\\nas always surprise sweet treats for the 1st ones on the dancefloor\\n\\u003c 3\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2362688\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":194,\"name\":\"Sister Midnight FM with Maxwell Owin, sosi, Damsel, Cleopatra \\u0026 Faye Frazer\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-04T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-05T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"05901788909a0ce7372d927779e5056a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Broadcasting energy straight from the booth to the dancefloor, we take over The Carpet Shop this April for a special fundraiser in support of our radio station.\\n\\nWe’re bringing together a lineup of residents who capture the sound of the station: expect deep selections, soul, bass pressure and everything in between.\\n\\nMaxwell Owin B2B sosi\\nDamsel\\nFaye Frazer\\nCleopatra\\n\\nAll proceeds from the event go directly toward supporting the station and keeping the signal strong. Come down, dance with us, and help power the next chapter.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2389528\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":175,\"name\":\"Easter at Seven Sisters Market\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-05T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-05T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ec10c9d404b606c5e6208a6e5e37dcea.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We’re so excited to invite you to our Easter celebration at Seven Sisters Market 🐣🌸\\n\\nWe’ll begin at the Community Space and then move around the market for a fun-filled afternoon of activities for everyone 💫\\n\\nJoin us for an Easter egg hunt, egg decoration, and plenty of joyful moments to share with family and friends 🥚✨\\n\\nCome celebrate with us, support local, and enjoy a special day in our community 🤍\\n\\nPlease let us know how many will be coming by messaging or calling: 07436214346 📲\\n\\nSee you there 💗\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":40,\"name\":\"meanwhile... easter sunday [15 hours]\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-05T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-06T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"785bfd66177c4b607afe8e2b63cf01fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"bbecks\\nDJ AV (live)\\nJared\\nMetal Upa (live A/V)\\nOliver Scala b2b Aiden Francis\\nRiva \\nTeecra b2b Julie Desire \\nWigs (1) (downtempo set)\\nYsanne \\n\\nA/V by Celestial Artillery\\n\\n+ ambient lounge takeover by COOKED\\n\\nWith installations by:\\nBad Art Presents: Michael Shaw\\nMETAL UPA\\nMaurice.tv\\nShare\\n__\\n\\nThe meanwhile… rabbit hole goes to new depths this Easter — more nooks, more crannies, more side-quests.\\n\\nQuietly tucked away in the abandoned sprawl of Meridian Water is Gaffe, where fifteen hours gives way to our first day-into-night indoor-outdoor adventure.\\n\\nInside, residents Teecra and Oliver Scala invite Julie Desire and Aiden Francis for an exclusive series of b2bs. Joining them are local favourites Riva, Jared, and Ysanne to soundtrack our fifteen hours together with five extended sets.\\n\\nGaffe’s outdoor stage hosts the return of cult favourite meanwhile… ambient lounge, with an exclusive takeover and bespoke menu from music-minded supper club COOKED offering respite from the dancefloor.\\n\\nInstallations galore as COOKED’s Metal Upa, Michael Shaw, and our very own Maurice.tv dials up our multisensory club concept for what is set to be a blockbuster bank holiday blowout.\\n\\nBegin at the beginning, and go on until you come to the end. If you don’t know where you’re going, any road can take you there…\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2295139\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":79,\"name\":\"Patterns present: Pub (Live), Rosa Methol and Lali\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-05T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-05T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"45ebe91196e8d0392f1209c543d0c995.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2385364\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":167,\"name\":\"mi-el presents Pulling Threads\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-05T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-06T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fcc22614281635bd079fa5a3573133fd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"number one champion sound\\ncourtesy of the original vibes cartel\\nfuelling ur bank holiday tun up\\nyou're welcome ☆\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2394292\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":95,\"name\":\"Eve Stainton Dance Workshop \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-07T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-07T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1b01c3f281d5904d64c23836d68166c7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Eve Stainton is an artist and choreographer born in Manchester and living in London, UK. They create multi-disciplinary performances that involve movement practices, welded steel/live welding, digital collage, and other invisible forces like drama and suspense. Their research is rooted in community, interested in how differently marginalised people experience and come into relationship with power structures and societal conventions. Often working with codes or tropes of gender, class and threat, revealing ‘behind the scenes’ mechanisms of working together to show a kind of reality that isn’t seamless.\\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026.\\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary.\\n\\nN.B The venue is not accessible, the studio is up two flights of stairs.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":180,\"name\":\"Sid Plimmer + Hackpen\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-07T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-07T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2044eee1c9f8aae2cd06a4d1e6a66d00.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands returns with another banger; Hackpen and Sid Plimmer make it a family affair at The Ivy House on Tuesday 7th April!\\n\\nHackpen is the new audio-visual alias of Moss Plimmer. Areas of interest include hammers, boiled eggs, the British coastal path, fossils cracking, pure wool, train travel, ‘happy friday’ (as a concept), soil, fire, pedestrians, the universal key, land mass, pen knives, pork pies, motorcycles in colour, daylight saving, the light and heat survival can, gargoyles, the meaning behind the mound, rocks, storm certificates, the west country and beer out the glass bottle.\\nSid Plimmer is a 24 year old artist from the Mendip hills in Somerset. His latest album is about a blue horse. It is about moving fast and standing still all at once. It is about diesel, social misfires and children of the gods stealing the sun.\\n\\nFormerly Plimmer released a number of projects under the now-defunct alias of BoyBovis. A trilogy of albums that dealt mainly with rurality, belonging and dark places underground.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/t63eb2f1f040\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":226,\"name\":\"Max Luthert — Through The Fallstreak (Live Album Launch)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-07T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-07T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bf7cc76608297159dc107c8bb6c24c86.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An intimate trio performance combining acoustic instrumentation and live modular synthesis for the launch of Through The Fallstreak.\\n\\nMax Luthert launches Through The Fallstreak with a live trio performance in Dalston.\\n\\nThe music sits within avant-garde electro-acoustic practice, combining acoustic instrumentation and live modular synthesis. The set will draw on material from the album, shaped in the moment through improvisation and interaction.\\n\\nPerformed by Max Luthert , Matt Robinson (piano) and Jon Scott (drums).\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/max-luthert-through-the-fallstreak-live-album-launch-dalston-tickets-1982875504010?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":94,\"name\":\"Violet Savage Dance Workshop \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-08T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-08T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ee7b5cce4b1e31815a6388df251c3ed5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Violet Savage is a dancer whose work explores movement at the intersection of sonic and visual art. Her practice draws from improvisation to inhabit the charged space between self and other, through workshops that engage with the tension between presence and memory to present process and outcome simultaneously. At the heart of these workshops is a desire to expand the experience of exploration from a solitary to shared creative act, to experience dance as liveness, care and learning in both individual and collective bodies, resisting the forces of competition and fatigue that pull us apart.\\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026. \\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary. \\n\\nN.B The venue is not accessible, the studio is up two flights of stairs. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":103,\"name\":\"Glitter Fatigue\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-08T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-08T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"badc0a83da9e7e5f2af9c1112a1286e0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"9 April – 2 May 2026\\n\\nSomething viscous comes toward us!\\nJoin us for Glitter Fatigue: a group exhibition plunging into rot, entropy, and the phosphorescence of decay.\\n\\nAcross the exhibition exuberance slips into quieter undercurrents, anxieties, and dependencies. Hyperfeminine residues morph into fetid forms. Fleshy manifestations vibrate in exhausted heaps. \\nGlitter Fatigue: a requiem for small-houred kin. \\n\\nFeaturing works by\\nLolly Adams\\nKate Dunn\\nDirrty Harry\\nSophie Lloyd\\nOrnagh\\nBoudicca Paloma\\nMiranda Pissarides\\nFrancesca Van Haverbeke\\nFrida Wannerberger\\n\\nPrivate View\\n8 April 2026, 18:00–20:00\\nLive performance by Rizzla La Fizz\\n\\nClosing Party\\n2 May 2026, 18:00–20:00\\nLive performance by Ornagh\\n\\nBy appointment only\\n9 April – 2 May 2026\\nTWO-PLUS-TWO, Stockwell\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":170,\"name\":\"Rest, Refuel, Resist! Filton 24 Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-08T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-09T02:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e6729a972b85b78782e243e48f368056.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On Thursday 9th April, we welcome London Community Defence to fundraise for the legal \\u0026 living costs for the Filton 24 after 18 months in prison without trial.\\n\\nIn August 2024, activists drove a van into the Bristol manufacturing hub of Elbit systems: Israel’s largest weapons firm. Once inside, they dismantled equipment amounting to £2 million in damage. In February, 21 of the Filton 24 were granted bail after the jury did not return guilty verdicts on a single charge. Next year they face retrial, though all currently face extensive legal \\u0026 living costs.\\n\\nJoin us on Thursday 9th April from 8PM as we fundraise for the Filton 24.\\n\\nPresale tickets available via the link below. ‘Donation Only’ tiers available if you can’t attend on the evening.\\n\\n£8 minimum donation on the door all night.\\n\\nDoor Policy\\nDalston Superstore is a queer space. We prioritise our LGBTQIA+ customers and will sometimes ask our straight \\u0026 cis allies to support us by not taking up room in our venue. Please be conscious of who this space is intended for and be respectful. Never assume sexuality or gender identity. We will never ask personal questions on the door.\\n\\nLow/no income access\\nWe reserve limited spaces for those who cannot afford the standard ticket price due to being on low or no income. Please email hello@dalstonsuperstore.com with at least 48 hours notice to enquire.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/londoncommunitydefence/2123798\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":96,\"name\":\"Luisa D. Rozo Dance Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-09T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-09T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f92057e43f8582954cd4470361816493.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Luisa D. Rozo is a London-based multidisciplinary artist, biodynamic craniosacral therapist and cultural producer from Bolivia. Originally formed in dance and choreography, Luisa has a longstanding career with the scenic arts, having specialised in participatory processes, light design and movement research. She has created, produced and consulted several large and small scale pieces that were shown in England, Poland, Bolivia, Norway, Italy, Lithuania, Spain and Germany, as well as sharing her own sonic work that experiments with música popular Latinoamericana, field-recording and melancholic R\\u0026B. As of 2025, Luisa is a member of The Horse Hospital Collective, running the historic countercultural venue at the heart of London.\\n\\nLuisa will facilitate exercises that activate the embodied observation of time, gently pushing our bodies to engage with questions of perception, movement and meaning through improvisational frameworks and simple craniosacral-informed movement phrases. \\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026.\\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary.\\n\\nN.B The venue is not accessible, the studio is up two flights of stairs.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":224,\"name\":\"SET 91 Open Series – Crit Circle with Elida Silvey\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-09T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-09T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4f9ed0683af05fde18cd1d29bcd7d0c0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SET 91 continues the Open Series with a Crit Circle led by Elida Silvey, a writer, editor and artist whose practice explores visual culture, identity and memory. This session offers a structured yet informal space for artists and writers to share work in progress and receive feedback through collective discussion.\\n\\nCrit circles have often been shaped by institutional or academic settings. This session reimagines that format as a more open, collaborative environment, where participants can engage critically while supporting one another’s development. The focus is on creating a space that is welcoming, constructive and grounded in mutual respect.\\n\\nThis crit-circle will run for 1 hour and 30 minutes, with participants joining as either ‘readers’, sharing their work, or ‘listeners’, contributing to the discussion. Each reader will have a set amount of time to present, followed by group feedback and conversation, with timing managed to ensure everyone has the opportunity to participate.\\n \\n\\nWho’s it for?\\n\\nThis session is open to artists, writers and practitioners working across disciplines.\\n\\nIt will be particularly relevant for those:\\n\\n- Developing new or in-progress work independently\\n- Interested in sharing and receiving constructive feedback\\n- Looking to engage with others in a supportive, discussion-led setting\\n\\nWhat to expect\\n\\nThe session will include:\\n\\n- A facilitated crit circle led by Elida Silvey\\n- Opportunities for selected participants (‘readers’) to share work\\n- Group feedback and discussion\\n- A collaborative and informal format\\n\\nReader guidelines\\n\\nUp to 1,000 words of text, or\\nUp to 5 minutes of video or moving image work\\n\\nOur aim is to build a community of artists that build each other up. Participants are encouraged to approach both giving and receiving feedback with care and consideration, contributing to a respectful and supportive environment. Any abuse will not be tolerated.\\n \\n\\nWhat you'll takeaway\\n\\nParticipants will leave with:\\n\\n- Constructive feedback on their work (for readers)\\n- Insight into different approaches to critique and discussion\\n- Greater confidence in sharing and articulating ideas\\n- Opportunities to connect with other practitioners\\n\\nEvent details\\nDate: 9 April\\nArrival: 6pm\\nSession time: 6:30-9pm\\nLocation: SET 91, 91 Tabernacle Street, Old Street, London, EC2A 4JN\\n\\nCapacity: 15 participants\\n- 7 reader slots (bringing work to critique)\\n- 8 listener slots\\n\\nThis event is run on a pay-what-you-can basis, with a suggested donation of £5.\\n\\nAs places are limited, we kindly ask that you only book if you are able to attend so that others who would benefit from the session are able to take part. \\n\\nIf you can no longer attend, please cancel your ticket so the space can be offered to someone else. \\n \\n\\nAbout the facilitator\\n\\nElida Silvey is a self-taught Mexican-American writer, editor and artist based in London. Her work explores visual theory and its relationship to identity, time and the construction of the self through (collective) memory.\\n\\nShe is an Editor at Montez Press and one half of Dream Sequence, an experimental film club dedicated to non-linear and hybrid cinematic practices. Her writing spans personal essays, poetry, criticism and experimental forms that explore how visual culture mediates lived experience. Her debut novel will be published by Montez Press in 2027.\\n \\n\\nAbout SET 91 and the Open Series\\n\\nThis session is part of the SET 91 Open Series, a programme of talks, workshops and discussions supporting artists in navigating, developing and contextualising contemporary practice.\\n\\nSET 91 is SET’s contemporary arts gallery on Tabernacle Street in Old Street, providing a non-profit platform for early-career and underrepresented artists to develop and present new work through exhibitions, performances and public events.\\n\\nLearn more: https://setspace.uk/set-91/ \\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34856/set-91-open-series-crit-circle-with-elida-silvey\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":213,\"name\":\"Trojan Horses \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-09T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"83dc05cfad28b5f5a15677c9792b2b62.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Trojan Horses explores how images can hold and carry meanings that are not immediately visible. Taking its cue from a text by Andrew Cranston, the exhibition considers how aesthetics can act as a point of entry into complex and often uncomfortable subjects.\\n\\nBringing together twelve artists working across painting and drawing, the exhibition is co-curated by SET studio members Tom Houlihan and Elisa Terranera, and is presented at SET Vauxhall.\\n\\nAbout the exhibition\\n\\n“Beauty can be a useful Trojan horse to smuggle in darker ideas”, writes Andrew Cranston in his book Never a Joiner. He is reflecting on his painting Vague feelings of dread (2022), where a small group of fish hover above the pearlescent tiled floor of a pond. For Cranston, their subtle, shifting movement recalls submarines and warships in the Mediterranean, becoming a way of expressing unease shaped by conflict and its ongoing presence.\\n\\nTrojan Horses takes this idea as its starting point. Bringing together painting and drawing, the exhibition asks how artists use aesthetics to engage with social and political realities.\\n\\nAcross the exhibition, the works touch on themes including class, feminism, war, mortality, identity and religion. Here, beauty is not simply decorative or resolved; it operates as a point of entry – something that draws viewers in before revealing more layered and challenging ideas beneath the surface. Or, as Cranston puts it, “darker ideas”.\\n\\nAll twelve artists share a background in observational drawing. At a time marked by political and technological uncertainty, Trojan Horses reflects on what this longstanding language of picture-making can still hold, and how painting and drawing continue to offer ways of engaging closely with the world today.\\n\\nEvent details\\n\\nOpening: Thursday 9 April, 6-9pm\\nDates: 9-26 April\\nOpening hours: Thursday – Sunday, 12-6pm\\nLocation: SET Vauxhall, Camelford House, 89 Albert Embankment, London\\nAdmission: Free\\n\\nThe exhibition is also viewable by appointment. Please contact: tomhoulihan7@gmail.com\\n\\nContributing artists\\n\\nSasha Alfillé, Joe Allen, Rebecca Ashton, Arthur Boothby, Lucy-Bruce Gardner, Bruno Diaz, Bart, Hajduk, Thomas Houlihan, Jack McGarrity, Keziah Mornin, Elisa Terrenera, and Dylan Williams\\n\\nAbout SET’s Associate Members Programme\\n\\nThis exhibition is presented as part of SET’s Associate Members Programme, which offers artists studio space alongside access to project spaces and opportunities to independently curate exhibitions, workshops, and events.\\n\\nThe programme supports a wide range of practices, from performance and installation to music, sound, print, and textiles, and is designed to provide space, visibility, and development opportunities for early-career and underrepresented artists working in London.\\n\\nPoster image: Elisa Terranera (@elisaterranera)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://setspace.uk/event/trojan-horses-set-vauxhall-exhibition/2026-04-09/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":212,\"name\":\"Doublewalker\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-09T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fe8e5bb26e659a7537a1cc34564069ed.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Doublewalker explores processes of repetition and fragmentation, and the differences that emerge through them. Taking its title from the etymology of ‘doppelgänger’, meaning ‘twin stranger’, the exhibition considers how objects and spaces can appear familiar while remaining slightly out of reach.\\n\\nBringing together seven artists working across sculpture, installation, and sound, the exhibition is curated by SET studio member Laura Higgins and presented at SET Vauxhall.\\n\\nAbout the exhibition\\n\\nUsing processes of fragmentation and remaking, Doublewalker examines the presence of distant yet recognisable symbols within contemporary culture. Through this, works repeat and rework familiar forms, drawing attention to the small differences between things that might at first appear the same.\\n\\nAcross the exhibition, artists explore personal relationships with place, often focusing on sites that might otherwise go unnoticed.\\n\\nPresented as one of the first exhibitions in SET Vauxhall, Doublewalker responds directly to its surroundings. As a repurposed building shaped through reuse, elements of its previous life remain visible. Through site-specific installation, the exhibition nods to these prior uses and the building’s existing structure, while giving it a new identity within the exhibition.\\n\\nThe exhibition also focuses on the spaces between objects and how we experience them alongside others. By repeating and breaking down forms, the works invite us to look more closely at objects and environments as their meaning begins to shift.\\n\\nSome works also touch on wider themes including colonial histories, inheritance and self-positioning within the current postmodern context.\\n\\nThrough these approaches, Doublewalker considers how repetition and difference shape the way we understand objects, spaces and the world around us.\\n\\nA live performance by Nell Castor will take place on the opening evening at 7:30pm. The work imitates the selling of medicine, creating opportunities for interaction between the artist and visitors.\\n\\nEvent details\\n\\nOpening: Thursday 9 April, 6-9pm\\nDates: 10-26 April\\nOpening hours: Thursday-Sunday, 12-6pm\\nLocation: SET Vauxhall, Camelford House, 89 Albert Embankment, London\\nAdmission: Free\\n\\nContributing artists\\n\\nNell Castor\\n\\nNell Castor is a sculptor and digital artist. Her work is founded on a personal lexicon of color and symbolic characters that wrestle with universal human emotions. Originally from the San Francisco Bay Area, she now lives and works in London.\\n\\nWebsite: https://nellclo.com\\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/nell.castor/\\n\\nSuzanne Elven\\n\\nSuzanne Elven navigates time at an angle, often recording collision and motion from several temporal stand points. Her current focus lies in foregrounding objects that come into zones of impact – drums, tennis rackets. Elven’s research lies in the balance between fiction and reality, drawing from recent work in set building which has her considering the lifespans and solidity of worlds.\\n\\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/suzanne.elven/\\n\\nKairi Tokoro \\n\\nKairi Tokoro is a Japanese artist based in London. His practice explores sound, sculpture, and performance. His work focuses on the interdependence of objects and human life—how human interaction with materials alters their shape, color, and function, and in turn, how these changes affect us.\\n\\nWebsite: https://kairitokoro.com/works\\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/kairitokoro/\\n\\nLaura Higgins\\n\\nLaura Higgins is a sculptor and visual artist who documents an ongoing process-led inquiry into connecting material with meaning. Often interested in fabrication processes, ways of bespoke making and the sites that facilitate making, the findings around new processes are employed and reimagined to evoke contemplation around hidden sites and personal memories. \\n\\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/lhiggins1616/\\n\\nBeatriz Mayorga\\n\\nAt its core, Bea Mayorga’s art practice investigates the concept of the replica, exploring how copying can both transmit knowledge and act as a tool of cultural control by focussing on materials that are dismissed as “fake”, such as imitation marble, artificial tears and false gold.\\n\\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/beaamayorga/\\n\\nElena Garcia-Sirvent\\n\\nElena Garcia-Sirvent is a sound and video artist based in London. Her practice explores the intersection of sound, materiality, and perception. Focusing on how sound can interrupt, penetrate, and reshape both physical and psychological environments. Inspired by ‘Foley’, She references the reproduction of everyday sounds, how sounds can be reimagined, reproduced and displaced.\\n\\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/elegarciasirv/\\n\\nIsabel Jones\\n\\nIsabel Jones’ work converges painting and sculpture. Exploring personal and communal cyclical mourning rhythms. Integrating personified objects with the found and handmade. Archiving care, love, and death.\\n\\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/izzygj0nes/\\n\\nAbout SET’s Associate Members Programme\\nThis exhibition is presented as part of SET’s Associate Members Programme, which offers artists studio space alongside access to project spaces and opportunities to independently curate exhibitions, workshops, and events.\\n\\nThe programme supports a wide range of practices, from performance and installation to music, sound, print, and textiles, and is designed to provide space, visibility, and development opportunities for early-career and underrepresented artists working in London.\\n\\nPoster design: Isabel Jones and Suzanne Elven\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://setspace.uk/event/doublewalker-set-vauxhall-exhibition/2026-04-09/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":181,\"name\":\"Solidarity with Lebanon Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-09T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-09T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1cae61127e704266e0c1eaf75b795b41.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us Thu 9 Apr at Pelican House for an evening of food, music, dabke \\u0026 solidarity. Raising funds for displaced families and lifesaving supplies for Civil Defence first responders in Lebanon. Come together, connect in community \\u0026 build movement ties.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://opencollective.com/london-for-a-free-palestine/events/solidarity-with-lebanon-fundraiser-cab8d737\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":92,\"name\":\"Andøya Album Launch - Kit Grill\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-09T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-10T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"44acadd6fc34f5ca3563d5afc539a08b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Album Launch for Kit Grill's new album Andøya.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2390498\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":33,\"name\":\"Conjuring #2 ft. Laura Groves, Hinako Omori + more\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-09T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-09T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ae729655e144a58b92c704a5479d2306.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Conjuring is a monthly live improvisation series curated by Studio Njoku, and presented by Club Cheek.\\n\\nIt brings together leading experimental musicians for collaborative, improvised performances. The project foregrounds musical dialogue, community building and spiritual expression.\\n\\nEach show features a unique lineup of musicians performing a one-time improvisation around a motif developed by Tony Njoku.\\n\\nHinako Omori is a composer, musician and producer. Her music offers immersive sonic environments in which to process and access emotional states. Hers is music with spirit and awareness; inviting the listener to turn inwards. She has toured and collaborated with artists including Kae Tempest \\u0026 Shabaka.\\n\\nLaura Groves is a multi-instrumentalist and songwriter, exploring themes of inner-worlds, pattern, memory, healing and environments, mixing song and experimental synthesised sound and electronic layering. Her past collaborators include Actress, Sampha, \\u0026 Fabiana Palladino.\\n\\nMaxwell Sterling is a composer, producer, and double bassist. He's developed a distinct sound working with double bass and modular synthesisers, combining his interest in improvisatory jazz frameworks, orchestral music \\u0026 electronic sounds.\\n\\nKenichi Iwasa is an improviser and multidisciplinary artist from Japan. Also known for his Krautrock Karaoke night, he has collaborated with musicians such as Beatrice Dillon, Tyson \\u0026 Linder Sterling\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/k69k68-conjuring-ft-laura-groves-hinako-omori-more-9th-apr-club-cheek-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":130,\"name\":\"24 Hour Cinema - Drop In Anytime (12PM-12PM)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7be7daa7342225cb391ef780c5af03a0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"24 Hour Cinema is a continuous, drop-in moving-image programme running for a full day and night in London.\\n\\nRather than operating as a series of discrete screenings, the event functions as a shared viewing environment. Films and video works are encountered at different hours and in shifting states of attention, as audiences arrive, leave, return, and re-enter the space across the 24 hours. The focus is on duration, rhythm, spectacle, and surprise — and on what becomes possible when cinema is allowed to exist beyond conventional schedules and expectations.\\n\\nCurated by Double Wonderful, the programme brings together some of the most exciting, innovative, and rarely seen moving-image work from around the world. The intention is to make full use of the 24-hour window: no hour is treated as secondary, and no time is wasted.\\n\\nRather than defaulting to slow or punitive installation-style presentation, 24 Hour Cinema foregrounds work that actively engages viewers. Films are selected for their energy, imagination, and ability to hold attention — even, and especially, overnight. The aim is not endurance for its own sake, but immersion: a cinema experience that remains alive at 3am as much as it does at 3pm.\\n\\nAudiences are free to drop in for minutes or hours, to leave and return, or to encounter work unexpectedly in the early morning. The atmosphere is calm and welcoming, designed to support collective viewing at unusual hours.\\n\\nThe event is free to attend and staffed continuously throughout the 24 hours, with professional security and overnight supervision in place. Audience wellbeing and responsible use of the space are prioritised at all times.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/24-hour-cinema-drop-in-anytime-12pm12pm-tickets-1984064386991?aff=DWIG\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":186,\"name\":\"The Judgement Hall Festival 2026\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-12T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3f15a6a3256f4e47d992b09d48f4ee44.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Judgement Hall Festival returns this April for three days of site-specific performance across sound, movement, and cinema. Presented as a once-yearly gathering, the festival brings together artists whose work is shaped by architecture, duration, and attention\\n\\nThis year’s programme deepens the festival’s curatorial focus through close collaboration with artists working at the forefront of experimental sound, choreography, and film. Each performance is developed in direct response to its setting, resulting in works that exist only within the conditions of this edition.\\n\\n\\nAcross two sites — St Barnabas and Rio Cinema — the festival unfolds as a sequence of distinct encounters. At St Barnabas, artists engage directly with the building’s scale and acoustics, transforming the space anew with each performance. At Rio Cinema, film and sound converge through special presentations and commissioned live scores, experienced through focused, seated listening\\n\\nDay 1 at St Barnabas Church\\n\\nNYX\\n\\nThomas Stone presents 'The Shunned Path'\\n\\nDay 2 at St Barnabas Church\\n\\nAbul Mogard presents 'Quiet Pieces'\\nPaper Bridge Dance Company \\u0026 RV present 'Raptures'\\nB.O.R present 'DISSECTION / DISSOLUTION'\\n\\nDay 3 at Rio Cinema\\n\\nNeptunian Maximalism Live Score of 'The Legend of Suram Fortress' (Special Restoration)\\nGazelle Twin \\u0026 NYX:Deep England - A performance film by lain Forsyth and Jane Pollard\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/thejudgementhallfestival/2050364\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":27,\"name\":\"Vespers present: Shell Company live\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c36f46066fae97e2694ce1cb3218627a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A special live into club extended session from Vespers\\nTwinning with Glasgow via Manchester\\nDark and dubbed out sounds to move erratically to\\n\\nShell Company live\\nWeird Weather live\\n12th Isle DJ\\nJay Duncan DJ\\n\\nNowhere is safe but know you are among friends, don’t settle.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2368759\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":161,\"name\":\"General Echo w/ The Reggae Locksmiths\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"151416502ddd066de77263a877d5eebd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Monthly reggae disco held in a beautiful old school social club, with a friendly inclusive crowd. This month we're delighted to welcome The Reggae Locksmiths aka Andy Smith (formerly the DJ for the legendary Portishead) and 7Locks (Flashback Records). They will be providing the dancers of Walthamstow with an evening of classic JA sounds to make you move - expect ska, rocksteady, dub, roots, dancehall and all points in between. £7 entry or £5 if you're a Trades Hall member. No advance tickets, just pay on the door (cash or card).\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":171,\"name\":\"The Big Jamaica Fundraiser: supporting the communities of Clarendon\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"31146007f5082c0916c18c1f7a3f3abc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Reggae Music brings us together for a good cause 🙏\\n\\nDon’t miss this massive event with top artists in support of the community of Clarendon through the aftermaths of the Hurricane Melissa.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":29,\"name\":\"The Return Of Timehri W/ Tim Reaper, Dwarde, DJ Chromz, Lady Passion, Moodswing, T Dunn, BP\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b903987eabde0875ea6155ddde46142b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The return of Timehri ina 2026 style!\\n\\nStrictly vinyl all night long\\n\\nTicket not required for entry. Early arrival recommended.\\nEntry subject to capacity\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":185,\"name\":\"Peace Militia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"113ff31c5762e0ccf22aefc91d4e0ecb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Militia assemble for a night of chug, leftfield and deep dancefloor sounds. Welcoming over Berlin based Courtney \\\"Chug Lord\\\" Bailey along side of some of London's best up and coming selectors. Expect the unexpected and dress to sweat!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2387642\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":221,\"name\":\"Koshari x Red Laser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"45262f849011b1ef3a8a8dc6a2e4dcdb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We’re unbelievably happy to be teaming up with Manchester’s Red Laser Records for our first official dance of 2026. Joining us are Pharaoh Brunson and Kickin’ Pigeon - Red Laser top brass and hands down two of the finest DJs in the North West.\\n\\nIf you’ve heard anything about Red Laser’s legendary residency at the White Hotel over the previous seven years you’ll know why we’re so excited about this one. It’s one of (if not the) best parties in Manchester, welcoming the likes of Franz Scala, Make a Dance and Hysteric to Salford’s greatest former MOT garage - alongside a roster of phenomenal residents.\\n\\nThe party is so good in fact that Trigger Happy got a bit too excited at the Christmas do in 2024, sacked off his 5am coach home and carried on dancing until the sun came up. It cost him £120 in train fares, a three day hangover and he still says it’s the best clubnight he’s ever been to.\\n\\nWe’ve been planning this link up for a while and it’s going to be a belter. Tickets will fly out, so don’t sleep!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2391130\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":254,\"name\":\"Koshari x Red Laser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-10T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4428291c515841edc32cf084b5868ee7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We’re unbelievably happy to be teaming up with Manchester’s Red Laser Records for our first official dance of 2026. Joining us are Pharoah Brunson and Kickin’ Pigeon - Red Laser top brass and hands down two of the finest DJs in the North West.\\n\\nIf you’ve heard anything about Red Laser’s legendary residency at the White Hotel over the previous seven years you’ll know why we’re so excited about this one. It’s one of (if not the) best parties in Manchester, welcoming the likes of Franz Scala, Make a Dance and Hysteric to Salford’s greatest former MOT garage - alongside a roster of phenomenal residents.\\n\\nWe’ve been planning this link up for a while and it’s going to be a belter.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2391130\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":159,\"name\":\"PolyDub Sound System w/ Floor Length Skirts, Inner Totality \\u0026 Nangi, JANDEM, Jelly Records, Mihnea\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-11T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-12T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8531a07708073093047c1569e27f5b19.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The time feels right, the scoops are rolling, the sound is coming out again. We’ll be welcoming the spring with an all-day-into-the-night journey, surrounded by both old and new faces. It shall be a slow start moving into more frenetic scenes as we reach an unknown peak.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":128,\"name\":\"Chalk Hands - \\\"The Line That Shapes The Coast Of Us\\\" Release Show\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3daa844468ea09f8c8dc81800f8be25e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nChalk Hands\\n\\\"The Line That Shapes The Coast Of Us\\\" London release party\\nCelebrating a new album from the Brighton skramz team, releasing 27/3 on the legendary Dog Knights Records\\n\\n+ support from\\nDeath Of Youth\\nNew emotional hardcore from London\\n\\nHemiptera\\nString-enhanced stadium crust\\n\\nElentári\\nNew quiet/LOUD from members of Battle Of Wolf 359 and Kias Fansuri\\n\\nSaturday 11th April\\nPiehouse Co-Op, nearest stations Deptford or New Cross.\\n\\n£10\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/chalk-hands-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":233,\"name\":\"THE3KAYAS + Luisa D Rozo + Nymity (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-11T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-11T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"11b3a344cc9a7b05919ead98a892b81f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For the first time we welcome THE3KAYAS, to sing on our cobbled floors her earthly lullabies, as well as screening her self-produced music video a.sassy.nation , a DIY short-film independently created alongside her daughter Akiko Bambi, telling the story of a quest to save the Sun and restore colour in the world\\n\\nOn the other hand, after a series of presentations of her latest solo at Bolding Gallery, Pie House Coop and Windmill Brixton, Luisa D Rozo brings her popstar fever dream performance La Barca to its last iteration; a physical performance within constellations of auto-biographical film, melancholic singing and soundscapes of \\n\\nThe evening will conclude with experimental sound London legend Nymity, bringing contemporary club culture into the premises\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"http://www.the3kayas-luisadrozo-nymity.gel.now\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":38,\"name\":\"Club Citrus: DJ Subaru, babyschön, Oh Henry, luvandula\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-11T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-12T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"74a70f58a94e50271e0a47099472823d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Club Citrus is back, returning to Unit 58 for our biggest party to date - and we’ve got something special lined up.\\n\\nWe’re delighted to welcome babyschön and her blend of sleazy rhythms, chuggy synths and leftfield energy. A weekly fixture on NTS and a trusted presence at DIY spots and festivals alike, she moves easily between house, new wave and weirder corners.\\n\\nAlso gracing the Club Citrus decks is DJ Subaru, Leeds-based DJ, producer and party-maker behind Pleasuremaxxx. With a background spanning underground club culture, production and label work, Subaru’s sets are expressive, deep and full of feeling.\\n\\nExpect curiosities across acid house and electronica from resident Oh Henry, alongside the deeper, hypnotic sounds of luvandula. Known for their celebrated o:rbyss events and mix series, luvandula delivers emotionally tuned selections spanning ambient, deep house and techno.\\n\\nClub Citrus is a space for everyone. We will not tolerate any form of racism, homophobia, transphobia, sexism, ageism or harassment. Respect the space, the artists, the staff and your fellow dancers.\\n\\nSee you on the dancefloor.\\n\\n–\\nHenry Everett is supported by the Early Career Promoter Fund which is\\nmanaged by PRS Foundation and funded by Arts Council England using Supporting Grassroots Music funding from DCMS.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2362111\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":118,\"name\":\"WORMHOLE (Day Party)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-12T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-12T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5cf8f6dace3b1f81dfd421448358d7bb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hi Worms, WE ARE BACK with the third edition of WORMHOLE.\\n\\nWe are back on Sunday 12th April for a very chic, very exclusive WORMHOLE day party.\\n\\nGET UR TICKETS WHILST THEY HAWT!!!\\n\\nThis edition we’ll be joined by a special visitor; Macadam resident travelling from across the pond, alongside them is the people’s poisonous princess, as well, we have an NTS resident who’s monthly show is a big ole work out, and finally… a superdoooper exclusive live performance from your fav drugless goblin all the way from Leyton!! wow!! (Full line up will be announced the week of the pardddy)\\n\\nTickets are available thru RA\\nTime: 12PM - 10PM\\nLocation: Hackney Wick (exact location announced the day before)\\n\\nSee you for a daytime dance on the 12th April, this one’s gonna get nastyyyyyy!!\\n\\nAccessibility information:\\n\\nPlease note that this event takes place on the third floor of an old building with no lift access.\\nUnfortunately, this means the space is not wheelchair accessible (if you want to chat further about this please email us/DM us).\\nThere are also no accessible toilets on site.\\nWe will not be using any strobe lighting, and haze will be kept to a minimum. If you would like to discuss access needs in advance, please feel free to reach out via Instagram DM (@wormholelondon)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2384634\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":72,\"name\":\"dance:music presents deep:listening with nono gigsta, rosamond martin and food by eli grom\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-12T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-12T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"70d64bac0d7306944f7056c11fd83de7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"what if the dancefloor was a space for deep listening? an experiment in club presence and dancefloor somatics with nono gigsta (dj), rosamond martin (movement facilitation) and eli grom (food), featuring a pauline oliveros sonic meditation.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/33702/dancemusic-presents-deeplistening-with-nono-gigsta-rosamond-martin-and-food-by-eli-grom\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":209,\"name\":\"SET 91 Open Series - A Patch Sunday Salon\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-12T16:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-12T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b8f12c2301c68d2ffcfdccbbe6d146a0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SET 91's next Open Series continues with 'A PATCH Sunday Salon', an exhibition and live programme led by PATCH, an interdisciplinary collective working across architecture, art and research. Bringing together works by the collective and its members, the exhibition explores diasporic experiences of the city and considers how architecture can be understood through alternative, community-led lenses.\\n\\nThe exhibition presents a retrospective of PATCH’s past projects alongside new work currently in development by the collective’s founders. Through sculpture, photography, publications and painting, the programme reflects on themes that have shaped PATCH’s practice to date, from food and the act of holding space to the evolving notion of home.\\n\\nAlongside the exhibition, the programme will include a live talk and Q\\u0026A reflecting on some of PATCH’s past projects, as well as a conversational salon returning to themes of home and holding space, asking how diasporic communities can be centred within fast-paced metropolitan environments in ways that are tangible, supportive and meaningful.\\n\\nWhy this matters\\nIn the context of ongoing gentrification, displacement and urban redevelopment, particularly in London, diasporic and marginalised communities are often disproportionately affected. This session responds to these conditions by opening up space for collective reflection and discussion.\\n\\nThrough participatory conversations, the event aim to cultivate an atmosphere of empowerment, collective consciousness-raising, and a way of learning how architecture might be perceived differently. \\n\\nWho’s it for?\\nThis session is open to artists, architects, spatial practitioners and those interested in the intersections of community, identity and the built environment.\\n\\nIt will be particularly useful for those exploring or developing work around:\\n\\n- Diaspora and urban experience\\n- Architecture and spatial justice\\n- Interdisciplinary and socially engaged practices\\n\\nWhat to expect\\n\\nThe session will include:\\n\\n- An exhibition of sculpture, photography and painting\\n- Interactive and installation-based work\\n- A live talk and Q\\u0026A with PATCH\\n- Salon-style discussions exploring themes of home and holding space\\n\\nParticipants will have the opportunity to engage with the work, contribute to discussion, and reflect on shared experiences and ideas.\\n\\nWhat you’ll takeaway\\n\\nParticipants will leave with:\\n\\n- Insight into PATCH’s interdisciplinary approach to architecture and art\\n- A deeper understanding of diasporic perspectives on the city\\n- New ways of thinking about space, community and belonging\\n- Opportunities for discussion and connection with others\\n\\nEvent details\\nDate: 12 April\\nArrival: 4:30pm\\nSession time: 5-7pm\\nLocation: SET 91, 91 Tabernacle Street, Old Street, London, EC2A 4JN\\n\\nThis event is free to attend and open to all, although attendance from early-career artists and practitioners is particularly encouraged.  \\n\\nAs places are limited, we kindly ask that you only book if you are able to attend so that others who would benefit from the session are able to take part. \\n\\nIf you can no longer attend, please contact us at ninetyone@setspace.uk to cancel your ticket so the space can be offered to someone else. \\n\\nAbout the facilitator\\n\\nTeshome Douglas-Campbell is an architectural designer, journalist, artist and educator, and co-founder of PATCH. His practice spans architecture, journalism and fine art, with a focus on the built environment and its social and cultural dimensions.\\n\\nInstagram: @patch_collective_ \\n\\nAbout SET 91 and the Open Series\\n\\nThis session is part of the SET 91 Open Series, a programme of talks, workshops and discussions supporting artists in navigating, developing and contextualising contemporary practice.\\n\\nSET 91 is SET’s contemporary arts gallery on Tabernacle Street in Old Street, providing a non-profit platform for early-career and underrepresented artists to develop and present new work through exhibitions, performances and public events.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34835/set-91-open-series-a-patch-sunday-salon\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":248,\"name\":\"Two.Five is Coming to London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-12T17:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-12T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"821afc8d49e95994750f5bb98d0ee7b4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Two Five analog short film competition: Live from London\\n\\ncome through on April 12 as we take over @piehouse.coop for an intimate evening of film, live performance and music, all in celebration of Two.Five, Egypt’s first Super 8 short film competition.\\n\\nafter a celebrated premiere at Cairo’s Zawya Cinema, we’re super excited to bring a curated selection of standout works to London for a rare big-screen showcase. Honouring the unfiltered spirit of these films, we’ve programmed a stacked live line-up of artists and DJs whose work mirrors this commitment to heritage and experimentation ✊🏾🫰🏾\\n\\nfeaturing:\\n@intibint\\n@fedzillamusic\\nSha3by Chic @koshari_fm\\n@zoefayaud from @disco.monde\\n\\n📍 Piehouse Workers Coop (Pies \\u0026 popcorn available!)\\ndoors at 5:45 PM, screening starts at 7pm shortly after a cassette tape set by Sha3by Chic\\ntickets @ £12 (Low income/Pay What You Can options available).\\n\\nmore info \\u0026 tickets available via link in bio.\\n\\nbrought to you by Andrew Awad, Ishy Pryce-Parchment \\u0026 The Two.Five Team. 🐝🫶\\n\\nfor discounted/free tickets or donation inquiries, please contact andrewlthr@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/two-five-live?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\\u0026utm_id=97760_v0_s00_e0_tv3_a1dennhazrln96_tp1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":136,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Unsane, \\\"Occupational Hazard\\\"\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-13T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-13T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"19e5d92b1e3ed3ca5c6071ce72cf4c76.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nUnsane\\nLegends of twisted, destructive noise rock, shaking the foundations of New Cross Inn for the first time\\n\\n+ support from\\nSuplecs\\nNOLA Power Trio\\n\\nChurch Of The Rat\\nApocalypse death punk\\n\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£20\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":155,\"name\":\"Screaming in the Dark\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-13T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-13T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e41be1f76b571dbc0b2856d2eb53c3b6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"It’s time to scream.  In ecstasy and agony, meaningfulness and meaninglessness, reaching and giving up.\\n\\nFrom the Dada sound poems of the early 1900s to haunting AI glitches of today, In The Dark has been rummaging through the sound archives, bringing together radio, podcasts and audio art that explore the human voice. What happens to our voices when they become recorded sound? From engraving them onto wax cylinders to digitising and cloning, can we still find the spirit of play that first prompted us to press record, cut tape and see what we got?\\n\\nThis event is curated by In The Dark’s Sarah Frosh and Nina Garthwaite.\\n\\nSarah Frosh is a London based producer with a background in anthropology. Working across  audio, research and music radio, Sarah’s drawn to the strange and unifying heart of what makes us human. \\n\\nNina Garthwaite is a multimedia artist whose work is deeply rooted in sound, with branches extending into the visual arts. Nina started In The Dark and she also teaches creative audio. She likes making weird things with silly people. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34595/screaming-in-the-dark?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\\u0026fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQMMjU2MjgxMDQwNTU4AAGn8rDV9ntVa00cIJr39fhkkP_3Nvx1SlMXZ3rxWBO4ZPQQexWfeWZaZCqAKzU_aem_Ly9Lc81zymuyH2i2X7GGQQ#anchor\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":97,\"name\":\"Bianca Scout and Elena Isolini (Daughter Mary) Dance Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-14T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-14T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2bc899c413acef5afc8aa5df07af61b2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Bianca Scout \\u0026 Elena Isolini (Daughter Mary) will be offering a workshop to develop “Act 1” of their next project. Daughter Mary began as accessible ballet workshops that were held weekly at SET Lewisham between 2018-2020. As long term collaborators across music, film and dance - Bianca \\u0026 Elena are now in the process of writing and workshopping “Anon’s Ballet” together. With Bianca’s background in dance and Elena’s background in film, together they approach storytelling through gestural and emotive group work. The movement blends classical ballet technique with unrestricted gestures while exploring scene making and character study. No previous dance experience required. \\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026. \\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary. \\n\\nN.B The venue is not accessible, the studio is up two flights of stairs. \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":262,\"name\":\"Fundraising Evening for St Mungo's\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-14T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-14T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"079ceaf0bab0e9823de7829de3e942da.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An evening of songs and improvised electronics, fundraising for St Mungo's homeless charity\\n\\nSt Mungo’s purpose is to end homelessness and rebuild lives. In the midst of some of the highest levels of homelessness and rough sleeping on record, we are needed more than ever. Last year we supported 26,012 people who were homeless, or at risk of it. Of these, 10,240 were people supported by one of our 14 outreach services. We ran 138 services in total, in London and across the South of England. Our work means we were able to provide somewhere safe to stay to 2,183 people every night.\\n\\nVal Cheesbrough is an alternative singer-songwriter, playing a mix of folk, math rock jazz and electronica. Drawing on inspirations from the real world as well as fiction and myth, his music aims to explore moments from the past alongside close examinations of modern day life.\\n\\nWaltzing:\\n\\nFormed of guitarists Valentine Cheesbrough, Daniel Fawcett-Tuke, and saxophonist Oskar Jones, the trio present music that blends their shared interest of jazz, electronic, and folk into soundscapes of musical amalgam that seek to temporarily transport listeners to places that are simultaneously present and distant.\\n\\nTheir influences include Floating Points, Nala Sinephro and Oneohtrix Point Never.\\n\\nCorin Veitch :\\n\\nLoves writing weird folky music about his family, places he’s been and hasn’t, politics, and made-up stories. His main influences include Randy Newman, Blake Mills, Big Thief, Sam Wilkes, Nina Simone, and many more.​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​\\n\\nJames Józef:\\n\\nMulti-instrumentalist, producer, and alternative-folk artist, James Józef weaves intimate, lyrically rich songs that explore vulnerability and introspection. Influenced by the likes of Joni Mitchell, Jeff Buckley, and Blake Mills , his sound is both timeless and contemporary, built on poetic songwriting and delicate arrangements. Recently attracting the attention of Sony Music Publishing and Decca, Józef is a name to watch for fans of emotionally resonant, genre-crossing folk.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/fundraising-evening-for-st-mungos-the-muddy-puddle-tickets-1985769353592?utm-campaign=social\\u0026utm-content=attendeeshare\\u0026utm-medium=discovery\\u0026utm-term=listing\\u0026utm-source=cp\\u0026aff=ebdsshcopyurl\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":230,\"name\":\"Analogue Animation Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-14T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-14T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6c33cc4623e5e16e3aadf7bdd5c50488.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Get creative in this introductory class to analogue/hand-made animation. All materials are provided, you just need your phone!\\nAll are welcome at this new series of analogue and print animation workshops with director Miranda Peyton Jones.\\nEach session, learn, experiment and have fun with different hands-on animation techniques! A space to try out new ideas and meet fellow experimenters. Expect to come away with a piece of moving image and your printed materials.\\nNo previous animation or drawing skills necessary, all are welcome.\\n\\n14th April:\\nThis class we will be using charcoal to create hand-drawn animated pieces.\\n\\nFor this workshop you will need a smartphone and the free app 'Stop Motion Studio'.\\nDownload prior to the workshop.\\nUnder 18s are welcome, but must be acompanied by an adult.\\n\\nIf you can no longer make the event, please reach out to mirandapeytonjones@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://14APR-analogueanimation.eventbrite.co.uk\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":98,\"name\":\"Zahra Van Nguyen Dance Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-15T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-15T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"08dfbb27552d33819ef3525218cda512.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Zahra Van Nguyen is a London-based choreographer and movement artist\\nspecialising in somatic and improvisational techniques. A graduate of Rambert\\nshe follows a strong foundation in classical ballet, training with ENB, Central\\nSchool of Ballet, Conditions Studio programme and then performing at ICA,\\nLondon Performance Studios, Ormside Projects, Turner Contemporary and\\nmore. Her performances merge storytelling through anatomy and pop culture\\nreferences, reimagining the communicative boundaries of movement through\\nexperimental, durational work that explores the body as a site of memory,\\nresistance, and transformation. Featured in Dazed 100, her work challenges\\ntraditional dance boundaries, prioritising embodied feeling over clean\\ntechnique while maintaining an intimate, politically charged, and spiritually\\nraw voice.\\n\\nZahra also works as a movement director collaborating across music, fashion,\\nand editorial with artists like Zukovstheworld, Bass Victim, Tohji and\\nVarg2™M, contributing to visual campaigns for Shayne Oliver Group, Nike,\\nIssey Miyake and more.\\n\\nBODY SONGS: LYRICISM AND DRAMATIC STRUCTURES IN SOMATICS \\n\\nThis workshop aims to explore and dissect the nature of movement as a self narrative tool and examine how adjacent it is in relation to dialogue, text, imagery and sound. We will practice improvisational techniques to explore how movement can be used as a narrative tool in different layers, not miming but embodying feelings, textures and atmospheres. We will practice composing images but through a somatic\\nlens. The structure of internal narrative, tone, focus, rhythm and texture are some of the many layers that we can explore through moving. We will experiment with text and score and the absence of it to enable us to play with building images and scenes in different ways using a range of exercises.\\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026. \\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary. \\n\\nN.B The venue is not accessible, the studio is up two flights of stairs. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":99,\"name\":\"Mya Cavner x Ballet for Non-Dancers Dance Workshop \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-16T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-16T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"75f417752797e65bff96a270ec82bc5f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Mya Cavner is a movement artist, curator, and 1/2 of Ballet for Non-Dancers. She also runs Movement at SET, which are open level dance sessions every other Sunday in Peckham. \\n\\nBallet for Non-Dancers is a collaboration by South-London based artist duo Edith Liben and Mya Cavner recontextualising who can call themselves a dancer through performance, workshops, and text.\\n\\nBallet for Non-Dancers invites you to explore the art of seduction. In this workshop we will explore using intentional movement to explore how to be present in our bodies and what it means to share that with others. Through collective and solo tasks, dancers are offered the space to reconnect with their inner sensuality and redefine what ‘sexy’ is to them.\\n\\nExpect hip swaying, mental stimulation, body rolling, hairography and much much more; we’ll work through all parts of our body - finding comfort through vulnerability in our skin.\\n\\nHeels, leg warmers, leos, lace, \\u0026 spandex are more than welcome! Come ready to strut your legs and stretch your minds… \\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026.\\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary.\\n\\nN.B The venue is not accessible, the studio is up two flights of stairs.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":134,\"name\":\"Don't Try / Chaos Reigns / Cage / Bullet + More\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-16T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5717638386de2a0c965b733019ff010a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life presents\\n\\nDon't Try\\nCanada's hardest, back for round 3\\n\\n+ support from\\nChaos Reigns\\nLondon mathcore party starters\\n\\nCage\\nSwiss hardcore freakmosh\\n\\nBullet\\nLondon new blood\\n\\nRabbithole\\nNew deadly hardcore\\n\\n\\nAfterparty downstairs in Stocks Bar ft. Erreurjean\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/_erreurjean_/\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£13\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/dont-try-2\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":287,\"name\":\"beyn-na-beyn presents Dissonant Echo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-16T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-16T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"898124b3c3f1fe8b2521862c3d434a61.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"an evening of listening and live performance to collectively channel our rage and find stillness in the communal\\n\\nbeyn-na-beyn presents Dissonant Echo\\nlistening to the sounds beyond,\\n\\nspiralling in sonic swells of the iranian santur,\\n\\nan exploration of the spaces in between,\\n\\na moment to let time melt away and tune in to the same frequencies\\n\\ndoors:18:30\\n\\nlistening Session: 19:00\\n\\nperformance:19:45\\n\\n@ Doomyoga \\n6 Sylvester Path, Hackney Central, London, E8 1EN, UK\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/beyn-na-beyn-presents-dissonant-echo-tickets-1986330583245?utm-campaign=social\\u0026utm-content=attendeeshare\\u0026utm-medium=discovery\\u0026utm-term=listing\\u0026utm-source=cp\\u0026aff=ebdsshcopyurl\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":120,\"name\":\"An Evening with Adele Bertei: No Wave Women \\u0026 Born in Flames, broadcast on Montez Press Radio.\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-16T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-16T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"71127e56304b12bb6423079fee7f7c80.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Adele Bertei didn't just witness the No Wave explosion; she helped ignite it. As organist for the Contortions and Brian Eno's assistant, she stood at the epicenter of a seismic cultural collision: punk fracturing into post-punk, Lydia Lunch screaming her first songs of rage, Kathy Acker rewriting the rules of fiction, Vivienne Dick pointing her camera at the edge of everything.\\n\\nHer memoir, No New York: A Memoir of No Wave and the Women Who Shaped the Scene (Faber\\u0026), finally tells the story that history forgot, of the boundary-breaking women who made No Wave possible. Nan Goldin's flash-lit portraits of gender fluidity. Kiki Smith excavating the mysteries of the body. Lizzie Borden tearing up cinema's rule book. Lizzy Mercier reinventing electric guitar rhythms. While mainstream culture wallowed in sexism and homophobia, these artists forged something fluid, fierce, and utterly uncompromising.\\n\\nJoin us for a night crackling with that same energy.\\n\\nThe evening opens with a reading by Adele, followed by a short musical tribute to Honey, her co-star in Born in Flames. A panel discussion on women in the No Wave movement follows, with Angela McRobbie, Amelia Abraham, and Adele in conversation, moderated by Emily Pope. The night closes with a screening of Lizzie Borden's landmark feminist film, Born in Flames, and a reception to carry the conversation forward.\\n\\nLine up:\\n\\nAdele Bertei is a musician and author. Her most recent book is No New York: A Memoir of No Wave and the Women Who Shaped the Scene (2026). Adele played a lead role in Lizzie Borden's Born in Flames, and was lead singer of the first out lesbian band, the Bloods. Her books include Peter and the Wolves (2020), Why Labelle Matters (2022), Twist: Tales of a Queer Girlhood (2024) and Sinéad O'Connor's Universal Mother (2025).\\n\\nAngela McRobbie is Prof. Emeritus at Goldsmiths, London and Fellow of the British Academy. Her most recent books are Ulrike Ottinger: Film, Art and the Ethnographic Imagination (2024) and Feminism, Young Women and Cultural Studies: The Birmingham Essays from 1975 Onwards (2024). Angela first met Adele in Birmingham in the feminist post-punk live music scenes. \\n\\nAmelia Abraham is a journalist and author from London. Her books include Queer Intentions: A (Personal) Journey Through LGBTQ+ Culture and her first edited photography book, Sex, Clubs, Dissent: Visualizing Queer Nightlife will be published in Spring 2026 by MACK Books.\\n\\nEmily Pope is a London-based artist working across film, sound, printmaking and writing. Her practice often takes the form of ongoing series, including The Sitcom Show (2016–), a “failed sitcom” documenting life under UK austerity. Drawing on experimental broadcast media, humour and satire, her work explores queer intersectional feminism, political rhetoric and class politics. Recent exhibitions include Ginny on Frederick; Quench Gallery; Karst; SARA’s; and Southwark Park Galleries. Her writing has appeared recently in Buffalo Zine, Elephant Magazine, Bittersweet Review, Sticky Fingers Publishing. She was an awardee of the LOEWE FOUNDATION / Studio Voltaire Award (2023–2025). \\n\\nMontez Press Radio is an experimental broadcasting and performance platform founded in 2018 with the goal of fostering greater experimentation and conversation between artists, writers, and thinkers through the medium of radio. This platform invites different corners of the art world to interact with each other in person and on air—a place where media finally meets flesh. We’re drawn to art that exists in the unexpected, the authenticity of sharing without a script, the sounds of ideas in the making, conversation that forgets there’s an audience. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34448/an-evening-with-adele-bertei-no-wave-women-born-in-flames-broadcast-on-montez-press-radio\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":251,\"name\":\"Competition + jb glazer + Megan Alice Clune @ Spanners [the bored fire album launch]\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"561f32f54e201c5824e5f80034172b50.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"glint music presents:\\n\\na triple bill of autotune, guitar, ambience and noise from Newcastle, London and Australia, to celebrate the release of Competition's new album 'the bored fire' out now on glint music.\\n\\nhttp://healthy-competition.bandcamp.com/album/the-bored-fire\\n\\nCompetition makes tender music about places and people, using sparse instrumentation and thoughtful field recordings to produce parts of a whole that tell u all about urself. New album 'the bored fire' alludes to a defunct shopping centre and the autotune balladry of Claire Rousay \\u0026 More Eaze's recent works.Previous releases include Pomme, also on glint, and Repetitive Music via Slip Imprint.\\n\\njb glazer is a producer and song-writer from london. His music focuses on emotional logic and tension, looking back through a digital history; using samples, guitars and loops to build something moving. Latest album Angel Repost was a Nina Staff Pick which was said to be a 'record full of cut-up alternative rock and low-bitrate sample collage experiments' and 'like being lost inside a virtual Hot Topic.'Previously releases include Cool Leather for glint, Ur K? for 33-33 and Compact Break for Them There. \\n\\nMegan Alice Clune is a musician, artist and composer based on Gadigal and Wangal lands. Her work explores the dynamic relationship between music, technology, the body and temporality through composition, performance and installation. In recordings described as ‘breathtakingly intimate’ (Bandcamp Daily) ‘visionary ambient’ (Rockerilla), and a 'pristine exercise in precise simplicity' (boomkat.com), Megan delicately balances an elemental tonal palette that is both sparse and emotionally rich.Over the past decade, Megan has presented work at major art institutions and experimental music venues across Australia, Asia and Europe, including Sydney Opera House, Art Gallery of New South Wales, The Substation (VIC), Institute of Modern Art (BNE), Silent Green (DE) and more. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":242,\"name\":\"Starter Car / Kissing Gate / New Hat\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-16T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9df6523dc590c6f540b7f2b81e875b39.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House presents three of South London's most exciting bands on a Thursday night in Nunhead.\\nStarter Car, fresh off the release of their new single 'Throwing Down' (Tapete Records), headline the evening. Support comes from Kissing Gate, whose 2025 debut album Funny Dream was one of our favourites of last year, and New Hat, who return to the stage with new material.\\nFour-piece Starter Car formed when songwriter Oisean relocated to London from Glasgow, bringing with him homeland influences (Belle and Sebastian, Teenage Fanclub). The result is country-influenced indie twang. Gig-hungry, the band were soon headlining cornerstone venues like Windmill Brixton, The George Tavern and Shacklewell Arms. This year sees the release of their debut album, Afterlight, a hooky reflection on the beauty and struggles of life, out via Tapete Records.\\nKissing Gate are a 5-piece art rock band formed in south london in 2023.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/D3428fb8b161\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":276,\"name\":\"SKIP THE WARMUP\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-16T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-17T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2a50a895faa99761943da068a8fdc12b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Coming out of London's blossoming Chicago Footwork Scene, this is a dancefloor-centric Thursday throwdown designed, on every level, to make you MOVE.\\n\\nThis is a passion project of friends \\u0026 family from top to bottom - we just happen to be friends with some of London's best DJs and performers (and we're saying that without any bias).\\n\\nHailing from Spain and coming up on a meteoric rise in London, bass and booty sensation BRAVA will be performing LIVE, giving us tracks that have been released on prestigous labels like Moveltraxx and Up Ya Archives... If that means nothing to you, know that they're fucking bangers. Her live performance is the closest I've ever seen dance music come to hardcore punk, while her tunes traverse the whole spectrum of largely 160bpm dance.\\n\\nShe'll also be DJing for 15 minutes and there might be a Linkin Park cover in that as well, I'm not sure LOL\\n\\nWe have one of the best DJs I've ever had the pleasure of seeing spinning for us, THEMPRESS. An impossibly hard worker in the London scene, Thempress co-runs Voices Radio and is a founder of the infamous queer club night BUMPAH. Behind the decks, it's total wizadry - all that stops me from staring open-mouthed at their mixing are my convulsions, because there's much, much, much more to her breakbeat-centric sets than multi-CDJ trickery. It's unadulterated heat.\\n\\nSOHOTSOSPICY is a pillar of London's Chicago Footwork community and is a lazer-focused footwork DJ, capable of shelling dark and deep weaponry that can suck the air out of a room and replace it with sub-bass; in the same set she's capable of reaching into her hot-girl bag to bring out the cuntiest club tunes. Expect some original edits too, which made me scream when I heard them the first time...\\n\\nWe'll have CARMA bringing her multi-genre madness, centering on the Club tunes native to her Baltimore home and extending as far as pan-African dancefloor heat. She's a ridiculously talented and energetic DJ and you are invited - no, REQUIRED - to shake your ass.\\n\\nDJ!CR will be opening with a BATTLE SET, where we'll be pitching four of London's dedicated Chicago Footwork dancers head-to-head. In our preliminary friendly we'll have NIMA and CLASSTRAITOR in a straight no-frills battle, followed by a multi-round, judged bout between scene up-and-comers MALT BEVERAGE, whose jazzy and funky style is a delight, versus JOSEPH WOOD, whose singeli and kuduro-inspired style is enticing. Totally different styles, maximum heat. Get down for doors.\\n\\nTix on RA or on the door!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2392975\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":219,\"name\":\"THE PELICAN HOUSE SPRING PARTY: Celebrating SIX MORE YEARS of Pelican!!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-17T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-18T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7e622b31a3fcfffb63f85fc186b93064.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"🚩🌻🌷 CELEBRATING SPRING - AND SIX MORE YEARS OF PELICAN HOUSE !! 🌷🌻 🚩\\n\\nThis one’s extra xxxtra spesh... \\n\\n...We've secured six more years of Pelican House !!\\n\\nFrom our humble beginnings, we remain humble and beginning - but we're no longer being evicted in December! Join us in celebrating the future of pelican and the arrival of spring, with the eclectic sounds of...\\n\\nSpecial Guest (live set) - swampy squelchy modular madness - all will be revealed soon! 🐸\\n\\nJay Duncan - local legend and top disco masseuse! 🔮\\n\\n– Joy Collective residents Bill Odyssey, Ben Voyage and Rosy Ross\\n– big sound system \\u0026 live lighting wizardry from @auratekh\\n– cheap drinks lovingly served by our Pelican baes\\n– Safe Only CIC, our trusted peer-led welfare team, looking out for us\\n\\nAs always, the party is political. We’ll be supporting creation of new community spaces at Pelican House, as well as grassroots organisations working in London and beyond.\\n\\nThey'll be limited tickets on the door, No One Turned Away For Lack of Funds (NOTAFLOF!).\\n\\n🎉 !! EVERYONE IS WELCOME: BRING YOUR FRIENDS !! 🎉\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/pelicanhouse/2119040\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":211,\"name\":\"SET Stage Gallery – Softer/Harder\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-17T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3ccc3e14676dab91c82502a2764f1ae0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SET Social’s SET Stage Gallery presents Softer Harder, a performance night and exhibition examining female sexuality and desire.\\n\\nThe exhibition considers how women are reclaiming their bodies and sexualities in a digital-first world. Inspired by millennial and Gen Z adolescence shaped by nights on Omegle, reading erotica on Wattpad, and reposting lewd gifs on Tumblr, it offers an intimate and often humorous exploration of digital culture and sex.\\n\\nEvent details\\n\\nPublic opening night and performance: Friday 17 April, 6-10pm\\nExhibition run: Saturday 18 April – Sunday 19 April, 2-8pm\\nLocation: SET Stage Gallery, 55a Nigel Road, Peckham, SE15 4NP\\n\\nTickets:\\n\\nEarly Bird – £6.13\\nGeneral – £8.30\\n\\n\\nExhibiting visual artists\\nAarony Bailey\\nAarony Bailey is a filmmaker and photographer based in South London. Through an honest and intimate lens, Bailey uses the camera to capture semi-autobiographical narratives surrounding femininity and sexuality, looking at the complexities of womanhood and the female body. Her honest and nostalgic explorations of intimacy, both platonic and romantic, invite the viewer to indulge in their own voyeurism, unpacking the nuances of shame and desire.\\n\\nShe materialises her work through the use of analogue film, specifically super 8, 16mm, and 35mm, as well as using various other vintage methods of image capture and production, such as polaroid photography and risograph printing.\\n\\nLily Bunney\\nLily Bunney is a London-based artist whose work explores the intersection of vulnerability and digital consumption. Bunney’s process and aesthetic is key to reading her work. Inspired by the interwoven history of the computer and the jacquard loom, her pointillist drawings play with the analogue and the digital; offering work which looks hyper-digital on the screen, and tactile in person.\\n\\nHer practice investigates how we construct and witness our own stories in an age of overwhelming narrative abundance, particularly examining the ways we use social media and popular culture.\\n\\nCharlie Henzi\\nBorn in 2001, Seattle, USA, Charlie Henzi grew up in the UK just outside of London. In 2023, she graduated from Central Saint Martins, UAL. She recently received her Masters in Contemporary Art Practise (2024) at the Royal College of Art. She is fascinated by images of women in popular culture, the gaze, the performed female, consumption and consumerism. After studying visual codes and language for years, she now creates works that draw directly from this and her personal experiences, that comment on the current zeitgeist.\\n\\nPerformance artists, readers, and poets\\nFopé Ajanaku, Tara Baukovic, Chloe Borthwick, Daisy Norris, Sabirin Osobole, Maricel Reinhard\\n\\nAbout SET Stage Gallery\\nLaunched in 2023, SET Stage Gallery is a volunteer-led, non-profit contemporary art space based at SET Social. The gallery prioritises artists with limited access to exhibition opportunities and supports a programme of monthly workshops, talks, screenings, reading groups, and exhibitions. All proceeds go directly to participating artists, supporting accessibility and sustainability within the space.\\n\\nCurator: Ayiesha Sankoh (@thereturnofshe)\\n\\nContact\\nFor questions, please email setstagegallery@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/set-stage-gallery-presents-softerharder-tickets-1985816762393\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":214,\"name\":\"AGAINST THE CLOCK: Ottomani Parker Nontet X Bint Mbareh\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-17T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-17T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ff579697daf20ba91712750db8c687a2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ottomani Parker is a band where it's hard to know where one number ends and the other begins.\\nWith Big Hands on samples, field recordings, rhythm, and fx, sounds are hallucinatory and effective. Yusuf Ahmed on the drums brings both fluidity and a trippy grid to the horns. Izz and Abraham Parker on Sax and trumpet, respectively, hold your hand through what seems to be a field of endless sunshine, buttery melodies bring you home. Buster Woodruff-Bryant on sax, whistles and an endlessly rebellious challenge bringing everyone onstage both together and apart. Hayato Takahashi resamples, bringing noisy responsive dynamic textures and historically informed observations on keys to the function - as you do. Phoebe Coco on the essential trinket line-up of special bells, curated keyboard sounds, a crunchy wooden collection of curiosities and environmental echoes. Bint Mbareh assembles the crew together at Vesper's for the first time - throwing in smoky vocals discounted for your ears only. \\n\\nWe really recommend you don't miss this special lineup of class-A bunnies. Big Hands was so excited he even hand drew the poster himself.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":20,\"name\":\"Near Field Communication 3.0\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-17T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-18T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b94ab2be7f122b4372caf477fd880c11.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"UK Garage All Nite Long\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":240,\"name\":\"Refractor On Tour: London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-17T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-18T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"63406845b5999a34bfb25caf22ca48ae.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"After the resonance of last year’s gathering, we return to London.\\n\\nWhat happened in that room stayed with us, the density of the sound, the closeness of the dancefloor, the sense that something real was unfolding beyond trends or formulas. It wasn’t just another stop on the map; it felt like a convergence.\\n\\nThis year, Refractor On Tour, London comes back to a bigger place, with a lineup that fully embodies the core frequencies of Refractor. Artists who move between fast techno, progressive trance, deep techno, psychedelic bass and dub-infused textures, not as genres, but as languages.\\n\\nWe don’t curate around hype. We curate around narrative, tension and release, shadow and light. Around that moment when the room locks into a shared pulse.\\n\\nExpect long blends. Hypnotic rhythms. Emotional arcs. A dancefloor built on trust and intention.\\n\\nOnce again, we gather, not to repeat what happened, but to push it further.\\n\\nSee you next April 17th\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2373083\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":158,\"name\":\"Acrylic Moves: Arch Party with DARNS \\u0026 Where's G All Night Long\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-17T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-18T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6aa00b2a4532f1a0578ab91b49a602f0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Our last party felt like we’d found a format that really works for us and the crowd we’ve developed. With that in mind, we’d like to present the first of two parties from us in 2026. Happening in a discreet and charming SW London arch, with Where’s G \\u0026 DARNS All Night Long.\\n\\nThese parties are how we channel our musical tastes, presenting ourselves and the people around us - and that’s how we intent to keep them. We’ve nothing but confidence that the gang will back what we’re going for, and enjoy this new space with us until the music stops.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2391393\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":279,\"name\":\"Acoustic State Of Consciousness w/ Viviana Caro\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-18T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-18T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"327a6133872516273611b88ea5ac2d33.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Iklectik is proud to announce a very unique event with doctoral researcher and sound artist Viviana Caro.\\n\\nThis is not a sound bath. Not a concert. Not a normal deep listening session. \\u2028\\u2028It's a 2-hour practice session, a communal container where sound is used as a technology to deliberately shift states of consciousness, comparable to those reported in psychedelic experiences, and then to understand how you can do it yourself.\\u2028\\n\\nViviana Caro's doctoral research sits at the intersection of neuroaesthetics, sound art, and consciousness studies. Her work focuses on how intentional listening in ritualistic contexts can induce altered states similar to those reported with psychedelics, no substances involved. Her methodology draws on empirical psychology, ethnomusicology, and immersive audio: a kind of work that usually stays within the walls of academic institutions.\\u2028\\n\\nOn the 18th of April, she opens her practice at Iklectik to two groups of twenty-five people. \\u2028\\n\\nA 2-hour session. Come ready to tap into sound differently.\\n\\nImportant notice: This event is not suitable for individuals with a history of serious psychological conditions (such as untreated psychosis PTSD, severe anxiety, or depression). It is also not recommended for those who are highly sensitive to loud sonic environments.\\n\\n20 places at £62 fees included\\n\\n5 underwage places - please contact info@iklectikartlab.com to secure\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/v3ybll-acoustic-state-of-consciousness-w-viviana-caro-18th-apr-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":264,\"name\":\"DOC'N ROLL: SPORTS BANGER X JEREMY DELLER\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-18T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99f562667d431e5d406527ed2b574bf9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Rio Forever: Opening Night launches the Rio Cinema’s 50th anniversary celebratory season of events with a special night combining film, music and Hackney’s creative spirit. At the heart of the programme is a community selection of films chosen by the Rio’s team, the people whose passion, knowledge and dedication have kept the cinema thriving for decades. Their picks reflect the eclectic tastes and independent ethos that have long defined the Rio. \\n\\nThe opening night centres around a unique party curated in collaboration with Jeremy Deller, Sports Banger and Doc’n Roll Films, three forces whose work shares a deep affinity with the Rio’s core values: community, DIY creativity and a lust for both grassroots subculture and counterculture. Together with the Rio's team, they will transform the space for a one-off celebration of radical creativity, outsider art, music and film under one roof. \\n\\nThe night reflects their shared commitment to DIY culture, subcultural storytelling and the local communities that shape contemporary art and music. Expect the unexpected - and see you in the dance.  \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://riocinema.org.uk/Rio.dll/WhatsOn?f=2383774\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":291,\"name\":\"Testo Hunkie: PROM\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-18T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0234efedcfb3f436ddefcc89965cc4de.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Love—but make it messy, sweaty, and collective.\\n \\n\\nFor one night, we’re rewriting the prom you deserved. Not the tidy, hetero fairytale—the real one: charged, chaotic, tender, awkward, electric. A prom where trans-masc joy takes centre stage, where devotion is loud, desire is shared, and the dancefloor belongs to us.\\n\\n\\n\\nWelcome to Testo Hunkie: Prom Edition—a love-soaked night of slow dances that turn feral, flirtations that last exactly three songs, and connections that might last longer (or beautifully don’t). Expect a room thick with longing, laughter, testosterone, glitter, and just a hint of emotional risk.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34565/testo-hunkie-prom?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":85,\"name\":\"Club Cheek x Spraoi Mór: Sound Metaphors DJs, Ellie Anderson, Residents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-18T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"def999e9dc89ccee26326a3d66a787b1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Club Cheek and Spraoi Mor join for a spring collaboration that's long overdue! The Dublin party starters and good pals come over to Brixton for an old fashioned rinse down and their bringing friends!  Sound Metaphor DJs based in Berlin are legends in the scene. From running their famed record shop full of odd ball oddities and left-field club sounds, their TV mix channel, podcast mix series and an array of record labels, sub labels and music outlets, they do it all. Over a decade promoting their own parties they are some of our favourite DJs and we are pumped to get them down to play on the rig for their Brixton debut.   After watching Ellie and Flash play B2B after Craig Richards late last year we knew we had to get her back again. Based in Bristol she is part of party crew Zen Arcade who run get downs with seriously killer line ups.   Supporting these are some of the best residents in the game, Dar, Holten, Narmy and OG.   See you all on the floor x\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2373640\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":205,\"name\":\"IRM x Ransom Note: Saeko Killy (Live) / Philipp Otterbach + more\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-18T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e0b4230bbb3810c9971b5d62f9973095.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Inner Rhythm Mysticism and Ransom Note are crossing swords to throw a series of intimate parties.\\n\\nSaeko Killy (Live)\\nPhilipp Otterbach \\nManuol Bone \\nTia Cousins\\n\\n\\nWe've invited Japanese producer Saeko Killy to perform live for the first time in London. Her 2025 release on Bureau B 'Dream In Dream' was pinned as one as The Guardian's top 10 experimental albums of 2025.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":166,\"name\":\"Out Of Body Pop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-19T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e6154b2e6c9f9cf2449ccdb94fbed1ee.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"'everyone given the space to be in full flow' - the Guardian\\n\\nhello friends! this is our seventh party, and our second party since we went through a whole feedback / research process and moved venue to HWK\\n\\nthe last event was so special, we're so excited to come back with an awesome lineup full of friends and family\\n\\nit's time to make out of body pop\\n\\n\\nDJ SET TIMES:\\n\\n12:00 HERNY -'ambient into electronica'\\n\\n13:30 Sophie Darling - 'from Cumbia to Kwaito'\\n\\n14:30 L KAE F - '90s US House \\u0026 proto-UK Garage' \\n\\n15:30 Jazzi Bobbi - 'all FLINTA electronic/ alt pop+'\\n\\n16:30 Shivum Sharma - 'soft + celestial club'\\n\\n17:45 kild - ‘fifth world electronics' \\n\\n18:30 Richie Reiter - 'Baile Funk+' \\n\\n19:30 Medallion Man - ‘Dubstep/Jungle Hybrids’ \\n\\n20:30 fin \\n\\n\\nArts Lineup: \\n\\nBanner-making workshop from Em-Dash (14:00-17:30)\\nTacit learning/ knotting from Laura Henry\\nImmersive visuals from Yuliya Zhevakina\\n\\nWHAT YOU CAN EXPECT\\n\\n(the link for our venue map and Instagram account is at the bottom of this page)\\n\\n1. a low-lit indoor Dancefloor with DJ sets, projected visuals and no flashing lights. Each set has a distinct sonic theme, see set times above!\\n\\n2.  a covered, outdoor Painting + Social Area paints and art tools provided for everyone, plus the guided, meditative sensory activity of knotting\\n\\n3. a bar with alcohol and non-alc options, plus pizza on sale inside the venue (inc vegan options) until 18:00 \\n\\n4. from 15:00 onwards we will have a Quiet area in the HWK cafe space, where you can paint or use one of our colouring-in books without conversation\\n\\n5. re-entry is allowed all day\\nHWK is 5 mins walk from the canal, if you want to literally touch grass then walk past Barge East\\nwe're also 10 mins walk from the V\\u0026A storehouse which is free and very cool\\n\\n6. genderless toilets and no-tolerance of harassment - we ask that you respect each other's space and think about those around you, especially if you’re a big guy with a loud voice like our founder Will!\\n\\n7. any profits from the event will go to Arts Emergency, a charity that helps young people from underprivileged backgrounds get into the arts\\n\\n…\\n\\nWe want to actively include people, and build a more ideal space for everyone, together.\\n\\nBeing neuro-inclusive doesn't mean that we're only focused on serving neurodivergent people or that we are fully accessible for everyone, but we will always work to improve the accessibility of OOBP in attainable ways as we develop. For a more deeply accessible, differentiated experience, we'd recommend checking out Disco Neurotico (for example, they run events with silent disco technology to avoid sensory overwhelm on the dancefloor)\\n\\nIf you have any questions for us in the runnup to the event, please message our @outofbodypop instagram account.\\n\\nOur music policy is wide but specific; we want to look forwards, exploring experimental but accessible sounds, music that’s fun and interesting, which you don’t tend to hear in clubs. Syncopated rhythms and big chords in all sorts of different forms.\\n\\nWe will be offering free paints and art tools for everyone to use, including a mix of white and pastel-coloured paper. \\n\\nWe are happy for you to take photos or videos, there will be lots of cute visual things to look at! We just ask that you keep it within reason (especially on the dancefloor) and the OOBP team will do the same; we have team members who we know are happy to be filmed, we won’t stand around at the side of the dancefloor filming everyone else or get up in their face with a DSLR when they’re dancing\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":253,\"name\":\"PARK\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-19T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8260d9ff8dd2e0d4d4d76634121bd33c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"IKLECTIK LIVE: PARK\\n\\nSunday, 19 April | 2-10pm\\n\\n‘PARK’ is a new event of Sunday daytime gatherings presented by IKLECTIK and curated by Atay Ilgun.\\n\\nEach event presents six unannounced live acts, punctuated by long, social intervals.\\n\\nLean into the afternoon, settle into the soft seating and soak in the summer sun, surrounded by urban wildflowers, the rhythm of passing trains, and graffiti.\\n\\nAll performing at IKLECTIK for the first time, we invite each artist to show up as their most present selves, free from the pressure of a traditional live set - whether sharing a demo made the night before, experimenting with sound, or exploring new ideas.\\n\\n‘PARK’ is a communal sanctuary - a safe space rooted in curiosity, surprise, genuine connection, and unfiltered expression.\\n\\nThis is a space for undistracted presence, so we maintain a no-phones policy. We invite you to leave yours in your pocket or bag as much as possible and simply soak in the afternoon.\\n\\nIf the ticket cost is a barrier, we offer a limited ‘no one turned away for lack of funds’ policy, please email atay@iklectikartlab.com.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/53br2w-park-19th-apr-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":250,\"name\":\"Free the Brize Norton Five Panel Discussion and Campaign Launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-19T17:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-19T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9edef2eeefb31441485b41373bd04d08.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us Sunday 19th April, 5:30pm at Palestine House for a discussion on British military complicity in the genocide in Gaza and state repression under terror legislation and National Security Act as the State kidnaps and imprisons activists without trial. \\n\\nPanelists include Matt Kennard, Dr. Asim Qureshi, T Hoxha and Nida Jafri. Chaired by Hamza Yusuf.\\n\\nFree the Brize Norton Five. Free all the prisoners. Free Palestine.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":225,\"name\":\"Puppet Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-20T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-20T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"115bb5f9a5e7e0c135932da648305e1d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Communal Clay Puppet Workshop\\n\\nUsing clay and slips you will be able to create a puppet, character, monster or creature. \\n\\nYou will be able to add colour and depth to your work with wild clay slips we have collected from around South London. And the option to have the piece fired and glazed with wood ash glaze.\\n\\nThe session will last 2 hours.\\n\\nTheses workshops will be more focused on the tactility of playing, practicing and learning  sculpture techniques. There is no pressure to make a ‘finished product’ or ‘perfect piece’.\\n\\nAt the end of the workshop if you wish to have your piece fired and glazed, we ask you pay an additional £10 to cover firing costs, glaze materials \\u0026 transport of your work. \\n\\nAny leftover clay at the end of the session will be recycled for future use, minimising wastage and keeping our workshops sustainable.\\n\\nPricing:\\nWe are updating our pricing scale, in an effort to continue to make our workshops accessible and affordable we are testing out a new ticketing format with two options: Standard and Concession tickets. \\n\\nPlease choose the ticket option that is appropriate for yourself.\\n\\nCommunal Clay CIC is a not-for-profit organisation, all profits made after covering core costs will be used to run more community workshops. \\n\\nConcessions Include: \\n-People receiving benefits Jobseeker's Allowance / Universal Credit / Housing Benefit\\n-Young people 16-21\\n-Disabled \\n-students from working class backgrounds \\n-carers \\n-single parents\\n \\nAll fired and glazed work will be ready to collect in roughly 4 weeks from SET Social, please be patient as the cold weather affects drying and firing times.\\nSometimes this may be longer or shorter depending on the weather and temperature as these effect drying speeds. \\n\\nPLEASE READ: Clay and ceramics are fragile materials until fired and glazed, on occasion things can break or become damaged during the drying and firing process', Communal Clay is not responsible for any damage that may occur during these. \\n\\nTickets are refundable if you message us 48+ hours in advance of the event date\\nRefunds - you will be fully refunded for the cost of the ticket but the booking fee will not be refunded\\nUnder 18's must be accompanied by an adult\\nCommunal Clay is not responsible for work that breaks during firing.\\nYour work must be collected within 4 weeks of being notified it is ready to collect from SET Social. After the 4 weeks unclaimed work will be given away.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":100,\"name\":\"Jules Cunningham Dance Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-21T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-21T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"234f9f77b63af61d4e1b446059ee2fac.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Jules Cunningham (they/them), originally from Liverpool, worked as an award-winning dancer for 20+ years with Merce Cunningham Dance Company and Michael Clark Company. \\n\\nJules founded Julie Cunningham \\u0026 Company in 2017, to create and present work that combines clarity of form with an interest in gender identity and the body. Jules uses movement language that draws on their technical dance training, expanding and queering it collaboratively, working between sound, text, visual art.  \\n\\nCreative work is informed by solo and collaborative movement exploration, queerness, lived experience of mental illness, disability and exclusion based on Jules’ working-class background and non-binary identity.  \\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026.\\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary.\\n\\nN.B The venue is not accessible, the studio is up two flights of stairs.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":135,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Insurgent / Prozpekt / The Burial Code / Paresthesia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-21T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-21T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"390bc1908361efdd7dbea7987a16cd3c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nInsurgent\\nBlastbeat emocore from France\\n\\nProzpekt\\nHeavy NEHC\\n\\nThe Burial Code\\nThree Swords Fury\\n\\nParesthesia\\nDeathcore youth\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross and New Cross Gate\\n\\n£12\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/insurgent-prozpekt\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":295,\"name\":\"Film Screening - Save Our Heritage by Winstan Whitter\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-21T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"70db6ff8670328f9d012803eb5005052.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Mildmay History Club is proud to host a screening of Winstan Whitter's film \\\"Save Our Heritage\\\".\\nThis follow-up documentary to Legacy in the Dust by Winston Whitter continues to focus on Dalston's significant Four Aces Club—once a vital cultural hub for London’s Caribbean community and a cornerstone of Black British music and social life. Building on the story of its closure and demolition, the film explores the campaign to save 4-12 Dalston Lane and how the loss of such spaces reshaped the community.\\n\\nBlending archival material with present-day voices, the film examines what remains, what has been lost, and how legacy endures beyond the physical landscape. It connects the fate of the Four Aces to ongoing struggles against gentrification, highlighting efforts to preserve cultural memory amid rapid urban change. It asks what it means to lose a place that held collective identity—and how that legacy survives in the people who refuse to let it be forgotten.\\n\\nJoin us for a special community screening followed by a Q\\u0026A with the director. Light refreshments will also be provided.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/film-screening-save-our-heritage-by-winstan-whitter-tickets-1986994863124\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":231,\"name\":\"Analogue Animation Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-21T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f4462c3b90d2a2e42ff3fb3ffc32ef53.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Get creative in this introductory class to analogue/hand-made animation. All materials are provided, you just need your phone!\\nAll are welcome at this new series of analogue and print animation workshops with director Miranda Peyton Jones.\\nEach session, learn, experiment and have fun with different hands-on animation techniques! A space to try out new ideas and meet fellow experimenters. Expect to come away with a piece of moving image and your printed materials.\\nNo previous animation or drawing skills necessary, all are welcome.\\n\\n21st April:\\nThis class we will be using paper cut-outs/collage to create animated pieces.\\n\\nFor this workshop you will need a smartphone and the free app 'Stop Motion Studio'.\\nDownload prior to the workshop.\\nUnder 18s are welcome, but must be acompanied by an adult.\\n\\nIf you can no longer make the event, please reach out to mirandapeytonjones@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://21APRanalogueanimation.eventbrite.co.uk\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":249,\"name\":\"GRAIN Presents: Tongue Depressor, Marija Kovacevic, Steve Noble + Caius Williams, Theodora Laird + Grace Black\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-21T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b2300a0e21a247b5407718afa1285c27.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"GRAIN is a concert series and archiving project for experimental and improvised music, largely happening within South Bermondsey, and programmed / produced by Caius Williams \\u0026 Theodora Laird.\\n\\nThrough programming and documenting new and adventurous music through collaboration, archiving, workshops, and performances, the project explores the ongoing dialogue between the transience of DIY art spaces and the communities that inhabit them. \\n\\n\\nTongue Depressor (New England, USA) is the duo of Zach Rowden and Henry Birdsey. They write and perform drone-based music with continually expanding instrumentation including bagpipes, double bass, pedal steel/lap steel, tape loops, harmonicas, organs, and bells. They tour regularly in North America, Europe, and the UK, and have released 30+ LPs, CDs, cassettes, and lathes on labels including No Rent, Astral Spirits, Xkatedral, Stoned To Death, Redscroll, Chocolate Monk, Full Spectrum, Dinzu Artefacts, Worried Songs, and Soundholes. Tongue Depressor maintains collaborations with a revolving door of third members including Austin Larkin, Weston Olencki, John McCowen, Jakub Battick, and Leila Bordreuil.\\n\\n\\nSerbian born, New York City based violinist Marija Kovačević works in classical, experimental and improvised music.\\n\\nHer project Music for Broken Violins is an exploration of sonic textures with broken violins, bows and their fragments. Marija has developed an idiosyncratic vocabulary of dragging strings, playing cracks, bowing broken bodies, wrapping loose hair and creaking pegs. In performance, there is a minimalist, ritualistic structure to her unembellished studies, as each instrument is approached in procession, with silence in between each visceral deviance from the accepted technical norms. In addition to four albums of solo work, broken violins also appear on Rainy Afternoon near Paris album with Thierry Müller, Push Broken Duet album with Romain Perrot (available on Chocolate Monk), Bez Vremena album with Paul Collins and Quentin Rollet (available on Astres d’Or) and most recently Playable Litter album with Theo Gowans (available on Scatter Archive). Marija’s fifth solo album is set for release this year on Relative Pitch Records.\\n\\n\\nSteve Noble is London's leading drummer, a fearless and constantly inventive improviser whose super-precise, ultra-propulsive and hyper-detailed playing has galvanized encounters with Derek Bailey, Matthew Shipp, Ishmael Wadada Leo Smith, Stephen O'Malley, Joe McPhee, Rhodri Davies and many, many more. \\n\\nIn the early eighties, Noble played with the Nigerian master drummer Elkan Ogunde, Rip Rig and Panic, Brion Gysin and the Bow Gamelan Ensemble, before going on to work with the pianist Alex Maguire and with Derek Bailey (including Company Weeks 1987, 89 and 90). He was featured in the Bailey's excellent TV series on Improvisation for Channel 4 based on his book Improvisation; its nature and practise. He has toured and performed throughout Europe, Africa and America and currently leads the groups N.E.W (with John Edwards and Alex Ward) and DECOY (with John Edwards and Alexander Hawkins). \\n\\n\\nTheodora Laird is a vocalist and multidisciplinary artist. Releases under her solo project ‘feeo’ have received critical acclaim. Theodora's practice has involved in tandem with an interest in situating narratives within freely improvised music, specifically through frequent involvement in the GRAIN residency.\\n\\n\\nGrace Black is an artist who makes sculpture, performance and music. Often this is as a part of duo Mosquito Farm who regularly perform across DIY venues in London and beyond.\\n\\n\\nCaius Williams is a musician from London who plays the double bass, guitar, and bass guitar. He works in collaboration with others, alongside various solo projects, often working with improvisation and explorations of resonance, and perception.   \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.thehorsehospital.com/events/grain-april21\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":243,\"name\":\"Joseph Futak + Wazdakka\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-21T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b7cd2f2f102a3997459adf5273a933d7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands is back for another special evening with legendary locals The PGs and Wazdakka. Not one to miss!\\n\\nJoseph Futak is a London based producer and artist, who's music quietly bridges the space between reflection, nostalgia, grief and the other spectres of human experience. His album 'Walking The Sea Wall' has a bleary eyed softness to it that recalls the moments between wake and sleep, past and present. While producing for many of London's most exciting acts, Joseph is slowly working towards the follow up record - a collection of songs that push further the corners of what was explored on 'Walking The Sea Wall', and will be debuting new material as part of this gig.\\n\\nWazdakka is Tom and Will, who are two guys having good times with big beats and drones.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/zcd376e3fcf4\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":296,\"name\":\"SOFT BODIES\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-22T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-22T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"14d7d5e7f015df7f39b4415c05b94a6e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sensuous soft bellied delusion. The romance of illusion. A temple of our own. The home.\\n\\nSubject to the state, external forces manifest themselves around a tense dinner table.\\nIn a perpetual cycle of use, the individual finds a vice to abuse. An escape. Middle class petrification, and mass pacification.\\n\\nTwo faces meet, two parallel mirrors, two adverse reactions: “Present” and “Absent”, our characters in this play.\\n\\nThese mirrors bounce images of reflection and projection onto one another.\\nSeeking a witness under the guise of “love.”\\n\\nThe omnipresence of absence itself, a looming god and toy for yearning satisfaction. There is no action in this piece, simply a battle of reactions.\\n\\nThe set is the gallery itself, with visual and performing artists feeding themselves and each other through atmosphere, compliance, and disruption.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2404974\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":255,\"name\":\"SKINSHIP\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-22T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-22T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":305,\"name\":\"Midori Jaeger – (Un)planted EP Launch + Ruta\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-22T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-22T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e102f4790b70b2f56bc6ad73fcfb4105.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Cellist, composer and vocalist midori jaeger launches her upcoming EP (Un)planted with a full-band performance in the intimate surroundings of St Pancras Old Church.\\n\\nmidori jaeger has toured the UK and Europe as a solo artist, with performances at Union Chapel, Queen Elizabeth Hall and EartH Hackney, and has travelled the world as a collaborative musician, appearing at Berliner Philharmonie, Royal Albert Hall, Barbican Hall and Royal Festival Hall. This show marks a special moment: an intimate unveiling of new music that brings her story, sound and band together in one space.\\n\\nBorn in Japan and raised partly in the UK, midori returned to Tokyo at sixteen before moving alone to London two years later. Each relocation was a replanting - a search for new soil. With family in Tokyo and New York and no fixed roots in the UK, she found her sense of home through music.\\n\\n(Un)planted is a musical painting of midori’s uprooting. Like the cello that was once a tree unplanted from its soil, the music depicts her own journey of uprooting through the multiplicities of mixed heritage, sexuality, growing up across different continents, partneredness, aloneness, to an eventual replanting and rootedness in the earth. (Un)planted is the first part of a two-part EP. The counterpart (Re)planted is due summer 2026.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/yo6qgx-midori-jaeger-22nd-apr-st-pancras-old-church-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":137,\"name\":\"Brokencyde \\u0026 Dot Dot Curve - Teach Me How To Scene\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-23T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-23T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e485c0d6a26d277a8d36f6a28f9b12b9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Be Sharp and Real Life present\\nBrokencyde \\u0026 Dot Dot Curve - the 00s crunkcore revival you never expected.\\n\\nSupport from Crostpaths \\u0026 Rebuilt Boys, bringing London queercore flavours to the sound.\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£20\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/brokencyde\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":318,\"name\":\"Library Transmission: Tunde's Film\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-23T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-23T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d83642c4f06bd22bd63efa0900c94e85.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This screening of Tunde's Film is the first event in the Notes from the London Commune series. \\n\\nThe evening will continue with an in-conversation with film directors Tunde Ikoli and Maggie Pinhorn, series curator James Elsey, and The Otolith Collective's Anjalika Sagar and Kodwo Eshun.\\n\\nTunde’s Film follows a group of youths in East London who decide to take matters into their own hands after economic turmoil and persistent police harassment. They form an armed cadre whose first objective is to rob a bank. The drama unfolds on the streets of Tower Hamlets as the racial and social faultlines of 1970s London are set to a Joan Armatrading soundtrack.\\n\\nNotes from the London Commune highlights moments from the pre-history of the liberation of London. The programme envisions the political imagination of black, proletarian, queer radicalisms as the seed, the soil and the star of a London yet to arrive.\\n\\nEach event presents a retrospective look at the histories of struggle in the city, from the vantage point of a near-future establishment of London's citywide workers' council. Each study session is hosted by a guest that brings selected texts from the Otolith Library into dialogue with Eman Abdelhadi and M.E. O'Brien's Everything for Everyone: An Oral History of the New York Commune, 2052-2072, and Peter Watkins' La Commune (Paris, 1871).\\n\\nDoors open at 5.30pm; event starts at 6pm and ends at 8pm.\\n\\nImage credit: Still from Tunde's Film, 1973. London Community Video Archive.\\n\\nThe Otolith Collective is supported using public funding by Arts Council England.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/library-transmission-notes-from-the-london-commune\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":270,\"name\":\"UNCOMMON\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-23T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a1af756cedd8ef624dabf470dd25c173.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"UAL Sound Arts BA YA3 Performance Event\\nIklectik, London, SE15 4ST\\n23rd April 2026\\nFree entry\\n\\nPerformance gathering for London College of Communication’s Sound Arts BA (Hons) Year Three students.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/avwab7-uncommon-23rd-apr-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":308,\"name\":\"CDR In Conversation with Shy One\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-23T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7a04a8f5697e238128a14edca5ba4c51.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Our current season of CDR Sessions continues with one of London’s most distinctive DJs and producers, Shy One, as we open a new chapter at our new venue, The Carpet Shop. For those new to CDR Sessions, each event includes an in-depth, production-focused interview with a guest artist, exploring their career and creative process. The talk is flanked by openCDR, where producers and artists of all levels and abilities have the opportunity to play their own music on some of the best club sound systems across the UK. All genres and styles welcomed!\\n\\nMali Larrington-Nelson AKA Shy One lives and breathes the eclecticism and diversity of her DJ sets and productions. Having started off DJing on pirate radio as a teenager, she has been influenced by the full spectrum of sounds her hometown of London has birthed and nurtured. Undeterred by those in the scene who called her beats “weird” or “different”, Shy One carved out her own sound, eventually catching the ear of Scratcha DVA, who released the Decaffeinated Love EP and her debut LP Bedknobs and Boomkicks on DVA Music.\\n\\nSince then, she has continued to grow into a somewhat undefinable sound that’s origins are undoubtedly London but take in a wide range of musical cultures, from hip-hop and jazz to house music and brokenbeat. With releases on Rhythm Section, Astral Black, Beats In Space and Apron Records, alongside a BBC Radio 1 Residency and NTS show, Shy One’s practice continues to evolve. Her latest album Mali, released on Touching Bass, further explores the lineage of Black British electronic music while reflecting her own history as a music lover growing up in London.\\n\\nJoin us for an in-depth conversation with Shy One, flanked by openCDR: your chance to bring along your works-in-progress and hear them played on The Carpet Shop’s sound system. We keep our events as accessible as possible, but if you are able, we would appreciate your support of CDR with a £5 donation ticket. Every contribution helps us continue creating space for producers and artists to connect, learn, and grow.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2407152\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":294,\"name\":\"Migrants’ Rights Network X Pomodoro Rosso Sangue X Pomo D’Orographies\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-23T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"01c4a162f3f403f0bb2f65ba49c39142.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a special evening reading of “Blood Red Tomatoes” and screening of “Pomo D’Orographies” followed by a discussion with campaigners from Migrants’ Rights Network.\\n\\n‘Blood Red Tomatoes’ is the recent book by Activist and militant Writer Diletta Bellotti, recounting how she initiated a nation wide advocacy campaign for migrants rights in 2019, intertwined with her experience staying at an informal settlement in the south of Italy for one month, hosted by the migrant workers.\\n\\n“Pomo D’Orographies” is a short film by Artist and Architect Francesca Paola Beltrame. The film exposes the connection of migration and trade of canned tomatoes between Italy and Ghana, layering animations and intimate conversations, to shed light on the multiple lifeworlds nestled within the tomato.\\n\\nThe presentations will be followed by a discussion together with Migrants’ Rights Network/campaigners and the attendees exploring topics of criminalisation across borders, campaigning tactics between Italy/UK and storytelling.\\n\\nThe event starts at 19 pm.\\n\\nBring your friends! Tickets are available online for 6£ or If ticket prices are a barrier, please email us at francescapaolabeltrame@gmail.com\\n\\nAll proceeds will go directly to Migrants’ Rights Network campaigns.\\nEvening hosted by Francesca and Diletta with the support of Migrants’ Rights Network.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/pomodoro-rosso-sangue-x-pomo-dorographies-x-migrants-rights-network-tickets-1987005823908\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":315,\"name\":\"BORN:FREE presents Veranda\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-23T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c688ad7905fd29c0bae8ec37a9e966c5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nBORN::FREE LDN presents VERANDA\\n\\nAn evening of sound, poetry, \\u0026 live experimentation. Expect an intimate, shifting space with a bit of serious dancing at the end!\\n\\nMA.MOYO (b. Zimbabwe) is a literary \\u0026 sound artist, author of Small Inheritances (ignitionpress, 2018), \\u0026 experiments with sound/text performance. Her works have been featured on various platforms including NTS, Boiler Room \\u0026 BBC Radio. Her debut album, a collaboration with Duncan Bellamy (Portico Quartet) was released under the moniker BZDB on AD93 Records (2024). Her debut solo EP is Viva Voce Vol.1 (Accidental Meetings, 2025); she’s currently working on her first full collection of poems.\\n\\nISABELLE BAAFI is the author of Chaotic Good (Faber \\u0026 Faber / Wesleyan University Press, 2025), which won the Jerwood Prize for Best First Collection, was shortlisted for the T. S. Eliot Prize \\u0026 longlisted for the Dylan Thomas Prize. Her pamphlet Ripe (ignitionpress, 2020) won a Somerset Maugham Award \\u0026 was a Poetry Book Society Pamphlet Choice. She edits at Poetry London \\u0026 Magma.\\n\\nNADEEM DIN-GABISI - storyteller working with music, poetry \\u0026 film. Nadeem's debut album OFFSHORE (Moshi Moshi) tackles themes of estrangement and identity with 'potent streams of consciousness'. Nadeem is 'inspired by Sierra Leonean pop music that is danceable despite the sorrowful lyrics...' OFFSHORE has received support from NPR, Fader (Best New Albums), The Quietus amongst others. Nadeem won the Fred Perry x Nicholas Daley Music Award (2021) \\u0026 is a former Somerset House Studios resident. Nadeem is one half of An Alien Called Harmony (alongside Momoko Gill), their debut EP (2024) was released by New Soil \\u0026 Total Refreshment Centre.\\n\\nKEMARR is a designer \\u0026 DJ from SW LDN where his Jamaican roots merged with his love for Hip-Hop, around grime \\u0026 garage music's peak. Known for his eclectic club selections \\u0026 elaborate style, Kemarr will take you on a journey through reggaeton, dancehall, afro house, baile funk and everything in between. Expect timeless classics fused with rare instrumentals and dubs.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2404058\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":223,\"name\":\"Performance Night \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-24T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-24T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"934c39c45b19a277f0c1e3fbdb3a6dae.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Featuring\\n\\nWilliam Joys x Dom Sebastian \\nMary Malone x Mica Georgis\\nBlythe\\nMaz Murray\\nStella Pearce\\n\\nCurated by Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writer's Room, Florence Trust\\n\\nDoors open at 6.30pm\\n7pm start, no late entry\\n\\n\\nPlus Exhibition of Photographs by \\n\\nEric Arnal\\nJeff Boyd\\nMica Georgis\\nStella Pearce\\n\\nExhibition continues 25th \\u0026 26th April 12-5PM\\nFree Entry\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":266,\"name\":\"Riverloom: a night of live ambient and experimental music\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"38d85dace66496632cba6b88efe4f374.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Mochyn Daer presents an evening of live ambient \\u0026 experimental music at The Bath House in celebration of their debut album, Riverloom, releasing 24th April.\\n\\nAcross the night, artists will present longform sets, merging the organic and electronic, where sounds unfold gradually. Moving between the intimate and the expansive, here music draws on natural processes, resonance, and repetition, creating environments that feel both grounded and otherworldly. Perfect for deep listening, meditation, community connection and grounded alignment as you go into the weekend\\n\\nExpect a cozy space, with low light and immersive soundscapes. Come to sit, lie down, or simply drift. Guests are invited to bring cushions, mats, blankets, to get as comfy and horizontal as possible in the space.\\n\\nLine Up:\\n\\nOutland Sea is an ambient drone experiment combining synthesis, found sounds, folk strings and woodwind. Shifting, generative rivulets furrow dense dronescapes into shrouds of distorted particulate. Melodic fragments surface, unfold and dissolve before being reabsorbed into the wider field, while textures flicker between the organic and the electronic.\\n\\nMochyn Daer is Welsh artist inspired by the meeting of the mythical and the mechanical. A place where ancient stories and songs resonate through modern circuitry, each amplifying the other, and finding powerful new meanings in the sound. They combine ethereal bilingual vocals, clarinet, gongs, field recordings, stones, shells and bells with modular electronics to shape a sonic cynefin, inviting you to step in and simply drift.\\n\\nTheir forthcoming release, Riverloom, is a meandering tapestry of ambient, folk, drone and experimental textures. Exploring what it means to weave with threads of memory and creativity, ever spinning back to their homeland of Wales. The album moves like water, carrying fragments of dreams, gathered river stones, half remembered melodies, inherited stories and field recordings collected from places they return to again and again.\\n\\nResonant Tide Collective are a trio of sonic wayfarers who combine gongs with modular electronics to craft powerful soundscapes that invite the audience on a journey into deep listening and sonic exploration.\\n\\nDrawing on the rich harmonic spectrum of gongs and the shifting interplay of live electronics, they shape environments that move between density and stillness, weight and suspension. Metallic tones bloom and decay, low frequencies gather and recede, primal rhythms pulse and swell, textures emerge gradually, like tides responding to unseen forces.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2404959\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":277,\"name\":\"Critical Mass London - 32nd birthday\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-24T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2058d81f914cb0856bedc7e692189a37.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Celebrating 32 years of Critical Mass London. \\n\\nAlways free, fun and easy. Reclaiming urban space for hundreds of cyclists, with music and general good-natured chaos. \\n\\nMeet up on the south bank under Waterloo Bridge at 7pm. Ride usually leaves approximately 7:30pm. Just show up on a bike (or roller skates, skateboard, etc.), no booking or ticket required.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":182,\"name\":\"Sacrifice Zone Presents: Josef Kurtz + Susu Laroche + Lord Tusk + Yeah You + Laurie Lynch (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-24T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9115bd1b8fddf1283c1de3aa03d71ca2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Excited to host a stacked line-up from Sacrifice Zone, the collaborative endeavour of Susu Laroche \\u0026 Josef Kurtz.\\n______\\n\\nJosef Kurtz is an artist based in London.\\n\\nHis work, equal parts emotive \\u0026 alien, breaks a window into a darkly psychedelic dream state, where genre tropes express and depress themselves in a mania of sounds and textures.\\n\\nHe has performed across the UK, evidence of past outings often washed away like the destruction of a buddhist mandala, remaining only in memory and word-of-mouth. He has recently begun a new emergence.\\n______\\n\\nSusu Laroche is an anagram of Chaos Lure Us and a multidisciplinary artist \\u0026 musician.\\n\\nHer 16mm short films have screened internationally including at London Short Film Festival (UK), Samawah Cinema (Iraq) and Nihilist Film Festival (USA). A comprehensive DVD collection of her cinematic work was released by Purge.xxx in 2023, while her debut photobook Chaos Rule Us was published by Wrong Eye Books in 2021.\\n\\nFollowing releases with Xquisite, Haunter Records and Accidental Meetings, her third album War Against the Lie was released in 2025 on Doyenne, following the launch of a collaborative project with Mobbs on Modern Love.\\n_____\\n\\nLord Tusk is a London-based artist who moves through music, visual art, and performance. A fixture in the city's underground, he navigates a diverse creative landscape with a DIY spirit, channelling his vision through his independent label, UltraWaveVisions. His output is a constant stream of studio albums, live shows, and exhibitions, interwoven with forays into musicals, poetry, fashion, and film. Lord Tusk's curatorial touch extends to ÜNDERGØDS, a quarterly club night that has gained a cult following for its eclectic mix of rare, unreleased, and experimental sounds. He invites listeners and viewers to explore the fringes of sonic and visual expression, offering a glimpse into a world where the weird and wonderful collide.\\n_____\\n\\nTo you YEAH YOU are to you a father daughter duo who let music invade the family context. Who let music dismantle the family car, using construct absurdity to redeem resented weekly Tesco shops and traffic jams. YEAH YOU are not who you said we are, but we are that inverted, and battery op. The content shifts depending on how many supermarket discounts we found. Known for their sneak-up picnic public invasions, perform mostly when uninvited but will always jump on chance to berate a strobe-cut stage, brawling electronic dirt pop, words and feet exert integral (instagram) distrust: you won’t hear what you see.\\n\\nWhy who? They only ever wanted to take back their solidarity with inertia. Creeping up behind a ‘don’t bite the hand that feeds you’ cultural climate, striving to unbuckle the gift economy. You let the lesson be yearn inappropriately. Warped into identity politics this could be an anti-formulaic deconstruction of the nuclear family and of psychic uniform, which normative roles serve to sustain. But in itself is just an improv life stream of the bottom 40: from 0 to -40. Diving in with an admittedly involuntary entropic approach, they provide something for all the family to enjoy/not enjoy.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/sacrifice-zone/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":300,\"name\":\"Ruthless Jabiru \\u0026 Ensemble Offspring: Black Ice\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-24T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7e13fc2794cba901fb36f586a05f12d4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A music-led reflection through and beyond Australia's Black Summer\\n\\nRUTHLESS JABIRU \\u0026 ENSEMBLE OFFSPRING: BLACK ICE\\nKnown now as BLACK SUMMER, the Australian wildfires of 2019–20 scorched an area three quarters the size of the UK. Lives, livelihoods, ecosystems, built structures, physical and mental welfare, entire species of fauna and flora were all decimated. But in the aftermath of untold destruction, there was a glimmer of hope: a re/turning to First Nations leadership on land management through cultural burning.\\n\\nJoin RUTHLESS JABIRU and ENSEMBLE OFFSPRING, together for the first time, for an imagined foray into the sound and emotional landscape of bushfire—told through the music of our composer contemporaries.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/ruthless-jabiru-ensemble-offspring-black-ice-tickets-1984757657582\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":105,\"name\":\"Mariposa: Bambinodj, mi-el, Pochola \\u0026 Faheezy\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-24T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-25T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4b3b0a89d6c64352655e1412c9945732.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2389783\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":169,\"name\":\"Brief Encounters x Transatlantic\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-24T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-25T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"77e6c76038900e94f6f7b9553df3cf3b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"With eyes and ears mutually cast across the channel, Brief Encounters joins forces with Berlin-based label Transatlantic to present a quietly volatile alignment of artists operating across the more ambiguous edges of club music. \\n\\nBrought together by a shared affront to convention and a set of ambient sympathies that push dance music to its limits, Torus joins Emma dj for a rare b2b; while upsammy returns her spacial approach to IDM and club to MOT following her 2025 residency. \\n\\nJennifer Walton debuts her new alias Secretary, stepping back behind the CDJs following the release of her Pitchfork and Quietus-acclaimed debut album Daughters to gift us with her meticulous approach to electronic music. And SUUTOO, fresh from a run of US shows, has been slowly establishing herself as one of London's most progressive voices working across sound, performance and world-building, drawing on noise and club music as tools for collective release and transformation. London based Jordanian-Irish artist DJ GAWAD - joined live by Palestinian rapper Pierre Pepe - takes a satirical, detail-driven approach to production; folding Memphis rap into warped, sharp, club-focused productions, heard in recent work with James Massiah on Contact High. They will be joined by a first-time b2b by residents soltura and Freestyler. \\n\\nExpect euro-kitsch and transmissions from London and the continent’s more absurd corners.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":116,\"name\":\"Skull Rub \\u0026 Clay Can Dance: Clay Sessions @ Aaja, Deptford\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T12:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-25T14:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7919de254eb9ec1dec9ad3e973135f06.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for the first in a series of guided afternoon hand building sessions. Think ambient \\u0026 soulful tunes, meditation \\u0026 clay sculptures, along with some laughs. Materials provided*. Music curated by Skullrub. \\n\\n\\n1230 - 2.30 pm clay sessions. We'll start off with a small meditation and some warm up exercises, followed by a longer pinch pot and coiling session. There will be an optional 20 minute coffee break.\\n \\n1430 til late afternoon: Unguided clay session continues along with the tunes. Hang around get a drink and enjoy the music. \\n\\n* Air dry clay will be provided. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":126,\"name\":\"Foraging Walk\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T13:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-25T16:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c623cf00e507b28c3653cdba876ff4bf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A guided walk in a lush community-run nature reserve in East London. \\n\\nWe'll be moving slowly, identifying plants and fungi, sharing their stories, and speaking about the broader themes surrounding foraging. This walk is designed to be accessible for those with any level of foraging experience.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/33947/spring-foraging-walk\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":101,\"name\":\"Boundary Condition: Haedong Lee \\u0026 Yidan Kim + Gisou Golshani \\u0026 Helin Karabil + Beachers\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-25T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"edc0e9309a6c8d1628d07cd63d7738ab.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Boundary Condition is a series of site-responsive, durational events investigating parallels between dark-jazz, hauntology, and music concrete as nostalgia-centric practices, trickling from the persistence and antagonistic fragmentation of certain memories. The project deploys a practice-as-research model of discoursing phenomenology of the various archetypes of atrophy through psychoacoustic, audible interdependence, and sombre studies on degradation, memory, and the politics of time.\\n\\nThis edition of Boundary Condition features 6 artists in a hybrid of audiovisual live sets \\u0026 immersive projections; oblique ceremonial forms, xenofeminism, ancient rituals, olfactory imagery, sonic resistance, counter hegemony, machinic desire, shamanic practices, uncertain futures, queer politics, ancestral memory, distorted textures, folk remnants, cassette collages, subtractive synthesis, climate grief, and a replica fox-hunting horn in a historic 12th century church.\\n\\nHaedong Lee \\u0026 Yidan Kim present Ecology of Death and Annihilation: A Ceremony for Things that Wither 죽음과 소멸의 생태계 : 사라지는 것들을 위한 세레모니\\nRooted in diverse ritual cultures from across the world, Haedong Lee and Yidan Kim's latest work is presented as a contemporary ceremony, a multi-disciplinary performance that pulls together various elements from the duo’s rigorous study of various ceremonial practices across East Asia and the wider Asian continent, and shamanic cultures found in West Africa and throughout Europe. Ringing various bells Lee has collected or created, playing wooden and metal percussive instruments used in rituals that span different cultures, chanting and overlaying hallucinatory synthesized and processed sounds, the two artists create a uniquely contemporary interpretation of ritual soundscapes, braiding remnants of folk songs with oblique ceremonial forms. They complement their meticulously engineered sonic ecosystem with physical actions and olfactory expressions that are harder to perceive on record, such as the gestures involved in the offering of incense and the materials that have historically been used in rituals and ceremonies. Scouring history, Kim creates a layered smell-scape from plant resins, leaves and bark like frankincense, agarwood and sage that diffuses as the performance unfolds. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_u8uOemAbHE \\n\\nBorn in South Korea and currently based in London, Lee and Kim are both seasoned interdisciplinary artists, with Lee concentrating his interest on sound and Kim primarily working with smell. And for almost a decade, their work has overlapped repeatedly as they have developed a way to harmonize their respective skills, exploring the history of ritual, ceremonial and multi-sensory experiences by merging installation and performance. Kim's interests took them to the Korean Traditional Incense Cultural Association, where they received a formal training in incense ceremony, allowing them to refine their approach to olfactory imagery. Lee meanwhile spent time imagining sound sculptures with metal, wood and the by-products of the Anthropocene, objects that allow him to reflect on ecological and civilizational crises while practicing restraint and control. 'Ecology of Death and Annihilation: A Ceremony for Things that Wither' first emerged in 2021, when it was debuted at Seoul's Oil Tank Culture Park, and it stretches Lee and Kim's art through the past and present and far into the future. Hypothesizing art itself is itself an ancient ritual, the performance establishes itself as a contemporary hybrid, where sounds, movements and smells mimic each others' temporal motions, appearing and disappearing to provoke consciousness itself.\\nhttps://yidankim.com/ \\nhttps://www.haedonglee.com/ABOUT \\n\\n\\nGisou Golshani \\u0026 Helin Karabil present Duaye Khaar دعای خار \\n‘Duaye Khaar’ (Prayer of the Thorn) is a textural imagining of uncertain futures, frustrated species and harsh landscapes. Inspired by Alhagi maurorum, a thorny desert shrub found on a road trip through northeastern Iran, channeling climate grief through elemental relations — salt, water, wind.\\n\\nGisou Golshani is a London-based artist, performing rituals of belonging and resistance through sound, performance and installation. Her performances blend folk mythology with grief practices from Iran to create intimate temporal environments. In her sonic palette, distorted textures, drones and field recordings merge with vocalisation to summon a surge against erasure. She experiments with storytelling modalities to reflect on feelings of doom and despair, while searching for possibilities of transformation and collective healing. \\nhttps://www.instagram.com/gisougolshani/?hl=en\\n\\nHelin Karabil is a London-based multidisciplinary artist whose work maintains and re-presents marginalised cultural histories with an interest in queer Middle Eastern identities. Engaging with digital media, sound, performance, and memory, they create live archives and immersive environments that safeguard endangered identities, counter hegemony, and embody erased histories, particularly in the Middle East. Using software like TouchDesigner, Karabil generates visuals in which ancestral memory, displacement, and queer presence coexist.\\nhttps://helinkarabil.wixsite.com/helinkarabil \\n\\n\\nBeachers presents Horns of Death\\nBeachers is the project of London-based Daryl Worthington. He works in the crossovers between accidental and composed sounds, hi and lo-fi audio, with a particular interest in the beauty of the mundane. This takes an array of approaches, from explorations of the materiality and tactility of radio signals through to analogue synthesis, field recording and cassette collages and sample-based computer music. Beachers releases have appeared on czaszka (rec.), Shimmering Moods, Fractal Meat, Wabi-Sabi Tapes and his own ineffectual suns label. His latest release, ‘Horns Of Death’ (ineffectual suns, 2025) explores a replica fox-hunting horn, processing and twisting its rattles, squeaks and blasts through computer and sampler.\\n\\n\\nRuben\\nRuben Sonnoli, performing simply as Ruben, is an Italian musician and producer based in London. With a background in jazz piano and composition for film, Ruben draws inspiration from neoclassical, jazz, and experimental electronic music. His work fuses harmony, melody, sound design, and real-world sound recordings, exploring their mutual interaction and the possibilities of interlacing disparate sonic forms and disrupting the conventional boundaries of “compatible” and “intrusive” sounds. This focus on blending varied elements has also led him to work on projects that combine sound and other media, such as dance and visual art. Ruben’s performances incorporate processed samples, subtractive synthesis, and live instruments, shaping musical environments where moving harmonies and evocative melodies mesh with sonic textures in a delicate balance between cohesion and discord.\\nhttps://www.kinzicastudio.com/about/\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cerpintxt.com/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":297,\"name\":\"SOFT BODIES\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ce3380d422271536dc2e648b6bcc495e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sensuous soft bellied delusion. The romance of illusion. A temple of our own. The home.\\n\\nSubject to the state, external forces manifest themselves around a tense dinner table.\\nIn a perpetual cycle of use, the individual finds a vice to abuse. An escape. Middle class petrification, and mass pacification.\\n\\nTwo faces meet, two parallel mirrors, two adverse reactions: “Present” and “Absent”, our characters in this play.\\n\\nThese mirrors bounce images of reflection and projection onto one another.\\nSeeking a witness under the guise of “love.”\\n\\nThe omnipresence of absence itself, a looming god and toy for yearning satisfaction. There is no action in this piece, simply a battle of reactions.\\n\\nThe set is the gallery itself, with visual and performing artists feeding themselves and each other through atmosphere, compliance, and disruption.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2404977\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":319,\"name\":\"Spring Solidarity Tapes\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c720eaf98f56095a1b44291752884065.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Our next event will focus on solidarity with those facing political repression in the UK. \\n\\nWe will hear from groups who support those who are alleged to have taken action against the imperialist war machine and are now confronted with the repression of the UK legal system. \\n\\nAll funds will go directly to these groups.\\n\\nTo help usher in the coming of Spring we have a night of high-energy experimental music \\u0026 djs. Come dance, donate funds, and learn how to get involved in vital solidarity work.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/35091/spring-solidarity-tapes-comfort-another-country-buffee\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":227,\"name\":\"PolyDub Sound System invites Mali Blakamix\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b91f887d586c83d2b26d075a8299accb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The highly mystical and atmospheric Blakamix International label and studio will be taking control of our sound system through Mali Blakamix. He carries on a unique dub style heritage tracing back to late 80s - early 90s Bedford, UK. With his own touch Mali transcends it into future-proof rhythms that are both tender and energising.\\n\\nThis is simply a rebellious and uplifting roots-rock-reggae-dub dance and you are invited. One for the heads and the curious alike, and certainly not one to be missed.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":39,\"name\":\"Acid Mothers Temple ft. Cotton Casino + Michael\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c2ae2e7a8c711fd0d0bb0e626648f77e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Baba Yaga's Hut Presents:\\n\\nAcid Mothers Temple ft. Cotton Casino\\n\\n+ Michael\\n\\nIklektic - April 25th\\n\\nAcid Mothers Temple \\u0026 The Melting Paraiso U.F.O. :\\n\\nKawabata Makoto : guitar, speed guru\\n\\nHigashi Hiroshi : synthesizer, fishin’god\\n\\nJyonson Tsu : voice, guitar, bouzouki, midnight whislter\\n\\nSatoshima Nani : drums, another dimension\\n\\nSawano Shozo : bass, hex man\\n\\nwith Cotton Casino : voice, synthesizer\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/ryw2or-acid-mothers-temple-ft-cotton-casino-michael-25th-apr-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":93,\"name\":\"CNI 3: Strange Brew Bristol\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a8696b6f98f2c74832c455e3bcce1c54.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SELN hosts its debut Bristol venture as part of the ever expanding event series “Celebrating New Industrial”. Somewhat of a second spiritual homeland for SELN, it’s with great pleasure the label hosts its first official venture in the West Country’s capital.\\n\\nAkua has cemented herself as one of the most distinctive techno DJs coming out of the U.S. in recent years. Forefronting the current generation of artists reviving the spirit of techno’s enduring velocity, her no-compromise mindset brings a full throttle intensity to her sets embodying an enthralling old-school sound while simultaneously keeping the pulse of the contemporary techno milieu.\\n\\nConrad Pack runs the SELN Recordings label with DJ Gonz, and his productions there explore the fertile terrain between tuff, rooted soundsystem steppers and high-BPM techno, while his evolving productions for Lost Domain explore a hard-edged but deep and dub-enriched sound with echoes early Downwards and Axis. Pack has been focussing of late on live performance, showcasing his focussed and distinct sonic vision of techno.\\n\\nDJ Gonz co-runs SELN recordings where his releases perpetuate focused melodic riffs joint with heavy leading percussion. Drawing on influences taken from free-tekno, dub and kuduro, his sound is both pensive, driving whilst still rooted in a soundsystem tradition. Previous output include The Messenger on Wain Records and most recently Magical Negro Overdrive.\\n\\nVega is the founder of UVB-76 Music and DROOGS, and a key affiliate of Ruffhouse. As both a DJ and producer he has played a central role in shaping the label’s sonic focus on atmospheric, deep, and technically refined drum \\u0026 bass and techno. Active within Bristol’s underground scene and frequenting platforms such as SWU/Rinse FM his sets and productions explore the darker and emotive edges of bass music while maintaining a strong emphasis on precision, depth, and sound design.  \\n\\nThere is a limited number of free tickets available for those who are unwaged / on UC. Please email selnrecordings@gmail.com to reserve one.\\n\\nThis event will be livestreamed [audio only] via celebratingnewindustrial.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.headfirstbristol.co.uk/whats-on/strange-brew/sat-25-apr-seln-presents-celebrating-new-industrial-150192#e150192\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":252,\"name\":\"Elastics: Beatrice M. b2b Manami, INGI (live), Wordcolour, Cam Joon b2b Flatcap\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-25T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7f96532e449825840ea010a7ab12baf3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":309,\"name\":\"The George Tavern Vintage Market\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-26T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5338503a60eda68e1de0ccfa9687063d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Here on Sunday 26th April 12-4pm: The George Tavern Vintage \\u0026 Makers Market! \\n\\nExpect fresh garms, beautiful handmade gifts, pints and impeccable vibes ✨\\n\\nIf that wasn’t enough you can spin some records with Aynjel’s Vinyl Open Decks, Seb \\u0026 Fil’s Moon Photo Booth is back again or even sew back on some buttons with Unravelled School’s Mending Club 🧶\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":325,\"name\":\"Hundred Years Gallery: Kate Carr, Magda Drozd, Milo Thesiger-Meacham\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-26T15:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-26T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c5c2ac5a541af5bef6877c75d45e7e3b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Three solos by Kate Carr, Magda Drozd \\u0026 Milo Thesiger-Meacham\\n\\nDoors 3.30 | music 4pm | £10 cash on the door\\n\\nKate Carr is a London-based sound artist working across composition, performance and installation. Her practice explores the encounters, textures and technologies entangled with field recording. In her compositional and performance work, she centres the ambiguities and fictions of field work, often combining recorded material with live foley practices and performances on instruments assembled from discarded materials.\\nHer work approaches space as relational, drawing on materials such as the layered sound of public environments and infrastructural vibrations from traffic flows and pedestrians. She regularly performs internationally and runs the sound art label Flaming Pines.\\nwww.gleamingsilverribbon.com\\n\\nMagda Drozd, born in Warsaw, is a composer, violinist, and sound artist living in Zürich and London. She has been releasing her music on the Swiss label Präsens Editionen (PE) since 2019, and further contributions have followed on Hallow Ground, Flaming Pines and Rivercore. Together with Nicola Genovese, she founded the duo Sopraterra, which released the LP ‘Seven Dances to Embrace the Hollow’ on PE and La Becque Editions in 2025. Her music has gained recognition from acclaimed outlets such as The Wire, The Quietus, BBC Radio 6 Music, BBC 3 New Music Show, NTS Radio, Ransom Note, groove and Polskie Radio.\\nDivided by Dusk, the Polish composer’s third solo album, carries the promise of a crepuscular otherworldliness. Inspired by Drozd’s stays in Japan, its rich tradition in ambient and experimental music, and a renewed engagement with her roots in Poland and its folk and ancient history, her work is a form of sonic excavation. Layers of dark-ambient tones intertwine with field recordings, textured violin, and luminous folk motifs, welcoming the listener into a liminal world—one filled with buried treasures.\\nwww.magdadrozd.com\\n\\nMilo Thesiger-Meacham works in sound, film, radio, text, composition and performance. For the European Capital of Culture 2022, he created a twenty-two-hour audio work using six thousand pieces of found material. In 2024 he was shortlisted for the Prototype Prize. Last year he published his first book, ‘Audible Heat’, on Tenement Press. Then he contributed to an edition of the Big Issue curated by 10Foot, Britain’s most prolific graffiti tagger. This summer he will be an artist in residence for Asociația STOL, Bucharest. He is Artistic Director of the community arts radio stations Resonance FM \\u0026 Extra.\\nsoundcloud.com/milotm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":284,\"name\":\"Ex-Easter Island Head + Rún\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"811d22acd8d32c23839abb4f7418ffe9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Baba Yaga's Hut Presents:\\n\\nEx-Easter Island Head + Rún\\n\\nIklkektic - April 27th\\n\\nEx-Easter Island Head are a UK-based experimental musical collective composing and performing music for solid body electric guitar, percussion and other instruments. The group plays multiple electric guitars augmented through mechanical preparations and extended techniques, creating hypnotic performances rich in repetition, shimmering drones and melodic invention through purposefully limited means.\\n\\nTheir records and live performances have received significant critical acclaim from the likes of The Wire, the Quietus and the New York Times. Favourably compared to the likes of Steve Reich, Glenn Branca and John Cage, the groups' music has been praised for its mixture of percussive drive, emotional warmth and playful experimentation.\\n\\nThey have performed worldwide in venues ranging from the tiny Scottish island of Iona to a 150-year-old brewery in Berlin, with major festival appearances including ATP, Supersonic and Le Guess Who? Collaborators have included the BBC Philharmonic, composer Arnold Dreyblatt and musicians Laura Cannell, Charles Hayward and Andre Bosman in the group Whistling Arrow.\\n\\nTheir library music releases Mechanical Landscapes 1 \\u0026 2 released by EMI/KPM have seen the group’s work used internationally for television and radio productions, whilst the groups’ own Large Electric Ensemble projects have seen the core quartet joining forces with forward-thinking musicians to make ambitious large scale performances across the UK and EU.\\n\\nThe group’s latest album Norther (2024) was named album of the year by Europe’s leading independent culture website, The Quietus. An interview in the same year for The Guardian described their music as “amongst the boldest experiments in British music”.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/eowg9d-ex-easter-island-head-rn-27th-apr-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":344,\"name\":\"The Sleeves (Tara Cunningham and Jack Cooper) - Two Day Residency\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a434791c85bbac34d9bca9471e7e9405.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A two day residency from The Sleeves - a duo of Jack Cooper and Tara Cunningham - to celebrate the launch of their album. \\n\\n\\nThe Sleeves are the duo of Jack Cooper and Tara Cunningham, both likely known to you as one half of Modern Nature.  Following an all-instrumental Mossy Tapes release last November, Cooper and Cunningham have recorded 10 new songs showcasing their vocal and guitar interplay with only the faintest echoes of prior efforts (individually or collectively), representing a fully realised leap forward from their largely improvised debut. \\n\\nThe Sleeves is a somewhat counter intuitive take on the guitar/vocal duo formula (provided you think there is such a thing) though it's not nearly as simplistic as \\\"the space between the notes\\\"  -- it would be the height of exaggeration to say an album this simultaneously expansive and incandescent is unprecedented.  But it doesn't happen nearly often enough, either. \\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://wegottickets.com/f/16242\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":236,\"name\":\"Jules Cunningham Dance Workshop \",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-28T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-28T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a7e798fc44a63da9b782a3e1612e7a01.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Jules Cunningham (they/them), originally from Liverpool, worked as an award-winning dancer for 20+ years with Merce Cunningham Dance Company and Michael Clark Company.\\n\\nJules founded Julie Cunningham \\u0026 Company in 2017, to create and present work that combines clarity of form with an interest in gender identity and the body. Jules uses movement language that draws on their technical dance training, expanding and queering it collaboratively, working between sound, text, visual art. \\n\\nCreative work is informed by solo and collaborative movement exploration, queerness, lived experience of mental illness, disability and exclusion based on Jules’ working-class background and non-binary identity. \\n\\nThis workshop is part of a series curated by the artist Mica Georgis as part of a Residency at The Writers’ Room, Florence Trust in April 2026.\\n\\nThe workshops are open to dancers and non-dancers. No previous dance experience is necessary.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.sadlerswells.com/about-us/supporting-artists/associate-artists/jules-cunningham/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":317,\"name\":\"The Common Press Poetry Night w/ Zain Rishi \\u0026 Friends\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-28T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-28T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ac8ef43e41eae4ae927732edcca7d904.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Calling all poets! Join us for our next Common Press Poetry Night on Tuesday 28th April from 7-9.30pm for a beautiful evening of performance from established poets and an open mic, hosted by Zain Rishi.\\n\\n🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤\\n\\nOur poets:\\n\\nZain Rishi is a writer from Birmingham, UK. He won the 27th annual Ware Poets Competition, placed third in the 2024 Oxford Poetry Prize and was highly commended in the Poetry Wales Award 2024-25. His poetry has featured in Magma, Wildness, Fourteen Poems, Gutter, Propel and various anthologies. He is currently based in Edinburgh. Noon is his debut poetry pamphlet.\\n\\nFrancis-Xavier Mukiibi is a poet and performer of Ugandan heritage from North London. He was the recipient of an Eric Gregory Award for his debut pamphlet, Mutabani \\u0026 [ ]ther Poems (Little Betty, 2025), and won Silver in the Creative Future Writers’ Award for 2024.\\n\\nSara Mostafa is an Egyptian poet \\u0026 writer based in London \\u0026 Glasgow. In 2024, she was highly commended for the Edwin Morgan Poetry Award.\\n\\nSylvie Jane Lewis has appeared in The London Magazine, Acumen, and fourteen poems. Her poetry placed third in the 2025 Bridport Poetry Prize, making her winner of the 2025 Bridport Young Writer Award. She is pursuing an AHRC-funded Literature and Film PhD at the University of Brighton, focused on the fairy in literary modernism and early film and photography.\\n\\n🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤🎤\\n\\nIf you’d like to read at the poetry night, arrive at 7pm to sign up. There will also be opportunities to sign up on the night and hop on stage. Please note that while we will do our best to accommodate as many readers as possible, we cannot guarantee that everyone on the list will have the chance to perform.\\n\\nSchedule\\n\\n7:00 pm - Doors open\\n\\n7:15 pm -  Sara performing\\n\\n7:30 pm - Open Mic slots\\n\\n7:45 pm - Francis-Xavier performing\\n\\n8:00 pm - Open Mic slots\\n\\n8:15 pm - Break\\n\\n8:30 pm - Sylvie performing\\n\\n8:45 pm - Open mic slots\\n\\n9:00 pm - Zain performing\\n\\n9:30 pm - Closing\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/35073/the-common-press-poetry-night-w-zain-rishi-friends\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":341,\"name\":\"Sebastian Rochford and Marie Kruttli\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-28T19:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ac5e38950fbe49050301d5d93867c120.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sebastian Rochford and Marie Kruttli\\nTue 28 April 2026, 7.45PM\\nStandard £15 / Vortex Members £7.5 / Students \\u0026 UC beneficiaries £6.25\\n\\nBook online\\n\\n\\nDoors 7:45 PM, Music 8:30 PM – 2 sets of music\\nLine-up:\\nMarie Kruttli – Piano\\nSebastian Rochford – Drums\\n\\nAbout:\\nThe duo will be playing music from Sebastian Rochford’s ECM album “A Short Diary” and some new music.\\n\\nBritish drummer and composer Sebastian Rochford first gained international acclaim as part of the experimental and electronic jazz outfit Polar Bear and has since collaborated with names like David Byrne, Brian Eno and Nadine Shah, while also being the touring drummer for Patti Smith. The drummer first appeared on ECM with Andy Sheppard’s band on 2012’s Libero and subsequently on Surrounded By Sea (2015) and Romaria (2018), before releasing his first leader-date for the label with his own compositions A Short Diary – in duo with Kit Downes – in 2023. The album is dedicated to Rochford’s father, Aberdeen poet Gerard Rochford (1932-2019) and to his family. According to Pitchfork, “‘A Short Diary’ rarely relaxes into a comfortable emotional space, though its mood is consistent in its muted qualities. it’s as honest a depiction of grieving as you might hope to hear.”\\n\\nMarie Kruttli is a swiss pianist, composer, producer who lives in Berlin. She was born in a village in Switzerland, in a family of musicians and started playing the piano at the age of 6. She first learned classical music and then switched to jazz (obtaining later on a bachelor and master at HEMU Lausanne and Hochschule Luzern academies). Marie received numerous prizes for her performance and composition work. The band that she has performed the most with so far is her trio (now with bassist Lukas Traxel and drummer Gautier Garrigue) but the artist is working now on a project called Dragon Life which was born from her producing work. It is a band that has two different constellation (duo and sextet) where she also uses her voice and synthesisers.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.universe.com/events/sebastian-rochford-and-marie-kruttli-tickets-65M0NB?ref=website\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":332,\"name\":\" A Taste of Home: African Cinema Series\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-29T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-29T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b54706440b37f1f84cc7b01b2ad408b9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Wed 29 April: The Indie Scene in Nigeria: A Shorts Programme\\n\\n1. A Body in Metaphor by Amanda Madumere – 00:12:08 \\n\\n2. Girl-Boy by Ajay Abalaka – 00:30:04 \\n\\n3. Happy Times by Khalil Agboola – 00:18:48 \\n\\n4. God’s Wife by Dika Ofoma – 00:15:09 \\n\\n5. Swimming in a Sea of Trauma by Ugo Azuya – 00:06:30\\n\\n6. Record Found Here by Lanaire Aderemi – 00:18:36 \\n\\nTotal Runtime: 1 hours 40 minutes\\n\\nPost screening Q\\u0026A with Raphel Famotibe and Ifeoluwa Olutayo\\n\\nAn evening celebrating the Nigerian independent film scene, with six shorts by filmmakers and artists from across the country. Through a varied lens, the works reclaim suppressed histories, highlight marginalised viewpoints and find joy and resilience in the everyday. \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://bookwhen.com/londonperformancestudios#focus=ev-szvza-20260429183000\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":340,\"name\":\"third season – Kate Mahony, fire good also bad, Knot\\u0026Yoke LIVE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-29T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-29T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c8824d6aa210d1b708a816f3beaff885.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"It’s time for a spring fling. A night of swirling noise and emotion.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.ticketsource.com/whats-on/london/avalon-cafe/third-season-kate-mahony-fire-good-also-bad-knot-yoke-live/2026-04-29/19:00/t-aaameyn\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":263,\"name\":\"Alvarezz - Album Release Show\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-29T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-29T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b72c38dccf1642540ea434782af3327b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Alvarezz performs his new album Desire Path / Exit Wound live at Spanners.\\n\\nHis second full length on Multibody Records, the album explores the sometimes contradictory ways emotions are experienced physically in relationships with a raw, vocal driven set underpinned by his production which never settles on easily definable genres, drifting between dark R\\u0026B grooves, bursts of noise, driving post-punk and fractious ambience.\\n\\nAlvarezz's first album La Linea Imaginaria received positive reviews in The Wire Magazine and The Quietus and his music has featured on NTS, Resonance FM, Rinse and Noods Radio.\\n\\nSupport on the night will be provided by London based artist No Home. Described as a ‘punk producer’ and ‘DIY experimental artist’ by the Wire Magazine, their first album “Fucking Hell”, was released in June 2020 and was named one of the “The 35 Best Rock Albums of 2020” by Pitchfork. Their second and most recent album, \\\"Young Professional\\\" was released in November 2022.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":337,\"name\":\"Dev/Null Presents #1\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-29T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-30T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a1639b13ccbd232753df8f35334ba035.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dev/Null brings together a bunch of his London DJ friends for a ridiculous mid-week jungle throwdown.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2410354\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":235,\"name\":\"Hiber Nation\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-30T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-02T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7871d5efcb66b008c217b16aa208d1f5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Social Spider is excited to present Hiber Nation, a 20-artist group exhibition curated by ekabo donyi, running from 30 April to 2 May 2026 at 162 Holloway Road, N7 8QD. In collaboration with Kat Easto, the gallery is transformed into a giant “blanket fort”, framing rest as a space of care, slowness, and refuge against contemporary cultures of grindset and hyper-productivity. Through installation, sculpture, painting, performance, and more, the exhibition brings together varied approaches to rest and its many forms.\\n\\nThe site will house a wide range of practices and materials. Long connected to spaces of rest and leisure, art has helped shape how pleasure, pause, and everyday life are imagined. Hiber Nation brings this relationship into focus, inviting visitors to reconsider rest as a shared cultural space. A public programme will run throughout the exhibition including a private view, artist workshops, and film screening inviting audiences to take part in a culture that cares for recovery.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":259,\"name\":\"Oskar Jones @ Next Door Records\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5f621a19a54b2098b7e0a0749cdc6fca.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Oskar Jones returns to the intimate setting of Next Door Records in quartet form with an array of fresh material, ripe for famished ears.\\n\\nLikened to the Esbjörn Svensson Trio, Oskar’s music simultaneously embraces space and groove, generating a sonic atmosphere that is active but not busy. His compositions focus on the intentionality of expression, honesty, and authenticity through pellucid, lyrical melodies and fierce grooves that straddle through-composition and improvisation.\\n\\nDescribed by GSMD as “fresh, contemporary jazz talent” at his most recent performance at the 2025 EFG London Jazz Festival, Oskar Jones is a versatile, award-winning composer, saxophonist and pianist, and a first-class 2025 graduate of the prestigious Guildhall School of Music and Drama’s Jazz Performance Masters, where he spent two years honing his saxophone and improvisational skills under the guidance of leading UK jazz musicians and composers Trish Clowes, Jean Toussaint, Iain Ballamy, and Mark Lockheart, among others, and for which he was a receiver of the 2024 Help Musicians Postgraduate Award.\\n\\nIn 2025 he hosted sold out shows with his new quintet at Oxford House, Next Door Records, and the Chelsea Physic Garden, and was also one of ten musicians from London conservatoires selected to be part of the London Transport Museum’s “Transported by Culture” programme.\\n\\nLine-up:\\n\\nTenor Saxophone - Oskar Jones\\n\\nDrums - Luke Brueck Seeley\\n\\nPiano - Joseph Game\\n\\nBass - James Leaver-Whitfield\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/X15a0e2c6242?dice_id=X15a0e2c6242\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":174,\"name\":\"3SR w/ Alicia, Able Archer \\u0026 scud\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-30T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-04-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4c3ec3c2be47c8d36a1bb14c399cf602.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On the edge of the SUTHERN FOREST, the sun refused to let go of the day. Once more he felt the pull to re-join SWEET MARTIN in the woodland, where they would forage for purple berries and harvest spud-trees.\\n\\n--\\n\\nDJ sets from:\\nAlicia (Terra Obscura) +\\nAble Archer (Texture Mag) +\\nscud (3SR)\\n\\nAnother BYOB ambient hang out at Shai Space, this time it's spring. \\n\\n\\n7:30 - 11pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":229,\"name\":\"Vespers live with Inès Cherifi, MM'99, NADIM, Dionokia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-04-30T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-01T14:33:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9a0e8866b09a217d5fd7cc7f3afc88ff.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Vespers Live\\n\\nInès Cherifi\\nMM’99\\nNADIM\\nDionokia\\n\\nApril 30th\\n\\nTickets on RA/Gel\\n\\nmulti-textural soundscapes carved with care into modern pop structures \\n\\nInès twists a classical violin background into pulsing landscapes of electronica\\n\\nMM'99 updates the witch house palette with a modern hyperpop flare (it’s coming back!)\\n\\nNADIM pulls fashion forward art noise from Egyptian ritual roots \\n\\nResident DJ Dionokia plays us out into the streets with elated rhythmic bangers\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":338,\"name\":\"Mutual Aid Fundraiser Raffle for Iran\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-01T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-01T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c86ea27a3b743b61eac50aa7c46a149f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join our Mutual Aid Fundraiser Raffle for Iran 🎟️\\n\\nAs a fragile ceasefire takes hold, friends and communities in Iran continue to live with the lasting impacts of war. With longstanding inflation placing enormous pressure on households even before the latest escalation of the US-Israeli war of aggression, people are already facing a severe economic crisis and one the world's longest internet shutdowns. The war has destroyed essential infrastructures - places of education and of work - from factories to hospitals. There is a scarcity of work and medicine, and our sustained support is needed more than ever. These wars aren’t abstract, they carry real human costs often disproportionately falling on the most vulnerable.\\n\\nAll funds raised will be distributed through trusted groups on the ground. They will ensure the distribution of the funds through tested routes built on years of work within different affected communities in Iran.\\n\\nJoin us this May Day for an evening of solidarity filled with  poetry, readings and music. Participate in the raffle to take home an artwork, a print or other special prizes. Contribute what you can - it will help us raise vital funds for those most affected. This includes medicine and medical care, support for displaced and migrant families as well as assistance for families of prisoners. \\n\\nStay tuned for more - we will be sharing details about the artworks and other prizes as well as the full evening programme soon!!\\n\\nHow it works:\\n\\nYou can take part in three ways:\\n\\n1) Event Ticket\\n\\nBuy a ticket to attend in person, either a solidarity ticket for £10 or a cheaper ticket for £7\\n\\nBoth of these will include 1 entry into our raffle draw. \\n\\n2) Raffle Ticket \\n\\nYou may  buy extra raffle tickets to have more chances of winning prizes. \\n\\nOr\\n\\nYou may buy Raffle tickets without attending the event. \\n\\n*If you are not attending, you have to be able to pick up your prize in London from a holding spot or you can nominate someone who is at the event to take it for you. \\n\\n3) Add Donation \\n\\nAny amount donations for the fundraiser. \\n\\nAddress:\\n\\nCubitt Artists\\n\\n8 Angel Mews, London N1 9HH, United Kingdom\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.zeffy.com/en-GB/ticketing/mutual-aid-fundraiser-raffle-for-iran\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":333,\"name\":\"!! MAY DAY AT PELICAN HOUSE !!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-01T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-01T23:45:00Z\",\"poster\":\"24db140ba967708584dd09ad63dd4d8a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us at Pelican for a night of cheap drinks, food, live music and solidarity! Arrive at six for UVW's Latin BBQ, stay for the liberatory music of Nu Earth Groove, bringing their global urban jazz funk sounds to the stage!\\n\\nWe’ll hear stories from our comrades currently at the frontlines of the struggle against war, empire, gentrification and work - alongside some exciting updates on the future of Pelican House!\\n\\nNu Earth Groove: a 9-piece house band, heavy on brass, bass and drums: built of musicians currently taking London by a storm, almost entirely improvising: creating together, in the moment, with you.\\n\\n£5 Donation // Free Entry for Striking Workers !!\\n\\nBYOB - BRING YOUR OWN BANNERS!!\\n\\nThe agenda for this years annual general meeting is as follows.... \\n\\n- 6pm: UWV BBQ !!\\n- 7pm: The Pelican Choir !!\\n- 8pm: RALLY !!!\\n\\n- 9pm-late: Nu Earth Groove!!!!!\\n\\nSEE YOU THERE!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/pelicanhouse/2168215\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":329,\"name\":\"For no reason of my own\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-01T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e8d8f344f0f88897528d8a8718562fee.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For no reason of my own\\nExhibition dates: 1 –24 May 2026.\\nOpening hours: Wed–Sun 12–5pm\\n\\nLaunch evening: 1 May, 6–8pm, free all welcome\\nFor no reason of my own is an archive display that introduces Justice \\u0026 Change, an ongoing research programme exploring how the law shapes our lives and how communities create justice beyond the limits of the legal system. Bringing together materials from the Brent Community Law Centre (BCLC) and the Young People’s Law Centre (YPLC) alongside films from Cinenova and London Community Video Archive and photographic materials from the North Paddington Community Darkroom, the display situates the law centre movement within a wider landscape of grassroots organising — documenting how working-class communities built infrastructures of mutual support, political education and resistance in response to structural inequality.\\n\\nThe BCLC was one of the first community law centres in the UK, founded in 1971 as part of a wider movement that emerged from a lack of accessible legal welfare for working-class communities. Underpinning this work was a central question: what is the role of a lawyer in working-class struggle? In response, BCLC developed an approach to law grounded in collective action rather than individual cases, while redistributing legal knowledge to community organisations across the borough. From this work grew the YPLC, a unique initiative within the movement that supported young people facing legal struggles in care, employment, education and the criminal legal system.\\n\\nFor no reason of my own takes its title from a text by the YPLC, If we can’t get our points across… we ought to have a spokesperson for ourselves (1981), which outlines the need for a specialised legal service for young people. Through correspondence, reports, newspaper clippings, photographs, moving image and paperwork, this presentation traces the conditions that made services like BCLC and YPLC necessary. These archival fragments speak to both legal histories and broader struggles around housing, racism, migration, labour and policing that shaped — and continue to shape — everyday life in Brent and beyond. By placing these materials in dialogue, we ask: what can we learn from collective and community action as a form of justice that extends beyond the limits of legal systems?\\n\\nInvitation to take care\\n\\nThere are materials in this archive display that document experiences of injustice against Black and other racialised communities. It may awaken your own needs for care in the context of journeys you have experienced, navigated, or witnessed. We encourage you to honour these needs as we share this work together. This could look like: taking a deep breath; pausing to drink water; stepping outside to walk around the Kilburn Square and market.\\n\\nWith thanks to BCLC founders and staff who have supported us in the research and development of the programme so far; Jamie Ritchie, Clive Grace, Sian Williams, Irene Grant Bannon, Maureen Vincent and Jeremy Smith, alongside The Willesden Trades Hall, Brent Museum and Archives (Emir Ghariani, Sarah Harrison), Bishopsgate Archive (Niamh Glanville-Frayne), Cinenova, London Community Video Archive, The Showroom (Scott Lawrimore), Richard Bevan and and Linda Mulcahy (Radical Lawyering).\\n\\nCurated by Lizzie Graham and Meera Shakti Osborne\\n\\nIllustration by Sofia Niazi\\n\\nFor no reason of my own is made possible with The National Lottery Heritage Fund.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":339,\"name\":\"1st of May: The Red in the Green – Screening, free pamphlet and collective reading \",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-01T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-01T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ca4ad451691f8ab929d5887bc5a2e5c2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Red in the Green will mark the 1st of May, International Workers’ Day. Celebrating the convergence of worker and environmental organising, the evening will begin with a film screening and discussion (Who bombed Judi Bari?, 2012, 92 mins) and conclude with a collective reading of excerpts from Peter Linebaugh’s pamphlet The incomplete, true, authentic and wonderful history of May Day. There will also be time to explore some of our growing ecological direct-action archival collection.\\n\\nThe incomplete, true, authentic and wonderful history of May Day\\n\\nAs has become customary, we will collectively read excerpts from Peter Linebaugh’s The incomplete, true, authentic and wonderful history of May Day to celebrate the convergence of labour struggles and ecological direct action, with some free copies of the text available on the day.\\n\\nRead The incomplete, true, authentic and wonderful history of May Day https://maydayrooms.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/peter-linebaugh-the-incomplete-true-authentic-and-wonderful-history-of-may-day.pdf\\n\\n**Who bombed Judi Bari? (Mary Liz Thomson, 2012) – 92 mins ** \\n\\nIn 1990, two prominent Earth First! activists, Judi Bari and Darryl Cherney, were car bombed in Oakland, California. They are then immediately investigated by the FBI for bombing themselves. Who bombed Judi Bari? Follows the subsequent lawsuit against the FBI, the complex history of Earth First!, the loggers and the controversy of tree spiking. Bari worked tirelessly to organise with workers in the logging industry in the American Pacific North West. Lobbying against the controversial tactic of tree spiking (inserting metal into trees to damage the saws of loggers) she aimed instead to unite workers in the extractive industry with environmentalists.\\n\\nWe are very pleased to have Andrew working as the researcher in residence for the next 2 years on the global economy, not global ecology archives. Andrew will lead a discussion on some of the important but often ill-remembered connections and collaborations between workers, union organisers and the ecological movement from our archival holdings.\\n\\nWorkers of the Earth, Unite!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.maydayrooms.org/e/87/may-day-the-red-in-the-green\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":314,\"name\":\"AMINO ACID\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-01T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-02T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f70fee3aebb53dfc4643f75011bada28.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kyoto-based artist, producer and DJ NTsKi brings her label and party series AMINO ACID to London as part of a special two-city edition taking place across Tokyo and London. For AMINO ACID, which has been developing out of Kyoto, this marks its first event in Tokyo and its first simultaneous city-to-city edition with London.\\n\\nIn October 2025, NTsKi released her third album Euphoria on the Ohio-based label Orange Milk. Blending club music, ambient and pop, her distinctive sound has gained attention both in Japan and internationally.\\n\\nThe lineup features Detroit-born, London-based producer, DJ and composer Tristan Arp, known for releases on Wisdom Teeth, 3024, SLINK, and his own Human Pitch. The night will celebrate the release of his new record (re)weave on Kapsela, with a live club set of improvised hand-drumming and polyrhythmic freakouts.\\n\\nAlso joining the night are artists closely connected to NTsKi: Daigos and Jyn of Tokyo-based minimal groove band D.A.N., London-based Taigen Kawabe of Psychedelic noise rock band Bo Ningen, and a live performance by NTsKi herself.\\n\\nThe London edition takes place at Spanners. Connecting cities and scenes, AMINO ACID brings together artists from Japan and beyond for a night where different musical worlds intersect.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2388740\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":201,\"name\":\"Triptych x Local Action: Hodge, Tom Boogizm, harpriya\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-01T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-02T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a76241be1cedbe1c2e907738440240fe.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Triptych and Local Action join forces for the first time at South London’s Ormside Projects – with sets coming from harpriya, Tom Boogizm and Hodge, ahead of a forthcoming LP for the label.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":334,\"name\":\"A Day of Global South Trans Solidarity\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-02T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ce2735ede508dbec4639fa93b71ce7bc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A day of trans solidarity by the Mutual Aid Network for Trans People in South Asia aimed at awareness building.\\n\\nIn early March 2026, the Government of India introduced and passed, within two weeks, the “Transgender Protection of Rights Bill, 2026” in both the lower and upper houses of parliament with overwhelming and at an unprecendented speed.\\n\\nWithin a week on 31st March, the president of India signed the bill into an act. No Trans communities across the country were consulted in the writing and passing of this bill.\\n\\nIn this time, Trans communities in India have been organising around the bill (now an act), creating a concerted effort to communicate the effects of the bill, while at the same time, forming litigation teams to challenge it in state and national courts.\\n\\n🔥This event is led by South Asian Trans people and our loved ones who want to engage attention to the connected nature of anti-gender movements around the World that have, in India and beyond, successfully used trans people as scapegoats in a time of active genocide, and racial-capitalist destruction around the world. We welcome people from across movements, spaces, and places to come together in solidarity with South Asian/Global Majority Trans, Intersex and GNC people.\\n\\nWe have designed this event as a full-day programme that will bring bits of trans organising and creativity from communities in South Asia for people across movements to engage with here in the UK. If you are not able to join us for the entire day, join us for the parts you like!\\n\\n🎨We will also have prints, merch, and a tarot table - please do buy things from the vendors, tip artists and generously fill up our donation box. All the money raised will go towards funding urgent trans healthcare in India.\\n\\n📰Read more about the act here: https://www.instagram.com/p/DW_fP08DBTR/?img_index=1\\n\\nWe will be hosting a super exciting raffle as well! All who buy an online ticket will automatically be entered into the raffle!\\n\\n🚀Limited tickets available at the door, raffle tickets available on the day and cash preferred!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/a-day-of-global-south-trans-solidarity-tickets-1987731992899\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":321,\"name\":\"PageMasters Zine Fair\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"14b93bafbf399722d297699ab840a260.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us at Art Hub on Saturday 2nd and Sunday 3rd of May for the PageMasters Zine Fair, where you will find a mix of independent publishers and hundreds of titles on our communal table.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":232,\"name\":\"Analogue Animation Workshop: Extended\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-02T16:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d254efe8e6547406318aec281f8d7b80.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Get creative in this introductory class to analogue/hand-made animation. All materials are provided, you just need your phone!\\nAll are welcome at this new series of analogue and print animation workshops with director Miranda Peyton Jones.\\nEach session, learn, experiment and have fun with different hands-on animation techniques! A space to try out new ideas and meet fellow experimenters. Expect to come away with a piece of moving image and your printed materials.\\nNo previous animation or drawing skills necessary, all are welcome.\\n\\n2nd May:\\nFor this extended class, expect to learn about storyboarding, animation prodction and even sound! We will be using a range of materials from paper cut-outs to charcoal and pastels.\\n\\nFor this workshop you will need a smartphone and the free app 'Stop Motion Studio'.\\nDownload prior to the workshop.\\nUnder 18s are welcome, but must be acompanied by an adult.\\n\\nIf you can no longer make the event, please reach out to mirandapeytonjones@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://2MAYanalogueanimaiton.eventbrite.co.uk\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":237,\"name\":\"M.O.T. + DAY + NIGHT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1d55374557c8c05452bc0b86c3cb15fb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We'll be transforming the outdoor yard for an open air event in the day on May 2nd, which will then follow into a double unit event for the night.\\n\\nWe'll be linking up with 160 Unity, Club Romantico \\u0026 Nyege Nyege for the occasion.\\n\\n160 Unity x MOT starts with a Chicago footwork dance class from Kelli Forman at 22:00-22:30 for anyone looking to sharpen their works before NIGHT begins.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2369146\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":257,\"name\":\"The Hotel presents... Rocheman, Raisa K, Excel DJ\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-02T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f9cde7e2f12452f6add8d95dfb09a500.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Hotel is proud to present its second evening at The Horse Hospital, to mark the release of Basin by Rocheman. \\n\\nBasin is released as TH04 in a luxurious vinyl edition designed by Thomas Bush, with a 12-page lyric booklet with artwork by Rocheman and Loz Keystone. \\n\\nTo mark the occasion, The Hotel presents an evening fully curated by Rocheman, with copies of the release available for sale. \\n\\nHotel regular Excel DJ shall open the evening with their ‘spiritual ☆ vibes’, shortly followed by a solo set by Good Sad Happy Bad-founding member Raisa K. JB Glazer of Glint Music fame will soundtrack the evening during the intro and in-betweens.\\n\\nThe evening will close with a quartet performance by Rocheman, performing songs from Basin and their newest EPs Virtua Saint and Angel Storm. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":328,\"name\":\"Reds in the Rainbow. A night dedicated to Mark Ashton\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"67117eb67e2014730341ae1f895d48df.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Reds in the Rainbow. A night dedicated to Mark Ashton\\n\\nSaturday 2nd May / 7pm - 12am\\n\\nA night of resistance, music, and radical solidarity. \\n\\nThis event honours the life and legacy of Mark Ashton — a pioneering LGBTQ+ activist whose work continues to inspire movements today. Blending culture, politics, and community, the night brings together history and celebration in equal measure.\\n\\nAbout Mark Ashton \\u0026 LGSM:\\nIn 1984, during the UK miners’ strike, Mark Ashton co-founded Lesbians and Gays Support the Miners (LGSM). At a time of intense marginalisation, LGSM raised funds and built direct solidarity between queer communities and working-class miners. Their work became a powerful example of how collective struggle can transcend identity and build lasting political alliances rooted in socialist and Marxist principles.\\n\\nMark’s activism reflected a deep belief: that liberation is interconnected, and that real change comes through unity, organisation, and mutual support. Under conditions of repression, police violence, and media hostility, LGSM organised material support for striking miners — raising funds, building relationships, and forging political unity. This was not symbolic allyship. It was class solidarity in action.\\n\\nTheir politics were rooted in Marxism, Communism and Socialism — a recognition that queer oppression and class exploitation are produced by the same structures, and must be fought together.\\n\\nWhat to expect on the night:\\n\\n- A talk about LGBTQ+ Socialism, Marxism and Mark Ashton’s life, politics, and legacy\\n- Live music celebrating queer resistance and culture \\n- Film screening of Framed Youth — Revenge of the Teenage Perverts from the London Community Video - Archive plus other archival footage \\n- Music for dancing to inspired by Pits and Perverts, Red Wedge and Rock Against Racism\\n\\nThis is not a passive night of remembrance. It's a space to listen, think, dance, talk and organise — rooted in the legacy of LGBTQ+ resistance and working-class solidarity. In a time of division, austerity, and ongoing attacks on both the working-class and LGBTQ+ communities, the politics of Mark Ashton remain urgent. \\n\\nThis night is about solidarity as practice, not theory, Socialism as collective survival, Queer liberation tied to working-class struggle. We don’t inherit these histories to admire them. We inherit them to continue them!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34960/for-a-friend-a-night-dedicated-to-mark-ashton\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":164,\"name\":\"Texture Magazine no.3 ~ Launch Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b68b50640e08c6830f7e7fb3f995cd0c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"UPDATE\\n\\nUnfortunately we have had to cancel this event.\\n\\nAll ticket holders will be refunded.\\n\\nWe are still launching the magazine on the 2nd May \\u003c3\\n\\n~\\n\\nJoin us for an evening of sounds, words, and moving images to celebrate the launch of Texture Magazine no.3.\\n\\nFeaturing:\\n\\nlive *international debut* by New York's poc\\nbeauty in the moment by Boy Lucid\\nsonic fractions by jb glazer\\nlivestream audio by soundcamp co-founder Mort Drew\\nspoken words by Christian Jones\\ndeejay stylings by Madjestic Kasual\\narchival netvideo by Organ Tapes\\nhatwise mythology by Adum Brate\\n\\n+ MORE TBA\\n\\n~\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":322,\"name\":\"Channel Orange Room\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3884bd8d6a87300a3463da99fca78b34.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Channel Orange Room 🧡\\n\\nOur flagship night ... Loud, unruly, and visually immersive.\\n\\nWhere underground energy meets artistic experimentation.\\n\\nOur main stage for the sonically brave.\\n\\nMay 2nd 2026:\\n\\n8-10PM | Art Exhibition | Tattoos | Styling Corner | Games\\n\\n10PM-3AM | 2-Room Party:\\u2028We’re taking over both rooms all night. Expect an incredible lineup!\\n\\nROOM 1\\n\\nLISA KEEKS\\n\\nRAIDAA\\n\\nFREDDIE XODOS\\n\\nAYCHIBS\\n\\nELLADHC\\n\\nROOM 2\\n\\nDONNIE SUNSHINE\\n\\nAMBRR\\n\\nDAMNSHAQ\\n\\nDADDY CHULO\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/6dlke3-channel-orange-room-2nd-may-the-orange-room-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":356,\"name\":\"MAXXING presents: Tonic\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-02T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"03d78667d0ae83a19d00a422876819a3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"02/05/26 | 10pm - 4am | Ormside Projects | 21+\\n\\nApproaching Maxxing’s four year anniversary in May comes a new experience: Tonic.\\n\\nAs mainline Maxxing events will continue to push emerging modern artists alongside curated visual spectacles, Tonic embraces the stripped-back essence of the dancefloor. Intimate, refined, and rooted in the preservation of club culture for the new era.\\n\\n21+. Lineup remaining unannounced.\\nDjing electronic dance music all night long.\\n\\nLet the smoke machine be your incense. Breath with me.\\n\\nTickets available via maxxing.uk\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.maxxing.uk/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":280,\"name\":\"CV FREQS\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ebf10bf43e50501e85566956de2f4741.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"CV FREQS events focus on how artists use their custom modular synthesizers for their live performances and music production. The community of CV FREQS is made up of synthesizer enthusiasts, researchers and builders, electronic musicians, audiovisual artists, and sound designers. CV FREQS invites anyone who is interested in learning more about what we do with our custom electronic instruments to come join us for a full live concert and gathering of modular synthesizer artists.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/bb89qo-cv-freqs-3rd-may-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":349,\"name\":\"54 The Gate presents GATE FASHION\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9b2e9764740acc56006b8b60b7c0bbb9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Cobblestone catwalk with some star walkers and walks. Over 100 bespoke fashion garments made by The Gate, using clothing salvaged from The Contemporary Wardrobe Collection. Styled by Alice Fraser, The Horse Hospital Collective, and associates. Makeup by Olivia Wiles (makruar), runway soundtrack by Rat Section.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":267,\"name\":\"3WD PARTY\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-04T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0f8c807992430b90ce0edd21898ab077.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a long evening at Avalon Cafe on Sunday 3rd May (Bank Holiday) \\u003c3 will be nice to see everyone. Long overdue a dance at Avalon!\\n\\nWe’ll be serving food, and spending some time discussing possibilities for 3WD 2026. Lots of great things came of this last time - vending machines, churches, etc’ - come chat. Strictly informal discussions.\\n\\nWe’ve got a very exciting line-up of: Rael,‘Tutorial Island’.., and BJ Holy performing live ✨ and Mellowdramatics, Culturalwerker, DJ Tissue and friends on decks.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":289,\"name\":\"Palestinian Sound Archive Local Angels Vol.2: The Scorpios + Dirar Kalash\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d5acf2f9a153079ef8b9348ef6fb69f5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for Palestinian Sound Archive x Local Angels Vol.2, where we invite new and old friends to the stage. Kicking off our early summer programme with some beautiful guests...\\n\\nThis time, The Scorpios are joining us in person for what will be an unforgettable set at our new home from home, New River Studios for May Bank Holiday. We're so happy that Palestinian composer and experimental musician Dirar Kalash for be warming up for the band, with vinyl played by Palestinian Sound Archive until closing time.\\n\\nThe Scorpios are a band originally form Sudan that melds Arabic rhythms and guitar chops (and a kind of swooning cyclical ecstasy) with a raw Eastern funk feel, properly dismantling cultural barriers in pursuit of a unifying rhythmic bliss. Heavy bass, synths, horns and percussions drive through traditional Sudanese forms to create a sound that owes as much to Detroit as it does to Khartoum.\\n\\nDirar Kalash is a multi-disciplinary musician and sound artist whose work spans a wide range of musical and sonic practices within a variety of instrumental, compositional and improvisational contexts. He has produced several solo and collaborative musical albums and is active as touring musician, who has also created several sound installations, live audio-visual performances and photography projects.\\n\\nPalestinian Sound Archive is a celebration of music, spoken word and album artwork from historic Palestine, mainly from the 1960s – 1990s. It is part of Majazz Project, a record label and research platform founded by Mo’min Swaitat in 2020, spanning everything from field recordings of Bedouin weddings to revolutionary albums from the First and Second Intifadas, dabke, instrumental, synth, poetry, soul, folk songs and jazz.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/palestinian-sound-archive-local-angels-vol2-the-scorpios-dirar-kalash-tickets-1987129764618?aff=erelexpmlt\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":350,\"name\":\"The Horse + Visit Me + Infinite Expanse (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-03T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"feead08850bcc13bf0dfe2642f55c673.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Horse is a six-piece group based between London and the Fens. The band self-released its debut album in a limited run of LPs and CDs in November 2025. Monorail Music described the album as \\\"a big melting pot of sound collages, strings, ambience and the stretching of what collaboration can sound like without constraint.\\\" At SJQ, the Horse will be playing a set of new material.\\n\\nNow firmly established as a 3-piece, Visit Me has been a slowly expanding project of phantom pop that started where willowy melodies wisp gently over wraithy drones and skeletal ostinato. Their debut album 'Daystar' comes out on April 22nd on Smudge Records.\\n\\nInfinite Expanse is a label run by London-based sound archivist and researcher Tom Gibbs. It began in 2017 as a YouTube channel focused on sharing music not otherwise available online, gradually evolving toward deeper explorations of the independent cassette scenes of the 1980s and ’90s.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/the-horse-visit-me-infinite-expanse-dj-tickets-1985920494659?utm-campaign=social\\u0026utm-content=attendeeshare\\u0026utm-medium=discovery\\u0026utm-term=listing\\u0026utm-source=cp\\u0026aff=ebdsshcopyurl\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":313,\"name\":\"Earthworm with TSUNIMAN, Kincaid [live], Avsluta, Millie McKee, Kilm [live] \\u0026 jeet\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-04T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0f7ecee0b20ff182373ff73590c00fd7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nEarthworm sprouts from the soil once more with sonic offerings from a whole host of local leftfield legends.\\n\\nThe 3rd of May sees us descend onto Club Cheek for an exploration into the realms of psychedelia via the portals of bass, dub, trance, ambient, spiritual sounds, techno et al…\\n\\nLeading the charge in no particular order:\\nTsuniman\\nKincaid (live)\\nAvsluta\\nMillie Mckee\\nKilm (live)\\njeet\\n\\nWhilst each artist brings a unique flavour, perspective and style to the table - all are united by a sense of curiosity, a passion for the natural and an adoration for the depth of sound and it’s translation into movement.\\nWe’re so excited to see this togetherness take shape and we hope you can join us in rolling around the proverbial swamp with us come bank holiday weekend.\\n\\nno one deserves to be priced out of a dance so if you’re struggling then just get in touch and we’ll sort something out, no questions asked ^_^\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2409836\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":345,\"name\":\"Pherotone 1st birthday with Madelic \\u0026 Elianne\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-04T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0ec3ad08a329f1cf7df1903e79789506.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pherotone celebrates its 1st birthday at one of London's best clubs - Venue M.O.T!\\n\\nPherotone is a female-led party for FLINTA \\u0026 queer communities, as well as respectful allies. We're all about creating moments of connection on the dancefloor and a safe space where DJs and dancers are free to express themselves fully.\\n\\nExpect high energy house, trance and techno with a health dosage of sass. What better way to spend Bank Holiday Sunday?!\\n\\nWe have an incredible all-FLINTA line-up gracing those famous decks with an immaculate soundsystem. We've been partying at M.O.T since it opened and will be making the most of every minute of our club takeover.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2402976\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":320,\"name\":\"Ormside presents: Nkisi, Trailcam, Conrad Pack (live), Astrid Sonne (DJ) \\u0026 Canje\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-03T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-04T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"804e005ce630308b944a82333be0f472.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For Sunday May Day bank holiday Ormside hosts a full throttle night of music from a wide berth of highly esteemed artists.\\n\\nWelcoming Tronto’s own Trailcam (latest alias of E-Saggila) whose output evokes a rich and dub-laden sound rooted within house and techno. Recent output on Northern Electronics and Short Span Records demonstrates a world constantly shifting with clean edges eroded by repetition and drifts alike. Having played throughout the EU circuit it’s a pleasure to welcome her to London for their Ormside debut.\\n \\nNkisi is the moniker of musician Melika Ngombe Kolongo - who, as no understatement, is a venue favourite. Influenced as much by ancient Kongo rhythms as rhythmic noise, Gabba and Belgian Hardcore her output reflects an acute focus on intensity.\\n\\nOff the back of intense roadtesting throughout Europe, Conrad Pack arrives for his first London liveset [and in fact gig] of 2026. Pack co-runs SELN Recording where his productions explore the fertile terrain between tuff soundsystem steppers and high-BPM techno. His more recent productions explore a distorted, hard-edged and dub-enriched techno sound which has been showcased on imprints including Lost Domain and most recently Semantica Records.\\n\\nAstrid Sonne is a composer hailing from Copenhagen, Denmark - now firmly located in London. Having garnered significant attention with her 2024 outing Great Doubt, highlighting the artist's ability to move from more abstract composition to a distinct vision of songwriting, she has also formulated a dedicated following via her monthly NTS residency. She will be closing the night with a focused DJ set.\\n\\nCanje (formerly Skins) is a Tamil-Canadian artist based in London. Originally a producer for Metro Zu \\u0026 Goth Money in the 2010s Canje has since pursued his own sound through his own solo projects including the 2022 LP “Never Curse”. Following recent works for live scores and performances he will open the night with a signature DJ set.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2412552\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":293,\"name\":\"Listening with ‘Still Noise’ - a sound workshop with Zhuo Mengting\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-04T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-04T14:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"69bacd246a426a4087715a2c8f925823.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"What counts as noise, and who gets to decide?\\n\\nListening with ‘Still Noise’ is a workshop exploring sound, space, and the ways noise and silence are organised around us.\\n\\nThrough discussion, listening and sound collecting, participants will explore why some sounds are treated as disturbance, while others pass unnoticed or are made to disappear. Guided by prompts from the artist, the session invites members of the public, artists and curious listeners alike to share recordings, take part in a short listening walk, and reflect on how personal, social and spatial contexts shape what we hear.\\n\\nNo previous knowledge or experience is needed, only curiosity and a phone or simple recording device if you have one.\\n\\nThe workshop will also introduce participants to open-source sound mapping platforms as creative tools for documenting, locating and thinking with sound beyond the session itself. The session forms part of the wider research and development of STILL NOISE,  a new performance project by Zhuo Mengting, while remaining a space for shared listening, reflection and exchange. \\n\\n\\n☀️ The workshop operates on a pay-what-you-can basis.\\n☀️ Participants can enjoy a selection of drinks at a discounted rate at etsdts (subject to availability).\\n\\n*Please note that the workshop venue is at lower ground floor and is not fully accessibly. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://buytickets.at/zhuomengting/2168949\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":149,\"name\":\"Punks For Palestine VI\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-04T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-04T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1a000098fadbb8cef2c750e4e62fea3c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Punks For Palestine VI\\n\\nAll proceeds split between \\nThe Sameer Project\\nProviding aid to displaced families on the ground in Gaza\\n\\nDa'm: Defend and Mobilize\\nSupporting direct action and activism in the UK against the Israeli arms trade.\\n\\nLouder than ever as this world grows harder. As always: hardcore, punk and hiphop joining forces in solidarity.\\n\\n\\nFeaturing\\nBuds.\\nBig riff emo punk\\n\\nChinned\\nThe Stevenage Grindcore Mafia, reunited for 1 night only. \\n\\nKemastry (CMPND)\\nShamanic wordplay from a uk hiphop legend\\n\\nKila Kosa\\nSouth London Hardcore\\n\\nMashaal\\nLondon hardcore by kids of immigrants.\\n\\nPerp Walk\\nChain stomp fury for the moshers.\\n\\nRitual Error\\nPost hardcore noise for the revolution\\n\\nSarsour\\n🪳🪳🪳\\n\\nShooting Daggers\\nLONDON QUEERCORE\\n\\nSpeit\\nIrish-Palestinian freedom rap\\n\\nUnwitnessed\\nBrand new London hardcore. Get down early and testify...\\n\\nYung Yusuf\\nRaw rebellious bars from the diaspora\\n\\nWe'll also have charity materials and information from other Palestinian relief efforts and demonstrations, as well as some new opportunities to support Palestinian arts and businesses in London.\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\nTickets £13\\n\\\"Solidarity Tickets\\\" £19 (optional extra donation)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/punks-for-palestine-2\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":244,\"name\":\"Global Cowboys + Ropeburn\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-05T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-05T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5ed9eb5eb2366618649377c281db8678.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands brings Ivy House stalwart Sam Gowans back to its iconic stage with his exciting new project 'Global Cowboys'. Alongside the new emo-folk band on the scene, Rope Burn. It's going to be a night to remember. Don't miss it.\\nGlobal Cowboys is a new project by Sam Gowans. Crafted in secret studio and home recording sessions, the Cowboys draw from influences in the janglier categories of 20th Century guitar music alongside the sound worlds of Eno and Television. Above all else, Global Cowboys guitar-led compositions aim to explore, in equal measure, the hopeful and the forlorn.\\nRope Burn is an alternative/slowcore/post-rock inspired quintet featuring trumpet and banjo based in London. The group hails from Ireland and the UK with songs that spill into each other to make a cohesive and fluid set with all members singing. Ropeburn pulls influences from Caroline, Alex G and American Football whilst featuring members from Blood Wizard, Kissing on Camera, Baggio and Bog Band.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/z9079beb56bd\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":378,\"name\":\"NLDC: Third Birthday\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"57b2e6e9dcf70f0a9ee0f91eb8c75c26.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"xxxxxxxxx\\nxxxxxxxx (xxxxxxxx xxx)\\nxxxxx xxxx\\nxxxx xxxxxx\\nxx\\nxxxx x xxxxxxxxx\\nxxxxx\\n\\nLineup exclusively in the NLDC Rinse.fm show 26.04.26 via Soundcloud.\\n \\nUsual birthday goodies.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":258,\"name\":\"GRAIN Presents: John Wall, Jack Dove + Caius Williams, Regan Bowering + Theodora Laird\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-06T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-06T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b0a4350d7eedd39fcdb4fe3eb3dbd78f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"GRAIN is a concert series and archiving project for experimental and improvised music, largely happening within South Bermondsey, and programmed / produced by Caius Williams \\u0026 Theodora Laird.\\n\\nThrough programming and documenting new and adventurous music through collaboration, archiving, workshops, and performances, the project explores the ongoing dialogue between the transience of DIY art spaces and the communities that inhabit them. \\n\\nJOHN WALL:\\nBorn 1950.\\nStarted composing 1990 and still going.\\nPlayed and collaborated with some good people.\\nThere is no promotional visual youtube material.\\n\\ngo here https://johnwall.bandcamp.com/\\nand here https://utterpsalm.blogspot.com/\\n\\nJACK DOVE:\\nis a musician and artist from London exploring contemporary composition methods through electronic experimentation and performance. Dove produces unpredictable listening experiences. He uses combinations of pyro, strobes, and other types of artificial light to interact with and control his homemade electronic circuits and mechanical machines, finding ways to generate unique sound textures from responding resonating objects.\\n\\nPrevious and ongoing shows include: Berlin Atonal '23, a carpark outside Bern train station, and ISC Club for Norient Film Festival 2022. He brings together his pyro-acoustic progressions annually at Fireworks, for the 4th and year in December 2024 at Ormside Projects, London.\\n\\nCAIUS WILLIAMS: \\nis a musician from London who plays the double bass, guitar, and bass guitar. He works in collaboration with others, alongside various solo projects, often working with improvisation and explorations of resonance, and perception.   \\n\\nREGAN BOWERING\\nRegan Bowering’s solo work explores the rhythmic and percussive potential at the intersections of improvisation, sound art and experimental composition. Her performance practice incorporates various combinations of drums, objects, amplification, microphones and feedback. Her debut solo release (Bezirk, Dec 2023) Solos for _ _ _ _ Spaces was described as “a play of contrasts, contradicting voluminous expressions with confined phrases, taming resounding feedback with faint percussive flutters, but one that feels driven by the desire to craft electrifying drama rather than pure autotelic dissonance.” (The Quietus). She is one third of a collaborative project with Li Song and Conal Blake, with two releases: “2 Movements” (Feedback Moves, 2024) and \\\"Music for Snare Drums and Portable Speakers\\\" (Infant Tree, 2023). Regan is currently a visiting scholar at Columbia University in NYC, as part of her ongoing practice-based PhD at Goldsmiths, University of London.\\n\\nTHEODORA LAIRD\\nis a vocalist and multidisciplinary artist. Releases under her solo project ‘feeo’ have received critical acclaim. Theodora's practice has involved in tandem with an interest in situating narratives within freely improvised music, specifically through frequent involvement in the GRAIN residency.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":288,\"name\":\"Nueen + Flora Yin Wong + Nexcyia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-06T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-06T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"da837ca5bf76f64976fec9f0ac31c955.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Mallorca-born and Barcelona-based, 𝐍𝐮𝐞𝐞𝐧 has been quietly shaping a singular voice within the contemporary electronic music landscape. His music moves between ambient, trap, and experimental realms - a delicate blend of atmospheric depth and rhythmic tension that reflects both emotional clarity and sonic curiosity. His new AV Live show, explores this and is influenced by his past and present productions accompanied by visuals from visual artist Mimi Bow. With acclaimed releases on Hyperdub, 3XL, and Stroom, and coverage from Resident Advisor, The Wire, Pitchfork, and FACT, Nueen has established himself as a distinctive voice among the new generation of producers. Following the release of Algorithmic Accompaniment with Jason Kolar on Stroom, Nueen will release a new album at the start of 2026.⁣⁣\\n⁣⁣\\n𝐅𝐥𝐨𝐫𝐚 𝐘𝐢𝐧 𝗪𝐨𝐧𝐠 is an artist \\u0026 writer from London. Her first two albums 'Holy Palm' and ‘Cold Reading’ were released on Modern Love and has appeared on labels PAN, Tectonic, Paralaxe Editions, Nyege Nyege, and Shelter Press. In 2023, she launched the experimental imprint Doyenne. She has played institutes like Palais de Tokyo Paris, The ICA London, MACRO Roma, MMCA Seoul, Fondation Beyeler Basel, Triennale Milano, Somerset House, The V\\u0026A Museum, Atonal Berlin, Unsound Krakow, MUTEK Peru / Buenos Aires / Montreal, ISSUE Project Room, WWWB Tokyo, SOTO Kyoto etc. Her first book ‘Liturgy', exploring the lines of fiction \\u0026 non-fiction through psychogeography was published in 2021 on PAN x Primary Information. In 2023 she launched a label and publishing house, Doyenne, releasing works from the likes of Alex Zhang Hungtai, Claire Rousay, YL Hooi, Teresa Winter, writers Heather McCalden, Mira Mattar, Lucinda Chua and Lisa Lerkenfeldt and more.⁣⁣\\n⁣⁣\\n𝐍𝐄𝐗𝐂𝐘𝐈𝐀 is the solo project of Adam Dove, a Paris-born, Berlin based American sound artist and sound designer. His work might be described as outsider ambient, blending underground experimental music with sound design, textural soundscapes, and sound mangling techniques. Moving through shifting samples, moods and emotional registers, he explores themes of otherness and belonging. Through dense layering and continuous audio manipulation, he creates ever-evolving pieces that draw listeners into a sonic journey, eschewing the over-visited constraints of a tempo grid.⁣⁣\\n⁣⁣\\n⁣⁣⁣𝐩𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐝 𝐛𝐲 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐫𝐚𝐥𝐝 𝐩𝐥𝐚𝐧𝐞𝐭⁣⁣⁣\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":true,\"cancelled_at\":\"2026-05-05T08:52:53.316185Z\",\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":247,\"name\":\"Lost Domain\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-06T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f2dabbeee6e6ad581ef7c1811f4e4d56.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"if you love images more than people\\nif you love sex with your reflection\\nif you love acid depression\\nif you love afterworld sound\\n\\n::: lostdomain :::\\n\\nin the heart of london's Glittering West End\\n\\n\\u003e\\u003e\\u003e\\n\\nHelen of Troy, 20 Hanway Street, London W1 –\\n(nearest tube: Tottenham Court Road) \\n \\nadmission via advance ticket or guestlist only.\\n\\n[[[ when you get there you will already be there ]]]\\n\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":390,\"name\":\"Stephen Belowsky - HONK Book launch at Plaster Store\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f7a719c93dd51b2e2dfef56b5166fe11.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The greatest rock n roll poet Stephen Belowsky book launch at Plaster Shop on 7 May. \\n\\nAfter honing his craft in New York’s Lower East Side, and becoming part of the anti-folk scene at the Sidewalk Cafe and Bowery Poetry club in the 1980s, Belowsky quickly acquired a steady loyal following, including music industry legends Sir Bob Geldof, Alan McGee of Creation Records and Andy Bell (Oasis, Ride).  \\n\\nA true citizen of the free world, Belowsky’s whirlwind journey has taken him around the world before finally finding a home in Perth, Australia. A countercultural legend and a dexterous storyteller, Belowsky’s poetry is marked by journalistic urgency. His work has appeared in various magazines as well as recordings on Alan McGee’s Creation23 label. For many years he was Virgin Australia Airline’s in-flight-entertainment pop-poet and has performed his award-winning poetry on stages around the world. \\n\\nHONK is one of the two debut titles published in Spring 2026 by 020-DESK-ZERO, a 24-hour poetry and sound art phoneline turned publishing imprint. Brainchild of the British artist and sculptor James Jessiman, the free phoneline is a nomadic platform for presenting boundary pushing writing, sound works and more.  It is accessible for free from any UK phone number by dialling 020-3375-9376.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":286,\"name\":\"Mouthpiece and Trail Shoes: nnscya and Wong Winsome Dumalagan \",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ad69df30787c9d048f1f47b124e75b99.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For their first ever performance in London, nnscya and Wong Winsome Dumalagan, two exceptional artists active in Hong Kong's vibrant art and performance scenes, will appear together at South London's Eat the Sunshine . Down the Sun.\\n\\nAnnisa Cheung aka nnscya will present a solo sound-based performance, followed by a screening of Wong Winsome Dumalagan's recent film \\u003cem\\u003eThe Vault of the Cloven Void 歇息日後，籬笆倒塌的園\\u003c/em\\u003e. Both artists will then bring their skills together in a collaborative performance. Finally, curator Edward Sanderson and the artists will chat about the works and their Hong Kong context.\\n\\nWe are grateful to Eat the Sunshine . Down the Sun (etsdts) for hosting this event. etsdts is an artist-run café/space in Kennington and we encourage you to support them by purchasing their (really) tasty food and refreshing drinks.\\n\\nDoors open: 19:00\\nPerformance starts: 19:30\\n(The cafe will be open throughout)\\n(Please note that the venue is in the basement and access involves stairs)\\n\\nBook early to avoid disapppointment. Only 25 tickets available!\\n\\nTickets £10\\n\\n📸 poster design by Wong Winsome Dumalagan / nnuu\\n\\n---\\n\\nLive Set:\\nnnscya\\n\\nScreening:\\nWong Winsome Dumalagan\\n\\nLive collaboration set:\\nnnscya + Wong Winsome Dumalagan\\n\\nArtists sharing with the curator\\n\\nCurated by escdotdot\\n\\n\\u003cstrong\\u003eAnnisa Cheung aka nnscya:\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\n\\nBandcamp: https://nnscya.bandcamp.com/album/pie\\nIG: https://www.instagram.com/nnscya/\\nWebsite: https://nnscya.com\\n\\nKnown as nnscya, Ching-yu Annisa Cheung is a composer, musician, and singer. Her work spans various musical genres, drawing influence from experimental music, industrial noise, classical orchestral, and alternative pop. Past works include installations, dance, and short film soundtracks, as well as chamber and orchestral composition. Inspired by daily trivia, she explores the crossroads of vibration and senses, sound and emotions, as in lived experiences, memories, and the tactility of the body, through her works.\\n\\n張靜瑜以 nnscya 的身份發表音樂。他的作品受實驗音樂、工業噪音、古典管弦樂，以及另類流行音樂影響，跨越音樂類型的邊界。過往作品函蓋裝置、舞蹈及短片配樂、室樂、管弦樂。他觀察日常瑣事，如生活經驗、記憶和觸覺萃取當中微小的訊號，探索當中有關震動與感知、聲音與情感的交錯。\\n\\n\\u003cstrong\\u003eWong Winsome Dumalagan:\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\n\\nMV by nnscya, directed by Wong Winsome Dumalagan: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pk6910mEQKM\\nIG: https://www.instagram.com/wsome_wd/\\nWebsite: https://www.winsomewongd.com\\n\\nWong Winsome Dumalagan’s practice revolves around videography, images, and installations, often rooted in the cultural contexts she traverses. She delves into understanding places, roots, and mobility, exploring how everyday narratives of people, nature, and objects construct knowledge, through both planned and serendipitous encounters. With videos and images she captured or collected from those she encountered, she sculpts and layers visuals, and often incorporates discarded household items, inexpensive and sometimes flawed materials, to create temporary spaces that are continuously reconfigurable, probing the boundaries of representation in both imagery and material. \\n\\n⿈慧⼼的實踐以錄像､ 影像和裝置為主 並且經常源⾃她所經歷的⽂化脈絡｡ 透過有計劃或偶然的旅程和相遇 她試圖理解地⽅､ 根源和流動性探索⼈､ ⾃然與物件的⽇常敘事如何構建知識｡ 她以⾃⼰拍攝或從遇到的⼈所收集得來的錄像和圖像作為原材料雕刻和層疊影像並經常同時以廢棄的家居⽤品､ 廉價或有瑕疵的材料建構出可以不斷重組的臨時空間思考影像與物質在再現上的界限｡\\n\\n\\u003cstrong\\u003eDr Edward Sanderson 李蔼德 aka escdotdot\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\nDr Edward Sanderson is a writer and curator researching non-mainstream sonic culture in China. They received their PhD from the Academy of Visual Arts, Hong Kong Baptist University in 2022. Sanderson is also building an archive of experimental sound and recently curated the museum survey, \\u003cem\\u003eIt Always Sounds Somewhere: Sounding Sound Practice in Chinese Mainland and Hong Kong Since the 1990s\\u003c/em\\u003e at the Beijing Inside-Out Art Museum. Together with Ingrid Pui Yee Chu, they co-curated \\u003cem\\u003eSounds Like Print\\u003c/em\\u003e (2023) and its associated programming, including several project commissions, conversations, and live performances for Tai Kwun Contemporary in Hong Kong.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":387,\"name\":\"Book Launch: Witness to the Hellfire of Genocide: A Testimony from Gaza\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"dbc276081813d6e8f919e53c1ce4fe22.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nJoin us for the launch of Witness to the Hellfire of Genocide: A Testimony from Gaza, a searing first-person account from inside the siege\\n\\nJoin us for the launch of Witness to the Hellfire of Genocide: A Testimony from Gaza (2025) by Wasim Said, a searing first-person account from inside the siege. This book refuses the distance that writing about Gaza often imposes, it is a testimony that holds you to the reality of what Gaza has been subjected to over the past three years.\\n\\nA 22-year-old living in Gaza, Wasim recounts his testimony as he watches the horrors that unfold in front of him. As much as it is harrowing, his testimony, also unveils a world that we must fight to save. In reading his words and bearing witness to the genocide, the book urges the reader to acknowledge their responsibility to join the struggle for Palestinian liberation. In that sense the testimony is transformed into a call to witness.\\n\\nIn conversation, Mezna Qato and Nihal El Aasar will discuss the book’s significance as a historical document, as literature and as a political intervention. They will discuss what it means to bear witness, how testimony functions under genocide and why this account demands to be read now.\\n\\nMezna Qato teaches history at the University of Cambridge. She is a founding steering member of LIbrarians and Archivists with Palestine, amongst other formations.\\n\\nNihal El Aasar is a writer, researcher, political analyst and an organiser with the Palestinian Youth Movement.\\n\\nHosted by Mosaic Rooms, in collaboration with Palestinian Youth Movement and PalFest.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/book-launch-witness-to-the-hellfire-of-genocide-a-testimony-from-gaza-tickets-1987993456945?aff=oddtdtcreator\\u0026keep_tld=true\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":369,\"name\":\"Bodypolitik 2\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"92b12f26e486ef30cd3621d2c2c943f2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pay What U Like\\nProceeds –\\u003e South London Children’s Arts Charities\\n\\nimprovised sounds 4 u 2 move 2\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":303,\"name\":\"Kiss Me You Fool\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7ea15cb44e61c42eab644bd8232138d4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nA warm spring evening of live sound, visuals and shared space, from 7 pm till late. Expect experimental electronics, bass, techno and harder rhythms. Asian food is served throughout. Zines, self-published work and merch available. Workshops and open sessions alongside the music. Come for a set or stay all night.\\n\\n☆*:.｡. o(≧▽≦)o .｡.:*☆\\n\\nm-onz is an algorithmic audio visual artist and founder of genre[fatigue]\\n\\np3b3 is a musician, producer, and live artist from Bordeaux. With a background in percussion and jazz, he creates groovy, sunlit techno influenced by old-school pumping tribe and 90s/00s hardtek. Blending Bordeaux’s electronic scene with free party culture, he improvises and experiments freely, making his music both engaging and human.\\n\\nXuanni_space has been active in the southern Chinese underground music scene since 2013. Starting from free improvisation with violin, her setup has evolved over the years into a Digitakt, a no-input mixer, and a Nintendo 3DS running DSN-12 — a synthesiser based on the MS-10 circuit design. She feeds signals into the mixer to generate feedback, letting unstable loops produce patterns she couldn't have planned. The DSN-12 lays in acid melodies. Her live sets collapse rave energy and noise into the same moment.\\n\\nKlamm draws from thumping Hard House to grinning growling Acid Techno to Pumping Tribe to create a sonic space you can have a ponder and get settled into a nice bop.\\n\\nMSO is a project by Mathias Obrzut, a multimedia artist working across still and moving image, sound, and graphic design. His work explores our interaction with the natural and artificial environment, examining the impact of technology on culture. A unique background in physics motivates his goal of bringing the subjects of art and science closer together, aiming to uncover new possibilities of representation.\\n\\nCYAN Yanyi Chen is a filmmaker, DJ and illustrator. Their work focuses on filmmaking and sound as practices of place-making and resistance. Their sets draw from 70s Cambodian rock, electronic, breakcore, and y2k nostalgic futurism.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2410759?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":34,\"name\":\"Conjuring #3 ft. Loraine James, Valentina Magaletti, Cameron Picton, Nkisi\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a889b17fdaf20bc53239aa140e4cf19e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Conjuring is a monthly live improvisation series curated by Studio Njoku, and presented by Club Cheek.\\n\\nIt brings together leading experimental musicians for collaborative, improvised performances. The project foregrounds musical dialogue, community building and spiritual expression.\\n\\nEach show features a unique lineup of musicians performing a one-time improvisation around a motif developed by Tony Njoku.\\n\\nCameron Picton is a guitarist and bassist who draws on American Primitivist, Brazilian and experimental musical forms. Previously of London prog group Black Midi, Picton is currently working on a new project, My New Band Believe.\\n\\nLoraine James musical approach displays voracious musical curiosity and an exciting, peerless approach to making music. She has released several acclaimed records on Hyperdub.\\n\\nValentina Magaletti is a queer drummer, composer, and multi-instrumentalist who treats percussion as a political and poetic instrument—an unruly body that refuses straight lines, fixed identities, and normative rhythms. Her work dismantles the boundaries between noise, ritual, and music, transforming ceramics, found objects, and skin-based textures into tools for resistance.\\n\\nNkisi produces intense, powerful club tracks equally influenced by African polyrhythms, hardcore techno, and ’70s Italian horror films. Gravitating toward the more aggressive side of dance music, yet maintaining a heavy emotional factor as well as a sense of dreaminess.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/53rx3d-loraine-james-valentina-magaletti-cameron-picton-7th-may-club-cheek-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":357,\"name\":\"Scenic Route presents thredd \\u0026 Hornet (support)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-07T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"950f3702156d63522bcde048b9df06c7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Thredd return for their premiere 2026 London live show. The super band consisting of Imogen \\u0026 The Knife, Max Winter \\u0026 Will Lister cultivating their 'Cold Pop' sound for people 'up for a party, down for a cry'.\\n\\nTheir debut album 'It's Lovely Come On In' garnered a swell of critical acclaim with support from the likes of Pigeons \\u0026 Planes, Line of Best Fit, Nina Protocol, 6 Music, Radio 1 and more.\\n\\nJoined by Hornet, an alternate pop singer, songwriter and producer from New Jersey. Her sounds blends emotive, ballad-like songwriting and vocal melodies with catchy synth lines and punchy production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2403125\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":327,\"name\":\"One Jazz \\u0026 Audio Gold presents On The Corner at The Mildmay\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-07T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-08T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a97a72fed69eee7dfd7e76e0eea4a150.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"One Jazz and Audio Gold proudly present Jamie Harms' Clio - LIVE\\n\\nA cure for isolation, CLIO is the latest project from saxophonist and composer Jamie Harms. A fluid group of some of the best young players in the capital, CLIO seeks to bring people together, both on the stage, and in the audience.\\n\\nSet up by Jamie initially as a way to connect with his friends through music, the group has since crystallised a new sound drawing on the depth of the UK's music scene.Playing original tunes and reinterpretations of other songs, inspired by a variety of artists including Kenny Wheeler, Porij, John Zorn, and Laura Marling.\\n\\nPlus DJ's Jez Nelson and Robin AG, all on the Audio Gold audiophile sound system.\\n\\n\\nMembers £10, Non-Members £12\\n\\nImportant - If you purchase a ticket as a Club member please be prepared to show your membership card at the door \\u0026 show our bar staff for member price drinks.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/mildmayclubandinstituteltd/2114472\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":245,\"name\":\"Potato + Morgan Noise + Big Oil\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-08T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5a27966861f13aae0dfc17b542300c33.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Potato headlines the first instalment of a special run of shows 'Round and Round' at The Ivy House, in celebration of their new single.\\nPotato is a six-human troupe hailing from South East London, quickly making their mark on the London art-rock scene with the release of their debut EP 'Stew' in 2024 and second surprise EP ‘Antiques and Interludes’ in March, 2026.\\nSupport comes from Morgan Noise and Glass Eel.\\nThis is not a night to miss.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/V2f19d2251b8\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":355,\"name\":\"Shortwave: attentions by Harilay Rabenjamina\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-08T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"17eee609e43825b54801f39b7444e809.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"London Performance Studios premieres attentions, a new live audio-visual concept album by Harilay Rabenjamina, that traverses familial, intimate and political registers. Blending pop, ambient, R\\u0026B, Malagasy and classical influences, attentions is part narrative cinematic performance and part pop concert. \\n\\nThe work unfolds between London, Paris, Antananarivo and Pessac, as it moves through shifting voices and registers, to explore forms of mobility across places, genres and modes of expression. The music is performed live with Thelia.\\n\\n7:30pm Doors\\n8pm Performance (50 min run time)\\nEnter event via Ormside Street.\\n\\nShortwave is a new festival of sound and performance unfolding across four independent venues in south east London: South London Gallery, London Performance Studios, IKLECTIK and ORMSIDE Projects. Bringing together international and local artists, musicians and DJs, the festival spans two nights of commissioned live works, experimentation and performance.\\n\\nFull festival programme: https://bookwhen.com/shortwave\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://bookwhen.com/shortwave/e/ev-sfl45-20260508193000\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":364,\"name\":\"attentions, Harilay Rabenjamina\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-08T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3aadf0e40045e29bc7dcc3b052e7456c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"London Performance Studios premieres attentions, a new live audio-visual concept album by Harilay Rabenjamina, that traverses familial, intimate and political registers.\\n\\nBlending pop, ambient, R\\u0026B and classical influences, attentions is part narrative cinematic performance and part pop concert. The work unfolds between London, Paris, Antananarivo and Pessac, as it moves through shifting voices and registers, to explore forms of mobility across places, genres and modes of expression. The music is performed live with Thelia.\\n\\n7:30pm Doors\\n8pm Performance (50 min run time)\\nEnter event via Ormside Street.\\n\\nShortwave is a new festival of sound and performance unfolding across four independent venues in south east London: South London Gallery, London Performance Studios, IKLECTIK and ORMSIDE Projects. Bringing together international and local artists, musicians and DJs, the festival spans two nights of commissioned live works, experimentation and performance.\\n\\nFull festival programme: https://bookwhen.com/shortwave\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://bookwhen.com/shortwave/e/ev-sfl45-20260508193000\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":388,\"name\":\"General Echo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-09T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"35dcb07331be19110b0f46f9ff00259f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Friday 8 May at Walthamstow Trades Hall, 8pm til midnight\\n\\nMonthly reggae disco in North-East London. The night is named after sadly departed MC Earl Anthony Robinson, the voice behind classic deejay tunes such as “Drunken Master”.\\n\\nFor our May session we’re very happy to welcome a true heavyweight to select at Walthamstow Trades Hall, in the shape of RS DIGITAL.\\n\\nWhen he’s not touring the world alongside DAVID RODIGAN (mixing for both his soundclashes and providing special DJ mixes for his BBC 1Xtra show), he might be participating in his own clashes against the likes of KING JAMMY. He can also be found working in world renowned recording studios as a sought after mastering and sound engineer. He mixed the bonafide lovers rock classic “With You Boy” by Revelation whilst just a teenager. Deeply involved in the East London sound system scene in both reggae and rare-groove capacities since those times, he has actively pursued and mantained a fundamental presence in British black music.\\n\\nCome and listen to some of the greatest music ever made in a beautiful old school social club.\\n\\n£5 members\\n£7 Guests and non-members\\nNo advance tickets, pay on the door\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":301,\"name\":\"floor length skirts, Jupi Ter, Nebo Arts DJs: Nebo Arts #10\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-09T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3f6af4a40f1a0a70afcacedb72310a03.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"------ A Friday dance in the SJQ basement to round off spring '26 -------\\n\\nGenre surfing and obscure internet finds from Ljubljana duo Jupi Ter for their London debut, alongside home turf guest Floor Length Skirts. Rounding off the equation are Nebo Arts DJs warming up from 9pm. Delirium inbound\\n\\nDress to impress\\n\\nSupported by Arts Council UK\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":299,\"name\":\"HELICASE - 004\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-09T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"809ef25cc3c7694b3b0b3545f5e57884.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"you hear it before you see it. a tear in space up ahead of you. you follow the light and the air starts to thrum around you. you step through without knowing why.\\n\\nthe portal is open. enter into another dimension.\\n\\n------------------\\n\\nhelicase merges the magic and intimacy of smaller capacity parties, with the production quality often only found on larger stages. \\n\\nfor our fourth outing the mothership lands with an all female line up of some of the best techno, trance and house DJs this side of mars. expect unearthly beats, out-of-this-world custom sound+lighting and maybe even some tiny green men...\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2357593\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":222,\"name\":\"Brief Encounters \\u0026 Kindred Spirits Present: Shortwave Opening Night\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-09T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e29537c8f3a8df1b3dbc9c6b4d38002d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Brief Encounters and Kindred Spirits present the opening night of Shortwave Festival with: Yawning Portal, VISIO, Jiyoung Wi, Nexcyia, LC and Harilay Rabenjamina.\\n\\nExpect a series of sonic experimentation and left-field club transmission reverberating the space between inner worlds and the dance floor. Across ambient collage, speculative narrative and low-end club pressure, the programme unites artists who treat sound as both a portal to memory and a conduit for transformation.\\n\\n//\\n\\nShortwave is a new festival of sound and performance unfolding across four independent venues in south east London. Bringing together international and local artists, musicians and DJs, the festival spans two nights of commissioned live works, experimentation and performance.\\n\\n//\\n\\nLondon duo Yawning Portal presents an experimental DJ exploring their sound from field recordings, found sounds and delicate samples, conjuring a euphoric sonic mirage.\\n\\nItalian polymath VISIO unfolds a time-bent universe steeped in melancholic digital folk, where the sacred and the anachronistic converge, blending acoustic fragments, voice and glitched synthesis.\\n\\nRotterdam-based Jiyoung Wi pushes narrative to the edge of perception through her “sound fiction” practice, navigating the shifting space between text, improvisation and sonic immediacy with risk-taking gestures and negative virtuosity. ‘\\n\\nBerlin-based producer NEXCYIA [DJ] shifts from his ambient-driven, highly textural musicality to construct hypnotic realms of ambient dub techno, IDM and bass. \\n\\nLondon-based selector LC brings her exploratory approach to DJing, echoing a deep connection with global grassroots.\\n\\nFrench artist Harilay Rabenjamina anchors behind the decks, propelling the immersive world of his mixed-media work, attentions.\\n\\n//\\n\\nBrief Encounters operates as a space for grassroots live experimentation and the occasional late-night gathering, grounded in an ethos of bringing the fringe to centre stage.\\n\\nKindred Spirits is a cultural incubator nurturing hybrid realities and championing community-centered narratives across global artistic currents.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":218,\"name\":\"Skull Rub: Migrants Rights Fundraiser ft. Leo Gibbon, Joshua Brinksman, Gudanese\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-08T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-09T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"16df7e4eba69bd87aa83ca3d9487328d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"MIGRANTS RIGHTS NETWORK FUNDRAISER.\\n\\nWe're back at CU Dalston, this time with an extra hour on the clock.\\n\\nHeadlining we have Leo Gibbon b2b Joshua Brinksman (Mudline). Leo is a producer and selector moving between grime, dubstep, garage and 140, known for his work with grime legend Trim and a regular on NTS via the Woodgrain show. He's joined by collaborator Joshua Brinksman and together the two crafted the stunning Brains mixtape for Mudline, a gorgeous blend of lovers rock and dancehall. Expect grime, dancehall and leftfield bass.\\n\\nWe also have the wicked Gudanese of Felt Soundsystem joining us, bringing bass, soca, riddims and everything in between.\\n\\nThe Skull Rub residents will be on support all night, expect the unexpected.\\n\\nAll proceeds go to Migrants Rights Network, who are doing the vital work of fighting back against the recent surge in far-right violence and anti-migrant hostility. Your ticket supports their community-led research into safety strategies for those navigating the worst of the UK's migration system.\\n\\nFriday 8th May, CU (Dalston), 30Hz Soundsystem, 10PM – 4AM.\\n\\nArtwork by the wonderful @tobyevansjesra\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2405615\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":239,\"name\":\"Moon Coral 18: Melina Serser, Shjva, Gwenan (live), DJ Rino, Timur Basha\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-09T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-10T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"13c848a54f252f4785170c4fe03e141c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"22 hours, Gaffe (open air + club) and a secret location\\n\\nMay 9 \\u0026 10\\n\\nComing up: Moon Coral’s extended spring get-together in north London. We’re bringing you two UK debuts – an exclusive set by Ukrainian kaleidoscopic talent Shjva, along with Gwenan’s long awaited club music live show. \\n\\nFilling out the rest of the line-up we have a special Melina Serser sunset open air closing, DJ Rino’s late night rollers and Timur Basha’s microscopic electronic essentials. Spud and Dora on resident duties as always. Come with us and let’s stay together. \\n\\n4pm Saturday till 2pm Sunday\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2392606\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":241,\"name\":\"Club Soft with SIM (live), Mina, TrYb, SANA \\u0026 Shryke\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-09T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-09T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0496a398d98cb7911e0937020678dc54.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Club Soft is a day party for adventurous music fans, where you can dance to global club sounds and experience the restorative power of the sound-system in an alcohol and substance-free space. Everyone is welcome, whether you are sober, experimenting with sobriety, or are just curious to try something new.\\n\\nFor this edition we are joined by Canadian producer SIM, who will be performing live. SIM pushes the boundaries of sound-system music, his sound is a mutative combination he has named Slow Tech, a fusion of dancehall, dub, techno, jungle and more. SIM is a prolific producer, artist, researcher and educator and we are so excited to have him join us at Club Soft! \\n\\nWe are also going to be joined by TrYb, a selector who brings an explosive, infectious energy to every dancefloor. A trusted broadcaster, TrYb hosts Highlife and Sunshine on NTS, Enter the Party on Oroko Radio, and TrYb and Friends on Voices Radio, carving out dedicated spaces for joy, community, and discovery. TrYb's sets move through diasporic club sounds, from bass-heavy club rhythms to sun-soaked grooves. We can't wait for her set! \\n\\nAlso introducing our residents:\\n\\nMina is a producer and DJ who has been making joyful and high energy club music for the last 10 years. Her sets span a wide range of styles, rooted in rhythm and euphoria, from dancehall to soca, bubbling to gqom and much more. Mina stopped drinking 8 years ago, and created Club Soft as an alternative event for electronic music lovers.\\n\\nSana and Shryke, are two rave architects, founders of community-focused club projects Club Co-op and Moonsquad. They are known for their exhilarating blend of global club genres. Expect jungle, 140, footwork, dubstep and everything in between.\\n\\nWe will also be running a free (with a ticket) movement workshop from 5.30-6pm, led by dancer Niamh Keady. The workshop will be a guided movement session for you to connect with your body and learn some simple moves to a set from our resident DJs. Niamh will give you tools to explore movement within a club-space at your own pace, no prior dance training or experience required!\\n\\n\\nWhat to expect at Club Soft:\\n- A Funktion One soundsystem\\n- Room to dance\\n- An intergenerational crowd\\n- Delicious alcohol-free drinks\\n- A camera-phone free dance-floor\\n- Adventurous global club sounds\\n\\n\\nClub Soft may be for you if:\\n- You used to love raving but feel regular late night club spaces aren't for you anymore\\n- You want to find fun things to do that don't revolve around alcohol\\n- You hate hangovers and want to party whilst still feeling great the next day\\n- You love adventurous dance music and want to hear it played on a great sound-system\\n- You're looking to cut down or stop drinking and want to find community\\n- You want to step out of your comfort zone and find a new confidence!\\n\\nThis is an 18+ event! \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":353,\"name\":\"IKLECTIK Presents: Shortwave Festival Closing Event\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-09T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-09T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a03c63f91118cadc56527a7a66bb18d5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For the closing night of Shortwave, IKLECTIK presents Joshua Woolford, I Am Fya, and K’BOKO showing distinct yet interconnected approaches to sound as an embodied and spatial practice.\\n\\nJoshua’s work is grounded in cultural research and their lived experience as part of the queer Black Afro-Caribbean diaspora in England, confronting socio-political violence through embodied knowledge, intuition, and the unseen as disruptive and generative forces.\\n\\nI Am Fya presents her latest visual album 'Homeland', a meditation on identity, culture, and radical self-love, navigating themes of otherness and belonging while reaching toward a deep spiritual connection with land and ancestors.\\n\\nK’BOKO is a Brazilian, Berlin-based music producer, performer, percussionist, music therapist, and social worker whose sound he calls “high ancient future vibes”, blending afrodiasporic rhythms with 808s, sub bass, and synths to create immersive journeys that bridge Afro-Brazilian cadences and global underground dancefloors.\\n\\nABOUT the festival:\\n\\nShortwave is a new festival of sound and performance unfolding across four independent venues in south east London: South London Gallery, London Performance Studios, IKLECTIK and ORMSIDE Projects. Bringing together international and local artists, musicians and DJs, the festival spans two nights of commissioned live works, experimentation and performance.\\n\\nFind the full festival programme at https://bookwhen.com/shortwave\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/nvdmy5-shortwave-festival-9th-may-iklectik-london-ormside-projects-london-the-clore-studio-orozco-garden-south-london-gallery-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":351,\"name\":\"forecast\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-09T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-10T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"333a2374ea60730d6ad03b952a993e87.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"deep moving dancefloor\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2408190\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":352,\"name\":\"Alternative Recreation Club\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-09T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-10T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2acad640ab634c6a7ba8918509cc7952.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Saturday 9th of May, Alternative Recreation Club opens a hidden space for a special curation of artists exploring the outer edges of experimental electronic music.\\n\\n***DM insta for ticket link and info***\\n\\nInsta - @a.r.c_ldn\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":323,\"name\":\"Puppet Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-11T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-11T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"052eda8abb68d4756bed88a51fd7bb39.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Communal Clay Puppet Workshop\\n\\nUsing clay and slips you will be able to create a puppet, character, monster or creature.\\n\\nYou will be able to add colour and depth to your work with wild clay slips we have collected from around South London. And the option to have the piece fired and glazed with wood ash glaze.\\n\\nThe session will last 2 hours.\\n\\nTheses workshops will be more focused on the tactility of playing, practicing and learning sculpture techniques. There is no pressure to make a ‘finished product’ or ‘perfect piece’.\\n\\nAt the end of the workshop if you wish to have your piece fired and glazed, we ask you pay an additional £10 to cover firing costs, glaze materials \\u0026 transport of your work.\\n\\nAny leftover clay at the end of the session will be recycled for future use, minimising wastage and keeping our workshops sustainable.\\n\\nPricing:\\nWe are updating our pricing scale, in an effort to continue to make our workshops accessible and affordable we are testing out a new ticketing format with two options: Standard and Concession tickets.\\n\\nPlease choose the ticket option that is appropriate for yourself.\\n\\nCommunal Clay CIC is a not-for-profit organisation, all profits made after covering core costs will be used to run more community workshops.\\n\\nConcessions Include:\\n-People receiving benefits Jobseeker's Allowance / Universal Credit / Housing Benefit\\n-Young people 16-21\\n-Disabled\\n-students from working class backgrounds\\n-carers\\n-single parents\\n\\nAll fired and glazed work will be ready to collect in roughly 4 weeks from SET Social, please be patient as the cold weather affects drying and firing times.\\nSometimes this may be longer or shorter depending on the weather and temperature as these effect drying speeds.\\n\\nPLEASE READ: Clay and ceramics are fragile materials until fired and glazed, on occasion things can break or become damaged during the drying and firing process', Communal Clay is not responsible for any damage that may occur during these.\\n\\nTickets are refundable if you message us 48+ hours in advance of the event date\\nRefunds - you will be fully refunded for the cost of the ticket but the booking fee will not be refunded.\\n\\nUnder 18's must be accompanied by an adult\\nCommunal Clay is not responsible for work that breaks during firing.\\n\\nYour work must be collected within 4 weeks of being notified it is ready to collect from SET Social. After the 4 weeks unclaimed work will be given away.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":true,\"cancelled_at\":\"2026-05-10T13:37:29.746563Z\",\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":307,\"name\":\"SCOBE. 5 - Edie Bailey + Gary Stewart / No Home / Pentu\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-11T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"acef5aa0dcfb59163717529c66d24491.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SCOBE 5 at Club Silly! Playful and interesting experimental music for freaks, sweethearts and oddballs \\u003c3 \\n\\n\\nEdie Bailey + Gary Stewart\\n\\nEdie and Gary imagine the Bristol Hum, a sonic phenomenon some experience as a constant low hum, through synthesiser drone that infects and destroys the lives of those who hear it.\\n\\n\\n\\nEdie Bailey is a London-based non-binary queer creative. A multi-disciplinary opera director, folk musician, experimental composer and improvising performer, they are passionate about making opera specifically for Trans and gender non-conforming artists.\\n\\n\\n\\nGary Stewart is a media artist whose work challenges the accepted definitions of identity and belonging through a range of theoretical, fictional and artistic frames. He’s a founder member of Dubmorphology and performs as experimental sound artist Bantu.\\n\\n\\n\\nNo Home\\n\\nNo Home is London based artist Charlotte Valentine. Described as a ‘punk producer’ and ‘DIY experimental artist’ by The Wire, their 2020 debut “Fucking Hell” was named one of Pitchfork’s “35 Best Rock Albums of 2020”. Their second album, \\\"Young Professional\\\" was released in 2022. \\n\\n\\n\\nPentu\\n\\nPentu is a London based producer, sound designer and guitarist, exploring experimental and ambient soundscapes, focusing on sounds that mirror the splintered reality of living in an online world. His 2024 album 'And I Saw My Devil And I Saw My Deep Blue Sea' was released through Mappa.\\n\\n\\n\\nTicket prices include club membership to club silly which will give you access to members benefits.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/mxdo6k-scobe-5-11th-may-club-silly-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":138,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - The Cabs\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-12T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-12T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bda59bb600e2048c5c31fbe3b96b8157.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nThe Cabs\\nJapanese emo / mathrock legends, reunited last year after disbanding in 2013. Now fully active again and bringing their intricate emotional intensity to the rest of the world, this is the first UK show on their first international tour. \\n\\n+ support from\\n\\nBreakfast With Bears\\nLondon emo-math anthems\\n\\nShoplifting 1080p\\nBlending shoegaze, jungle and screamo into weird shapes with a guitar and a Nintendo DS.\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross and New Cross Gate\\n\\n£15\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/the-cabs\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":234,\"name\":\"Pearla, Joseph Futak \\u0026 Lilo at Hillstation Cafe \",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-12T21:45:00Z\",\"poster\":\"390f952b89a5962d4dc6c4f2c8e0e949.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"South east London mainstay Joseph Futak teams up with New York based indie folk artist Pearla for an exciting evening of new music ahead of the release of her new album 'Song Room'.\\n\\nPearla's music touches on the bridge between what is real and surreal. Her first album 'Oh Glistening Onion, The Nighttime Is Coming' is a refreshing exploration of both the mysteries of the external universe and our place in it, whereas her new record 'Song Room' turns inward - reflecting on love and the bridges we share between people, and their ability to collapse and stretch time. While this new collection of songs marks a more introspective turn, they are undeniably of the same magical idiosyncratic DNA that runs through all of Pearla's songwriting.\\n\\nHer music has been heralded on Pitchfork, NPR, Brooklyn Vegan and others, this is gig marks her London debut.\\n\\nJoseph Futak is a London based producer and artist, who's music quietly bridges the space between reflection, nostalgia, grief and the other spectres of human experience. His album 'Walking The Sea Wall' has a bleary eyed softness to it that recalls the moments between wake and sleep, past and present. While producing for many of London's most exciting acts, Joseph is slowly working towards the follow up record - a collection of songs that push further the corners of what was explored on 'Walking The Sea Wall', and will be debuting new material as part of this gig.\\n\\nThey will be joined by Lilo, one of London's most striking folk duos. The songs of Helen Dixon and Christie Gardner contain a captivating intimacy that can only come from their 15 year friendship. Their eye on the world both external and internal has a timeless sensitivity that is unique to them. Their debut album ‘Blood Ties’ was released last year to critical aclaim.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":385,\"name\":\"Nāda Sonics — IRL Listening Session #4\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-13T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-13T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d99ccadf09e9a8f60ce816c3ca1f330d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Nāda Sonics is an exploration into the world of raga and tala -based music. Broadcast on NTS Radio since 2023, Sway of the Verses shares the intricacies of raga music, an ever evolving ancient musical tradition weaving through the numerous musicians, instruments, ragas, time-cycles and concepts of this genre.\\n\\nThe Nāda Sonics—IRL: Listening Session is a chance to experience this spiritual, moving music in a collective situation, an uninterrupted listening session of 90 mins, sat on the floor on cushions, sipping tea and melting away to the vibes. In an overwhelming, discordant world of chaos, this is an oasis of calm.\\n\\n7:00 pm Doors open, come through for some chai and get yourself comfortable\\n\\n7:45 pm Listening Session: Sway of the Verses will lead you through a number of recordings all connected with the theme of the session, contextualising the music, musicians, and recordings.\\n\\n——\\n\\nSway Of The Verses is a radio presenter, DJ, graphic designer and artist. His residencies on NTS, Voices Radio and Sister Midnight FM have specialised in raga based music, diving into a mix of ghazals, qawaali, Punjabi folk, Indo-Jazz, lo-fi ambient music from the South Asian Diaspora, and more club orientated vibes. His dj sets vary from very considered long-form ambient sets, to crafting genre and bpm fluid explorations across ambient, jazz, hip-hop, dub and the many forms of electronic music; and has performed some standout sets at We Out Here, Dancing Family Festival, Daytimers Festival, Tate Lates, as well club sets all over London.\\n\\nLAKE is an artist-run curatorial and research platform based at Enclave, Deptford. Its programme focuses on sound-led, spatial, and durational practices, prioritising installation, listening-based events, performance, and public experimentation over fixed exhibition outcomes. Operating as a site for testing, research, and extended installation, supporting artists and practitioners working with sound, moving image, and spatial practice through both curated projects and developmental access.\\n\\nLAKE and Sway of the Verses invite you to share this experience in Deptford in an intimate setting, sitting on the floor, sipping chai and concentrating solely on the music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2426605\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":386,\"name\":\"An Evening of Techno-Negativity with MayDay rooms and Thomas Dekeyser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-13T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-13T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0195dc4ed4356bed234642789c5a5adf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for an evening diving into the long histories of technological resistance, with MayDay rooms and Thomas Dekeyser.\\n\\nAt a time when Big Tech grows increasingly enmeshed with authoritarian control, how do we resist? One path, the new book, TECHNO-NEGATIVE: A LONG HISTORY OF REFUSING THE MACHINE argues, is to look deeply into the archives. From the Luddites to medieval monks banning tools, seventeenth-century loom burners, revolutionary lantern smashers, and computer arsonists, history is riddled with critical junctures where people have recognised and resisted the machine as a violent, sometimes deadly force.\\n\\nWhich traces in the archives does our current techno-dystopian moment call us to bring back to life? How do we draw energy from radical pasts without romanticising them? An informal panel with the author of the book (Thomas Dekeyser) will explore these questions, and will be followed by a chance to read through techno-negative archives, including Mayday Rooms’ own collections.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.maydayrooms.org/e/88/an-evening-of-techno-negativity-with-mayday-rooms-and-thomas-dekeyser\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":405,\"name\":\"Dirar Kalash \\u0026 Friends: Electro-acoustic Residency\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-13T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-13T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"19200bb1cd4b4d9e5aaf78be657ad769.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Three nights of experimental improvisation with Dirar Kalash \\u0026 Friends.\\n\\nGritty and effervescent, Dirar Kalash's experimental music is known to be transcendental and deeply embodied. An extraordinary Palestinian sound artist, Kalash pushes boundaries in his sonic work with a vast repertoire of collaborations, including artists such as Nicolas Jaar. For this series, he invites:\\n\\n\\nMAY 13 - BARBIE MUKODA - Flautist and improvised blending classical and experimental sound worlds through tone and silence.\\nMAY 22 - MARYSIA OSU - Harpist, producer, and composer who blends classical, ambient, and electronic music.\\nMAY 27 - ROXANNA ALBAYATI - Cellist \\u0026 artist blending experimental music with cross-cultural improvisation and multimedia performance.\\n\\nStudio 12 is an intimate art space with a custom sound system \\u0026 cocktail bar in Camberwell, London. It's dedicated to art, music, poetry and film, rooted in transnational solidarities.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dirarxstudio12.eventbrite.co.uk/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":139,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Chasing Dolls / Vienna / Death Of Youth / Sweet Fish\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-14T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-14T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5b6e4f210f37c67edbf4edec4a537fdf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nChasing Dolls\\nTrowbridge Twinklemo\\n\\nVienna\\nMidlands sadgaze\\n\\nDeath Of Youth\\nLondon Emocore\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/deathofyouthukhc/\\n\\nSweet Fish\\nMath-punk-screamo-lofi-party-sad\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate or New Cross\\n£10\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/chasing-dolls\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":268,\"name\":\"Laughing\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-14T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-14T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e7c24655ab9ebc5e99bc5c3a0417d9ac.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"“Laughing” release party.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2412460?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\\u0026fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0DMTAwAHNydGMGYXBwX2lkDDI1NjI4MTA0MDU1OAABp3aqCIiIew3FAFTgZ7Lk9bH6osBZvWjSrwFuysjnX48aVHl48cpp4CVu5O5I_aem_PgK8Myd1ZC_R_g90lcXg5Q\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":415,\"name\":\"UNFOLD: Short Film Screening // WCL Mind \\u0026 Wondering CIC (free)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-14T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-14T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a938f913e9ac68ba655970f1d614b0a1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"11 people living with complex mental health came together to make powerful short films to challenge stigma and undergo therapeutic shifts.\\n\\nJoin us for an evening of 5 short films created through Wondering CIC’s collaborative filmmaking project in partnership with WCL Mind during mental health awareness week.\\n\\nOver 14 weeks, 11 new filmmakers with lived experience of mental health challenges came together to make powerful biographical films exploring resilience, identity, and mental health. This is the first public screening of their work so please come and join us for a celebration of creativity, storytelling, and community. This work was designed to create therapeutic shifts for the participants so come and here their stories!\\n\\nThe evening will feature:\\n🎬 60 minutes of short films made by lived-experience filmmakers\\n🎤 Reflections and conversations with the filmmakers\\n\\nAt Wondering CIC, we believe storytelling, art, and community are essential to addressing the mental health crisis. By placing cameras in the hands of people with lived experience, we empower individuals to own their stories, develop professional skills, and make authentic work that offers an unfiltered insight into the full spectrum of mental health.\\n\\n📅 Date \\u0026 Time: 14th May 2026 // Doors @ 18.00 \\u0026 Films Start @ 18.45\\n📍 Location: Club Cheek\\n🔗 www.wonderingcic.co.uk\\n📧 info@wonderingcic.co.uk\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/unfold-short-film-screening-wcl-mind-wondering-cic-free-tickets-1987779757765\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":342,\"name\":\"Argia (Tara Cunningham / Caius Williams / Theo Guttenplan)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-14T18:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-14T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"230c93258288d2dc9f5a0ab4edaf00c3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Downstairs at The Vortex\\n\\nDoors 6:45 PM, Music 7:15 PM – 1 set of music\\n \\n\\nLine-up:\\nTara Cunningham – Guitar\\nCaius Williams – Double bass\\nTheo Guttenplan – Drum kit\\n\\n\\nAbout:\\nArgia is the trio of Tara Cunningham, Theo Guttenplan, and Caius Williams. They released their self-titled debut album in May of last year, and plan to make music together forever.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.universe.com/events/argia-tara-cunningham-caius-williams-theo-guttenplan-downstairs-tickets-FB1QKG\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":23,\"name\":\"Harry Christelis – 'Preserving Fictions' Album Launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-14T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-14T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0de5f2aa635dcb45feed1d14aa3b6bff.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Guitarist and composer Harry Christelis presents his new album, Preserving Fictions — an exploration of how music and art can serve as a means to preserve and document the seeming truths we see, hear, feel, and experience every day. This record sees Christelis delve deeper into a sound world that has become synonymous with his name, fusing elements of jazz and folk traditions with ambient drones and delicate electronic textures to create a truly immersive listening experience.\\n\\nFeaturing his long-standing quartet of Christos Stylianides (trumpet/effects), Andrea Di Biase (double bass/synth), and Dave Storey (drums), the highly acclaimed musicians break free from their traditional roles within the jazz idiom. Instead, they embrace a deeply communal approach to improvisation, colouring, shaping, and delineating every moment of each piece together. Across the adventurous album, the listener is taken on a journey that moves through dreamy psychedelic trips, expansive soundscapes, delicate moments of intimacy, and furious bursts of energy — all seamlessly bound by a tone that holds sombre and hopeful feelings in harmonious equilibrium.\\n\\nHarry Christelis: guitar\\n\\nChristos Stylianides: trumpet\\n\\nAndrea Di Biase: double bass\\n\\nDave Storey: drums\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/q27yao-harry-christelis-album-launch-concert-14th-may-the-old-church-stoke-newington-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":343,\"name\":\"Church of Sound: Derya Yildirim and Grup Şimşek\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-14T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-14T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e706d79574472494c87f3b0c73263b20.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Derya \\u0026 Grup are a quartet unlike any other. First, is the transcendental voice of Derya Yildirim herself. Singing entirely in Turkish, Yildirim's voice is wonderfully rich, brimming with the confidence \\u0026 range of a vocalist many years her senior. Dynamic \\u0026 deliciously drifting, it drizzles honey on all that which it adorns. The perfect companion is to be found in the beautiful playing of the band - theirs is a sound that spans from soul, to Anatolian folk, to psych rock \\u0026 beyond, even frequently calling to mind the beats of Roc Marciano or Jay Versace. These varied flavours combine deliciously into a wonderfully easy-to-listen-to whole.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/ryqenr-derya-yildirim-and-grup-imek-7th-may-st-james-the-great-church-of-sound-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":411,\"name\":\"UPPERCUT VOL.7 with Black Fondu, Form Affinity, Orlanda\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-14T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-14T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a0b17d799e504dbc710ae1d00fd52caf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets on the door still available.\\n\\nBlack Fondu: London based Accra born artist whose performances veer between dissected electronica, manipulated hip-hop and abstract grime; heated in energy with alien multi-layered patches. Moving between punk, hip-hop and experimental scenes they perform with effuse force.\\n\\nForm Affinity: Form Affinity is a London based 4 piece emopunk/spacerock project.\\n\\nOrlanda: Electronic pop duo based in London. Having escaped Los Angeles 2049, they’ve touched down now, in 2026, to seek out a prophet and a dream.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":290,\"name\":\"TIARA NIGHT TAKEOVER\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-15T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"55a965c9c80730756f63c907aaa883e8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hello Beautiful Humans . Tiara missed you\\n\\nJoin us on May 15th as we take over The Piehouse Co-op once again for a wondrous night, filling the arches with sonic flows and creative displays from an array of Caribbean, POC, and Queer Music Makers and artists. From bone carving sculptures and poetic immersion to the alluring cascading Melodies that will alter your system.\\n\\nI am so excited to embrace you all in a night fueled by Black Queer Creativity.\\n\\nTiara loves you\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/34651/tiara-night-takeover\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":429,\"name\":\"Palestine Fundraiser: Window to The Spirits at The Exchange\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-15T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-15T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e35140e1f5841abf994568ed2135e06e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A night of poetry, music and art to raise funds for Palestine.\\n\\nJoin us on the 15th of May as Window to The Spirits hosts a Palestine Fundraiser at our community hub.\\n\\nAfter two successful and beautifully busy fundraisers at the exchange, Window to The Spirits returns to the hub to turn our fundraising efforts to Palestine ♥️ Attendees can expect an open mic of poetry and music, live painting on the night by @artandsoulxo which will be donated for a fundraising auction, a live poet on typewriter who will take donations for a personalised typed poem and a stall/table which will sell Gazan crafts.\\n\\nCome and join us for a bustling night full of art, poetry and conversation - with all proceeds going to Palestine. ♥️💚\\n\\nPoster graphic created with a photograph by Eddie Gerald, 2021 in Al-Khalil.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/palestine-fundraiser-window-to-the-spirits-at-the-exchange-tickets-1988190183359\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":260,\"name\":\"Matthew Ryan Thomas / Garden Centre / Kevin!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-15T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-15T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b7276eb561c0224ef73207221afab786.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"FRIDAY MAY 15th sees us welcome POP GOD Matthew Ryan Thomas to The Ivy House for a very special headline set, with support from indie pop greats Garden Centre and Animal Soup. And all for FREE!\\n\\nEstablishing himself as a devout student of pop, Matthew Ryan Thomas’s commitment to dizzying showmanship and the suspension of one’s disbelief is what makes the invitation to his ‘wee world’ all the more enticing. For fans of Robyn, Troye Sivan and STEPS.\\n\\nA keen-eyed songwriter, half cynical, half childlike in his curiosity, Garden Centre's Max Levy plumbs surreal meaning from life’s peculiarities and regularities. He has a knack, not unlike Randy Newman, to make his listener feel affection for the characters within his songs. The train conductor, the man asleep at his desk, the kid on his dirt bike — characters who may otherwise inspire little thought from us in our real lives — here, draw out a feeling of deep connection.\\n\\nPresented as part of The Ivy House Beer Fest - an annual weekend of guest beers, ciders and culinary delights \\u0026 three days of FREE live music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/U65052aa87f5\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":183,\"name\":\"Sticky Buttons at The Bath House w/ POLY-RITMO \\u0026 FANTASY IN ORBIT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-15T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"38864e07a904d3eeefd095f2fcdec55d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sticky Buttons hand over the dance floor to the finest vinyl collectors. Deep vinyl digs, private press gems and anti-algorithmic curation all rolled together on one of London’s tastiest soundsystems. This is a dance floor for the open-minded and open-hearted with two left feet.\\n\\nPOLY-RITMO -  DJ, musician, broadcaster and Bathhouse homie. Her appreciation for music from across the globe has been shaped through her time at Sounds of The Universe and studies in Ethnomusicology at SOAS. This curious mind isn’t afraid to mix music past and present. Her sets are often percussive, soulful and super eclectic, everything we love here at Sticky Buttons. \\n\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/poly_ritmo/\\n\\nFANTASY IN ORBIT - go your own way, ride into the stars till you circle the world and arrive back a new person. Known for his immersive sets, Fantasy is a digger of all things obscure digging deep for rare and forgotten vinyl. Blending transportive genre-less sounds, his sets drift through lo-fi, folk, ambient, post punk, techno and beyond. \\n\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/fantasyinorbit/\\n\\nSTICKY BUTTONS - London based record label known for their close connection and reissue of Nigerian boogie legend Dizzy K’s full catalogue as well as their obsession for bringing to light records that sit outside your regular labels. Be that Balearic Amazonian psych Folk Ballards, heavy hitting Kwaito jazz thumpers or Puerto Rican cinematic psych rock jams. Sticky Buttons love the weird and wonderful. DJ sets cross everything with healthy helpings of contemporary blisters. \\n\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/sticky.buttons/\\n\\nDOORS 7PM\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":443,\"name\":\"The School Of Night\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-15T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-15T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"abf2b06ad76dc77a352b348dba27db6d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Last summer, The fabled School of Night made their debut on the hallowed boards of Sands Studios, to mark The School's 20th anniversary. The match of improvised pyrotechnics with the gilded beauty of Sands was so perfect - and so popular! - that they're back by popular demand for another gig this May.\\n\\nExpect high-wire improvisation, impossible feats of verbal dexterity and brilliant new, off-the-cuff works by various authors, old and new.\\n\\nThe School has performed at the National Theatre, the RSC, Shakespeare's Globe and the Royal Court, as well as in festivals and theatres from Texas to Elsinore, and from Hay-on-Wye to Liverpool to Kuala Lumpur.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsmusic.eventive.org/schedule/698a1b1c6c8b8b101fed3c55\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":199,\"name\":\"Niche × TiHKAL @ Club Cheek 15.05\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-15T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c3f08784c6e8427b0278d558db362152.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Niche x TiHKAL @ Club Cheek May 15th 🍄\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\n𓍊𓋼𓍊𓋼𓍊\\n\\nFriday 15th May\\u2028\\n10pm to 6am\\u2028\\n\\n@ Club Cheek\\n\\u2028\\nSW9 7JJ\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\n£7 (limited) / £12 / £16\\u2028Tickets via gel 🎟️\\n\\n𓍊𓋼𓍊𓋼𓍊\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\nFungi Assemble! \\n\\nFor our second instalment of 2026, Niche teams up with Wordcolour’s TiHKAL label for a night deep psychedelic sounds at our new favourite South London spot: Club Cheek\\u2028.\\n\\nLose yourselves in an all-night edition of immersive hypnotic vibes. We’re excited to welcome Berlin’s Marylou, one of our favourite cinematic selectors, alongside scene legend Basic Chanel, subterranean live sets from McGregor and Om Ensemble, a b2b from TiHKAL stalwarts Wordcolour and St. Amp, and Niche founder Ikävä Pii completing the lineup.\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\n𓍊𓋼𓍊𓋼𓍊\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\nMarylou\\nBasic Chanel\\nMcGregor (Live)\\nSt. Amp b2b Wordcolour\\nOm Ensemble (Live)\\nIkävä Pii\\n\\n𓍊𓋼𓍊𓋼𓍊\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\nCurated by Ikävä Pii and Wordcolour\\nArtwork by ROOO\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":358,\"name\":\"System Revival with Steve Bicknell, Rosati, faux naïf\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-15T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ddafddbf584362ef79df1f3636503c70.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"STEVE BICKNELL is in himself a legacy.\\nHistorically no doubt of one London's most influential humans in techno / experimental electronic and club music from so many different angles.\\n\\nHe brought people together at his LOST warehouse shows throughout the 90's and 00's where Jeff Mills was a resident ...\\n- as well as later being a staple at the legendary PLASTIC PEOPLE (rip)\\n\\n\\u0026 his absolutely incredible and timeless releases (via several aliases) on LOST RECORDINGS / COSMIC RECORDS are without a doubt still having impact and huge influence on today's producers and DJs\\n\\nROSATI --\\nItalian artist based in Amsterdam - has been working hard and growing a lot over the past years in his tastes / productions / DJing / live shows / and curating his label Global Pulse.\\n\\nFocusing on vinyl djing he's bringing a unique mix of old and new generation techno and house full of energy!\\n\\n\\nFAUX NAÏF -- one of London's staples and an unmatched depth of music knowledge\\n\\nRooted in goth, darkwave, synth, EBM, post-punk and new beat, whilst leaning into the sounds of techno and electro at the same time, she is a masterful selector!\\n\\nMERCH SALE at the venue - info TBA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2406793\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":261,\"name\":\"Steely Dan 2 / Sinatra Lives! / Scrounge / flytrap / tall child / Free Lunch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"682d2b3d158374c1320151e4013199c5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House hosts a full day of FREE live music on Saturday May 16th.\\n\\nWe are joined by Steely Dan 2, a 9-piece band performing the hits of your favourite yacht rock heroes. Enmeshed by an enduring infatuation with the eclectic and timeless grooves of Steely Dan, this motley hive-mind of intrepid musicians will blast through the sharpest avenue of the discography. Expect the hits.\\n\\nThey follow Sinatra... Lives!: A Tribute to Frank Sinatra featuring many Ivy House favourites, past and present. This will be very, very special.\\n\\nEarlier in the day we showcase some of South London's finest contemporary voices, with sets from Scrounge, flytrap, tall child and Free Lunch.\\n\\nPresented as part of The Ivy House Beer Fest - an annual weekend of guest beers, ciders and culinary delights, plus three days of FREE live music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Qb39e96a3cff\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":127,\"name\":\"Foraging Walk\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T13:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T16:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2eca2c7f5e87468a168af57603e8f13d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A guided walk in a lush community-run nature reserve in East London. \\n\\nWe'll be moving slowly, identifying plants and fungi, sharing their stories, and speaking about the broader themes surrounding foraging. This walk is designed to be accessible for those with any level of foraging experience.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/33948/spring-foraging-walk\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":157,\"name\":\"Whomp Day Party: Luisa, Richard Gregory, Lora Mipsum, Annie G\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"41f9edbaca6eceda9ad2ded5f1d81364.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\n❀.ೃ࿔*°❀.ೃ࿔*°❀.ೃ࿔*°❀\\n𝒲𝐻𝒪𝑀𝒫 𝒟𝒜𝒴 𝒫𝒜𝑅𝒯𝒴\\n𝒮𝒶𝓉𝓊𝓇𝒹𝒶𝓎 16𝓉𝒽 𝑀𝒶𝓎\\n❀.ೃ࿔*°❀.ೃ࿔*°❀.ೃ࿔*°❀\\n\\nAfter a six-month hiatus, Whomp is BACK to kick-off summer at a brand new venue: Tottenham's Gaffe. We're taking over and reimagining the courtyard for eight hours of magic from 3pm to 11pm.\\n\\nAs always, 100% of our profits go directly to charity.\\n\\nKeep dancing to change lives.\\n\\nEarly bird tickets are available now at a discounted rate — prices go up at the door, so get it whilst it's HOT.\\n\\n_______\\n\\nSAFE WHOMP NOTICE\\n\\nEvery Whomp is a sanctuary for self-expression, creativity, and unbridled joy on the dancefloor. We have zero tolerance for racism, sexism, transphobia, homophobia, body negativity, ableism, or any form of discrimination.\\n\\nWe also do not tolerate violence, non-consensual touching, spiking, sexual harassment, catcalling, or stalking of any kind.\\n\\nIf you witness or experience any of these behaviours, please speak to our bar staff immediately. And if you're feeling unwell, please stay home and join us next time — we'll miss you, but your health and everyone's safety comes first.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2368955\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":419,\"name\":\"Mirror Movies #3 [PROMOTERS EDITION]\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-17T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"af0becfdc669c33b0d337a4443e3e196.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"NOYBmusic presents:\\n⋆ Mirror Moves #3 [PROMOTERS EDITION] ⋆\\n\\nAfter two almost sold out events last year, Mirror Moves returns to Hoxton Cabin on Saturday 16th of May for a special edition showcasing some of the most important players of the London grassroots promoters scene (plus one international guest from Amsterdam).\\n\\n1 Event, 2 Rooms, 2 Line-ups, very little overlaps for maximum enjoyment. Groundfloor bar (6PM start) vibes will be Soulful and Deep House + Garage while in the Basement (9.30PM start) we'll serve IDM, Techno, Breaks, 140 and up to Footwork, for those experimental fast paced sounds we all need deeper in the night.\\n\\n---- FULL LINE UP (A-Z) ----\\n\\n⋆ Alfaz [Salotto Sounds]\\n⋆ Bryan By Day [LZRD MUSIC]\\n⋆ dj ennui [Sensitive Boys Club]\\n⋆ DJ FUNGHOUL [Ghoul Dance]\\n⋆ LYLO [IsBurning (AMSTERDAM)]\\n⋆ MAÏS [Leese Geese]\\n⋆ Make Money Mafia [Nan's Basement]\\n⋆ NOYB [Mirror Moves]\\n⋆ Paperplane [Tilted]\\n\\nWelcoming, multi-genre, boundaryless:\\ncome with open hearts and minds to elevate your souls.\\n\\n⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆ ⋆\\n\\n6PM-3AM // 18+ // ID NEEDED\\nMain Bar is FREE ENTRY, Basement is TICKETED.\\n132 Kingsland Rd, London E2 8DP\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2393382\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":354,\"name\":\"Magda Drozd: Divided by Dusk (live), with LI YILEI\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"74b67fc7e01a498e496653a120831c8a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Magda Drozd: Divided by Dusk (live), with LI YILEI\\n\\nSat 16 May \\n7 PM \\nRaleigh Chapel, N16 8QQ \\n\\nNight is about to fall, the day slowly fades away — it is this twilight time that Magda Drozd’s latest album inhabits. Divided by Dusk, the Polish composer’s third solo album, carries the promise of a crepuscular otherworldliness. Inspired by her stays in Japan, its rich tradition in ambient and experimental music, and a collaboration with flautist Rai Tateishi, alongside a renewed engagement with her roots in Poland and its folk and ancient history, her work unfolds as a form of sonic excavation.\\nLayers of dark ambient tones intertwine with field recordings and textured violin, invoking long-gone, unspecified rituals and fragments of inherited histories.\\n\\nMagda Drozd, born in Warsaw, is a composer, violinist, and sound artist living in Zürich and London. She has been releasing music on Präsens Editionen since 2019 and runs her own label, Rivercore.\\n\\nAlso on the bill is LI YILEI with a solo set. Li Yilei is a Chinese-born, London-based artist and composer whose work moves through tacit listening, perceptual thresholds, and the quiet tensions between presence and disappearance. Guided by a quietly mystic approach to sensing, Li treats sound as a porous field of attunement where intuition, resonance, and the barely perceptible begin to speak.\\n\\nWorking across tapes, theremins, objects, and self-built devices, their compositions unfold through restrained gestures, creating spaces where attention deepens and thresholds blur.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2421235\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":382,\"name\":\"New Kyd Presents: Joy(ce)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bd6d23b6262e3be0602c7ba8b11e6525.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In 2006, the body of Joyce Carol Vincent was found in her London flat nearly three years after she had died, her TV still flickering. New Kyd’s solo Joy(ce) attempts to dance this absence: to trace what it means to vanish while visible.\\n\\nThe piece unfolds as a fugue of solos, moving between rupture and ritual, meditative movements and stillness, mourning and invocation. New Kyd channels muses across time and style, Isadora Duncan’s abandon, Graham’s rituals of sadness, Wigman’s whimsy, Billie Holiday’s vulnerability. Joy(ce) reflects the architectures of visibility and erasure around womanhood from a hauntologist* perspective.\\n\\nJoy(ce) is a choreographic séance that presents Joyce as a symbolic figure of spectral resistance**. A meditation on solitude, memory and the shimmering echoes of those like Joyce Carol Vincent who slip away unnoticed. But revived through reminiscence.\\n\\nKyd performs an unpplugged version of this seance\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":298,\"name\":\"Zlom w/ Julek ploski, Charlie Osborne, leisure fm, omoo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-16T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f64ddaaf1e55c3d508f12988e2bd511d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Get ready for a night of theatrical grandeur, unfolding between mythic excess and inward emotional rupture, featuring a UK debut from Julek ploski, performance by Charlie Osborne + sets from our residents: leisure fm and omoo  ♪.*⁽⁽ ◝꒰´꒳`∗꒱◟ ₎₎\\n\\n----------\\nJulek ploski\\n\\nJulek ploski™ operates fluidly between maximalist, hyper-digital chaos and tender, emotional introspection. He boldly fuses cinematic, symphonic-opera grandeur, high-octane rave beats, lyrical piano melodies, and twisted echoes of trap and metal. Ploski’s music moves through liminal spaces, blending euphoric club energy with a sense of paranoid urgency, all while holding space for inward soft intimacy.\\n\\nCharlie Osborne\\n\\nCharlie Osborne (b. 1999, Cardiff) is a London-based artist working across video, performance, music, writing and painting. Working through poetic vignettes, their practice employs a fictive logic to theatricality and the hyperreal. Drawing on horror aesthetics in both style and strategy, the work takes hybrid form—shock-rock essay-concert, noise performance, magical-realist story—shaped by screamo, synth-punk, hypnagogic pop, screaming harmonica, and a never-ending love-story rendered polyphonically. Osborne’s characters, video, sculpture and live shows are conceived as a spiritual dimension, where existential excess and the folly of modernity drive conspiracy and phenomena—replying through a new mythicism.\\n\\nleisure fm\\n \\nlondon-based polish twin electronica duo – leisure fm – utilise stretched-out beats and basslines, manipulated field recordings, and distorted vocals to create murky soundscapes to dissociate to… \\ntheir work explores themes of repetition and rumination, with most tracks composed of loops with sullen lyrics – weaving a loose narrative about esoteric fables, behavioural cycles, and mercurial relationships\\nrecently, they have been exploring capricious electroclash and broken dance music sounds to sulk to… \\n (¬`‸´¬)♩𖦹 “moody in the club”\\n\\nomoo(@omoo_gosh)\\nResident DJ on the decks throughout.\\n\\n♪.*⁽⁽ ◝꒰´꒳`∗꒱◟ ₎₎\\n\\n1930 - late…\\n\\nfree concessions memberships available through cafe oto website to access members tickets \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/zlom/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":292,\"name\":\"Fax 6\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-17T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2af9205b3426383b91e2ea8ddc82091d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dance Music all Night\\n\\nTea Es G / K9ty / Nilrey / Mixed Results\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2419603\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":359,\"name\":\"Influences\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-16T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-17T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b4031a390afa6fc2b3ebf1b3449445e3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Influences returns for another night of jungle flavours at our new location in South London - Ormside.\\n\\nMaking his debut is the one and only Kid Lib of Green Bay Wax! This man needs no introduction as his tunes and sets have been mashing up the place for a long time. With releases on many of the biggest jungle labels in existence, including Future Retro and AKO Beats, you can expect an hour of some absolutely amazing jungle.\\nKid Lib has a meticulous approach to his set curation, this one is not to be missed!\\n\\nAlongside our usual bunch of selectors, legendary label, Creative Wax owner, Madcap returns for the first time since our first event. We waited to long to be honest. Expect a top notch selection and maybe a little bit of scratching from this master of the art of mixing!\\n\\nAs always we have the Don of scene, DJ Stretch, blessing us with his usual Influences style jungle selection. His sets are always jam packed with unreleased dubs consisting of many of the biggest tracks to bless a sound system. Its smiles for miles and always a highlight!\\n\\nDecibella constantly adds a delicate touch to our nights, but don't think she wont drop some absolutely devastating tunes, bringing the rough with the smooth of her particular style and fashion!\\n\\nDarkspin is a firm favourite who always supports the industry artists, big and small! Expect dubs and rugged flavours, lots of familiar soul samples incorporated into contemporary 165bpm tunes, as well as some rough neck ragga vocals. He knows the code!\\n\\nD-Lo will be digging deep, bringing his usual old school 94/95 jungle selection, instilling familiarity for the OJs and an education for the newcomers.\\n\\nOur MCs will be hosting with a variety of styles and personalities. Bringing fun, jokes and musical knowledge to the narration of the night! Big up to Shockin B, MC Bassline and Shylo!!!\\n\\nBe Cool - Be Nice - Be Family\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2363737\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":272,\"name\":\"L.O.V.E.\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-17T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-17T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9ee320a8308cf2beb94d36412384d396.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A party dedicated solely to exploring the lineage of Soul \\u003e Funk \\u003e Disco. \\nSome of the most generous and connective music ever made; carrying both the weight of injustice and the hope for liberation. Born from a need for freedom, expression and joy in the face of hardship, these weren’t just genres but cultural movements. Black, queer and marginalised communities now had spaces that they could exist on their own terms, in their own sound. This is music that brings all walks of life together and gets you feeling something true.. you are alive and not alone !!\\n\\nSaunas will be open as usual, book your time slot on our website.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":316,\"name\":\"Opera Sunday\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-17T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-17T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6ddbf3c34eb7a564046008257c69c275.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Opera Sunday is back ! Spanners May 17th with Jeffrey Hinton \\u0026 Dance With Me - if you remember the last time Jeffrey played then you’ll be extra excited for this one\\n\\nhope to see you there\\n\\n£10 OTD\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":140,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Outta Pocket, Hold My Own, Violent Offence + More\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-17T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-17T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2821cc37e2e6b42a59437740494a36cc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nOutta Pocket\\nBay area heavy shit\\n\\nHold My Own\\nPure hardcore rage on DAZE\\n\\n+ UKHC Support from \\nViolent Offence\\n\\nRegress\\n\\nHeadstone\\n\\nBlood Money\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross and New Cross Gate\\n£15\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/outta-pocket\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":141,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents: Angel Statue Metalcore - A Mourning Star, Crowquill + more\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-18T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-18T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2d39fe342b0db278cd31968f642cad14.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nA Mourning Star\\nVancouver metalcore\\n\\nCrowquill\\nDistorted northern mathcore nightmares\\n\\nWarden\\nDeathcore devastation\\n\\nKill The Snitch\\nNew London skramz, with nods to disembodied and Reuben.\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£12\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/a-mourning-star\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":348,\"name\":\"The Gate presents: Nadeem Din-Gabisi + Richard Phoenix (DJ) + Labake Sabbath + Dan Johnson + Mr AKA Amazing + Wayne's Drones + Gate Loops + Love Permanent\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-18T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f139f1ba39b7a1962301a330d5b07371.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Gate is an arts space for adults with learning disabilities based in Shepherd’s Bush, West London. We’ve been running for over twenty years and have a freeform, collective approach to exploring art with our members. People are free to express themselves creatively in any manner they choose to, but we also provide a space where people hang out, meet, form friendships, and find support in navigating the system. We think there should be a Gate for everyone, on every street corner.\\n\\nGate members have collaborated with Klein, Sly and the Family Drone, Mariam Rezaei, LA Timpa, 10Foot, Café OTO, the ICA, The Horse Hospital, Supernormal Festival, Spanners and Strange Brew / Cube Microplex (Bristol) to name a few.\\n\\nCheck their weekly show on Resonance FM hosted by Labake Sabbath:\\nhttps://www.mixcloud.com/Resonance/playlists/gate-kicks/\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/the-gate-may-2026/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":428,\"name\":\"Event 001: Grounded Transcendence (Day 1)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-19T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-19T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"efec25d02f61e73186196914ac6af3b7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Cake Architecture's takeover of Domus showroom over Clerkenwell design week, will temporarily transform the space into an experimental testing ground, exploring space, sound and surface through the typologies of a Gallery (Day 1), Listening Room (Day 2) and Club (Day 3). Creating a temporary platform for cultural production. Each Day the space will adapt and a new collective will curate the music line up, complimented by exhibitions, talks and workshops throughout the day.\\n\\nInstallation: Cake\\nSound System: Big Ears\\nLighting: Jarrod O'Connell\\nVisuals: Wasted Space\\n\\nDay 1 Gallery:\\n\\nTango will take the helm for the opening party. They are an event series inspired by the invisible agreements of tango: improvisation, shared listening, and movement shaped through collective rhythm. Moving between tension and release, intimacy and distance, it explores how people move together through rhythm, attention, and atmosphere.\\n\\nAlso present will be an exhibition: Grounded Transcendence. Exhibits from Artist, designers and photographers exploring nightlife and rave culture.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2439107\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":246,\"name\":\"Richard Lewis + Odina\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5bdade6ff1c057889f26c571dbf538e7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Come along to another edition of New Lands, and you can listen to the addictive tones of Richard Lewis and the wizardry that is Odina.\\nOdina is the solo project of Catalan singer, songwriter, and composer Blanca Romeo de la Higuera. Her early musings, vulnerable and intimate, like a whispered diary entry, quietly captivated millions on Spotify. Now, she is embarking on a new album chapter set to see the light of day in 2027: a baroque-pop dreamscape where innocence fractures and meaning hides in the surreal. This is music that wanders—through identity, through absurdity, through the soft chaos of the self. Odina’s world is raw, strange, and searching, a place that feels both far away and deeply familiar.\\nRichard Lewis are an Oxford/London duo. Their EP ‘Live in Vienna’ came out in 2023, and they are currently working on their first album.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/O534963aad4d\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":416,\"name\":\"UNFOLD: Short Film Screening // WCL Mind \\u0026 Wondering CIC // Haringey Community Cinema (free)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-20T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-20T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9a654b4b63baaeff7c6d71ed377073a4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\n11 people living with complex mental health came together to make powerful short films to challenge stigma and undergo therapeutic shifts.\\n\\nCollaborative screening with Haringey Community Cinema!\\n\\nJoin us for an evening of 5 short films created through Wondering CIC’s collaborative filmmaking project in partnership with WCL Mind during mental health awareness week.\\n\\nOver 14 weeks, 11 new filmmakers with lived experience of mental health challenges came together to make powerful biographical films exploring resilience, identity, and mental health. This is the first public screening of their work so please come and join us for a celebration of creativity, storytelling, and community. This work was designed to create therapeutic shifts for the participants so come and here their stories!\\n\\nThe evening will feature:\\n🎬 60 minutes of short films made by lived-experience filmmakers\\n🎤 Reflections and conversations with the filmmakers\\n\\nAt Wondering CIC, we believe storytelling, art, and community are essential to addressing the mental health crisis. By placing cameras in the hands of people with lived experience, we empower individuals to own their stories, develop professional skills, and make authentic work that offers an unfiltered insight into the full spectrum of mental health.\\n\\n📅 Date \\u0026 Time: 20th May 2026 // Doors @ 18.00 \\u0026 Films Start @ 18.45\\n📍 Location: Lordship Co-op Hub\\n🔗 www.wonderingcic.co.uk\\n📧 info@wonderingcic.co.uk\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/unfold-short-film-screening-wcl-mind-wondering-cic-free-tickets-1987780279325\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":421,\"name\":\"Workshop: how to cannibalise the dead with Izdihar Afyouni\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-20T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-20T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9647ca69255e520d1269a130ba9b4632.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us on Wednesday 20th May, 6:30–8:30pm for how to cannibalise the dead, a discursive participatory performance and workshop with Palestinian artist Izdihar Afyouni.\\n\\nExploring consent, narrative, authorship, and re-representation, this session examines how narratives are shaped and exploited as they cross geographical and cultural borders. Participants are asked to interrogate the direct and indirect violence that results from the circulation of stories, especially when cultural institutions exclude the original authors or subjects from the production and presentation of their narratives.\\n\\nCombining participatory performance and discussion, the session invites participants to prepare a first-hand oral testimony in advance, submitting it as either a written text or a voice note for transcription prior to the session. This can be a personal story or a published first-person account, brought as material to be used within the workshop (guidance and examples will be provided in the sign-up form).\\n\\nWorking in groups, participants will randomly select a testimony and adapt it into an institutional format, such as exhibition text, a media output, or a programme proposal.\\n\\nThe workshop will consider the violence of the unknown narrative, how value is assigned to stories, how control can be reclaimed in spaces where narratives are shaped without consent, and what it means to refuse institutional gatekeeping and resist the pressures of funding bodies.\\n\\nPlease arrive from 6pm for a prompt 6:30pm start.\\n\\nThis free event will take place at Auto Italia and is open to artists, curators, and cultural workers working across socially and politically engaged practices. To book, follow the link here or email info@artworkassociation.org\\n\\nIzdihar Afyouni is a queer Palestinian multidisciplinary artist and writer working across large format painting, participatory performance, film and text. Their practice draws on Palestinian literature, oral testimonies, BDSM practices and colonial archives to interrogate carceral and genocidal colonial logic and political (ab)uses of the body, often using site-specific and participatory structures that collapse the space between spectator and subject. She is co-editing and writing for the upcoming publication Needles in the Eye: Refusal and the Necropolitics of Cultural Production with Gelare Khoshgozaran.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf4elTXXGploM7Q-2A4KO412zp9lc9V5yUDIQJz7d_93htCgg/viewform\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":436,\"name\":\"AMPLIFIED 04: Jichael Macksons, Betterpetra x Joel, Nadim\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"27ae5c0986a0f2a08533d51dc03afe0f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Advance sold out - Tickets available OTD\\n\\nJichael Macksons: An ambient, electronic sound that  explore a familiar, textural dissonance that can only be consoled by poppy vocal stims that scratch. The Macksons provide an idealist apocalypse as we soon face the end of the world.\\n\\nBetterpetra x Joel: Joel is a multi-instrumentalist and producer making dark, beat-based atmospheric electronic music. Betterpetra is a producer and vocalist drifting between ambient dreamscapes and dissociative dance. Playing live as a duo for the first time, they blur their worlds and see what happens.\\n\\nNadim: Vocalist and producer, NADIM, music informed by Egyptian rituals, blended with drone, post-industrial, and noise. Rooted in performance art and underground club culture, their live shows are high-intensity and immersive, unfolding like a Greek tragedy with DJ set-like sequencing, with a strong emphasis on soundscape and fashion\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":400,\"name\":\"indek + Ans M + Mailer\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5896051920ead64a97078d715c8c8f04.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Experimentsal breakcore musician indek is joined by textural composer Ans M and modular synthesis musician Mailer for an evening of electronic intricacy\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":13,\"name\":\"Dave Huismans presents In Transit LIVE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-20T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3e969078b46bd272b336f778a6732da4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dave Huismans (ex_libris, A Made Up Sound, 2562) presents In Transit, a self-titled LP of arresting downtempo vignettes, with origins dating back to over a decade ago.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/dave-huismans-presents-in-transit-live/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":360,\"name\":\"FORM + Eastern Margins presents: Bed\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"edf6c9a5f8493a20b0f9643e0f7a36e1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2409508\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":466,\"name\":\"Our Flag, Our People: LIVE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"101954059b5c7147874c8a932887ad3a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"​The zine is finally here, and we’d love for you to join us and celebrate!\\n\\n​Our Flag Our People explores the conditions that govern what it means to be British.\\n\\n​We’re getting together for an evening to bring these pages to life. It’s a chance to hear directly from our contributors about the stories behind their work and the big ideas we kept coming back to while putting this issue together.\\n\\n​We'll be in honest conversation about what’s on our minds, followed by live poetry from the people who wrote the rules for this issue.\\n\\n​There'll be music and drinks throughout the evening, with the opportunity to buy the newly released physical edition!\\n\\n​So come through, grab a copy, and catch up with the community.\\n\\n​Our Flag, Our People: LIVE at Pelican House.\\n\\n​📆 When: 21st May 2026, 5pm - 9pm\\n\\n​📍 Where: 144 Cambridge Heath Rd, Bethnal Green, London E1 5QJ\\n\\n​🎟️ Tiered Tickets (£5 - £15)*\\n\\n​🫂 Age Restriction: 18+ (due to bar usage)\\n\\n​*Please contact dyar@youththegap.uk to claim a free ticket for those who cannot afford the lowest tier.\\n\\n​Please note for entry to this event, you must sign up to be a member of Pelican House Social Club by signing the final question 🙋🏽‍♀️\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://luma.com/o06m0c80\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":142,\"name\":\"The Death Metal Violence Tour\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6699eb5b9448c45e3f64f4a45d62ce50.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life and Crowd Force Booking present\\nThe Death Metal Violence Tour\\n\\nfeaturing\\nDysentery\\nBoston Death Metal Beatdowns\\n\\nAnhedonia\\nDetroit Deathcore Devastation\\n\\n.357 Homicide\\nManchester Maniacal Slams\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest station New Cross Gate or New Cross\\n£17\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/dysentery\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":413,\"name\":\"Against Apathy // 001 ~ Resisting Zionism \\u0026 Imperialism\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ce27049fa3ea8ff2f6aa7a5fbb6cedd8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Against Apathy is an event bringing people together to mobilise, get activated, meet others and realise that we all have a role to play in creating change and resisting. This edition will focus on how to resist Zionism and imperialism, locally and globally. \\n\\nThe event will feature 14 individuals actively involved in resisting Zionism in many different ways, spaces and formats, who will share a bit about what they do and how it might be possible to get involved. \\n\\nSpeakers: \\nSara Masry ~ actress, writer, filmmaker\\nTyrone Scott ~ Head of Campaigns at War on Want, newly elected hackney Councillor\\nLaith ~ Palestinian youth movement\\nRay ~ Forensic Architecture’s Gaza team\\nJacob ~ Doikayt Collective, Jewish Bloc for Palestine\\nDania ~ palestinian lawyer from Jerusalem \\u0026 \\nManon Louis ~ research and investigations\\nZeashan ~ Artist, former INGO worker\\nGabriel Speechly, Producer - kaddish (how to be a sanctuary)\\nAla - Pal Arts Collective \\nMaud ~ migrants’ rights lawyer\\nseb ~ journalist, fundraiser \\nclara ~ fundraiser, organiser\\nSadhbh - queers for palestine\\n\\n\\n\\nWe will then break into small groups to get to know each other, discuss how we could use our own skills to do more or get active in new ways, and learn more. \\n\\nThis will be followed by live music by Pink Seasalt and g0d’s fave, and there will be food and drinks available all night. The event will also be a fundraiser (pay what you feel) with all profits going to grassroots orgs and families in Lebanon, Iran and Palestine. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":368,\"name\":\"Haringey Community Cinema presents 'The Stuart Hall Project' (dir. John Akomfrah) + Guests\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"34c3e9c8f57f1b2689ab1ce6df144caa.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for our new screenings as part of Black History Haringey 365.\\n\\nIn fact, one must note that at every moment Black peoples have sought, for themselves, to assert what freedom might mean and look like, those desires and acts toward freedom have been violently interdicted. It is this ongoing interdiction of a potential Black freedom that I have termed the long emancipation.— Rinaldo Walcott, The Long Emancipation: Moving Toward Black Freedom\\nBecause Black history is not a month, Haringey Community Cinema (HCC) invites you to a powerful series of screenings exploring Black histories, politics, culture, and struggle across the globe. As part of this series, we are interested in examining what Rinaldo Walcott framed as ‘the long emancipation’ through the use of moving images. This series brings into focus how colonialism, empire, racism, gender and sexuality have structured the ways Black life and thought are represented, questioned and resisted on screen.\\nOur programme includes films that centre Black voices and perspectives, alongside works that raise questions about how Black history is mediated and by whom.\\nWe begin with the first chapter of Frantz Fanon’s The Wretched of the Earth, read by Ms Lauryn Hill in Concerning Violence (dir. Göran Hugo Olsson). Next, Shari Frilot’s Black Nations / Queer Nations? chronicles the groundbreaking March 1995 conference on lesbian and gay sexualities in the African diaspora. To welcome Spring, we will shift our attention to the crucial role played by music in key moments of the Cold War with Soundtrack to a Coup d’Etat (dir. Johan Grimonprez). We will close with The Stuart Hall Project (dir. John Akomfrah), reflecting on the work and enduring legacy of Stuart Hall.\\nFor this edition, we have curated a list of readings that we encourage you to explore before the screenings.\\nOur guest speakers for hosting our community conversations will be revealed in the coming weeks.\\nThrough films, readings, and post-screening discussion, we will engage with questions of power, representation, memory, and history, and with the ongoing fight for justice in our communities and beyond.\\nAs always, our screenings are free to attend and open to all.\\nThis event is funded by the Haringey Council for Black History Haringey 365. This event is organised in collaboration with the Sussex Centre for Cultural Studies at the University of Sussex\\nBooking / Waiting List / Cancellation\\n\\nPlease only book if you are confident you will be able to attend, as seating at this venue is limited. Due to safety regulations, walk-in entry cannot be guaranteed.\\nThe registration form includes a small number of questions collected for reporting purposes. All data will be anonymised. Each attendee is required to complete the form. If you are booking on behalf of someone else and do not know an answer, please enter or select' N/A' where applicable.\\nDue to the venue’s limited capacity, the event may sell out.If this happens, you can be added to the waiting list. When a ticket becomes available, you will receive an email to book it, and you will have 24 hours to complete your booking.\\nIf you are unable to attend the event, please cancel your ticket(s) so that your place can be offered to someone else.\\nAbout the film\\n\\nThe Stuart Hall Project traces the journey of Stuart Hall, who left Jamaica for Oxford in 1951 and went on to become a defining voice in the emergence of cultural studies and a major force in British intellectual life. Drawing entirely on archival film, photographs, and the music of Miles Davis, the documentary mirrors Hall’s own fluid, exploratory thinking as it moves through questions of memory, identity, and the shifting political landscape of the late twentieth century. The result is a rich, layered portrait of the man whose ideas helped shape the New Left and transformed how we understand culture itself.\\nTrailer\\nAbout our Guest Speakers\\n\\nDr Clive Chijioke Nwonka is Associate Professor in Film, Culture and Society in the School of European Languages, Culture and Society within UCL’s Faculty of the Arts and Humanities, and a Faculty Associate of the UCL Sarah Parker Remond Centre for the Study of Racism and Racialisation. Prior to UCL, he was Lecturer in Film and Literature the Department English and Related Literature at the University of York and the London School of Economics and Political Science, where he was an LSE Fellow in Film Studies within the Department of Sociology.\\nNwonka is the Principal Investigator on the Arts and Humanities Research Council funded project The Colour of Diversity: A Longitudinal Analysis of the BFI Diversity Standards Data and Racial Inequality in the UK Film Industry (2021-2024), a major study of race and racism in the UK film sector and the efficacy of cultural diversity policy.\\nOrsod Malik is a curator of exhibitions and archives, writer, independent researcher, and the Executive Director of the Stuart Hall Foundation. Malik’s work explores transnational cultural and political entanglements in historical narratives to consider the possibility of shared histories.\\nMalik has curated exhibitions and developed programmes for several cultural organisations including, The Stuart Hall Foundation, International Curators Forum (ICF), Black Cultural Archives, Institute of International Visual Arts (iniva), Prince Claus Fund and the British Council. Malik also serves as a Trustee at The Common Guild, a visual arts organisation in Glasgow.\\nWhy your donations are important?\\n\\nPlease read carefully! We’re introducing a Community Pricing to help cover the costs of our events. Choose the ticket tier that best reflects your current circumstances— considering income, housing, caring responsibilities, health, and day-to-day financial pressures. We trust you to choose what feels right. More on this system here.\\nHCC is run by volunteers and does not receive any funding at the moment. Every donation you make will help us to support local venues and to organise other free screenings.\\nIn a time of rising living costs and persistent barriers for marginalised communities in producing and accessing films that reflect their experiences and aspirations, we are committed to making our screenings free or pay-what-you-can.\\nAbout the venue\\n\\nChestnuts Community Centre offers a fantastic community facility and community programme in the heart of South Tottenham. The building is located in Chestnut Park (closest tube station is Seven Sisters), and is fully accessible. If you have any accessibility needs or questions, please contact us at haringeycommunitycinema@gmail.com.\\nAbout HCC\\n\\nHaringey Community Cinema (HCC) was launched in April 2025 and is run by volunteers. Inspired by Brixton Community Cinema, HCC is aimed at bringing residents of Haringey together through film. Our mission is to showcase films that challenge, inspire, and spark critical reflection—films that make us think and act. Visit our website.\\nCovid Policy\\n\\nHCC does not currently have an official COVID-19 policy. However, we remain mindful that many people are still vulnerable to the virus. We kindly ask attendees to take the following precautions to help keep our events safe and accessible for everyone:\\nIf possible, please take a lateral flow test before attending.\\nIf you test positive or are experiencing any COVID-19 symptoms, please do not attend, even if you feel well.\\nWe welcome and encourage the use of masks inside the venue for those who wish to wear them.\\nPlease be considerate of others' comfort levels and respect requests for physical distance.\\nThank you for helping us create a safer and more inclusive space\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/hcc-presents-the-stuart-hall-project-dir-john-akomfrah-guests-registration-1987940484503\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":381,\"name\":\"DANCE NOT DANCE: where the body dissolves and movement persists\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c47aff6e985ea0edf938c3383ae879e2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"DANCE NOT DANCE imagines and portrays what choreography looks like both with\\nand without dancers: when movement is spoken, heard, and imagined rather than\\nseen. Through percussion, dance, voice, text, and electronic sound, the work unfolds\\nas a layered environment in which the audience and their individual experience\\nbecomes the eventual site of the dance.\\nFeaturing The Drum Also Dances (Freddie Krone, drums and Zac Priestley, dance)\\nand Breath Quartet (Marcus Herne and Margot Wilson), the evening moves between\\nembodied rhythm, disembodied choreography, and live improvisation. The two\\ngroups will come together for a collaborative piece at the end of the evening.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":420,\"name\":\"Ridley Road Music Showcase \\u0026 Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cdbbae2d0eb77f23545b82d2c74e4340.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Don't miss this historical night of poetry, live music performances, DJ vinyl sets showcasing the talent of Ridley Road. There will be unmatched jerk chicken and other finger foods. \\n\\nTraders from Ridley Road Shopping Village will share their testimonies from the last years of struggle against the gentrification of Dalston which threatens their livelihood and the entire community. \\n\\n \\n\\nMeet people from the campaign, and get involved. \\n\\nAll donations will go directly to the Ridley Road legal defence fundraiser. \\n\\n \\n\\nCapacity is LIMITED, make sure to get your tickets ASAP! We expect to sell out! \\n\\n \\n\\nRidley road Shopping Village traders need your support. They are being evicted. Support them in their fight to secure a fair and permanent future in our community!\\nTraders in the Ridley Road Shopping Village have been fighting eviction for almost a decade. \\n\\nThey have beaten unlawful eviction notices, planning applications and managed decline. Through it all, they have continued to represent a hub of predominantly black businesses, offering culture and life to underserved communities in Hackney and beyond.   \\n\\nOn 31 March, some traders along with the community peacefully resisted attempts by security to close the market. They now have weeks at most to prepare and finance a court case for their right to stay.  \\n\\n A community occupation is helping them keep the space running. \\n\\nThis community fundraiser will allow traders to take their fate in their own hands, by defending their tenancy rights in court. It will show them that Hackney is behind them and that we believe in their right to exist. It is one essential component of a wider campaign against gentrification, displacement, and contempt for Hackney’s own heritage. \\n\\nFor almost a decade, Save Ridley Road have said: Ridley Road is the beating heart of Hackney. \\n\\nRidley Road is an eco-system. A threat to one part of the road has knock-on effects for ALL. \\n\\nPlease donate to this legal defence fundraiser. Every penny counts and will go towards securing the future of the parts of our borough that we value most.\\n\\nFunds raised will primarily be any legal costs involved in a court defence of traders’ tenancy rights. Secondary expenditures will be on equipment needed to sustain the occupation.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/36011/ridley-road-music-showcase-fundraiser\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":424,\"name\":\"Zancudo Berraco + aircode + ex.sses + King Monolith\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3e586c04525ea4b3fc63c3e559595e07.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"False Locust is excited to present four artists found in the darkest, most thrilling corners of experimental electronic music.\\n\\nZancudo Berraco is the explosive experimental techno alias of Portuguese multi-instrumentalist Henrique Apolinário. A dedicated sonic explorer, he crafts loud, full-spectrum, and fast-paced live sets designed for pure dance-floor catharsis.\\n\\naircode is a Swedish producer based in London whose music is typified by dubwise dynamics, sonic capaciousness, and permutable elements of percussion, voice and piano. They have performed across Europe, and put out records on the labels TT (formerly Tobago Tracks), Takuroko, Alien Jams, Gin\\u0026Platonic and NHS along with a number of self-released Bandcamp drops. \\n\\nex.sses (she/they) is an experimental producer and DJ. ex.sses fuses heavy bass, broken drums and textural sounds, from her resident shows on Balamii and Netil to her guest mixes for NTS, Kiosk Radio she has built a bass led palette of sounds, unconfined by genre. ex.sses’ ties to experimental sound and club culture have since manifested in releases on TT, BAIT, Traverse, glint, Earful of Wax, Cherche Encore and Hard Return and has premiered on DJ Mag, Mixmag and Bad Tips. These releases have gained attention over the years, resulting in dark, club focused DJ sets across the UK and Europe. Her live electronic performances expand on ex.sses’ exploration of noise, textural sounds, poetry and the gendered body. \\n\\nKing Monolith blends noise, dub and reckless sampling to form a chaotic style of dance music; constantly on the edge of collapse into full blown noise.\\n\\nPoster by Matej Siska.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":265,\"name\":\"Amena and Ziad Hisham: A Night of Egyptian Jazz\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"783baa087eaa21dd78e37233827b42ab.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A night of contemporary Egyptian Jazz featuring 2 outstanding artists?  Yes please.   See you there.\\n\\nZiad Hisham is a visionary guitarist and composer blending the expressive depth of jazz with the rich heritage of Egyptian music. Weaving intricate melodies, deep grooves, and improvisational storytelling into a seamless fusion of East and West. Performing for over a decade, Ziad has developed his instrumental project alongside collaborations with renowned artists such as Grammy Award winner Fathy Salama, Sheikh Mahmoud El Tohamy, Sara Moullablad, Luka Salam, Mohamed Abo Zekry, and Amena. His work has taken him across diverse musical landscapes, from contemporary jazz ensembles to traditional Arabic ensembles and experimental fusion projects.  \\n\\nAmena is a singer/songwriter from Cairo, Egypt. Growing up in the vibrant city, she developed a love for both Arabic and Jazz music.  As she studied at Guildhall School in London, she aims to create music that blends her cultural roots with the harmony and rhythms of Jazz.  In her newest project, she draws inspiration from pioneers of Egyptian/Levantine musicians like Sayed Darwish and Rahbani Brothers.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/amena-and-ziad-hisham-a-night-of-egyptian-jazz/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":453,\"name\":\"The Man With The Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c5c339f3b7e246128fb0d8d5ec46d87c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":361,\"name\":\"I BECOME YOU - Lo Simple - Album release party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5c309ef5f411fe7045e74087cb2fcf85.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lo Simple's debut album release will be celebrated with a night of music and performances.\\n\\nLo Simple are a London-based trio of Ignacio Salvadores (Gal Go), Sheiva, and Danny Jerome, cutting through the noise to find beauty in distortion and build something distinctly their own. They carve out a space where the expansive soundscapes of post-rock collide with the melodic haze of shoegaze and the jagged edges of leftfield pop.\\n\\n\\nI BECOME YOU - LO SIMPLE via THEFT / MINIMIZZATI\\nComing together bringing their own perspective on what navigating life really means, and each bringing their own perspective, while drawing on a collective instinct for experimentation and emotional depth. Born from a desire to translate internal experiences into something universally felt, the album explores connection, identity, and emotional healing. Much of its writing emerges from the subconscious, giving the record a raw, intuitive energy.\\n\\nMAY\\nLeft field pop star from London\\n\\nItsmyluckyday\\n\\nBorn out of an impromptu late night studio session, itsmyluckyday the brainchild of Rafi George and Die Katze.\\nTraversing the boundaries of folk, rock and electronic synths, their music exists in a place\\nsomewhere between dreaming and waking.\\n\\nDIONOKIA\\nblends latin bass, dembow, UK funky and bubbling into percussion-heavy, rhythmic and bouncy sets. Inspired by Caribbean sounds, she focuses on creating energetic, inclusive dance floors built on movement and connection.\\n\\nOriana\\nA London-based singer-songwriter writing dreamy, introspective songs shaped by honesty and emotion. With soft vocals and a storyteller’s touch, her performances unfold differently each time, settling into an intimate, gentle space.\\n\\nDoors at 19:30\\n£15 otd\\nPay what you can before 20:00\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2422717\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":449,\"name\":\"Scouts, Ice Baths, Ollie Bentley\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-21T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5278e59cb063789b6c2860e9e0a6020e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Advanced sold out. Tickets still available OTD \\n\\nScouts: Scouts are a post-punk four-piece from South East London, blending noisy, atmospheric textures with the raw intensity of punk. Drawing from influences that range from post-punk to trip hop and shoegaze, their sound is restless and evolving, driven by experimentation and high-energy live performances.\\n\\nIce Baths: London based Ice Baths take influence from cult heroes such as Swell Maps, Television Personalities, Wire, US Maple – all restless energy and angled aggression. Lyrically there is a bleakness and darkness, though the band prefer the listener to reach their own conclusions as to lyrical themes.\\n\\nOllie Bentley: Made in Peckham, singer of Pig City Committee and thereminist of Omertà. \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":441,\"name\":\"SONIDERA: Sailing through La Amazonía\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"79491770d1b5b9d66da7e2b9c40dbf55.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For this May SONIDERA, THH welcomes the curation of Nervio Vago Dee Jay, aka Sonido Martines, opening sonic worlds that undulate through the dense vegetation of La Amazonía\\n\\n4 hours of specially selected hits and gems that often accompany the sailing of boats through the rivers of the rainforest, exhibiting a legacy of radio-based networks for the distribution of musical influences, that encounters face to face with one of the richest biodiversities in the whole of world\\n\\nFREE ENTRY 6pm-10pm\\n\\nNervio Vago Dee Jay is a digital alias of record collector Javier Martines, a Bolivian-based connoisseur with more than 27 years of experience being a music selector, fiddler and dealer of the rarest projects of música popular from the south. As of 2021, Nervio Vago Dee Jay has had a vinyl focused NTS show called Humo Mundial, describing him as a ‘cratedigger extraordinaire’.  \\n\\n-------\\n\\nSONIDERA is a social event that platforms music from the Global South,  articulating sonic discourse through carefully selected playlists and a safe environment for dancing and collective enjoyment\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":446,\"name\":\"Dirar Kalash \\u0026 Friends: Electro-acoustic Residency – Marysia Osu\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"96b74ad9e2eb4ec1d02b95e852c006d6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Three nights of experimental improvisation with Dirar Kalash \\u0026 Friends.\\n\\nGritty and effervescent, Dirar Kalash's experimental music is known to be transcendental and deeply embodied. An extraordinary Palestinian sound artist, Kalash pushes boundaries in his sonic work with a vast repertoire of collaborations, including artists such as Nicolas Jaar. For this series, he invites:\\n\\n\\nMAY 13 - BARBIE MUKODA - Flautist and improvised blending classical and experimental sound worlds through tone and silence.\\nMAY 22 - MARYSIA OSU - Harpist, producer, and composer who blends classical, ambient, and electronic music.\\nMAY 27 - ROXANNA ALBAYATI - Cellist \\u0026 artist blending experimental music with cross-cultural improvisation and multimedia performance.\\n\\nStudio 12 is an intimate art space with a custom sound system \\u0026 cocktail bar in Camberwell, London. It's dedicated to art, music, poetry and film, rooted in transnational solidarities.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/dirar-kalash-friends-electro-acoustic-residency-with-studio-12-tickets-1988393935788?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":347,\"name\":\"FUNDRAISER: A history of Afro-Cuban Cinema film screening\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f43e004f5ef6c49d23c2458e7631f4cc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In support of Tramas Cine Diáspora Africana, a Havana-based project dedicated to the often invisibilised presence and impact of Afrodescendant Cuban filmmakers. The films in this program span the advent of cinema in Cuba to the present day. These films document Afrodescendant culture in its breadth: from the historic Black communities of old Havana to middle-class families on the outskirts, from African spiritual singing traditions to the rigour and precision of the ballet of the Afro-Cuban dance company Conjunto Folclórico Nacional de Cuba. The program also demonstrates the poetic, experimental, and always creative nature of Afrodescendant filmmakers, whose approaches often ran parallel to the mainstream.\\n\\nAll proceeds go to support the future work of Tramas Cine Diáspora Africana.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/fundraiser-a-history-of-afro-cuban-cinema\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":274,\"name\":\"djank / Crazy Paving / Or Sobre Blau\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6452a54a2d3a6e32c4b3a417104fb670.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House presents a night of incredible new music, with some of the most exciting new voices in the scene.\\nFormed by Taylor Pollock, djank is the amalgamation of all of the kitschy antiques your grandparents hoarded and all of the beers you stole in highschool. Formed into a big mess of heavy guitars, four part harmonies, DIY videos, and lofi cassette loops, djank take inspiration from folk, midwest emo, 90’s pop, and whatever records or snippets of audio they find in charity shops and on Internet Archive.\\nRobbie Carman’s new project, Crazy Paving, released their debut EP at the end of last year. Though the material is written by Robbie, the band recorded and perform live as an energetic seven piece. The group consists of members from other bands of the same scene (nudista, Flypaper, Wilshaw, Moon Balloon, Baggio) and are very comfortable with each other on stage, this makes for a great show. Clearly influenced by the likes of Beck, The Clean, Buzzcocks and the Undertones.\\nOr Sobre Blau is Kiran Leonard and Andreu G. Serra, whose new album Making Friends is out on June 2nd via Stroom TV. Harmonically, the duo's debt to Slint's ambivalent dissonances and the misshapen free blues of Loren Connors and Bill Orcutt remains evident. Added to this, the more expansive sound on “Making Friends” draws from wells as varied as Title Fight's scrappy emo, Yellow Swans' ultra-thick blasted-out fuzz, and Maher Shalal Hash Baz's cracked arborescent chamber music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/U0c381b33993\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":437,\"name\":\"HORSEPOWER\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-23T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f576cd2692a7cfcaba4ddb1cf85a212c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"HORSEPOWER is a new party focused on FLINTA+ dj-producers in and around the capital.\\n\\nSliding scale tickets OTD.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":462,\"name\":\"Hop Skotshne\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9ecfc1ed51e34e91f6c2d800d7b7ab2b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A fun and dynamic Klezmer band who play fabulous traditional Klezmer tunes. Taking the authentic repertoire of Jewish wedding music from Eastern Europe, and adding their unique and inventive interpretations, the band will take you on an emotional journey into the world of klezmer music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsmusic.eventive.org/schedule/698a1ca54e8b0e3dce936fbc\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":330,\"name\":\"Roots on the Corner #43. CREATION REBEL Sound System meets ROOTS SENSATION Sound System.\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-23T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"027d5e0e12608b48b7ae921764c52b4f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We ready for the next round of Roots on the Corner, Yes we are!!\\n\\n\\nMay the 22nd is going to be a night of heavy, deep \\u0026 spiritual roots music!! Yes yes its going to be a historical revival of the old meets the new, meets the upliftment, meets the connection, with you, with earth, with all as one! And to make sure we fulfil this promise to all of our skankers we have called upon the Souljah's; CREATION REBEL sound system ft. Tudor Lion \\u0026 Ras Terry Gad and ROOTS SENSATION sound system ft Ramon Judah (Resident Sound 2 returns!). \\n\\n\\nSo expect Dubwise, Roots, Steppas (Dub Techno) and of course healing basslines, at the very lovely Distillery N17 in Tottenham Hale, the Home of Pirates Grog Rum. \\n\\n\\nAs its our 10th year we are continuing with those give back vibes, and have launched online £5 / £10 Super Early Bird tickets so grab yours, as it's £15 on the door. \\n\\n\\nExpect the usual giveaways and good vibes and we'll see you at the bar getting those Rum punches! Looking forward to skankin with ya! \\n\\n\\nDoors open 10pm - 5am. Last Entry 3am. Nearest tube: Tottenham hale.\\n\\nVENUE - DISTILLERY-N17, Unit 25, Mill Mead Rd, London N17 9QU, UK\\n\\nPirates Grog.\\n\\n\\nPlease bring ID, over 18\\\"s only.\\n\\nCASH \\u0026 CARDS accepted.\\n\\n(Online Ticket sales close 11am 22nd May.)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.rotc.uk/event-details-registration/roots-on-the-corner-43-creation-rebel-sound-system-meets-roots-sensation-sound-system\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":484,\"name\":\"-----\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T22:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-22T22:31:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7fd0581b368482c27dafd27d0669c42e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":362,\"name\":\"SYPHEN [AFTERPARTY]: Slikback, Nkisi, Exploited Body, MRWIZE, Blood of Aza b2b Mvcoko, Y'sohnt\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-22T23:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-23T05:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"329614d9fc6ee86ca8f7c2f360a2ea5b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Diasporic Explorations.\\nA celebration of blackness.\\nA celebration of duality.\\nA celebration of music.\\nA celebration of performance.\\n\\n\\n[NIGHT] ORMSIDE PROJECTS\\n23:30 - 05:30\\nW/ Blood of Aza b2b Mvcoko, Exploited Body, MRWIZE, Nkisi, Slikback, Y'sohnt\\n\\n[DAY] ICA\\nDoors: 17:00\\nCurfew: 23:00\\nW/ Aho Ssan, Blood of Aza, Lord Spikeheart, Mvcoko, Slikback\\n\\n\\n\\nCombined DAY \\u0026 NIGHT tickets can be purchased through the DAY event listing and include entrance for the afterparty at Ormside Projects.\\n\\n\\nConcession tickets are available for those who may otherwise be unable to attend. A number of tickets are also held in reserve for the unwaged global majority.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2401580\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":471,\"name\":\"Worlding Soundings\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-23T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"03df94c1ca288e9725cf3639e689ac7f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Worlding Soundings is a series of one-day residencies proposed by Acoustic Survey Art Lab, at and with WORLDING, launching this May in Southwark, London (one-day each month). It brings together complementary approaches: sound, visual and performative arts. Come for full-day residency or for the evening sharing and hangout from 6pm (tiered tickets).\\n\\nThese full-day sonic \\\"residencies\\\" are for everyone (no music skills necessary but also welcome), artists, musicians, performers, movement practitioners, and curious participants. They were designed as an immersive, time-generous experience. \\n\\nResidency Prospective Schedule:\\n\\n10am - 11pm:       welcome, sound history \\u0026 theory short intro\\n11 - 12pm:             1rst workshop with sound \\u0026 listening explorations\\n30 min personal break \\n12:30 - 13:30pm:  communal lunch with food by Zar's Plate\\n1:45 - 2:45 pm:     2nd workshop with words, voice and graphic explorations\\n15 min break\\n3pm - 4pm:           3rd workshop with sculpture, drawing \\u0026 sound\\n5 - 5:45pm:           assisted individual projects\\n15 min break\\n6pm:                       nibbles \\u0026 evening Public Sharing \\n9pm                        evening finish\\n10pm:                     closing time\\n\\nEach day-session is different, unfolding around a theme/specific angle, providing an open environment for improvisation, listening, recording, and cross-disciplinary sound practice, combining short contextual \\u0026 historical background, guided exercises, practical sound-making techniques, reflection, communal plant-based meals (included in whole-day price), and an evening hangout \\u0026 sharing event. \\n\\nAcross the sessions, participants will be invited to work with voice, found objects, recording devices, everyday materials, environment, space, and collective sound-making.\\n\\nHighlights include:\\n- improvisation with guest artists\\n- listening and recording exercises\\n- practical sound-making techniques\\n- communal plant-based meals\\n- evening hangouts with performances, often leading to conversation and participation\\n- Evening refreshments \\u0026 nibbles \\n\\n\\nSaturday 23rd Guests:\\nSound Artist Jakub Rokita\\nVisual artist, Dancer and Choreographer Constança Saturnino\\nVisual Artist Diogo Pimentão\\nCurator, Podcaster and Writer Joana P. R. Neves\\n\\nA collaboration between WORLDING x Acoustic Survey Art Lab. WORLDING offers a context shaped by exchange, experimentation, care, food, and public-facing artistic activity. Acoustic Survey Art Lab brings a research-driven practice exploring the sonic character of spaces through deep listening, site-responsive recording, and live experimentation.\\n@worldingproject\\n@cmykscum\\n@joanaprneves\\n@diogopimentaodaily\\n@zars.plate\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":392,\"name\":\"Bodega Nights ~ Green Alley Studios Exploring New Horizons\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ca6f3657203f0e10b657abe9842b9b5f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"💥 It’s official! Green Alley Studios is changing hands as we venture out into the world, exploring new horizons 💫 We are so grateful to have found this space in Bethnal Green, to have taken the leap of starting up the studios and having the most wonderful people join us! We’ve had many great parties, markets and exhibitions and had the joy of working side by side with long term and new found friends 🌱 Many things have changed since the beginning and new adventures in the world have lured us away, and the space is now being handed over to a wonderful group of studio members to enter into a new chapter!\\n💥 To celebrate this ending and new beginning we have partnered with our friends Bodega Nights to throw another one of their amazing boogie fests and come together in a last dance and music frenzy for Green Alley Studios as we know it 💫\\nWe’ll have a Flea Market during the day and DJ’s from 3pm 🎶 Happy Hour until 7pm! Come hang out, come boogie!\\n\\n🪆 Flea Market: 11 - 5pm\\n🪩 Music: 3pm - 2am\\n📍 Cambridge Heath road E2 9RA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":431,\"name\":\"Gaffe presents: A day to night adventure\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f19f0194cdf227eb25c4f3b92bce569f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"May 23 sees Gaffe open both courtyard and warehouse for a full day to night session built around movement between spaces, moods and tempos.\\n\\nOutside in the courtyard, Luca \\u0026 Leo set the tone on home ground before handing over to a rare extended session from Cabanne. A defining figure in French minimal and long associated with the Yoyaku universe, Cabanne’s deeply reduced, playful and hypnotic approach is best experienced with time to stretch properly.\\n\\nRunning alongside this, the warehouse hosts an ambient programme for International Synthesiser Day, led by Infinite Monkeys live improvisation. Expect spontaneous electronics, modular drift and a softer listening space that offers a welcome counterpoint to the movement outside.\\n\\nAs evening folds in, focus shifts fully to the main room for the night session.\\n\\nAdi opens with patient selections and dance-led instincts, setting the room with intent before Que Sakamoto brings his unmistakable blend of machine soul, eccentric groove and emotional leftfield house. Nina Yamada follows with sharp control and fluid movement through percussive rhythm and stripped-back pressure, before Annyrock drives things deeper with the kind of direct, high-energy precision that thrives in late hours.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2413779\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":302,\"name\":\"West London Dub Club Chapter VII - Vedic Roots meets Touch Above\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-23T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9f4a7641e83c8d13d9694563a9b9303b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"West London Dub Club presents Chapter VII: VEDIC ROOTS meets TOUCH ABOVE\\n\\n5PM-11PM\\nSaturday 23rd May 2026\\nThe Dominion Centre 112 The Green, Southall UB2 4BQ\\nFood - Music – Merchandise\\nALL TRIBES WELCOME!\\n\\nVedic Roots Sound System\\n-Outta West London\\n-Rana, Taran \\u0026 full crew\\n\\nTouch Above Sound System\\n-Outta North London\\n-Brian De Lion, Highway Man \\u0026 full crew\\n\\nBoth playing on their own full sound systems\\nStrictly heavyweight business till done!\\n\\nInstagram \\u0026 Facebook - @WestLondonDubClub\\n\\nTravel\\nTube: Southall (Elizabeth Line) 6 Min Walk\\nCar: Large car park next to venue\\n\\nTickets\\nAdvanced starting from £10 + booking fees\\nM.O.T.D (More On The Door)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2420979\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":430,\"name\":\"9 Years of M.O.B - A Story of Rave\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-23T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3a1f8f1bcca573300f35c61815fa7a86.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"M.O.B celebrates 9 years of existence this coming bank holiday weekend.\\n\\nOur story is one that is deeply rooted in rave culture, a movement that transformed the very fabric of society in this country and elsewhere. Rave was birthed at the intersection of the socio-political upheaval of digitalisation, the economic decay of post industrial-cities and the affirmation of queer and marginalised communities. \\n\\nBehind the emergence of this phenomenon in the UK is sound system culture which was pioneered by Black communities across the country. Shunned and rejected from places of leisure and entertainment, they \\\"seized the means of production\\\" of music and arts and gave themselves the ability to socialise and express themselves, inspiring a generation of young people to do the same. Thus was born the legendary sound system: Spiral Tribe.\\n\\nOur guest for this event is 69db, a prominent member of Spiral Tribe and an early proponent of live electronic performances in raves. Spiral Tribe and 69db are the root of much of what exists in the rave scene today, so what better way to celebrate our anniversary than by highlighting this inspirational figure.\\n\\nJoining 69db for this event is a fittingly live-heavy bill of amazing performers: xár num, the live alias of Primordial Ooze - one third of the Cortex of Light project / Bones Tan Jones, stunning vocalist + live electronic act and body performer / Van Dyke Browne, the DJ moniker of the person behind Vinyl Hunter record shop / 27 Eggs, the live jam act by our three M.O.Bsters Ab Ru, Bubble People and Max Burstyn. \\n\\n69db pres. Wave Arising (Spiral Tribe - Live)\\nxár num (Live)\\nBones Tan Jones (Live)\\nVan Dyke Browne (DJ)\\n27 Eggs (Live)\\n\\n(Part 2 as always... details will be sent to Part 1 ticket holders)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/mob/2211961\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":278,\"name\":\"Costumes of Sound\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-23T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2df4a4d623d3e46d4c4a0fead6e6f16c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us on Saturday, the 23rd of May, with Luca Bosani, Isabell Castro, Katy Howe, Natalie Price Halfslund.\\n\\nThrough live performance, wearable art, costume making, and sonic environments, this event brings together artists working across these intersections, questioning rigid definitions and categories, and reconsidering the hierarchies and histories of mediums and practices.\\n\\nWe gather to reflect on what is generated and how, what comes before or after, whether it is the moving body, recorded sound, or the engagement with fabrics. Each piece holds these questions open, allowing meaning to emerge through making.\\n\\nYou are invited to witness, to move, to dance, to show up in your own expression, and to stay with the uncertainty and excitement of creation as it happens.\\n\\n7 PM Doors\\n\\n7.30 PM Performances start\\n\\nDj and exhibition space open in intervals throughout the evening\\n\\n11 PM close\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/g5xpwa-costumes-of-sound-23rd-may-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":238,\"name\":\"Terra Obscura w/ OK EG, Garçon, Daniel[i], slyn \\u0026 alicia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2c169d61411cf43bf3992831e94d94ea.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Terra Obscura is happening again after a year of dreaming, plotting \\u0026 planning a comeback that is sure to ruffle your feathers ... Expect your recommended dose of ambient, downtempo and left-field club sounds. Exploring this special new venue South London cocoon Club Cheek, we can't wait to share our new ideas with you.\\n\\nFor this comeback edition, we feel very lucky to have Gravity Pleasure’s slyn taking us through the ambient opening and the Australian duo OK EG presenting their ambient live show to follow. Taking us from the downtempo realm into the dance is none other than Garçon followed by the incredible live set from daniel[i] and our own alicia taking care of the closing set. Our hearts flutter just thinking about spending this evening and night with you all !!\\n\\n\\nTogether, we will take off from the comfort of carpets, beanbags and cushions in our cozy ambient setup and slowly tickle your ears and bodies until we reach the feral dance euphoria lurking on the other side of midnight.\\n\\nYour guides through the night will be announced in the next week.\\n\\n✧･ﾟ: *✧･ﾟSee you on the cloud! ･ﾟ✧*:･ﾟ✧\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2405843\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":371,\"name\":\"Sagome: giesse, Saskia (live), DJ Autosleeper, Nice Strangers\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-23T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d5b42aedc1e325257fffb7bd76f821b3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An exciting return of one of the hidden gems of the Italian club scene - giesse aka ssiege - plus a dance-oriented live set from Tokyo-via-Bristol producer and sound artist, Saskia. \\nSagome founders Nice Strangers and DJ Autosleeper to open the night and play in between sets.\\n\\n~~~\\n\\ngiesse \\ngiesse is an Italian DJ and producer whose sonic language is defined by contrast: restraint and impact, structure and instinct, tension and release. His sets move with intention, shaping linear yet unpredictable journeys through tightly controlled dynamics and detailed transitions. His style draws from a minimal and physical approach, combining sharp percussive energy with moments of spacious, hypnotic calm. He is the co-founder of the HMZ label and also works under the alias SSIEGE, a parallel project focused on atmospheric and cinematic soundscapes, with releases on YOUTH and Knekelhuis. In 2025, he released an EP on Hundebiss, marking another chapter in a practice rooted in club pressure, percussive force, and physical energy.\\n\\nhttps://soundcloud.com/giesse999\\n\\n\\nSaskia (Live)\\nA sound artist from Kanagawa, Japan, Saskia explores the deep connections between space, emotion, and music. Now based in the UK, she creates works that move between ambient and rhythmically experimental sound, while also performing live and DJing. Her latest LP es, released in 2024, is an experimental narrative that explores “something invisible yet undeniably present”, touching on vitality and the power of observation. Guided by the concept of “Sound to _____ this magnificent cell,” her music constantly invites listeners on new journeys.\\n\\nhttps://soundcloud.com/saskia-n3\\n\\n\\n____\\n\\n\\nAndrea Campisi is supported by the Early Career Promoter Fund which is managed by PRS Foundation and funded by Arts Council England using Supporting Grassroots Music funding from DCMS.\\n \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":379,\"name\":\"Patterns: 9AM-5PM with Cashu, Fergus Jones, Nuno Beats, Raf Reza and Lali\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-24T09:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b88f6ed0fec30f9e181a86221822a800.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Clock in, Clock out \\n\\n\\nBalcony open all day / Natural Light in the Dance Floor / Food Available\\n\\nCashu (Mamba rec) \\nFergus Jones (Felt) \\nNuno Beats (Príncipe) \\nRaf Reza \\nLali \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":412,\"name\":\"Ground Support [COMMUNAL CLAY \\u0026 LUCIE MACGREGOR]\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-24T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3b245f0b7c956a109818384da8f86376.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ground Support - A Collective Workshop on Material Cycles \\u0026 Connection, led by Lucie Macgregor at Set Social's Garden. \\n\\nJoin us for Ground Support, a workshop exploring cycles of matter, language, and care through collective sculptural making and reflection. Rooted in themes of circularity, planting, translation, and our relationship to land, this session invites participants to work with paper pulp and potatoes as anchors for connection and transformation.\\n\\nGround Support is an invitation to slow down, to make with care, and to consider how language, materials, and community can be continuously reshaped and re-rooted.\\n\\nThe workshop will have a collective reading of the Ground Support text, exploring the idea of repurposing language. Participants will focus on letters or fragments that resonate with them, transforming these into personal symbols from abstract shapes formed from memory, intuition, and text. \\n\\nThe workshop is process focus, and you will have a paper pulp keepsake to take away. \\n\\nNo prior experience is needed. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":476,\"name\":\"Tissue 17\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-24T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a87ebae00ae3b549f1ffc285f467e800.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tissue Fundraiser for Lucy Peterson with readings. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/tissue-17-lucys-london-fundraiser-tickets-1988571231083?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\\u0026fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQPOTM2NjE5NzQzMzkyNDU5AAGnhmAdA2yG8NvuG-AD-mP43BUYu1RsPbMG_vnNSrF6e7YCzCpavEbE9DVoRF0_aem_P0QxHOHg1TcglQpYpoPg_Q\\u0026utm_id=97760_v0_s00_e0_tv3\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":406,\"name\":\"Black Obsidian Sound System x Pssound System\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-24T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"67ff89486bb66cb2bff52c69421f3c58.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Black Obsidian Sound System (B.O.S.S.) is a queer, feminist sound system collective from London, founded in 2018 by Black and POC queer and trans artists, DJs, and activists. Channeling Caribbean sound system traditions and UK club DIY spirit, they use music as a tool for resistance, healing, and collective joy. With their mobile sound system, they organise parties, protests, and educational events that bridge club culture, activism, and art. In 2021, they were nominated for the Turner Prize but simultaneously voiced criticism of the institution behind the prestigious award. Staying true to their values of community, B.O.S.S. creates inclusive spaces that centre Black, queer, and trans voices, reinterpreting the sound system tradition in a way that feels more urgent than ever.\\n\\nPSST is an intersectional feminist platform fighting for more inclusion in music and nightlife through events, workshops, a database and a community sound system, which they built during one of their workshops.\\n\\nPSST \\u0026 BOSS connected a year ago in Brussels to celebrate PSST' 7th birthday, and this time, PSST is traveling across the UK with their Pssound System, and this gig is their first stop!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2428498\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":383,\"name\":\"glint music: knotted + Funny Games + Henry Cyer + Pyromunchkin bank holiday fest @ the horse hospital\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-24T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a69cd3403147f4f373d9a8430a325850.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"late may bank holiday party\\nto celebrate the release of the beautiful Trampoline\\nwe're going to play the record through on the beautiful Horse Hospital system\\nand have other people play live to celebrate knotted.\\n\\nCDs available \\n\\ndivineglintmusic.bandcamp.com\\n\\nknotted plays in imaginary fields ,stretching time then shrinking it, joining found sounds ,tying voice memos of loose ideas with her favorite guitars and sincerity ,allowing clarity to bubble up for a moment then throwing it back to the whirlpool\\n\\nher album Trampoline is out now on glint music: https://knotted.bandcamp.com/album/trampoline\\n\\nTrampoline is a tall spiral staircase turning into a smooth tornado that moves below the sand finding blue and reaches high toward yellow.\\n\\nTrampoline spreads between folk, noise and ambient,,, rooted always in a kind of spiritual relationship to sound and city\\n\\n---\\n\\nfunny games is a boy from london who wants you to dance to his songs: https://www.ninaprotocol.com/releases/running-on-2\\n\\n---\\n\\nHenry Cyer is an artist and musician, whose work has been praised by The Wire magazine for its “unashamedly vaunting ambition”.\\n\\nHis musical work explores forms of otherness within the performer, taking cues from literary techniques, architecture and avant-garde composition to craft and collapse his distinct song form.\\n\\nHis live appearances use dimly lit space to immerse the viewer in an intense sonic experience – equally scenic and emotive – as a means towards a shared transcendence.\\n\\nCyer has performed live at Cafe OTO, Ormside Projects, Barbican Centre, Mayhem Kbh, amongst others.\\n\\nHe runs The Hotel.\\n\\n---\\n\\nPyromunchkin is a new band featuring rory j s and douglas neville. they played their first show at spanners last month. rory j s released 'murky j' on glint music last year: https://rjssound.bandcamp.com/album/murky-j-2 and douglas is a writer and artist who has been in more bands than we will ever know...\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":275,\"name\":\"family affair: a party for palestine with Anna Wall, Mariiin, Olita, Dora and Sheriff Boo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-24T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-25T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f1cd9954153a5956f6333d03c7068d18.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On Sunday 24th May, we return to MOT for a Bank Holiday party - raising urgent funds for the ongoing crisis in Gaza with 100% of profits going to MSF UK.  On the night we welcome a stacked host of amazing artists to play together for the cause, for our eighth fundraiser party in the capital.   With a longstanding residency at fabric and two great labels under her belt, Anna Wall is a true pillar of London’s underground. On the night, she shares the booth with the fiercely infectious Mariiin, as the two deejays go stride-for-stride for three electric hours.   Also exercising some big 'n bad booth synergy on the night are none other than London’s Olita and Dora. By no means strangers to going head-to-head, most recently with an all-night long session together up in Manchester, these two brave explorers of sound bring their groove ladened oddities to the fore.   We really can't wait for this.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2358646\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":273,\"name\":\"Back to Breath: JON DIXON\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-25T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-25T14:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4f7f8404ae62885ec9a0b775254b4e47.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Introducing our new series: Back to Breath.\\nInviting live musicians to play alongside our founder Barbora as she guides you through breathwork.\\n\\nOur first session welcomes Detroit legend Jon Dixon: keyboardist, producer, and core member of the iconic Underground Resistance collective. Trained in classical piano from fifteen and mentored by jazz legend Marcus Belgrave, his sound fuses Detroit jazz with electronic music - what he calls \\\"Hi-Tech Jazz.\\\" In 2015 he founded his own label, 4EVR 4WRD (Forever Forward), to push that sound further. Alongside his music career, Jon works as a music therapist at the Children's Hospital of Michigan. He'll be playing keys live as Barbora leads you through a series of connected breathing exercises.\\n\\nBarbora Pátková a.k.a B'licious is a singer, producer, transformational guide and founder of Innervisions Alchemy; a wellness space and cultural hub in SE London. Holding a Master of Natural Sciences from Cambridge, she combines rigorous scientific thinking with intuition-led facilitation. As the voice of The Heliocentrics, she has performed at Glastonbury, Roskilde and Worldwide festivals, sharing stages with Marshall Allen, Bilal and Madlib, with a new Strut Records EP dropping this April for Record Store Day 2026. Through Innervisions Alchemy, she weaves ritual \\u0026 holistic practices, creating the conditions for people to access their own innate capacity to heal.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":454,\"name\":\"The Man With The Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-27T14:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-27T16:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c5c00ffa8c40df5641614e4f741c6daf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":475,\"name\":\"AMPLIFIED 05: The Home Service, Jackie Sees Red, Postcard\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-27T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9a9a46fc3a64b5155ca96af8b58627a4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets still available OTD \\n\\nAmplified is a night dedicated to giving up and coming local artists the limelight, it is not about spectacle - its about connection, craft and being present in the music.\\n\\nThe Home Service: The Home Service are a South East London wonk-rock band making sharp, melodic guitar music with a distinctly British sense of character. Formed in the underbelly of the Goldsmiths University music block in 2021, the band write songs that are grunge-edged, power-pop-minded and full of crooked riffs, bitter humour and big melodic instincts.\\n\\nJackie Sees Red: With seething guitar, abrasive sounds, and poetic lyrics, Jackie's seeing fucking red.\\n\\nPostcard: A spilt drink over a DJ set up sparked a chance meeting and the beginning of Postcard, a London based indie rock band consisting of Al (Vocals/Rhythm guitar), Jamie (Lead guitar), Oisin (Bass) and Joe (Drums).\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":447,\"name\":\"Dirar Kalash \\u0026 Friends: Electro-acoustic Residency – Roxanna Albayati\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-27T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d3dde5b2921a7348b4ff4dcac7ef3a60.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Three nights of experimental improvisation with Dirar Kalash \\u0026 Friends.\\n\\nGritty and effervescent, Dirar Kalash's experimental music is known to be transcendental and deeply embodied. An extraordinary Palestinian sound artist, Kalash pushes boundaries in his sonic work with a vast repertoire of collaborations, including artists such as Nicolas Jaar. For this series, he invites:\\n\\n\\nMAY 13 - BARBIE MUKODA - Flautist and improvised blending classical and experimental sound worlds through tone and silence.\\nMAY 22 - MARYSIA OSU - Harpist, producer, and composer who blends classical, ambient, and electronic music.\\nMAY 27 - ROXANNA ALBAYATI - Cellist \\u0026 artist blending experimental music with cross-cultural improvisation and multimedia performance.\\n\\nStudio 12 is an intimate art space with a custom sound system \\u0026 cocktail bar in Camberwell, London. It's dedicated to art, music, poetry and film, rooted in transnational solidarities.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/dirar-kalash-friends-electro-acoustic-residency-with-studio-12-tickets-1988393935788?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":460,\"name\":\"Heat Seeking\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-28T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5a7c99a21d5ef27e00d59a7653b34fc7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Public opening event: Thursday 28 May, 6-9pm \\nDates: 29 May-12 July \\nGallery hours: Thursday – Sunday, 1-6pm \\nAdmission: Free\\n\\nSET 91 presents Heat Seeking, the inaugural exhibition of our second six-month curated programme. Bringing together new works by Millie Earthy, Joe Garcia, and Francisco Zhan, the show explores printing techniques as processes of transformation, reproduction, and desire.\\n\\nAbout the exhibition\\n\\nHeat Seeking is a group exhibition exploring printing techniques as processes of slippery reproduction and desire. Using a variety of methods including 3D printing, paper clay, decals and UV printing, the exhibition brings together works shaped by slow, almost devotional processes requiring precision, alongside playful and often humorous exchanges between image and material.\\n\\nFundamentally, it is a show about desire, attending to its different forms: commodification and branding, transubstantiation in Chinese joss paper traditions, the politics of excess, texture, and the buffoonery of rebranding and repurposing industrial materials with personal imagery.\\n\\nThe pairings inhabit their own kind of poetry as images are forged with light, heat and exposure onto unexpected surfaces, producing fragile, mutable containers. Heat Seeking understands printing as a process shaped as much by risk as control, where material and image meet in unstable and often surprising ways.\\n\\nAbout the space\\n\\nSET 91 is SET’s first in-house curated contemporary arts gallery, located in Old Street. Dedicated to supporting early-career contemporary artists, the gallery provides a non-profit platform for experimentation, collaboration, and the presentation of new work beyond commercial pressures. \\n\\nFor press enquiries, email press@setspace.uk\\n\\nFollow us on Instagram at @set91set\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":497,\"name\":\"Doc'n Roll x Rio: PARAÌSO UK Premiere + Q\\u0026A\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-28T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-28T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8f6a706aa6b61cdde0a5a24b446621d2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Doc?n Roll presents the UK Premiere of PARADISE (Paraìso), followed by a Q\\u0026A with director Daniel Mota and producers Jo?o Ervedosa and Maria Guedes. This exhilarating documentary dives into Portugal's early 90s dance music explosion, with raves of epic proportions and a new sound which was then referred to as ?underground house music from a paradise called Portugal?. \\n Deftly knitted together by director Daniel Mota from never-before-seen VHS archives, home footage and prime-time TV clips, we're dropped us into castle raves, sweat-soaked dancefloors and the heart of decentralised DIY movement that spread far beyond Lisbon and Porto. First-hand interviews with DJs, promoters, dancers and producers map the birth and evolution of a scene built by community, curiosity and euphoria. \\n More than simply a nostalgia flick, PARADISE is a vivid portrait of cultural revolution and its afterlives. It captures a moment when dance music reshaped identity and possibility, while quietly questioning how nations remember, support or neglect their cultural pioneers. Euphoric, emotional and defiantly independent, this is none other than rave history.\\nPARADISE is shown in Portuguese and English and is part-subtitled.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://riocinema.org.uk/Rio.dll/WhatsOn?f=2239065\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":498,\"name\":\"magCulture Meets No Way Back\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-28T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-28T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"673eaf84646be660606c550af1cd4b95.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a special evening with No Way Back, highlighting what we can learn from previous youth subcultures\\n\\nNo Way Back, the publication dedicated to resurfacing long-lost music and subculture journalism, returns with its second issue in May. To mark its publication, editor and co-founder Andy Crysell joins us at the magCulture shop to talk about the making of the magazine and the thinking behind the magazine’s strapline: Learning From, Not Longing For, The Past.\\n\\nSpecifically: not cosy nostalgia, but backstories showing through-lines to what could emerge next; pushing back against ‘platform amnesia’—digital feeds that strip culture of lineage and context; recognising breakthrough moments in independent creativity that formal institutions ignore; and how, unless championed, ideas originating in marginalised or minoritised communities are often taken and credited elsewhere.\\n\\nPicking up on these themes—and bringing a cross-generational perspective —Andy will be joined by Campaign award-winner, trends forecaster and senior strategist at Seen Studios, Gursharan Panesar.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/magculture-meets-no-way-back-tickets-1989642705893\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":485,\"name\":\"UPPERCUT VOL.8 with Brie, Crap Stallion, Camoia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-28T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-28T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d0bd016e60f2ffa9338701b0c38cc22a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets still available OTD\\n\\n\\nBrie - Birthing their own nutty brand of silly billy-core, pimple popper punk, Brìe make their steady return to the internet following a three year-long streaming detox with brand new EP “Abinger Hammer”, out now on Big Richard Records.\\n\\nCrap Stallion - Hardcore heavyweights and garage-punkers \\n\\nCamoia - alternative, electronic noise pop\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":444,\"name\":\"inklingroom\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T07:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-29T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e253b17186bbbbc6a7aeca8d890562a9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"inklingroom presents an evening of live performance, contemporary dance and experimental music at Iklectik.\\n\\nFeaturing a live performance from plus44Kaligula (+FourFour Kali-gula) — the project of composer, producer and performance artist Cally Statham — blending voice, movement with a peculiar microphone-as-sculpture installation into an eerie and hypnotic world of experimental pop and avant-garde electronics.\\n\\nElisabeth Mulenga presents ‘The Back Of Her Neck’ (score by Damsel Elysium), a solo dance performance exploring exploring how inauthenticity can be as resonant, and exposing as vulnerability, working with cycles of alienation and reconciliation that can sustain and make evident the performer's agency within the vulnerable themes explored.\\n\\nAlso performing live is Ramilda — Estonian cellist and experimental artist Kirke Gross — combining cello drones, live electronics and improvisation into deeply atmospheric soundscapes.\\n\\nDJ sets till late by inklingroom DJs.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/n1712cf1c9c1?dice_id=n1712cf1c9c1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":478,\"name\":\"Circles on the Floor\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-31T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7e0a16da8c567584efde290f7182e4a9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SET is pleased to present Circles on the Floor, a group exhibition curated by Polly Plowden at SET Vauxhall.\\n\\nBringing together four artists working across interdisciplinary practices, including installation, performance, and video, the exhibition is informed by years of inquiry into the contemporary art phenomenon of placing virtually anything in a circle on the floor.\\n\\nCentral to the installation is a custom-built bar, with drinks served by The Pegram Collection.\\n\\nEvent details\\n\\nOpening: Friday 29 May, 5-9pm\\nDates: 29-31 May\\nOpening hours: 12-5pm\\nLocation: SET Vauxhall, Camelford House, 89 Albert Embankment, London, SE1 7TP\\nAdmission: Free\\n\\nContributing artists\\n\\nCecilia Sargent - Cecilia Sargent explores notions of aspiration, desire and failure within her interdisciplinary practice. Often with a performative D.I.Y materiality – her work aims to visualise the tragicomic emotions of trying but never quite getting it right.\\n\\nLucas D’Praser Corp - Lucas D’Praser Corp restages images and objects to create speculative memory. He sets relics in a material tension to interrogate the politics of backwardness, and its aesthetic potential.\\n\\nPolly Plowden - Polly Plowden explores the rehearsal of reality within everyday life, examining how chaos, repetition, and mediation shape meaning through quieter, overlooked narratives embedded in domestic spaces.\\n\\nAlex Heard - Alex Heard makes performance, video and installation which often explore frictions of bitterness, refusal, or absurdity. A concern of his has been the carbon-capture of ‘meaning’ in the field of contemporary art.\\n\\nAbout SET’s Associate Members Programme\\n\\nThis exhibition is presented as part of SET’s Associate Members Programme, which offers artists studio space alongside access to project spaces and opportunities to independently curate exhibitions, workshops, and events.\\n\\nThe programme supports a wide range of practices, from performance and installation to music, sound, print, and textiles, and is designed to provide space, visibility, and development opportunities for early-career and underrepresented artists working in London.\\n\\nPoster design: Lucas D’Praser Corp\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":143,\"name\":\"Algae Bloom - 'I Am Everyone I've Met' 10th Anniversary Show + Last London Show\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-29T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6aacf3410ce63be9fb3a5c264fc0a4f8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nAlgae Bloom\\nCelebrating 10 years of 'I am everyone I've ever met' with their last shows for the foreseeable future, we're very lucky to bring you a rare London appearance from some UK Screamo legends\\n\\n\\nPlus a stellar supporting cast of...\\n\\nCold Holding\\nSouthampton duo, reunited for the occasion\\n\\nincaseyouleave\\nTwinkling Screamo Stars, Suis La Lewisham\\n\\nI'm Sorry Emil\\nLondon Screamo future classics\\n\\nClosed Hands\\nGet screamoshional. Members of Grey Market, Affray and Sewer Trench\\n\\nGood Carl\\nIt's their 10th birthday too! UK emo rockstars back for 2 nights only. Get down early.\\n\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£13\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/algae-bloom\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":451,\"name\":\"Tides EP Launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-29T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"84c0ef696b4f70704fb1ad85832908e9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tides EP Launch - ambient \\u0026 experimental night with an all trans line up\\n\\nLaunch gig for Mer Sounds' upcoming debut ambient release : Tides. Tides is an exploration of being transformed by water, time folding in on itself in cycles, inexpressible feelings… a sonic recreation of being submerged in ocean tides.\\nSupported by an incredible line up, all responding and expanding on the EP, with ambient soundscapes, improvised electronics, ethereal singing, field recordings, amplified violin and cello, tapes and movement…\\n\\nAll tickets proceeds in support of the Leonardo 3.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2435053\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":450,\"name\":\"Kilmorie, Envie, KV!TKA\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-30T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2345762e13338ae79b57b98378b2bb92.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets still available OTD\\n\\nKilmorie: Are a 4 piece band hailing from SE London; devotees of off kilter electronic leaning guitar music. Influences include Water From Your Eyes, Model/ Actriz, (Kid A era) Radiohead, MBV, Young Fathers, Underworld.\\n\\nENVIE: ENVIE, formerly known as Dystopia, are an East London alternative rock trio crafting dark psychedelic soundscapes, soaring guitar riffs, and moody, emotionally charged vocals. Inspired by the spirit of nostalgia for alt-rock \\u0026 pop, ENVIE reclaim space for women of colour in a genre where they have long been underrepresented.\\n\\nKV!TKA: KV!TKA is a four-piece alternative band based in London. Drawing inspiration from Sonic Youth, Slint, and Cocteau Twins, KV!TKA mixes  ethereal textures with abrasive noise. Their sound merges soft, haunting vocals with distorted guitars and atmospheric melodica to create a unique contrast.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":439,\"name\":\"Heith + METATERME (Elvin Brandhi \\u0026 Emiddio Vasquez) + Ansuman Biswas + Karina Sletten (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-29T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5362e946ce7eb77d6091f8d41b935ada.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Four artists explore relations between the analogue and the digital, the organic and the synthetic, in the unique setting of Hackney Wick's Bath House.\\n\\nHeith's music exists where organic and digital elements clash, merge, and transform. His songwriting evokes both reminiscence and curiosity, creating sonic spaces that feel both familiar and alien. This is especially evident in his 2022 opus X, wheel where synths, percussion, and electronics intertwine with organic textures like guitar and voice, constantly shifting in an intricate balance. Escape Lounge, released on PAN in 2025, charts unmarked musical territory — one that draws from the experimental pop of '90s trip-hop, the introspective songwriting of 2000s indie-folk, and the lush, dreamlike haze of Mediterranean psychedelia. For Escape Lounge, Heith draws inspiration from contemporary digital spirituality and interpretations of experience that are crossing over from cultural niches into the mainstream – including internet-based conspiracy theories and psychological operations. The album presents a sonic diary recorded across Milan, Berlin, London, and Stockholm, crafting a post-informational folklore while exploring new territories in personal songwriting. In 2024 he was commissioned by CTM to present his most ambitious and acclaimed show yet, Inverted Vertigo featuring multiple musicians, theatrical staging, and a bespoke LED video ring hung as a swinging pendulum. In 2025, Heith debuted a collaborative audiovisual performance The Talk with James K and Günseli Yalcinkaya, commissioned by Sonar Festival, Terraforma, Nuit Sonores, and Reworks. Since founding his label Haunter Records in 2013, Heith has played a key role in Milan's music scene, also becoming part of the curatorial team at the legendary Macao space. Over the years, he has released a string of EPs ('Laguna' 2018, 'Mud' 2019, 'Lo Zoo di Venere' 2020) and collaborated with artists such as Puce Mary, Visio, and Kareem Lotfy. Earlier this month, Heith released his gorgeous \\\"5th world music\\\" collaboration with Indonesia musician Tarawangsawelas entitled Duori via Stroom.\\n\\nElvin Brandhi and Emiddio Vasquez come together as METATERME, a sound experience based research and practise, redefining the sacred in the tempo of the NOW. They met accidentally, through a series of uncanny coincidences in Lebanon, Kurdistan, Brazil via Finland, thus accidentally demonstrating the physicality of connectivity. In their quasi-nomadic practice of creative displacement, they deterritorialise circuits of interference, intersections of influence, and cultural awareness. They strongly believe in the importance of making space for nightmares, conditions for the space to dream, unfreezing the limbs of resilience. They held a performance as exorcism in the Cyprus Pavilion during the Venice Biennale in collaboration with Poncili Creacion. In this dark, warm space with a surround system, they tried to reach sauna sensory extremes through sound, catharsis, and transformation in the performative costume shifts of Poncili brothers. This has inspired them to elaborate on this concept of “curse reverse”, group healing through intimacy, empathy and catharsis and an environment where we are all safe to attend to the extremes of our psychological composition, extremes which are being triggered ever more as war, media, consumption, and normalisation of terror governments engulfs our screen-bred youth.\\n\\nAnsuman Biswas has an international practice encompassing music, film, live art, installation, writing and theatre. It has included directing Shakespeare, translating Tagore, designing underwater sculptures in the Red Sea, travelling with Tantric minstrels in Bengal, being employed as an ornamental hermit in the English countryside, touring with Björk, surviving blindfolded for days in an unknown place, playing a thousand-year-long piece of music, crossing the Gobi Desert with nomadic shamans, playing with Oasis, collaborating with neuroscientists in Arizona, living for a week with nothing but what spectators chose to give him, singing for 24 hours non-stop, organising grassroots activists in Soweto, meditating in a box for ten days with no food or light, creating a musical in a maximum security prison, silently bathing strangers, being a soloist with the London Philharmonic Orchestra, holding seminars in a Burmese monastery, running a nightclub in Hamburg’s red light district, being accredited by the British Association for Counselling and Psychotherapy, redesigning Maidstone High Street, playing with terminally ill children, making a radio telescope sing and dance, being locked in a Gothic tower alone for forty days and nights, flying on a real, live, magic carpet, and stopping time.\\n\\nKarina Sletten is an artist from the Norwegian West coast. Her DJ sets express the associations she makes with other artists on the bill, showcasing pathways and interests that intertwine a plethora of genres and timelines. Karina’s work spans sound art, performance, installation, and relational public practices. She explores the relationships between sound, space, text, environment and perception in innovative ways.\\n\\nPoster by Matej Siska.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":271,\"name\":\"The Whole Routine: Edward Thomasson\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-29T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"33ed96620a1b0f7ebf75eac825c20f3e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Whole Routine is a musical performance about control and longing by Edward Thomasson, created in collaboration with songwriter Robbie Ellen and composer Charlotte Harding, and performers Adrian Quinton, Andrew Kerton, Clara Andersson, Penelope Granycome, Simon Tipping, and Yasmine Holness-Dove. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.londonperformancestudios.com/the-whole-routine-2026\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":473,\"name\":\"TEJ QUARTET EP RELEASE / KIRAN LEONARD / LOTTIE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-29T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"24a790d41cc527933c13d0cfb0ef57b4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"2horse records presents\\n\\nEP release for the TEJ Quartet - featuring four electric guitars\\n\\nBYOB EVENT\\nSmall capacity venue, advance tickets advised\\n\\n\\nsupport from\\n\\nKIRAN LEONARD\\nLOTTIE\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":306,\"name\":\"POMP!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-29T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c21152088341f6d5b34c561551d68fc3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"IT'S BACK.\\n\\nAfter a break POMP! is back to toy with your taste level, curl your hairs and tickle your taste buds. Boasting a fine cast of freaks in unhinged pop superstar Femmi, drag troll Die Lemma and inflatable sensation Jane Norman. Hosted by the sticky \\u0026 sweet Dirrty Harry, this instalment of the sensational aternative cabaret will be one to remember, for better or worse.\\n\\nFRIDAY MAY 29TH // DOORS 8PM // SHOW 9PM//\\n\\nCOME ONE COME ALL!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/35436/pomp\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":417,\"name\":\"CLUB SMOOCH\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-30T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e43bf7bf43c4fe0d91a1b4a92f0ffb35.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hey there gorgeous you look like you’re up for a good time ;)\\n\\nCLUB SMOOCH is back again with 6 hours of non-stop SEXY VIBES in the heart of Dalston, curated by four of the underground community’s FINEST SELECTORS\\n\\nSLUTTY techno, HOT latin flavours, booty shakin BASS and NASTY beats to get all the ravers HOT UNDER THE COLLAR. Dress for the HEAT\\n\\nxxx---LINEUP---xxx\\n\\nEVSKA // @evskadj\\n\\nIt’s dj evska, your local slavic beat baddie! Serving heavy, sweaty blends of techno, latintek and bass, she’s danced her way through every basement in Edinburgh and shared the booth with icons like x-coast and dj fuckoff. Expect big beats, cheeky vocals, and pure groove\\n\\nFENNA // @joe_fenna\\n\\nOoh la la it’s FENNA! Maker of mischief, player of tunes and general raiser of eyebrows. While you’re reading this he’s already put his usb in and started charming your in-laws. Described by nobody as ‘the greatest and handsomest, most interestingest person/DJ of our time’, you will most likely want to go snog someone during his set but not him cause he’s in a committed relationship ;).\\n\\nVERTEX // @mixedbyvertex\\n\\nVERTEX, a person all too familiar with a cheeky lil club smooch (pardon the pun) is bringing you a mix so unpredictable yet so intimate, channeling the sauciest electronic music to get you moving and grooving throughout the night\\n\\nSpecial guest to be announced x\\n\\nMoney shouldn't stop a baddie from having a good night so if you are low on cash, drop us a DM/email and we'll sort you out with a hot n heavy discount ;)\\n\\n£10 OTD\\n\\nDon’t be shy, come party with us xoxo\\n\\n—————————————————\\n\\nCLUB SMOOCH has zero tolerance for ANY forms of harassment or discrimination. Can't play nice? Stay at home x\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2423487\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":372,\"name\":\"HARDBACK: Nocturnal Omissions\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-29T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-30T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"33c8c4d6db56fd77c8dc07f5c6873dae.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"HARDBACK debuts with Nocturnal Omissions - a heavy-handed lineup of experimental DJs and live acts.\\n\\n“Let the velvet red glow wash over you, and bask in the bass’ glory; Become one on the dance floor.”\\n\\nNo racism. No sexism. No homophobia. No transphobia.\\n\\nHardback contains smoke and strobe lights, which may trigger photosensitive epilepsy.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2422423\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":452,\"name\":\"Collective Aid’s Launch Session\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-30T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"344ac5d0316289c4ca8d37dc112e7467.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Collective Aid’s Launch Session is an open evening of food, drinks, art, and conversation to welcome our summer campaign, No More Deaths. Come meet people. Make things. Stay late. Be part of what comes next. All funds support Collective Aid’s work on the ground.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":434,\"name\":\"Common Ground - A Fundraiser \",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-31T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9a6bcd0cdb4f95385a234ff88ca47891.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This fundraiser supports Community Assets for Society Housing, a Lewisham-based organisation that helps create new housing co-ops.\\n\\nLocal DJs all night long hosted by Water Rul3s. Scuba divers, melody whisperers and ghost disc jockeys welcome.\\n\\nGet down early (7pm) to have a pie and chat with us about co-ops, CASH or anything else. No silly questions!\\n\\nThe night will also include an auction of earthly delights, so get your senses ready.\\n\\nCommunity Assets for Society and Housing (CASH) is a volunteer run Community Benefit Society founded by people living and working in co-ops, who want to create more co-operative spaces. CASH works with new and established co-ops, supporting them with their vision, operation, and governance, and access to finance.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2424901\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":281,\"name\":\"Chthonic: Descent\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d681214cd32276994c8461034dd41feb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Chthonic: Descent is a new event series presented by Iklectik that will examine and exhibit the evil and extreme that surrounds us. Picking up where Chthonic Festival last left us, the programme will invite artists with a particular focus on Metal/Doom/Punk/Noise and more, invoking an overwhelming and underworld atmosphere within the walls of the space. The broadening of the programming will be a true sign of Iklectik being a space to harbour all things boundary pushing and extreme. Happy to announce the artists for the first event on Saturday May 30th.\\n\\nFeaturing:\\n\\nGORGON VOMIT\\n\\nTruly violent and primitive war metal that doesn’t offer a second of reprieve on stage\\n\\nBASTARD MYCOSIS\\n\\nShuffling perversion of down tuned, mid tempo brutal death metal\\n\\nNOH\\n\\nSlow, extended drone forms of weight texture and distortions\\n\\nINTERNAL OBJECT\\n\\nSolo, uneasy electro acoustic noise project from Gabrielle Sheehan. Haunting saxophone and harsh noise from DIY devices\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/k6gl38-chthonic-descent-30th-may-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":455,\"name\":\"The Man With The Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-30T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1354abd075dd85a4ba9f6e839710280d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":269,\"name\":\"Demdike Stare, Coby Sey, U, Elle Andrews\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-31T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3f5ce29f6b908da0163c76c448c5d260.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A night of shapeshifting electronic music.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2414072\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":374,\"name\":\"Dream Archive\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-31T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"37fc470e96feeceaca7d91f70b505a69.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"DREAM ARCHIVE — Saturday 30th May\\n\\nFollowing our first two gatherings, we are very happy to be opening the space again and continuing the journey.\\n\\nTickets are extremely limited and priced to reflect the intimacy of the space.\\n\\nDream Archive is not a club night. It's a space dedicated to deep, focused listening. The environment is designed to help you slow down, disconnect from external noise, and reconnect with yourself. This is not just a room for music, it’s a place for restoration, reflection, and renewed perspective.\\n\\nNo talking. No phones. No distractions.\\n\\nThe room is fully analogue, powered by a beautiful handmade Core sound system, and holds a small capacity of people.\\n\\nGuest DJs:\\n\\nDJ Sundae (Idlepress) - responsible for a handful of revered compilations, including the much-loved Sky Girl comp with Julien Dechery, built from years of dedication to digging and a deeply considered approach to music. His sets reflect that same sensibility, moving fluidly through ambient, folk, dub and leftfield electronics with sublime finesse.\\n\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/idlepress\\n\\nFloor Length Shirt - an obsessive record collector who leaves no stone unturned, crafting free-flowing sets that feel both unpredictable and authentic, drawing listeners into a strange absorbing world. \\n\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/floorlengthshirt/\\n\\nResidents: \\n\\nFantasy In Orbit \\nhttps://www.instagram.com/fantasyinorbit \\n\\nMil Ca\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/mil_miu \\n\\nDoors 21:30\\nMusic 10pm — 5am.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":376,\"name\":\" in two minds with softi, simkin + shottel — fundraiser for The Sameer Project\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-31T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ec4953db9bc315be8c99095e6ca27e1a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"in two minds\\n\\nour inaugural party at Unit 58, with music from softi, simkin and shottel.\\n\\nAll funds from the event will be donated to The Sameer Project, a grassroots organisation supporting displaced families in Gaza.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":365,\"name\":\"JOKKOO X ORMSIDE presents: MBODJ / Nazar / Nexus / Covco / Seventimes\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-30T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-31T05:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99d7501c969fa1a78eda20c99ec0924a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In collaboration with Barcelona-based pan-African collective JOKKOO, ORMSIDE presents MBODJ, Nazar, Nexus, Covco and Seventimes.\\n\\nFounded in 2017, JOKKOO takes its name from the Wolof word for connection, and acts as a vital platform and binding tissue for experimental and avant-garde arts across the African continent and its global diaspora. Occupying and disrupting performance and club spaces alike, the 6 members of JOKKOO develop diverse practices as individuals and in collaboration – forming an intricate and close-knit community that both grounds and expands.\\n\\nOn May 30th, representing JOKKOO are MBODJ and Nexus (The performance duo made up of B4mba and Mooki6). Joining them are three artists close to Ormside’s heart: “Rough-Kuduro” innovator Nazar, INFINITE FXX founder and NTS resident Cõvco, and DJ and TEARS co-organiser Seventimes.\\n\\nSupport from Carhartt WIP.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2422646\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":503,\"name\":\"Devon's Road x PJ Ents. presents AM 2 PM\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-31T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-05-31T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f35c6e1b5c12b744b322d4cc7a730c4e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Devon's Road and PJ Entertainments Bizness come together to bring you a multi-genre all day all night party at the laid back \\u0026 relaxed Avalon Cafe in Bermondsey!\\n\\nDaytime party vibes + sizzling BBQ + selection of reggae, house, hardcore, acid house and bass + some v. special guest DJs.\\n\\nCome down, recharge and unwind!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2427398\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":396,\"name\":\"Fundraiser for Palestine \\u0026 Sudan, in memory of Sara\",\"start_time\":\"2026-05-31T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-01T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0f98619c0f7bb119c853923978df9d90.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us on the evening of the 31st of May as we come together to remember our beloved Sara on the first anniversary of her passing.\\n\\nIt will be a meaningful evening dedicated to honouring her memory by raising funds for the causes she cared about most.\\n\\nTogether, we’ll support Sudan and Palestine, all in Sara’s name.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":490,\"name\":\"Sip \\u0026 Collage with Connor Kawaii\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-01T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-01T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3321eec2a9f81e0396a3deda02ca4fc4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join me at the iconic Catford Rhum Arrange Bar nestled just off the beaten path of Deptford \\nWe will make a signature broken vinyl collage together using vinyl fragments and mixed materials. As seen in many of my past exhibitions such as 'Vinyl Autopsy' my most recent sold out exhibition.\\nThe price of the signature broken vinyl collage framed is £150 hence why the workshop is the same price. \\nThis hands on experience is perfect for anyone looking to explore their creative side, whether you're a seasoned artist or just starting, It will be a night to remmeber. A commissioned artwork like no other.\\nYou can expect; great vibes, great food, great drinks, great people and an unforgettable night.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/sip-collage-w-connor-kawaii-tickets-1990229060696?sg=c47b26d45424449a3b2999a62106143cf5d334c04f7860eb3b97ed65719c0b8e34ceb3a1850e78c2ee7cbb7e9afb05021251acffe402e470b17888098a239bf6f4258d91efebf41566b778beac\\u0026aff=ebdsshios\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":501,\"name\":\"hothouse bookclub - Nova Scotia House\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-02T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b9d05bef5c61c7a0eb0d84776ad5d40e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hi everyone! Our next book will be Nova Scotia House by Charlie Porter.\\n\\nNova Scotia House is a “meditation on grief, Johnny looks back at his relationship with his life partner, Jerry, after his AIDS-related death. When they met, nearly thirty years ago, Johnny was 19, Jerry was 45. They made a life on their own terms in Jerry’s flat: 1, Nova Scotia House. Johnny is still there today, but Jerry is gone, and so is the world they knew.“\\n\\nIt’s fiction and discusses themes like gay rights, the gentrification of London, urban relationships to nature and of course mentions the climate crisis as a context in which all of the story plays out.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.ticketsource.com/hothouse-book-club/hothouse-bookclub-nova-scotia-house/e-rpdaxk\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":407,\"name\":\"Same Old + Flypaper\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-02T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-02T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2cacc596ebec18f65f8c7f8c454b5ed2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands is back at The Ivy House for another stormer. On Tuesday June 2nd we're joined by Same Old and Flypaper!\\n\\nThere’s a gentle, fuzzy warmth nestled inside the timeless chord changes and whimsical lyrics that characterise the sound of Same Old. Each song is delicately lo-fi and charmingly wonky, drawing references from the likes of Ivor Cutler, Laura Marling and Randy Newman.\\n\\nPurchase a ticket before 26.05 and receive a FREE PINT of New Lands lager at the show!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":492,\"name\":\"The Log Books: Tash Walker and Adam Zmith in conversation with Amelia Abraham\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-03T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-03T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cbe24f5bd4946ee4251ba33c639eb9df.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us when we welcome Tash Walker and Adam Zmith to discuss their new book THE LOG BOOKS: VOICES OF QUEER BRITAIN AND THE HELPLINE THAT LISTENED with Amelia Abraham at Palm 2 Event Space.\\n\\nIn a crawlspace at the offices of Switchboard, a queer helpline in operation since 1974, lies dozens of log books kept by volunteers describing the phone calls they had taken: a teenager whose parents had kicked them out of home for dressing as the wrong gender; a lesbian terrified of having her baby taken away from her; a man arrested for chatting up another man in a public toilet; a young person wanting to know how to come out.\\n\\nThese logs were traces of tens of thousands of queer lives, a bridge to a past hidden from people like Tash Walker and Adam Zmith in their youth, captured by people who lent an ear to those in need. Walker and Zmith came of age in the time of Section 28, a law which banned councils and schools ‘promoting the teaching of the acceptability of homosexuality as a pretended family relationship’. In recovering these logs, they encountered people grappling with feelings, questions and problems both familiar and different, and set out to learn from – and sometimes speak to – those on both sides of the calls.\\n\\nCharged with joy, gossip, sensuality, humour and sometimes fear, and with a potent relevancy to the world today, these stories are brought together in THE LOG BOOKS. Walker and Zmith capture queer lives in stunning detail, embarking on a journey of both collective history and self-discovery and propelling it into the very foreground of our national history.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/the-log-books-tash-walker-and-adam-zmith-in-conversation-with-amelia-abraham/tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":531,\"name\":\"Palestinian sound archive \",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-03T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-03T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c2560163e80b5207e3ddcf7f477ae201.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Palestinian Sound Archive returns to Cafe OTO for a programme looking at Palestinian Bedouin life, culture and celebration through film, live performance, archival sound and storytelling.\\n\\nAcross Bedouin communities, music, poetry and oral history have long been central ways of carrying identity, memory and place. Sound is not separate from daily life: the grinding of coffee, animals moving out to pasture, voices travelling between tents, songs recited on camelback, wedding music stretching across days. Much of this archive has been sonic rather than material - held in the body, passed from one generation to another, kept alive through performance, repetition, movement and gathering.\\n\\nThe evening includes a live performance by Palestinian Bedouin artist, Lobna Sana, from the Naqab region. Sana’s multidisciplinary practice works across architecture, film, sculpture, mapping, curation and activism, addressing the social and spatial conditions of Bedouin life under occupation and the ongoing struggle over land, memory and recognition. Her work asks how architecture, image, sound and collective practice can document what is being erased, while also imagining forms of repair, return and continuity.\\n\\nKeyboardist, improviser and organiser Dan Nicholls embraces sound as a tool for liberation, exploring the carrying and channelling of ideas, meanings, energies and somatic responses. As co-organiser of the event Free Movements and the improv series Bodypolitik, Dan’s close connection to Palestinian artists and friends has vitally informed an approach to sound/ space-making which is rooted in community and art as a necessary political agitator.\\n\\nThere will also be a live analogue DJ set from Palestinian Bedouin artist Mo’min Swaitat and Dan Nicholls, drawing from the Palestinian Sound Archive’s collection of cassettes, field recordings and popular music histories from Palestine and beyond.\\n\\nWe’ll be screening Susya, a beautiful black-and-white documentary by Max Sänger, followed by a Q\\u0026A. The film looks at Palestinian Bedouin life in the Occupied West Bank village of Susya, where territorial disputes with Israeli soldiers and settlers shape daily life. Every walk with the sheep becomes a negotiation over remaining pasture. Resistance appears through perseverance, storytelling, memory and the act of continuing to live on the land.\\n\\nThis event explores archival practice as a decolonial methodology and an act of resistance: sharing sounds, images and stories that document Palestinian heritage, culture, celebration, dance and survival, while keeping those histories active in the present.\\n\\nArtwork by Mustafa al-Hallaj.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/palestinian-sound-archive-lobna-sana-live-susya-sc/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":394,\"name\":\"Lightbulb Moments\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-04T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-04T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bd26ff6962ae3c1d7abd6abe9f45b0c8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us @dalstongarden for a free, open event with music, performance, house band, and spoken word. A space shaped by lived experience, creativity, and recovery.\\n\\nA coproduced afternoon of creativity and performance with testimonies from our community members who have experienced homelessness and addiction.\\n\\nThis is a free event and everyone is welcome!!\\n\\n📍 Dalston Curve Garden\\n🗓️ Thursday 4th June2-4pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":144,\"name\":\"Pigeon Pit \\u0026 Cheap Dirty Horse\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-04T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-04T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ffc68c0956c535b7e7470337c2acf1ca.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life, Be Sharp and Firejam present\\nPigeon Pit\\nEmotional folk-punk anthems from Olympia, WA.\\n\\nCheap Dirty Horse\\nRowdy queer trash-punks from Nottingham\\n\\n+ Support from\\nSweet Fish\\nSparkling emo friends from London\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/sweetfishband/\\n\\nBillie Skreamz\\nAnarchist folk screams from Manchester\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/billie_skreamz_music/\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/pigeon-pit-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":422,\"name\":\"I hv done brain check they say not much with Carmen Hutchins\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-04T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-04T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f1d3434c1acf9694d03c19c59eb1671a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for I hv done brain check they say not much, a participatory performance and discussion with artist Carmen Hutchins.\\n\\nThis event offers a glimpse into the constant, rolling landscape of living with seizures. Structured as a performative reading group, it delves into the cryptic and charged typings found in the comment sections of random videos and cursed forum threads online. Hutchins edits and interweaves this found text with her own reflections and asides, creating a detailed mise-en-scène that portrays an experience of having seizures.\\n\\nParticipants are encouraged to sit in the unease of these perennial states of unrest, and to consider how such conditions resonate within their own lives and the lives of others. \\n\\nMoving beyond the typical image of the convulsing figure, the work gestures towards a vast, neglected underbelly of community who are seeking solution and connection. Pushed to the fringes by the systemic failures of the capitalist humdrum and fragmented healthcare systems, they urgently demand immediate, compassionate attention. \\n\\nDate \\u0026 Time: Thursday 4th June, 6.30–8.30PM\\n\\nVenue: Auto Italia, 44 Bonner Road, London, E2 9JS\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScKJeEJ60BRScf5K-NXSTEVT0-2hleeZ-oxWzwNAwt1MMRywg/viewform\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":552,\"name\":\"Bodypolitik 3\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-04T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-04T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ba4ed5f16a41ce7c50f1a00fad032f70.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Bodypolitik 3 with Bint Mbarah, Tristan Arp, Lou Zon, A Psychic Yes, Dan Nicholls and more \\n\\n7-11pm at Vespers, Rye Lane\\n\\nPWYW all proceeds to charity\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":512,\"name\":\"Nails on Clouds (1)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-04T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-04T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"062f0fd33d99a9c638e06075218d7135.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Nails on Clouds is a night of live music spanning multiple genres, showcasing original talent - indie/electronica atmospheric rock hosted in a unique venue space in south London.\\n\\nOur first event :\\n\\nWINTER AT SEA ((post rock / folk))\\nFour piece acoustic band at the crossroads of folk, post rock, and ambient. Featuring members of Louse, Poseidon, Blackhorse Road, Flies are Spies from Hell.\\n\\nOCCULT STEREO ((experimental rock / psychedelic rock)) \\nA boundary-pushing solo project of Greek-American multi-instrumentalist Alex Eliopoulos, blending experimental, psychedelic, and noise rock into immersive, improvisation-driven soundscapes.\\n\\nDISTORTION 639 ((Techno / Electronica)) \\nLondon-based live techno act blending hypnotic nu-gabber and post techno elements with ethereal, siren-like vocals and thunderous live drum beats.\\n\\nASTRA PENTAXIA \\u0026 THE SONIC TELEPATHS ((electro / synthpop / disco))\\nA rainbowgoth performance trio combining campy ‘80s synthpop with a wide array of euphoric and experimental textures.\\n\\nEVA SCOTT ((electronic / folk))\\nA singer-songwriter weaving drama from Celtic, rave, alt rock/pop influences to keep energy and emotion flowing on the dancefloor\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2419527\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":395,\"name\":\"Positive Pressure tape release party with Tubby\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-04T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-05T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"41a3e36ecd5daad96848322942f223ca.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To celebrate the release of our upcoming debut tape 'Around the Dial: Grime on Pirate Radio 2003-2008', we've invited the legendary DJ Tubby down to Peckham's Greyhound basement for a rare performance. Long time Rinse FM resident and FWD regular, we couldn't think of a better DJ to help us present our new cassette to the world. \\n\\nWith support on the night from: \\nDJ Argue \\u0026 Bus \\nEthics \\nX-Pert Pir \\nYou'll be in good hands for a night showcasing the golden years of grime and dubstep.\\n\\nCopies of the tape will be available to purchase at the venue during the party\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":438,\"name\":\"Bogdan Du Sol presents Charlie Schine, Spraytan, betterpetra\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-04T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-04T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8c6dedab3a3e6ef941fccf41ce252f46.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us on June 4th for a night of eclectic, exploratory, and dreamy sounds at Avalon Cafe. A lineup drifting between intimate pop experiments, dancefloor energy, and hazy leftfield textures.\\n\\nBogdan Du Sol presents:\\n\\nCharlie Schine – New York-based artist blending dancelofi and off-kilter club sensibilities, and one half of the live electronic act Jumplink.\\n\\nSpraytan – London duo making pop and dance music for CEOs, TikTokkers, British holidaymakers, and professors alike.\\n\\nbetterpetra – navigating ambient dreamscapes, R\\u0026B-inflected tones, and dissociative sonic spaces, crafting a world that feels both intimate and otherworldly.\\n\\nCome join us!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2439299\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":399,\"name\":\"Dumb Club 001: Speckman, Coldsteel, 1700 grade, Madjestic Kasual, DJ Pitch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ecfdb160570ec723cc63fca95b5a7145.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"STFU\\nAll sorts, all night\\n\\nSpeckman\\nColdsteel\\n1700grade\\nMadjestic Kasual\\nDJ Pitch\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2433673\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":499,\"name\":\"misdigest @ oitij-jo arts space 001\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6ba85407620eb0ca16d55438a317c75f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"BFTT\\u0003@bfttyco //\\nXT1ANA @xt1ana //\\nDJ AZ @amenapzaman //\\nBUBZ @bubzdjbubz //\\n\\nThe first in a series of immersive Audio Visual events showcasing the art of London based artist Misbah Anjum-James (misbahbydesign). Each event will be a unique combination of cutting edge music whilst the audience is taken on a dive into the mind of the artist. No one event will ever feel the same to the next. \\n\\n\\nOITIJ-JO has been running since 2013, focusing on celebrating \\u0026 sharing Bangla-rooted creative arts with the public in the UK. By supporting our events you are helping to raise vital funds to help continue the work they do.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":282,\"name\":\"Stephen O'Malley + Dawn Terry\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-05T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7ed0bb6c8afbbff74ccaa4c543417249.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Baba Yaga's Hut Presents:\\n\\nStephen O'Malley + Dawn Terry at IKLECTIK, June 5th\\n\\nStephen O’Malley is a guitarist, producer, composer, and visual artist who has conceptualized and participated in numerous drone and experimental music groups for over two decades – SUNN O))), KTL, and Khanate being among his best-known creations. Wildly prolific, O’Malley’s oeuvre is defined by its remarkable breadth, complexity and multidisciplinary interests. It includes collaborations with a wide range of experimental artists, including Scott Walker, Kali Malone, Alvin Lucier, choreographer Gisèle Vienne, the authors Dennis Cooper and Alan Moore, Peter Rehberg, Fujiko Nakaya, Jim Jarmusch, Johan Johansson, experimental music research centers IRCAM, INA-GRM (Paris), EMS (Stockholm) and many others. O’Malley is also a vigorous live performer and has toured around the world since 2000. His live performances feature a reverberating fog of electric guitar minimalism – sorcery that challenges boundaries of space and time.\\n\\n--\\n\\nDawn Terry produces work that is heavy, dreamlike, open and hypnotic both solo and in her band Bong II. In her recent music Dawn has turned towards acoustic resonances provided by accordion, hurdy-gurdy, and voice. Both cleaner and denser than ever before, Dawn is now producing large scale minimalist landscapes characterised by an austere openness, barely punctured by hypnotic drumming or slowly intoned vocals and stories of survival and vengeance.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/nv9rx5-stephen-omalley-dawn-terry-5th-jun-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":391,\"name\":\"Jack Parlett in Conversation with Amelia Abraham\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-05T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d8cd8f6df6ed8f2d95d433c9574130e5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Flamboyance is Jack Parlett’s follow up to his acclaimed Fire Island (A Housmans bestseller of 2022). This new book has all the qualities one has come to expect of Jack’s work; big hearted and erudite in equal measure.\\n\\nFlamboyance ignites every aspect of our lives, from art and entertainment to ritual and protest. The word conjures exuberance and unashamed passion; in thought, expression and dress. Yet historically the term ‘flamboyant’ has been reserved for the over-the-top and the outré, invoked at times as a pejorative innuendo or worse.\\n\\nIn his fascinating new book, Jack Parlett argues for its value as an empowering and creative force, illuminating the ways in which flamboyance is a fundamental aspect of human conduct that both marks and transcends difference.\\n\\nTaking in an eclectic array of examples, from Gothic architecture to the orange flowers of Dungeness, and populated by figures such as Oscar Wilde, James Baldwin, Elton John, Amy Winehouse, Lil Nas X and Chappell Roan, this is a book about flamboyant art and the art of flamboyance. And having both aspired to it and rejected it, Jack recounts his personal relationship to flamboyance while also finding new meanings of the word, exploring its surprises and contradictions, and reconnecting with its radical power.\\n\\nJack will be joined in conversation with Amelia Abraham. They with be in conversation for around 45 minutes to an hour, followed by a q\\u0026a and signing session.\\n\\nAs always, tickets are priced on a sliding scale. If you are unable to pay for a ticket please do not hesitate to contact us at shop@housmans.com, and a free ticket will be made available.\\n\\nIf you choose ‘book + entry’ your copies of the book will be available to collect on the evening. If you would like to collect it earlier, or arrange for delivery, please contact us (postage is £2.95). Telephone 020 7837 4473 or email shop@housmans.com.\\n\\nDoors Open at 6:45pm, Event Starts 7:00.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/book-launch-flamboyance-with-jack-parlett/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":442,\"name\":\"The CUSP LP Release Party w/ Paradise Nothing, Ketan Jandoo, DJ Proteus @ The Horse Hospital\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-05T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fd2d296c32304d047d5b78f8e86e8bc7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\\"GUM, MONEY \\u0026 OTHER CRIMES: SELECTED TRACKS 2020-2023\\\" is the new LP and first vinyl release by The CUSP out on June 5th on Depression Glass Records (Los Angeles).  A compilation of singles, EP tracks and remixes, the LP gathers material from the initial years of the project which was only previously issued on digital and cassette formats.  \\n\\nJoin The CUSP and fellow support acts Paradise Nothing, Ketan Jandoo and DJ Proteus for a night of eclectic sounds. \\n\\nThe CUSP is the project of songwriter/producer Lucas Fitzsimons: Argentinean-born, LA-raised, now eeking out a living in London.  The sound has been described as left-field indie, post-punk, acid and dub, but who's counting.  \\n\\nParadise Nothing is an artist based in Brighton, UK who will offer a set of Algerian-inspired experimental noise.  \\n\\nKetan Jandoo, member of 3D Jesus and former housewife of the Himalayas will be performing bungaroosh death ballads, accompanied by Jacob Stirrat on violin.  \\n\\nForged in Sheffield, DJ Proteus plays experimental electronics and underground industrial sounds from past to present and will be playing tunes throughout the night.  \\n\\nTICKET BUNDLE INCLUDES AN LP + ENTRY FEE.\\nTIX WILL BE £12 ON THE DOOR.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":410,\"name\":\"A Shopping Trip to Remember \",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-05T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"51112c83c8d90b98b2de0baf944b7f02.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A Shopping Trip to Remember is an experimental concert series devised by Hannah McLoughlin, Samuel Leith Taylor and Shannon-Latoyah Simon. Each edition invites together a wild and ever evolving lineup of artists to share works in progress, live experiments, and performances that thrive in uncertainty. A Shopping Trip to Remember is rooted in collaboration and curiosity – creating space for experimentalists across sound and interdisciplinary practices.\\n\\nIf you like the unexpected…join us on 5 June 2026 at 7:30pm at Hundred Years Gallery.\\n£10 (cash/card on the door — no one turned away for lack of funds!), or £8 advance!\\n\\nPerformances by:\\nThe New Adults (Shannon-Latoyah Simon + Matt Rogers) \\nHannah McLoughlin + Friends (trio)\\nWorm Salad (Dr Cameron Auchterlonie Dodds + Samuel Leith Taylor)\\nMaya-Leigh Rosenwasser\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":409,\"name\":\"CLUB GEOFF: The Engine Room (UK/DE) + The Shining Tongues (UK)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f5f952b56d641186becf797e6b949af4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"CLUB GEOFF presents a night of hypnotic noise, cosmic drone, and post-whatever psychedelics. THE ENGINE ROOM are are a UK/Germany based improv trio featuring alumni from GOD and Terminal Cheesecake, creating intuitive psychedelia and freeform kosmiche excursions. THE SHINING TONGUES perform shamanic, cascading art-songs for the benefit of all living beings. Expect a whirlpool of folk, drone, pop music, psychedelia, gothic and art rock. The spaces between will be filled by our resident ghost selector, DJ Naproxxen.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://theshiningtongues.com/event/6564250/762035429/club-geoff-the-shining-tongues-uk-the-engine-room-uk-de?fbclid=IwY2xjawRquaxleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETBnYWV4Y2hSMHp6RGtoeGFVc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHim4gS5oVGnr66x8D7oLKbz3u-R2Nv1YYcD_YGcAmMo-S3WGUPMU0NUSGH82_aem_j1ON_eePCKdDHcZXbdXH7Q\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":488,\"name\":\"E.M.T + Anja Ngozi + Francesca Fulmini + Emotionite\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f1a231d9211a8bbac1c6fb63f898182a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"E.M.T, Anja Ngozi, Francesca Fulmini and Emotionite gather together for a night of meditation, exploration and Freedom of expression.\\n\\n\\nBiographies\\n\\nE.M.T:\\n\\nLondon’s polymaths Natty Wylah \\u0026 Ku-Ro will be debuting a new sonic presentation. Harnessing play – meditations on the everyday magic of the concrete city. Gentle and crazed, like a babies eyes observing through the kaleidoscope.\\n\\n\\nAnja Ngozi:\\n\\nQuietly redrawing the lines between genre and style - producer, DJ, composer and visual artist Anja Ngozi explores transience and space within harmony and disharmony, feeling out the sonic connections to emotions.\\n\\n\\nFrancesca Fulmini:\\n\\nLike getting home after the rain. Francesca Fulmini's cadence simultaneously sheds your wet clothes with the day’s worries too. Through grungy depths to R'n'B toned embraces, her warmth offers intimacy and retreat from the outside world. \\n\\nThe singer, songwriter, producer and multi-instrumentalist will be performing her new unreleased music through a solo set with vocals, a baritone guitar and keys.\\n\\n\\nEmotionite:\\n\\nEmotions are living inside us all. Sometimes we understand them, sometimes we do not. In the form of frequencies and vibrations I'm translating my inner world in all its glory and mess to evoke a sense of catharsis within myself and the audience. Bouncing through whatever genres, melodies and tempos feel right. Music is a place to feel free and understood. #movethemhips #tapyourfeet #bobyourhead\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":504,\"name\":\"\\\"I'M CLOSE\\\"\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"427faf3acc092aaf2b5ad564db3716f6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"You asked, we answered... the first iteration of the Piehouse's new in-house lesbian club night has landed with an unbelievable lineup of local legends and international acts alike. From gqom to breaks to bassline, come sweat with us\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":533,\"name\":\"thumbprint ❂ OK EG (Live), Marie K, Caim\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2157ee75209d3ec181c734d144199391.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"our last interaction, before summer unfolds.\\n\\nOK EG (Live)\\nMarie K\\nCaim\\n\\n90 minutes of live psychedelia from the inimitable Australian pair is framed by two of the Netherlands’ most refined selectors.\\n\\nan evening to hold on to, as we head towards longer days.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2428335\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":304,\"name\":\"Forever \",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-05T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ad90451cd1978efecc44f33f09cc3ba9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Forever 03 @ Venue MOT\\n\\nUnannounced line up, live music and DJs, 21+, no phones\\n\\nForever is Big Dyke Energy's sister party, for the dykes, dolls, t boys, faggots, friends \\u0026 family.\\n\\nWe've got a very exciting night planned before we go on a summer break 😈\\nOne of our BDE fam and international superstar talent will be joining us for a b2b extravaganza! \\nDebut live sets, divine decor and a proper silly sexy night of dancing and chatting shit in the smoking area. \\n\\n\\nAccessibility info on our Instagram highlights (@_4ever_4ever_4ever_)\\n\\nWe have a limited number of low income tickets available, please get in touch if you need \\u003c3\\n\\nNo refunds available - we will activate the resale service once the event has completely sold.\\n\\nI'm gonna keep dancing forever, me x\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":502,\"name\":\"Cubitt Community Press Issue #3 Launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-06T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9c3a0c29188cb2ab46d0e598351b3905.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us at Culpeper Community Garden for the summer launch of the third edition of the Cubitt Community Press Newsletter! \\n\\nBetween February and May 2026 Cubitt Community Press worked with locals to create a map of Islington bringing together historic and current day community resources, working from an open call that gathered over 50 sites across the borough. \\n\\nOur map brings together youth centres, cultural spaces, community resources, historic sites of radical action, and locations connected to personal stories, alongside a hand-drawn map of Islington. Memories of the borough’s radical histories sit alongside present-day resources and stories shared by the people who live here now.\\n\\nHand made and printed by our community in Islington using our the cubitt community risograph printer. \\n\\nABOUT THE EVENT\\n\\nJoin us to learn more about Cubitt’s Community Distribution and resource centre, pick up a copy of our newspaper and get involved in our project. \\n\\nThis is a relaxed event where we’ll hear from some of the contributors as well as make merch for our emerging community press, think limited edition stickers, badges and more! \\n\\nWe’ll also be setting up a temporary library in the garden with publications on community infrastructure, DIY publishing, and radical local print histories, featuring Emmie, a mobile community library and workshop structure.\\n\\nLight snacks + drinks provided.\\n\\nABOUT EMMIE\\n\\n“Emmie, The Cubitt Press Kiosk” is a mobile structure collaboratively built by architecture students Emma and Lumie in an attempt to activate public space in London and learn through encounters. Constructed from reclaimed and scrap materials, Emmie moves between sites across the city, carrying books, tools, workshops, and conversations with her.\\n\\nShe acts as an ever-evolving platform for self-organised learning, participation, and experimentation outside formal institutions, embodying forms of civic urban agency in a city where third spaces are increasingly scarce. Emmie’s unfinished and adaptable character is central to the project: people are invited to modify, expand, inhabit, and reinterpret the “…” of “Emmie, The …” over time (like Emmie, The Mobile Library for example), making the structure itself a record of shared use, imagination, and urban authorship.\\n\\nMore information HERE. \\n\\nABOUT CUBITT COMMUNITY DISTRIBUTION CENTRE  \\n\\nCubitt is building on Islington’s history of radical publishing with our community press: a place to gather, share stories, record our neighbourhood and support local justice projects. \\n\\nThe community distribution centre is a space to amplify stories from our borough across London (and beyond). We are working with print and radio to support local organising, creative resistance, and collective storytelling as tools for radical imagination.\\n\\nFREE FOR ALL TO ATTEND, book a ticket so we know who’s coming!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cubittartists.org.uk/Event/cubitt-community-press-issue-3-launch\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":535,\"name\":\"Deptford Dub Club: Return to the Source\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-06T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-07T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ad4e5eabd3d24428eddb7f035eda4f33.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Deptford Dub Club are thrilled to be coming back to the source; this will be our first session in Deptford for 9 years. So chuffed are we, that we’re pulling out all of the stops for this session at the Piehouse Co-op. Hold tight for at least 7 hours of music of Jamaican origin, presented in Soundsystem style, for FREE. All of our selectors were participants in the Club when it was resident in the hood.\\n\\nRas Danny Dread\\n(AKA Ras Danny Mosiah) will be putting the needle to the groove on the wheels of steel, to close the show. Widely known through his work with the monumental Jah Shaka Soundsystem, over many decades. One of our closest amigos, his sets are always wicked.\\n\\nSoft Wax\\nRoots Reggae selector since the mid 70s; he remembers the music being life changing. Since then he has plied his craft sporadically across London town, around the country and across the Herring Pond. He’s familiar to regulars at Deptford Dub Club, where he has been the resident selector for a decade and a half. For this session he’ll be focusing on militant Roots; his sets are always stirring.\\n\\nNatty Nick\\nThe club delighted to welcome the vibrant Nick back to select. He’s been a regular of the Club since its inception; more broadly, he’s a well-established figure on the South Eastern Reggae scene.\\n\\nDuppy Sista Sound\\nTo start the afternoon we will be welcoming the young lionesses Duppy Sista Sound to the wheels of steel. Expect a carefully chosen selection from Sista Jaz, she tears the place down with her selections and always plays up a storm.\\n\\nResident soundsystem L.A.D.S will be pulling out all the stops for the occasion, bringing out their system for the first time since the fateful halloween flood.\\n\\nFREE No Ticket Required\\n5 pm til late.\\nLicenced Bar and fine pies\\n@ the Piehouse Co-op\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":456,\"name\":\"The Man With The Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-06T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d8fee1ff8a5841e085d6bdfc2ff9fc2d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":440,\"name\":\"Elvin Brandhi + Sara Persico, Assyouti, Colombian Drone Mafia, dj burrower\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5b46423b204fa800b317c035c51dc9cf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Elvin Brandhi and Sara Persico combine their distinct yet complementary practices in a duo that engages with layered, intricate vocal textures. Voice, rhythm, and abstraction interact continuously, oscillating between intimate whisper and industrial exhale. Elvin Brandhi, a global nomad originally from Wales, blends distorted beats with her improvised stream-of-consciousness lyrics, creating a volatile soundscape that is both chaotic and captivating. Her extensive collaboration history and participation in international festivals highlight her dynamic artistry and commitment to innovative music. Sara Persico, a Berlin-based artist from Naples, merges her powerful vocals with analog electronics, field recordings, and samples. Her music, featured at renowned festivals and venues, navigates abstract electronic sounds, bass-heavy club music, noise, and vocal experiments, reflecting her versatile and fearless approach. The duo constructs a precarious, semi-liquid soundscape in which splintered pulses, sparred voices, and interwoven peaks itch along the edges of perception to explore the intimate margins of the self. Their performances unfold as evolving, mutating sonic structures, constantly evolving and resonating with audiences worldwide.\\n\\nBorn and raised in Egypt’s crowded and disordered capital Cairo, Assyouti is among his generation’s most distinct and unapologetic voices. Juggling hypermodern bass mutations, warped dancefloor snaps and percussive club experiments, he draws energy from the chaotic stimulus he grew up engulfed by. As a DJ, he balances his love of the hardcore continuum with sounds from the world’s furthest recesses, moving fluidly between supercharged, frenetic feverisms and moments of introspective emotional hypnosis, usually weaving (in and out of) both creating high-pressure dancefloor narratives fueled by a sense of theatrical disorientation. Since relocating to Berlin, Assyouti has become a regular on the European club circuit, appearing at venues such as Tresor, The White Hotel, Garage Noord, La Station, OHM and Ankali, as well as renowned festivals including Unsound, Berlin Atonal, CTM and Uganda’s Nyege Nyege. In 2024 he founded No_Stone alongside Barcelona-based DJ and selector Jehia, an event series and cultural platform reflecting his commitment to expansive, cross-pollinated adventurous music. His debut EP, Shakhrama, was released in 2022 on High Digital, showcasing his wide-eyed, borderless musical interests. Followed by a stronger second EP on Shepard Tone, exploring his own take on jungle and breakbeat mayhem, alongside releases on labels such as DAWN, Hundebiss, Paradoxe Club, PAYNOMINDTOUS and a slew of other imprints. Noisy and at times aggressive, his productions melt visceral but challenging rhythms with distorted vocal and drum samples, processed beyond recognition into buzzsaw post-punk sonics rich with detailed sound design yet still hitting with the blunt force of a sledgehammer. \\n\\nColombian Drone Mafia is a cabalistic odyssey through shrouded realms of sound. CTM: \\\"The alias of a shadowy composer whose craft bends the primal forces of synthesis and the raw immediacy of field recordings, CDM forges spaces where the experimental and the archaic coalesce. In live ritual, immersive drones slither like specters through tangled jungles, while furtive ambiences prowl, unseen but felt, threading through the undergrowth with predatory patience. The air hangs thick with sonic tension, a relentless intertwining of memory and dream, where the echoes of an ancient continent’s sprawling landscapes are reborn in sound. This is no mere music but an invocation—a descent into melodic primordialism that feels both intimate and immeasurable. Rhythms rise and fall like the breath of the forest, while the unseen vibrates with a spectral presence, leaving the listener ensnared in a web of half-forgotten reveries. This is a spell cast in sound, a communion with the unyielding spirit of the land.\\\" Philip Sherburne: “Colombian Drone Mafia is a music of tensions that refused to resolve, of frictions that throw off sparks that blossom like the flowers of their latest album’s title. It’s in that tension, that resistance, that dreams take root”.\\n\\ndigging (for) the underground music scene in Cyprus for the better part of the last decade, dj burrower has been facilitating inner and outer motions on dancefloors, basements, seasides and forests, with some cult following, supragenre sets. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":414,\"name\":\"Kurtág100\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c72592bbf98b1b5d881d9e63884daf94.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Celebrating György Kurtág's centennial\\n\\nClare Spollen, Maya-Leigh Rosenwasser and Fernando Yada Rodrigues share pieces from Kurtág's Játékok (Games) for solo piano and piano 4-hands, alongside works by Laurence Crane, Eva-Maria Houben, Jürg Frey, Tōru Takemitsu, Luciano Berio, Morton Feldman and J. S. Bach.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/kurtag-100-tickets-1989035773542?aff=oddtdtcreator\\u0026_gl=1*1ys6lik*_up*MQ..*_ga*MTc1MzcwOTc3Mi4xNzc4Mjc2MTk3*_ga_TQVES5V6SH*czE3NzgyNzYxOTYkbzEkZzAkdDE3NzgyNzYxOTYkajYwJGwwJGgw\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":401,\"name\":\"Offside (2006)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-06T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-06T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2efd32448895a27d6279c57a1678e698.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a viewing of Offside (Dir: Jafar Panahi, Iran) as part of a month long series of screenings which celebrate marginalised voices through the prism of football to coincide with the 2026 Men's FIFA World Cup.\\n\\nOffside (Persian: آفساید) is a 2006 Iranian film directed by Jafar Panahi. The film is about a group of girls who try to watch a World Cup qualifying match but are forbidden by law because of their gender. Female fans are not allowed to enter football stadiums in Iran on the grounds that there will be a high risk of violence or verbal abuse against them. The film was inspired by the director's daughter, who decided to attend a game anyway. The film was shot in Iran but its screening is banned there.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":366,\"name\":\"MATED 3 YEAR ANNIVERSARY: Shauwdii, Katie Shannon, Lolina, Ghost Dubs, Rebbushka, Xterea\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-06T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-07T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"318f7daad99faacd395a7952b97788c1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"3 YEARS MATED\\n\\nJOIN US 6TH JUNE AT ORMSIDE PROJECTS\\n\\n£10-18 TICKETS AVAILABLE VIA DICE\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/mxd5rv-shauwdii-katie-shannon-lolina-rebbushka-xterea-6th-jun-ormside-projects-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":384,\"name\":\"dance:music with charlie dear and xin\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-07T15:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-07T16:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4ff624cfbbac47a749c154617fc98d5f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"dance:music is a regular facilitated movement session, and does what it says on the tin... soundtracked to (dance) music of all flavours and transmitted through the ormside soundsystem, these sessions use the dancefloor as a space for listening and somatic exploration. \\n\\nsession 006 is led by dancer, yoga + aerial teacher, and somatics facilitator charlie dear, whose weekly somatic movement classes at waking dreams explore internal awareness, breath, and subtle body shifts. she'll guide dancers in cultivating embodied presence through moving to dance music.\\n\\n* please note ormside sadly does not have step-free access\\n\\n* bring water, and wear comfy clothes and shoes for moving in\\n\\n* we'll start at 15:30 so please try to arrive a few minutes early\\n\\n* if you'd like to come and can't afford it shoot xxxiiinnn[at]protonmail[dot]com an email and we'll try to sort a spot, capacity pending x\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":457,\"name\":\"The Man With The Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-07T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-07T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fc67d176c5395ab842d1c0c7db7b2db4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":518,\"name\":\"Conjuring ft. Damsel Elysium, Abi Asisa, afromerm\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-07T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"123467423d0b5f92e1650ec6528e437e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Conjuring is a monthly live improvisation series curated by Studio Njoku, and presented by Club Cheek.\\n\\nIt brings together leading experimental musicians for collaborative, improvised performances. The project foregrounds musical dialogue, community building and spiritual expression.\\n\\nEach show features a unique lineup of musicians performing a one-time improvisation around a motif developed by Tony Njoku.\\n\\nDamsel Elysium is a multi-instrumentalist and composer. Damsel's deeply intuitive practice crosses the boundary between experimental sound art, avant-pop, contemporary classical, and electronics, blurring the lines of genre, discipline and expectation.\\n\\nAbi Asisa is a producer and electroacoustic cellist whose work blends classical, jazz, and experimental influences. By layering and manipulating her cello, she creates textured, emotionally rich soundscapes that sit between composition and improvisation.\\n\\nafromerm is an Oram award-winning composer and sound artist. Her work draws from contemporary, jazz, and experimental disciplines, blending electronic elements with live instrumentation, field recordings, and vocalisations, to create electroacoustic soundscapes that immerse us in the elemental mythology of her project.\\n\\nLara Aisha is a classically trained, experimental and electroacoustic flautist, whose new duo combines flute with modular synthesizer. She's influenced by classical contemporary, jazz, African and Asian cultural flute music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/2w8ew7-conjuring-ft-damsel-elysium-abi-asisa-afromerm-3rd-jun-club-cheek-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":145,\"name\":\"Bastard Hymns Over London - Excide \\u0026 Hollow Suns\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-08T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-08T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"73cdb23805b7aa01125c1198a75bc650.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nBASTARD HYMNS ACROSS THE UK\\nExcide\\nCarolina fury on Sharptone Records\\n\\nPlus special guests\\nHollow Suns\\nIce Grills nu-grunge\\n\\nWears Me Out\\nSouth East Emotional Hardcore\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£15\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/excide\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":505,\"name\":\"Un/stable: Benedict Drew / Angharad Davies / Alex McKenzie\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-08T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-08T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c1d263203645bef7117ca9d24e29db3d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Un/stable series showcases improvised music, with two sets from a trio formed of Benedict Drew,  Angharad Davies, and Alex McKenzie.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://wegottickets.com/event/695559/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":546,\"name\":\"Pindrop presents: Folk in the Round\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-08T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"79b68138b3601d5a5fa3773c96423984.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pindrop Presents: Folk in the Round!\\n\\n::::::\\n\\nEmily Izen Row: Ethereal Folk (full band)!\\n\\nRopeburn: Post Folk Rockers\\n\\nDefender: Art Pop\\n\\nFionnuala Mary Bradbury: Cream of the Crop Singer Songwriter\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2450036\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":425,\"name\":\"Burn Brighter, It's Cold Out..., Inner Dog, The Chomp \\u0026 Living Spite | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-09T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-09T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1f11823b903f52ae50cfe3b9ce480fc6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents - \\n5 new heavy sounds from the underground\\n\\nBurn Brighter\\nAnthemic big riff shoutalong hardcore\\n\\nIt's Cold Out... I Should Kill Myself\\nWhitebelt aggro mathcore\\n\\nInner Dog\\nPost-hardcore bangers\\n\\nThe Chomp\\nNew stompy hardcore from members of Safest Spaces\\n\\nLiving Spite\\nHeavy moshcore\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£9\\nDoors 6pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/burn-brighter\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":555,\"name\":\"Analogue Animation Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-09T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-09T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f03096c2cc6d4097af1730bb69bbe268.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"All are welcome at this new series of analogue and print animation workshops with director Miranda Peyton Jones.\\nEach session, learn, experiment and have fun with different hands-on animation techniques! A space to try out new ideas and meet fellow experimenters. Expect to come away with a piece of moving image and your printed materials.\\nNo previous animation or drawing skills necessary, all are welcome.\\n\\n9th June:\\nThis class we will be using paper-cut-outs to create analogue animated pieces.\\nVenue: The HUB, 42 Bonar Rd, London SE15 5FB\\n\\nFor this workshop you will need a smartphone and the free app 'Stop Motion Studio'.\\nDownload prior to the workshop.\\nUnder 18s are welcome, but must be acompanied by an adult.\\n\\nIf you can no longer make the event, please reach out to mirandapeytonjones@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/analogue-animation-workshop-tickets-1990504291920?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":537,\"name\":\"KINSHIP\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-10T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-10T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"30b5cd4d4a661b340392757e0cfa7024.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This 10th of June, join us for a night of KINSHIP - Fundraising for East Congo\\n\\nFeaturing:\\n ❤️‍🔥The Jupitarians\\nNew Psych rock trio of Rochelle on bass, Rez on guitar and Neng on drums. They know what it means to move differently in spaces not built for them and that’s why they came together, taking the people along and beyond 🚀 \\n@thejupitarians\\n\\n❤️‍🔥 Ku-ro\\nWith a child like temperament Ku-Ro roams the stage - tender heart in one hand and chaos in the other. Raw articulation through lyricism, saxophone outbursts, fragmented soundscapes that blur the lines between reality and the imagination.\\n@kurothenomad\\n\\n❤️‍🔥 Kaneng Lolang \\u0026 Mawulikplimi Dossavi  Songs sourced from rememory, animism, awe, all benevolent darkness and the raging forces of nature, accompanied by  Éwé percussionist Mawulikplimi Dossavi\\n@kanenglolang   @noel_drum_n_drum\\n\\n❤️‍🔥 Rago \\nA South London multidisciplinary artist delivering a one-man performance built around his SP-404. Blending hip-hop, jazz, punk, and experimental sound, his lyricism navigates inner-city life, addiction, mortality, and social tension, set against cinematic, emotionally rich compositions.  Rago will also DJ\\n@ragofromthelo\\n\\n\\nAll proceeds go to displaced people in east Congo where the unimaginable horrors and human rights abuses intensify with the recent US and UAE plan to deploy a paramilitary unit of 3000 personnel to oversee the ongoing plunder and rape of Congolese land and people, all in the name of minerals that power our digital world and “green” technology. \\nPlease follow @focuscongo for updates on the situation \\n \\nFREE CONGO\\nLONG LIVE THE SPIRIT OF LUMUMBA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/35945/kinship\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":482,\"name\":\"The Man With The Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-10T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-10T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ae876c2809bf0f7807eeff97bbcaef94.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nJohn Bird in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films Production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":576,\"name\":\"SMUT Press – Cruising Archaeology II: Eurotrash – Book Launch and Signing\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-11T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2a4a742b1e9700f6bbd82a3d26726bd1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us next Thursday at Climax London to celebrate the launch of Cruising Archaeology II: Eurotrash, the long awaited follow-up edition to the 2024 cult bestseller by @smut_press 💖\\n\\nThe project builds on the initial edition’s success by expanding the breadth of archaeological sites to various locations scattered across European cities including Berlin, Athens, Dublin, Barcelona and Paris. The diversity of cruising areas, including woodland areas, public toilets, palatial gardens, sex clubs and beaches, speak to the inventive, site-responsive forms that cruising assumes and situating desire both within the folds of a city’s infrastructure and natural landscape.\\n\\nSee you there!\\n\\nThursday 11th June\\n6-8pm\\n\\nClimax London\\n8a Herbal Hill\\nLondon, EC1R 5EJ\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":549,\"name\":\"A Great Big Net\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7d93ff27c74863937aeed1467ee8aa7d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Exhibition dates: 11-28 June 2026\\nLocation: Project Space 3, Ground floor, SET Vauxhall, Camelford House, 89 Albert Embankment, London, SE1 7TP\\nOpening hours: Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, 12-5pm, and by appointment. To book, please contact daisynutting@hotmail.co.uk\\nPublic opening event: Thursday 11 June, 6-9pm\\nArtists: Massimo Franco, Ned Elliott, Daisy Nutting, Agnes Treherne, Tara Versey, Johannah Gibbons, Kate Walton, Ben Williams, Olly Williamson\\nAdmission: Free\\n\\nOpening Thursday 11 June at SET Vauxhall, A Great Big Net brings together nine artists working across drawing, printmaking, and painting, curated by Daisy Nutting.\\n\\nThe exhibition takes the motif of the net as a dual structure: one that can simultaneously isolate us from our world and link us to it.\\n\\nHere, the net serves as a cipher for systems of power, borders, and geometric fences, as well as the networks we use to navigate them. Using the net as a compositional structure that forms both the skeleton and exoskeleton of the works on display, A Great Big Net considers the precise moment when the freedom of the grid hardens into a trap.\\n\\nContributing artists\\n\\nMassimo Franco - Massimo Franco currently lives and works in London. Recently he’s made a return to printmaking, specifically a return to the book format. Notably this work displays an interest in part to purely abstract imagery. Massimo completed his training painting at Glasgow School of Art, drawing at Royal Drawing School and printmaking at Camberwell College of Art.\\n\\nNed Elliot - Ned Elliott is an artist from London. His subject is nature, and his focus moves from the small to the cosmic. His gaze is drawn to those things which are simultaneously frail and beautiful; a moth, a feather, a flower. He depicts how different elements of existence, sentient, insentient, intersect and coexist in the world, creating pictures which grow out of the confusing and elusive beauty of life.\\n\\nInstagram: @ned_elli0tt\\n\\nDaisy Nutting - Daisy Nutting is an artist exploring memory, storytelling and perceptions of ownership. Documenting moments of balance and imbalance within nature, Daisy’s etchings, drawings and paintings are made from a desire to connect with her surroundings and an attempt to take ownership of land that is not hers, suggesting that the memory of a place is a kind of possession to rival capitalist notions of accumulation and proprietorship.\\n\\nInstagram: @daisynutting\\n\\nAgnes Treherne - Agnes Treherne lives and works in East Sussex. Drawing from life underpins her painting and printmaking – her drawings are a response to the transcendent nature of the world.\\n\\nInstagram: @agnestreherne\\n\\nTara Versey - Tara Versey works across painting, printmaking and drawing, exploring the emotional and physical experience of being alive. Combining observation, memory and imagination, she creates works that seek balance between the human form, architecture and the natural world. Raised in London, her interest in geometry, anatomy and shifting identities informs compositions that reflect the complexity and fragmentation of human experience.\\n\\nInstagram: @tarajversey\\n\\nKate Walton - Kate Walton lives and works in Glasgow. Working across painting, drawing, and printmaking, she records people, objects, and landscapes through observation. These notations form a visual memory, used to construct images where figures and environments are compressed within pictorial space.\\n\\nInstagram: @kateswalton\\n\\nBen Williams - Ben Williams lives in Glasgow making paintings from arranged objects and figures which he comes up with either from drawings or by other means.\\n\\nInstagram: @williams_b_a\\n\\nOlly Williamson - Olly Williamson currently lives and works in London, and grew up in a village outside of Preston. He makes work about quiet situations of life; utilising intense observation and experimental structures of composition. His images reflect the underlying rhythms of the people and world he sees around him – hoping to make the everyday feel monumental.\\n\\nInstagram: @omw_painting\\n\\nAbout SET’s Associate Members Programme\\n\\nThis exhibition is presented as part of SET’s Associate Members Programme, which offers artists studio space alongside access to project spaces and opportunities to independently curate exhibitions, workshops, and events.\\n\\nThe programme supports a wide range of practices, from performance and installation to music, sound, print, and textiles, and is designed to provide space, visibility, and development opportunities for early-career and underrepresented artists working in London.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":519,\"name\":\"Queer Cinema for Palestine 2026: No pride in genocide\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-11T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d2cb5671c000dc80ea488e17fb6b99d4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"London for a Free Palestine, Shake the CIV and Queers for Palestine are proud to host a screening of short films as part of the Queer Cinema for Palestine 2026, a global film festival organised by the Palestinian Campaign for the Academic and Cultural Boycott of Israel (PACBI).\\n\\nIsrael attempts to instrumentalise our identities as queer people to “pinkwash” its image while committing genocide against Palestinians. In response, we hold this event during Pride month to re-affirm that there is no pride in genocide. No-one is free until we are all free!\\n\\nTicket sales will got to Al Qaws, Shake the CIV and Da3m.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://opencollective.com/london-for-a-free-palestine/events/queer-cinema-for-palestine-2026-no-pride-in-genocide-c2aba767\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":550,\"name\":\"By Hand By Eye By Ear\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"587f7db83096e092a9487bc376f7cc3f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Location: Project Space 3, Ground floor, SET Vauxhall, Camelford House, 89 Albert Embankment, London, SE1 7TP\\nExhibition dates: 11-27 June\\nOpening hours: Saturdays (13, 20, 27 June), 1-5pm, and by appointment. To book, please contact handeyeear@gmail.com\\nPublic opening event: Thursday 11 June, 6-9pm (features performances by artists)\\nArtists: David Sappa, Domènec Miralles, Ewan Peng, Jenny Pengilly, Pei, Rob Shuttleworth, Rupert Earl, tongktongktong, YUNA阿尘\\nAdmission: Free\\n\\n\\nOpening Thursday 11 June at SET Vauxhall, By Hand By Eye By Ear is a new group exhibition bringing together analogue and digital DIY sound objects and light installations curated by artist and SET Studio member Jenny Pengilly.\\n\\nBuilt from found materials, discarded items, and everyday electronics, the works on display explore how sound and visuals can be coaxed from unexpected sources and overlooked technologies. Rejecting polished interfaces and digital convenience, the participating artists embrace hands-on experimentation, chance encounters, and material limitations as creative drivers.\\n\\nSurfaces vibrate, circuits respond to natural phenomena, and kinetic gestures become instruments. Here, sound and visuals are treated as something discovered—unearthed through play, trial, and close observation. Together, the works propose alternative ways of making, listening, and visualising, where ingenuity replaces excess, and the familiar is reimagined as strange, expressive, and alive. \\n\\nConceived as a shared space for connection, creative crossover, and peer learning, the exhibition functions alongside a public programme of collaborative workshops, live performances, and ongoing invitations for visitors to interact and play.\\n\\nPUBLIC PROGRAMME AND EVENTS\\nYardYard Workshop\\nSaturday 20 June, 2-6pm\\n\\nJoin artists from the 嘢嘢YardYard collective to experiment with sounds and making. This hands-on, drop-in workshop invites visitors to make DIY wind instruments (such as a canister xūn and straw flute) from material waste. You can also customise electronic circuit-bent synth instruments with Pei and try out Ewan Peng’s modular synth.\\n\\nNote: The general exhibition remains fully open to visitors while the workshop is running.\\n\\n\\nCLOSING AND PERFORMANCE NIGHT\\nSaturday 27 June, 6-8.30pm\\nAn evening of live, improvised audio-visual sets and sound experiments taking place across the exhibition space.\\n\\n\\nContributing artists\\n\\nRob Shuttleworth - Rob Shuttleworth is an artist exploring the creative potential of accessible techniques and materials, highlighting the process of making as a language of expression. He performs and composes under the moniker Haddow, improvising with handmade instruments and found sounds, and shares these methods via the ‘Unprecious Instrument’ workshops. He also co-runs live sound art event SAOM, produces monthly radio broadcasts for arts journal FIELDNOTES, and works as an illustrator and designer for various music related projects.\\n\\nInstagram: @robshuttz / @haddowsound\\n\\nDavid Sappa - David Sappa works across sound sculpture, improvisation and field recording. Their projects take shape through site-responsive processes, using found or discarded objects—such as iron nails, driftwood, shells, glass, rope, brick, willow, plastic, frayed metal, burnt cinders and bone—reconfigured and animated to reveal tender frictions and material instability. Sappa’s work explores material memory, porous temporality, care, neglect, and their relationship to wider social systems.\\n\\nInstagram: @dalosap\\n\\nJenny Pengilly - Jenny Pengilly is a multidisciplinary artist working in learning and social engagement. Her practice focuses on the sensory exploration of materials and making to facilitate play, experimentation, and collaboration. Key projects include Static Studios, a nomadic recording studio and label developed with children; the Experimental Tunes and Children radio show on RTM.fm; and the Electronic Audio Club, a peer-led community group exploring DIY electronic audio.\\n\\nInstagram: @colourcillider\\n\\nRupert Earl - Rupert Earl is a multimedia visual artist using video-feeds, found objects, and naturally occurring reactions as the foundation of his work. Merging live-feed video projections and light-emitting installations, his practice explores organic interactions through real-time improvisation with physical materials.\\n\\nInstagram: @visuals_ru\\n\\n嘢嘢YardYard - 嘢嘢YardYard is a DIY subculture space and artist-led micro label connecting digital communities with physical gatherings. Established in 2024, YardYard operates as an experimental collective centred around sound, presence, and shared attention. The group pushes back against commercialised culture and rigid hyper-specialised roles, preserving a space for open listening and alternative voices.\\n\\nInstagram: @yard_yard_space\\n\\nYUNA阿尘 - YUNA阿尘 is a musician and multimedia sound artist who animates physical objects and digital environments. Working with site-specific listening, minimal mechanisms and game logic, she cultivates fragile moments and glimmering states of presence between bodies and communal technologies.\\n\\nInstagram: @yunaa_sparasii\\n\\nDomènec Miralles - Domènec Miralles is a Catalan-Italian digital artist based in London. Working with code-based tools, game engines, and custom-made visual and textual AI models, Domènec explores how new technologies change the way we think, communicate, and express ourselves. His work examines ideas like self-deception, human reliance on technology and non-linear ways of creating and acting.\\n\\nInstagram: @boladelolor\\n\\nTongktongktong - London-based multimedia artist Tongktongktong builds immersive, surreal worlds where invisible forces become tangible. Through real-time audio and visual systems, her work blurs the boundary between the virtual and the physical.\\n\\nInstagram: @tongktongktong\\n\\nPei - Pei is a multi-disciplinary artist whose practice focuses on sound art, DIY instrument making, and sculpture. Their work explores the connection between marginalised identities and noise.\\n\\nInstagram: @pppppphhhh6759\\n\\nEwan Peng - Ewan Peng is a multidisciplinary artist based in London, specialising in installation and sound art. He is dedicated to exploring the edges and connections between sound, body and machinery. His current work primarily explores the relationship between modern technology and the body through rituals of cybernetics and esotericism.\\n\\nInstagram: @ewan_peng\\n\\nAbout SET’s Associate Members Programme\\n\\nThis exhibition is presented as part of SET’s Associate Members Programme, which offers artists studio space alongside access to project spaces and opportunities to independently curate exhibitions, workshops, and events.\\n\\nThe programme supports a wide range of practices, from performance and installation to music, sound, print, and textiles, and is designed to provide space, visibility, and development opportunities for early-career and underrepresented artists working in London.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://setspace.uk/event/by-hand-by-eye-by-ear/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":433,\"name\":\"Selthe and Cuckoo Spit in the Round\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-11T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7b29eae8bd6cdadfa1f7d086e9013f48.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"selthe, cuck0ospit, veryskeleton, miathunderska at the piehouse 🎓 tickets on Ra early bird 6 / 7 / otd\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2437520?utm_source=ig\\u0026utm_medium=social\\u0026utm_content=link_in_bio\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":461,\"name\":\"Velveteen EP Release Show w/ sadplanet\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-11T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"39f7ab3a5fc9dcd821ef9c501bd297e9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Velveteen are set to release their second EP on Noon Records on the 12th of June, 2026. Join them at The Stag's Head in Hoxton on Thursday 11th of June for a release show alongside the excellent sadplanet. Doors from 7pm.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":565,\"name\":\"Street Scenes - Hair Comb Therapy\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-11T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e295b290703ae8982f9a807f63e69f9d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We get together on the streets with games, stories and interesting objects. We find a patch and host little activities there and then.\\n\\nThis week, we offer a mellow comb massage to strangers, soothing the scalp, charming the streets.\\n\\nCome along and enjoy the kerbside by playing and meeting friendly strangers. All activities are free, all people welcome.\\n\\nGet in touch to help us run more street events this summer.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":283,\"name\":\"KOGG\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-11T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5ca81c26654b72b4e0da4c7b00a8b850.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"KOGG launch their debut album Mechanista with a live multimedia performance at London's Iklectik.\\n\\nCombining experimental electronica, contemporary composition and creative invention, KOGG (composer / performer / instrument makers Selena Kay and Cerys Hogg) are joined by a four-piece brass section for the first time.\\n\\nLive electronics, DIY contraptions, video and acoustic instruments weave together to create off-centre melodies and elastic rhythms, intertwining with live and pre-recorded projected visuals.\\n\\nExperience music that is theatrical, tactile, and mischevious for one night only.\\n\\nSupport act tbc.\\n\\nThis performance and album release has been supported by PRS Foundation’s Women Make Music. http://prsfoundation.com/\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/bbolao-kogg-11th-jun-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":487,\"name\":\"Ufonic: Megabasse / Grady Steele pres. Nausea\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-11T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-11T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"510c0c04011467b86b4a6b9c83e87139.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"After over two years, we're finally back in London, landing at Hackney's recently inaugurated Raleigh Chapel for two special shows. Welcoming self-taught musician Pierre Bujeau for his solo project Megabasse as well as composer Grady Steele who will premiere his latest work \\\"Nausea\\\", released on Felt earlier this year.\\n\\nDoors at 19h30 / First show at 20h\\n\\n✿✿✿ Megabasse\\nMegabasse is the solo project of Pierre Bujeau when he is not playing with Omertà or Tanz Mein Herz. The setup, twin Fender amps, and his double-necked guitar would suggest heavy distortion sound walls, but it's quite the opposite — Through gentle repetition, Pierre carefully builds a tapestry of sound patterns that both unfold and interlace over time. On his 2019 LP \\\"Discorde\\\", The A-side, “à la Chapelle Sainte-Anne de Bricquebec,” was recorded within a Normandy chapel, while the B-side, “au Hangar à Dirigeables d’Ecausseville,” was captured in a historic airship hangar. On both side, it feels like the space the sound inhabits slowly folds into the music, a psychedelic and collective dream we're looking forward to welcome at Raleigh Chapel.\\n\\n✿✿✿ Grady Steele pres. Nausea\\nComposer, promoter and DJ, Grady Steele is the co-founder of the travelling rig Formant Soundsystem and runs the event series GS Presents in Paris since 2023 — Both projects responsible for providing space for forward-thinking dancefloors.\\nAs a composer however, Grady's two releases, \\\"Marsaskala\\\" on Archaic Vaults and \\\"Nausea\\\" on Felt, emerge as bodies of work that feel profoundly personal and intimate. At Raleigh Chapel, Grady Steele will present \\\"Nausea\\\" for the first time. Released on Felt in April 2026, Nausea materializes as one of our favorite pieces of music this year, beautifully extending over seven movements, like a collection of vignettes, memories of loved ones as seen on a cathode ray tube television.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2445751\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":483,\"name\":\"The Man With The Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-12T15:15:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-12T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8ddc2dab91672a2508b2ec744f4a74a9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films Production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":516,\"name\":\"Nashpaints + Henry Earnest w/ Relaxkev+IR\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-12T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a11b7d92aaf2f6f8cb784c6a6e78b2f1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dublin’s record label MirrorWorld lands at The Horse Hospital with three live performances from Nashpaints, Henry Earnest \\u0026 Relaxkev+IR\\n\\n----\\n\\nNashpaints is a musician from Dublin making and performing music in a broad variety of styles linked by a love of heavy atmospheres. He was a member of the band PRINC€SS. His second solo album Everyone Good Is Called Molly was released in February 2026 via MirrorWorld. \\n\\n----\\n\\nHenry Earnest is a producer and songwriter from Dublin. Following their debut album Dream River as well as recent activity as a member of PRINC€SS (wherethetimegoes) and production on Maria Somerville's Luster (4AD), Big Blue was released through MirrorWorld in 2024 which saw them continue to explore their love of experimental pop-music. \\n\\n----\\n\\nRelaxkev + IR are a duo based in London and Plymouth respectively. Ethereal vocals and guitar spills into synth drone – their music moves between hazy atmospheres and full-blown ballads. Their debut EP All Over the Road is forthcoming.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":508,\"name\":\"Nashpaints + Henry Earnest w/ Relaxkev + IR, Live at The Horse Hospital\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-12T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f173a8ddc22a7ffe946a5bc7c2c0b5da.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dublin’s record label MirrorWorld lands at The Horse Hospital with two live performances from Nashpaints \\u0026 Henry Earnest.\\n\\nNashpaints is a musician from Dublin making and performing music in a broad variety of styles linked by a love of heavy atmospheres. He was a member of the band PRINC€SS. His second solo album Everyone Good Is Called Molly was released in February 2026 via MirrorWorld. \\n\\nHenry Earnest is a producer and songwriter from Dublin. Following their debut album Dream River as well as recent activity as a member of PRINC€SS (wherethetimegoes) and production on Maria Somerville's Luster (4AD), Big Blue was released through MirrorWorld in 2024 which saw them continue to explore their love of experimental pop-music. \\n\\nRelaxkev + IR are a duo based in London and Plymouth respectively. Ethereal vocals and guitar spills into synth drone – their music moves between hazy atmospheres and full-blown ballads. Their debut EP ‘All Over the Road’ is forthcoming. \\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.thehorsehospital.com/events/mirrorworld\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":551,\"name\":\"misdigest @ oitij-jo arts space 002\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-12T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fbf8e28e313c3dc2c92fbe4b03a73362.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Charisse C @charisseec //\\nFiyahdred @fiyahdred //\\nAction Yakson @actionyakson //\\nAmpy @ampygram //\\n\\nThe second in a series of immersive Audio Visual events showcasing the art of London based artist Misbah Anjum-James (misbahbydesign). Each event will be a unique combination of cutting edge music whilst the audience is taken on a dive into the mind of the artist. No one event will ever feel the same to the next. \\n\\n\\nOITIJ-JO has been running since 2013, focusing on celebrating \\u0026 sharing Bangla-rooted creative arts with the public in the UK. By supporting our events you are helping to raise vital funds to help continue the work they do.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":568,\"name\":\"Lely \\u0026 Hida - music for solo piano\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T15:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"59ed279998d29efceb14772c046bd5d0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"two outstanding works for solo piano, each just over an hour long. \\n\\nTaizo Hida - The Rain Traces Its Outline (first UK performance)\\n\\n[interval]\\n\\nJohn Lely - Listing (first performance)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/lely-hida-music-for-solo-piano-tickets-1989859759105?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":480,\"name\":\"Lely \\u0026 Hida - music for solo piano\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T15:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"973f1d6a5ca27fc185ec5f7e9129c8b3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"first UK performances of experimental works by Taizo Hida and John Lely\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/lely-hida-music-for-solo-piano-tickets-1989859759105?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":493,\"name\":\"NIGHTLIFE SOLIDARITY TOWN HALL\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T14:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2b4c32061553445e5383c0e0a87c0b84.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"🔊Join us for the first NIGHTLIFE SOLIDARITY TOWN HALL🔊\\n\\nthis is an open forum to discuss building worker power in nightlife, share issues and strategies, one year on from KKR/ Superstruct boycotts \\n\\nOpen to all and any people involved in nightlife \\n\\nPlease join and share this message far and wide💪 \\n\\n📅 Saturday 13th June \\n📍Pelican House, E1 5QJ \\n🕝 arrive 2:30, 3pm start, 4 finish \\n\\nThis town hall is part of the wider No Borders Fair - there will be food, music, workshops throughout the day.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/35950/no-border-fair\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":513,\"name\":\"Sky People𓂃release event\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cfc7d4221022850acb8375fee068261c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"𓂃 𝘚𝘬𝘺 𝘗𝘦𝘰𝘱𝘭𝘦 release event𓂃\\nDeptford Beach, SE83GH\\n13/06/26 4-9pm\\n\\n˚ a gathering on the Thames in June with lovely people performing music, for the release of 𝘚𝘬𝘺 𝘗𝘦𝘰𝘱𝘭𝘦 by\\n𝘉𝘰𝘺 𝘓𝘶𝘤𝘪𝘥 𓂃 out 24/05/26 on Roca ་༘ donations welcome\\n\\nUltan O'Brien\\nFriendly Improvised Orchestra (Willow Swan, Séan Being, David Sappa, Cliché Touppée, Lorena Isabel Shapiro, Mosquito Farm, Ben Boswell)\\nSkip and Milu DJ\\nBoy Lucid\\n\\n₊there will be 𝘔𝘰𝘣𝘺'𝘴 bar on tour from Limerick city with herbal drinks..𓂃 ࣪ food and snacks are welcome for sharing་༘ \\n\\nFree event with donations welcome\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":605,\"name\":\"TEST EVENT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":467,\"name\":\"Father of Lies by Folu Odimayo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d65f6fcd3f3e0a810cbba8c3ceded36a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Father of Lies is a film and performance based installation created by Filmmaker and artist Folu Odimayo.  The work takes a look at the mainstream media and it’s role within the facilitation of the Genocides particularly in regards to Palestine; it’s enabling of war and conflicts across the last century as well as it’s position in creating divisions within society. Explored within a sound collage that oscillates between archival news, political soundbites from now up till the 1930s as well as a conversation between a journalist and a newspaper editor about journalistic impartiality. The work looks at unravelling the threads of what the news has become, who it truly serves and whose voice it really speaks to and from.\\n\\nCredits:\\n\\nDirector, writer and producer - Folu OdimayoSound\\nDesigner – Seirian Griffiths\\nAnimator - Harry Quirk\\nSet Designer- Zahira Odimayo\\nActor – Dave Newman\\nActor - Flora Douglas\\nPerformer - Alex Henderson\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":540,\"name\":\"Darcy Harding, Wildwood Daddy, Searchlight\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-14T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"08ea7d7cb7b46d0462b07a1be98798b2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Darcy Harding - Darcy Harding is a London based independent artist, playing alongside her band, she blends alternative folk americana with groovy rhythms, jangly guitars and rocky percussion, taking inspiration from the folk rock genre.\\n\\nWildwood Daddy - Wildwood Daddy is a folk singer weaving intimate, unfiltered stories of sex, alcohol, and love into hauntingly delicate compositions. Her voice is soft, tender, and almost fragile, floating over arrangements of violin and guitar that feel both rustic and deeply emotive. There is a striking contrast at the heart of her sound, a gentle, almost lullaby-like delivery paired with raw, vulgar subject matter, creating songs that feel disarmingly honest, bittersweet, and quietly confrontational.\\n \\n\\nSearchlight - Searchlight is the solo project of Finn ap Cawkell, a musician from the hills of the South Downs. A recently recorded EP utilised a friend’s tape recorder, broken violin, feedback and noise to create the textures behind 5 very well written folksy songs. Live, the act currently consists of beautiful songs reminiscent of Andy Irvine and Dick Gaughan, at times even Belle and Sebastian, this is alongside some energetic Celtic guitar flat picking.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":470,\"name\":\"CNI 4: SELN meet Tanum Sound at EXIT Glasgow\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-14T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"17bcc24c85626f08c3474d32e2220d31.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Bios:\\n\\n13.06.26 - SELN MEETS TANUM SOUND\\n\\nSELN return to Glasgow's EXIT to join in communion with Tanum Soundystem for the ever expanding Celebrating New Industrial series.\\n\\nSue Lèwig is German based artist originally hailing from Berlin. Blending post-techno, downbeat with industrial influences, her sound draws an exciting line between freetekno / schranz with an almost ethereal edge. Combined with mesmerizing live performances and soaring vocals, her music moves between hypnotic tension and an experimental techno energy. Following releases on BPitch, TM8 and Hector Oak’s KAOS it is a pleasure to welcome Sue for her debut UK show.\\n\\nJunior Loves is a producer and DJ based in London. Throughout several well established releases on the legendary 5 Gate Temple label alongside his own self releases he has showcased his own steppers sound which is both reduced, tough and highly functional yet laden with spiritual depth.\\n\\nConrad Pack runs SELN Recordings label alongside DJ Gonz, where his productions explore the fertile terrain between tuff, rooted soundsystem steppers and high-BPM techno. His evolving productions for Lost Domain explore a distorted, hard-edged but deep and dub-enriched techno sound with echoes of Obscurum, early Downwards and Axis.\\n\\nMellowdramatics is a DJ and operator of Tanum and Black Obsidian Sound Systems. As a selector their style is expansive and frenetic, flitting within darker mutations soundsystem music. Cutting their teeth at squat raves, they have since become a feature of the London club scene, alongside performing internationally including Ohm, Palais de Tokyo and MoMa PS1.\\n\\nNo one turned away for lack of funds\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2446325\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":559,\"name\":\"TapeScape\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-13T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9b434a90b667927e226f7c6fbb1d7b43.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We will play three specially selected cassette tapes in a public, outdoor location in North London. Includes Pataphysical – Hapticality (Good Morning Tapes) and two others of a broadly similar mood.\\n\\nTapeScape soundtracks unusual spaces with moving, analogue sounds.\\n\\nGuests will be asked to maintain silence during the listening, although we will be in public space so who knows what happens, it’s a soundtrack to whatever we experience there.\\n\\nStarts at 9pm, runs for 2 hours. Actual location is a 15 minute walk from Seven Sisters station TBA on the Speckle site on the day.\\n\\nThis will be held in a public location and no ticket is required although supporters will help us cover costs, host better events, and web3 users will enjoy special access in future.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.speckle.se/tapescape-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":486,\"name\":\"Few Crackles present Bushes \\u0026 NTN\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-13T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-14T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0b64c8a0613aed1581dfedfa481f86c0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Few Crackles label don NTN travels from sunny Provence to sunny London for a link up with Bushes at everyone's fav arch. Call it part 2 of a B2B began at infamous Marseille spot META last summer. Dub, raw house \\u0026 techno, funky +++ played fast and loose. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":602,\"name\":\"World Naked Bike Ride London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-14T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-14T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"20768fda929bd46cd5785a00984bf5c7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Various start locations and times for feeder rides, which all combine together later on. \\n\\nPlease see the website or social media for more info.\\n\\nFREE and no registration required - just turn up.\\n\\nNudity is not mandatory (but encouraged!). You can be \\\"as bare as you dare\\\"\\n\\n\\n\\nWNBR London is a not-for-profit, unincorporated association. It is a membership organisation, defined by its constitution. The campaign seeks to draw attention to its themes by being a fun, well-behaved, lawful spectacle that delights the public and attracts media attention. It is affiliated to WNBR UK and to the global World Naked Bike Ride network. It is not connected to other protest, cycling or naturist organisations.\\n\\nCleaner environment, safer roads, healthier lifestyles, better attitudes!\\n\\nThe ride demonstrates the vulnerability of cyclists and is a protest against car culture. WNBR is a worldwide campaign with a number of linked themes.\\n\\nIts objectives are to:\\n\\n    protest against the global dependency on oil\\n    curb car culture\\n    obtain real rights for cyclists\\n    demonstrate the vulnerability of cyclists on city streets\\n    celebrate body freedom\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":542,\"name\":\"Irisworm, The Orbazoid, DEBT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-14T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-14T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ecf1d115cb87b606dcfe73e591fe3b60.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets still available OTD\\n\\nIrisworm - Inspired by the Thames Valley Scene of the late 80s, irisworm brings to light a revival of shoegaze with a heavier alt rock twist.\\n\\nThe Orbazoid - The Orbazoid plays an eclectic blend of jazz rockish sounds like nobody has ever heard before. Come and see the trombone led spectacle for yourself.\\n\\nDEBT - DEBT are a queer no-wave trio based in South London. Drawing on influences from groups like McCarthy, Au Pairs, Squid, and Goat Girl, their songs cover a mixture of sex and politics, where the two intertwine to create a set that can be soft and heavy, ironic and earnest.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":426,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Freya / Low Life / Temperance / Guided By Malice\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-15T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-15T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"239e38a45395dccc6b8a883054a84d43.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nFreya\\nApocalyptic metalcore featuring Karl Buechner of Earth Crisis, back at full strength and ready to explode.\\n\\n+ Support from\\nConvulsion\\nKent grinding hardcore\\n\\nxTemperancex\\nNew straightedge hardcore ft. members of Break Them and many more\\n\\nGuided By Malice\\nNew London metalcore, members of Bullet\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\nMonday 15th June\\n£14\\nDoors 6pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/freya-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":402,\"name\":\"Copa 71 (2023)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-15T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-15T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8b6ed16969910ba78c312b84918a4a08.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a viewing of Copa 71 (Dir: Rachel Ramsay + James Erskine, USA) as part of a month long series of screenings which celebrate marginalised voices through the prism of football to coincide with the 2026 Men's FIFA World Cup.\\n\\nTold by the pioneering women who participated, Copa 71 is the extraordinary story of the 1971 Women's Soccer World Cup, a tournament witnessed by record crowds that has been written out of sporting history - until now.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":564,\"name\":\"Dirar Kalash \\u0026 Momoko Gill + Des Visages\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-15T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-15T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"91d741449762f26d743e689e16952279.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An evening of sonic improvisation by multi-instrumentalists Dirar Kalash and Momoko Gill, accompanied by live AV and electronic experimental duo Des Visages, amidst their European tour\\n\\nDirar Kalash's work spans a wide range of musical and sonic practices within a variety of instrumental, compositional and improvisational contexts. He is mostly known for his politically driven soundscape / electro-acoustic project \\\"The Sonic Front\\\", and the compositions \\\"we can't breathe (for eric garner, george floyd, and frantz fanon)\\\" and \\\"by any means necessary (for Malcolm X)\\\".\\n\\nMomoko Gill is a London-based composer, producer, drummer, vocalist, and multi-instrumentalist whose work moves fluidly between jazz, soul, electronic production, and experimental ambient textures. Raised in Japan in a family of musicians and music lovers, Gill took up drums and percussion to make herself heard amidst a pianist uncle, a guitarist brother, and a singer mother , before relocating to London where she studied anthropology and became embedded in the city’s vital experimental music community.A self-taught drummer, producer, songwriter, and vocalist, she has brought her unique touch to collaborations with Matthew Herbert, Coby Sey, Tirzah, and Nadeem Din-Gabisi. Years of extensive touring as a drummer, keyboardist, and vocalist have honed her distinctive compositional and production instincts.\\n\\nDes Visages is an experimental duo formed by Chilean musicians César Vidal (saxophone) and Jorge Care (electronics and visuals). Their work explores the interaction between acoustic, electronic, and visual elements through improvisation and real-time performance. In 2025, they released their debut EP in Geneva, Switzerland, premiered at the Black Box of the HEM and later presented at Fête de la Musique. In 2026, the duo recorded their second album, “aleas”, at the Dijktheater in Amsterdam, and the same year they've been touring accross Switzerland, France, The Netherlands, England and Denmark.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":408,\"name\":\"Add Some More Blue + Daisy Jean Russell\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-16T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-16T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6a0255a328cd5430bfe9c42df202b8da.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands is back at The Ivy House for another stormer. On Tuesday June 16th we're joined by Mia Rae and S.W Gothic!\\n\\nAdd Some More Blue is a creative synth and bass lead project by Mia Rae making alternative RnB/ electronic indie taking wider influences from jazz, post punk and dance music. The project is made up of a live band of friends that met at Trinity Laban and have carved out unique and ambient sounds with their individual influences, original ideas and approaches to their instruments. If you like: Vegyn, Kelela, John Glacier, Stereolab, Jockstrap and Blood Orange.\\n\\nA soft-hearted song slinger from South London, Daisy Jean Russell writes reflective indie folk shaped by playful melodies and tender songwriting. Drawing inspiration from Brian Wilson, Arthur Russell, and Wings, her songs search for meaning in everyday moments and the quiet connections between people. With support from Real Kind Records, Daisy is set to release her debut EP this summer.\\n\\nPurchase a ticket before 09.06 and receive a FREE PINT of New Lands lager at the show!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":538,\"name\":\"Superyacht\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-16T19:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-16T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7a73b3e0c5d0ffa221f83673e9ba7827.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Improvising ensemble and buoyant object Superyacht presents a set of new music by trombonist James Graham\\n\\nSuperyacht is an ensemble of musicians in and around the free improvisation scene in London.\\n\\n\\nThey interest themselves in acoustics, spatiality, indeterminacy, frequency relationships, great wealth and excessive consumption.\\n\\n\\nLike all superyachts they are neither here nor there, but are importantly quite large.\\n\\n\\nThis debut performance at The Horse Hospital will present five new pieces ahead of a release on SN Variations later this year.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":556,\"name\":\"Analogue Animation Workshop: Text!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-17T18:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-17T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"41057307cc5e364fd70d29c7b4f6b542.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Get creative in this introductory class to analogue/hand-made animation. All materials are provided, you just need your phone!\\nAll are welcome at this new series of analogue and print animation workshops with director Miranda Peyton Jones.\\nEach session, learn, experiment and have fun with different hands-on animation techniques! A space to try out new ideas and meet fellow experimenters. Expect to come away with a piece of moving image and your printed materials.\\nNo previous animation or drawing skills necessary, all are welcome.\\n\\n9th June:\\nThis class we will be using a range of materials, including paper cut-outs, charcoal and more to create hand-crafted text animations.\\nVenue: Helm, 3 Borthwick St, Deptford, London, SE8 3GH\\n\\np.s. More narative drived workshops will be coming up so if that's more your jam then follow my instagram @mirandapeytonjones for updates!\\n\\nFor this workshop you will need a smartphone and the free app 'Stop Motion Studio'.\\nDownload prior to the workshop.\\nUnder 18s are welcome, but must be acompanied by an adult.\\n\\nIf you can no longer make the event, please reach out to mirandapeytonjones@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/analogue-animation-workshop-text-tickets-1990559528133?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":592,\"name\":\"NO CLIQUE x RESONANCES\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-17T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4eaf1b8af8a44752a80fcf226408956c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Improv Greatest Hits present No Clique x Resonances ! This month we team up with composer Dom Matthews for a show concentrating on acoustic sounds. Uniting artists from different musical backgrounds and subcultures, one-time groups are curated that embrace...\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/oea9ry-no-clique-x-resonances-17th-jun-folklore-hoxton-london-tickets?lng=en\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":459,\"name\":\"Louis + Lottie + Rael + Adaer\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-17T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9b69e75a03dff73357a4aff8b3da64ad.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"LOUIS GRACE RELEASE PARTY W/ PERFORMANCE AND FILM SCREENING\\nsupport from lottie rael and adaer\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":500,\"name\":\"Aftermath (1)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-17T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99c4c060d14222aad6daa2d5172de480.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Monthly book club hosted by TUFF\\n\\n17 June 2026, 7–9PM\\n\\nHouse of Annetta, ground floor left hand room\\n\\n£3 suggested donation (contribution to the running of the house)\\n \\nEvery session will be held on the anniversary of a disaster or breakdown. Aftermath (1) marks 50 years after the June 1975 Standpipe Drought - via Bodies of Water by Astrida Neimanis, we will use this event as a starting point to think through infrastructure, ecology, economics and the politics of water.\\n\\n*Aftermath is a monthly book club held at House of Annetta exploring what happens after catastrophes - of industry, colony, extraction, eruption, storms and economic breakdowns. Through books, essays and shared discussion, the group will trace what lingers, shifts or emerges in the shadow of disaster. Readings will move across fiction, theory, history and spatial practice, opening conversations around ecology, labour, landscape, infrastructure and repair. The bibliography will evolve through conversation and invited guests, and will work towards producing a collective publication, book or exhibition that sits outside of institutional frameworks.\\n\\nJoin us to read, listen and/or discuss!\\n\\nPlease get in touch if you have any specific accessibility needs for either the session itself or accessing the venue. Unfortunately House of Annetta is not wheelchair accessible - see here for their guidance: https://cryptpad.fr/pad/#/2/pad/view/oXP0LSfuxq8-o+4iQ9lakB4oJrVKtjyUODLupCKBaUI/\\n\\nPoster by Sam Rowe\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/36564/aftermath-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":561,\"name\":\"Ingrown + King Street / Flesh Prison / Rabbithole | Real Life @ the Piehouse\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-17T22:45:00Z\",\"poster\":\"67b76627cf1b2cb00e546cb99e74d128.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nIngrown\\nFeral Idaho powerviolence\\n\\n+ support from\\nKing Street\\nLondon Style Hardcore\\n\\nFlesh Prison\\nBN1 Powerviolence Stomp\\n\\nRabbithole\\nFilthy Hardcore Death Youth\\n\\nWednesday 17th June\\n£12\\nDoors 7pm\\nLondon\\nPiehouse Co-Op\\n213-214 Edward Place, SE8 5HD\\n\\nNearest stations New Cross and Deptford\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/ingrown\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":463,\"name\":\"Mandalakia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-17T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-17T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"24940212375270ea333a218327e08c32.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A London born project that celebrates Greek Rebetiko and closely related traditional music. With a distinctive approach, the band weave together the vibrant tapestry of Eastern Mediterranean music with the harmonic progressions and rhythms of contemporary styles. The result is a fresh, new wave of Greek music, one that communicates the plurality of the vibrant London music scene while strongly reflecting on its origins and creating a joyful, holistic soundscape. \\n\\nThe group are seasoned musicians within the genre and have performed in various projects such as The Turbans, Don Kipper and Idrisi Ensemble and at highly acclaimed establishments such as WOMAD, BBC Radio and The Royal Albert Hall.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsmusic.eventive.org/schedule/69e39ccf665e3a73f2eb61b1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":228,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Twenty One Children, Ursula \\u0026 more\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"afea632079bd834f5188fb9875edd96e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nTwenty One Children\\nLACE UP YOUR MOSHING SHOES. DIY Hardcore grit from the heart of Soweto.\\n\\n+ Support from \\nUrsula\\nDistressed hardcore violence from California\\n\\nSecond Skin\\nStompy London Hardcore from some familiar faces\\n\\nShunkai\\nEmocrust revolutionaries\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£12\\n\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/21-children\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":613,\"name\":\"Workers and the World: Fighting Ecological Crisis from Within - Book Talk\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4380fd702856cb2acc93199a098da763.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"PRESENTATION + TALK WITH LORENZO FELTRIN\\n\\nWorkers are not doomed to be merely the victims of environmental devastation. As Lorenzo Feltrin shows, they can be key actors in preventing it. Because labour supports an unsustainable system of endless growth, it holds a central place in any strategy for our long-term survival.\\n\\nBringing Italian workerist theory into dialogue with a range of traditions from dependency theory to ecofeminism, Feltrin examines the intersection of labour and nature across the globe. By addressing several urgent dimensions of the ecological crisis, such as automation, precarious employment, imperialism and social reproduction, he offers a new framework for understanding how labour struggles and environmental justice are intertwined.\\n\\nAll Welcome - 18:30 for  food, 19:00 start! \\n\\nSome food will be provided - feel free to bring some for yourself or to share. Comrades who eat together, fight together!\\n\\nPlan C\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/planc/2204490\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":572,\"name\":\"Against Apathy // 002 ~ Resisting Gentrification and Landlordism\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7eacd1ab3741c6c3400ff8ed41d40203.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Against Apathy is an event bringing people together to mobilise, get activated, meet others and realise that we all have a role to play in creating change and resisting. This edition will focus on how to resist gentrification and landlordism, locally and beyond.\\n\\nThe event will feature 8 individuals actively involved in resisting gentrification in many different ways, spaces and formats, who will share a bit about what they do and how it might be possible to get involved.\\n\\nSpeakers TBA.\\n\\nWe will then break into small groups to get to know each other, discuss how we could use our own skills to do more or get active in new ways, and learn more.\\n\\nThis will be followed by music, and there will be food and drinks available all night from Ridley Road Social Club kitchen. The event will also be a fundraiser (pay what you feel) with all profits going to the Save Ridley Road campaign.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":494,\"name\":\"From the Same Night – DIY Ephemera Toolkit\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"737d7648e5f0991a20efd20d2e1c7ed4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us on Thursday 18th June, 6:30 – 8:30pm for From the Same Night – DIY Ephemera Toolkit, a zine-making workshop with artist Reuben Brown.\\n\\nFrom the Same Night – DIY Ephemera Toolkit is a portable archive and a DIY-ephemera-making toolkit designed as part of “club [construction]”, an ongoing research project exploring queer nightlife, memory, collective archives, and the social and political histories embedded within club culture.\\n\\nParticipants will be provided with a toolkit containing a curated selection of reproduced club culture artefacts: handmade flyers pulled from walls, floor plans, archival photographs, press clippings, found graphics and other traces of nightlife communities.\\n\\nWhile each toolkit contains more or less the same selection, the acts of cutting, collaging, annotating and reconfiguring produce distinct and deeply personal reimaginings of the archive that may be playful, narrative, critical or abstract. The resulting zines form a temporary collective record: a set of parallel interpretations that speak to the multiplicity of queer memory, the impossibility of a single authoritative narrative, and the ways nightlife is remembered, forgotten, retold, misremembered and rebuilt.\\n\\nThis free event will take place at Auto Italia. To book, follow the link here or email info@artworkassociation.org\\n\\nReuben Brown (b.2001)[he/him] is an emerging visual artist, club-creative and researcher based between Belfast and Dublin, Ireland. He is the founder and creative-director of “club [construction]”, an Irish club-collective and research platform, and he is currently completing a Master of Research (MRes) in Fine Art by Practice at the National College of Art \\u0026 Design, Dublin, supported by the NCAD Postgraduate Futures Scholarship. He is also a studio artist at Flax Artist Studios, Belfast.\\n\\nHe has exhibited locally, nationally and internationally, including several notable solo-exhibitions in Belfast, Dublin, London and Berlin. Notable projects include; “€URODANC€” at Pallas Projects/Studios, Dublin [June/July 2025], “In the dusk…” at Culterim Galerie, Berlin [February 2026], and “Propagate” at Catalyst Arts, Belfast [February 2025]. His artistic praxis has received support from the Arts Council of Northern Ireland through the National Lottery and An Chomhairle Ealaíon / the Arts Council of Ireland, and has been reviewed by District Magazine, Four Four Magazine, and DAZED, who recently named him as a “young creative you need on your radar” [November 2025].\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdk1q9GfyJUsS-a2uiH837n6qKnvS9ETv0Oa0fWtmAoqOsmaA/viewform\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":521,\"name\":\"olive wreath single launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e1b20e4ef8329f9ad6cf30a2cd681463.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"olive wreath launch debut single ‘cold warm green blue’ with support from Ropeburn. Promoted by DHP Family.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/orAvzSrzx3b?sharer_id=5c41c4760e0d4e42d921c7dc\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":335,\"name\":\"XS: gillielove + AILISH\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"29e9f483bf0d7c34601b5c875fa46170.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For the first of a new series, ex.sses invites gillielove + AILISH. \\n\\ngillielove is a producer and dj from Paris via Australia, whose music moves 'through weightless dub, pressure-shifting bass and downtempo breaks'.\\n\\nAILISH is an experimental sound artist and dj whose music builds world through field recording sampling and processing. \\n\\nDrawing from her interest in live art, sonic world building and left field club music, ex.sses brings together artists from different practices to build a night at the intersections. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":523,\"name\":\"3D Jesus - Release Show\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"76d8205359c899b5b89064bba1ecc6a6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"With support from: \\nBint Mbareh \\u0026 Big Hands\\nTHE NARRATOR\\nHostage Wallet\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":393,\"name\":\"Broadcast 15\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-19T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3f1f036e7c112e7a1528e2a867ac4c09.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Celebrating 15 years of Hyetal’s album Broadcast, the record will be performed live in full with vocalist Alison Garner. Broadcast received critical acclaim for its fusion of early dubstep experimentation, cinematic synth scores, dream pop, and underground dance music.\\n\\nExpect an evening of truly live electronic music, moving from ambient and downtempo into more rhythmic club-leaning sounds, alongside DJ sets from some of London’s finest selectors.\\n\\nLive: 19:00 - 23:00\\nDJs: 19:00 - 1:00\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/dk2m3e-broadcast-15-18th-jun-the-greyhound-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":554,\"name\":\"SOUND TRAVELS - LIVE EXPERIMENTAL NIGHT AT STUDIO 12\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"36178db1ac0a6fcf89db7e56607cdf02.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us at Studio 12 for an evening of live experimental music featuring:\\n\\n•⁠ ⁠Hawazin O — @hawazin.o\\n•⁠ ⁠⁠Dan Nicholls — @dan___nicholls\\n•⁠ ⁠Patricia Doors — @patriciadoors\\n•⁠ ⁠Utopian_Realism — @utopian_realism\\n\\n📅 THU 18 JUNE\\n🕖 7–11 PM\\nat Studio 12, SE5 7JZ\\n\\n@thestudiotwelve_\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":324,\"name\":\"XS \",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-18T19:40:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":621,\"name\":\"YELLOWUHURU, Big Leg, Fizzy Disc, A Psychic Yes + LaLi\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"741f6a5b42929a456ecc972c413205b2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This Friday, just ahead of the shortest night of the year, Lali and A Psychic Yes host a night of dancefloor catharsis. The lineup features a rare UK appearance from Tokyo’s YELLOWUHURU, showcasing his focus on driving low-end and organic textural sound. Party trickster Big Leg plays the club for the first time with his uniquely bewitching, wide-reaching selections, alongside the unpredictable grooves of local legend Fizzy Disc. Hosts Lali and A Psychic Yes complete the bill with a b2b, drawing across a vast set of influences.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2447820\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":514,\"name\":\"Starter Car Single Launch with Global Cowboys\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-19T22:15:00Z\",\"poster\":\"53bb80e157d9b163cb1d7b62baa57952.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join Starter Car as they celebrate the release of their second single, Kicking, with a double header of Scottish-fronted indie rock. \\n\\nStarter Car\\nFour-piece Starter Car formed when songwriter Oisean relocated to London from Glasgow, bringing with him homeland influences like Belle and Sebastian and Teenage Fanclub. The result is country-influenced indie twang full of hooks and harmonies. Having recently spent time holed up in the recording studio, expect plenty more music ahead of their UK tour in September. \\n\\nGlobal Cowboys\\nGlobal Cowboys is a new project by Sam Gowans. Crafted in secret studio and home recording sessions, the Cowboys draw from influences in the janglier categories of 20th Century guitar music alongside the sound worlds of Eno and Television. Above all else, Global Cowboys’ guitar-led compositions aim to explore, in equal measure, the hopeful and the forlorn. \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":534,\"name\":\"PA System Launch Party @etsdts\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-19T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0bf8dfc90c6e99076aed6ab5c96d2318.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"PA system Launch PARTY!  Come show us some love on the 19 June Friday.  We will be presenting our new PA, sound system in our experimental sonic basement for the first time!  Thanks to all artists who participated in our fund raising event back in April.  \\n\\nA listening bar vibe, with a turntable, few favourite records from Jonathan and I (angela wai nok).  You are also welcome to bring your favourite record and we could all listen to it together with drinks!!! \\n\\nIt’s gonna be raw, fresh, exciting and well I guess still a bit of lofi and improv vibe during the evening. \\n\\nDonations for future events are welcome!  Support us please ~ \\n\\n📅 19 June Friday \\n⏰ 1900 starts \\n📍Eat the Sunshine . Down the Sun (basement 💦)\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":true,\"cancelled_at\":\"2026-06-17T14:11:12.072272Z\",\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":601,\"name\":\"SECOND DAUGHTER IV - she was never one body\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2bda02d307ffc6ff12de81e1cae6c877.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"a night of exhibition works and live performance exploring the collective body\\nfeaturing: @isabellezetterstrom @katya_sykes @jacein.space @hollylou.jones @cosimavonmoreau @akasha_mari3 @kajalmistry__studio @posyesc @a.lissssssa @rosarugosaaaaaa @misery________________pleasure\\n🪱🪰⚠️\\n\\nFRIDAY 19TH JUNE\\n7PM-LATE\\nat: @eastwaybaths\\n\\nTICKETS: £6 or £7.50 OTD\\n\\nproject direction @lucychappell_\\ncuration by @hollylou.jones @noda.lichen @lucychappell_\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/second-daughter-iv-she-was-never-one-body-tickets-1991229660517?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":604,\"name\":\"Love Tutorial, Three Hares, MOXON\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"540fb2f84db1946998f05ca273a8956c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets still available OTD \\n\\nLove Tutorial - Love Tutorial is as much a post-modern art project as it is an indie band. With power pop ballads that draw as much from the novels of Don DeLillo as they do the albums of Prefab Sprout, the South London 5-piece are effortlessly slicing through the detached ironic malaise of the 2020s and Making Music Sincere Again.\\n\\nThree Hares - Three Hares are a London based band formed in early 2025. Their blend of noisy guitar sounds, and ambient textures has taken them from Latitude festival to Brixton’s Windmill. Drawing on their love of time signatures, guitar bands and Cornish rabbit-based motifs, Three Hares have spent the first half of 2026 gigging around London.\\n\\nMOXON - Moxon has gigged extensively throughout Yorkshire and London selling out multiple venues while consistently releasing exciting new music and setting indie dancefloors alight - HOTVOX\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":469,\"name\":\"Mija Milovic \\u0026 Ned Ferm (duo), Tu Sha, Zeynep Ağcabay: Nebo Arts #11\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-19T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"765a96705d82f3deae575ceb3e67d302.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"** SEASON CLOSING NIGHT **\\n\\nLondon-via-Zagreb collective Nebo Arts present the closing night of a 4-part event series in London with an evening of live performances and sound at Cafe OTO, bringing together experimental artists from London, the Balkans and beyond.\\n\\nMija Milovic \\u0026 Ned Ferm (duo)\\nTu Sha\\nZeynep Ağcabay: Nebo Arts #11\\n\\nAn intimate programme moving between post-club ambient, post punk and open-ended jazz forms, with a focus on new material and evolving projects.\\n\\nDJ programme to follow.\\n\\nSupported by Arts Council England\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/mija-milovic-ned-ferm/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":618,\"name\":\"misdigest @ oitij-jo arts space 003\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"89579cc8827b5eb71a2a0d510bc5df72.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"ELF\\nDRECO\\nK9\\nLOLINGO\\nRAPTURE 4D\\nRENZ\\nSI*BL\\nTIMMA T\\nVEEPERIERA\\nVERTEX\\n\\nThe third in a series of immersive Audio Visual events showcasing the art of London based artist Misbah Anjum-James (misbahbydesign) and this time we are going heavy on all things Grime and Dubstep. Each event of ours is a unique combination of cutting edge music and an ever growing collection of immersive visuals. No one event will ever feel the same to the next.\\n\\n\\nThe Charity OITIJ-JO has been running since 2013, focusing on celebrating \\u0026 sharing Bangla-rooted creative arts with the public in the UK. By supporting our events you are helping to raise vital funds to help continue the work they do.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":515,\"name\":\"BODIES ELECTRIC : SARAHSSON X GUILDHALL LIVE ELECTRONICS ENSEMBLE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4eebff57f95204a0cde78ae6f44c167d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A Guildhall Live Electronics Ensemble will collaborate with composer, performer and instrument-maker Sarahsson to explore materiality in sound, electroacoustic processing and spectral improvisation. \\n\\nWorking with Sarahsson's own non-traditional instruments following the sculptures of Elmar Daucher, François Baschet and Hans Reichel, they will perform electroacoustic and spectral compositions responding to amplified acoustics and rebuilding timbre. Relying on the resonant qualities of wood, steel, granite and different reflective chambers, to encourage and respond to the naturally occurring partials within different materials as they are live processed.\\n\\n\\n\\nGuildhall Ensemble performers: \\n\\nAmber Davies, Anna Latham, Eleanor Lee, Genia Isachenko, Philippa Godsalve,\\n\\n\\n\\nOpening sets :\\n\\n \\n\\nGenia Isachenko will perform an improvisation with radios and transducers. \\n\\nMiu Puntoomsinchai will be play the Khaen in both traditional and western styles, focusing on various approaches to creating ambient soundscape and texture through live processing. \\n\\n\\n\\nBios\\n\\nBODIES ELECTRIC is a platform for live electronics performance and research comprised of musicians and alumni from Guildhall School’s Electronic and Produced Music department. Collaborating through live music performances to explore creative scores, evolving compositions, somatic practices and bespoke material entanglements within music expression. By conjuring tangible physical and emotional states through experimental forms and collectively constructed timbres, they aim to create rich sound worlds for both the audience and performers to immerse themselves in. The project aims to create opportunities for collaboration and ensemble performance within live electronics and electroacoustic communities, and to invite dynamic collaboration between musicians, instrument-makers, choreographers, filmmakers, and dancers. \\n\\nSARAHSSON\\n\\nDevonshire-born Sarahsson is a composer, producer, multi-instrumentalist, performance artist and DJ living and working in Bristol. Inspired as much by the natural world as she is by gore and harsh noise, Sarahsson fuses elements of classical music with metal, experimental electronics and folk. Her 2022 debut album ‘The Horgenaith’ draws on personal and cultural mythologies of femininity, transition and synaesthesia.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":583,\"name\":\"Congo Natty x Don Letts x Annia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7a32da300f61b1aa3c4a2816592f9aaa.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A legendary jungle, reggae and dub takeover at The Fox \\u0026 Firkin this June, from Congo Natty – one of the true pioneers of the Jungle movement; and Don Letts, the DJ that single handedly turned a whole generation of punks onto reggae.\\n\\nJoined by rising star, singer-songwriter Annia, blending elements of R\\u0026B, soul, indie, and Caribbean genres such as dancehall and soca, creating a sound that is both deeply personal and universally felt.\\n\\nExpect a night of deep reggae and jungle cuts, form the best in the scene.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/congo-natty-x-don-letts-x-annia/\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":491,\"name\":\"GDANSE w/ Bethan, Mr Assister, Planet R.A.F\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-19T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5e0fa4392e51788c411b40d4a6cd7ca3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"HOW TO TRAIN A HAPPY MIND.\\n\\nTHE ENTIRE PATH EXPLAINED.\\n\\n⇄ Bethan ⇄ \\n● ↑ ●\\nMr Assister ←───→ Planet R.A.F\\n                          ● ↓ ●\\n\\nLimited capacity – Grab an advance ticket to guarantee entry.\\n\\n...\\nAddress:\\nArch 504, Ridgway Rd\\nLondon SW9 7EX\\n£5 / £7 ADV / More OTD\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/gdanse/2233155\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":285,\"name\":\"Warrington-Runcorn New Town Development Plan - All Dayer\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-20T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9abeef119d8171ae03294f0eb558bfa0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Baba Yaga's Hut Presents:\\n\\nWarrington-Runcorn New Town Development Plan\\n\\nLoula Yorke\\n\\nPolypores\\n\\nA’Bear\\n\\nSulk Rooms\\n\\nKylie Monologue\\n\\n3pm to 11pm at IKLECTIC\\n\\nEarly Birds - £25\\n\\nFull Price - £30\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/eorvqw-warrington-runcorn-new-town-development-plan-all-dayer-20th-jun-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":522,\"name\":\"No More Silence\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-20T17:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7587374cdd16b8ee4c5e15bca50a8e15.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us at Worlding to close Refugee Week together, close our exhibition of Deaths at Land and Sea and launch our latest investigation into UK border externalisation. The evening will feature reflections on the report's findings, spoken word, participatory art-making, poetry reading from Mana Misaghi, music, and a DJ set from Funky Chapati, alongside the kind of conversations that only happen when the right people are in the same room.\\n\\nFood from Amrutha, homemade drinks, and Collective Aid merchandise will be available throughout the evening, so come early, stay late, and settle in. As part of Collective Aid's No More Deaths campaign, all proceeds will directly support our work with people on the move across Europe's borders.\\n\\nTickets available now and on the door.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":448,\"name\":\"Pleasure Promise\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ed04bbfeaf4266e0143c148351868673.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pleasure Promise takes over Spanners for a full-spectrum dive into raw, analogue-led club music.\\n\\nHeadlined by Beau Wanzer, whose output spans industrial, acid and no wave abstractions, the night leans firmly into the darker edges of the dancefloor.\\n\\nSupport comes from Wes Baggaley the DJ cult favourite of raw rhythms and pulsating electronic bass.\\n\\nAn intimate session.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2416583\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":539,\"name\":\"Kasperia, Hari The Cosmic Cowboy, Abi-Fay\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b53153dc4d80713b295b4423d145ada6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kasperia - Kasperia is a rising hard rock band from Birmingham, UK, fusing the raw power of classic rock with a modern flair. Kasperia delivers high energy live shows that channel the spirit of rock’s golden era while captivating modern audiences. Their performances combine iconic covers with original tracks such as crowd favourites “Dead Letter” and “Keep Walking,” showcasing their growing songwriting prowess and tight musical chemistry. For fans of Led Zeppelin, Black Sabbath, Rush and Heart\\n\\nHari The Cosmic Cowboy - Forged from the interplanetary collision of melodic Mercury and seductive Saturn, Hari the Cosmic Cowboy and his band of galactic cosmonauts bring you the best mix of psych-rock, blues and astral folk this side of Andromeda with an abstract money back guarantee to get you dancing.\\n\\nAbi-Fay - Abi-Fay is a young English singer-songwriter, violinist, pianist, and classical singer known for blending pop, jazz, and R\\u0026B with personal lyrics, often performing with her band, and gaining traction as an independent artist with gigs and releases...\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":458,\"name\":\"Or Sobre Blau (Ubaldo and Kiran Leonard) | John Edwards / Daniel Thompson (duo) | Luke Cowan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2a282fe967de9e20c0e9d12730786a4f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A night of music celebrating the launch of Making Friends by Or Sobre Blau (Ubaldo and Kiran Leonard). Featuring John Edwards and Daniel Thompson (duo) and Luke Cowan.  \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":336,\"name\":\"Testing the Water presents: Tom Boogizm, Aircode (live), Daksh b2b Mag\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-20T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"65aed152d83c83f3279d11e08778d08b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"After dipping our toes into more ambient pools earlier this year, Testing the Water returns to its more club‑leaning side. For this edition we’re welcoming three artists who each approach rhythm from a different angle, but share a commitment to keeping things loose.\\n\\nTom Boogizm needs little introduction to anyone who’s spent time in the UK’s weirder corners of the dancefloor, kept one eye on Boomkat’s end‑of‑year lists, or tuned into NTS. As the mind behind Shotta Tapes and the soulful, barbed, occasionally political (but never preachy) world of Rat Heart (after all, what does happen if you just eat crisp?) he’s built a universe where oddball melody, busted rhythm and tape‑warped texture fold naturally into each other. A long‑time architect of mutant club logic, his sets move with that unmistakable Boogizm feel: broken but rolling, loose but laser‑focused, stitched together with the kind of instinct you can’t fake. Whether leaning into bassier sounds or dropping a Mark E. Smith banger, he’s one of the few DJs who can make a 200‑cap basement feel like a world unto itself.\\n\\nWe’re also thrilled to be welcoming back Aircode for a live set - her first with us since one of our earliest TTW nights back in 2022. Since then her work has only grown sharper, stranger, and more emotionally charged, folding scattered percussion, marshy pads and digital grit into something that feels both intimate and volatile.\\n\\nKicking off the night, Daksh returns to TTW after a gorgeous set for us at Shai Space, this time stepping into a more club‑facing mode. Paired with Testing the Water’s own girlboss Mag, the two will be setting the tone for the night with pressure, patience and perhaps some curveballs.\\n\\nAs always: come early, stay late, and remember to stay hydrated.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2427160\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":560,\"name\":\"Febuary (Matinee show) | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-21T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"54b5c6935588b175d1a4af54a06ecad0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nfebuary\\nThe most exciting band in the world. Matinee added as you all sold us out so fast.\\n\\nGood Carl\\nReunited rockstars playing you the 108th best emo song ever\\n\\nSevy Verna\\nUnderground skrim riffs\\n\\nSunday 21st June\\nDoors 1pm\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+ \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/febuary-matinee-show\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":377,\"name\":\"Febuary in London | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-21T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"23e8d01654fc2a797451852ce410533b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"febuary\\nOne of the most exciting bands in the world. Uncompromising, distressed emoviolence taken to new heights.\\n\\n+ a huge supporting cast of\\nCady\\nUK Screamo legends\\n\\nMountain Peaks\\nNorfolk emoviolence anthems\\n\\nI'm Sorry Emil\\nGolden age screamo bangers\\n\\nSevy Verna\\nUnderground skrim riffs\\n\\nSunday June 21st, New Cross Inn, £15\\n\\nNearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/febuary\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":418,\"name\":\"HOLY\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-21T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"75217bbe75f133a2fbc409432032f69d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nOn Sunday 21st June HOLY will be returning to Cu in Dalston for a summer solstice special with South London dub don Sons Of Simeon as our very special guest.\\n\\nIf you've ever been lucky enough to catch one of the Sons Of Simeon sets then you'll understand why we're so excited to get them down to HOLY. Packed with dubplate specials, blazing dub sirens and mic chat chanting down Babylon this is dub futurism done London style.\\n\\nAs always DJ support comes from residents Richard Fearless and Tom Dubwise who will be delivering a 100% vinyl journey into the depths of dub in it's myriad of mutations from 70's roots to contemporary steppers, dub techno, dubstep and beyond.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2440458\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":593,\"name\":\"Solidarity Tapes Summer Solstice Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-21T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ab90de4d0900f2478b16f404cd0bdbf9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Solidarity Tapes and Piehouse Workers CO-OP return with party to celebrate the Summer Solstice and to raise funds for Palestine Music Space.\\n\\nhttps://palestinemusicspace.com/\\n\\nFeaturing performances from\\nBaggio\\nAll Maudra\\nLiv Wynter\\nNick Granata (Shovel Dance Collective)\\nZia Ahmed\\nTen Minute Tales\\nCigotine DJ\\n\\nKaraoke likely.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":591,\"name\":\"Stanley Welch - D. Jean-Baptiste - Barreleye\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-21T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c627f47d5cd63b70a412947904277589.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Horse Hospital welcomes a programme of Chicago - London creative exchange, built upon experimentation. Each group explores the edges and interior of the song, but does so in ways wholey unique to themselves. Be prepared for introspection and total rhythm. \\n\\nBios: \\n\\nStanley Welch is a musician and composer from rural Cornwall, based in Glasgow and London. Welch creates explosive and winding songs, turning over themselves, finding unexpected corners and avenues of form within the whole. He takes the classic notions of songwriting and lets his audience, alongside him, examine them under a microscope. Stanley Welch is one half of the London-based electronic record label NorthSouth records.\\n\\nD. Jean-Baptiste is a performer from Chicago experimenting with song by any means necessary. No show is the same, no set follows the same arch. Songs stretch beyond their limit. Silence is a weapon.\\n\\nBarreleye is a band currently straddling the Atlantic Ocean, with members based in both Chicago and London. Borne of the midwest, these three youngsters take on new worlds with hippy axes, frivolous ears, and steady tardiness, ever in the footsteps of the American Chicken. A sceneless, spineful amalgam, landlocked and poised to unlock your mind from the unstupid.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":403,\"name\":\"Mario (2018)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-22T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-22T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"438db9e2ecd2ff60252614823809c5da.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a viewing of Mario (Dir: Marcel Gisler, Switzerland) as part of a month long series of screenings which celebrate marginalised voices through the prism of football to coincide with the 2026 Men's FIFA World Cup.\\n\\nMario is a 2018 Swiss romantic sports drama film directed by Marcel Gisler. The story revolves around two sportsmen who meet while playing football against other teams in a shared location and quickly develop feelings for one another.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":614,\"name\":\"Book Launch: Fearful in Gaza\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-23T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"668116ca553de6a468934191060b3149.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join Maqam for the launch of Fearful in Gaza, a gripping memoir by Abdalhadi Alijla uncovering the deeply personal realities of life in Gaza\\n\\nJoin us at Pelican House for the London launch of Fearful in Gaza, a memoir by Dr. Abdalhadi Alijla.\\n\\nThe evening will feature a conversation with Dr. Alijla, moderated by Nidal Al Haj Sleiman, opening space for reflection on memory, survival, displacement, and the lived realities of Gaza.\\n\\nThe event is free and open to everyone. Guests are warmly invited to attend the conversation, take part in the Q\\u0026A, and stay for the book signing afterwards.\\n\\nBooks will be available to purchase at the event. Pre-orders will also open soon via the MAQAM website. https://www.maqam.uk/books/p/fearful-in-gaza\\n\\n\\nEvent details\\nDate: Tuesday 23 June\\nTime: 7–10 PM\\nVenue: Pelican House\\n144–148 Cambridge Heath Road\\nBethnal Green, London\\nE1 5QJ, UK\\n\\nSchedule\\n7 PM – Doors open\\n8–9 PM – Book launch conversation with Dr. Abdalhadi Alijla, moderated by Nidal Al Haj Sleiman\\n9–10 PM – Q\\u0026A and book signing\\n\\nEntry: Free and open to all.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/book-launch-fearful-in-gaza-tickets-1990880924438\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":389,\"name\":\"Colin Webster / Mark Holub | Caroline Kraabel / Aga Ujma / Alex McKenzie | Agata Genissel / Joshua Barfoot \",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-23T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a88121fd618fb50076192ea3be623a43.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Improvised music from Colin Webster / Mark Holub (duo), Caroline Kraabel, Aga Ujma, Alex McKenzie (trio), and Agata Genissel / Joshua Barfoot (duo). \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":629,\"name\":\"The Man with the Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-24T14:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-24T16:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"26f27b2414dd7b842fbdf3b616ba408a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, with Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza, Andrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\n\\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films Production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":481,\"name\":\"Somewhere Press w/ Slowfoam, Sina \\u0026 Nosewise\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"838778347b16b0c1485e005fd4f16bf1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Slowfoam + Sina play 3 live dates across London, Newcastle and Glasgow ahead of their forthcoming albums for Somewhere Press. They're joined by London-based Nosewise for an intimate evening of nocturnal dreamweaving in Spanners. The event will be soundtracked by Somewhere Press DJs, Lizzie Urquhart and caapi. \\n\\nTickets £8-11 ADV / £13 OTD\\nAll event revenue goes to the artists. Solidarity tickets help us cover costs and increase artist fees.\\n\\n--\\n𝗦𝗹𝗼𝘄𝗳𝗼𝗮𝗺\\n\\nSlowfoam, aka Madelyn Byrd, is a sound artist, performer, DJ, and educator exploring sonic-somatics and the ecopoetics of home and transformation. Slowfoam embodies an innate sensitivity to texture and somatic response, alchemising field recording, found hums and drones, electroacoustics, voice, guitar, and sound design into genreless whirls. \\n\\nSlowfoam's debut album Transcorporeal Portal was released with Somewhere Press in 2024, and included in Bandcamp’s best of Ambient. Their sophomore album, Night Rider, follows later this year, revisiting a teenhood in the Sonoran Desert through Wild West fantasy. Night Rider weaves the synaesthesia of memory and streams of (un)conscious meanderings with a buzzing palimpsest of the American Southwest.\\n\\n𝗦𝗶𝗻𝗮\\n\\nYet another starlet borne of Naarm’s prodigious nexus, Sina emerges from the trip-hop murk of Dregs’ widely adored, eponymous ’23 entry. Her recent single, Olympus, for Somewhere Press, is the first sign of bigger things on the horizon. It blooms from reverbed guitar, synth pads and longing vocals with a sense of strung-out, romantic pathos and sensuality that colours much of the best work from the city at the far end of the world.\\n\\n𝗡𝗼𝘀𝗲𝘄𝗶𝘀𝗲\\n\\nSharing a name with certain medieval hounds, Nosewise is the alias of one member of the London-based project Twin System. His music can be found on said label, along with new imprint ‘Ó Maidhin’.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":363,\"name\":\"Jacana People\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"82abac9915b63611f75aa8240509d9a8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"dollop presents Jacana People\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2384625\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":615,\"name\":\"Magazine launch: WEEKEND\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-24T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"248ed987cb31d0f1c55dd00b6f8c81c9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Wednesday June 24 @ 7:00 pm – 8:30 pm\\nCOME AND CELEBRATE THE LAUNCH OF A BOLD NEW POETRY MAGAZINE AT HOUSMANS. FEATURING LUKE ROBERTS, HARRIET ROSE AND OTHERS.\\n\\nThis is a free event, please book your tickets below. Feel free to BYOB. 🙂\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/magazine-launch-weekend/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":620,\"name\":\"AMPLIFIED 06: Vera Sacra, Curbside Lambsear, Iris Inc.\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e80c27fd31fdb848e26d84badf932535.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets still available on the door.\\n\\nVERA SACRA is the solo project of Emily Marks, a Sheffield-raised, South London-based producer who wields her cello and synth to create songs spun from the ether. Blending field recording from the Dark Peak moorlands, honest songwriting and textural intricacy, her writing crosses a range of styles - from soft ballads to deconstructed club and surreal ambience - kept cohesive by her cello.'\\n\\nCurbside Lambsear is Annabelle Mödlinger and Magdalena McLean. The collaboration explores rough textures and soft intentions, weaving together elements of pop, folk, and improvisation with influences of drone, dub, and post-punk. The project began as a way for Magdalena and Annabelle to experiment with writing music together, using early sessions to learn new instruments, the process of recording and writing on DAWs. Their musical output is the result of time spent together in the studio fusing disparate influences into collage; phone notes, little poems written on public transport, field recordings, sample loops, rehearsal voice memos and string melodies merge, realign, and sometimes coalesce into songs.\\n\\nIris Inc. takes you down a trip of Dark hoppy electronic beats.\\n\\nAmplified is a night dedicated to giving up and coming local artists the limelight, it is not about spectacle - its about connection, craft and being present in the music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":146,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Contention x Clique x Apothecary x Mortal Spirit\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-25T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-25T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"008514d41ddaeddae5b10a3198b839fd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nContention\\nStraightedge mosh artillery on DAZE. Played a legendary show for us last Summer, back to beat their own record.\\n\\nClique\\nBig riff hardcore on Closed Casket. Yr moshin.\\n\\nxApothecaryx\\nVEGAN STRAIGHT EDGE\\n\\nMortal Spirit\\nElite straight edge moshing crew\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/contention-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":616,\"name\":\"Still Formation, by Jess Gough\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-25T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-04T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b3bbb5bc0c8195fa5aba44b5d762899b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A world accumulates, image by image. This is a place of strange, sweet light, where fog bewilders, caves beckon and smoke curls out of craters. Landscape is not what it seems. A certain liquidity pervades. Viewpoints tilt. Glaciers slurp. Pathways gleam.\\n\\nDrawn from eight years of work, Jess Gough’s photographs describe a world in transition, where matter is unsettled and everything slips between states: clotted shorelines, pearly ridges and rocks that appear gelatinous. Curious openings appear in earth and metal, where natural and human-made forms echo one another in a shared, borrowed vocabulary.\\n\\nIn Still Formation, darkroom handprints sit alongside photopolymer etchings and their iridescent metal plates - part image, part relic - each a sustained study of materiality, following surfaces until the familiar tips into the unknown.\\n\\nJoin us for the opening reception 25.06.26\\nRSVP Info@1014.gallery\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":652,\"name\":\"Inframetropolitan Systems: Edward George on Frankie Knuckles + Louis Moreno on Janet Jackson\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4b54070f65811e994ad530010c97d428.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"First of three sessions on the musical production of space and memory, space and politics.\\n\\nEdward George on Frankie Knuckles. \\n\\nLuis Moreno on Janet Jackson.\\n\\n!!! GUCU STRIKE FUNDRAISER !!!\\n\\nGOLDSMITHS UCU HAS VOTED TO MOVE TO INDEFINITE STRIKE FOLLOWING THE IMPOSITION OF 100% PAY DEDUCTIONS.\\n\\nTHIS TALK IS FREE BUT IF YOU ARE ABLE YOU CAN DONATE TO THE GUCU STRIKE FUND.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":true,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":578,\"name\":\"Taosol Jam\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-26T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"72299fe557ab5bb2417af4f94eb3b206.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"TAOSOL is not just an artist collective; it’s a thriving community where creativity, activism, and human connection intersect. They run London’s first live and electronic fusion jam session, creating an open and inclusive space for musicians, singers, rappers, dancers, poets, and DJs of ALL genres to come together on stage and express themselves freely. The jam session is a night of electrifying freestyling and open decks for DJs who not only spin their magic but also collaborate seamlessly with artists to create spontaneous, genre blending music. \\n\\nFounded by LAILANA in December 2022, TAOSOL is rooted in the belief that art can unite and inspire action. The name itself is a reflection of this ethos, ‘Tao’ means “human” in Tagalog, and ‘Tawasol’ means “connection” in Arabic, symbolising the blend of her heritage and the essence of what the collective stands for: human connection and the power of collective expression through the universal language of music in all its forms.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/taosol-jam/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":623,\"name\":\"UPPERCUT VOL.9 with KGB Quartet, Rebuilt Boys, You Forever\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-25T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-25T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"98de3ddc3b05ed04ddb066656eaaac04.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tickets still available OTD. \\n\\nKGB Quartet - ‘The genre-bending, all ways changing collective’ KGB Quartet take the Deptford Junction for a night of ‘chaotic soundscaping’.\\n\\nRebuilt Boys - Rebuilt Boys are a transgender Electronic Sass-Noise duo formed in Peterborough, UK in 2024. They have drawn comparisons to The Blood Brothers, Machine Girl and Death Grips.\\n\\nYou Forever - You Forever are an experimental, folk-noise duo that delve into a world of ambient and textured angles, shifting through genres and time.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":464,\"name\":\"Dudu Kouate, Kadialy Kouyate \\u0026 Fred Thomas\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-25T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-25T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7a2edc5a8513412c6cc77d27e6b645fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Drawing on the ancient Griot traditions of their ancestors, Kadialy’s intricate original compositions are brought to life through the cosmic free-jazz philosophy Dudu honed with the Art Ensemble of Chicago. ECM artist Fred Thomas anchors the trio, his broad practice as an improvising musical polymath grounded in a deep connection to West African music. The result is a rich tapestry of haunting vocals, virtuosic kora, exploratory percussion, and subtle double bass grooves.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsmusic.eventive.org/schedule\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":651,\"name\":\"Research is Poetry\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-26T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"575f87b76af510b8d321583552c46060.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Knots presents our first night of Research is Poetry, hosted at Pelican House on June 26th from 6-9 pm. \\n\\nThis will be fundraising for our Co-op registering fee, so we are able to do more noise nights, develop long form productions, and host community workshops, from an art-workers led perspective. If you're interested in learning more about the Knots Co-operative, please email us!\\n\\nResearch is Poetry is a peer-to-peer learning event inviting Knots collaborators, alumn, and audiences to bring in essays, slides, poetry, photography, and other creative forms of research. We invite you to discuss history, current events, politics, art, and culture through a class-conscious lens using lived experience, theory, and research. \\n\\nIn an era of AI summaries and digital slop, let's remember that research is poetry, and needs us to contextualise it. \\n\\nLineup to be released. Submit your presentation here: https://forms.gle/u3RpfkGELYPFkg1k8\\n\\nFind more information on us at knotsnoise.carrd.co!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/36941/research-is-poetry\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":563,\"name\":\"Club Commons x Feminist Library Book Launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-26T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-26T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"919d7beb2f90677c7935389d129123cf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nJoin us for an intergenerational queer conversation weaving together archival memory, nightlife history, and collective futures.\\n\\nThis evening brings together three icons who shaped London's lesbian and queer scenes from the 1980s and 90s to today: Katherine Griffiths, DJ and researcher who participated in grassroots lesbian nightlife in London through the 80s and 90s; Yvonne Taylor of Sistermatic, the pioneering Black lesbian sound system; and Gin of Nite Dykez, DJ, promoter, and event producer, all of whom feature in the book Club Commons: Moving Bodies to Grow Movements in Queer Nightlife and Beyond by Anjali Prashar-Savoie, out now with Velocity Press.\\n\\nAlongside the talk, Holobiont presents Naked Souls: a queer archival oracle card intervention as \\\"an invocation of queer clairvoyants against gentrification of the heart and mind.\\\" Drawing on histories unearthed from the 56A Infoshop and Southwark Archives, Naked Souls is a deck of oracle cards/fortunes/spells, that invokes obscure queer histories, to chart alternative maps for our futures. It is playful and sometimes frivolous, existing in a makeshift between poetry and instruction.\\n\\nOriginal archival flyers from the 1980s and 90s will be on display throughout the evening.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/club-commons-x-feminist-library-book-launch-tickets-1990654364792\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":548,\"name\":\"Infinite Expanse Presents: Synergy Trilogy + Prophetic Justice Ministry + Luke Cowan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-26T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-26T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"815fc02a9901a17ba23190ad92b16070.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Infinite Expanse brings together two Melbourne artists — Synergy Trilogy and Prophetic Justice Ministry — and London's Luke Cowan to mark the release of Synergy Trilogy's self-titled debut album.\\n\\n\\n~~~\\n\\nSynergy Trilogy is the dream pop/neo folk/experimental project of Tilly Cameron (Perfect Sleeper) and Izzy Martin (Storia Felice). Threaded through with spoken word storytelling, Synergy Trilogy creates a sonic conduit for dream-borne incantations and meandering poetry, weaving through genre, time and space, meeting somewhere in the middle of the air. Their self-titled debut album is released by Infinite Expanse in June 2026.\\n\\nProphetic Justice Ministry is the psychic sound-whirl of Australian songwriter and producer Sam Perry (Who Cares?). Progressive electronic, ambient, psychedelic pop, tape loops, samples, guitar and vocals. In 2023, Perry released Electric Hell 2, followed by Prophetic Justice Ministry Vol. 1 in late 2024. His third album, Key To World Peace, is released between Night School Records and Hobbies Galore in June 2026.\\n\\nLuke Cowan is a composer and musician based in London. He has self-released a small collection of enviro-ambient works which are deeply imbued with the geography and atmosphere of the fenland landscape in which he grew up. Various configurations of piano, strings, brass and reeds form the basis of his arrangements, which are woven also with the sounds of non-traditional instruments such as pinecones, spoons, wine glasses and handfuls of grains. This open approach to arrangement, combined with a vérité approach to recording, gives his music an undeniable pastoral quality, as well as a certain vitality. Improvisation is central to Luke's creative process, and in his work he seeks to strike a balance between the preconceived and the spontaneous. His latest album, SPRiNG!, is out now on Infinite Expanse.\\n\\n~~~\\n\\nTICKET BUNDLE INCLUDES ENTRY + LP COLLECTED ON EVENING\\nTICKETS WILL BE £16 OTD\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":543,\"name\":\"Celeste Madden, Eistir, Mannequin House\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-26T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8f0aa2298c1d3f1021fba09730cb1c87.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Celeste Madden - Celeste Madden is a 23-year-old British singer-songwriter celebrated for her eccentric and surreal musical style. Influenced by 90s rock and a love for guitar reverb, her autobiographical songs explore deep emotions with a touch of humour. Backed by her live band, Celeste has played venues like Rough Trade East, the Windmill, and The Victoria. Her latest EP, 'Is It Really Goodnight?', was released this year, being featured by Steve Lamacq, Amy Lamé and Abbie McCarthy.\\n\\nEistir - Sounds from the other side. Ambient folk made in Northern Ireland. Reinvention of producer Ewan Samms’ jam-based songwriting project. \\n\\nMannequin House -  Mannequin House is a marriage to rock’n’roll with an affair with the club. Big bluesy riffs mix with acid bass, drum machine, synths, piano and dual vocals in a love letter to all music that makes us move. Drawing from British 90s rock, melody and structure is central to the music, along with a fascination with the narcotic wit of New York’s leather clad Suicide, Lou Reed and the Strokes. These elements combine for music that soundtracks a night out that starts in a North London boozer and ends in a Peckham Kitchen.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":641,\"name\":\"Altered Levels Vol.1 ft. Years of Denial\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-26T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1be75574024f18740f02e17ecd167e6c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"ALTERED LEVELS VOL.1 brings together experimental live performance, techno, EBM, dark electronics, audiovisual installation and expanded club culture for a night unfolding across multiple sensory layers at Peckham Levels.\\n\\nA hybrid audiovisual gathering where sound, moving image and spatial intervention merge into a single immersive environment.\\n\\nPresented by Altered Images and Iklectik, the event marks a new collaboration between two platforms committed to experimental art, underground music and immersive audiovisual experiences in London.\\n\\nFeaturing headline performance from Years of Denial alongside Machine Woman, Inda Flo, Gertie Adelaido and more, the programme moves between live sets, DJ performances, projected visuals, installation work and evolving digital scenography.\\n\\nExpect shifting atmospheres, holographic textures, projected architectures, noise, bodies, light and movement — from dusk till dawn.\\n\\nIMAGE / SOUND / MOVEMENT\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/wwpx8n-altered-levels-vol1-ft-years-of-denial-26th-jun-iklectik-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":367,\"name\":\"SBLMNALSIGNL #002\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-26T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0e2831ff602ad3d2f575fcb5d3be43f2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SBLMNALSIGNL ROUND 2 INCOMING\\n26.06.26 // ORMSIDE PROJECTS\\n\\nintroducing a seriously stacked lineup for the 2nd edition of SBLMNALSIGNL..\\n\\n⟡ @dmx_krew live electro set\\n⟡ @soundtransparent special live set for orson recording’s 20th anniversary\\n⟡ berlin based savy records head @ida_savy\\n\\nbrought to u by\\n@ara_u____ ~ @nostaticautomatic\\n@medallionmanmusic ~ @looselipsevents\\n@taniaatyabi ~ @_ tempaural _\\n\\nSAVE THE DATE\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2404427\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":624,\"name\":\"Pride: Wellness Festival \",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"85c8a272330ccd13af71cb840f332581.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sound baths, saunas, somatic dance, poetry, yoga, tarot, massage… the list goes on - We’re celebrating queer talent and expression all Pride weekend at Innervisions Alchemy, 27 \\u0026 28 June.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://momence.com/Innervisions-Alchemy/Pride---Wellness-Festival-/137516930?skipPreview=true\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":670,\"name\":\"Seven Sisters Market Summer Fiesta\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"272fc0a8cac9d8374e5167601207f472.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"☀️🎶 And now for the grand finale of our Community Summer Festival... Summer Fiesta en el Barrio! 🎶☀️\\n\\nJoin us for two days of music, culture, creativity and community at Seven Sisters Market as we celebrate the start of summer and the incredible energy that makes this neighbourhood so special.\\n\\n✨ DJs and live performances\\n💄 Make-up stations \\u0026 gemstones\\n💃 Dance and community activities\\n🌎 A cultural installation celebrating the people, stories and heritage that make our community unique\\n🍴 Amazing food from our market traders\\n🎉 And plenty more surprises!\\n\\nWhether you're warming up before the concert or simply looking for a great weekend in Tottenham, there's something here for everyone.\\n\\n📍 Seven Sisters Market\\n📅 27–28 June\\n\\n🔥 Stay tuned\\n\\nMusic. Culture. Community. En el barrio. ❤️🌴🎶\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":562,\"name\":\"56a Infoshop 35th Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7c6b6420b42857fb8a5ae25856001286.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Come one come all!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":529,\"name\":\"DEPTFORD JUNCTION SATURDAY SCHOOL - EVERYWHERE AT ONCE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fda6a02d436a3a065d9ddc5b20588441.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This June, Deptford Junction is taking part in Everywhere At Once powered by The National Lottery. It’s the UK’s biggest music festival on your doorstep: 1000+ gigs, 400+ venues, 1 weekend. Come and celebrate live music with us from 26–28 June.\\n\\n#EverywhereAtOnce #BecauseOfYou\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":375,\"name\":\"INFERNO: The Relaunch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8979f75c9fbb0b06b24ea1e1c47230ce.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"INFERNO: The Relaunch\\n\\nPart I of The Red Summer\\nSaturday 27 June\\n3pm - 11pm\\nThe Distillery N17\\n\\nINFERNO returns.\\n\\nNot bigger. Closer.\\n\\nAfter eleven years of building one of London’s most recognisable queer dancefloors, we begin a new era at our new long term home in Tottenham.\\n\\nThis is a soft reset. Smaller capacity. Sharper focus. Daylight through the windows. Bass you feel in your ribs. Bodies moving without spectacle.\\n\\nFor those who were with us at The Yard, you’ll remember: for three years we didn’t announce lineups. The trust was the point.\\n\\nWe’re returning to that.\\n\\nNo advance announcements. No hierarchy on a poster. The music will speak for itself. The room will shape the energy. What matters is who we are together, not who is headlining.\\n\\nExpect summer techno. Expect sweat. Expect controlled hedonism. Expect intimacy that only happens when a space is built on community rather than scale.\\n\\nThe Distillery holds roughly a third of our previous capacity. This will sell out. If you want to be part of this first chapter of The Red Summer, move early.\\n\\nThis is not about spectacle. It is about intention.\\n\\nINFERNO: The Relaunch is the first of four gatherings across June, July, August and September.\\n\\nOpen arms. Open dancefloor. A new era.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://inferno.eventcube.io/events/94045/inferno-the-relaunch\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":674,\"name\":\"AFRIKAN MOVEMENTS #11 \\\"Freedom Dance\\\" – ALPHA \\u0026 OMEGA SOUND SYSTEM AND ALKEBULAN AFRIKAN WARRIORS SOUND SYSTEM\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"52d99e174fd80cfda36a0a4020cbbd7d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"🎵 Alpha \\u0026 Omega Sound System, Alkebulan Afrikan Warriors Sound System, Prince Zebulon, Empress Jasmine, Princess Warriyah Linn, Spiritual Dub Doctor, Mark, Ricky\\n\\n£10 OTD cash and card\\n\\nFood and drink available\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":495,\"name\":\"JHL, Hyph11e, \\u0026 Silver Waves ft. Angelina Toros\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"643ec0a647c57871a5d86ff8201c91ba.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The event will feature a live A/V performance by Silver Waves and Angelina Toros, expanding on the sonic and visual world of Aninstar, a brain-melting amalgam of orchestra, pop, noise and drone that cultivates widescreen soundscapes rapidly shifting between the hellish and the heavenly.\\n\\nThe night will also include the London premiere of a new live set by JHL, developed from their upcoming mixtape. Built around dark, noisy and angular production with flashes of pop sensibility cutting through, the performance will be intimate and stripped back: voice, production and presence at the centre.\\n\\nFollowing the live performances, the evening continues with a DJ set by Hyph11E, affiliated with SVBKVLT.\\n\\nPlease be aware these is a flashing light warning for this event.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/f6c84f88bf12?dice_id=f6c84f88bf12\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":630,\"name\":\"The Man with the Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-27T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"30d0948649ed9bd7182e3683dd4b7f35.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, with Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza, Andrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\n\\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films Production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":575,\"name\":\"Sagome 028: Nuke Watch (album launch) w/ Peter Zummo + Heta Bilaletdin + Mag (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"20b6263d0a7d17b6194a8a317db7841f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To mark their new release ‘Fusion’ on Sagome, Nuke Watch perform at Cafe Oto for the first time ever and will be joined by trombonist Peter Zummo for part of their set. Plus, a live blending sampling, voice, and electronics from Finnish multimedia artist Heta Bilaletdin, and a DJ set from Testing the Water honcho, Mag.\\n\\n\\n£16 OTD // £14 Advance // £10 Members\\n\\n~~~\\n\\nNUKE WATCH\\n\\nNuke Watch is a New York based collective that specializes in a mix of free-jazz fusion and textured polyrhythmic Fourth World propulsion. The long running friendship and psychic connection of its founders Chris Hontos \\u0026 Aaron Anderson (aka Beat Detectives) enhance their signature ritualistic rhythms, mutant modular synthesis, nimble keyboard runs, vibrant sampling and unidentified skronk.\\n\\nThey have released records on The Trilogy Tapes, Post Present Medium, Patience/Impatience, Commend/RVNG and Moon Glyph. They will be touring the UK in support of their new album “Fusion” out this summer on the London based label Sagome\\n\\n“[Nuke Watch] could be called world music in the sense that if you folded up the world into a funnel and shook it and made everybody slide down onto a plate full of people they didn’t grow up with, they might end up making this.” - Sasha Frere-Jones, 2025.\\n\\n\\nHETA BILALETDIN\\n\\nHeta Bilaletdin is a multidisciplinary artist from Finland, who works with sound, experimental music, and moving image. Her sonic compositions blend home and field recordings, singing, electronic and acoustic instruments, samples, found objects and tapes to create collages, dusty beats, deconstructed pop and musique concrète. In addition to live performance, she works with sound through exhibitions, sonic sculptures, radio pieces, and workshops. Her visual work consists of films and installations, gravitating toward poetic forms of resistance, subtle connections, rituals, patterns, power structures and hidden choreographies in our coexistence. \\n\\n\\nPETER ZUMMO\\n\\nPeter Zummo is a composer and trombonist who works with the trombone and other instruments in multiple genres. He collaborates with artists in related media, including composers, poets, bandleaders, choreographers, directors, and filmmakers. He functions equally as a supporting character and a principal artist.\\n\\nProduction credits include Indian Ocean’s Treehouse/School Bell, with Arthur Russell, on Sleeping Bag; H*E*R, by Yvette Perez, on Persian Cardinal; Zummo With an X, on Loris Records, New World and Optimo Music; Experimenting With Household Chemicals, on XI; Downtown Only, on Lovely; Arthur’s Landing, on Strut; Lateral Pass and Frame Loop, on Foom; Dress Code, on Optimo; Deep Drive, Tone Bone Kone, and Deep Drive 2+ on Unheard Of Hope; Watermelon Sun, with Tom Skinner, on Brownswood; Thinking A View, with Eddie Ruscha, on Fourth Sounds. What’s Not Enough About That, with Bex Burch, on Vula Viel; Slybersonic Tromosome, with Tom Hamilton, on Penumbra; Second Spring OST, and contributions to Wind Layers and Duet Layers, on 7K.\\n\\n\\nMAG\\n\\nMag is a London-based DJ and sometime promoter, running experimental-leaning gig/club nights as Testing the Water. Behind the decks she works with off-centre rhythm, piecing together sound in a way that favours tension, negative space and the edges of club form.\\n\\n~~~\\n\\nAndrea Campisi is supported by the Early Career Promoter Fund which is managed by PRS Foundation and funded by Arts Council England using Supporting Grassroots Music funding from DCMS.\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/sagome-028/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":600,\"name\":\"CLUB PLEASURE Presents: Heatwave\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f7a8f055a23a29696b95054f4c648971.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"CLUB PLEASURE Presents: Heatwave \\n\\nWe're back for a sexy summer edition, serving up a second helping of musical heaters for a hot, sweaty boogie at BGWMC for our CLUB PLEASURE Presents: Heatwave!\\n\\nBack under the heart of Bethnal Green Working Men's Club, 42-46 Pollard Row, London E2 6NB on Saturday 27th June 2026 9pm-3am.\\n\\n** LINE UP **\\n\\nFidel (BASH) \\nMilk Shandy (Club Tantrum, Dalson Superstore, Leatherette) \\nStav B (Dyke March, No.11)\\nPUBLICTOILETDISCO (TIMC, Locomotive Disco)\\n\\n+ Barbs, Jane Norman \\u0026 Dak Attack\\n\\n \\n\\nEARLY DOORS DRINK DEALS \\u0026 HAPPY HOUR at BGWMC. \\n\\n \\n\\n*at CLUB PLEASURE, expect to move and groove soundtracked by a selection of east london's finest DJ's spinning sexy sounds of house, disco, italo, hi-nrg + more. *\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2454650\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":310,\"name\":\"MouseFX Live In London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-27T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c50a9b37bd1305e40612baa3191a60cb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"*** VENUE CHANGED *** -\\u003e Oitij-Jo Art Space\\nCongee Sounds and Heavy Hong Kong Presents: MouseFX Live In London\\n\\nCantonese Reggae Dub singer MouseFX unites his mother tongue with messages of Love and Humanity — bridging global connection through ancestral vibrations, while staying true to the Rastafarian spirit and values.\\n\\nA cornerstone of the Hong Kong Reggae and Dub scene, MouseFX has released numerous collaborations including Skunga Kong (Jamaica) and deDUBros (Italy), most recently on the fiery new single Judgment Day, alongside his own original dub steppa productions.\\n\\nA rare appearance for the London dub community, featuring local sound system Trinity All Stars, Mr Tee and Congee Sounds — come join us for a night of East Asian dub flavour. \\n\\nLine Up:\\nMouseFX | Chakka C | Mr Tee | Trinity All Stars | Heavy HK Sound\\n\\nRoots · Dub · Reggae · Steppa\\n27th June 2026\\nNEW VENUE: Oitij-Jo Art Space\\n10pm – 2am\\n£10 online · £15 on the door\\n\\n廣東話雷鬼第一人 MouseFX，自1990年起一直活躍於香港地下音樂場景。由 Ice Stone 2、Crazy Lion、Sensi Lion 狻猊，演變成今日鼠叔叔獨樹一幟的個人聲音風格。\\n\\nMouseFX 始終堅守 Rastafari 的價值觀，推崇人性之美。無論處境多麼艱難，他無分國界、無分膚色，以廣東話為愛、和平與團結發聲。\\n\\n在牙買加錄製的專輯 《MouseFX in Jamaica》在港引起巨大迴響。近年與意大利製作單位 deDUBros 合作的作品風味更貼近根源雷鬼 Dub 路線。其個人製作的 Steppa 作品亦日趨成熟，最新單曲《活著實在美麗》更得到東南亞 Dub 巨人 Red I 操刀 Dub Mix，再上一層樓。\\n\\n來自遠東的根源音樂使者 MouseFX，攜同長期合作單位 Heavy HK、Chakka C，闊別8年再度踏足歐洲。連同倫敦土炮 sound system Trinity All Stars、Mr Tee 及 粥聲 Congee Sounds，共聚一堂。\\n\\n倫敦阿鼠 Live Gig，不容錯過！\\n\\n演出陣容：\\nMouseFX | Chakka C | Mr Tee | Trinity All Stars | Heavy HK Sound\\n\\nRoots · Dub · Reggae · Steppa\\n\\n2026年6月27日\\nOitij-Jo Art，倫敦\\n晚上10時 – 凌晨2時\\n網上購票 £10 · 場館購票 £15\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":633,\"name\":\"Haringey Screens Queer Cinema for Palestine\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-28T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"086b83855f0ba51ef78810d3eb643ca3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Queer Cinema for Palestine (QCP) announces No Pride in Genocide (June 2026). Local screening of films selected for QCP \\u0026 conversations.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/haringey-screens-queer-cinema-for-palestine-registration-1990078097160\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":649,\"name\":\"Black Obsidian Sound System 8th Birthday!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-28T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ed8c9de98cae03f84a9e793eafe859dc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"8 years of the sound system and an exciting summer ahead. \\nDjs, performances, games, cake, the whole shebang\\nCome shake a leg. \\n\\n3pm - 10:30pm \\n\\n97 Stoke Newington High Street (the new Common Press Book bar location.)\\n\\n\\n\\nLineup : \\n\\nDJ Flight \\n\\nAin Bailey \\n\\nCarma \\n\\nRabz \\n\\nrare treat  \\n\\nSippin' T \\n\\n \\n\\n+ B.O.S.S' very own:\\ndj dae\\n\\nmellowdramatics \\n\\nsecret lover\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nBio\\nBlack Obsidian Sound System (B.O.S.S.) was established in the summer of 2018 with the intention of bringing together a community of queer, trans and non-binary black and people of colour involved in art, sound and radical activism. Following in the legacies of sound system culture they wanted to learn, build and sustain a resource for our collective struggles. The black-led system, based in London, is available to use or rent by community groups and others with the purpose of amplifying and connecting them.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37038/boss-8th-birthday\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":661,\"name\":\"Save Lewisham Shopping Centre Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-28T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"138bbafa42035bc205445c7287eeeb87.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On the 28th June 3-10pm, we will be dancing the day away with the sounds of young local DJs \\u0026 performers at Piehouse Coop in Deptford. Expect day party vibes… plenty dancing… a special raffle with some very special prizes… all whilst celebrating \\u0026 supporting the local campaign fighting to save Lewisham shopping centre from the rampant gentrification spreading far and wide across the city.\\n\\nThe work that is being done to fight off this redevelopment is hard graft… it takes love, it takes time \\u0026 it takes $$$MONEY$$$!!!\\n\\nSo join us!...\\n\\n📅 SUNDAY 28th JUNE\\n⏰ 3-10PM\\n📍 PIEHOUSE COOP SE8 5HD\\n\\n🎟️ Tickets:\\nStandard £8\\nLow-income £5\\nSolidarity ticket £15\\n\\nSuper solidarity ticket £25\\nBestest ally ever ticket £50\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37005/save-lewisham-shopping-centre-piehouse-coop-fundraiser\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":557,\"name\":\"Nicola Genovese: Infinite Stage – Chapter I\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-28T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8a3fdc137f3dac0b19fe4cedcda5896a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A performance by Nicola Genovese\\nwith:\\nMagda Drozd\\nJeonghan Yoon\\nAlice Köppel\\nLelah Neary\\nArianna Ransley\\nUmlilo \\n\\nInfinite Stage is a solo exhibition conceived as a dormant stage, activated twice through a 45-minute live performance. The works on view inhabit multiple states: while existing as sculptures within the exhibition space, they transform into scenery and props during the performances. Video works function as the skeletal framework of the performance timeline, shaping its rhythm, pacing, and progression.\\n\\nAt its core, Infinite Stage examines the relationship between death and digitality. In post-capitalist society, the denial of death is already deeply embedded within systems of consumption, preservation, and endless production. Through contemporary technology, this denial reaches a new dimension. “Ghostbots” — chatbots generated from a deceased person’s emails, photographs, memories, and digital traces — enable the living to sustain conversations with the dead, blurring the boundaries between memory, simulation, and presence.\\nThe performance unfolds through a sequence of interconnected scenes in which live music, dance, readings, and video interactions become entangled. Rather than operating as a multidisciplinary project, Infinite Stage is driven by the accumulation and layering of media. Its aesthetic oscillates between a baroque density of forms and silent, meditative intervals, creating a sustained tension between excess and stillness.\\n\\nSunday 28 June – 6pm (sharp)\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://luma.com/infinitestage?e=evt-ytMofqTcHOFp6fK\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":642,\"name\":\"Linden Archives - In Photos and Words\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-28T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7d839f3bed54c8371096a9eb35ee7b5d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Stuart Linden Rhodes 'Linden' was the roving reporter for APN and the Gay Times during the early to mid 1990s. Covering mainly the north of England his columns for those magazines were titled: Out \\u0026 About with Linden. The use of a pseudonym was due to concerns generated by draconian Clause 28 legislation sanctioned by the Tory government of the era.\\n\\nStuart Linden Rhodes was also a lecturer at a local further education college, the pseudonym 'Linden' adopted to protect his career in teaching. \\n\\nAt home in North Yorkshire during the covid lockdowns of 2020-21, Stuart Linden Rhodes established the Linden Archives, an online window into the thriving gay scene of the 1990’s. Scanning and digitising thousands of 35mm negatives of queer scene photographs. Not only to preserve his work but also to give the people in the photographs the opportunity to access them after almost three decades of them languishing in his loft. Linden Archives the Instagram account has since gained a substantial following and continues to grow. \\n\\nStuart’s photography seeks to encapsulate a people defiant in the face of the AIDS crises and discriminatory laws, alongside uninhibited photographs of such as Vivienne Westwood, Jean Paul Gaultier, Derek Jarman, Take That, Julian Clary, Peter Tatchell, Paul O'Grady, East 17 and many more. He photographed not only the nightlife but also major events such as Gay Pride and Mr Gay UK, exploring an explosion of growth in a diverse northern UK queer scene and club culture. A period which was also marked by HIV and AIDS, homophobia and discriminatory laws. \\n\\nTo date his photography has featured on BBC television \\u0026 radio interviews and in numerous magazines and newspapers including The Guardian. Imagery from the archives have been exhibited at galleries across the UK from Elgin in Scotland to Blackpool, Coventry and London.\\n\\nHis photography has also been acquired by Manchester City Art Gallery for their permanent collection.\\n\\nThe Stuart Linden Rhodes archive is now part of The John Rylands Library collections in Manchester and available for research purposes. \\n\\nOn the 28th of June, Stuart Linden Rhodes will be sharing and discussing some pieces of his archives at the Dalston Site of The Common Press.\\n\\nCome and join us for an evening of conversation, with a Q\\u0026A that will follow a slideshow of iconic pictures Stuart has taken over the years.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/36582/linden-archives-in-photos-and-words\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":423,\"name\":\"Album launch: Robert Stillman Margate Radio Strings + Drummers  With support from Paul Camo + James Jordan Johnson \",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-28T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-28T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f0fc60c6dd04bad9aa21eace103ae92f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\\"Margate Radio Strings + Drummers\\\" is Robert Stillman's suite of chamber music stemming from the archive of his monthly solo improvisation broadcasts for Margate Radio. To create the work, Stillman listened through to over 5 years of his monthly shows-which  ranged from solo saxophone explorations, to ethereal DX-7 atmosphere, to punishing mixer feedback- and  selected a series of his favorite excerpts, transcribing and arranging them for 'low string quartet' of violin, two cellos, and double bass, and giving the drummers free reign to improvise within this dynamic landscape. The result is a hypnotic, dreamlike journey through Stillman's musical mind, animated by the brilliance of six musicians with whom he's worked regularly in various contexts over the past decade: Raven Bush (violin); Kareem Dayes and Francesca Ter-Berg (cello); Tom Herbert (bass); Tom Skinner and Sean Carpio (drums and percussion). This event marks the release of the limited edition double-vinyl of the music from Margate Radio. \\n\\nPaul Camo and James Jordan Johnson collaborate through live sound performance, using sampling, live instrumentation and found text to form new, sometimes legible and sometimes illegible, relationships between genres and themes. The session unfolds across four CDJs, moving between structure, disruption and shared listening.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":662,\"name\":\"Open Piehouse\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-29T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-29T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"39c8563f05bcbd29e33e018f58819549.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We are so excited to announce that the Piehouse will be undergoing some (much needed) renovations! Come down for some DJ sets and a chance to get a first look at the brand new Piehouse.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/event/536mll-open-piehouse-29th-jun-piehouse-co-op-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":404,\"name\":\"Bend It Like Beckham\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-29T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-29T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f06b30d9b34e014775da3026190af9ea.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a viewing of Bend It Like Beckham (Dir: Gurinder Chadha, UK) as part of a month long series of screenings which celebrate marginalised voices through the prism of football to coincide with the 2026 Men's FIFA World Cup.\\n\\nJess Bhamra dreams of playing professional football, but her Sikh parents have plans for her: a law degree and a marriage. Jules, a white female striker, spots Jess playing football and invites her to join the local women's team.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":627,\"name\":\"Puppet Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-30T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-30T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c8dec355ac16c9b52a9634a37635deea.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Communal Clay Puppet Workshop\\n\\nUsing clay and slips you will be able to create a puppet, character, monster or creature.\\n\\nYou will be able to add colour and depth to your work with wild clay slips we have collected from around South London. And the option to have the piece fired and glazed with wood ash glaze.\\n\\nThe session will last 2 hours.\\n\\nTheses workshops will be more focused on the tactility of playing, practicing and learning sculpture techniques. There is no pressure to make a ‘finished product’ or ‘perfect piece’.\\n\\nAt the end of the workshop if you wish to have your piece fired and glazed, we ask you pay an additional £10 to cover firing costs, glaze materials \\u0026 transport of your work.\\n\\nAny leftover clay at the end of the session will be recycled for future use, minimising wastage and keeping our workshops sustainable.\\n\\nPricing:\\nWe are updating our pricing scale, in an effort to continue to make our workshops accessible and affordable we are testing out a new ticketing format with two options: Standard and Concession tickets.\\n\\nPlease choose the ticket option that is appropriate for yourself.\\n\\nCommunal Clay CIC is a not-for-profit organisation, all profits made after covering core costs will be used to run more community workshops.\\n\\nConcessions Include:\\n-People receiving benefits Jobseeker's Allowance / Universal Credit / Housing Benefit\\n-Young people 16-21\\n-Disabled\\n-students from working class backgrounds\\n-carers\\n-single parents\\n\\nAll fired and glazed work will be ready to collect in roughly 4 weeks from SET Social, please be patient as the cold weather affects drying and firing times.\\nSometimes this may be longer or shorter depending on the weather and temperature as these effect drying speeds.\\n\\nPLEASE READ: Clay and ceramics are fragile materials until fired and glazed, on occasion things can break or become damaged during the drying and firing process', Communal Clay is not responsible for any damage that may occur during these.\\n\\nTickets are refundable if you message us 48+ hours in advance of the event date\\nRefunds - you will be fully refunded for the cost of the ticket but the booking fee will not be refunded\\nUnder 18's must be accompanied by an adult\\nCommunal Clay is not responsible for work that breaks during firing.\\nYour work must be collected within 4 weeks of being notified it is ready to collect from SET Social. After the 4 weeks unclaimed work will not be our responsibility. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":660,\"name\":\"CEASELESS VI\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5c380737fdf3cee3a703059633905755.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ceaseless – created by Siren \\u0026 Alexander Montserrat circa 2023- has carved out space for emerging artists in London working outside the usual circuits.\\n\\nNow in its sixth iteration, it has quietly become a consistent platform for artists operating between experimental music and club culture.\\n\\nThe series refuses fixed geography, moving nomadically between basements, churches, and club spaces across the city - each venue chosen for its sonic capacity rather than its postcode.\\nCeaseless programs around intensity and intent. The nights are built as much for endurance as for pleasure. It's pulled together a committed audience hungry for music that takes risks, and artists willing to privilege sensation and instinct over marketability.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2454564\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":667,\"name\":\"Draw your boss: Street Scenes\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-30T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99ea9e66a7c1964132651590b1e7dccb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For this event we will be inviting members of the public to draw portraits (sympathetic, caricatural or otherwise) of their bosses.\\n\\nStreet Scenes runs events in public space for strangers to meet. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":666,\"name\":\"Draw your boss\",\"start_time\":\"2026-06-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-06-30T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ae6d93c7a680180bfcda27c8af206638.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For this event we will be inviting members of the public to draw portraits (sympathetic, caricatural or otherwise) of their bosses.\\n\\nStreet Scenes runs events in public space for strangers to meet.\\n\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":665,\"name\":\"SELF STORAGE (Private View)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-02T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-02T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a5f5ba66828eef6b9f5de5735676ffe9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An exhibition exploring the cupboards, basements, and lofts of artists and museums.\\n\\nFor our next upcoming exhibition SELF STORAGE Sweet ‘Art is collaborating with workers from London Museum, as well as the historic building, House of Annetta. In this exhibition, nine artists will be taking inspiration from their museum workplace, as well as from the fabric and content of the House of Annetta: marrying themes of personal and national ‘storage’. \\n\\nAs museum workers, the exhibiting artists engage with a vast repository of the nation’s storage of historical artifacts and objects daily, whether we frame such objects as simply the nation’s ‘knick-knacks’ or significant treasures. Each artist investigates a collective understanding that this work is not merely a neutral gathering of objects, but a practice which tells much about our society. That ‘storage’ is a way in which groups can construct identity, archive collective memory, or privilege the narratives of some with public display, while ‘storing’ away the stories of others from a public gaze. We as individuals in personal spaces, also confer value by retaining, rather than disposing of certain objects, and use acts of ‘storage’ to make space for objects or ideas to be present, ordered or manageable. \\n\\nFor this show, artists Chantal Makar, Edward Welch, John Chase, Jordan Furze, Mariam Hussein, Nikki Braunton, Noa Smith, Rianna Shanāz, Riva Boutylkova and Sam Rees have drawn upon their existing art practice to create new, site specific work utilizing materials from their own personal stores of physical items as well as personal narratives, as well as from Annetta’s basement, responding to the building as a repository of history which has been restored and reclaimed.\\n\\nJoin us on Thursday 2nd July for the opening party, with drinks kindly sponsored by Crate Brewery and Sipmith Gin, performances and more! We are asking people to book either an early slot (arriving at 6pm) or later slot (7.30pm) just so we have an idea of numbers in the space. As the house has strict capacity guidelines, we might have to ask you to wait if we reach capacity.\\n\\nAbout the donation option: Our coffers are currently empty so are funding this event from our personal money. We'd love to reclaim our funds AND make a donation to House of Annetta which is a registered charity. Please donate what you can. To give you an idea, if everyone we expect to attend the PV donates £4, we reclaim our personal costs. If everyone donates £5 or more, we can also give a donation to HoA.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/36057/self-storage-private-view\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":698,\"name\":\"NAFS x LOGMA : Pride Rooted in Solidarity\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-02T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-02T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4580c9680971275ea5b7504a340ea5d9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for an evening of chai, dessert, conversation and community.\\n\\n\\n\\nThis Pride, we come together in solidarity with Queer SWANA (South West Asian and North African) communities across the region and diaspora. As many members of our community navigate displacement, financial hardship, isolation and uncertainty, we believe that gathering together remains a powerful act of care.\\n\\n\\n\\nHosted by NAFS and generously supported by Logma, this event is an opportunity to connect, reflect and build community in a welcoming and inclusive space.\\n\\n\\n\\nAttendance is free, and donations are warmly encouraged.\\n\\n\\n\\nDonations will support the ongoing work of NAFS, helping us create and sustain spaces for Queer SWANA people to gather, connect, create and find community. Your support enables us to continue building spaces rooted in connection, care and belonging.\\n\\n\\n\\nWhere does my donation go?\\n\\nDonations support the ongoing work of NAFS, including community gatherings, cultural programming, workshops, mutual support initiatives, and creating safer spaces for Queer SWANA people in London. At a time when many members of our community are navigating displacement, financial hardship, isolation and uncertainty, your support helps ensure these spaces remain accessible and community-led.\\n\\nOpen to Queer SWANA people, friends and allies.\\n\\n📍 Logma, Hackney\\n📅 2 July 2026\\n⏰ 18:00–20:30\\n\\nIf you are unable to attend but would still like to support our work, donations are greatly appreciated.\\n\\nPride rooted in solidarity.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.zeffy.com/en-GB/ticketing/nafs-x-logma-pride-rooted-in-solidarity\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":653,\"name\":\"Inframetropolitan Systems: Dhanveer Singh Brar on Gil Scott Heron.\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-02T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e9d19e94edcb7cb6f9a919de6589a549.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Second of three sessions on the musical production of space and memory, space and politics.\\n\\nDhanveer Singh Brar on Gil Scott Heron.\\n\\n!!! GUCU STRIKE FUNDRAISER !!!\\n\\nGOLDSMITHS UCU HAS VOTED TO MOVE TO INDEFINITE STRIKE FOLLOWING THE IMPOSITION OF 100% PAY DEDUCTIONS.\\n\\nTHIS TALK IS FREE BUT IF YOU ARE ABLE YOU CAN DONATE TO THE GUCU STRIKE FUND.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":696,\"name\":\"Women and the Spanish Civil War, with Meirian Jump\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-02T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c84fd6f51eb98462ef6867c99741afec.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Battle of Cable Street brought into sharp focus the threat of fascism on the home front and inspired many to volunteer for the International Brigades to fight Franco in Spain. Famous accounts of the British response to the Spanish Civil War—including those by Orwell and Laurie Lee—tend to focus on men and the military experience. In reality, there was a much broader movement in solidarity with the Spanish Republic, encompassing medical aid, the care of refugee children, and community organising—in which women played a leading role.\\n\\nDiscover the stories of these anti-fascist women, too often hidden from history.\\n\\nMeirian Jump will share material and reflections from the unique collection of the Marx Memorial Library.\\n\\nMeirian Jump is the Director of the Marx Memorial Library (MML) \\u0026 Workers’ School. An archivist, she has worked at MML—home to the most significant and comprehensive archive on the Spanish Civil War in the UK—for over a decade. She is also the granddaughter of International Brigadier Jimmy Jump, whose memoir, The Fighter Fell in Love, was published by The Clapton Press in 2021.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/36180/women-and-the-spanish-civil-war-with-meirian-jump\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":689,\"name\":\"Archiving From Below: We Won’t Move! (into your institutional collection) with Lani Hanna\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-02T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ab06ddd4d74ada3d5ac3b98b6f8210cb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This workshop considers counter-institutional archiving as a tool to fight gentrification. Counter-institutional archives have a dual struggle in rapidly gentrifying cities, first the labor to archive resistance histories and second to resist displacement and institutional incorporation themselves. In this workshop we will discuss several examples of counter-institutional archives that simultaneously operate as social and political infrastructure and consider how they manage to negotiate the maintenance of their space and improvise institutional relationships. Through this discussion we will also look at various tactics from the collections of these spaces that highlight resistance to gentrification.\\n\\nOver the past decade or more, Lani Hanna has centered the relationship of counter-institutional archives and gentrification both in volunteering with Interference Archive in NYC and as a researcher. The workshop will be built around several key themes and examples from this research as well as a more informal and open collective discussion and brainstorming.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.maydayrooms.org/e/93/archiving-from-below-we-wont-move-into-your-institutional-collection-with-lani-hanna\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":658,\"name\":\"Adventures In Dub #14\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-02T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"23caceef4da9b7e20953cd07c2848d56.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SLICKnBOBBY's monthly Dub night in Brixton alongside DJ Snuff and special guests. Food available from EN ROOT. Expect a warm friendly environment and full live sound system.\\n\\nDoors at 7pm. First live set 8pm, second live set 10pm. DJ's until midnight.\\n\\nNOTE:\\nTicket price inc. membership to Club Silly giving access to members benefits.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2466465\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":558,\"name\":\"Al Wootton (Holy Tongue / Moin)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-02T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-02T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b84811bbb5c8b18c22e302371125a65b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This isn’t a club night.\\n\\nIt’s a space to listen, to be present, to feel.\\n\\nA rare London session bringing together three boundary-pushing live acts; spanning deconstructed dub techno, live sax improvisation, and abstract electronic songwriting.\\n\\nAL WOOTTON (Holy Tongue / Moin) • Stripped-back, system-focused dub and rhythm. Rare headline live AV set, from the artist formerly known as Deadboy.\\n\\nBEN VINCE (AD93) • Otherworldly sax explorations and ever-evolving textures\\n\\nPYTKO • Emotional, voice-led experimental electronica\\n\\nLimited capacity. Ritual Space.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2393413\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":691,\"name\":\"Life of the Party LIVE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-03T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"021bba9a44f24beda4eedf9dc8d0bbed.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"*** LIVE SHOW AT PELICAN HOUSE, LONDON ***\\n\\nSpecial guests: Josh Virasami (London Renters Union), Aydin Dikerdem (Southwark Councillor), Ash Sarkar (Journalist)\\n\\nJoin us for our first ever live show at Pelican House, our spiritual home in East London. With three very special guests - soon to be announced - join us for a drink and we'll take you through the hot left party news and analysis of the last month. \\n\\nDoors 6pm.\\nShow starts 6:30pm.\\nBar until 10:30pm. \\n\\nTickets\\nStandard: £5\\nSolidarity: £10\\n\\nWe're all volunteers, and every pound goes towards keeping the podcast rolling. Please be as generous as you can! If you want to come but genuinely can't afford a fiver, email us at podlifeoftheparty@gmail.com. \\n\\nAbout Life of the Party\\n\\nLife of the Party takes you inside the debates, personalities and politics shaping new left parties in the UK. Hosts Shanice, Jonas and Joe bring critical analysis, unfiltered takes, and lively debates about left parties and the future of the UK left. \\n\\nAbout Pelican House\\n\\nPelican House is a social centre for worker organising, movement building, experimental arts \\u0026 culture. This is a Pelican House Social Club event. Buying a ticket will automatically sign you up as a member (for free), and means you can enjoy drinks at our bar.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/lifeoftheparty/2251612\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":532,\"name\":\"Décalé\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-03T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"aec00b5d408f532ac264ad4b5193d491.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\n​​Décalé makes its first appearance at Cafe Oto with an evening of sonic and visual experiments, bringing together four artists working with moving image, live performance, improvisation, inner and outer landscapes.\\n\\nSimeon Barclay will perform An Ode To a Crow — “Come on an excursion through Yorkshire, along arterial roads that bear witness to an industrial legacy, birthing a sonic heartbeat that serves as a symphony to didactic desire, memory and transformation. Through words spoken, and a sonic and visual landscape, I shall doff a hat to the purveyors of electronic pop in the region, and the high fashion that was their armour.”\\n\\nJuline Hadaya’s Double Life performance will explore the entangled self suspended between two timelines: the past and the future.\\n\\nHannah Catherine Jones will present a largely improvised set, channelling grief from recent bereavements through a multi-instrumental set-up, including theremin, synthesisers, loopers, fx and samples.\\n\\nDrawing from her multiple known and unknown aliases, Laila Sakini will perform a mini set utilising percussion, voice, piano, found sound, electronics and whatever’s close to hand.\\n\\nDécalé is programmed by Leila Arenou, Kadeem Oak and Chooc Ly Tan.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/decale/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":668,\"name\":\"Hoxton Cabal: MAÏS, vene.tia, Smudge Proof (Vinyl Only)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"15bcfba5d4849bf312ffa266744581e7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Cabal favourite MAÏS takes the reins for July, curating a stellar line up of London-based underground talent.  MAÏS is joined by Voices Radio resident, Venetia, along with long-time friend of the Cabal, Smudge Proof.  All vinyl, all night.  See you in the Cabal.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":597,\"name\":\"Twin System\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c2efd85bb29d0247317f2cdf11ebdd1f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Floor Length Skirts \\u0026 caapi\\n\\nTwo pals whose music selection we revere \\n\\nCollector + digital archivist FLS is the creator of the glorious 'Unruly Sun' mixtape we released last October, a youtube channel for the ages \\u0026 a wealth of mixes all over the place\\n                            (https://twinsystem.bandcamp.com/album/unruly-sun) \\n\\ncaapi is one part of 'Somewhere Press', runs their own equally special project 'blush', and is the next provider of a mixtape on TS which we will be sharing soon\\n\\n9:30 - 3am\\nJuly 3rd\\n\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":659,\"name\":\"Expert Death 11: Shed, Bake, Fig + Davidson\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c64bd452fca8c4aeca8c81394bb76351.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Expert Death are back. Bi-monthly events live from our new home of Ormside Projects.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2420612\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":664,\"name\":\"Tripsitter invites Mr Assister \\u0026 Shimmy \",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T22:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T03:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"61b69f845480bd0f189a50faef9599db.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"No frills. No filler. Just sound and Psychedelic energy\\n\\nA late one built for those who know - Tripsitter welcomes Mr Assister, a seamless selector who runs the label beam records which is well worth checking out with some great releases out already. Joining him we have 2/3 of the Shimmy London DJs, Professor Roth \\u0026 Dirigible who will be digging through their collections to share some under the radar gems with you. Joining them we have Frank Hawles, J. Fredrick and Tripsitter showing what they are all about after the first event.\\n\\nExpect stripped-back energy, deep cuts, and a floor that stays locked from start to finish.\\n\\nLow light. Heavy rotation. Proper system pressure.\\nThis is for the heads.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":596,\"name\":\"CLUB SMUT PRESENTS: BLOW MY DOPAMINE! (Official Robyn Afterparty)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"40f69d28cf9f4e0c58762ad386e65cc7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"OMG! ARE YOU READY TO HAVE YOUR DOPAMINE BLOWN?\\n\\nSMUT PRESS IS DELIGHTED TO PRESENT THE OFFICIAL AFTERPARTY FOR ROBYN'S LONDON DATE OF HER SEXISTENTIAL TOUR.\\n\\n\\nFRIDAY 3RD JULY 2026\\n\\n11PM-5AM\\n\\nRADIAL, 39B MARKFIELD ROAD, LONDON, N15 4QA\\n\\nFEATURING:\\n\\nLO-LOW\\nJAY DUNCAN\\nBYRON YEATES\\n\\n\\nSEE YOU THERE X\\n\\n\\n\\n_____\\n\\n*For those attending who receive a guestlist ticket, there will be a mandatory donation of £10 on the door. This donation will be distributed between HEAL Palestine and Barbs' fundraiser.\\n\\nEvent artwork by SMUT Press. T-shirt printed by Maggotdeath666.\\n\\n____________\\n\\nSMUT Press is a London-based queer publishing project and party platform, redefining what print and nightlife can do. Founded in early 2022 by Jordan Hearns \\u0026 Jack Scollard, SMUT support and commission queer artists to produce printed matter. Since 2024, the project has expanded beyond the primary domain of publishing to include events to coalesce and connect the communities the project is situated; between nightlife and artistic production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":569,\"name\":\"plentyppl 2nd Birthday\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-03T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"211c62b17f1792e7753cdb37f9ae24c0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\\"plentyppl\\\" is a night focused on the care-free enjoyment of Black dance music.Sounds weave through various genres such as Broken Beat and Soulful House and their musical roots including Jazz, Funk and Soul.\\n\\nJust like that, two years of plentyppl are behind us.\\n\\nAs a thank you all for the nights you've spent dancing with us we bring you a very special dance headlined by the plentyppl board of directors at Peckham's favourite arch (and somewhere we've been meaning to touch) The Carpet Shop.\\n\\nHere's to many, many more years.\\n\\nTickets are £10 OTD before midnight and £15 after.\\n\\nSee you in the dance\\nplentyppl x\\n\\nNOTES:\\nNo entry after 2am\\nPlease bring your physical ID\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2439044\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":672,\"name\":\"Cafe Oto Summer Fair\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-04T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"627d67217541e61c43441c86e6a2e30f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nThe annual Cafe OTO Summer Fair is back! Celebrating some of our favourite publishers and labels. Free entry! With...\\n\\nAs Far As The Eye Can Travel\\nbison\\nBurley Fisher Community Press\\nCentral Bazaar\\nChild Be Strange\\nDivided\\nEarthbound Press\\nFeedback Moves\\nFrom the Lips to the Moon\\nHouse of Annetta\\nInfant Tree\\nLol Coxhill Archive\\nPalestinian Sound Archive\\nRhys Trimble\\nSagome\\nSistah Space\\nSpillll\\nSyrian Cassette Archive\\nVeer Books\\nWorkers for a Free Palestine\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":703,\"name\":\"SET Social Grand Reopening Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-04T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-05T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0158cfcb7a84212f62961a76e3fa26c3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Date: Saturday 4 July\\nTime: 12pm-3am\\nLocation: SET Social, 55a Nigel Road, Peckham, London, SE15 4NP\\nAdmission: Free daytime entry (with £3-15 suggested donation encouraged) | OTD tickets from 6pm. Member tickets £5/non-member guests £7\\nAccess: Step-free \\u0026 wheelchair accessible\\n\\n\\nAfter our temporary closure, we’re thrilled to be reuniting our community for a massive day-to-night Grand Reopening Fundraiser! Join us at SET Social this Saturday 4th July, from 12pm til late, as we throw open the doors for a celebration packed with DJs, stalls, workshops, performances, and more.\\n\\nIt’s an open invitation to come support the space you’ve helped us build, kickstart the next chapter together, and strengthen our foundations for the year ahead.\\n\\nTHE LINE-UP\\n\\nEverything on the day until 6pm is free to attend, but please remember that the bar, the raffle and in-kind donations are the heartbeat of our recovery.\\n\\n12-5pm | Community Market: Packed with local independent makers selling ceramics, zines, prints, vintage clothes and more.\\n\\n12-5pm | Drop-In Craft Table\\nA relaxed creative space to sit down, doodle, and make something beautiful. Completely open to all ages and skill levels.\\n\\n12-5pm | Book Sale with Literacy Aid UK\\nHosted by Literacy Aid UK, improving book access for everyone.\\n\\n2-4pm | Gardening workshop with the SET Social DIY Community Garden\\nA relaxed, drop-in session inviting you to get involved with the community garden. Expect planting, sharing tips, chatting, and learning more about how the garden is cared for collectively. No experience needed.\\n\\n2-4pm | I’m Your Biggest FANzine Summer Special with Drawing People Together\\nA brilliant, drop-in zine workshop hosted by Drawing People Together. Think word searches, bedroom posters, and fanfiction. All materials provided. Free to attend (donations welcome)\\n\\n3-4.30pm | Camera Clinic Drop-In with Negative Space:\\nGot an old film camera gathering dust or acting up? Bring it along for a quick diagnostic troubleshoot. Aaron will also be running a pop-up shop selling film, cameras, and essential camera gear.\\n\\n4:30pm | THE RETURN OF PECKHAM AND NUNHEAD ELVIS\\nBack by popular demand after their packed-out winter show – this time on the BIG STAGE! Do not be late for this, the room fills up fast!\\n\\n6.45pm | Welcome Back Speech:\\nA brief word from the SET Team to officially thank you all and open the next chapter of SET Social.\\n\\n9pm | The Grand Raffle Announcement\\nWe’ll announce the lucky winners of the raffle. You can buy a ticket during the day to win amazing prizes donated by local Peckham businesses and the wider SET community.\\n\\n9.30pm | DJs\\nOur lineup of DJs (TBC) take over the decks to keep us dancing late into the night.\\n\\nWHY WE ARE FUNDRAISING FOR SET SOCIAL\\n\\nWhile Saturday is a joyful celebration of being back together, it is also a vital rallying moment for our venue.\\n\\nRunning an independent, DIY space in London right now is incredibly tough and requires a lot of careful planning. As a non-profit charity, we operate on a lean, community-focused model where every penny we make goes directly back into our art and community programme and keeping our doors open. This model is very effective at keeping our space accessible, but it relies on a steady cycle of trade from our bar, café, memberships, and bookings to stay sustainable.\\n\\nBeing forced to close unexpectedly for six weeks during our recent lease transition hit us hard. Our core operation costs didn’t pause while our doors were shut, and missing a month and a half of trading interrupted the steady financial cycle that keeps our operations stable.\\n\\nWe’re launching this fundraiser as a proactive step to bridge that gap, recover our financial footing, and ensure we can continue to support our community to the fullest.\\n\\n\\nOUR 23,000 GOAL!!\\n\\nTo recover from our recent closure and ensure our community impact continues, we’re pushing forward with a £23,000 community fundraising campaign. This goal has been calculated to cover the core overheads and utility costs we accrued while our doors were shut. By clearing these outstanding costs now, we ensure that our future revenue can go exactly where it matters: back into our arts programming and community initiatives, returning us to the stable footing required to sustain our mission.\\n\\nWithout reaching this goal, our recovery will be much slower, and we may be forced to operate at a more limited capacity. This could mean reduced opening hours, a scaled-back arts programme, and fewer subsidised community sessions. By hitting our target together, we avoid those compromises entirely and can focus on growing our support for local artists and community groups.\\n\\nTo be absolutely clear: This campaign is a proactive step to ensure our continued operation and stability. We are not facing any immediate closure threats; rather, we’re acting now to secure the resources needed to keep our space and programming thriving for our community.\\n\\nEvery single penny raised through this campaign goes directly into strengthening the foundation and stability of our Peckham venue, allowing us to continue to maintain and evolve our programme, while ensuring the communities who need us can rely on us to be around for years to come. We absolutely love our community here, and we are constantly astounded by how supportive and kind you have been over the years, and especially over these last few weeks. It is our community who make SET Social, and by extension, SET, what it is today.\\n\\nWe’re aiming to build momentum this Saturday by clearing the first £5,000 hurdle, and we’d love your support in helping us clear this first hurdle.\\n\\nCome celebrate, dance, and help us build this next chapter together.\\n\\nHOW YOU CAN SUPPORT US (BEYOND THE FUNDRAISER)\\n\\nIf you can’t make it this weekend, you can still play a massive part in protecting our future through the following:\\n\\n1. Donate to our GoFundMe appeal\\nPlease consider contributing directly to our digital campaign online. Because SET is a registered charity, you can also select Gift Aid at checkout to add an extra 25% to your donation at absolutely no extra cost to you. Donate here: https://gofund.me/05e73b65f\\n\\n2. Become a SET Social member\\nSign up for membership giving you year round access to our space plus lots more benefits for just £12 a year (= £1/month). This provides us with predictable, recurring revenue to plan our programming months in advance. (Please note: Membership is completely free for our immediate SE15 neighbours, though if you wish to pay anyway, your contribution will mean a lot!).Sign up here: https://setspace.uk/social/become-a-member/\\n\\n\\n3. Donate in person\\nLook out for physical donation buckets dotted around the hall and red bar from Saturday to the end of September for quick, small contributions.\\n\\nEssential information for the day\\n\\nAccessibility: SET Social has assisted step-free wheelchair access, including an accessible toilet. You can find out more about the venue’s accessibility features here: https://setspace.uk/social/accessibility-at-set-social/ \\n\\nFamilies and children: Families are incredibly welcome. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent or guardian.\\n\\nParking: There is no parking available on site; we highly recommend coming via public transport (we are just a short walk from Peckham Rye station).\\n\\nOutside drinks: As mentioned, please do not bring outside food or drinks into the venue or garden space. Our charity status relies on bar sales to survive!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://setspace.uk/event/set-social-grand-reopening-fundraiser/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":625,\"name\":\"FILTH\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-04T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3d6435563a4f1aff5c7e88e3412f8e51.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"FILTH is a London-based queer nightlife project built by working-class organisers, DJs and creatives reclaiming space on our own terms.\\n\\nLaunched in response to the increasing corporatisation of Pride and queer culture, FILTH exists as an alternative - rooted in community, not branding; cooperation, not extraction.\\n\\nWe centre the people who actually make queer nightlife what it is: grassroots artists, organisers, and working-class creatives who are too often sidelined, underpaid, or expected to stay silent to stay booked.\\n\\nNo sponsors. No corporate alignment. No interest in reproducing the same bullshit systems that are hollowing out our scene.\\n\\nJust loud, political, joyful dancefloors - built by us, for us!\\n\\nAccessibility:\\n- Our venue is step-free and wheelchair accessible\\n- Accessible entrance via Blundell Street\\n- Multiple accessible toilets\\n- Spaces to sit down and yap\\n- Free carer tickets available - drop us a line to organise\\n- Any other questions - filthismypolitics2322@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2402167\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":657,\"name\":\"Day + Night Special - Oldboy, Adam Pits, Amaliah, Special Guest, Carré, Jenny Sparks\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-04T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-05T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cbe3ad8e3aa718115f4f40a0a41e1239.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\n16 hours, 11 artists and counting \\u0026 outdoor + indoor capability to groove on a day into the night adventure at one of the most exciting spaces in emerging in Ldn this summer\\nPowered by a strong will and Funktion One sound.\\n\\nAdam Pits\\nOldboy\\nAmaliah\\nSpecial Guest\\nBody Clinic\\nJenny Sparks\\nPluralist\\nCarré\\nSafina\\nDanno\\n\\nTickets moving quick, secure now to avoid disappointment.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2433844\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":626,\"name\":\"Dreams and Ghosts with Dominic Pettman \\u0026 Everyday Analysis\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-04T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-04T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"af4e8a3fb053831136e1abd1a221afad.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a conversation between two of the most exciting theorists of the digital realm, Dominic Pettman and Alfie Bown\\nWe are delighted to welcome our friends Everyday Analysis back to Housmans for what promises to be another stimulating reflection on the agonies and aporias of contemporary culture.\\n\\nThis time we have Dominic Pettman joining us, to talk about some of the recurrent ideas that animate, his recent publications, The Forgetting of Dreams: Selected Oneiric Residues (published by Everyday Analysis) and Ghosting: On Disappearance (Polity, 2025).\\n\\nDominic is emerging as one of our major theorists of the digital world. His work is especially accomplished at interrogating modes of disconnection, loneliness and alienation that could only really exist now; in an epoch almost entirely mediated through a digital reflection of itself.\\n\\nblurbs:\\nThe Forgetting of Dreams: Selected Oneiric Residues\\n\\nWe process our lives through riddles, mysteries, ciphers, and enigmas – but we hesitate to share these with friends and family. In times gone by, as for Freud, dreams were considered a key to cosmic secrets. Today, in all sorts of ways – both subtle and not – we are discouraged from sharing the content of our dreams, unless we happen to be indulging in that most anachronistic ritual: lying prostrate on the psychoanalyst’s couch. Anywhere else, an anecdote that begins, “Last night I dreamed . . .” is usually met with a sigh and a defensive glazing of the eyes. In our over-burdened world, any sharing of dreams is always already perceived as over-sharing. Contrary to this, Pettman argues – the more we share tales of our isolated nocturnal journeys, the better chance we have to understand the topography of our collective conundrum. \\n\\n\\nGhosting: On Disappearance\\n\\nAbandonment is as old as time, but ghosting is a modern twist on this ancient experience. It translates this age-old phenomenon into our modern world of screens, delete buttons and blocking options. Ghosting is not only an unpleasant experience, or cowardly act, but a symptom of our increasingly spectral – that is, mediated and virtual – relationship to the world. The overabundance of new modes of communication has invited an almost infinite number of contacts and conversations. At the same time, it has also offered an unprecedented opportunity for ignoring messages from others. And just as we invented the car crash when we invented automobiles, we also encouraged ghosting when we created the internet.\\n\\nGhosting creates an empty space in our minds: a space faithfully tracing the silhouette of the one who ghosted us. But unlike traditional ghosts, today’s ghosters simply disappear, leaving behind a form of haunting that is closer to mourning: mourning for someone who is not in fact dead. In putting a kind of preemptive mourning into our everyday affairs, ghosting tells us much about the current human relationship – or non-relationship – to a shared sense of mortality, purpose, and spirit.  \\n\\nThis book – the first sustained analysis of ghosting – traces the source of this vexed experience to, and through, our current media ecology, technological networks, political landscape, collective psychology, romantic mantras, and deep sense of social neglect.\\n\\nDominic will be joined by the brilliant Alfie Bown, Senior Lecturer in Digital Media Culture and Technology at King’s College London. Alfie is the author of numerous brilliant interventions into the worlds of digital studies, Marxism and psychoanalysis. His most recent books are Alfie Bown, Post-Comedy (Polity, 2024) and Dream Lovers: Capitalism and the Gamification of Relationships (London: Pluto, 2022).\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/dreams-and-ghosts-with-dominic-pettman-everyday-analysis/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":663,\"name\":\"Channel Orange Room\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-04T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-05T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ce2caf91a23e13efd01a3d51d80409c8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Channel Orange Room is an immersive club night that celebrates creativity by fusing music and other art forms.\\n\\nOur flagship night will celebrate our favourite DJs alongside live performers TBA!\\n\\nExpect sounds from around the world: House, Amapiano, Afrobeats, RnB, Hip Hop, Baile Funk, Dancehall \\u0026 more.\\n\\n8-10PM | Live Performances TBA\\n\\n10PM-3AM | 2-Room Party:\\u2028We’re taking over both rooms all night.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/bboqgx-channel-orange-room-4th-jul-the-orange-room-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":432,\"name\":\"Club Soft x Tropical Waste - An alcohol-free open air party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-05T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-05T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"95ad87f8863cd13806a1277f9882000d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Club Soft and Tropical Waste are proud to present a new kind of party for London. \\n\\nAn outdoor dancefloor. Heavyweight sound courtesy of Felt Soundsystem. DJs playing cutting-edge club music all day long. An alcohol-free bar serving delicious mocktails, slushies and 0% beer. An all-ages entry policy, from 0 all the way up. \\n\\nThe scene is set for a beautiful summertime party at Gaffe in Tottenham, where the focus is fully on music, movement and intergenerational raving. \\n\\nMusic comes courtesy of friends, fam ‘n special guests who play on-point, fwd-thinking sounds from scenes around the globe:\\n\\nBryte (live) - Bringing his infectious afro-electronic rap energy.\\n\\nHaleemi - The Skullrub member who specialises in the finest diasporic selections. \\n\\nMina b2b Cheza Lucina - Expect soca and carnival vibes mixed with high energy club mutations. \\n\\nNoli (hybrid live) - The rising young junglist fuses amen science with live viola. \\n\\nSana b2b Shryke - Fwd-thinking club music specialists who span tempos and know how to heat the ‘floor. \\n\\nSeb b2b Raji Rags - Chicago footwork, juke, jungle, high speed fusions and infectious edits. Their NTS session went down in history so they’re going dad2dad IRL. \\n\\nAs well as the music we’ll also be hosting:\\n\\n-A family movement workshop run by Niamh Keady\\n-A kids soft play + craft area\\n-Food served by More Life More Love\\n-An alcohol-free bar run by ARC Bristol\\n\\nFamily info:\\n-All under 18s must be accompanied by an adult\\n-1 adult can accompany 2 under 18s\\n-Please bring hearing protection for your children\\n-A baby changing table will be available\\n\\nGetting to Gaffe:\\nNearest train station is Meridian Water, the venue is a 15 min walk! \\n\\nClub Soft and Tropical Waste are two promoters who specialise in cutting-edge club music and pushing London’s club culture into the future. Come join us as we create an innovative new event format for our city. See you down the front \\u003c3\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":681,\"name\":\"Loop Sessions LDN 031 w/ Frenquency\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-05T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-05T19:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4ca713f89486bea55d21e3f24068add1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Loop Sessions LDN is a chapter of a global sample flip challenge, since 2016. Just come along with your laptop or beatmaking device of choice, MPC, SP404, etc (plus headphones, of course). Everyone has 3 hours to make a track using the curated samples by our guest, at 6pm we play them all on the sound system. All genres and skill levels are welcome. \\n\\nWe've been keen to have a Footwork / Juke artist curate the sample crate since day dot. It's an important cornerstone in sample culture. So, for our July guest, we have Frenquency over from the Netherlands. Providing the goods in the big smoke 🇳🇱\\n\\nHe's released a heavyweight catalogue of music across a lot of labels from SATURATE! to 4NC¥, and Samsara Beats. And he's extensively toured around the world to play his high-energy live sets. Fusing Jungle, Halftime, and Ghettohouse into his 160 sound.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":207,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Stress Positions\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-05T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-05T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1e8b1995d30dae447f09dab2a8ddd3ef.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nStress Positions\\nExpect the unexpected. Furious futurist hardcore and junglist D-beats on Three One G Records. \\n\\nSupport from\\nTension\\nFrantic Stompcore\\n\\nBorn In April\\nScreamo melodrama\\n\\nSarsour\\nSide-to-side distortioncore\\n\\nClouded\\nMetalcore murder riffs\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£13\\n14+, u16s with an adult\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/stress-positions\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":631,\"name\":\"The Man with the Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-05T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-05T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3ac53820b83fe6f9413d37313531de5d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, with Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza, Andrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\n\\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films Production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":256,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Diploid\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-06T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-06T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0ff915c8e463af52bc5e7e6f0f778cdc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nDiploid\\nFrantic, unhinged grind from Melbourne. Mind breaking noise worship.\\n\\n+ Support from\\n[Filler]\\nNew London powerviolence from members of Katolik / Hello Bastards / I Like Bugs\\n\\n\\u0026 more....\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£12\\n14+, u16s with an adult\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/diploid\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":373,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0b392e6a9f148c6deb2f965295f5f04a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A festival of disappearing images. Things that can’t be saved. Across disciplines: film, performance, theatre, music, talk. \\n\\nDay tickets are also available via gel (linked below). \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":509,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (1): Alya Al-Sultani / Fatima Lahham / nunez (trio) | Kenichi Iwasa / Regan Bowering / Harry Murdoch (trio)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-06T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"197ddcbc9f4b2272a1034b64a1c4a08d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":573,\"name\":\"Samba Jean-Baptiste, Keeper, Taylor Richardson, Yuri Umemoto\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-06T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-06T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bd8e283f6f9110403c6f3879dd90aa6a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"LINEUP CHANGE: \\n\\nSamba Jean-Baptiste\\nKeeper\\nTaylor Richardson (DJ)\\nYuri Umemoto (DJ)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":510,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (2): Open Secret | bod [包家巷] | Daniel Gatenio\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-07T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"34f84147f9109a43144bd9e1129ee1e2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":684,\"name\":\"A People's History of the Anti-Nazi League, with Geoff Brown\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-07T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6a243a39d0f424cebeb2297e677e34ad.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Anti-Nazi League (ANL) was formed in 1977, an important example of a “United Front” approach to resisting the far-right. The ANL has a particular connection to Tower Hamlets because of its link to Rock Against Racism and its huge concert in Victoria Park on 30th April 1978, attended by 100,000 people. Tower Hamlets teacher Blair Peach was also a member of the ANL. Geoff Brown's book looks at the history of the ANL and why its tactics remain relevant today.\\n\\nGeoff has been an active socialist and trade unionist since the late 1960s and was an ANL organiser in Manchester from 1977 to 1979 and later worked for the University and Collee Union (UCU). He has written extensively on apartheid and anti-racism.\\n\\nThe Common Press bookshop is twenty yards from a particularly important landmark in the resistance to the far right. During the 1970s and 80s, the top end of Brick Lane was where the National Front used to gather and sell their racist materials, until they were driven away by the local Bangladeshi community and anti-racist activists, including the ANL.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/36181/a-peoples-history-of-the-anti-nazi-league-with-geoff-brown\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":637,\"name\":\"More Eaze, nykolaes \\u0026 Daniël Paul, Pyromunckin, Tara Clerkin Trio (DJ)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-07T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-07T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"75bcc2853e25b937183a837e529f069b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"More Eaze, \\nnykolaes \\u0026 Daniël Paul, \\nPyromunckin, \\nand Tara Clerkin Trio \\n\\nplay Avalon Café on 7th July 2026\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":547,\"name\":\"Non-Threatening Boys + Nick50 + Callum J Cocker\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-07T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-07T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4e8a3ef7485468b96b6e789e68346e58.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The final New Lands before a well deserved summer break sees some familiar and beloved faces take to The Ivy House stage; Non-Threatening Boys + Nick50 + Callum J Cocker.\\n\\nBuy a ticket before Tue 30 June and get a free pint of New Lands lager at the show.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":570,\"name\":\"The Hotel presents... Hours for Jerome at The Cinema Museum\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-08T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-08T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e62e090660f3bba2fb723d52497878e8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To mark the release of ‘Basin’ by Rocheman – a 21st century masterpiece of devotional art – The Hotel proudly presents a screening of Nathaniel Dorsky’s magnum opus ‘Hours for Jerome’.\\n\\nHours for Jerome is a cinematic lyric poem dedicated to Dorsky’s partner, artist Jerome Hiler, documenting aspects of their daily life in Manhattan and New Jersey. The film is entirely silent, and rooted in a centuries-old tradition of devotional art, from stained glass painting to medieval illuminated manuscripts and books of hours.\\n\\nThis event offers a rare chance to see the work of Nathaniel Dorsky in the UK, rarely shown due to the fragile and scarce nature of its existence.\\n\\nAs Nathaniel himself puts it:\\n\\n“My films only exist as 16mm film prints and I have kept them in their original and intended format as I feel that that is what they actually are. Any digitizing of them would be a reproduction or reduction of them and not the original experience that I have intended.\\n\\nI find the more humane quality of light and the warmth and body of the physical image of celluloid projection to be essential to how my films communicate. My films speak to the body of the viewer and the digitization of them removes their more weighty physical presence and limits their ability to communicate or function as I have intended. Shifts of weight on the cut are an important part of my articulation.\\n\\nI know that keeping them exclusively as film prints has greatly reduced my audience, but I sincerely feel that this sacrifice is worth the preciousness of what is preserved. My film shows have become more like live performances or perhaps like going to a museum and seeing an actual painting rather than a reproduction as such. Seeing the actual painting is to be in touch with the very eros of a work. How often have I fallen in love with a painting in real life and then seen a reproduction of the painting. Yes, some basic information is translated but the actual thing one loved has vanished.\\n\\nSo for now I cherish the physicality of 16mm film projection. It is like an acoustic instrument. I love its body and warmth, its vulnerability and intimacy, its tenderness and earthiness. I can only hope that my fans will continue to be able to travel to see my film shows and that we can all participate in something quite special and rewarding midst a rapidly changing world.“\\n\\n\\nBasin LP will play through The Cinema Museum’s sound system before and after the screening.\\n\\nTH04 copies of Basin will be available for sale at the event.\\n\\nWith thanks to Light Cone, Angel and The Decision Maker.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":511,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (3): Mark Leckey | Klein | R.I.P. Germain | 54 the Gate\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-08T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-08T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9fdf58ac3a9d6c9feba1c4c4d15ad434.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":541,\"name\":\"Illegal Data: Stolen Velour, FLOCO \\u0026 Aria SL - Underlight album launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-08T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9338dc8e7791dcca695557c4535c738c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Illegal Data!? In London!? hahaha no way thats sick hahaha\\nBut wait its more socially accomodating 'gig times' and on a week day to blow away the mid week cobwebs!? sounds so sick hahah wow!!\\n\\nTo celebrate the release of 'Underlight' the debut album from Stolen Velour, FLOCO \\u0026 Aria SL we are putting together this very special album launch show at the beloved Spanners in saaaaaaaaaf laaaaandaaan. Line up has been described by many as 'biblical', 'iconic' and 'down right daft' [respectfully].\\n\\nSTOLEN VELOUR, FLOCO \\u0026 ARIA SL [live]\\n\\nLOL K [live]\\n\\nAMY [live]\\n\\n\\nWednesday 8th July\\nSpanners, Arch 504 Ridgway Rd, London SW9 7EX\\n7:30pm - 11pm\\n\\nTickets: £8adv / £10otd\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":147,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Shai Hulud\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-09T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-09T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"44f8fce698891acf3b28cbab5f083811.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nShai Hulud\\nYeah that's right. Shai Hulud at New Cross Inn. Metalcore legends for over 30 years.\\n\\n+ Support from\\nAfraid To Die\\nNew Dark UK Hardcore supergroup on The Coming Strife. Members of every band ever.\\n\\nand more to come...\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£15\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/shai-hulud-2\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":654,\"name\":\"Inframetropolitan Systems: Lynnée Denise on Prince\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-09T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-09T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"381443b4f9b31fd00719b083e0e5b701.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Third of three sessions on the musical production of space and memory, space and politics.\\n\\nLynnée Denise on Prince.\\n\\n!!! GUCU STRIKE FUNDRAISER !!!\\n\\nGOLDSMITHS UCU HAS VOTED TO MOVE TO INDEFINITE STRIKE FOLLOWING THE IMPOSITION OF 100% PAY DEDUCTIONS.\\n\\nTHIS TALK IS FREE BUT IF YOU ARE ABLE YOU CAN DONATE TO THE GUCU STRIKE FUND.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":524,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (4): Existers\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-09T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-09T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1d0404fd11b0b27bea6309888940ecd1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":702,\"name\":\"raxil4 @50: raxil4's Stabat Mater\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-09T20:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-10T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a9db0e7fa63705782d84838ebedf3502.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To celebrate 50 years of prolific drone artist raxil4, we shall be presenting the debut of his first experimental operatic work – the Stabat Mater.\\n\\nBased on a 13th century Latin text, The Choir of Babel, a multilingual choir will perform the piece in as many languages as possible at the same time.\\n\\nSet to a drone noise background featuring a large ensemble of some of raxil4’s most frequent collaborators and some of London’s finest improvisers, including members of the Apocalypse Jazz Unit, the London Improvisers Orchestra, and the GPS theremin trio. Combined with visuals by video artist Egle Saka creating a landscape to enhance the atmosphere.\\n\\nThe work is split into five pieces, each representing a different stage of grief.\\n\\nThe text has been set to music over 300 times. Now, after 20 years in the making, it is raxil4’s turn. A spectacle not to be missed.\\n\\nWarning: Some performances might use strobes and/or flashing lights.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/Bb804c84efb5?dice_id=Bb804c84efb5\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":644,\"name\":\"'IMISSMYMOM II' - IMISSMYMOM Album Release at Deptford Junction with Sunken + Restless Taxis\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3dcfb0a6d7494e08264f985e967aee32.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"IMISSMYMOM II – Album Release Show\\n\\nSouth London via Toronto band IMISSMYMOM return to Deptford Junction to celebrate the release of their second album, IMISSMYMOM II, released the same day via independent imprint THEFT.\\n\\nEmerging from London's warehouse party circuit, IMISSMYMOM are a five-piece band pushing heavy music into new territory. Drawing from punk, rap, techno, DIY and experimental influences, they have built a reputation for combining crushing intensity with emotional vulnerability, creating a sound that is as raw as it is uncompromising.\\n\\nLed by Tennessee and backed by Cameron, Marley, Kyle and Tommy, the band quickly became one of the most distinctive voices in London's underground scene. IMISSMYMOM II marks the next chapter in their evolution, arriving alongside visuals developed in collaboration with acclaimed Creative Director Ib Kamara.\\n\\nJoining them on the night are London's own Sunken and Restless Taxis.\\n\\nSunken - London's Sunken channel grunge, shoegaze and alternative rock into dense walls of distortion and melodic intensity. Their music balances crushing guitars with atmospheric textures and introspective songwriting, earning them a growing reputation on the capital's underground guitar circuit as one of the scene's most promising new acts.\\n\\nRestless Taxis - East London's Restless Taxis are a DIY, queer and POC-led band whose sound collides shoegaze, noise rock, psychedelia and UK sound system culture. Formed in 2019, they've built a reputation through London's DIY venues and squat parties, creating music that draws equally from '90s guitar music, rave culture, dub and Caribbean influences. Their immersive live shows have made them one of the most distinctive emerging bands in the city's alternative scene. \\n\\nExpect noise, catharsis and a proper album launch from one of the city's most exciting emerging bands.\\n\\n*** This event operates a NOTAFLOF policy (No One Turned Away For Lack Of Funds). We want everyone who would like to attend to be able to do so. If you are unable to afford a ticket, please email imissmymom.band@gmail.com or info@deptfordjunction.co.uk, and we will arrange a ticket for you. Please contact us before the day of the event. ***\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":639,\"name\":\"A Sensored Evening \",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T12:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6c8484349c1f5a4496c3bb25793a6a27.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Come to the basement to play, connect and create.\\n\\nOn July 10th, Sensored is taking over Love Affair Basement.\\n\\nWe invite you into The Basement to create, play, and connect in an immersive evening of live performance and creativity.\\n\\nDress code: Come as you are party.\\n\\nDJ @majordomdrag\\n\\nLive Performances from:\\n\\n@pamela_von_horn\\n@skully1888\\n@fotisnoir\\n@julietpeaches_\\n@clapmutt\\n\\nJuly 10th\\n7:00 PM until Late\\nLove Affair Basement\\n324 Hackney Rd, London E2 7AX\\n\\nSpace is limited, and the energy will be magic. Secure your place in the ripple.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":647,\"name\":\"Diaspora Dance: Fundraiser for Lebanon \\u0026 Gaza\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"21c948310c4756205b6399b08ad86d61.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Doikayt Collective presents Diaspora Dance: a party bringing together Jewish anti-Zionist communities with Palestinian and Lebanese comrades, and allies from across the movement, to dance and raise funds for families facing dispossession and genocide at the hands of the Zionist entity.\\n\\n📍Piehouse Co-Op, 213-214 Edward Pl, SE8 5HD\\n\\n⏰ Time: 8pm until 1am.\\n\\n🎤 Join us for a short Kabbalat Shabbat service before moving into a night of live music and DJs from across our communities, including:\\n\\n- Talata (live) \\n- Habibtati (DJ)\\n- Sachana (DJ)\\n- DJ Bubbela (DJ)\\n- Polyphemus (DJ)\\n\\nThis event will be raising funds for families in Lebanon, and through ToteFreedom, a multifaith direct aid initiative supporting networks of families and community projects in Gaza.\\n\\nPlease email us at doikaytcollective@gmail.com or DM us on Instagram (@doikaytcollective) if you are struggling for funds but still want to come.\\n\\nMore info coming soon! \\u003c3\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":643,\"name\":\"Baggio + Prayer Tech + Henry Nielsen\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-10T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a3fbcf7bfc74297ab05d519c9d235c82.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Baggio return to The Ivy House for the first time in almost a year (!!!), with Prayer Tech and Henry Nielsen supporting. NOTAFLOF.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/baggio-prayer-tech-henry-nielsen-tickets-1992361900076?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":632,\"name\":\"The Man with the Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-10T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f7d14d933aa9916fb33a201861edbbab.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\"\\nRead John Bird's review in THE BIG ISSUE\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, with Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza, Andrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\n\\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films Production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":525,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (5): Charlie Osborne | Richard Layzell: La Busqueda | Ship Sket\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-10T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5022647a1631da036bc2ccd234c43ba3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":594,\"name\":\"FINAL IMAGE night with O YUKI CONJUGATE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c28d45760ba98c6f5f0869304c652366.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Final Image hosts a label night at Spanners on the 10th of July with a one-off preview of O Yuki Conjugate's new live set of reworked old material and revisited archival VHS \\u0026 Super 8 films. This will be OYC's first gig in four years. Before and after the set, the label's very own Laura Not will be DJing.\\n\\n\\n\\n- O YUKI CONJUGATE (OYC) were formed in Nottingham in 1982 on the wave of experimental music that emerged out of Post Punk. Quickly moving on from their early industrial and electronic influences, OYC began exploring the then-unfashionable ‘ambient’ genre, combining grit with beauty to produce mesmerising atmospheric soundscapes.\\n\\nTheir relaxed work attitude, wilful obscurity and general aversion to the music industry has maintained a secrecy around them but reissues have unearthed the hidden beauty of their music. Scene in Mirage (1984), Into Dark Water (1987), Peyote (1990) and Equator (1995) have all found retrospective praise and a new audience. Recent releases have been on World of Echo, Utter and Optimo as well as their own label FINAL IMAGE.\\n\\nOYC are currently in their fourth incarnation - based around core members Andrew Hulme and Roger Horberry - and are coming out of a recent hibernation to play new shows. Spanners will be their first since the Watching Trees festival in 2022 and will present reinterpretations of older material for the first time.\\n\\nThe performance will also include film work by Hulme, who has simultaneously reinterpreted the band's 80s VHS and super 8 footage. The result will be a mesmerising exploration of the sonic territory OYC have christened “dirty ambient” – multi layered, hyper textural, distinctly gritty and magically unreal.\\n\\n\\n- LAURA NOT is an artist and DJ. Behind the decks, she has been collaging unusual music and curating radio programmes focusing on experimental sounds, like (x)=musik on Lyl Radio. Other than DJing, she co-runs the label Final Image and has released music on imprints such as Infant Tree and Kashual Plastik.\\n\\n\\n- FINAL IMAGE is a label of music, film and art which existed originally for a short time in the 80s (with releases by O Yuki Conjugate, Pump, John Avery amongst others) and has now been reactivated by Andrew Hulme and Laura Not to explore new sonic horizons as well as to reissue archive material.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":713,\"name\":\"K9 Presents @ Oitij-Jo Arts Space \",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-10T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4e1a7e33c2e9a5714e522ec617395006.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"K9 has assembled a killer cast of DJs and very special guests for a Summer Session.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":687,\"name\":\"Chef Takeover at Studio 12: Tala Bashmi x Sylvia Vavik-Flåten\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-11T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"455f4e7c97846b05b1117f8aa93fbc39.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A Chef Takeover at Studio 12: a day of food, drinks and vinyl.\\n\\nSaturday July 11th \\n\\nChefs Tala Bashmi and Sylvia Vavik-Flåten bring the flavours of their homes together in a collaborative, playful menu, in a relaxed setting.\\n\\nHosted in Studio 12’s courtyard, which feels like your back home best friend's back yard, you’ll hear a vinyl selection curated by Tala Bashmi and Patricia Doors while you eat. \\n\\nFood is served from 1pm - 3pm, set out on a communal table, for you to help yourself at your own pace, alongside an experimental bar menu by Sana Barclay.\\n\\nAfterwards join us for a drink as DJs carry the afternoon into the evening.  \\n\\nSaturday July 11th\\nDoors: 12 pm\\nFood: 1 – 3 pm\\nMusic: 3 – 8 pm\\n\\nTala Bashmi is an award-winning Bahraini chef celebrated for redefining Khaleeji cuisine through a contemporary, heritage-led approach. After training at the Culinary Arts Academy in Switzerland and working in leading European kitchens, she returned to Bahrain to open ‘Fusions by Tala’, one of the region's most acclaimed restaurants. Her accolades include MENA's Best Female Chef (2022), The Best Chef Awards Three Knives (2024), and the Estrella Damm Chefs' Choice Award (2025). She is also a UN Tourism Gastronomy Ambassador.\\n\\nSylvia Vavik-Flåten is a Mexican-Norwegian chef, culinary educator and founder of Sylvia's Mexican Kitchen. With over 20 years of experience, she is known for authentic Mexican cuisine and inventive Mexican-Nordic cooking rooted in heritage, sustainability and storytelling. A winner of TV2's Norges Grillmester, Sylvia has cooked internationally across Mexico, Finland, Iceland and Norway, creating immersive dining experiences, teaching, consulting and developing her artisan salsa collection inspired by Mexican techniques and Nordic ingredients.\\n\\n\\nStudio 12\\nCornerstone Studios\\n1 Addington Square\\nSE5 7JZ, London\\n\\nPlease be on time, food will only be served within allocated times (for real). *Note* Sunday timings run one hour after Saturday's schedule. \\n\\nFOOD Tickets are for food + 1 welcome drink. Additional drinks can be purchased at the bar. We give our non-alcoholic drinks as much love as our cocktails.\\n\\nFree entry after food is served, arrive early capacity limited.\\n\\nDue to the nature of this shared menu, we are unable to accommodate dietary requirements or food allergies. \\n\\nFamily/Children friendly. Dogs welcome on a lead.\\n\\nStudio 12 is fully accessible.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":435,\"name\":\"CLUB SMUT PRESENTS: FREAK!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-11T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8db81922176f7f0e463afe237ee2ece2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"CLUB SMUT PRESENTS: FREAK!\\n\\nSUMMER DANCE PARTY EXTRAVAGANZA!\\n\\nSATURDAY JULY 11TH\\n\\nGAFFE, 1 ANTHONY WAY, N18 3QT\\n\\n2PM - 6AM\\n\\nQUEER DANCE PARTY\\n\\nFEATURING:\\n\\nCÁIT\\nELKKA\\nEOIN DJ\\nFAFF (LIVE)\\nJ ARIA\\nJORDAN HEARNS\\nKETIA\\nMISS PARKER\\nSEB ODYSSEY\\nSHIVUM SHARMA\\n\\nINSTALLATION BY\\n\\nJENKIN VAN ZYL\\n\\nSEE YOU THERE X\\n\\n\\n\\n_____\\n\\n*Ticket prices are based on tiered timing. This is designed to maintain a steady flow of people at the door. Please respect the time tier allocated to your ticket. Late arrivals will be subject to a late fee on the door (£10). This is non-negotiable.\\n\\n**If you arrive considerably after your allocated ticket time it may not be possible to allow you to enter. In order to keep a flow of people during the event we cannot account for everyone to arrive at the same time and later on in the evening. Please respect these conditions of the ticket sale and respect the decision of those working the door. \\n\\n***As always, we remain committed to keeping our events as accessible as possible - if you are unwaged or low-income please reach out to us directly for access to community tickets. Priority is given to our BIPOC and trans* siblings, however these are limited and distributed on a first-come, first-served basis.\\n\\n****For those attending who receive a guestlist ticket, there will be a mandatory donation of £10 on the door. This donation will be distributed between Anaka Women's Collective and Controlling Chemsex.\\n\\n*****We are proud to be partnering with The Love Tank - a not-for-profit community interest company (CIC) that promotes health \\u0026 wellbeing of under served communities through education, community building, research, events, outreach, and communication + design. They will be distributing various harm-reduction leaflets and talking about some of the services they provide.\\n\\nEvent artwork by Jenkin Van Zyl\\n—\\n\\nSMUT Press is a London-based queer publishing project and party platform, redefining what print and nightlife can do. Founded in early 2022 by Jordan Hearns \\u0026 Jack Scollard, SMUT support and commission queer artists to produce printed matter. Since 2024, the project has expanded beyond the primary domain of publishing to include events to coalesce and connect the communities the project is situated; between nightlife and artistic production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":526,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (6.1): Jeremy Gilbert and Stephen Coates\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-11T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9c64f0eee83fe4cd2b42a4c6b39eb8aa.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Day 6 of Disappearing Images. A conversation between Jeremy Gilbert and Stephen Coates.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":701,\"name\":\"IKLECTIK 12th Anniversary Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-11T17:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3cdcfe468615cb618deb7e4f208d0ed3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"These twelve years have been defined by uncompromising sound, bold experiments, beautiful chaos, and an ever-growing community. Over time, we have expanded beyond music to embrace performance and body-based practices, and our NOMADIK adventures, taking IKLECTIK outside our walls to build new collaborations and discover communities wherever we land.\\n\\nFrom Waterloo to Peckham Levels, through change, uncertainty, eviction, and reinvention, we have kept moving thanks to everyone who has believed in us: our artists, audiences, volunteers, collaborators, supporters, and the incredible IKLECTIK team.\\n\\nLET’s PARTY!\\n\\nOn Saturday 11th July, we invite you to join us to celebrate 12 years of weird sounds and beautiful creatures.\\n\\nTickets are “pay what you can” because we want as many of you there as possible. Any additional support will go directly towards producing the event and sustaining our future work.\\n\\nLine up:\\nQuieting (London premiere)\\nDUSHUME X DHANGSHA\\naya (DJ SET)\\nRrose (Live techno set)\\nmore acts TBA.\\n\\nSaturday 11 July. Doors 6pm.\\nCome celebrate 12 years of IKLECTIK with us\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/D35de3808f63?dice_id=D35de3808f63\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":527,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (6.2): Plastique Fantastique with Gentle Stranger + dove / Christine Kirubi + National Rails\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-11T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0a6595d7b0e421437b8f0ffa5d636d4b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":685,\"name\":\"ORMSIDE presents: DJ Sotofett\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-11T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4b961e1e87dffd86434bb91372988f42.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"ORMSIDE presents DJ Sotofett, returning for an all-night-long session channelling five decades of sound system music\\n\\nOver the past 20 years, Tresor resident and cult producer DJ Sotofett has been pushing an uncompromising vision across experimental and dance music - releasing a wide spectrum of shimmering dub techno, percussive disco, electro and more.\\n\\nExpect an extended 6hr set spanning decades of dance history, referencing decades of dance history, from jazz and dub explorations to techno futurism.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2464441\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":694,\"name\":\"Delito invites: DAMAGED\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-11T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"683b95629f7eaf954bc203344059b0c3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Matteo Manzini B2B Georgio Oniani \\nFranco Reyna \\nRoman\\n\\n\\n\\nThere's no school like the old-school.\\n\\nWe're back (already!), and this time we've invited the iconic DAMAGED (Matteo Manzini B2B Georgio Oniani) for a rare comeback.\\n\\nIf you know the story of DAMAGED, then you know there was only one place right for the occasion, Dalston, where it all started.\\n\\nJoin us next month as the new-school (rep'd by Roman and Franco) meets the old-school.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2466240\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":579,\"name\":\"New Regency Orchestra\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-12T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a752f5f00a7ece2a8fa82dc75a7ccc3b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Regency Orchestra will be headlining the second show in the four-part outdoor summer series celebrating the best of London jazz from the artists shaping the scene. Inspired by the musical melting pot of NYC in the 1950s but channeling the punch and power of a whole host of London’s best Latin and jazz musicians, New Regency Orchestra are one of London’s most electrifying acts. An 18-piece Afro-Cuban big band, they blow new life into some of the finest music from that golden era, when jazz luminaries like Dizzy Gillespie and Charlie Parker were joining forces with Cuban greats like Machito and Chano Pozo.  From early 1950s René Hernandez and Tito Puente, through to the 1970s salsa of Rafael Labasta and Orlando Marin, produced and performed with fresh fire, their debut album has been getting plaudits and plays far and wide.  Also performing on the day will be Joe Bristow (SEED Ensemble, Balimaya Project, Black Midi, Olivia Dean and more), Son Solero and Mansilla.\\n\\nSupported by a grassroots music grant from Arts Council England, helping us continue to champion emerging artists and live music in the community.  All events support Lewisham Donation Hub, a local charity providing vital support to those facing acute hardship across South East London.  The largest pub garden in SE London will have street food, drinks, and a laid-back summer atmosphere. Families are welcome, with free entry for children, market stalls, and activities to keep little ones entertained.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/new-regency-orchestra/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":720,\"name\":\"movement at set | ex dancers, non dancers \\u0026 club dancers \",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-12T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T15:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b8fced71b7ce20f23e060ebaa2075c84.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"bi-weekly movement sessions hosted at set social ~ an open space to get in touch with your body through dance, somatics, choreo \\u0026 more ✨🎷❤️‍🔥🎹\\n\\nthese sessions are all levels and no previous movement experience is required. you can expect a mixture of guided movement, textual offerings, and durational dancing, but no two classes are the same. as always all bodies are welcome.\\n\\n🪩 led by flo pearl \\u0026 mya cavner. \\ncheck out our insta (@movementatset) to see our upcoming guest teachers \\u0026 what's on with us.\\n\\nSUNDAY, JULY 12\\n2-2:30 soft arrival\\n2:30-3:30 moving\\n\\nwe can't wait to move with u xxx \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":699,\"name\":\"Sudan \\u0026 Palestine Fundraiser Market\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-12T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"64ced1324938bb87ee8179fd002b919b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Come and join us for a summer market for Sudan and Palestine, in memory of Sara 🪽\\n\\nThis will be a big one - it’s at the new @breadandbutter_arch , next to Hackney Central station, and we’ll have new vendors as well as some of our loyal sellers! The market will come straight after the screening of the Wimbledon final, running from 4-9pm. \\n\\nWe’ll also have food and music, and as always all ticket profits will be donated to grassroots orgs and families in Palestine and Sudan. ❤️💚🖤\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":704,\"name\":\"Paria Farzaneh x Alma Fundraiser Abdorrahman Boroumand Center for Human Rights in Iran\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-13T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f3c7b698ce54918037f0e754968a8d9f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A night of music in solidarity.\\n\\nJoin us at Ormside Projects for a fundraiser supporting the Abdorrahman Boroumand Center for Human Rights in Iran, an independent organisation dedicated to documenting human rights abuses, promoting accountability, and advancing democracy and the rule of law.\\n\\nBringing together a diverse lineup of London's most special DJs and live performers, the evening celebrates the power of community, creativity, and collective action. Proceeds from the event will go towards supporting the Centre’s ongoing work.\\n\\nLineup:\\n\\nAngel d’lite\\nKasra V\\nMia Koden\\nSleepier b2b Impey\\nThe Narrator (Live)\\n\\nOrmside Projects\\nSaturday 12 July 2026\\n7PM–1AM\\n\\nCome dance, connect, and support an important cause.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2481443\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":528,\"name\":\"Disappearing Images (7): Capital City (with Wounder) | Angusraze\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-12T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d39c55888e2633ed52c6694d8003a9f4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":427,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Steatopygous / Render. / Pityspeed / Hiding From Mirrors\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-13T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-13T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"da79c0ee2b41f9b8e2be8778e768f44e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nSteatopygous\\nScreamo mosh youth, blew us all away in Feb so obviously gotta do this again\\n\\nRender.\\nEmotional hardcore epics\\n\\nPityspeed\\nSassy queercore from members of Good Cop and Gender Warfare\\n\\nHiding From Mirrors\\nNew London screamo dreams\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£9\\nDoors 6pm\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/steatopygous-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":671,\"name\":\"Pindrop presents: Folk in the Round\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-13T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-13T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"109ed3aec726eed94e210d0a45b9417a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pindrop Presents: Folk in the Round!\\n\\n::::::\\n\\nEmily Izen Row: Ethereal Folk (full band)!\\n\\nRopeburn: Post Folk Rockers\\n\\nThe Last Whole Earth Catalog: alt ensemble songsmiths of the highest calibre\\n\\nFionnuala Mary Bradbury: Cream of the Crop Singer Songwriter\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2476243\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":208,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Psycho Mosher\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-14T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-14T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1397d32ef6e951462d99932aecc5e612.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nPsycho Mosher\\nCrossover thrash insanity from Colombia!\\n\\n+ Support from\\nRAD\\nBrighton Crossover Thrash\\n\\nEmergency Broadcast\\nStraightedge Hardcore\\n\\nForced To Run\\nNew London metalcore riffs\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£9\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/psycho-mosher\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":711,\"name\":\"Against Apathy // 003 - Towards Direct Action\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-14T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-14T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"005e8a804076d56e626651f1573ff849.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Against Apathy is an event bringing people together to mobilise, get activated, meet others and realise that we all have a role to play in creating change and resisting. This edition will focus on direct action, for various causes. \\n\\nThe event will feature 8 individuals actively involved in direct action in many different ways, spaces and formats, who will share a bit about what they do and how it might be possible to get involved.\\n\\nSpeakers TBA.\\n\\nWe will then break into small groups to get to know each other, discuss how we could use our own skills to do more or get active in new ways, and learn more.\\n\\nThis will be followed by music, and there will be food and drinks available all night from Ridley Road Social Club kitchen. The event will also be a fundraiser (pay what you feel tickets, suggested price £10). \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":609,\"name\":\"Slowly, slowly the tongue unrolls\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-14T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-14T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"295e47fb6c589cec07e47a376c1fc275.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Performance poetry and sound curated by UCL Special Collections and Monitor Books\\n\\nUCL Special Collections and Monitor Books present Slowly, slowly, the tongue unrolls: an evening of poetry and sound bringing together some of the most interesting experimental poets and artists at work today. Inspired by UCL’s internationally renowned Small Press Collections of independently produced literary little magazines, experimental art and poetry, this event will feature performance poetry, sound art and screenings to celebrate 60 years of small press collecting at UCL. It also concludes two projects rooted in these collections: Monitor Books’ tenure as the inaugural UCL 2025 Small Press in Residence, and the 2025 Liberating the Collections Visiting Fellowship held by Andrew Whiteman (AroarA, Apostle of Hustle, Broken Social Scene), for which he focused on rare sound poetry recordings.\\n\\nFree, but booking required\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/slowly-slowly-the-tongue-unrolls-an-evening-of-poetry-and-sound-tickets-1989212716784?aff=oddtdtcreator\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":729,\"name\":\"TRASHHHEAP: Using Trash for Performance\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-15T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-16T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"147bff9cf0808e41abfa1017048dbd4e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"TRASHHHEAP: Using Trash for Performance is a workshop led by Jean and Cabbage the Clown, two alt-drag performers who see trash as treasure. \\n\\nAs drag things (rather than queens or kings), Jean and Cabbage resist commercial and conventional restraints of gender and drag. They explore the worlds of discarded objects and rejected things, animating and embodying mundane items to create fantastical, ridiculous stories and characters. \\n\\nAcross two workshop sessions participants will be supported through the development of a new or existing drag, cabaret or live performance act, using found materials to inspire and create looks, characters, props, and stories.\\n\\nThe first session, on Wed 15 July, will focus on developing a new act in response to a found object. The second session, on Thu 16 July, will involve creating a new physical costume or prop, to bring an act to life. It is possible to attend either or both of the workshop sessions.\\n\\nThe sessions are aimed at practitioners interested in drag, cabaret and alternative comedy and performance modes, who wish to refine their visual identity and to make their practice more sustainable. However, participants from all backgrounds and practices are welcome, and no previous experience is expected or required. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.londonperformancestudios.com/trashhheap\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":690,\"name\":\"POINTS OF DEPARTURE: A Harry Cleaver reader book launch with Robert Ovetz\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-16T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"88775975051e1731e259a49e0f242244.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join Robert Ovetz in launching Points of Departure: Refusal of Work and the Crisis of Capitalism: The Collected Writings of Harry Cleaver (Common Notions 2026)\\n\\n“Refuse work. Revolt against capitalism. Read Harry Cleaver. In that order. Repeat.”\\n\\nPoints of Departure: Refusal of Work and the Crisis of Capitalism: The Collected Writings of Harry Cleaver is a definitive collection of Harry Cleaver’s best unpublished, translated, or lesser known writings on the refusal of work, class composition and “inversion of the class perspective,” the crisis of capitalism. He shows the ongoing necessity of re-reading Marx theory to understand, find points of departure from, and finally end capitalism before it ends us. The reader is co-edited by Robert Ovetz, author, organizer, lecturer and former long-time student of Cleaver, and author and organizer Kevin Van Meter.\\n\\nPoints of Departure will be released on Common Notion Press’s new Class Compositions series in September 2026. A special edition has been released to coincide with the June 2026 Labor Notes conference in Chicago and will have a full release in October 2026. Copies of the special edition of the book will be available for the talk.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.maydayrooms.org/e/96/points-of-departure-a-harry-cleaver-reader-book-launch-with-robert-ovetz\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":598,\"name\":\"Vive Le Punk (1993) Screening\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-16T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"eb9ce8b08c51f82515d9f01354a09a42.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A rare screening of Vive Le Punk [1993], an exclusive documentary made by Roger K Burton, featuring Malcolm McLaren \\u0026 Vivienne Westwood talking in depth about their extraordinary collaboration together, the evolution of their Kings Road shops and those groundbreaking punk designs that took the fashion world by storm between 1971 and 1980. The couple were captured on film at the Horse Hospital on the eve of our very first exhibition, Vive Le Punk. We will also be displaying select pieces featured in the original exhibition.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":599,\"name\":\"Vive Le Punk (1993) Screening\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-16T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"eac5e1d61318cc4c0be0bb3c143865a6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A rare screening of Vive Le Punk [1993], an exclusive documentary made by Roger K Burton, featuring Malcolm McLaren \\u0026 Vivienne Westwood talking in depth about their extraordinary collaboration together, the evolution of their Kings Road shops and those groundbreaking punk designs that took the fashion world by storm between 1971 and 1980. The couple were captured on film at the Horse Hospital on the eve of our very first exhibition, Vive Le Punk. We will also be displaying select pieces featured in the original exhibition.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":346,\"name\":\"Ostraca at the Piehouse | Real Life x Cady\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-16T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"596198007bfe52ecc4af2cc521987db1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life and Cady present\\n\\nOstraca\\nBlackened Skramz legends in the UK for just 2 shows!\\n\\nSupport from\\nCady\\nNegative blastbeat screamo\\n\\nJotnarr\\nRaw screaming crust\\n\\nChristina Carpenter\\nNew London skrim\\n\\n\\nPiehouse Co-Op, nearest stations Deptford or New Cross.\\n\\n£12\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/ostraca\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":721,\"name\":\"What Are We Now, Bullmaera, KAYE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-16T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-16T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f1a9bb92e3f8a617cecbe02a46db52d5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"What Are We Now - Ranging from alternative rock and folk to punk and nu metal their mix really begs the question “what are we now?” With their funky guitars, melodic basslines and aggressive drums they keep it rocking and all they want to do is play, play and play.\\n\\nBullmaera - Are a 4 piece punk-rock influenced band based in London. They have been consistently  gigging throughout London and plan to continue this throughout the year. Their independently released first EP ‘China Shop’ consists of 5 songs and they plan to release more in the near future. \\n\\nKAYE - Dream grunge trio, blending noisy instrumentals with ethereal vocal melodies.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":635,\"name\":\"Michael Speers | Mosquito Farm | Li Song + Regan Bowering + Conal Blake\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-17T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-17T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cb9dae0c9ab4c88c61f2338927922944.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Performances from Michael Speers, Mosquito Farm, Li Song + Regan Bowering + Conal Blake\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":758,\"name\":\"Bassweight Cuts \\u0026 NLDC: 'For The Youth' Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-17T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cff3078b496a6b99121e214dce239388.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Substrada x Ekstr x 11th Hour\\nTeffa\\nWiwson\\nTenshu x Shan\\nWBash x River\\n\\n\\nWe are extremely proud to announce our first collaborative event with NLDC, and our first ever event in the UK. We are picking up what we started with our For The Youth charity compilation, and turning it into a live fundraiser event. All of the artists involved will be participating for the cause and all funds raised will be donated to injured and displaced children in Palestine and Lebanon. This wouldn't be possible without the support of NLDC who have graciously offered to host and run this event free of charge at Cu in Dalston, London.\\nWe personally wanna give a big shoutout to them, all of the artists on our For The Youth charity compilation, and all of the artists who will be performing at this event. Without you guys none of this would be possible.\\n\\nThis is a limited capacity event. On the door ticket sales only. All funds will be donated to people who need it more than we do. Come show some support and enjoy an incredible night of Dubstep for the youth.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":517,\"name\":\"Awake All Hours presents: Conrad Pack (Live), Caroune, St. Amp, szoryn\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-17T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a5f561ae2ccc78469495432aea81c9fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nAwake All Hours returns for a back-to-basics club event at Tottenham’s newest venue, radial.\\n\\nFriday 17 July\\n10pm-3am\\n£11 adv\\n\\nConrad Pack (Live)\\nCaroune\\nSt. Amp\\nszoryn\\n\\nWe are very excited to welcome dub techno brutalist and SELN Recordings co-founder Conrad Pack for a live set. His work brings together stepping four-four dub, hard-edged industrial techno, and weird, haunting melodies to craft some of the most compelling sounds in London’s underground.\\n\\nWe’re also joined by Osmura co-founder and low end psychedelia specialist Caroune, who will bring bpm-spanning bass weight, as well as andandand’s szoryn and resident St. Amp.\\n\\nAs always, if you are on low income you can send us a message via Instagram or email for a cheap ticket link. No one turned away for lack of funds.\\n\\nradial address: 39b Markfield Rd, N154QA, London, United Kingdom\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":741,\"name\":\"ÜNDERGØDS 11\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-17T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"443ef9bce55851a286543dbb63fb88ec.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lord Tusk of UltraWaveVisions sets in motion the Eleventh installment entitled ÜNDERGØDS which is a term used to describe the highly talented but underrated underdog, the immaculate Undergoddesses and Undergods.\\n\\nFeaturing some of my favourite Top underground selectors from London:\\n\\nLaurie Lynch\\nLord Tusk\\nAnnabel Fraiser\\nBahamian Moor\\n———————————————\\n∆ Resident Ündergøds selector Laurie Lynch a.k.a LL will provide his signature style of music to uplift entice, stimulate and get you dancing.\\n\\n∆ Annabel Fraiser will be debuting her first time at Ündergøds proving an incredible selection of eclectic and deep esoteric vibrations. She was designed to play this nite and we’re excited to finally have her on board.\\n\\n∆ Finally I present one of my favourite and most cherished selectors to the turntables ‘Bahamian Moor’ for there long awaited return. Expect nothing but the best.\\n\\n∆ Your host Lord Tusk will be the anchor and middle earth between the guest, playing unreleased music and a new music for all subterraneans and abyss dwellers.\\n\\n———————————————\\n\\nAll folly will be relinquished for this event of unapologetic music beyond most peoples perceived recognition, unmerciful audio waves providing eclectic stimuli and a night of adequate debauchery\\n\\nThis event is for the those who seek alternative experience and unheard inspirational shit! If you looking for basic bitch music this is not for you however all are welcome.\\n\\nFriday 17th July\\n11-6am\\n@ormsideprojects\\nSE15 1TR\\n\\n£11.50 Early bird tickets\\n£15 on the door\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2458404\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":676,\"name\":\"The Dynasty of Dub\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"343d6858d196384f2b577f7bd11cb8c8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Green Urban Music prsents; The Dynasty of Dub.\\n\\n8 hours of conscious Roots Reggae, Dub from 1pm to 9pm on Saturday the 18th of July, at the Dance Hall Club, 1 Navigator Square, London N19 3TD .\\n\\nIt is a stone throw from Archway Tube.\\n\\nSelectors on the day \\n\\nThe legendary Shere Khan with Ras Terry Gad blessing proceedings on the mic\\n\\nProviding the vibrations of inspiration and wisdom  will be Jah Prophecy \\n\\nDean Dubs from FuzionliveRadio whole heap of tunes.\\n\\nThe impressive young and upcoming selector Leo Roots \\n\\nFor this event  selectors will be playing on the Dance Hall's very highly quality Club System. \\n\\nDon't miss out on this ital session..\\n\\nCome and edify your heart  mind and soul.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.skiddle.com/whats-on/London/The-Dance-Hall/The-Dynasty-of-Dub/42509506/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":636,\"name\":\"TALK: Michael Speers \\u0026 Regan Bowering Talking About Drums\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T15:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bccb7ee4ac9034d7bb29059f4ff6469b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Researchers and musicians Michael Speers and Regan Bowering talking about drums\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":752,\"name\":\"BCA Youth Programme’s Celebration of Black Spirituality \\u0026 Liberation\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T17:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d712dda6f9c631dd024b812e2dd5759f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"One month before Carnival, join the BCA Youth Programme for a celebration of Black Spirituality and Liberation. This one-off building-wide activation will include a pop-up exhibition, short film and ‘Black Life, Black Sounds’ listening session exploring the intersection of spirituality, music, Carnival and political consciousness within the Black British community.\\n\\nCurated by Black Cultural Archives’ Youth Programme, a network of 18-25-year-olds of African and Caribbean heritage looking to make their first steps into the arts and heritage sector, this is an event you don’t want to miss!\\n\\nEvent schedule\\n\\n1:00 PM – Doors and pop-up exhibition open\\n\\n1:30–2:30 PM – Catered lunch\\n\\n3:00–3:45 PM – Film screening\\n\\n4:00–4:45 PM – 'Black Life, Black Sounds' listening session\\n\\n5:30 PM – Doors and pop-up exhibition close\\n\\nWhilst the event is free, we ask that you consider donating to Black Cultural Archives. All proceeds go to BCA, allowing us to further our impact in the communities we serve.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://blackculturalarchives.org/events/black-spirituality-liberation\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":468,\"name\":\"KONTEKST Film Festival 2026: ENTANGLEMENTS\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-19T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9e404905fb3dc572394b1f051fe7c459.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"KONTEKST Film Festival is back! A team of emerging curators and grassroots organisers have put together a festival of experimental and ethnographic film, art and thought by up-and-coming artists, researchers and makers again. This year’s festival will take place on the 18th and 19th of July at Conway Hall in Central London, and explore the theme \\\"Entanglements\\\"; engaging with multispecies encounters and relationships, and complicating the keyword “nature”. \\n\\nFrom microbial ecologies to interspecies care, or environmental collapse to queer kinship with plants and animals; KONTEKST now wants to showcase critical art that subverts the mechanised, hierarchical, sanitised constraints of our anthropocentric reality. Our open call saw over 250 submissions from across the world, and our final programme entangles and disentangles relationships across species, the ever-underestimated complexity of our ecosystems, and global interconnection steeped in politics, technology and violence. \\n \\nWe look forward to a weekend of film, installation, workshops and live performance. At the forefront of our event is connection, accessibility and a hope that you might leave the venue with a slightly different perspective than you came in with.\\n\\nCheck out the full programme on our website and get your tickets now!\\n\\nKEY INFO:\\nLocation: Conway Hall, 25 Red Lion Square, WC1R 4RL, London.\\nOpening times: Sat 13:00-22:30; Sun 13:00-18:00\\nTickets: Saturday (main day) is ticketed, entry on Sunday is free.\\nAccess: See the FAQ section on our website.\\n\\nAFTERPARTY: \\nJoin us for the festival afterparty starting at 6:30pm on Sunday 19th at Coven Headquarters (30 Old Compton Street, W1D 4UR London). Please note the tickets to the afterparty are SEPARATE from the festival tickets, and are £5 for our festival guests, and £10 for everyone else!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.conwayhall.org.uk/whats-on/event/kontekst-film-fest/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":743,\"name\":\"Montez x Forma Summer Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d37c849caf0f2d81fb5762fc30d41905.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for our annual summer party, this year in collaboration with Montez Press.\\n\\nTo celebrate their four month residency at FormaHQ, we are co-curating a special day-long event with Montez Press and Montez Press Radio in our rooftop garden on Great Dover Street. Featuring performances, installations and readings from:\\n\\nNWAKKE\\nD Mortimer\\nSoledad Santana\\nKaz De Roiste\\nJosh Quinton\\nDream Sequence\\nBabeworld\\nJames Jordan Johnson\\nM Lissoni\\nKrystle Patel\\nJala Wahid (Slow Crush)\\n+ more to be announced\\n\\n\\nCome along for drinks, food and fun. Montez Press Radio will be broadcasting live throughout the day.\\n\\nFree entry, everyone welcome!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfyLrAFGWV6ijpOp9ummIssNvw5AD4WKmPayjAkCcyrbDErQA/viewform?mc_cid=3f931055cc\\u0026mc_eid=b2fe007f4a\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":744,\"name\":\"Ain Bailey: Sonic Stories\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T17:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"365455832c2664efcfea09f6828b077a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ain Bailey’s Sonic Stories workshop takes as its starting point Maybe It’s Because I’m A Londoner, Bailey with Elaine Mitchener’s Art On The Underground commission. The project's genesis reflects on Bailey’s recounting of the loss of more than 70 important cultural, social and community spaces across London over the last 50 years. \\n\\nAcross cities, and London in particular, music venues, community centres, clubs, informal meeting places and artist-led spaces have faced increasing pressures from redevelopment, rising costs and changing patterns of urban life. These losses are not simply physical; they also affect networks of care, shared histories, cultural memory and collective identity.\\n\\nThrough listening, sound, conversation, and collective reflection, we will explore and reflect on the erasure of places of gathering, creativity and belonging, and what is at stake when they disappear.\\n\\nThis iteration of Sonic Stories is presented as part of The Trembling City: Sound, Cities, and Spatial Justice, a series of workshops and public programmes conceived by sonic theorist Gascia Ouzounian and developed with Ibraaz as part of the Sonorous Cities project.\\n\\nWe invite participants to share 2/3 sounds and sonic moments from their lives that have particular resonances, and that speak to these important and much missed spaces.\\n\\nExpressions of Interest\\n\\nTo participate in the workshops, please submit the following to soncitiesproject@gmail.com\\n\\n-  Name and contact details\\n\\n-  A short statement (around 50-100 words) describing your interest and motivations for attending. If relevant, please also include details of your research or creative practice background.\\n\\nPlease send your expression of interest by July 9. \\n\\nPhoto: Katarzyna Perlak\\n\\nAin Bailey is a composer, artist and DJ. She facilitates workshops considering the role of sound in the formation of identity, and the exploration of memory and sound. In 2020 Bailey and Ego Ahaiwe Sowinski created a composition and print entitled Remember To Exhale for Studio Voltaire, London. Previous exhibitions include And We’ll Always Be A Disco In The Glow Of Love, Cubitt Gallery, London (2019); Version, Wysing Arts Centre, Cambridge (2021); Atlantic Railton which was part of the Listening To The City sound installation programme in the 2021 Serpentine Pavilion; Untitled: Our Wedding for the Black Melancholia exhibition at CCS Bard (2022), New York, USA and Trioesque for Bruckenmusik 27 in Cologne, Germany (2022), the installation Four (2024) for FACT Liverpool’s Resolution research project. The most recent commission was The Jamaica Project (2026 )for Camden Art Centre, London. She was the 2022-23 Cavendish Arts Science Fellow at Girton College, University of Cambridge. In June 2026, she opened her sound commission with Elaine Mitchener for Art On The Underground at Waterloo Station.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/ain-bailey-sonic-stories\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":312,\"name\":\"~\\\\\\\\LILITH//~ ¤¸¸.•´¯`•¸¸.•..\\u003e\\u003e 🎀 𝒷𝒶𝓉𝒽𝑒 𝒾𝓃 𝒸𝓊𝓅𝒾𝒹’𝓈 𝓰𝓸𝓸❀ 🎀 \\u003e\\u003e..•.¸¸•`¯´•.¸¸¤\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"baaeea21ccb631e41e7d4e71c9f02daf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"lilith luvrs invite you to\\n¤¸¸.•´¯`•¸¸.•..\\u003e\\u003e   🎀  𝒷𝒶𝓉𝒽𝑒 𝒾𝓃 𝒸𝓊𝓅𝒾𝒹’𝓈 𝓰𝓸𝓸❀  🎀   \\u003e\\u003e..•.¸¸•`¯´•.¸¸¤\\n\\n🌀north london - riverside party spot 🌀 we writhe under a willow tree 🧚🏻‍♂️\\n\\nevent location sent to ticket holders the day before\\n\\n🍬˜”°•.˜”°• CUPID’s SELECTORS •°”˜.•°”˜🍬\\n\\nㅤꨄ︎ miu miu brings melted sounds and boundary pushing bass entanglements to our little water side spot all the way from NEW YORK \\nLISTEN: https://youtu.be/UMXvMEN--q4?si=vcgbr4sjMyoOiSAE\\n\\nㅤꨄ︎ DJ GONZ, artist, producer and DJ brings moody steppers and deep rumbling sonics that vibrate across your body  \\nLISTEN: https://selnrecordings.bandcamp.com/album/magical-negro-overdrive\\n\\nㅤꨄ︎ Unknown Niece no genre left untouched, south London cutie, creator of flowers club night and host of SLIPPYVISION radio show \\nLISTEN: https://youtu.be/xoya0Gz2B2o?si=lBOrbX3VtpKPFHzr\\n\\nㅤꨄ︎ GRADY STEELE, experimental artist, and founder of indelible Formant Sound System powering Lilith all day long\\nLISTEN: https://youtu.be/outfzSGy_OQ?si=luDW4SN1WQppXhOf\\n\\n+++ lilith luvrs \\n\\nㅤꨄ︎ Love infused performance by Apocalyptrixx \\n\\n🥵cupid’s pursuits (more tba)👀\\n★jelly wrestling \\n★sauna\\n★basic bitch bbq\\n\\n★Powered by Formant Sound System \\u003c3\\n\\n______\\n\\nThis event is paid for out of our own thinning pockets. We would love to be able to pay our artists (crazy, I know), and putting on events (especially outside of the clurbbb) is not cheap! \\n\\nWe just about break even if everyone spends £15 on  a ticket and buys a drink or 2 from our (cheap!) bar. If you’re feeling flush we have a £20 option. A ticket gets you access to the best party ever and also food from the bbq, snacks, sauna and cute activities and music all day long. If you’re lucky you may even get shot by cupid’s arrow 💋 we thank you for your service to silliness x\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":719,\"name\":\"TCB - The Toni Cade Bambara School of Organizing\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T14:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2630e4debc30920886ae647b96136cc0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Overview\\nA biography of the Black feminist writer, filmmaker and cultural worker, whose life became a masterclass in art, community, and resistance.\\n\\n\\nTCB - The Toni Cade Bambara School of Organizing (2025, 105 minutes) is a biography of the influential writer, filmmaker and cultural worker, who with humor and deep insight, inspired a generation of artists to dedicate themselves to community empowerment. The film is structured as a series of lessons on cultural organizing, gleaned from Bambara's life and shared by her friends, colleagues and students.\\n\\nThis is the second screening of of HCC's Summer Programme Making the Revolution Irresistible.\\n\\nAbout the film \\u0026 filmmakers\\n\\nTrailer (on the official film site).\\n\\nAWARDS\\n\\nBest Feature Documentary (Juried)\\n2025 BlackStar Film Festival (USA)\\n\\nBest Feature Documentary (Audience)\\n2025 BlackStar Film Festival (USA)\\n\\nFeature Documentary – Award of Excellence in Creativity\\n2025 Seventh Art Independent International Film Festival (India)\\n\\nAudience Choice Award\\n2026 Seattle Black Film Festival (USA)\\n\\n\\n\\nLOUIS MASSIAH: Director \\u0026 Producer\\n\\nLouis Massiah is a documentary filmmaker and the founder of the Scribe Video Center in\\n\\nPhiladelphia, He has developed production methodologies that assist first time makers author their own stories, including the Precious Places Community History project, a collection of 150 documentaries; Muslim Voices of Philadelphia; The Great Migration - A City Transformed, and The Tenants of Lenapehocking in the Age of Magnets.\\n\\nMassiah’s documentaries include The Bombing of Osage Avenue, W.E.B. Du Bois – A Biography in Four Voices, Cecil B. Moore, two films for the Eyes on the Prize II series, A is for Anarchist, B is for Brown and TCB – The Toni Cade Bambara School of Organizing.\\n\\n\\n\\nMONICA HENRIQUEZ: Director \\u0026 Editor\\n\\n\\n\\nMonica Henriquez is a Venezuelan/Dutch freelance film and video editor/director, based in the UK since 1978. She trained at the BBC in the 1980s, and worked as an editor for Channel Four (UK) in several projects on Latin America, notably the Marc Karlin Nicaragua Series (1985-1991); Faction Films Fidel (1998). For the U.S. network PBS, she was editor of WEB Du Bois – A Biography in Four Voices (1995), and was researcher/associate producer of The Hugo Chavez Show Frontline (2008). She was Producer/Director of Gynecological Chronicles (1992) and Director/Editor of Murder \\u0026 the Feather Boa (1996), both for Channel Four UK. Recently she was the Editor/Director with Louis Massiah as Producer/Director of TCB - The Toni Cade Bambara School of Organizing.\\n\\n\\n\\nAbout our Guest Speakers\\n\\n\\nDr SM Rodriguez is a scholar-activist and Assistant Professor of Gender, Rights and Human Rights at LSE's Department of Gender Studies. Their research examines the impact of racialisation, criminalisation, ableism, and gendered and sexual control on people of African descent. Their first monograph, The Economies of Queer Inclusion: Transnational Organizing for LGBTI Rights in Uganda (2019), analysed the effects of transnational advocacy on Ugandan LGBTI organising during the period in which Uganda's \\\"Kill the Gays Bill\\\" was under consideration.\\n\\nTheir current work explores the globalisation of abolitionist feminist praxis and the political processes shaping gender and sexual identification, including the Nonbinary Identity Project. They have also launched Black Queer Movements, a global knowledge-exchange hub for LGBTIQ activists of African descent, and The Black Professors Pipeline, a UK racial equity initiative in higher education.\\n\\n\\n\\nMonica Henriquez is a Venezuelan/Dutch freelance film and video editor/director, based in the UK since 1978. She trained at the BBC in the 1980s, and worked as an editor for Channel Four (UK) in several projects on Latin America, notably the Marc Karlin Nicaragua Series (1985-1991); Faction Films Fidel (1998). For the U.S. network PBS, she was editor of WEB Du Bois – A Biography in Four Voices (1995), and was researcher/associate producer of The Hugo Chavez Show Frontline (2008). She was Producer/Director of Gynecological Chronicles (1992) and Director/Editor of Murder \\u0026 the Feather Boa (1996), both for Channel Four UK. Recently she was the Editor/Director with Louis Massiah as Producer/Director of TCB - The Toni Cade Bambara School of Organizing.\\n\\nBooking / Waiting List / Cancellation\\n\\n\\nPlease only book if you are confident you will be able to attend, as seating at this venue is limited. Due to safety regulations, walk-in entry cannot be guaranteed.\\n\\nThe registration form includes a small number of questions collected for reporting purposes. All data will be anonymised. Each attendee is required to complete the form. If you are booking on behalf of someone else and do not know an answer, please enter or select' N/A' where applicable.\\n\\nDue to the venue’s limited capacity, the event may sell out.If this happens, you can be added to the waiting list. When a ticket becomes available, you will receive an email to book it, and you will have 24 hours to complete your booking.\\n\\nIf you are unable to attend the event, please cancel your ticket(s) so that your place can be offered to someone else.\\n\\nWhy your donations are important?\\n\\nPlease read carefully! We’re introducing a Community Pricing to help cover the costs of our events. Choose the ticket tier that best reflects your current circumstances— considering income, housing, caring responsibilities, health, and day-to-day financial pressures. We trust you to choose what feels right. More on this system here.\\n\\nHCC is run by volunteers and does not receive any funding at the moment. Every donation you make will help us to support local venues and to organise other free screenings.\\n\\nIn a time of rising living costs and persistent barriers for marginalised communities in producing and accessing films that reflect their experiences and aspirations, we are committed to making our screenings free or pay-what-you-can.\\n\\nAbout the venue\\n\\nLordship Hub is a vibrant community centre and café at the heart of Lordship Rec, Tottenham’s largest park. The building is fully accessible, but located inside the park. If you need to be dropped off next to the building's main entrance (with the ramp), please contact us early so we can arrange the park's gate to be open. If you have any accessibility needs or questions, please contact us at haringeycommunitycinema@gmail.com.\\n\\nAbout HCC\\n\\nHaringey Community Cinema (HCC) was launched in April 2025 and is run by volunteers. Inspired by Brixton Community Cinema, HCC is aimed at bringing residents of Haringey together through film. Our mission is to showcase films that challenge, inspire, and spark critical reflection—films that make us think and act. Visit our website.\\n\\n\\n\\nAbout Haringey \\u0026 Tottenham For a Free Palestine\\nOrganising in Haringey and Tottenham in solidarity with Palestine. To follow us: Instagram.\\n\\nCovid Policy\\n\\nHCC does not currently have an official COVID-19 policy. However, we remain mindful that many people are still vulnerable to the virus. We kindly ask attendees to take the following precautions to help keep our events safe and accessible for everyone:\\n\\nIf possible, please take a lateral flow test before attending.\\nIf you test positive or are experiencing any COVID-19 symptoms, please do not attend, even if you feel well.\\nWe welcome and encourage the use of masks inside the venue for those who wish to wear them.\\nPlease be considerate of others' comfort levels and respect requests for physical distance.\\nThank you for helping us create a safer and more inclusive space.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/tcb-the-toni-cade-bambara-school-of-organizing-registration-1991305021925\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":553,\"name\":\"Koshari \",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-19T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d1e8ac122af7625490dbacf9c5694c80.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Remember our parties at the Post Bar? Dancing from sunshine into the early hours? A distant memory since that beloved Tottenham venue shut down suddenly earlier this year, but what if we told you there was a campaign to reopen the Post as a community-run music venue, and that you could contribute to this campaign by... coming to this event?\\n\\nMeet us at @distillery.n17 on 18 July for a classic Koshari day/night party to raise funds for @friendsofpost. We're really excited to be playing at Distillery for the first time - we've got the place from 4-4, and we'll be joined by a crack team of guest DJs to put fuel on the fire. Don't miss this one.\\n\\n@sofieok__\\n@izzi_thein\\n@poisonzcora\\n@eda_seyhan\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":688,\"name\":\"Housing Reading Series: Huw Lemmey In Conversation With Juliet Jacques\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"23e29575b265bbd49402eba0364aa868.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Aren’t you just SICK of gay fiction about nice boys just trying their best? BORED\\nof the sort of cosy political satire that makes Alistair Campbell chuckle?\\n\\nFINALLY! After years of waiting, Huw Lemmey’s cult classics are back in print::\\nCHUBZ: The Demonization of My Working Arse and RED TORY: My Corbyn Chemsex Hell,\\ntwo novels of terrifying predictive force and eye-watering sexual potency, an antidote\\nto the grimly worthy bourgeois queer novels and tedious political fiction of our time.\\nLemmey’s novels depict the loopy political world of the past decade with the power\\nof a vicious Cassandra, imagining a world of Brexit and Trump, PM’s Boris and Nigel,\\nyears before they came to pass. Set within a London gripped between authoritarianism\\nand a genuine rupture in the healthy sexual order of things, CHUBZ and RED TORY\\nremain the sleeper hits of our time, quietly seeding disquiet and insurrection into the\\nover-stimulated lizard brain and under-stimulated rectal ampulla of the GREAT British Public.\\n\\nObscene? Potentially. Criminal? Maybe. Sick? Probably. But worth buying? UNDENIABLY!\\n\\nJoin the author LIVE and IN FULL FLESHY PERSONHOOD at Housmans, in conversation\\nwith the esteemed political-cultural powerhouse Juliet Jacques, to discuss these arse-warping,\\nmind-bending SATIRES FOR OUR TIME. Run, don’t walk!\\n\\nThis is a free event, but if you would like to reserve a copy of the book(s), you can saw so through the ticket portal\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/housing-reading-series-huw-lemmey-in-conversation-with-juliet-jacques/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":590,\"name\":\"Złom with excel dj, new flesh, Wash Electra, london community laptop orchestra\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-18T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4429fe816ec5e1dd2e77101629508932.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"an experimental sonic scrap yard\\n\\nwe return to spanners once again ♪˞͛◖₍ᐢ. ̫.ᐢ₎◗˞͛♪\\n\\nzłom - Polish for 'scrap metal' - is a series of musical gatherings across London, mixing live acts and djs across genres\\n\\nwith:\\n\\nexcel dj\\n\\n\\\"i have something to offer, i'm not in control\\nmusic releases and other objects found on web-site.lol, glint music, lost domain if i get round to it lol, bandcamp, soulseek, and just like hanging out with friends and shit\\\"\\n\\nnew flesh\\n\\nNew Flesh's output as a producer and DJ works to combine a background in Hardcore, Power Electronics and Metal with EBM, Electro and Deconstructed Club. This brings a wide range of sounds focused more towards texture and mood than any single genre or style.\\n\\nwash electra\\n\\nWash Electra is a London-based DJ, promoter and radio host. He is\\nthe founder of art collective and record label inklingroom, and hosts a monthly residency on Noods Radio.\\n\\nHis sets drift between leftfield-bass music, halftime rhythms and\\nwhatever else feels right at the time. Less interested in genres than\\nhow things are connected, he leans on atmosphere, percussion and\\nlow-end pressure to keep things moving.\\n\\nHe has played across London and the UK at venues including FOLD, The Cause, The Glove That Fits, Strange Brew and Space289, alongside artists such as GAIKA, upsammy, object blue, μ-Ziq, Silvia Kastel, LYZZA, Flora Yin-Wong, Osheyack and DJ Narciso.\\n\\nlondon community laptop orchestra\\n\\nThe London Community Laptop Orchestra (LCLO), is an all-abilities laptop ensemble and research project. Participation is central to the group with audiences invited into the learning process, exploring the limitations of their own devices to better understand how contemporary technological systems function. We are open to anyone, no experience required. Only a laptop.\\n\\nWe invite the audience to bring their laptops as well and be involved in whatever piece we are doing :)\\n\\n7 - midnight ˚‧º·( 。ᗒ ‸ ◕✿)\\n\\nnotaflof (dm us for a reduced cost ticket)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2464514\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":595,\"name\":\"ENDPHORIA: LOVE IS THE END \",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-18T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-19T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6caf89423116f6f8fbfe271198c5c5f9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"London’s new intelligence-agency-funded party series XPHORIA announces its inaugural non-transactional networking “Black Site” for the soul: LOVE IS THE END, featuring deep-state citypop, Bureaucratic Sublime ambient, black-budget trip-hop, and angelic data-exfiltration pop.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":769,\"name\":\"KONTEKST Film Festival Afterparty\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-19T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-19T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"493eaec79dfe4ccadec3e93514fe1961.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us this Sunday 19 July for the final act of KONTEKST Film Festival 2026: an evening of funky tunes and rhythm that defies genres and blends trance, electro, afrotech, (cunty) techno, deep bass-driven grooves and more! 💥🎶🪩\\n\\nSpotlighting a diverse line-up of talented early-career DJs, we hope to create an atmosphere of community, connection and celebration after our conceptually-engaging 2-day programme of the grassroots-focused festival of ethnographic and experimental film, art and thought!\\n\\nIn order to qualify for a discounted £5 afterparty ticket, make sure you come to the festival either on Saturday 18 or Sunday 19 July. Otherwise the standard entry is £10.\\n\\nOn the decks:\\n\\nPolly Chronic - https://soundcloud.com/pollychronic\\nMIMI - https://www.mixcloud.com/Mimi_Bouvier/\\nPetru B - https://soundcloud.com/badea-petru\\n\\nSKYE - https://soundcloud.com/skyyyyyyyyyyyyyye\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/pynbok-kontekst-kff2026-official-afterparty-19th-jul-coven-central-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":634,\"name\":\"Mapping Resistance: An evening of collective listening to Gazan voices with Ambient Gaza, Shahd Alnaami \\u0026 Rim Irscheid.\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-19T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5faeb4c1bbb86b64ea0e1b114d680ce7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Combining engaged listening and banner making, this interactive listening session makes audible the testimony of Palestinians in Gaza, from singing on Gaza beach, to a beloved bookshop in Gaza City, to an aunt’s farmland in Rafah. Words materialise on textile while sounding in space, highlighting the importance of engaging with all our senses to understand the lived experience of Gazans under occupation and genocide. Following this session, join poet and writer Shad Alnaami (in Gaza via Zoom), art collective Ambient Gaza, and textile artist Rim Irscheid to discuss Gazan life, challenge dehumanising media representation, and celebrate stories and joyous experiences. Participants will be able to leave responses to Gazans to share thoughts and wishes with communities who generously share their stories with us.\\n\\nDoors are at 6pm, please note that the listening session starts at 7.30pm promptly.\\n\\nThe event is free, but registration is required. All optional donations will go to Gazan aid through Ambient Gaza's trusted networks. Find out more about their work at www.ambientgaza.org. \\n\\nBios:\\n\\nAmbient Gaza centres the voices and lived experiences of Palestinians in Gaza and beyond. Through ambient recordings, oral testimonies and music, the project serves to cut through representations of Gaza coloured by media violence and spectacle, offering instead a deeply personal and place-based archive of sound. The project is rooted in a radical politics of listening, with features in Glastonbury 2025, We Are Not Numbers, Another Sky Festival, Cafe Oto and Radio Al Hara. The project continues to grow through new living archives, site-based soundscapes, and creative collaborations.\\n\\nShahd Alnaami is a Palestinian writer, translator, and workshop facilitator from Gaza. She studies English Literature and Translation at the Islamic University of Gaza. She is the author of The Writings of Shahd Alnaami and However Fragile. Her work has been published by Al Jazeera, We Are Not Numbers, The Electronic Intifada, and other international platforms. She also works with AWID as an Arabic-English translator. Alongside her writing and translation work, she facilitates workshops exploring a variety of themes connected to storytelling, reflection, memory, and community.\\n\\nRim Irscheid is an ethnomusicologist, curator and textile artist working with hand embroidery, field recordings and found materials. Combining ethnographic research, curatorial practice and arts-based methods, her work looks at artist-led institution building, emotional aspects of creative labour and interpretations of care in curatorial activism. Some of her research-based articles and essays can be found in Sonic Matter, field notes Berlin and Norient. Her mixed media installations address sensory aspects of memory making and ambivalent feelings towards ‘home’ and have been exhibited at Cafe OTO, Modern Art Oxford and London Design Festival.\\n\\n\\nThe event has been generously supported through the Public Engagement Small Grant of King’s Doctoral College and comes out of the UKRI/ERC-funded Beyond1932 research project at King’s College London (award reference EP/X022749/1).\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/mapping-resistance-an-evening-of-collective-listening-to-gazan-voices-tickets-1992085675882\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":645,\"name\":\"Seaming To | Marcia Bassett | Victoria Keddie\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-19T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Seaming To is described by BBC Radio 1 as “the voice of the 21st century” and by Robert Wyatt as truly “avant-garde”, Seaming’s solo work moves between voice, electronics, avant-pop, composition and cinematic sound-worlds. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":792,\"name\":\"The Reopening of Losing A Home by Paul Majek\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-20T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-28T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bc1f1af260032c9c68f172f1e1d5cee4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We are delighted to announce the reopening of Losing A Home, a solo exhibition by @paul_majek , curated by @ritamajek of @m0ji.hq , as part of the @whitechapelgallery Backyard Biennial: East.\\n\\nFollowing an incredible first run, we’re honoured to bring the exhibition back from 20–28 July 2026, giving those who were unable to experience it the first time another opportunity to step inside this deeply personal exploration of memory, home and belonging.\\n\\nThrough layered paintings, sculptural installations and personal archives, Losing A Home explores the emotional and spiritual weight of displacement, where physical absence merges with inner dislocation. Set within the domestic architecture of @houseofannetta , the exhibition transforms the space into an immersive environment where sound, scent, light, family objects and archival memories come together to extend the conversations within the artworks.\\n\\nTo celebrate the exhibition’s final week, we warmly invite you to LOSING A HOME: THE FINISSAGE on Friday 24 July, 6–9pm. An evening marking the close of the exhibition with friends, conversation and reflection. We’d love to see you there!\\n\\nPlease RSVP via the link in our bio.\\n\\nExhibition Dates: 20–28 July 2026\\nFinissage: Friday 24 July 2026 | 6–9pm\\nLocation: House of Annetta, 25 Princelet Street, London, E1 6QH\\n\\nWhether you’re returning or visiting for the first time, we hope you’ll join us for this special reopening and closing celebration.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://moji.artsvp.com/dda746\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":724,\"name\":\"The Man with the Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-20T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"427b7f9238e3275b33b1535d27bf8224.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\" John Bird — The Big Issue\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, with Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza, Andrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others and the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\n\\nAlso with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":772,\"name\":\"Para-Phrase #3\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-20T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-20T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"30e9c1368cbb37ccba9449fe3b816661.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Para-Phrase is a performance series for works that sit between disciplines and resist a single mode of attention. Curated by Zhuo Mengting, the series brings together artists working across sound, words, voice, body, image, object and action, creating encounters where different practices remain in tension, overlap, interrupt and reshape one another, and unsettling how audiences are invited to look and listen.\\n\\nThis edition features the UK premiere of Diana Lola Posani’s growling performance SCREAM AS IF YOUR ORGANS WERE MADE OF GLASS, the UK premiere of Jamie Man’s live electronics and film projection set WHEN THE RAINBOW BECOMES SKIN, and a new collaboration between Mengting Zhuo and Jiaying Kou.\\n\\nAn evening of feminised, marginal and non-normative forms of voice and presence, with the artists’ bodies producing unstable forms of address through extreme vocal technique, embodied action and noise in electronic and unamplified forms:\\n\\n— Vibrant matter rising from internal darkness — voice given to a suspended body — signal and meaning lost and found at the threshold —\\n\\nTrigger warning: the event contains images of flesh-hook suspension and full frontal nudity\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/para-phrase-3-diana-lola-posani-jamie-man-mengting/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":753,\"name\":\"HOUSMANS POETRY SERIES: JD HOWSE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-21T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"07a7c55e6c9a372b819582636ed61f23.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"It starts with the Buggery Act of 1533. Or perhaps the arrest of Eleanor Rykener. Or perhaps the execution of James Pratt and John Smith. The truism goes that queer people have always been here, but for as long as there have been written records of us those records have dealt with our suppression, criminalisation, and punishment. How can we construct a sense of our own history when its wilful erasure has been violently enacted time and time again across the centuries? \\n\\nComposed over a ten year period, Noises Again is a hugely ambitious and staggeringly complex literary collage that blurs the lines between literature and visual art. Stringing together scraps of text from history books and pornographic novels, newspaper clippings and love letters, drunk sexts and court records, JD Howse explores the buried, obscure ephemera of gay history and returns with a text by turns violent, tragic, erotic, and confounding. This is a truly singular book, defying characterisation, description, and logic. \\n\\nOUR POETS\\nJD Howse is a writer who works across poetry, prose, and collage. His debut collection Just Meat Not God was published in 2022 and he has published a number of pamphlets and artist’s books. He has a BA in English and an MA in Creative Writing from Royal Holloway, University of London, and is the curator of Permeable Barrier. \\n\\nAzad Ashim Sharma is the director of the87press and Editor at Philosophy and Global Affairs, the CLR James Journal, and The Hythe Review. He is a PhD Candidate in English and Humanities at Birkbeck College, University of London. He is the author of three poetry collections, most recently, Boiled Owls (Nightboat Books / Out-Spoken Press, 2024) which was shortlisted for the Jhalak Poetry Prize. His second collection Ergastulum: Vignettes of Lost Time (Broken Sleep Books, 2022) was the recipient of the Caribbean Philosophical Association’s Guillén Award. In July 2025, Azad was inaugurated as the Poet Laureate of the Caribbean Philosophical Association. He lives in South London.\\n\\nCalliope Michail is a poet and translator, currently undertaking a PhD at King’s College, London. She is the Poetry Editor of Stillpoint Journal, and her work has appeared in various publications.\\n\\nVJ René is the author of two pamphlets of poetry, Scavengers (Salo Press, 2021) and HYDRA (Marble Poetry, 2020). Recent critical and creative works appear in Victorian Popular Fictions Journal, Forum Journal and the Australasian Journal of Victorian Studies.​\\n\\nOliver Zarandi is a writer and filmmaker. His debut, Soft Fruit In The Sun (Hexus Press), was described as being like ‘getting a hug from David Cronenberg.’ His follow-up, Body Horror, was shortlisted for the Prototype Prize in 2024. He is currently in development on his first film, Skinny Boy.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/housmans-poetry-series-jd-howse/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":742,\"name\":\"East End Voices: Community, Activism and Identity\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-22T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-22T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4fe06d9d4c2a1f711ad9f331a2a6120d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join Four Corners, London Community Video Archive and Oitij-Jo Collective for an afternoon of screenings and discussion.\\n\\nThis screening event showcases shorts that engage with community, activism and identity from the 1970s to the present, drawing on archive material including a community video magazine, a documentary on Bengali families’ housing struggles, and a film about young people’s attitudes to racism, alongside shorts by contemporary Bangladeshi creators.\\n\\nLondon Community Video Archive will be showing Despite TV video magazine, issue one (Despite TV/Spectacle 1984, 42 mins).\\n\\nFour Corners will be showing two films: A Safe Place to Be (Director Simon Heaven, 1980, 30 mins) and Divide and Rule – Never! (Newsreel Collective, 1978, 41 mins). A Safe Place to Be is an exploration of the housing discrimination faced by the Spitalfields Bengali community in the 1980s, this documentary looks at how people were struggling for better lives. Unusually, it features Bengali voices, even if they are all male. Made by local director Simon Heaven, it was shown on Channel 4 in 1981. Divide and Rule – Never! Young working-class Londoners – first and second generation Black and Asian immigrants, as well as ex-National Front members – discuss their experiences of racism in 1970s Britain, and fight back with rock and reggae. Screening followed by discussion.\\n\\nOitij-Jo Collective will be showing Gaali Kothon — A Tale of Swear Words (Mahamuda Aktar (Monisha), 2024, 16.06 mins). This short docu-fiction investigates the prevalence of sexist and misogynistic swear words existing in Bangladeshi society and culture, but also universally recognised. Mahamuda Aktar Monisha is a feminist, queer activist and filmmaker from Dhaka, Bangladesh, currently based in Dublin. She is dedicated towards dismantling deep-rooted social injustices through the use of arts and activism, and using storytelling to challenge social norms.\\n\\nThis event is part of Backyard Biennial.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.whitechapelgallery.org/book-instance/?book=79201ARPJVGJDVHGPRNNRLJCTHHVGNJTL\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":748,\"name\":\"Library Transmission: Sarah Maldoror’s Dialogic Cinema\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-22T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-22T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c1687800e1fb466c490595738e1e3ab8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sarah Maldoror’s Dialogic Cinema is a screening and discussion between artists that curate and film curators that archive. The screening of Aimé Césaire, Un homme une terre /A Man, A Land (1977), which is followed by a conversation between Annouchka de Andrade, June Givanni and The Otolith Collective, is one episode in the intergenerational programme Excavating Legacies developed by June Givanni that connects forty years of Pan-African cinema across five continents, expanding public access through free exhibitions, publications, screenings and workshops. \\n\\nAimé Césaire, Un homme une terre is one of three films Sarah Maldoror dedicated to the work and life of Aimé Césaire. It brings together scenes of Martinique’s black sand, mountains and gardens with dramatisations of Césaire’s La Tragédie du roi Christophe/The Tragedy of King Christophe (1963) performed by actors from the Théâtre National Daniel Sorano and poetic recitations by Bachir Touré to compose a dialogic portrait of the renowned avant-garde poet, dramatist, essayist and politician. The wide-ranging exchange between Césaire and Maldoror, filmed as they walk along the coast of Martinique, testifies to their decade-long friendship. It demonstrates Maldoror’s profound engagement with Césaire’s incandescent insurrectionary poem Cahiers d’un retour au pays natal/ Return to my Native Land (1939) and simultaneously, reveals Césaire’s appreciation of Maldoror’s approach to film as a dialectical medium of interpersonal interchange, poetic imagination and pedagogic energy.\\n\\nAimé Césaire, Un homme une terre exemplifies Maldoror’s documentary aesthetic. We see one portrait of two intellectuals thinking aloud in front of the camera: Césaire as a thinker and poet, Maldoror as a director and artist, with cameos from Leopold Sedar Senghor and the bronze statue of King Ghezo seen in Mati Diop’s Dahomey (2024). Aimé Césaire, Un homme une terre constitutes one out of Maldoror’s many documentaries that amount, in their totality, to a cine-syllabus for a Black Radical Aesthetics. The poetic trajectory of Négritude as a historical movement opens onto the political horizon of Pan-Africanism, which in turn enables us to hear, see and think about the pasts, the presents and the futures of black intellectual tradition made audible and visible through Sarah Maldoror’s dialogic cinema. \\n\\nJoin us for a screening of Aimé Césaire, Un homme une terre and a conversation around the work and life of Maldoror understood, in the words of Yasmina Price, as filmmaker-historian-archivist-educator.\\n\\nDoors open at 5.30pm; event starts at 6pm and ends at 8pm.\\n\\nThe Otolith Collective are supported using public funding by Arts Council England.\\n\\nImage credit: still from Aimé Césaire, Un homme une terre, 1977, Sarah Maldoror © INA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/library-transmission-sarah-maldorors-dialogic-cinema\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":646,\"name\":\"Minor Renaissance #1: Alexander Tucker \\u0026 Magda Drozd\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-22T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-22T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d6dd840c1a96c3c5337543e7991f0ebc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Minor Renaissance — concert series for experimental contemporary practices\\n# 1 with Alexander Tucker \\u0026 Magda Drozd\\n\\n22 July 2026 \\nDoors 19:30 \\n\\nThe Horse Hospital \\n\\nMinor Renaissance, a concert series for experimental music, invites audiences to listen for new relationships between instruments and electronics, between composed and improvised material, between inherited techniques and wayward contemporary practices. Rather than a rebirth announced by a movement, it points to smaller transformations — fragile, unfinished, and briefly held in common. Curated by Magda Drozd. \\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":756,\"name\":\"Liana Zhen-Ai \\u0026 Astrid Sonne present Normal Dreams\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-22T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-22T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b5ba5d0a51bfe453b3f61539f4e1f8c9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"'Normal Dreams’ is a new performance by dancer Liana Zhen-Ai and musician Astrid Sonne.\\n\\nFirst presented as a part of the Pairings series at La Mama Experimental Theatre Club in New York, curated and produced by Cameron Sczempka, now brought to London via Club Cheek and Qu Junktions.\\n\\nExpect never heard before songs, movement, noise, probs and a video call from the big apple.\\n\\nUnwaged tickets available, contact venue for more information\\n\\nLimited tickets available\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2488783\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":611,\"name\":\"Ben Jones \\u0026 Xavier Lynn Double Headline Show\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-22T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-22T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"19875626bce147c7d54067689faf4c81.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ben Jones returns to the Fox \\u0026 Firkin to host another night of incredible live music and sharing the stage with top American guitarist, Xavier Lynn. Xavier Lynn is a guitarists’s guitarist who has some of the deepest pockets on earth. From Atlanta, Georgia, you may have heard him perform with Ghost Note, Nono Neon, Jon Cleary, Sam Fribush Organ Trio and countless others. This will be his SE London debut show and he’ll performing his own original music.\\n\\nBen is a gifted multi-instrumentalist/producer whose reputation is firmly established in the London music scene. Over the years, Ben has worked with artists including Sam Smith, Jacob Collier, Mary J Blige, Sir Tom Jones and Jazmine Sullivan but has always made time for developing his own material. Projects such as DivaGeek brought the attention of musical royalty, Lalah Hathaway, leading him to produce music on one of her Grammy winning records. On his latest release ‘No Simulation’ he’s introduced the vocoder as a way of carrying his songs. With help from some of Londons finest musicians and vocalists, he can’t wait to bring his music in all it’s different forms, LIVE, DIRECT and CORRECT to the Fox and Firkin!\\n\\nSeeing these 2 perform together with other surprise guest on the night is certainly something you do not want to miss.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/ben-jones-xavier-lynn-double-headline-show/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":148,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Racetraitor\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5ee2893a1e335ad7747a58cd981c4401.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\nRacetraitor\\nLegends of confrontational, righteous, hardcore extremities. Only their 2nd time ever in London, and perhaps never more lyrically relevant than right now\\n\\n+ support from\\nHour Of Reprisal\\nNorwich Edge Metal\\n\\nTemple Guard\\nRiff devastation from UKHC legends\\n\\nAfraid To Die\\nTurmoil worship for moshers. Record out on TCS on Feb 6th!\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£16\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/racetraitor\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":656,\"name\":\"Nyege Nyege presents NAKIBEMBE (Outdoor show)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2aa88038b74bdb4a9ead9fc5c5063171.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Giant Wooden Xylophone – Polyrhythms – Traditional Ugandan Music\\n\\n“A dense tangle of sound, from which distinct melodies, basslines, and rhythms emerge, each musician’s abstract part combining into an entrancing whole.” — Jim Hickson, Songlines\\n\\nThe Nakibembe Xylophone Troupe from Uganda performs on the embaire, a giant wooden xylophone played by six musicians, creating hypnotic, joyful music.\\n\\nThe troupe has built an international reputation through performances at WOMEX, CTM Festival, Bourse de Commerce (Paris), Holland Festival, Roskilde Festival, Forde Festival (Norway), and more.\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/nyege-nyege-presents-nakibembe-outdoor-show/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":762,\"name\":\"LOAM 001\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d0285698fbf19099d84cf953c8fc8423.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"LOAM 001\\nDATE: 23.07.2026\\nTIME: 18:00 - 24:00\\nLOCATION: Autumn Three, 39 Autumn Street, E3 2TT, London\\n\\nLOAM is an intimate listening space for dense, organic, and experimental sound. Practice over status. Raw collaboration.\\n\\nThe name comes from fertile soil - richness through mixture, not purity. For its first edition, six artists move through one continuous evening: dense and organic ambient, downtempo, experimental, IDM, deconstructed club. Not six sets - one arc.\\n\\nLow lighting. Floor cushions and seating alongside standing space close to the sound. No correct place to be.\\n\\nLineup (A-Z): Desireè, dgbt, Johana, Laura MRLS, New Flesh, Wvrm Pool\\n\\nTickets Info:\\nEarly Bird: £8 + £1.20 RA booking fee\\nGeneral Admission: £12 + £1.80 RA booking fee\\nOnline only\\nAll proceedings are equally split between the invited artists\\n\\nSnacks and drinks available at the bar.\\n\\nCome early, stay close to the sound.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2479362\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":740,\"name\":\"Something Longer\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9900d6ce903094a5244d1a8ceeb1fb35.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Open to everything but pushing for something longer. A space for poetry, but also for essays, letters, short stories, fragments, and more.\\n\\nOpen to everything, but pushing for something longer. We invite you to go against the fashion of the quick and easy. A space for poetry, but also for essays, letters, short stories, fragments, diary entries, unfinished thoughts, or anything else that asks for a bit more space. Bring something you’ve been carrying. Read slowly. Listen.\\n\\n\\n\\nIf you’re interested in reading, there will be a sign-up at the event. Come early — slots will be limited. We’re prioritising depth over quantity.\\n\\n\\n\\nSEP will be selling their incredible handcrafted products throughout the evening.\\n\\n\\n\\nThis event is hosted by Studio 12, an intimate art space with a custom sound system and cocktail bar in Camberwell, London. Dedicated to art, music, poetry, and film, it’s a space rooted in transnational solidarities.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":566,\"name\":\"Kit Records Summer Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b22bb83cb2b552817adcca7b88f49aca.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"London label and arts community Kit Records celebrate another year of audio-visual goodness, with their traditional summer social. Expect brilliant performances, creative chats, and records / tapes / stuff galore. \\n\\nThis year we are proud to present live shows from the wonderful Vic Bang and YOTO, both visiting from Buenos Aires. New signing shen ao will also perform work from his brilliant recent tape, and we will be treated to a dj set from the wonderful k_means too. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":773,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction Presents: Best Band, Dogs Hosting Fleas, Oliver Bentley\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"33f7575f75b01c8b585b149133f7e314.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Bogrock progenitors and protectorate of London pub rock. Art Punk Waltz with added poetry and singing drummer. Bar preacher Rhythm n Blues, Rock n Roll and Groove Funk. Punk for 2026 to the year 3000 - out of the back end of the Avant Garde. Join Simon, Richard and Cai on their quest for reality art and maximum fun. For fans of Baffy + Stan Dingwater.\\n\\nDogs Hosting Fleas is a unique fusion of self-taught and classically trained musicians, blending deep-rooted influences from folk, math rock, and funk. Their sound is an intricate mix of technical precision, rhythmic complexity, and soulful groove, creating a style that is both dynamic and unpredictable. With a spirit of experimentation and a passion for pushing musical boundaries, Dogs Hosting Fleas deliver a sound that is as fresh as it is compelling.\\n\\nOliver Bentley: Made in Peckham, singer of Pig City Committee and theraminist of Omertà. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":683,\"name\":\"CLUB CHEEK ᨳଓ Kinn † UH † Āriya\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"38a07ea4a60d1f68c395c91646f35252.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kinn\\n\\nKinn is the brainchild of Artist, Sound Designer and Rocheman Lead Guitarist, Fred Lomas.\\n\\nAfter a string of high profile live performances (ICA, Southbank Centre, Pace Gallery, The White Hotel and residencies at Ormside Projects and Cafe OTO), Kinn has been aloof from live shows in 2026, as he leads up to REDACTED INFORMATION.\\n\\nThis currently rare live outing will expose some of the left turns Kinn has been developing in the studio this year, expect live-drum-machine-wizardry, MIDI-prowess and cathartic doomer aesthetics.\\n\\n‧°𓏲ּ𝄢𓍯ᥫ᭡.\\n\\nUH\\n\\nUH is the brother/sister duo of Dominic and Finn Kennedy, uniting bedroom-burbling hardware jams \\u0026 narrative vignettes. Overtime, they’ve honed a cathartic, live, experimental acid-trancelike sonic world, touching on their heritage, pastoral idylls, and staple styles from breakbeat to broken beat to balladry.\\n\\n‧°𓏲ּ𝄢𓍯ᥫ᭡.\\n\\nĀriya\\n\\nĀriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria, Āriya, Aariya, Aariyah, Aariah, Ariah, Aria. \\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":465,\"name\":\"Simon Woolf presents Alex Clarke and Donovan Haffner in \\\"Alto Summit\\\"\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-23T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-23T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"69ad65a9cc7fbc2209862eee173fe964.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Featuring the brilliant alto saxophonist Alex Clarke in a programme with Donovan Haffner, backed by the rhythm section of Fraser Urquhart and Joe Dessauer.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsmusic.eventive.org/schedule/69a463a6b1512faeacdd0e5a\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":622,\"name\":\"life is beautiful presents: libiversary festival\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3383a54fbdf737f8c32c596eaf068ca1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"in celebration of their 3 year anniversary, life is beautiful presents their debut festival: libversary.\\n\\n\\nthe festival will be comprised of 3 nights, at EartH theatre, Dalston, showcasing various artists from across the life is beautiful constellations, featuring many of the special guests and collaborators of the past 3 years of life is beautiful.\\n\\neach night will feature 1 dj \\u0026 1 large scale live performance.\\n\\nnight one will be a presentation of a new dance piece by Elisabeth Mulenga \\u0026 Violet Savage, titled 'Floods in Waiting', with an original score composed by feeo. this dance piece will be preluded by a special dj set by artist, curator \\u0026 organiser TTB.\\n\\nnight two will feature a dj set by Mike Levitt (artist, dj \\u0026 founder of Ormside Projects), followed by a two-part live performance by the life is beautiful septet: aloisius, Bianca Scout, NWAKKE, Isaiah Hull, Jasper Maurice, THE NARRATOR \\u0026 abi asisa + joined by special guests: Coby Sey, Damsel Elysium, May Kershaw, SHAUWDII, Angelina Nonaj, Riot \\u0026 Kenichi Iwasa\\n\\nnight three will open with a special dj set by Slauson Malone 1, followed by a large scale multi-disciplinary improvisation performance by orchestra379, which will feature the entirety of night one \\u0026 two's lineups, plus some additional artists (such as dancers: Roisin Salmon \\u0026 Sari Mizoe \\u0026 saxophonist Isaac Robertson).\\n\\neach night will open at 5pm, with life is beautiful dj sets, vegan Caribbean food \\u0026 drinks available by Zionly Manna, as well as exclusive merch for sale, and books for sale or swap.\\n\\n\\nfull current lineup includes:\\naloisius\\nBianca Scout\\nNWAKKE\\nIsaiah Hull\\nJasper Maurice\\nTHE NARRATOR\\nabi asisa\\nCoby Sey\\nSlauson Malone 1\\nMay Kershaw\\nViolet Savage\\nElisabeth Mulenga\\nfeeo\\nDamsel Elysium\\nAngelina Nonaj\\nMike Levitt \\nKenichi Iwasa\\nRiot\\nshuawdii\\nTTB\\nJames Massiah\\nRune Kielsgaard\\nIsaac Robertson\\nSari Mizoe\\nRoisin Salmon\\nNova Varnrable\\n+ more\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":474,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - My Rushmore / Cainhurst / Closed Hands / My Theatre Friend\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-24T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a318c104fff17a333952ff2192c0e61f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nMy Rushmore\\nRagged and joyous emo anthems from Glasgow\\n\\nCainhurst\\nEmoviolence vampires from Bristol\\n\\nClosed Hands\\nChaotic screamosh from London\\n\\nMy Theatre Friend\\nCaptivating lo-fi screamo from London\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\nDoors 6pm\\n£11\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/my-rushmore\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":783,\"name\":\"Awaiting Home: Opening Night and exhibition\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-31T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"74c79cf7e27bfef8b2935bb159b46c45.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"6:30pm- Doors Open \\n\\n7pm- Welcoming \\n\\n7:45 – 8:45pm Collective Counter-Mapping — Brittle Projects\\n\\nJoin curator duo brittle who will be activating Awaiting Home through a participatory counter-mapping exercise. Drawing from Jamaica Kincaid’s writing on gardens, inheritance and diasporic memory, the session invites participants to consider how we hold places in memory and imagination.\\n\\n9:00 – 9:30pm Live Performance — Saurabh Shivakumar\\n\\n9:45 – 10:25pm Live Performance — Aley Baracat\\n\\nCuratorial Note: \\n\\nFrom one to another we move. We move internally to places of home within, we move externally to places of safety and belonging. We sit with the temporality and fleeting moments of flight in the air. Grasping for the familiar; within space. We hold on to kin. She (the earth) offers safety to nest, to root and build. Connection to earth is connection to the grains of soil our ancestors walked. The wind moves… always, across borders and seas, we move alongside the wind, with our feet planted deep to the core of the earth. \\n\\nShe (the earth) is a witness. The ways land is turned into assets, boundaries, or battlegrounds. She witnesses the changes to temporalities. She resists, heals, and remembers.\\n\\nAwaiting Home, brings together artists working with moving image, photography, digital and analog storytelling, opening portals that explore stories of people and the lands that hold them, revealing the complex relationships between landscapes and people. The artists weave together the intermediary between bodies and the ground they inhabit. \\n\\nWho has the right to stay? Who is pushed to move? What does it mean to own, to borrow, to inherit, or simply to care for this temporary place we call home?\\n\\nCurated by Culture Shock | @cultureshockcuration\\n\\nPalestine House, London | Exhibition running from Friday 24th – 31st July 2026\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/palestinehouse/2300971\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":650,\"name\":\"Noise Art Workshop\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-24T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ca001d16e66d5883c301f77f9a1ba45f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The workshop is a beginner's intro to creating sound art on Pure Data. The goal is to work towards a basic foundation in generating noise using Pure Data, controlling and altering audio signals using number generators. The workshop aims to provide all the basic skills needed to utilise Pure Data's audio processing functions, and provides a jumping off point for attendees to create their own unique pieces of sound art. As an introduction to Pure Data's as a visual programming language, attendees will learn how to use basic objects such as message objects, bangs and sliders, waveform generators including oscillator, noise and phasor, effects such as low pass filters, as well as writing elements into an array to create visualisations of their waveforms. The final outcome can range from retro beep boop sounds to intense bursts of noise.\\n\\n \\n\\nCome for two hours of noise, and an hour of music, snacks, and drinks.\\n\\n \\n\\nTechnical requirements:\\n•⁠  ⁠Screen/projector for demonstration\\n•⁠  ⁠Visitors will need to each have a device with Pure Data vanilla downloaded\\nhttps://puredata.info/downloads/pure-data\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37024/noise-art-workshop\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":675,\"name\":\"AFRIKAN MOVEMENTS #12 \\\"H.I.M. Haile Selassie | Earthstrong Ileyvibrations\\\" – JAH LION MOVEMENT SOUND SYSTEM AND ALKEBULAN AFRIKAN WARRIORS SOUND SYSTEM\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T01:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f29105023a2b42c9a50b306e2afa7e33.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"💥🪘Salute all warriors!!!!! Alkebulan Afrikan Warriors Sound System , running since 1994, and owned by Prince ZebuLion, launched on the sound system circuit in 2018, and have featured on LifeFM.TV for 12 years. We maintain the tradition of sound systems like Sir Coxsone, Jah Shaka, Jah Youth , Aba Shanti I, and have played alongside Oneness High Vibrations, Ma-Kaya, Jah Orthodox, King Majesty, Tafari Warriors, Technics Worldbeat, Roots Tradition Roundbeat, Balistic Rootikal, Concrete Lion, and many more. Jah Lion Movement, from Reading have played up and down the UK from Bristol, to Leicester and beyond, have decades of experience and have worked with seasoned artists like Barry Issacs. It is an honour to present this meeting in the month of His Imperial Majesty's Haile Selassie I Earthstrong. 🪘💥\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.skiddle.com/whats-on/Uxbridge/BROOK-HOUSE-FC/Afrikan-Movements-12-Presents/42502159/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":797,\"name\":\"Off The Record \",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4f5e55f83ea8a6e599a1bd32a3b689f8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Public opening event: Friday 24 July, 7-10pm\\nExhibition run: Saturday 25 – Sunday 26 July, 2-8pm\\nLocation: SET Social, 55a Nigel Road, Peckham, SE15 4NP\\nAdmission: Limited free RSVP, then £5 donations\\n\\nOff the Record is an upcoming immersive installation at SET Stage Gallery, unveiling the vital contributions of the unsung heroes of London’s underground rap scene. Behind every viral video, sold-out event, and career-defining moment, there is a dedicated photographer who captured the scene, a journalist who narrated the story, and an event producer who orchestrated the show. For one weekend only, the London artists working “off the record” take centre stage to celebrate their efforts in documenting and building the underground rap scene.\\n\\nCurated by the multi-talented Mobolaji Babalola (@toomanyfishb), this gathering brings together photographers, videographers, A\\u0026Rs, event producers, set designers, lighting designers, journalists, and visual artists.\\n\\nMobolaji is a set designer (@bfixedit_) and event producer. Having built sets for prominent rappers like Ceebo and Saiming, whilst also working as an art director and event producer for @prettytwistedlive, she has fast become a major force behind the scenes. Earlier this year, she held her debut solo exhibition, showcasing her work within the underground rap scene and the wider creative landscape. Now, she is turning the spotlight back onto her own community.\\n\\n\\nAbout SET Stage Gallery\\nLaunched in 2023, SET Stage Gallery is a volunteer-led, non-profit contemporary art space based at SET Social. The gallery prioritises artists with limited access to exhibition opportunities and supports a programme of monthly workshops, talks, screenings, reading groups, and exhibitions. All proceeds go directly to participating artists, supporting accessibility and sustainability within the space.\\n\\n\\nCurator: Ayiesha Sankoh (@thereturnofshe)\\n\\nFor questions, please email setstagegallery@gmail.com\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/set-stage-gallery-presents-off-the-record-tickets-1992691280261?\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":779,\"name\":\"SLG International: Conrad Pack \\u0026 Fig\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"be9c79973a09816b91fd9a22fb142947.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SLG International returns for its summer session, hosted for the first time at the Avalon Café. This edition brings together Conrad Pack and Fig for a focused exploration of high‑velocity techno and dub‑rich industrial pressure.\\n\\nWe encourage your attendance as we observe this occasion in the era of Computer Music (TM).\\n\\n- SLG Intl.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2475153\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":370,\"name\":\"Testing the Water presents: Tristan Arp \\u0026 yingtuitive, Ecka Mordecai, Ru (12th isle)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c5fa271bef84cbf79e05d0df19a0c769.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"For this edition we’re migrating north of the river to one of our favourite intimate spaces: The Old Church in Stoke Newington. With gorgeous acoustics, comfortable seating and a cheap bar, it’s the perfect place to stretch out into slower currents and stranger shapes. \\n\\nTristan Arp is a producer, DJ, composer and cofounder of the label Human Pitch, born in suburban Detroit and now based in London. His 2024 release on Wisdom Teeth, 'A Pool, a Portal', married hallucinatory modular synths with cello, found sound and spoken word, creating a rich sonic world in which machines mimic nature and acoustic instruments merge with their digital counterparts.\\n\\nTristan will perform alongside friend and collaborator, London‑based producer yingtuitive. A classically trained pianist whose musical identity draws from Southeast Asian traditions, electronic experimentation, and diasporic reflection, they craft soundscape that feel both intimate and expansive, as reflected by their debut album Letters To Self 寫情書. Together, their sounds form a shared ecosystem - two distinct practices folding into a single, evolving organism.\\n\\nWe’re also thrilled to welcome Ecka Mordecai, a multi‑instrumentalist whose work has made her a favourite at Café Oto, including releasing on their in-house label. Situated between sonic, performative and olfactory disciplines, her work is driven by sensation: entwining cello, horsehair harp, voice, eggflute, scent and improvisation into time-based objects expressive of emotional complexity.\\n\\nRounding out the night is our close pal Ru, best known as one‑third of the cult Glasgow label 12th Isle and for his much‑loved radio shows as Millennium Dust. Expect a set that drifts between dubwise pressure, fourth‑world shimmer and the kind of deep‑cut selections only Ru can pull together.\\n\\nDetailed, textural electronics and acoustics in a space built for slowing down and sinking in. Come early, stay till close.\\n/\\nSet times will be announced via instagram @testi.ngthewater\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":708,\"name\":\"Re-Enchantment Readings: Annakeara Stinson | Becka White | Iqbal Hussain | MPS Simpson | Thảo Tô\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9fecfe232413309192aaa915f69685bf.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Enjoy a night of live reading courtesy of our fabulous readers. \\n\\nLine up: Annakeara Stinson, Becka White, Iqbal Hussain, MPS Simpson, Thảo Tô\\n\\nRe-Enchantment is an interdisciplinary network exploring art, literature, and criticism. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":638,\"name\":\"The Erogenous Zone #1: CONFESSIONS\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b8f419ee4be0a221eef6b34dda204a01.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"𓆩❤︎𓆪 Your presence is requested at The Erogenous Zone #1: CONFESSIONS 𓆩❤︎𓆪\\n\\nEscape this mortal coil and descend into a nether realm of queer delirium on the eve of Trans Pride. Commune with your fellow sinners and the crème de la crème of London's underground.\\n\\nSULTRY LIVE SAX \\u0026 KEYS (Sax Tape)\\nSLINKY BURLESQUE (Apocalyptrixx)\\nSEXY COCKTAILS (Sana, from Studio 12)\\nSENSUAL READINGS (Lux)\\nSINFUL SNACKS (Lorna)\\nSNEAKY CONFESSIONS BOX (all of YOU)\\n\\nHosted for you by none other than Lucifer himself.\\n\\nDress code: devious\\nBYO: confessions \\u0026 readings to share\\n\\nJuly 24th\\n8PM doors, formances from 9PM\\nopen til 12AM\\n\\nLocation shared with ticket holders the day before the event. It will take place in South East London. \\n\\nNo tickets on the door.\\n\\n____________________\\n\\nAccess Information:\\n\\nThe event takes place in a basement, 11 steps down from ground floor. One small step up to enter on ground floor. \\n\\nEmail earth@affectalien.lol for no income tickets. \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":584,\"name\":\"Northern Soul Live - The Signatures\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3410310ce73d30d96d04fd2674928681.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"10-piece live band The Signatures bring the classic sound of Northern Soul to life. \\n\\nExperience the soul-stirring magic of The Signatures, The Official backing band for many original Northern Soul artists, as well as being featured as the house band for the Northern Soul Special on The Craig Charles Funk and Soul Show on BBC 6 Music\\n\\nImmerse yourself in the energy of a ten-piece live band, showcasing their exceptional talent in their own distinctive style. The Signatures, along with their power and expression, have worked with more original artists than any other band in the UK delivering a truly authentic performance.\\n\\n+ Gig ticket includes a vinyl-only afterparty from the crew behind Heart of Soul Lewisham – running till late.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/northern-soul-live-the-signatures-24th-july-2026/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":567,\"name\":\"DIAKI RADIO FUNDRAISER: Rotational, Tash LC, Mina, Teddy Kitano, Sho Gabi, Joseph Wood\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"377fbc6000b1ee00e47e1313cf453d84.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On July 24th at AAJA, Deptford: Rotational, Tash LC, Mina, Teddy Kitano, Sho Gabi, and Joseph Wood join forces to raise funds for Diaki Radio FM, DJ Diaki’s community radio station being built in Siby, Southern Mali.\\n\\nAs the conflict in Mali continues to intensify, with hundreds of civilians killed in recent weeks and widespread displacement, access to trusted local information is more important than ever. Community radio projects like Diaki Radio FM play a crucial role in helping people stay informed, access essential resources, and remain connected to one another.\\n\\nAcross much of Africa, where access to electricity and digital infrastructure can be limited, radio remains one of the most accessible and widely consumed forms of media. Diaki Radio FM will provide a platform for the people of Siby, helping to preserve and celebrate Mandé culture while offering access to local news and public information.\\n\\nEvery contribution will help get Diaki Radio FM on its feet, supporting the community of Siby and access to reliable, community-led media. Donate to Diaki’s GoFundMe on his instagram page (@djdiaki.officiel).\\n\\nThe Diaki Radio Fundraiser brings together key figures who have helped amplify African and Afro-diasporic sounds. Rotational, Tash LC, and Mina have each built strong international profiles as touring DJs and broadcasters, while staying closely connected to the scenes they move through. They come together on the 24th for Diaki, his work, and the wider social impact of his project.\\n\\n9pm start\\n\\nAddress: Comet Pl, London SE8 4EP\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2459139\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":574,\"name\":\"SSAP: DJ Frog, ddwy, LT, Medium J\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4a32a19a44e1bf5d0541454bd16bb14d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SSAP party hits London for the first time this summer ~ DJ Frog hops across the pond for a debut in the big smoke alongside ddwy, LT and Medium J. \\n++ wheeling in our favourite soundsystem from the Bassfreight family.\\n\\nA gathering of the hyphal web.\\nAll welcome ~ bring your people.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":747,\"name\":\"JIJEI X ORMSIDE / MC ZKW / onoola-sama / Grandmixxer / DARKIO BLACKS\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-24T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"307e5bc14c1d370b721b771cecea957a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"JIJEI X ORMSIDE\\nA one-off JIJEI x ORMSIDE\\n\\nSpeed-run through drill, bouyon, funk br, grime and club loading into your fav playable map,\\n\\nOrmside lineage veterans meet new challengers from recent JIJEI lore.\\n\\nChoose your hero.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2476158\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":736,\"name\":\"Flickers From The Fen | Whimsy, Witchery \\u0026 Dungeon Synth\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"dbbe7611690875b7bb9ea6c83796fd3c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Cross Live \\u0026 Crypt Of The Wizard present\\n\\nFlickers From The Fen\\nA full-band showcase of medieval whimsy from the dungeon synth wizard\\n\\nLandsraad\\nDune-inspired ambient odysseys\\n\\nApoxupon\\nTexas fantasy synths\\n\\nSaturday 25th July\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest tube stations New Cross Gate \\u0026 New Cross\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\\nDoors 6pm\\nTickets via pit.live\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/flickers-from-the-fen\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":445,\"name\":\"Another Subculture: Neutrals (Slumberland/Static Shock), Marcel Wave, Morreadoras, Benny Lager and the Tops\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b04c46b59618b787596fa1baeae73447.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"ANOTHER SUBCULTURE presents\\n\\nNEUTRALS (Slumberland, Static Shock Records; Oakland, CA)\\n\\\"The Bay area's most hated post punk/indiepop trio.\\\" \\nhttps://neutrals.bandcamp.com/album/new-town-dream\\n\\nMARCEL WAVE (Upset! the Rhythm)\\nStories and toe tappers, post punk returners\\nhttps://marcel-wave.bandcamp.com/album/something-looming\\n\\nMORREADORAS\\nSynth punk romper stompers\\nhttps://morreadoras.bandcamp.com/album/s-t-demo\\n\\nBENNY LAGER AND THE TOPS\\nThe spirit of pub rock present, triples all round\\nhttps://bennylagerandthetops.bandcamp.com/album/live-and-loud\\n\\nat New River Studios (N4 1DE), Saturday 25th July 2026.\\n£12/6 here and on the door (cash and card).\\n18+, venue has flat access, toilets are gender neutral, bar is Loud and Silly\\n\\nAnother event from \\\"THE LONDON PUNK NEWSLETTER\\\"\\nanothersubculture.co.uk\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":764,\"name\":\"Abdullah Miniawy presents The evens, Rahma\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"da3e193a8231659fc5615bfcc15c6dbe.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Abdullah Miniawy presents The evens, Rahma, a live performance developed with a flutist and a whistler. The work explores the temporal and expressive qualities of breath and wind, unfolding through a fragile interplay of voice and instruments.\\n\\nDrawing on bird calls and the tonal language of the Indian flute, the performance builds through imitation, repetition, and variation. The act of calling becomes central, shaping a shared sonic space oriented toward listening and gathering.\\n\\nSpanning music, poetry, and performance, Miniawy’s practice often engages with political voice and collective experience. The artist’s work is shaped by his early involvement in the Egyptian revolution and subsequent collaborations across experimental music contexts. \\n\\nDoors open at 6.30pm; event starts at 7pm and finishes at 8pm.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/the-evens-rahma\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":695,\"name\":\"Icons Of Dissent: Imam \\u0026 Negm — Second Edition\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"10ceeba197d1a81512e67736cf9b5d3b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Following a sold-out first edition, Echoes of Resistance returns with another evening celebrating the songs and poetry of Sheikh Imam and Ahmed Fouad Negm, this time featuring an expanded repertoire of songs and stories.\\n\\nFor decades, the duo gave voice to workers, students, political prisoners, and ordinary people across the Arab world. Through sharp satire, moving poetry, and unforgettable melodies, Imam and Negm became two of the most influential cultural figures of modern Egypt.\\n\\nJoin us for a night of live music, storytelling, and solidarity as we revisit some of their most beloved works and explore the stories behind them.\\n\\nPerformed by\\nLaila Samy — Vocals\\n\\nOmar Khater — Vocals\\n\\nTarek Elazhary — Oud\\n\\nZiad Hisham — Percussion\\n\\nEvent Details\\nDate: Saturday 25 July 2026\\nDoors Open: 7:00 PM\\nShow Starts: 8:00 PM\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/imam-negm\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":723,\"name\":\"SOUND TRAVELS - LIVE EXPERIMENTAL MUSIC NIGHT AT STUDIO 12\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99baff41afddc717ebd847bcee2a809d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Composer and sound artist Vic Bang joins Patricia Doors for an improvised live performance.\\n\\nThe evening also features LOTO, an experimental music duo by Yoto and Lola Lamar, in a tragicomic performance.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":725,\"name\":\"The Man with the Plan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-25T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a68193ddd57fa89ec141fb627491b9a7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A young student, Flea (Sophie Jenkin), discovers the 1942 Beveridge report – and its comprehensive vision for a better society. Flea’s fantastical journey takes her amongst Beveridge’s Five Giants: Want, Disease, Squalor, Idleness \\u0026 Ignorance and the whirl of politicians, ineffective policies and missed opportunities across the decades until now.\\n \\nBased on texts and speeches by Beveridge and politicians, the film is a moving account of Beveridge’s vision, the desperate need for it today and a passionate call for action.\\n\\n\\\"an urgent film for our desperate times…a full-blown exposition on why if we had done what Beveridge advocated we might be in a better place today.\\\" John Bird — The Big Issue\\n\\nStarring Simon Callow as William Beveridge, \\nwith Sophie Jenkin, Mark Thomas, Alan Cox, Neil Gore, Neil D'Souza,\\nAndrew Tiernan, Hal Cruttenden, Michael Mears, many others\\nand the voice of Miriam Margolyes. \\nAlso, with the appearance of Sir Michael Marmot, Kate Pickett, Danny Dorling and\\nmany other academics, campaigners and activists.\\n\\nWritten and directed by Christine Edzard.\\nProduced and edited by Olivier Stockman.\\nA Sands Films production.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://sandsfilms.eventive.org/films/the-man-with-the-plan-6984ee5b0a5c263491bcdb6b\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":778,\"name\":\"True Pride\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8fee6b4d7657358bbedc2f7fc2e0825c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On the occasion of London Trans Pride, two NYC goddesses are coming to London with their entourage to deliver an all-night Xtravaganza for the local community.\\n\\nThe night will be hosted by the iconic Ceyenne Doroshow, founder of G.L.I.T.S. and godmother of the Black Trans Lives Matter movement, and world renowned activist Qween Jean, founder of Black Trans Liberation and first-ever trans Tony award winner.\\n\\nTwo venues:\\n\\nAvalon Cafe Bermondsey (7:30pm-4:00am)\\n\\nOrmside Projects (11:30pm-6:00am)\\n\\nTickets grant access to both venues via a wristband provided on the day.\\n\\nMost tickets will be available on the door: £5 for trans and non-binary community members, £10 tickets for POC, and £20 standard price.\\n\\nNo one turned away for lack of funds.\\n\\n120 advance tickets sold online at £20 via RA, which also accepts donations for the event.\\n\\nRevenues from 60 full-price tickets will be donated to @londontranspride. Proceeds from all other tickets and donations will support performers and G.L.I.T.S.\\n\\nFinal set times will be published on the day on @nighthawks.glits instagram page.\\n\\nA very special thank you from G.L.I.T.S. to all the performers and individuals involved in making this event possible.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2492512\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":706,\"name\":\"Diversion presents: Material Things, Minus Kendal, Mag\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ce616977a9c15ac77ea0b7f1b8a459d4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"t’s been a while since we’ve had an opportunity to do an event at spanners, mid summer parties in the dreamy archway really have a special feeling to them.\\u2028\\n\\nWe’re extremely excited to present Material Things, an elusive band and collaborative project of Stewart, one of the founding minds behind the beloved and definitive label- 12th isle. Since the first release on the label, a well developed relationship has emerged between Scotland’s Stewart and London-situated drummer Pike Ogilvy, the latter’s percussion featuring fully on the second album- to our mind an impressively dense (but spacious), wiggly and textural work, pike’s live rhythms sparring with synthesised bass, pads and pings.\\nCheck out both releases on the 12th isle bandcamp.\\nI’ve been told on good authority theres lots of yet-unheard material (things) that may be debuted on the 25th. Buzzing!\\n\\nSupport from the singularly talented digger and long (long) time NTS resident, Minus Kendal. Criminally under booked, fully stocked with incredible tunes and raring to go, Fin will be playing for two hours after the band, until closing time.\\nOne of his very incredible and very recent contributions to the musical sphere, the label Ó Mhaidin, first with a compilation album (‘Toothpaste for your Elephant’) sports some of the craziest and best tunes we’ve heard in ages. Cant really sum it up past ecstatic superlatives, but the wildly eclectic nature of the album really runs through Fin as a person, his taste and of course selection.\\u2028\\u2028\\n\\nMag, having moved back to London from Glasgow quite recently, has already made more moves in the big smoke than most do in a few years.\\u2028Her event ‘Testing the water’ moved down with her and although it sounds like it might be dipping a toe, I would argue the theres alot more splashing involved. (Theres actually a TTW the night before- on the 24th, in a church, featuring 12th isle’s Ru, if you can quite believe your luck.)\\u2028Dedicated to the weird and experimental, her mixes and dj sets have definitely wormed their way into the ears and minds our little south east London scene. \\u2028Regular shows on Glasgow’s Buena Vista, ambient sauna outings and sets supporting some huge names at corsica all attest to Naomi’s tekkers.\\nThe perfect opening set to get down n check out while working through Spanner’s bar offerings.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":678,\"name\":\"Cosmic Slop – London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cf0161db288993ae26cb9c7f5369b359.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"COSMIC SLOP - LONDON - CARPET SHOP - SATURDAY 25th JULY\\n\\n____________________________________________\\n\\n\\n\\nLondon Family we're finally coming back to boogie with yall !!!!! \\u0026 for the first time we'll be at Carpet Shop :P\\n____________________________________________\\n\\n\\n\\nAll funds raised directly support MAP Charity's work, including supporting the education project, ensuring the charity can continue delivering creative education to young people. Find out more at @mapcharity\\n\\n____________________________________________\\n\\n\\nDoors open @ 11pm Last entry for ticket holders is midnight\\n\\n\\n____________________________________________\\n\\nTickets only available through our website!! Please don't buy from anywhere else.\\n\\n____________________________________________\\nTICKET PROCEDURE\\nOnce we have confirmed your tickets, a QR code will be sent to the email used to purchase the tickets. Have your QR code ready for our box office staff on the night!\\n\\n____________________________________________\\nIf you're from a marginalised community and can't afford the full ticket price, we have a cheaper ticket option for you \\u003c33\\n\\n\\n____________________________________________\\n artwork by BOSSdaddy\\n\\n____________________________________________\\nPlease note, tickets are non-refundable \\u0026 we do not allow tickets to be re-sold or transferred into a different name.\\nWe have updated our ticket price which now includes a booking fee.\\n\\n____________________________________________\\n#musicislove\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://cosmicslop.org/product/tickets/cosmic-slop-london-carpet-shop-saturday-25th-july/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":380,\"name\":\"INFERNO: London Trans+ Pride Afterparty\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-25T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"54ce3f09ec289c255a1a12dc5da06a6d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Part II of The Red Summer\\nSaturday 25th July\\n11pm - 5am\\nThe Distillery N17\\n\\nAfter the march, we gather.\\n\\nEach year London Trans+ Pride grows. Larger. More visible. More undeniable.\\n\\nIn a climate where trans lives are constantly discussed, debated and politicised, choosing to come together on a dancefloor feels both simple and significant.\\n\\nINFERNO returns to N17 for a late night following LT+P.\\n\\nThis is not an official afterparty. It is something closer to home.\\n\\nINFERNO is founded by a member of the London Trans+ Pride team, INFERNO has always existed alongside the movement. The dancefloor has never been separate from the world outside it.\\n\\nExpect Catharsis. Harder sounds. A room that understands why it is there.\\n\\nAs always, lineups will not be announced in advance.\\n\\nWhat matters is who we are together.\\n\\nTrans people centred.\\nTrans artists platformed.\\nRespect expected.\\n\\nCapacity is limited. There will be no guest list.\\n\\nIf you want to be in the room, secure your place early.\\n\\nPart II of The Red Summer.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://inferno.eventcube.io/events/94047/inferno-london-trans-pride-afterparty\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":585,\"name\":\"Tokyo Riddim Sunday\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-26T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c98bcb72d3eb51d712b90f7e239bf885.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tokyo Riddim returns to its spiritual home, Fox \\u0026 Firkin, for a full summer Sunday of live music, DJs, record digging, Japanese market stalls and family-friendly outdoor energy.\\n\\nAfter a series of packed London parties, Tokyo Riddim Sunday brings the sound back to where Tokyo Riddim Band first came alive: a cross-cultural meeting point between Japanese music, reggae, dub and record culture.\\n\\nLive on stage, Tokyo Riddim Band brings together three generations of Japanese female musicians with reggae-rooted drums, heavy bass, city pop guitar and live dub mixing. Led by legendary keyboard player Izumi “Mimi” Kobayashi, with saxophonist Megumi Mesaku – a key figure in London’s reggae scene and a close collaborator of Jah Shaka – vocalist Ayana, and producer Kay Suzuki on siren and dub effects, the band has become one of Time Capsule’s most joyful live projects, turning the Tokyo Riddim compilation series into a living, dancing, dubwise celebration.\\n\\nJoining them live are Swans from Kanagawa, Japan, whose laid-back, dubwise instrumental grooves make them a perfect match for a summer afternoon in the Fox garden.\\n\\nAcross the day, DJs Nina Yamada, Shoko Yoshida, Table From Three and Izumi “Mimi” Kobayashi will move through reggae, dub, Japanese grooves, tropical sounds, soulful oddities and summer dancefloor selections.\\n\\nFrom midday to 5pm, the garden will also host a record fair organised by VDS London and various Japanese market stalls, alongside a Double Dutch performance by HARIBOW KIDS at 3pm, making this an all-day gathering for music lovers, families, diggers and dancers.\\n\\nCome early, stay late, and spend a summer Sunday in the Tokyo Riddim universe.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/tokyo-riddim/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":768,\"name\":\"movement at set | queer heels workshop with sula castle x moving discourse\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-26T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T15:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"23453d3e6715a5a9f2a858fa4a6a2438.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Movement at SET x Moving Discourse x Sula Castle 👠\\n\\nINDEXING is a queer heels workshop exploring fields of perception and how we might miss each other within them.\\n\\n✨ Everyone is welcome, no experience is necessary, and wearing heels is optional ✨\\n\\nThis session welcomes a collaboration with Moving Discourse, a platform for performative thinking and choreographic practice through video, text, \\u0026 workshops. As part of chapter 2: Vision and Flesh, Moving Discourse has invited choreographer Sula Castle to co-lead this workshop.\\n\\nFor more details and to explore Sula Castle’s contribution, currently on view at Moving Discourse.\\n\\nJULY 26\\n2-2:30 soft arrival\\n3:30 moving\\n\\nc u on the dance floor 🪩\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":544,\"name\":\"Abigail Toll | Seán Being / Oliver Turvey (viola duo) | Flynn McHardy\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-26T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-26T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"18305efea72f54f20eb0c73c75e4df0b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An evening of experimental music from the sound artist and composer Abigail Toll, a viola duo comprised of Seán Being and Oliver Turvey, and a solo set from Flynn McHardy.\\n\\nAbigail Toll is a sound artist and composer working with electroacoustic composition, chamber ensembles, extended tuning systems, and multichannel installation. Her practice constructs deep-listening environments from ongoing research into psychoacoustics and resonance. Her second album Idol (Superpang, 2025), nominated for the German Critic’s Prize and her debut Matrices of Vision (Shelter Press, 2023) was presented as an ensemble commission by KW Institute of Contemporary Art at the Klosterruine. \\n\\nOliver Turvey is an artist working across sound and performance. A longtime member of the group Midlight, he also performs with Hilary Woods and Gabriel Ferrandini. His practice sits at the intersection of site- and subject-specific improvisation, utilising electronics, violin, viola, DIY instruments, and spoken word. \\n\\nSeán Being is an Irish musician working across a range of modes of composition and performance. They have collaborated widely among circles in Ireland, Portugal and London, including lately as a member of Irish group Princ€ss and as instigator of the riverside event series, Car Musick. They work with site-specific solo performance through a variety of means—recently plainchant, feedback, pianos and car horns—thinking through spatial, social and historical bases of music performance. Seán has an MA from the Dutch Art Institute (2024) and currently lives in London.\\n\\nFlynn McHardy is a London based musician. He works with guitar and electronics in solo and collaborative contexts. He is concerned with the investigation of listening as both method and material. His work has been released by Superpang and has featured on BBC 3’s Late Junction, NTS Radio, and Resonance Extra. He also plays in the band Hedgehog.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":606,\"name\":\"proto-clowns (almost there) 27 July\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-27T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9bedcc670a5802b40d1c774bd39bb862.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"‘proto-clowns (almost there)’ is a work-in-progress! An absurdist show about a holy mother who stalks her adult child featuring…just Samra Mayanja. Existing somewhere between clowning, poly-vocal cunty-theatre and the dregs of live art. \\n\\nThe performance explores the notion that 'there is no better place to hide than behind the mask of motherhood'. As always, Samra’s work is about what we do for love and is always giving a delirious dose of laugh-cry-laugh-cry-laugh. \\n\\nCommissioned by Battersea Arts Centre, with support from Kai Theatre (Brussels), Horse Hospital, Live Art Development Agency and Wysing Arts Centre. \\n\\nDoors: 7.30pm\\nStart: 8pm\\nAt: Horse Hospital, Colonnade, Bloomsbury, London, WC1N 1JD\\n\\n📷: Jemima Yong\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":781,\"name\":\"The Common Press Poetry Night w/ Kaiden Ford\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-28T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-28T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e5c6faeec0cd5b36545810ca6720986f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Common Press Poetry Night has become a popular event for writers and poets to showcase their work and launch poetry collections. \\n\\nJoin us on 28th of July from 7:00 PM to 9:30 PM for an evening of poetry \\u0026 OPEN MIC, hosted by Prince. \\n\\n \\n\\nOur special guest, Kaiden Ford, will be joining us to perform excerpt from her book I Am Suing My Parents for Emotional Abuse.\\n\\nIf you’d like to read at the poetry night, arrive at 7:00 PM to sign up. That will be your opportunities to sign up on the night and hop on stage. Please note that while we will do our best to accommodate as many readers as possible, we cannot guarantee that everyone on the list will have the chance to perform.\\n \\n\\nSchedule\\n\\n7:00 pm - Doors open\\n\\n7:15 pm -  Kaiden performing\\n\\n7:30 pm - Open Mic slots\\n\\n7:45 pm - Kaiden performing\\n\\n8:00 pm - Open Mic slots\\n\\n8:15 pm - Break\\n\\n8:30 pm - Kaiden performing\\n\\n8:45 pm - Open mic slots\\n\\n9:00 pm - Q\\u0026A for Kaiden \\n\\n9:30 pm - Closing\\n\\n \\n\\nTerse, erudite and brave, I Am Suing My Parents for Emotional Abuse is the first collection of poems from this emerging talent, and gives an authentic and unfiltered insight into the inner world of a young, black, queer person coming to terms with their identity and moving from victimhood to self-realisation and self-love. Framed around vignettes and memories, these poems are raw, uncompromising, and incredibly brave. They convey a wisdom and talent beyond Ford's age in numbers.\\n\\nThe collection also expresses itself as physical artefact - printed in a special black ink on striking blood-red paper and naked-bound with black thread, it features an expressive design comprised of remixed Rorschach ink and photographs by art director and photographer Martin Perry (Creative Director of Out There and Homoculture).\\n\\nFind out more about I Am Suing My Parents for Emotional Abuse at www.iamkaidenford.co.uk\\nFor more info please contact: iamkaidenford@gmail.com @iamkaidenford (Instagram)\\n\\nThe Common Press Poetry Night w/ Kaiden Ford\\nDetails\\nThe Common Press Poetry Night has become a popular event for writers and poets to showcase their work and launch poetry collections. \\n\\nJoin us on 28th of July from 7:00 PM to 9:30 PM for an evening of poetry \\u0026 OPEN MIC, hosted by Prince. \\n\\n \\n\\nOur special guest, Kaiden Ford, will be joining us to perform excerpt from her book I Am Suing My Parents for Emotional Abuse.\\n\\nIf you’d like to read at the poetry night, arrive at 7:00 PM to sign up. That will be your opportunities to sign up on the night and hop on stage. Please note that while we will do our best to accommodate as many readers as possible, we cannot guarantee that everyone on the list will have the chance to perform.\\n \\n\\nSchedule\\n\\n7:00 pm - Doors open\\n\\n7:15 pm -  Kaiden performing\\n\\n7:30 pm - Open Mic slots\\n\\n7:45 pm - Kaiden performing\\n\\n8:00 pm - Open Mic slots\\n\\n8:15 pm - Break\\n\\n8:30 pm - Kaiden performing\\n\\n8:45 pm - Open mic slots\\n\\n9:00 pm - Q\\u0026A for Kaiden \\n\\n9:30 pm - Closing\\n\\n \\n\\nTerse, erudite and brave, I Am Suing My Parents for Emotional Abuse is the first collection of poems from this emerging talent, and gives an authentic and unfiltered insight into the inner world of a young, black, queer person coming to terms with their identity and moving from victimhood to self-realisation and self-love. Framed around vignettes and memories, these poems are raw, uncompromising, and incredibly brave. They convey a wisdom and talent beyond Ford's age in numbers.\\n\\nThe collection also expresses itself as physical artefact - printed in a special black ink on striking blood-red paper and naked-bound with black thread, it features an expressive design comprised of remixed Rorschach ink and photographs by art director and photographer Martin Perry (Creative Director of Out There and Homoculture).\\n\\nFind out more about I Am Suing My Parents for Emotional Abuse at www.iamkaidenford.co.uk\\nFor more info please contact: iamkaidenford@gmail.com @iamkaidenford (Instagram)\\n\\n\\nKaiden Ford is a trans artist, poet, and performer whose work spans film, literature, nightlife, and the body itself. Born in New York and now based in London, she has built a practice rooted in her identity, sexuality, and emotional life. She has published two poetry books, starred in and co-created acclaimed short films, headlined international nightlife events across Europe and New York, and fronted global brand campaigns. Her work is visceral, intimate, and impossible to look away from.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37572/the-common-press-poetry-night-w-kaiden-ford\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":607,\"name\":\"proto-clowns (almost there) 28 July\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-28T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-28T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"123413a24cd547d3a9fb1854ddf8289a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"‘proto-clowns (almost there)’ is a work-in-progress! An absurdist show about a holy mother who stalks her adult child featuring…just Samra Mayanja. Existing somewhere between clowning, poly-vocal cunty-theatre and the dregs of live art. \\n\\nThe performance explores the notion that 'there is no better place to hide than behind the mask of motherhood'. As always, Samra’s work is about what we do for love and is always giving a delirious dose of laugh-cry-laugh-cry-laugh. \\n\\nCommissioned by Battersea Arts Centre, with support from Kai Theatre (Brussels), Horse Hospital, Live Art Development Agency and Wysing Arts Centre. \\n\\n📷: Jemima Yong\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":789,\"name\":\"The B.O.S.S Social @ The Africa Centre\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-29T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-29T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"56eb67554192b343e9d0aac9791bd2ca.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We’re taking over The Africa Centre on Wednesday 29th July for the first edition of the BOSS Social!\\n\\nThis space intends to connect ravers, nightlife workers and the wider Black/POC queer community outside of the conventional party space to encourage conversation, form new solidarities and create a relaxed environment to get to know others with a passion for the dance.\\n\\nFor the first edition, we’ll be providing some questions about your experiences of Black nightlife, what you would change about it, and what you feel its future could look like. You’ll have an opportunity to answer these questions and discuss ideas ‘Round-Robin’ style, moving around the room and socialising with new connections, alongside people you may have shared a dance with at one of our functions. \\n\\nWe’ll also be running an open decks throughout the evening, with 20 min slots available - if you’d like to DJ on the night, you can sign up at the start of the social, bring your USB!\\n\\nTimings\\n\\n6-6:45 - Landing in + Open Decks\\n\\n6:45 - 8:20 - Intros and discussion + Open Decks\\n\\n8:20 - 9 - Open Decks + Landing Out\\n\\nAccessibility\\n\\nThe bar is wheelchair accessible. The toilet in the space is partially accessible, wheelchair users will have to be accompanied as there is a door that needs to be opened to gain access. There will be a quiet space available on the day. For any more accessibility requests / information, please email veronique@theafricacentre.org.uk\\n\\nOpen Decks Info\\n\\nPlease make sure your USB is synced using the latest version of Rekordbox for your files and playlists to function correctly.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37942/the-boss-social-the-africa-centre\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":806,\"name\":\"On Writing and Value: Julia Bell, Helen Charman, Livia Franchini and Amber Husain in conversation\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-29T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-29T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"195cd1c54136fb26eab1cf2346dfe1fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for an evening of conversation about the relation of writing to value. What is 'bad writing'? What kinds of stories should we tell about illness? Julia Bell, Helen Charman and Amber Husain will discuss their contributions to Too Little, Too Hard, a new collection of essays on work and value, with co-editor Livia Franchini. \\n\\nIn recent years, countless arguments have been made for and against the enduring value of literature: reading improves mental health and offers refuge from the news cycle; the novel is dead, poetry obsolete, writers AI-replaceable. Too Little, Too Hard adds nuance to these discussions by asking professional writers what they actually think about literary value, and their underexplored working conditions.\\n\\nPreorder the book here: https://peninsulapress.co.uk/products/too-little-too-hard\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://burleyfisherbooks.com/products/on-writing-and-value-julia-bell-livia-franchini-and-amber-husain-in-conversation\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":805,\"name\":\"Sculpture Garden: An evening of poetry, readings and responses\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-29T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-29T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5456ef904ba30916ec6e1083aa2a549e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Artists and writers respond to T. Venkanna’s 'Sculpture Garden', an exhibition exploring national identity, desire, sex, power and the body\\n\\nAn evening of readings by artists, writers and poets responding to the themes and works within T. Venkanna’s current exhibition, Sculpture Garden.\\n\\nWriter Eva Gold, poets Rashed Aqrabawi, Bhanu Kapil and Mantra Mukim and artist, researcher and writer Michiko Oki, will draw inspiration from the themes explored in Venkanna’s exhibition, including ideas surrounding sex, desire, power, violence and transgression.\\n\\nComprising a series of new egg tempera paintings on board, Sculpture Garden is Venkanna’s first institutional solo exhibition. Together, the paintings create a complex portrait of national identity and the persistence of desire, as Venkanna documents the body as both a site of liberation and control.\\n\\nLead Programme Supporter: Blanca \\u0026 Sunil Hirani Charitable Trust. Programme Supporter: The Burger Collection with additional support from the T. Venkanna Exhibition Circle, The Studio Voltaire Council and Art Fund's John Ruffer Curatorial Grant.\\n\\nAbout T. Venkanna\\n\\nT. Venkanna (b.1980) Gajwel, India; lives and works in Hyderabad, India. Selected solo and group exhibitions include: The Human Theatre, Gallery Maskara, Mumbai (2025); Politically Charged, Aicon, New York (2024); Asia Now, Modesti Perdriolle Gallery, Brussels (2023); The Art of India, Clarinda Carnegie Art Museum, Iowa (2021); Looking for Peace, Sakshi Gallery, Mumbai (2017); and Trajectories: 19th – 21st Century Printmaking from India and Pakistan, Sharjah Art Museum (2014).\\n\\nAbout Michiko Oki\\n\\nDr Michiko Oki is a London-based cultural researcher, writer and lecturer. Her work focuses on the aesthetic and hedonistic power of dark imagination, particularly in the form of allegory and fiction. She also explores polytheistic perception as a means of transgression that challenges the violence of identity thinking and the normalisation unique to monotheistic belief systems.\\n\\nAbout Eva Gold\\n\\nEva Gold works across sculpture, installation, writing and drawing to explore questions surrounding desire, agency and consent. Alongside a materially driven sculptural practice, she uses narrative writing to examine the complex, nuanced and often contradictory nature of desire, and the ways that is produced by, and against, the power structures which contain it.\\n\\nAbout Rashed Aqrabawi\\n\\nRashed Aqrabawi is a writer born in Amman, Jordan. His work has appeared in BOMB, The Poetry Review, Los Angeles Review of Books, and more. He is the winner of the 2024 BOMB Poetry Prize and the author of the pamphlet Christ, Mountain Road (Blown Rose, 2026). He lives in London.\\n\\nAbout Mantra Mukim\\n\\nMantra Mukim is a poet and essayist from Raipur, India, currently based in Oxford. His debut collection, Glitchwork (the87press), was published in April 2026.\\n\\nAbout Bhanu Kapil\\n\\nBhanu Kapil is a Fellow of the Royal Society of Literature. She is the author of several full-length collections, including How To Wash A Heart (Liverpool University Press) and Incubation: a space for monsters (Prototype). Bhanu is an Extraordinary Fellow of Churchill College and the recipient of the TS Eliot Prize, a Windham-Campbell Prize, the 16th International Poetry and People Prize, a Cholmondeley Award and a Judith E. Wilson Poetry Fellowship. Since 2020, she has collaborated with Blue Pieta, a choreographer, dramaturg and performer, with whom she has written a new work, Autobiography of a Performance.\\n\\nAccess\\n\\nIf you have any questions or need assistance with your visit, please feel welcome to contact us at +44 (0) 20 7622 1294 or info@studiovoltaire.org. Read Studio Voltaire's full access information here.\\n\\nImage credit\\n\\nT. Venkanna, Tota (detail), 2026. Image courtesy of the artist and Gallery Maskara\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/sculpture-garden-an-evening-of-poetry-readings-and-responses-tickets-1992423417075\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":686,\"name\":\"Book Launch: International Freak Robin Farquharson And The Dream Of Psychedelic Revolt\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-29T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-29T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7dabbce9a5a15d725a71f0a23d9e3751.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Born in 1930 into a privileged South African family, Robin Farquharson was part of a new wave of intellectuals tasked with reimagining society in the wake of World War II—until a phone call from God brought everything crashing down.\\n\\nUnder the gaze of the secret police and his own mounting paranoia, Farquharson fled to Swinging London and tried to reinvent himself as a countercultural guru. Along the way, he helped to have South Africa banned from the Olympic Games, authored an unclassifiable memoir of queer street life, and climbed to the top of the mysterious White Panther Party. Then, just days after founding the pioneering Mental Patients Union, flames ripped through his home and Farquharson was gone.\\n\\nDrawing on meticulous archival research and extensive new interviews, International Freak marshals an extraordinary cast of characters in order to tell Farquharson’s story for the first time. Equal parts experimental biography, social history, and psychedelic true crime, this is a portrait of a singular man and the world he sought desperately to transform.\\n\\nWe are delighted to welcome M. Syd Rosen (author of this utterly compelling biography) and Owen Hatherley to Housmans to discuss the life of this truly remarkable hero of counter cultural Britain.\\n\\nAs always, tickets are priced on a sliding scale. If you are unable to pay for a ticket please do not hesitate to contact us at shop@housmans.com, and a free ticket will be made available.\\n\\nIf you choose ‘book + entry’ your copies of the book will be available to collect on the evening. If you would like to collect it earlier, or arrange for delivery, please contact us (postage is £2.95). Telephone 020 7837 4473 or email shop@housmans.com.\\n\\nDoors Open at 6:45pm, Event Starts 7:00.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/book-launch-international-freak-robin-farquharson-and-the-dream-of-psychedelic-revolt/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":754,\"name\":\"Race Rhythm Revolution | Session 2: Organic Music Society: A cosmos of being otherwise\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-29T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-29T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1ecdd09ef5493fc16a5bf598fd3c4789.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Rhythm Race Revolution is an 8-week course with Aditi Jaganathan that uses music and its attendant cultural texts, as a site of deep study, through which ideas of race, gender, colonialism, healing and transformative justice are collectively explored. It is a radical learning space tracing the sonic(s) of resistance. \\n\\nSession 2:\\n\\nOrganic Music Society: A cosmos of being otherwise\\n\\nUsing the life and practice of Don Cherry, we will move with the ways in which he created a mirror, for life to reflect the radical impulse of music. Through improvisation and a deep study of global music, we will witness the power of his learnings through the music he wove with others. \\n\\nReading lists will be provided to those who book. Places are limited.\\n\\nBio \\n\\nDr Aditi Jaganathan is a thinker and creator, writer and dreamer. Having worked at the intersections of law, culture and politics in various capacities, Aditi is motivated by a politics of refusal, living in rupture as rapture; turning away from hegemonic worlds of oppression and tuning into something different, beyond the world we live in and moving to the rhythms of an elsewhere. It is this compulsion which guides her pedagogy in the education work she does. Riffing off education for liberation, she creates spaces of (un)learning as a site of radical praxis, using tools of music, film and visual culture, to unpack the ways in which ideologies of oppression and liberation travel through cultural production.\\n\\nReading lists will be provided to those who book. Places are limited.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tzkrti.com/en/events/4124\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":680,\"name\":\"wing! - (WORTH SCANNING FOR) Residency #3\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-29T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-29T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f78a5eb49856404803e94732cb0d7998.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The third and final show of wing!'s residency at Avalon Cafe to celebrate the release of his second EP. Curating 3 nights of live acts spanning electronica, hip hop, jazz, ambient and post rock. Supports TBA.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/r765fd8aca6c?dice_id=r765fd8aca6c\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":608,\"name\":\"Kirk Barley Arc album launch, with support from Tara Cunningham \\u0026 Thea HD.\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-29T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-29T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c86516f2f50dbc42e6c4b06cf4b69fe1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kirk Barley is a Yorkshire-born composer and sound artist working with field recordings, instrumental fragments, found sounds and alternative tuning systems. His new album Arc explores just intonation, off-grid sequencing and shifting rhythmic structures through a sparse palette of guitar, clarinet, metallic percussion and electronic textures. Drawing on minimalism, sample-based hip-hop, dub techno and post-rock, his music moves between detailed acoustic sound and quietly unfolding electronic forms.\\n\\nTara Cunningham is a guitarist who operates predominantly within improvisational and experimental music. She released her album Almost - Not Exactly via Nonclassical in August 2025, with more solo music to be released later this year. Ongoing projects as a collaborator and side person include: The Sleeves, Modern Nature, Sebastian Rochford, Red Snapper, Liam Noble, Laura Jurd and Caius Williams.\\n\\nOdda Recordings label owner Thea HD brings together lesser-known and overlooked sounds, moving between old soundtracks, library music, experimental electronics and other curious corners. She’ll be selecting records throughout the evening.\\n\\nWednesday 29 July\\n7pm–11pm\\nSpanners, London\\n\\n£10 advance / £12 on the door / £8 unwaged\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":835,\"name\":\"test event\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-30T15:01:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-30T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":795,\"name\":\"Holding Company\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-30T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0feec9731c5afa30ca0f351adef78f74.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dates: 31 July – 23 August\\nPublic opening event: Thursday 30 July, 6-9pm \\nGallery hours: Thursday – Friday, 1-7pm\\nAdditional viewings on the weekend are available by appointment. For more information and to book an appointment, please contact: aram@masharqa.com\\nAdmission: Free\\n\\nCurated by Aram Masharqa, the show probes the holding company as a fundamentally intangible corporate structure, bringing together new or unseen works and performances by H M Baker, José García Oliva, Luke Gould, Markéta Slaná, Maya King-Dabbs, Samra Mayanja, and Tawfik Naas.\\n\\nAbout the exhibition\\n\\nHolding Company is a group exhibition spanning object-based and event-based practices. Beginning from the place of neoliberal financial capitalism, the exhibition considers the affordances of ‘passive’ or ‘umbrella’ legal entities in the arts. While holding companies—corporate structures set up purely to hold assets and shield liability rather than produce goods—are everywhere in the contemporary art world, this show looks to the structure itself as a productive conceptual anchor.\\n\\nEmbracing rather than resisting the cultural rise of ‘corpcore’, the exhibition approaches this specific form of company on its own terms. If the gallery model is a kind of traditional company structure, perhaps the future of the gallery is holding companies all the way down: uber-streamlined, with staff and physical space abstracted out of the equation, and risk neatly packaged.\\n\\nAlongside the exhibition, ‘Holding Company’ features a public programme of three scheduled meetings, collectively titled ‘Out of Office (OOO)’, with talks between Aram Masharqa, Tawfik Naas, José García Oliva, and Samra Mayanja.\\n\\nAbout SET 91\\n\\nSET 91 is SET’s first in-house curated contemporary arts gallery, located in Old Street. Dedicated to supporting early-career contemporary artists, the gallery provides a non-profit platform for experimentation, collaboration, and the presentation of new work beyond commercial pressures.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":818,\"name\":\"A Night for Venezuela | Food, Music \\u0026 Fundraising\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-30T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cf0cc97b0a0a1a9dfd0d8cf0f8872d92.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Latin beats, Venezuelan food, raffle prizes and a great atmosphere. Join us on 30 July to raise vital funds for Venezuela.\\n\\nJoin us on 30 July for a very special night to raise funds for those affected by the earthquake in Venezuela 🇻🇪\\n\\n\\nYour ticket includes a traditional Venezuelan dish and a drink, alongside an evening of Latin beats, fantastic food and a great atmosphere.\\n\\nThere will also be a charity raffle on the night, with incredible prizes generously donated by artists, business owners and members of the community. Raffle tickets will only be available to purchase in person during the event.\\n\\nRaffle tickets will only be sold in person at the event.\\n\\nExtra food will also be available to buy on the night.\\n\\nCome, eat, dance and help us raise vital funds for Venezuela.\\n\\n🎟️ Book your ticket. Bring your friends. Let’s fill the room for Venezuela.\\n\\nAll proceeds will go to Healing Venezuela.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/a-night-for-venezuela-food-music-fundraising-tickets-1993555894345\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":807,\"name\":\"TRANSLATIONS (I): AN EVENING / (feat.) Sophie R. Lewis, Pauline Le Goff, Yě Yě, Janani Ambikapathy, Rashed Aqrabawi, Rayane Sabbagh\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-30T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"34d760e0d055ecb135e73e5ad301ccad.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We are pleased to announce Translations I, the first in a series of occasional events featuring translators and their translations, at The Broadway Bookshop on Thursday 30 July 2026. The evening will feature readings by Sophie R. Lewis, Pauline Le Goff, Yě Yě, Janani Ambikapathy, Rashed Aqrabawi, and Rayane Sabbagh.\\n\\nDoors 6.45pm; readings from 7.15pm.\\n\\nEntry is free but spaces are limited. Please RSVP: books@broadwaybookshophackney.com\\n\\nSophie R. Lewis is an editor and a translator from the French and Portuguese. Her translation of Noémi Lefebvre’s Blue Self-Portrait (Les Fugitives) was shortlisted for both the Scott Moncrieff Prize and the Republic of Consciousness Prize in 2018, and her translation of Nastassja Martin’s In the Eye of the Wild (New York Review Books) was a winner of the non-fiction translation prize from the French-American Foundation in 2022. She is the translator of Nastassja Martin’s latest book, East of Dreams (New York Review Books), from which she will be reading at the event.\\n\\nYě Yě is a poet and translator. She is the founder of Poetry Lab Shanghai and Nü Editions, and the author of three poetry collections: The Other Side (Letter Records), South (Clearing Books), and The Yellowing Roots of Not (Nü Editions). Her poems and translations have appeared in AGNI, Tripwire Journal, SNOW lit rev, Oxford Poetry, Modern Poetry in Translation, Voice \\u0026 Verse Poetry Magazine, and PEN America, among many others. She has been awarded a PEN/Heim Translation Fund Grant 2026 for her translations of Jike Ayou’s work.\\n\\nJanani Ambikapathy was born and raised in Chennai. She was awarded her PhD in English from the University of Cambridge. Her recent poetry pamphlet If Not Theirs was published by Veer2. Her poems, essays and translations have appeared at the Poetry Foundation, Lana Turner, Circumference Magazine, Firmament, Modernism/modernity and elsewhere.\\n\\nRashed Aqrabawi is a London-based poet born in Amman. He won the 2024 BOMB poetry prize and his debut pamphlet is Christ, Mountain Road (Blown Rose).\\n\\nTranslations: An Evening is an occasional series of events featuring translators and their translations. Working in pairs with “companion” readers, translators will read their translations while companions will read the original texts — or vice versa. Moving back and forth from one language to another, the readings’ aim is to mimic the estrangement of translation — the gap that opens up between sound and sense — and to capture the moment before coherence, or the moment of incoherence.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.broadwaybookshophackney.com/event/translations-i-an-evening-feat-sophie-r-lewis-pauline-le-goff-ye-ye-janani-ambikapathy-rashed-aqrabawi-rayane-sabbagh/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":520,\"name\":\"Velveteen w/ Holy Springs @ Aces \\u0026 Eights, NW5\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-30T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-30T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"df0b94cfb40f7f28e763332799501d79.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Velveteen with support from Holy Springs live at Aces and Eights in Tufnell Park, NW5.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":673,\"name\":\"Jolly Discs Presents (Pt. 3): RAP + Betty Hammerschlag + Toxic Positivity\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-30T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e85b45875083cb85648fc653c724ce7a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"RAP\\n\\nTired of The Home Counties, RAP are on the road once again. RAP is a project formed by Guy Gormley and Thomas Bush in London, 2009. With backgrounds in dance/metal/improvised musics, collaboratively they pursue more traditional song forms. Their forays into pop music, approached from different angles, have been documented across five albums to date. Their sixth, Navigator, is due September 2026 via Jolly Discs.\\n\\nSeparately they have been steadily pursuing their solo projects under various guises. Thomas Bush has recently released Guld (Lost Domain) and Rejoining (Kasual Plastik). He has a tour forthcoming with Sam Bardsley and plays frequently across Europe. Guy Gormley has been developing the labels Lost Domain, Jolly Discs, and Wain Records as well as releasing his own music under various aliases. He has a records under his Hollow Acid and Doomed monikers forthcoming on Lost Domain. \\n\\n\\nBetty Hammerschlag\\n\\nBetty Hammerschlag makes music.\\nBetty Hammerschlag is not real.\\nBetty Hammerschlag exists somewhere between memory and fiction.\\nBetty Hammerschlag has coined #cloudfolk — not a genre, more a gesture.\\n\\n\\nToxic Positivity\\n\\nToxic Positivity is a duo consisting of Acolytes and Alobhe. Formed in Berlin in 2017, Toxic Positivity is the current name given to a longstanding collaboration that has previously manifested in SoundCloud uploads, live performances and collaborations like ‘idk demo’ on Alien Jams ‘Nervous System’ compilation. Alongside Toxic Positivity, the two have featured and collaborated across each other's respective projects such as Acolytes ‘new world psychic trauma’ (Xquisite Releases, 2020), and Alobhe’s ‘Silicon’ (NEOPRIMITIVE, 2022). \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/jolly-discs-presents-pt3/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":716,\"name\":\"Eistir, Sam Horan, Albertine\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T07:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-31T11:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d84d6ea25c3c23713e1dbb3a0dd77217.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Eistir - Sounds from the other side. Ambient folk made in Northern Ireland. Reinvention of producer Ewan Samms’ jam-based songwriting project.\\n\\nSam Horan - Alt folk singer-songwriter of Cornish \\u0026 Irish descent. Intricate guitar arrangements and unconventional colours worked into tuneful songs. A regular on BBC Radio Wales and BBC Radio 6. \\n\\nAlbertine - Banshee classical jazz folk\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":812,\"name\":\"DUBLIFE EDITION 49: ROOTS YOUTHS SOUND FEAT GULLY ROOTS MEETS KING MAJESTY\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T01:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b2c1d24f6bca11a52b7af9774190217c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"DON'T FORGET DUBLIFE EDITION 49 ROOTS YOUTHS SOUND SYSTEM FEATURING GULLY ROOTS MEET KING MAJESTY SOUND SYSTEM FRIDAY 31ST JULY AT THE BROOKHOUSE FOOTBALL CLUB FREE PARKING AND MUSIC AND ITAL FOOD STALLS SPREAD THE WORD BLESS\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/dublife-edition-49-roots-youths-sound-feat-gully-roots-meets-king-majesty-tickets-1992484855840\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":774,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction Presents: Eistir, Sam Horan, Oscar Roche, Albertine\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d5555abba4df736aeb6fa9554cf875a8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Eistir - Sounds from the other side. Ambient folk made in Northern Ireland. Reinvention of producer Ewan Samms’ jam-based songwriting project.\\n\\nSam Horan - Alt folk singer-songwriter of Cornish \\u0026 Irish descent. Intricate guitar arrangements and unconventional colours worked into tuneful songs. Also featured on BBC Radio Wales and BBC Radio 6.\\n\\nOscar Roche - Acoustic guitar and a set of all-new material, written between bus journeys in Mexico and on Friends' couches in London.\\n\\nAlbertine - Banshee classical jazz folk.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":718,\"name\":\"Folk Critique + Cambridge Companion to Folk Music – launch event\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-31T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"67e2f316f2546e73c1119fa5c2ff761c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"‘These things were on the walls in Tudor times: some of them are really old, some not so old. But that tradition of discussing song, which I would love to find traces of – there must be some traces but, like with a lot of vernacular culture, they evaporate.’\\n\\nPlease join us for a double launch, celebrating the publication of Folk Critique, a new pamphlet from Ross Cole and the Fair Organ collective; and the Cambridge Companion to Folk Music (edited by Ross Cole), a groundbreaking new collection of essays on traditional culture and its continuing power in today’s world.\\n\\nThe evening will include a discussion of folk revivalism, nationalism, resistance and what it means to take an attitude of ‘folk critique’; performances from Angeline Morrison, the Black British Folk Collective, Mataio Austin-Dean and Jacken Elswyth; and readings from Aisha Farr and Grace Connolly Linden.\\n\\nWe hope attendees will stay to have a drink and a chat afterwards.\\n\\nGenerously supported by The Leverhulme Trust.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/folk-critique/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":710,\"name\":\"Saint Abdullah \\u0026 Jason Nazary | Russell Square\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-31T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"12ed22dc68e612552fcad5e666ee1c70.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Live music from Saint Abdullah \\u0026 Jason Nazary (NYC), with support from Russell Square.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":589,\"name\":\"Joseph Futak + Ropeburn + Hackpen\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-31T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d26e2d8ca2aeff763d683c9728e6418c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Round and Round presents: 'Birthday'. \\nJoin us to celebrate the new single 'Birthday' from South East London's musical wizard Joseph Futak. With support from new projects on the scene, Ropeburn and Hackpen. Expect banjos, expect accordions. Of course, the show will be In The Round.\\n25 tickets with a cassette available of Joseph's new single, all recorded individually by Mr Futak himself. When they're gone, they're gone!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":777,\"name\":\"Ellipsis w/ BV/XT (Ben Vince \\u0026 Xterea), OSSIA + SHAUWDII\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ef2bf625476e77d8d5d411b9ce7766d5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This new project merges Vince’s unique approach to instrumentation and sonic manipulation of the saxophone with Xterea’s deep, astral textures and intricate drumwork. Both prize improvisation as a mode of pure creation, reaching ecstatic highs through immersive transcendental physicality rooted in a mutual appreciation for sound system culture.\\n\\n    Hailing from AD 93 and 5 Gate Temple labels respectively, Ben Vince and Xterea offer a fresh take on the hardcore continuum, blending haunted textures with unconventional rhythms and devastating sub bass.\\n\\n          Ossia's sound world is an amalgamation of heavy-weather, beyond-good-and-evil soundsystem poetics, channelling raw and rootical techno, isolationist abstraction, and dub at its most turbulent and raw-nerved and space-time-warping.\\n\\n          Shauwdii is multi-disciplinary artist who's eclectic DJ sets span a wide spectrum of sounds and styles, always in tune with the space and the dancefloor.\\n\\n          Very limited capacity, book in advance to avoid disappointment.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2488187\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":765,\"name\":\"The Liberated Film Club: Mica Levi\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-07-31T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"21eb1aadea9a50d2a98e5b8ba28f5d56.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Liberated Film Club concludes its yearlong season marking Close-Up's anniversary with two events on July 31: the first programmed by Marc Isaacs, the latter by Mica Levi.\\n\\nMica Levi is musician and composer based in South London. They are known for their film scores for Jonathan Glazer (The Zone of Interest, Under the Skin) and Nan Goldin (Memory Lost, Sirens). Recent works include Rubber Soul, Smoker and The Bag. Recent solo releases include slob air, H and seventeenth april. They are a member of the band Good Sad Happy Bad and recently exhibited a collection of paintings Episodes 2023-2025 at Tramps, Paris.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.ticketsource.com/close-up-cinema/t-qmaooqz\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":577,\"name\":\"Mega Mega w/ Moina Moin (live)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-07-31T22:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6d5561fedb3cef1b31d800a691e00e48.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"From the creative world of Mermaid Chunky 'Mega Mega' presents a high energy night of live music and DJs. Playful and eclectic live shows fusing organic and electronic elements including a special live set from the band's own Moina Moin and guests Phoebe Massey and Hatwalk alongside special guest DJ sets from their extended family for a riotous party in the heart of South East London.  \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/mega-mega-w-moina-moin-live/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":775,\"name\":\"This is What It's Like\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-05T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5b858513904b608133072dc6a8f61d4a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"This is What It’s Like is an exhibition of text and textiles by Patrick Benson. Themes of response, surface, and closeness are explored through 24 pieces and 7 essays. Sketching different groupings of felt. Little transmissions, some that come stitched, some that come otherwise. \\n\\nAn exert from writings on response:\\n\\\"Big thing, big room. There you go. It is yours now it is yours forever. Response comes from re meaning again and spondere meaning pledge. Your response to the big thing is the making of the pledges it gives you. Three pledges. You are for it as it is for you. You give time. It returns itself in three parts. Those are the pledges. You can’t choose which pledges you take or the contents. You can catch them if you look for falling things, unraveling ones. You can mould them if the room is big enough. And you can choose to keep them to yourself or share them with the big thing. And sometimes if you share them with the big thing it won’t even mind. They are for you. The big room has space in it. It can fill quite quickly.\\\"\\n\\nThe collection also includes a book and a selection of handmade clothing. For some examples of the pieces and more information, see patrickbenson.co.uk/thisiswhatitslike\\n\\nThe opening days for the exhibition are:\\nSaturday 1st August 12-6pm\\nSaturday 8th August 12-6pm\\nSaturday 22nd August 12-6pm\\nSaturday 29th August 12-6pm\\nSaturday 5th September 12-6pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/this-is-what-its-like-tickets-1994544661775?aff=oddtdtcreator\\u0026_gl=1*ctioju*_up*MQ..*_ga*ODEyODY4NzY2LjE3ODQ1NDI3Mjc.*_ga_TQVES5V6SH*czE3ODQ1NDI3MjUkbzEkZzAkdDE3ODQ1NDI3MjUkajYwJGwwJGgw\\u0026keep_tld=true\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":749,\"name\":\"WORDS ARE WALLS / LES MOTS SONT DES MURS / PALABRAS SON PAREDES\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T16:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"282207610c9ac5809fe3a99b49fab07d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"What does it mean to inhabit a hybrid, multilingual space in our publishing work? How can translation become a collective, creative, and experimental process?\\n\\nExercises in collective translation led by Seán Elder, Sam Castro \\u0026 Anahí Saravia Herrera In this workshop, we will work with archival materials (from Cubitt and beyond) to explore how DIY and grassroots approaches can inform translation practices. Through a series of playful collective exercises, we will experiment with different ways of approaching text, poetics, language, and meaning across multiple languages.\\n\\nWORDS ARE WALLS is the first in a new series of events run by Cubitt Distribution Centre, imagining the ways that collective publishing practices might relate contemporary organising and art-making in our locale, with histories of radical print and podcast.\\n\\nLES MOTS SONT DES MURS is Cubitt’s first collective translation workshop, which will take place in the context of The Hospitable Threshold: 25 Years of Angel Mews, which includes both archival materials from Cubitt’s history, and a new version of Anne Tallentire’s series ‘Setting Out’ which uses measurements of the interior spaces of buildings, and constellations of the activity inside them, to be captured in gallery settings.\\n\\nPALABRAS SON PAREDES will engage with the relationship between architecture and language, and include experimental translation techniques undertaken collectively. Translation will be imperfect, resistant, and at times, either practical, poetic, or both. Cubitt staff will be on-hand to form groups in French and Spanish. If you would like to form a group in another language please email ahead.\\n\\nWords Are Walls / Les Mots sont des Murs / Palabras son Paredes is part of ‘Collective Publishing Practices’, a programme hosted by Cubitt Distribution Centre (CDC). The programme centres work by community publishers, artists, writers, translators and organisers working through print, collective methodology and community distribution as modes of social action.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cubittartists.org.uk/Event/words-are-walls-les-mots-sont-des-murs-palabras-son-paredes\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":816,\"name\":\"Kindred Street Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c3ad6a6d2152c3fce604fe0d9fefa003.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Kindred Street Party 📡\\n\\nSaturday the 1st of August.\\n2pm till 8pm.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":811,\"name\":\"THE DUB CHAMBER CHAPTER 1: ITAL POWER MEETS MIGHTY TABOT\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T01:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d67d029fa18de5fb1335495265e34755.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"NEW VENUE NEW CHAPTER DON'T FORGET SATURDAY 1ST AUGUST THE DUB CHAMBER PRESENTS ITAL POWER SOUND SYSTEM ALONGSIDE THE MIGHTY TABOT SOUND SYSTEM AT THE HAYES AND YEADING FOOTBALL CLUB\\nSPRINGFIELD ROAD HAYES LONDON\\nDOORS OPEN 6PM TILL 1.30 AM FREE PARKING\\nSPREAD THE WORD AND LINK BLESS 🙌 🙏 🔊\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-dub-chamber-chapter-1-ital-power-meets-mighty-tabot-tickets-1992487440571\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":707,\"name\":\"QUEER PROM '26\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7e9bae1310dc2b60f9be2efb29207ed0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"QUEER PROM returns to SET Social for the 3rd time...\\n\\nThis time raising funds for Lucy Peterson's Gender-Affirming Surgery - all proceeds will go directly to Lucy.\\n\\nThe prom band will return with some new special guests including...\\n\\nTiberius B\\nNiCKY\\nStuart Mckenzie\\n\\nDJs...\\n\\nMaxou\\nMacy see\\n\\nThe last two events have SOLD OUT so don't miss out.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":790,\"name\":\"HOUSMANS READING SERIES: Valerie Hsiung with Verity Spott, Andrea Brady and others\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a9aa8f62d094cc7532f79ea4ce873f53.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We are delighted to welcome the incredible Valerie Hsiung to Housmans, visiting us from the mountains of Colorado in USA. Joining her we have some of the finest poets working in Britain today.\\nWe will be celebrating Valerie’s latest book, The pedestrian: a poet’s novel, a body, a house, where childhood ungrieved meets the horror of displacement.\\n\\nEmerging from the dark ecology between lullaby and ghost story, The pedestrian meanders down a labyrinth of divinatory time where crimes demand a more defective detective. To conjure the source of this text’s trauma, the poet becomes a ritual detective, tracing the wound by its shadow. Meaning emerges through distortion and echo—courting what cannot be seen head-on to create a haunted grammar of grief. An ill pastoral of displacement, The pedestrian turns domestic spaces into underworlds, the body of the exiled child into a prophetic threshold—it listens as much as it speaks, attuned to forces beyond itself.\\n\\nAmelia Zhou is a writer and researcher. Her book Repose, which interweaves poems, fiction, and lyric essay, was awarded the 2022 Wendy’s Subway Book Prize and published in 2024. She is a PhD candidate in English at the University of Cambridge, where her research examines the political-aesthetic role of photographic images and tropes in predominantly Anglophone life narratives from the 1970s to the present. She is also currently the Emerging Critics Fellow at the Sydney Review of Books. Born and raised in Sydney, she lives in London. \\n\\nAzad Ashim Sharma is a writer and publisher based in South London. He is the director of the87press. His work includes Against the Frame (Broken Sleep Books, 2022) and Ergastulum (Broken Sleep Books, 2022). His work has featured in publications such as the Asian American Writers Workshop, Stand Magazine, Gutter Magazine, the journal Social and Health Sciences, SPAMzine, MIR Online, and Wasafiri. He is a Chase-funded PhD Candidate in English and Humanities at Birkbeck College, University of London. He is the recipient of the Caribbean Philosophical Association’s Nicolás Cristóbal Guillén Batista Outstanding Book Award 2023. He lives in London. \\n\\nVerity Spott is a poet, blogger, teacher, carer and musician from Brighton, England, and publisher of the independent publishing house Iodine Press. Verity’s books include Click Away Close Door Say (Contraband, 2017), Prayers Manifestos Bravery (Pilot Press, 2018), Hopelessness (The 87 Press, 2020), Songs of the Morning (slub, 2023) and The North Road Songbook (Pilot Press, 2024). Since 2006, Spott has run the monthly poetry and performance event Horseplay in Brighton.\\n\\nAndrea Brady is an American poet and lecturer at Queen Mary University of London. She is the author of eight books of poetry including, Desiring Machines, The Blue Split Compartments, The Strong Room, and Cut from the Rushes. She has performed in Europe, Canada, the US, Lebanon, and Chile, and has been invited to speak about poetry by the British Academy, British Council, the BBC, the Arts Council, and the Poetry Society. Her work has been translated into numerous languages, including French, German, and Croatian.\\n\\nGhazal Mosadeq is a poet, editor and translator. She is the founder of Pamenar Press, an independent publisher of poetry, translation, hybrid and critical writing. Her own work has been published by Sheirsman, Fence, Arc Poetry, Firmament, Asymptote, Modern Poetry In Translation and Ugly Duckling Presse (forthcoming), among others. She is a member of the editorial advisory board for the Journal of British and Irish Innovative Poetry.\\n\\nValerie Hsiung is a poet who writes between worlds, where language meets ritual and abolition meets afterlife. Drawing on diasporic, ecological, and metaphysical inquiry, her books dissolve the borders of poetry, prose, performance and philosophy into a single listening body. She is the author of eight full-length books, including The pedestrian (Nightboat Books), The Naif (Ugly Duckling Presse), The only name we can call it now is not its only name (Counterpath), To love an artist (Essay Press), and outside voices, please (CSU). Recipient of fellowships and residencies from the Camargo Foundation and Lighthouse Works as well as grants from Foundation for Contemporary Arts and PEN America, she teaches writing at the limits of language at the Jack Kerouac School of Disembodied Poetics at Naropa University. Her ceremonial work and pedagogy has been studied by researchers on the subject of emancipatory practices including Sophie Orlando. Born to Chinese-Taiwanese immigrants in Cincinnati, Ohio, she now lives in the foothills of Colorado.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/housmans-reading-series-valerie-hsiung-with-verity-spott-andrea-brady-and-others/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":819,\"name\":\"Vespers presents with Asphodèle, JUPiTA, Suki Quasimodo, Blue Ringed Baby \\u0026 Kamī\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5e3989441a99729b944909aa9e4fe790.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"vespers hosts Asphodèle from the U.S. in our presents series, breaks music and experimental ambient live with a host of cutting edge warm up acts.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":761,\"name\":\"Amalgam Melee by Marika Peura\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-01T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"38e791027b49f3490c226289455c95d1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Finnish choreographer Marika Peura presents a one-off performance of Amalgam Melee, a work that explores the artist’s inner contradictions in relation to cultural heritage, Brownness, Whiteness, and the hierarchies of power and violence embedded within society.\\n\\n\\nAmalgam Melee sets off from the artist’s inner contradictions in relation to cultural heritage, Brownness, Whiteness, and hierarchies of power and violence within Finnish society. These frictions operate as a double-edged force, exposing how the body is shaped by, and implicated in, the mechanisms of white supremacy.\\n\\nOn stage, Peura wears pink tsinelas (flip-flops in Tagalog) and a hela belt (helavyö in Finnish), a decorative knife belt traditionally part of the South Ostrobothnian regional costume worn by men. These objects, drawn from distinct cultural lineages, become charged symbols of heritage. Through them, Peura explores the body where the mechanisms of white supremacy are present both as the exerciser of power and the subject of it.\\n\\namalgam melee refers to a chaotic or unstable condition where multiple elements merge into a single, disorderly mass. Here, “amalgam” implies a mixture and combination, while “melee” evokes a confused situation involving struggle and conflict. The work delves into the emotional and expressive body; within the conflicts of this third space, as the means and potential to reach a political sense of self.\\n\\nIn partnership with the Finnish Institute in the UK and Ireland. \\n\\nChoreography, concept, performance, dramaturgy: Marika Peura\\nSound design: Tiikka Drama\\nSpatial design: Una Auri\\nLight design: Luca Sirviö\\nDramaturgy: Caroline Suinner, Ricardo\\nCostume design: Helmi Hagelin\\nProducer: Kaisa Nieminen, Marika Peura\\nCo-production: Zodiak – Center for New Dance\\nPR photos: Haliz Yosef\\nPerformance trailer: Teemu Kyytinen\\nSupported by: Kone Foundation\\nLondon performance: produced by Alice Agency\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ica.art/book/748601\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":617,\"name\":\"grounded *SUMMER MELT* w. Dual Monitor, Wordcolour, Delay Grounds, ohmydais\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-01T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b2c6c0ee036eb271da77b64672020178.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"@grounded.with debuts at M.O.T this August with a special edition..\\n\\n(｡◕‿‿◕｡) SUMMER MELT (｡◕‿‿◕｡)\\n\\nbriefed to bag all their waviest and most psychedelic selections, Delay Grounds invites Londons finest forward thinking producers and DJs to trip sit us all for an evening hazy heaters\\n\\ncome have wobble\\n\\ngrounded.with is a party with a mind to bring clubbing down to size. it’s a focus on music as well as people, a zoom in on the user experience that looks to the floor rather than the sky, paying attention to the detail at our feet -\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2466529\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":745,\"name\":\"B.O.S.S. at The Beach!\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-02T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"71a98d2fc9ab217d982de98a5eb0e395.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"B.O.S.S. warmly invites you to an all ages coach trip to Hayling Island on Sunday 2nd August.\\n\\nA day out for our Black LGBTQIA family and their loved ones where we get out of the city for a bit, \\n\\nstick our toes in the sea, eat together, and have a few hours of sound healing, workshops and dj sets on the beach before we head back to London.\\n\\nThe plan is to leave from London Whitechapel station at 10AM and return around 9PM.\\n\\nWe will have collective members acting as welfare and liaison points on the day. \\n\\nIn your ticket cost a packed lunch, as well as access to all of the workshops on the day is provided. \\n\\nPlease email us at blackobsidiansoundsystem@gmail.com with any access or support requirements at least 3 days ahead of the event, thank you!\\n\\nTicket Tiers* :\\n\\nUnwaged / On Benefits : £30 - This ticket is for individuals who struggle to make ends meet, who are unemployed or under employed and struggle to afford basic needs\\n\\nGeneral Admission : £50 - This ticket is for individuals who are employed, can afford their basic needs, and have access to savings but do not have a lot of money left over at the end of the month\\n\\nPay it forward : £60 - This ticket is for individuals who are employed, can afford basic needs, have expendable income, access to savings and still have enough money left at the end of the month.\\n\\nUnder 18 or over 65 : £15 - This ticket is for individuals aged under 18 or over 65 (please note under 16s will need to be accompanied by a responsible adult)\\n\\n~Please note all tiers are subsidised, this is a not for profit event~\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37432/boss-at-the-beach\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":825,\"name\":\"Nu Earth Groove X Felt Soundsystem\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-02T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e36a77222aa28b18a14ebff3a31a5db0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Nu Earth Groove's ʟɪᴠᴇ ɪᴍᴘʀᴏᴠɪꜱᴇᴅ ɢʟᴏʙᴀʟ ᴜʀʙᴀɴ BASSY ᴊᴀᴢᴢ ꜰᴜɴᴋ ʟɪʙᴇʀᴀᴛɪᴏɴ ᴍᴜꜱɪᴄ alongside Felt's eclectic DJs and heavy weight sound system\\n\\naaand ᴡᴇ ᴀʀᴇ ʙᴀᴄᴋ !!! i know u already missed us so we’re bringing u a very special one … Nᴜ Eᴀʀᴛʜ Gʀᴏᴏᴠᴇ X Felt Sound system AUGUST 2nd DAYTIME pardyy n we are gasssedddd\\n\\nꜰᴏʀ ᴛʜᴇ ꜰɪʀꜱᴛ ᴛɪᴍᴇ at Felt’s legendary Lordship Rec event, there will be a BiG band —8 piece no less— bringing ʟɪᴠᴇ ɪᴍᴘʀᴏᴠɪꜱᴇᴅ ɢʟᴏʙᴀʟ ᴜʀʙᴀɴ BASSY ᴊᴀᴢᴢ ꜰᴜɴᴋ ʟɪʙᴇʀᴀᴛɪᴏɴ ᴍᴜꜱɪᴄ straight to your eardrums\\n\\n\\n\\nAccompanied by:\\n\\nCommunity discussions on building a better society\\n\\nSpeakers from Respace, Tottenenham Families Fight Back aaand many many more !!\\n\\n\\n\\nviiibess ina skatepark\\n\\nfreee food for the peoples !!\\n\\ngood viiibess \\u0026 inshaallah sunshinee\\n\\nas we boogy on dowwwn\\n\\nsee you sooon xoxo\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/nu-earth-groove-x-felt-soundsystem-tickets-1995070259853\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":796,\"name\":\"MIAAN Cookout\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-02T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"cfa558a809d31d5e2bafa7039bb177e4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"It's summertime kabob time! this is the warmest invitation to our upcoming cookout hangout on the 2nd of August at Studio Twelve! We will have tunes, games, kabobs, veggie options, drinks and more! Come thru, bring ur friends, family, neighbours, and enemies! 15 pound entry includes food!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":709,\"name\":\"(A)MOL presents: Conna Haraway, Burning Pyre \\u0026 Mirror Organs\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-02T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c1aa11e6dcf05ec6508dc39960b0c778.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A late Sunday afternoon offering of downtempo, trip-hop and dub-infused electronics at the Horse Hospital. \\n\\nConna Haraway returns to London after an impeccable run of releases on Theory Therapy and Short Span. Oscillating between etherial ambient and intricate rhythms, Conna's live shows are blissed out, shape-shifting sermons, captivating audiences with a physicality thats as textile as it is hypnotic. The Glasgow producer also runs the co:clear label. \\n\\nFresh off their most recent release \\\"Imago\\\", Newcastle's Burning Pyre returns to London for a new performance showcasing their unique blend of modern-classical electronica. Emotive ambience meets skittering rhythms, with vocal features from Australian poet 3NDLES5 and Shell Company lead-vocalist Rosabella Allen. Burning Pyre also co-runs the Eastern Nurseries label. \\n\\nMirror Organs is the project of London-via-Zurich producer, songwriter, and designer Bene Pooley. Existing between club culture, experimental electronics, and pop abstraction, the project recontextualises dancefloor rhythms and textures into introspective compositions. \\n\\n(A)MOL arranges musical outlets for underground musicians. This is the second edition. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":784,\"name\":\"Lammas in the Garden: A Black British Folk Collective celebration\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-02T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f78e79794719d5e23a3a33cf28cb4ce9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lammas in the Garden: A Black British Folk Collective Celebration, an all-dayer taking place on 2 August at Glengall Wharf Garden. Join us as we gather once again for a day of music, community and celebration.\\nLive music, workshops, food, drinks and harvesting!\\n\\n\\nLineup and more details TBA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37848/lammas-in-the-garden-a-black-british-folk-collective-celebration\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":735,\"name\":\"Dub Revolution book launch, panel discussion and live dub experience! – w/ Adrian Sherwood (On-U Sound) + Ras Digby (Sir Jessus) + David Katz (Dub Me Always)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-02T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-02T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"68accf4d5afa74cc7bfdb296291f38f0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To celebrate the launch of David Katz's Dub Revolution: Jamaica's Sonic Innovators and the Birth of Remix Culture, Cafe Oto is proud to present a night tracing dub's evolution from its origins in the Kingston ghettos during the early 1970s to new mutations in Britain and beyond. Beginning with a panel discussion on all things dub featuring Katz, Ras Digby of Sir Jessus sound system and Adrian Sherwood of On-U Sound, we will later be treated to a live dub experience mixed in real time by Adrian Sherwood from his vast sonic archives and a supporting DJ set by Ras Digby, featuring rare vintage dubs of the 1970s and 80s and exclusive one-off dub plates from reggae's most treasured era.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/dub-revolution/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":682,\"name\":\"Un/stable: Crystabel Riley / Sue Lynch / Ross Lambert\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-03T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-03T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"42f24c209bc3d46d11a5a7e1ae936b2e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Un/stable series showcases improvised music, with two sets from a trio formed of Crystabel Riley, Sue Lynch, and Ross Lambert. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":786,\"name\":\"Horizontal Practices: Encountering Ghosts and Avatars\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-04T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-05T13:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c686dda30c7c84f70df48a6d08f2be33.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Encountering Ghosts and Avatars is a movement and reading workshop, led by Gian Singh Sanghera-Warren and Imke Felicitas Gerhardt. \\n\\nThe workshops explore how we encounter the ‘real’ Other in virtual space, as well as the virtual Other—the avatar—in real space. This embodied research draws from the ideas of Mark Fisher, Brandon LaBelle, and Emmanuel Lévinas. \\n\\nWorking with imagination, these ideas will be expanded upon and explored from a bodily and spatial perspective, to investigate our relation to the ghost or avatar. Participants will be guided through simple somatic tasks and improvisation exercises. These are suitable for all levels, with no dance or movement experience necessary.\\n\\nEncountering Ghosts and Avatars contextualises places and performances where ghosts or avatars seem present, loosely suggesting that the avatar is the ghost reimagined: “a version of the self, deconstructed, observable through some sort of augmented view”.\\n\\nGian Singh Sanghera-Warren (he/they) is an interdisciplinary dance artist and performer, born and based in East London. Gian’s practice is informed by digital culture and contemporary trends, uncovering how the virtual world can be a site of both personal and communal memory. \\n\\nImke Felicitas Gerhardt (she/they) is a performative researcher from Germany, currently based in London. Imke is the founder of Moving Discourse, a platform dedicated to the documentation, archiving, and critical discussion of Performance Art and movement-based practices. \\n\\nHorizontal Practices is a strand of London Performance Studio's programming dedicated to promoting peer-to-peer learning and non-hierarchical spaces for conversation. These take form as discursive events, professional training and curated guest workshops. \\n\\nHorizontal Practices responds to the need for and importance of space for experimental modes of exchange that sit outside the context of institutional ‘education’ frameworks. As with the rest of the LPS programme, queer and feminist practices and those which sit in-between visual art and theatre are at the core of Horizontal Practices. \\n\\nThe workshop takes place in Studio 5, which is located on the ground floor with step-free access and has an accessible toilet. All toilets are gender-neutral. There is access to a kitchen with drinking water and kettle, some refreshments will be provided but you are welcome to bring your own. Please wear comfortable clothing.\\n\\nThis workshop runs twice; first on 4 Aug and it is repeated on 5 Aug.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37983/horizontal-practices-encountering-ghosts-and-avatars\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":814,\"name\":\"Queering the Voice Workshop with Guy Harries\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-05T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-05T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"541a35ddd6ae35fc93d71571510c6a47.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"a creative workshop - drawing, writing, sounding with multi-disciplinary artist Guy Harries\\n\\nThe voice on the page, the voice out loud, the voice as others hear it. Queer Voices is a two-hour workshop at Tenderbooks that moves through all three, starting with a poem and ending in sound. \\n\\nRunning through all of it is queering as a method: a way of looking at the world, questioning what gets taken for granted and finding new ways of experiencing. \\n\\nThe workshop is open to all levels and backgrounds, and is especially suited to anyone curious about voice, writing and new ways of making. You will leave with a poem of your own, a freer voice and a sharper sense of the questions worth asking. \\n\\nCapacity is limited, please RSVP to hello@tenderbooks.co.uk\\n\\nGuy Harries\\n\\nComposer, performer and sound artist Guy Harries makes operas, choreography and musical works that explore queer experience, including the documentary operas SINGULAR and QueerLove. He is also a trained counsellor, which informs the unhurried and attentive way he holds the session. www.guyharries.com\\n\\nOpen Narratives\\n\\nA publishing and events programme highlighting LGBTQIA+ voices through a series of newly commissioned printed matter, live readings, exhibitions and workshops. Open Narratives at Tenderbooks is funded by Arts Council England. \\n\\nThe event is organised in collaboration with: Westminster LGBT+ Forum, Tenderbooks Open Narratives and the University of East London\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tenderbooks.co.uk/blogs/events-window/queering-the-voice-workshop-with-guy-harries-wednesday-5-august-6-8pm-rsvp\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":810,\"name\":\"Street readings by all\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-05T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-05T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3eb00f2fd7a6776d99f84927673d2822.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Jovial readings from varied text, by and for passers-by. Bring a book or read from one of ours.\\n\\nWe will have readings from individual readers, and also circle readings where each person reads no more than five paragraphs and passes the book, to spread the spotlight.\\n\\n100 Stoke Newington Road, \\nN16 7XB\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":692,\"name\":\"GRAIN Presents: Theodora Laird, Mica Levi \\u0026 Angharad Davies / Brandon Lopez \\u0026 Caius Williams\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-05T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-05T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"90d698409b13e79b5a917b95e8b40495.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"GRAIN is a concert series and archiving project for experimental and improvised music,  programmed / produced by Caius Williams \\u0026 Theodora Laird.\\n\\nBrandon Lopez \\u0026 Caius Williams (duo)\\nTheodora Laird, Mica Levi, Angharad Davies (trio)\\n\\nDoors 7:30, Music 8PM (2 sets with an interval)\\nNO ADMISSION DURING THE SETS\\n\\n\\nBRANDON LOPEZ:\\nis a bassist and composer living in New York City. His work deals with improvisation, finding new sonic possibilities on the double bass.\\n\\nCollaborations with the likes Fred Moten, Gerald Cleaver, John Zorn, The Mat Maneri Quartet, Nate Wooley’s “knknighgh”, Satoko Fuji, Zeena Parkins, Ingrid Laubrock and Tom Rainey, Standing On The Corner, Cecilia Lopez, Ash Fure, Joe Morris, Tyshawn Sorey, and many others.\\n\\nPlaying with the New York Philharmonic 2019 season as a featured soloist with the New York Philharmonic in the premier of Ashley Fure’s “Filament” under the baton of Jaap Van Zweden. His solo work has been featured at the Met Museum in a live collaboration with silent films by directors Stan Brakhage and Germaine Dulac. His collaborative work with Fred Moten and Gerald Cleaver was critically acclaimed by publications of note and won Best of Jazz 2022 in the NYTimes. His most recent solo recording won best of 2023 in the NYC Jazz record. He’s been awarded the Van Lier Fellowship (2018) and Jerome Artist in Residence (2020) at Roulette Intermedium, The Artist in Residence at Issue Project Room (2018), commissions from the Robert D. Bielecki Foundation for the recording of SUN BURNS OUT YOUR EYES (2022), 2023 NYSCA grant for the multimedia piece NADA SAGRADA premiered at the Vision Festival, and an award in 2020 from the Doris Duke Charitable Trust.\\n\\nHe is currently a instructor of improvisation and double bass at the New School for Jazz.\\n\\nCAIUS WILLIAMS:\\nis a musician from London who plays the double bass, guitar, and bass guitar. He works in collaboration with others, alongside various solo projects, often working with improvisation and explorations of resonance, and perception. https://caiuswilliams.bandcamp.com/\\n\\nTHEODORA LAIRD\\nis a vocalist and multidisciplinary artist. Releases under her solo project ‘feeo’ have received critical acclaim. Theodora's practice has involved in tandem with an interest in situating narratives within freely improvised music, specifically through frequent involvement in the GRAIN residency.\\n\\nANGHARAD DAVIES\\nis a Welsh violinist based in London working with free-improvisation, compositions and performance. Her approach to sound involves attentive listening and exploring beyond the sonic confines of her instrument, her classical training and performance expectation.\\n\\nMICA LEVI\\nis a musician and composer born in Guildford and living in South East London.They use programming software, written notation and improvisation to produce music. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":817,\"name\":\"Library Transmission: Mysteries of July\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-06T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-06T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"daea74e3fcc29493cca218b73b755845.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Notes from the London Commune highlights moments from the pre-history of London's liberation. The programme envisions the political imagination of black, proletarian, queer radicalisms as the seed, the soil and the star of a London yet to arrive. Each event has presented a retrospective look at the histories of struggle in the city, from the vantage point of a near-future establishment of London's citywide workers' council. \\n\\nDirected by Reece Auguiste, founding member of the Black Audio Film Collective (BAFC), Mysteries of July (1991) takes as its subject the unexplained deaths of Jamie Stewart and other young Black men in police custody in the UK. Auguiste combines talking head interviews and dramatic reenactment with a series of intimate tableaux to explore the intense suffering of those grieving the dead. Layering official accounts with witness testimony and static images, the BAFC construct a history beyond the constraints of the hegemonic archive. \\n\\nThe final event of Notes from the London Commune, Mysteries of July is the product of a burgeoning period of integrated practice in cinema. Over their fifteen years of work, the BAFC created not just films, but a cinematic infrastructure which revolved around communal pedagogy and production. Mysteries of July builds on an aesthetic and social perspective which finds community in past and present struggle. \\n\\nThis screening will be followed by a conversation between director Reece Auguiste, series curator James Elsey and The Otolith Collective. \\n\\nDoors open at 5.30pm; event starts at 6pm and ends at 8pm. \\n\\nThe Otolith Collective is supported using public funding by Arts Council England.\\n\\nImage credit: still from Mysteries of July, 1991, Reece Auguiste and the Black Audio Film Collective.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/library-transmission-mysteries-of-july\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":804,\"name\":\"Somebody Should Have Pressed Record by Galia Admoni in conversation with Luke Kennard\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-06T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-06T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4b0d65030d3fbb65cd357b416292b8da.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Galia Admoni and Luke Kennard read from and discuss their new books, each preoccupied, in different forms, with performance, invention and the unstable boundary between inner life and the world as it is lived.\\n\\nAdmoni’s Somebody Should Have Pressed Record is an experimental narrative poem tracing a relationship with an imagined version of Joseph Gilgun. Drawing on auto-destructive art and existentialist fiction, it locates romance at the edge of unreality, where loneliness becomes animate and the figures we conjure begin to make demands of their own.\\n\\nKennard’s Black Bag reimagines the campus novel as a study in concealment and estrangement: a penniless actor accepts a job that requires him to sit, unseen, inside a black bag at the back of a lecture hall. At once comic and disorienting, the novel attends to masculinity, usefulness and the odd theatricality of contemporary existence.\\n\\nMoving between the absurd and the intimate, both books are concerned with the pressure that fantasy exerts on ordinary life: the roles we construct, the presences we sustain, and the cost of maintaining them. The authors will read from their work and be in conversation, followed by audience questions.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://burleyfisherbooks.com/products/somebody-should-have-pressed-record-galia-admoni-luke-kennard\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":782,\"name\":\"Activating the Archives - National HIV Story Trust\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-06T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c0e59e4af07a13f86b3b991da6545415.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"What is an archive and what does it do? How do we engage with the stories that lay within? And what does it mean to activate and respond to an archive, particularly one with such a diffuse set of experiences and an overwhelming socio-political history?  \\n\\n\\nJoin the National HIV Stories Trust Archive Volunteers for an evening of sharing creative responses and working to understand the memory and care housed within the National HIV Stories Trust archives.  \\n\\n\\nRefreshments provided.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38137/activating-the-archives-national-hiv-story-trust\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":793,\"name\":\"Cubitt Ceilidh Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-06T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"60b316dc8460d86e18b7d392bd2ef402.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Cubitt takes over Cafe OTO for a cèilidh, a social evening and cultural celebration common in Gaelic cultures, raising funds towards the costs of Cubitt’s recently announced move.\\n\\nFounded by artists in 1991, Cubitt is one of London’s oldest artist-run cooperatives. For thirty-five years, it has supported artistic experimentation through its affordable studios, non-profit gallery and education programme, while creating opportunities for artists and curators at formative stages in their careers.\\n\\nCubitt’s work extends far beyond its building. Its longstanding community and education programmes bring artists together with young people, schools, older residents and local communities across Islington, creating space for learning, participation and exchange.\\n\\nAfter twenty-five years at Angel Mews, Cubitt is working to secure a new permanent home from which it can continue supporting experimental artistic and curatorial practices in the heart of London.\\n\\nThis cèilidh is an opportunity to gather around Cubitt at a crucial moment, celebrate everything it has built and help carry it into its next chapter.\\n\\nFollowing the roaring success of Cubitt’s previous cèilidh, we are joining forces with Cafe OTO for a second edition in its much-loved East London home.\\n\\nAt the centre of the evening will be live cèilidh music and dancing, performed by a one-night-only band assembled by friends and members of Shovel Dance Collective, with the full musical line-up announced shortly.\\n\\nCubitt staff, artists, friends and supporters will also contribute poetry readings, a fundraising raffle and DJ sets throughout the evening.\\n\\nDress is informal, although kilts are warmly encouraged. Our fear an taighe—master of ceremonies—and caller for the dancers will be Cubitt Director of Programmes Seán Elder.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://dice.fm/partner/tickets/event/9232no-cubitt-cilidh-fundraiser-6th-aug-cafe-oto-london-tickets\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":727,\"name\":\"Corder\\u0026friends\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-06T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-06T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"222f29cb6ef69d76ead3beea22b5d06f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join Daze Corder for a night of music and performance at Love Affair Basement in the August heat, gathering funds and warmth for The Outside Project's Trans Winter Night Shelter.\\n\\nEnjoy an eclectic (and marvellous) lineup of artists exploring performance through cover, copy, and homage. It might be experimental, it might be spectacular. There's only one way to find out.\\n\\nSo many artists, performers, and people find themselves through others and their work - reading, idolising, embodying. This is a space to explore it. What does it mean to find yourself by being someone else?\\n\\nAnd there might be karaoke.\\n\\nLineup to be announced soon @d_corder_\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":734,\"name\":\"fupper, the dengie hundred and not:hulme\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-06T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-07T11:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9e895c42b63c6b5f2739e1054bd61739.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Fupper (live), The Dengie Hundred (live) and not:hulme (dj) will be performing at Spanners on the 6th August for the album launch of ‘Nullius” by Fupper out on Wrongspeed records this summer. \\n\\nFupper\\n\\nFupper (Simon Hughes) will be performing tracks and collages based around the new album ‘Nullius’ which is the fourth Fupper album for Wrong Speed records and comes with a limited edition companion book of the same name. \\n\\nThis album marks Fupper’s 22nd release and fifth book in a project that has lasted for over 30 years with releases on Wrongspeed, Tritone, Jonson Family, Inversions and Diwasou.\\n\\nThe Fupper sound is a blend of nostalgic guitar, down-tuned xylophone, harmonica, slumbering bass, crumbling rhythms fed through manipulated 1/4” tape loops spilling out their own found sounds and curios, gathered together on a 4 track and sampler and let breath until they find their way. \\n\\nSlipstream, wabi-sabi soundtracks and text that celebrate imperfection and transience. \\n\\nwww.fupper.co.uk\\nwww.fupper.bandcamp.com\\n\\n\\nThe Dengie Hundred \\n\\nThe Dengie Hundred is an ongoing project, always in flux, which responds to landscapes, bodies, everyday objects and field recordings. The project includes lo-fi love songs on debut Brackenbank; ferric, guitar-drenched psychogeography on Lammas Land; an album built from samples taken from a piece of plastic tubing, stretched to near-impossible limits, on Tube; two collaborative, shamisen-centred albums with Japan Blues; and two albums of gothic dream pop with writer and singer Gemma Blackshaw.\\n\\nThe Dengie Hundred’s eclectic approach to music making is held together by an underlying dub sensibility, reverb and delay, creating a sonic hall of mirrors where emotions and atmospheres, influences and found sounds get smudged into strange, otherworldly tableaus.\\n\\nCollaboratively and solo, The Dengie Hundred has released music on Sagome, DDS, Somewhere Press, Altered States Tapes, Ethbo, World Of Echo, and their own imprint Tain Records.\\n\\nhttps://tainrecords.bandcamp.com/music\\n\\nDJs not:hulme (Final Image)\\n\\nnot:hulme are Laura Not and Andrew Hulme when they team up at the decks to dj.\\u2028Laura Not is an artist and dj, working visually and sonically through the medium of collage and curating radio programmes focussing on experimental sounds such as (x)=musik on Lyl radio. Andrew Hulme is a musician and film-maker. He is a founding member of the post-industrial ambient band O Yuki Conjugate and has been active in several other projects such as A Small Good Thing, Gush and most recently dis fac. Laura and Andrew also make music together as a duo and run the label Final Image where they release new and archival material.\\n\\nhttp://soundcloud.com/nothulme\\nhttp://finalimage.bandcamp.com\\nhttps://infanttree.bandcamp.com/album/almost-something-2\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":823,\"name\":\"Noisy Women Present | Phil Minton's Almost Instant Feral Choir\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-06T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-06T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1f7114f8d142f4c3c05c522e32abb8a8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"With Faradena Afifi, Steve Beresford, Iris Colomb, Charlie Foloronsho, Chris Freeman, Aurelie Freoua, Leanne Holroyd, Ningrui Liu, Jo Morrison, Maggie Nicols, Carys Mai, Majik Ogunwa, Jenni Roditi, Anjalika Sagar, Nini Sakhri, Bettina Schroeder, James Smith, Nicky Smith, Julian Woods, Gina Fergione \\u0026 more!\\n\\nThere will be a solo from Faradena Afifi \\u0026 a trio from Jo Morrison, Jenni Roditi, Phil Minton \\u0026 in the first half. \\n\\n\\n--\\n\\nThe Feral Choir project is a series of vocal workshops with non-professionals, leading up to performances. It originated in the late 1980’s when I was asked to do some workshops with ‘non-singers’ in the Musik Centrum Stockholm. The success of these led me to develop the idea further. The choir consists of a three day workshop and performance, not only for singers but for anyone who takes a delight in the freedom to experiment. I encourage participants to take a vocal leap and explore all vocal possibilities through exercises and improvisations, over the workshop period, leading to a concert.\\n\\nFeral Choir workshops and performances have subsequently been held in many different places around the world including Berlin, Centre for Performance Research Cardiff, Musickzentrum Munich, Tokyo, Angelica Bologna, City Festival Lausanne, Institute for Living Voice Antwerp, Baltimore, Nante, Brest, Oxford, Paris, Oakland, Melbourne, St. Paulo, Rio de Janeiro, Bristol, Pau, Florence, Le Man, Trondheim, Rotterdam, Ghent, Zurich, Nancy Vandoeuvre, Poitiers, London, Amsterdam, Warsaw, Brugge, Strasbourg, and Aberystwyth.\\n\\nSome of the choirs have been made up of professionals, sometimes actors and musicians, but many have been amateur groups with no previous musical interest or experience. These have been particularly rewarding, as has the work with teenagers in Belgium and Holland, and the responses from the participants have been overwhelmingly positive.\\n\\nwww.philminton.co.uk \\n\\n--\\n\\nThe Noisy Women Present is a multi-disciplinary creative hub championing diversity and collective virtuosity. Our concerts, workshops and events embrace improvised and experimental music, movement, art and poetry. We believe in individual expression as part of a collaborative, liberating experience.\\n\\nIn 2024 TNWP were awarded a fellowship by the Serpentine Gallery as part of its Support Structures for Support Structures programme. These are awarded to artists at the forefront of social practice, community practice and collaborative working. \\n\\nOur associated ensemble, the Noisy People’s Improvising Orchestra, explores these ideals on a grander scale, and welcomes performers with neuro-diversity and learning differences.\\n\\nPlease get in touch if you’d like to book us for performances and/or workshops.\\n\\nwww.noisywomenpresent.co.uk/\\n\\n-- \\n\\nPoster: Aurelie Freoua\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":712,\"name\":\"Choreographic Devices V\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-07T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-07T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f9b54b96e354202d8a4343e9282a2867.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Choreographic Devices is an itinerant annual research platform dedicated to choreographic and post-dance practices across artistic, discursive and curatorial fields.\\n \\nSince 2022, and against the pressured backdrops of permacrisis and depletion, Choreographic Devices has been testing how bodies, material assemblages, organisational forms and modes of being alongside one another might be choreographed otherwise. Drawing on a broad ecology of practices and bringing together key local and international practitioners, the platform understands choreographic inquiry as extending beyond the event itself into its organisational architectures. Its modular and scalable format moves fluidly between integrated multi-day programmes, screenings, discursive exchanges, workshops and performative gatherings.\\n \\nFor its fifth iteration at Mimosa House, Choreographic Devices presents a moving-image programme exploring the choreographic as an expanded methodology for organising relations across bodies, images, perception and time. Selected by friends and allies of Choreographic Devices, the assembled works approach moving image as a site of choreographic inquiry, inviting new ways of sensing, composing and orienting perception across cinematic and choreographic registers.\\n\\nChoreographic Devices is convened by Murat Adash, Ofri Cnaani, Sara Sassanelli and Edgar Schmitz, and produced by Sara Sassanelli (Alice Agency), with technical support by Jack Hogan.\\n\\nLead Image: Slob Air (still) by Mica Levi made in collaboration with Izzy Moriarty Thompson, Joe Auborn and Jack Parton. Starring Madi Swain\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":787,\"name\":\"Voicing Project Work In Progress \",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-07T17:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-07T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4fee48830e3d745883d66566dcaab7e7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"As we reach the end of our residency we will be presenting new choral pieces alongside physical work developed during our time at The Writers Room. \\nWe will be pitching '2 Birds'.\\n\\n17:30 - Doors Open \\n35 Britannia Row, N1 5QH\\nTickets £5\\nNo one turned away for lack of funds.\\n\\n\\nEmail voicingproject@gmail.com for more info.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":813,\"name\":\"ROOTS SUMMIT PRESENTS KING MAJESTY MEETS JAH ORTHODOX\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-07T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-08T01:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2d9dfa3b7d81a17dc8e2a0c81ac5c30b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"🟥🟨🟩ROOTS SUMMIT 🟥🟨🟩 KING MAJESTY MEETS JAH ORTHODOX AUGUST 7th 2026 BROOKHOUSE,HAYES\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":655,\"name\":\"Nick Granata Album Launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-07T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-07T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"da9b32a9873127c7739ee9f2ebb21585.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To celebrate the release of the debut solo album from Nick Granata - My Heart is Running Backwards! A Martial Artist! With a Closed Fist! Woof! - we will be hosting a gig at The Ivy House.\\n\\nPerforming on the night will be\\n\\nNick Granata (full band)\\nBig Oil\\nJosh Barfoot\\n\\nTickets £7 - no one turned away for lack of funds.\\n\\nThe Ivy House is a single-floor venue that has a single step at its entrance, with a gender neutral toilet. There will not be a sign language interpreter at this event. This will be a standing event, but if you require seating please let us know and we can accommodate. Any questions please feel free to email us at tom@doubleda.re\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":722,\"name\":\"Patterns: NZO (Live), KD22LR and Lali\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-07T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-08T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b097a5a87bb9a6544e7259a75d588400.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":838,\"name\":\"GROOVY GROOVY London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-07T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-08T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"90eb77388e6bc72abf4d2970206faacd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"London massive… are you in the mood for a sexy party? If you are, you’re in luck. GROOVY GROOVY is back in town at M.O.T on Friday August 7. You are cordially invited to join us in cooking up this late summer dance.\\n\\nGROOVY GROOVY is a New York based DIY community of ravers on a life-long journey to Planet Groovy - a spiritually-charged space intended for raw creative expression. Akanbi will lead this English excursion alongside two London-based guardians of the dance, Neffa-T \\u0026 Tailor Jae. Expect mind-expanding \\u0026 body-rocking boogie music all night long. These 3 DJs bring an organic \\u0026 bubbly energy to the dance each \\u0026 every time. Your enjoyment is absolutely guaranteed. The iconic Unit 18 at M.O.T is the terminal to Planet Groovy. Come \\u0026 rock with us…the world could end after this night.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2485318\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":530,\"name\":\"Day \\u0026 Night Refugee Fundraiser (Skull Rub X High Hats X Felt Sound System)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-08T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-09T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0532820472360a37b105af852abb51dd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A stacked day + night festival brought to you by three London collectives, Skull Rub, HIGH HATS, and Felt Sound system (also providing their heavyweight sound system). Raising vital funds for Lewisham Donation Hub and Plateful Cafe, both of whom are doing substantial bits to support migrants and locals in need.\\n\\nProviding the fuel for the dance is Plateful Cafe, a social enterprise supporting refugees through culinary training. They will be on-site all day serving up incredible food handmade by the refugees they support, with all proceeds going directly back into their mission.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":733,\"name\":\"Haunting in Tandem: a one-day dance and performance festival\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-08T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-08T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9d930a4b595e2d05d2e478c71e85b36b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Artists haunt this city, from its financial centres to its residential backstreets. In 2026 London our work occupies the ghost space of collective dreaming: the ghost of movement, as a social object, shared, multiplied.\\n\\n‘Haunting in Tandem’ unites over 20 artists from the Chisenhale Dance Space artist community, bringing their work together in a one-day festival spanning film, dance, live choreography, music and performance. This will be a day of discovery - works simultaneously popping up in hallways, stairwells, bathrooms, offices and (of course) our iconic studios. Tickets go from £8 - £12.\\n\\nAs our community continues to rethink our position in advance of a change to the CDS site, this program asks, what can our bodies do here, that we can’t do anywhere else? What seeds has our building (occupied and artist-run since 1983) sown in us?\\n\\nWith performances from Alice Labant, Sean Murray, Max Percy, Yuka Hayashi, Stošija Zrinski, Satoshi Date, Manuela Albrecht, Moyra Cecilia Silva, and Nimai Sham.\\n\\nWorkshops from Ashley Lim, Zoe Tankard, and Lucy Turner.\\n\\nShort film screening curated by Michael Mendones (artists TBA).\\n\\nThis is event has been curated by Ophey Chan and Renée Bellamy.\\n\\nIt has been produced by Sonya Woodruff.\\n\\nGraphic design by Mara Never.\\n\\nACCESSIBILITY NOTES: Sadly, our building does not have step-free access. Parts of the program will be streamed for those not able to join us in person. We do not have BSL interpretation for this event, but will make sure that works and live speech are captioned wherever possible. A quiet space will be available for parts of the event, and there will be staff onsite to help with welfare needs. \\n\\nChildren are welcome at the event, but some works will feature nudity.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://whatson.chisenhaledancespace.co.uk/events/chisenhaledancespace/2305450\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":827,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction Presents: Portrait Generation, Details, Bubble Gun\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-08T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6f2c6d02a28f0318252d5f44841f8fa1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Portrait Generation: Portrait Generation are a UK alt-rock band from Southend. Known for driving guitars, raw energy and unapologetically honest songwriting. Their sound is led by powerful female vocals and grounded in real-world themes.\\n\\nDetails: Formed in 2024 by guitarists Nick Dawson \\u0026 James Green, bassist James Beddow and drummer Ross Wallman. The band are heavily influenced by artists such as We Lost The Sca, This Will Destroy You, Mogwai and Slint. Each member brings a very different perspective to the mix, with rich and diverse. back stories in the vibrant alt rock, post hardeore and the experimental electronic noise scenes of Essex and London.\\n\\nBubble Gun: Starting in 2025, Bubble Gun mixes Garage Punk and Hip Hop, singing songs about executions, creepy girls and pessimism. His 3-piece band play punky guitar with bass over live break beats.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":794,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction: Portrait Generation, Details, Cigarette Kixxes\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-08T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b1e31941f7c073d4eb2b09d543a475d1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Portrait Generation: Portrait Generation are a UK alt-rock band from Southend. Known for driving guitars, raw energy and unapologetically honest songwriting. Their sound is led by powerful female vocals and grounded in real-world themes.\\n\\nDetails: Formed in 2024 by guitarists Nick Dawson \\u0026 James Green, bassist James Beddow and drummer Ross Wallman. The band are heavily influenced by artists such as We Lost The Sca, This Will Destroy You, Mogwai and Slint. Each member brings a very different perspective to the mix, with rich and diverse. back stories in the vibrant alt rock, post hardeore and the experimental electronic noise scenes of Essex and London.\\n\\nCigarette Kixxes: Cigarette Kixxes is a 3-piece rock band from London. Rez, Neng and Seamus formed in the summer of 2025. Their songs were put together through a mix of jamming and sharing early sketches of tracks, influenced by Grunge, Psychedelic Rock, Hip Hop and Punk.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":726,\"name\":\"Erstwile\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-08T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-09T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ecacd6d413574ff2ef59c42d70bc008a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"the missing h presents...\\n\\na denial of what is current. \\nthe armatures of contemporary craft. \\na music erstwhile encountered.\\n\\ndownstairs in the tin-foil chamber of Deptford will be:\\n\\nGema German and Gary The Tall on saucers. \\nZrad Durmin and Simone Perspex on the ones and zeros. \\n\\nExcavators adhering to a strict 80’-89’ commandment. \\nEBM, Electro, Post-Punk, New-Wave, Industrial, New Beat amongst relatives.\\n\\nAugust 8th\\n10pm - 3am\\n\\nThe Bunker Club\\n46 Deptford Broadway\\nSE8 4PH\\n\\n£8 entry \\nCash only bar (atm nearby)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":679,\"name\":\"SLIVER • 004\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-08T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-09T07:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"380ffbfcb3ec419f4ed6cc52679cf2a7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"from the deepest of dreams we astir from our bliss \\nwhispers breathe in the air, an awakening not to be missed ⟢\\n\\n⟡ 08.08 • S L I V E R • 23:00-07:00 ⟡\\n\\nANNX\\nMATRIARK B2B MONA SAGE\\nSLINKY KINKY\\nTANGELA\\n\\nFlowing, moving, growing, evolving…\\n\\nA celebration of excellence in London's queer trance and techno scenes ⟢\\n\\nAfter a one-year hiatus since our last encounter, our 4th edition births a brand new season of SLIVER.\\n\\nOur re-birth inhabits our city's favourite Steam Room at FOLD and we’re excited to invite two international artists to guide us in ritual alongside a selection of our favourite local enchanters, including a new SLIVER resident debut.\\n\\nSLIVER is first and foremost a FLINTA+ and queer space. Anyone with an open heart who is a part of the queer communities or considers themselves an active ally is welcome to celebrate with us.\\n\\nAt its core, we believe that each sliver shines just as bright as the next. There will be no hierarchy and set times are to remain unannounced.\\n\\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \\n\\na r t i s t s :\\n\\n⟡ a n n x ⟡\\nInspired by cities and dancefloors where she’s lived and explored, ANNX’s unique seductive sound echos within her psychedelic selections across trance, prog, psy, techno, tech house, dubstep and more.\\n\\nAnna’s commitment to the scene goes beyond the booth, she carefully identifies niche sounds that are missing in the UK and has become a staple for psychedelic music on London’s club circuit. In 2021, she founded Whomp, a non-profit party in London which she now co-runs with Lora Mipsum. In 2023, she started a brand-new project perspectives• with lighting designer Nicole Gordon. Most recently, she joined the Above Below music team.\\n\\n\\n⟡ m e l a t i ⟡ \\nMelati steps in for Matriark who can no longer make it to London for her b2b with Mona Sage. \\n\\nSpawned from an unapologetically deep, psychedelic and sensual sound, Melati meanders the wider realms of techno, trance and psy, weaved together in a style that favours mesmeric blends with technical precision.\\n\\nAs an artist, venue manager and promoter, Melati’s relationship with music is intrinsic to every aspect of their life. From a Masters of Architecture that explores the spatial, social and political position of nightclubs in a city to a tangible body of on-the-ground work in venues, Melati has lived and breathed the spaces in which we find sanctuary throughout all of their adult career.\\n\\n\\n⟡ m o n a s a g e ⟡\\nBorn into a family of musicians in sunny Toulouse, it’s evident where Mona got her natural musical flair from.\\n\\nMona’s famously energetic, eclectic arsenal of tracks mirror her own vibrant personality. A desire to entertain sees her sets meticulously weave between techno, breakbeats, electro and all the rich, deep and driving bits in between.\\n\\n\\n⟡ s l i n k y k i n k y ⟡\\nWith a thirst for growth, she moves with a intuitive flow that is felt through her sets. She builds a cocoon of energy on the dancefloor, weaving high-energy pumpers, psychedelic textures and chuggy, hypnotic techno, pulling every room she touches into a trance.\\n\\nEvery set is constructed with intent: a dialogue between physical movement and emotional resonance. Slinky Kinky’s performances are designed to charge the atmosphere, pulling dancers into her orbit and keeping them there until the very last beat.\\n\\n\\n⟡ t a n g e l a ⟡\\nTangela’s style of aural storytelling is as distinct as it is varied. She guides the listener through deep, subby, subterranean worlds; encouraging listeners to float up through spacious, textural soundscapes full of unexpected turns, all with a nimble and playful touch.\\n\\nWith her strength lying in versatility of genre, her sound is undeniably psychedelic, \\u0026 one with deep connection to the Australian bush she soundtracks so regularly. She transports you with intention to moments in leafy clearings, hazy morning rays poking through the gumtrees, thumping kicks drenched in subby, dubby, gurgling undertones.\\n\\n\\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \\n\\ne n j o y m e n t :\\nThis is a space for celebration, exploration, expression and positive release. It is encouraged to participate mindfully with awareness of yourself and the space you fill.\\n\\nb o u n d a r i e s :\\nPlease leave any assumptions of gender, sexuality, race, ability or identity at the door and proceed to interact with those who give enthusiastic consent. We expect the community to treat themselves, each other and the space with kindness and respect.\\n\\nn o u r i s h m e n t :\\nWe implore you to immerse yourself in the party, the music and the space and enjoy it at your own pace. We will not be serving food this time, so feel free to bring snacks to fuel your body to dance until the sunrise. The venue will not permit liquids of any form.\\n\\nl i m i t s :\\nStrictly 21+.\\nPhysical ID is mandatory for entry.\\nPhotography will not be permitted.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":580,\"name\":\"Steam Down Soundsystem X Imaginary Millions\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-09T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-09T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4d4d20c2725527061d247ffd8797497a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Southeast London’s legendary Steamdown are coming to the garden with the Imaginary Millions crew.\\n\\nSteam Down is a British Afro-Punk band, weekly event and music community based in London. In a finely tuned alchemy of sound, space and energy, Steam Down have mastered the art of enriching human emotional, social and collective state of being through music.  Founded by multi-instrumentalist, composer and producer Ahnansé in 2017, the initial event was created to connect London based musicians and producers. Since then it has evolved into a weekly event where Steam Down artists and its extended musical family generate spontaneous sonic soundscapes reflecting their lives in the city.  Steam Down has quickly become a household name in London’s music scene, receiving two Jazz FM awards including the innovation award sponsored by Mishcon De Reya and live experience of the year award sponsored by Yamaha UK featuring Kamasi Washington. In addition, Sky News produced a full feature on Steam Down and its fundamental role within London’s flourishing jazz scene.  Imaginary Millions started off as a live jam in Shoreditch where regulars came to expect two hours of incredible non-stop live improvised music where any member of the audience could get up and sing, rap, speak, dance as they felt moved. Imaginary Millions have also had one of Soho Radio’s most exciting radio shows over the last 5+ years. Expect live jams, eclectic mixes, poetry that speaks to this time and a celebration of creativity in all of its forms.  More to be announced.\\n\\nSupported by a grassroots music grant from Arts Council England, helping us continue to champion emerging artists and live music in the community.  All events support Lewisham Donation Hub, a local charity providing vital support to those facing acute hardship across South East London.  The largest pub garden in SE London will have street food, drinks, and a laid-back summer atmosphere. Families are welcome, with free entry for children, market stalls, and activities to keep little ones entertained.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/steam-down-soundsystem-x-imaginary-millions/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":824,\"name\":\"Touching Bass Carnival Jam 2026: Wiley (Jungle Set), FAUZIA, Nidia, Kikelomo, ZENA meet SLICKNBOBBY \\u0026 More\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-09T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-09T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"716cc417448177f26719d8c1ab15e80f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Now in its fifth year, the Touching Bass Carnival Jam unites the finest names across the soundsystem continuum and beyond for an all-ages-welcome, pre–Notting Hill Carnival gathering of music, dance and food.\\n\\nIn collaboration with Felt Sound System, we mark ten years of Touching Bass inna Brixton—alongside friends, sonic lynchpins, and a new wave of future ones-to-watch—for a Sunday session for the books.\\n\\nTopping the bill is the grime godfather himself WILEY with an incredibly rare return to his jungle MC roots; backed by FAUZIA on decks. Local titans ZENA and SLICKNBOBBY collide for an Ethio Jazz-meets-dub live special in celebration of their latest release.\\n\\nAs ever, the wider spectrum of Afro-diasporic sonics also finds home: KIKELOMO and FAT-LÏP traverse its full length and breadth, while Príncipe Discos’ NÍDIA sweats the dance with the percussive rhythms of Lisbon's south. Meanwhile, Dennery Segment and bouyon are represented by UK-via-Saint Lucian don TOP KLAS. \\n\\nTouching Bass stewards ERROL and MS. SANKOFA pepper the final seasoning on what is always a highlight of our calendar year.\\n\\nThere’ll be space for kids in our dedicated children’s area. If unnu hungry, come nourish your belly with the finest in Caribbean food; lovingly provided by the Chaneti Eats/Hills of Troy family.\\n\\nArtwork: Teshome Douglas-Campbell ‘Dancehall 2’\\n\\nSupported by New Balance\\n\\n--\\n\\nPLEASE READ:\\n\\n- Physical ID is required for entry\\n- Under 18s must be accompanied by an adult\\n- Under 16s enter free; 16-18 year olds will be charged £10.00 on the door\\n- We advise parents to provide ear protection for babies/small children.\\n- A dedicated child's area and baby-changing facilities will be provided for babies/small children; standby for more info\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2441079\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":826,\"name\":\"Loop Sessions LDN 032 w/ Apollo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-09T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-09T19:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"34c351e4ea0ea3dd7778f1ec7d0046fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Loop Sessions LDN is a chapter of a global sample flip challenge, since 2016. Just come along with your laptop or beatmaking device of choice, MPC, SP404, etc (plus headphones, of course). Everyone has 3 hours to make a track using the curated samples by our guest, at 6pm we play them all on the sound system. All genres and skill levels are welcome.\\n\\nWe have a UK Hip Hop legend in the building for session 32. Beatmaker \\u0026 rapper Apollo aka Apollomakingbeats, from the iconic super crew 'Champions Of Nature' with Jehst, Lewis Parker, Supa T, etc. \\n\\nHe's still active cooking up the heat. Check out his recent project, The Moncoo City EP. Plus, he drops regular videos on his IG page \\u0026 YouTube channel. We grew up listening to this man's music, so we're very excited to have him as a guest curating the samples.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":831,\"name\":\"Alien I\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-10T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-10T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2c5bc3e404bf8dde361ca4a62bf8f64e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Alien I is a group/band/night built up from text messages, kinship and slow work\\n\\nWe’ve got some weird stories to tell you and some nice music to share. Come listen and hang out!\\n\\n~ Lewisham Art House\\n\\n~ 10 August, 6.30pm\\n\\n~ £5.00\\n\\n\\nRael \\u0026 Flint, ft. Lottie, Ruby and Grace: We started a band to tell a tale about the undergrowth\\n\\nTony Onuchukwu: “I just wanted to let you know that I’ve had a crush on you for the last 5 seconds”\\n\\nHannah Walton: Guard Hairs To The Light is a performance about you, Hannah, and a horse\\n\\nToby Evans-Jesra: “I got a story about a chilli I want to read somewhere (the chilli is magic)”\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":830,\"name\":\"Laila Sakini + Rebecca Salvadori + Ella Fleck\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-10T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-10T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"58b823a48e0f2b03e279ef51e3792e4f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An assortment of sensory explorations designed to work in tandem to provide a night of full immersion expanding on traditional notions of experience. A silent film, a bespoke scent, a reading and a musical performance.\\n\\nThe event brings together three London based artists: multi instrumentalist Laila Sakini, filmmaker Rebecca Salvadori with writer and artist Ella Fleck.\\n\\nThere will be a screening of seminal silent film EMPATHY by Rebecca Salvadori. Ella Fleck will recite a reading and emit a bespoke scent made for the occasion via an automated machine. Multi instrumentalist Laila Sakini will perform an extended set of new and known works from her discography.\\n____________\\n\\nLaila Sakini\\n\\nMulti-instrumentalist, vocalist, producer and performer Laila Sakini is London based, Melbourne born.\\n\\nHer major works include Like A Gun (EP), Vivienne (LP), Strada (EP), Into The Traffic, Under The Moonlight (LP), Princess Diana of Wales (LP), Cupo (LP w/ Valentina Magalett) and Figures (LP w/ Dr Lucy Van) among several single, EPs and cassette release on her series Mystery Messages.\\n\\nWorking with piano, voice, guitar and silence Laila creates dynamic and textured environments that provide the listener with space to develop their own meanings and responses.\\n\\nLaila has performed at: Cafe Oto, Galeria Zé dos Bois, Berlin Atonal, De Nor, Listen! festival, Gaudeamus Festival, Meakusma x Arkaoda, The London Handel Festival, Wunkderkammer Festival, Ponto d’Orvalho, Intonal Festival and among others.\\nShe has been featured several times in The Wire Magazine, graced the cover of Switzerland’s cult Zweikommasiben music magazine, been featured on BBC1, in Frances’ Les Inrockuptibles, LA’s AQNB, Belgium’s Gonzo magazine, Italy’s Blow Up and in several specials on NTS Radio, LYL, Dublab, Red Light.\\n\\nElla Fleck\\n\\nElla Fleck (b. 1993, London, UK) is a London-based artist and writer. Her practice examines the entanglement of psychosexual ideologies within invisible systems of technology. She works across installation - using infiltration, sound, architecture, language, scent and chemical-signalling.\\n\\nShe holds a BA in English Literature from Exeter University (2014) and is completing an MFA in Fine Art from Goldsmiths University of London (2026). Upcoming exhibitions include Goldsmiths MFA Degree show (2026); Ehrlich Steinberg, Los Angeles, CA (2026) and Matt’s Gallery, London, UK (2027). Previous exhibitions have taken place at 15th Kaunas Biennial, Kaunas, LT (2025); Piccallili Gallery, London, UK (2026); St Margaret’s House Chapel, London, UK (2025); Season 4, Episode 6, London, UK (2024); Nada House, Governor’s Island, NY (2024) and Semester 9, Amsterdam, NL (2024). Fleck’s work features in publications such as i-D, Plaster, The Toe Rag and Emergent.\\n\\nRebecca Salvadori\\n\\nRebecca Salvadori is an Italian-Australian artist and filmmaker working across moving image, live performance, and installation. Over the past fifteen years, she has developed a distinctive body of work at the intersection of contemporary art and experimental music, creating intimate portraits of musicians, clubs, and communities that blur the boundaries between documentary, expanded cinema, and performance. Rather than treating film as a fixed medium, she approaches it as a way of thinking, developing works that take the form of films, performances, site-specific commissions, and expanded moving-image installations\\n\\nSelected works include Rave Trilogy (2017–2020), The Sun Has No Shadow (2022), TRESOR TAPES (2022), Messengers (2022–ongoing), A Forbidden Distance (2024), and Not Running (2026). Collaboration is central to her practice, and she has worked with artists and musicians including Lucy Railton, Nhu Xuan Hua, Mark Fell, Coby Sey, Okkyung Lee, Saint Abdullah, Eomac, Charlie Hope, and Alabaster DePlume.\\n\\nHer work has been presented at the Institute of Contemporary Arts (ICA) London, FOMU – Photography Museum Antwerp, Triennale Milano, the Serralves Museum, Porto, and the Timișoara Architecture Biennial (BETA), among others, as well as at major experimental music festivals including Sonic Acts Biennale, CTM, Berlin Atonal, Unsound, Rewire, Le Guess Who?, and Sónar. In 2025, she received the Italian Council Grant from the Italian Ministry of Culture to develop and internationally produce her first feature-length film.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/laila-sakini-rebecca-salvadori-ella-fleck/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":755,\"name\":\"Earth and Bones Residency ft. Anna Chai \\u0026 Richard Ọlátúndé Baker (first night)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-10T19:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-10T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5d9710c9ff72997d5dbfc066aba664c3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Doors 7:45 PM, Music 8:30 PM – 2 sets of music\\n \\n\\nLine-up:\\nIdris Rahman – Woodwinds\\nLiran Donin – Double bass\\nAnna Chai – Saxes, Flutes\\nRichard Ọlátúndé Baker – West African drums and percussion\\n\\nAbout\\nIdris Rahman and Liran Donin. Together they are creating a fully improvised compositions as they explore unique melodies, intimate sonic spaces, textures and meditative grooves influenced by the wide variety of music the two have assimilated into their sound.\\n\\nFollowing their EU tour and second sold out release the two will celebrate their third limited release with a three day residency hosting some of UK unique voices!\\n\\nFrom Indian and north African inspired rhythms and all the way back to raw ecstatic melodies, the two are incorporating a wide palette of instrumentation including double and electric bass, bass clarinet, tenor sax, bamboo flutes, Tibetan singing bowls, percussion, voices and electronics they create musical worlds that take the listener on a unique spiritual and emotional journey striking the balance between song based forms and open structures.\\n\\nThis special three day residency will see them collaborate with some of their favourite musicians, allowing improv and experimentation to predominate.\\n\\nEach night will begin with a duo set by Earth and Bones followed the second set inviting guests to an improvised conversation.\\n\\nThis will be a special residency allowing deep exploration of sonic worlds and a chance for meditative and hypnotic connections, a series not to be missed.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.universe.com/events/earth-and-bones-residency-liran-donin-and-idris-rahman-tickets-PBQ23C\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":843,\"name\":\"Circadian Radio\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-11T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"10b1a0a3fbe5f097f49dab3698cd3546.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Circadian Radio is a night of performances by poets and writers, at Housmans Bookshop. \\n\\n★ The night features performances by: Hesse K, Francis Jones, Sara Mostafa, Oisín Roberts, Jordan Minga, Phoebe Eccles, Maya Uppal, Will Aghoghogbe and open mic slots ★\\n\\nDuring the evening, the performances are offered in solidarity with our dear friend, a writer who is fundraising anonymously for combined visa and top surgery costs. As anonymous fundraisers often slip to the back of people's mind, this event has been organised by their friends to encourage donations to their gofundme.  \\n\\nThere will be a donations based bar with both soft and alcoholic drinks at the venue. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38334/circadian-radio\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":828,\"name\":\"FREE DRUMMING WORKSHOP FOR FLINTA BY VALERIA PACIFIC\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-11T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-11T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6a391e4e53e5881a9ac3429539da8558.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a special drumming workshop in Burgess Park led by Valeria Pacific, the first artist in residence as part of Studio 12's Residency Programme: A Door to Experimentation.\\n\\nThis workshop invites FLINTA participants to explore the drum not only as a musical instrument, but as a technology for communication, community building, presence, collective care and self-expression. Drawing on bullerengue and other Afro-Colombian traditions, we'll learn foundational techniques and rhythms, reflect on the historical relationship between women and the drum and build confidence through a shared practice. (Bring your own drum - all drums welcome)\\n\\nAbout Valeria: Valeria Pacific is a drummer, DJ, community organiser and cultural producer. She is the director and lead drummer of Akolá Tambo, and co-founder and director of Bullerengue Circle. Her work has played a key role in giving visibility to bullerengue in the UK and Europe.\\n\\n*** Meeting Point Burgess Park - Club House Cafe ***\\n\\n_____\\n\\nDiscover the exciting programme we've curated throughout the residency, featuring workshops, performances and opportunities to engage with the artists as they develop new work.\\n\\n'A Door to Experimentation' brings together three emerging artists who are expanding their practice from traditional folk music into experimental, collaborative and cross-disciplinary music-making. Throughout the residency, they are mentored by Patricia Doors, exploring new approaches to sound, performance and creative exchange.\\n\\nThis residency has been made possible with the generous support of Arts Council England, Anglo Chilean Society, Movimientos and CASA.\\n\\nAbout Studio 12\\n\\nStudio 12 is an intimate art space and bespoke cocktail bar in Camberwell rooted in transnational solidarities — dedicated to art, music, poetry and gathering.\\n\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":763,\"name\":\"The Feminist Texts We Can’t Read: How Non-Translation Silences East Asian Movements\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-12T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-12T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4855f40cd67f05457c542c04cf0a0c59.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us on Wednesday 12th August, 6:30–8:30pm for The Feminist Texts We Can’t Read: How Non-Translation Silences East Asian Movements, a reading and discussion group with artists Soo Hyun Lee and Riley Tu. \\n\\nThis session explores East Asian feminist thought that remains largely unavailable to English-speaking audiences.\\n\\nDrawing on key texts from Japan and South Korea, the session asks how translation shapes the circulation of feminist knowledge, and what is lost when influential writing remains untranslated. Through excerpts from works by Ueno Chizuko, Jinsook Kim and Soo Hyun Lee, participants will consider how colonial histories, linguistic hierarchies and publishing structures shape which feminist ideas, histories and political struggles become visible in global conversations.\\n\\nThe session also introduces feminist organising in South Korea following the 2016 Gangnam Station murder, including the sticky-note memorials that transformed public space into a site of collective testimony and protest.\\n\\nAlongside these texts and case studies, participants will examine the geopolitics of translating both fiction and non-fiction, exploring how different forms of writing carry cultural, political and emotional meaning across languages. Together, these materials offer insight into feminist resistance in East Asian contexts while opening broader questions about translation, visibility and transnational solidarity.\\n\\nStructured as a collective reading and discussion, the event invites participants to read, reflect and exchange ideas. No prior knowledge is required. All reading materials will be provided and introduced during the session.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeVLpjfKm_1EUxNuo-sqVYtqnSrU5Khw1JRYeUkasOrYyYLDA/viewform\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":803,\"name\":\"Rhythm Race Revolution (RRR): Session 3 | Journeying the pluriverse with(in) Alice Coltrane\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-12T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6c4163390a9fd87036582237052f13d4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Rhythm Race Revolution is an 8-week course with Aditi Jaganathan that uses music and its attendant cultural texts, as a site of deep study, through which ideas of race, gender, colonialism, healing and transformative justice are collectively explored. It is a radical learning space tracing the sonic(s) of resistance.\\n\\nSession 3: Journeying the pluriverse with(in) Alice Coltrane\\n\\nIn this session we will traverse with and through the spiritual memory of Alice Coltrane, sedimented in the capacious archive of her music. We will dance in the liminality of her search for nirvana, and her deep yearning for collective spiritual transcendence. Journeying with her artistry we will tease out the mellifluous threads in her self-determined tapestry of liberation.\\n\\n“Jazz came about not through a book but through a flight of memory\\\" Édouard Glissant, 1990\\n\\nBio \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tzkrti.com/en/events/4342\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":496,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents | The New Wave Of UK Emo - mishikui, Prom, Funeral \\u0026 Wimp\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-13T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-13T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5605b837b687f4197d9f0e2bf686fa9b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nThe New Wave Of UK Emo\\n\\n4 new sad sounds from the underground:\\nmishikui\\nProm\\nFuneral\\nWimp\\n\\nThursday 13th August\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£10\\n\\nDoors 6pm\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/mishikui-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":799,\"name\":\"Lol K - present Languid Haunt the Trees – with support from Ha Kyoon + Charles Hayward \\u0026 CJ Calderwood\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-13T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-13T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ed348847ed342182ccafd48321644e48.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lol K are the South London duo of artist and musician CJ Calderwood and DJ and producer Junior XL. Among the vast sources they draw from in their songcraft are genres as diverse as post classical, grunge, and contemporary club music. Their highly varied output maintains focus by continually seeking to connect multiple – seemingly distant – sonic worlds.\\n\\nOn last year's ‘Languid Haunt the Trees’ (33-33), the duo developed upon the morphing, bass-heavy sounds of their debut album ‘climbing/holding/falling’ (Halcyon Veil) expanding on their worldbuilding through greater lyrical expression, while still delivering a diverse selection of instrumentation utilising flutes, saxophone, and warped pianos. In Lol K’s \\\"genreless\\\" live set, Jersey kicks clash against doom-laden atmospherics, soaring string sections, and detuned riffs.\\n\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/lolk.unofficial/\\nhttps://lolk.bandcamp.com/\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/lol-k-present-languid-haunt-the-trees/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":857,\"name\":\"Valeria Pacific solo showcase: A Door to Experimentation\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-14T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-14T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d22546cd9056b714aaf4dd912a246f0b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for Valeria Pacific’s Residency Showcase, marking the culmination of her journey as the first artist in Studio 12’s Residency Programme: A Door to Experimentation.\\n\\nAfter two weeks of research, experimentation and creative development, Valeria will present her first solo live performance, offering an insight into the ideas, sounds and discoveries that have emerged throughout her residency.\\n\\nAbout Valeria: Valeria Pacific is a drummer, DJ, community organiser and cultural producer. She is the director and lead drummer of Akolá Tambo, and co-founder and director of Bullerengue Circle. Her work has played a key role in giving visibility to bullerengue in the UK and Europe.\\n_____\\nDiscover the exciting programme we've curated throughout the residency, featuring workshops, performances and opportunities to engage with the artists as they develop new work.\\nA Door to Experimentation brings together three emerging artists who are expanding their practice from traditional folk music into experimental, collaborative and cross-disciplinary music-making. Throughout the residency, they are mentored by Patricia Doors, exploring new approaches to sound, performance and creative exchange.\\n\\nThis residency has been made possible with the generous support of Arts Council England, CASA, Movimientos, and the Anglo Chilean Society. \\n\\nProgramme Development \\u0026 Partnership: Nora Laraki\\n\\n\\n____________\\n\\n\\nMuestra de Residencia de Valeria Pacific\\n\\nAcompáñanos en la Muestra de Residencia de Valeria Pacific, que marca la culminación de su recorrido como la primera artista del programa de residencias de Studio 12: A Door to Experimentation.\\n\\nTras dos semanas de investigación, experimentación y desarrollo creativo, Valeria presentará su primer concierto en solitario, compartiendo con el público una mirada a las ideas, sonidos y descubrimientos que han surgido a lo largo de su residencia.\\nSobre Valeria\\n\\nValeria Pacific es baterista, DJ, organizadora comunitaria y productora cultural. Es directora y baterista principal de Akolá Tambo, y cofundadora y directora de Bullerengue Circle. A través de su trabajo, ha desempeñado un papel fundamental en la difusión y visibilización del bullerengue en el Reino Unido y Europa.\\n\\nDescubre el emocionante programa que hemos creado a lo largo de la residencia, con talleres, presentaciones y oportunidades para conectar con los artistas mientras desarrollan y experimentan con nuevas obras.\\n\\nA Door to Experimentation reúne a tres artistas emergentes que están expandiendo sus prácticas más allá de la música folclórica tradicional hacia formas de creación musical experimentales, colaborativas e interdisciplinarias. A lo largo de la residencia, los artistas cuentan con la mentoría de Patricia Doors, explorando nuevos enfoques del sonido, la interpretación y el intercambio creativo.\\n\\nEsta residencia ha sido posible gracias al generoso apoyo de Arts Council England, CASA, Movimientos y la Anglo Chilean Society.\\n\\nDesarrollo del programa y alianzas: Nora Laraki\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":479,\"name\":\"Iona Zajac / Dorothy / Marsy\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-14T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-14T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3f06ff1165f57fda7325ed63cf55f623.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House presents Iona Zajac, Dorothy and Marsy, a week before they all head to the Welsh valleys to perform at Green Man Festival 2026.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":612,\"name\":\"Kinesis x Earth Frequency Soundsystem\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-14T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-15T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a9b7fa447efa18cce58c1c0d667fef04.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Two stalwarts of the underground scene come together for a collaborative journey from all ends of UK bass and free party culture.\\n\\nPowered by the weighty Earth Frequency Soundsystem and covering styles across dubstep, footwork, jungle, tekno, and hardcore by both DJs and live acts, you'll be sure to be moving in all directions in a flurry of body popping ankle flicking head banging fist pumping skanking.\\n\\nAll things point to Distillery N17, hidden in an industrial estate with room to experiment with a showcase of lights, fabric and installations by our resident team and selected artists.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n++++++++++\\n\\nWe have a limited number of free tickets for those who can't afford one. DM @kinesis_ldn on IG or email kinesis.ldn@gmail.com if you need one, no questions asked :)\\n\\nKinesis and Earth Frequency Soundsystem are queer-friendly spaces for everyone to have fun and feel free - we have a zero tolerance to transphobia, racism, homophobia, sexism, ableism, harassment, violence and oppression of any form.\\n\\n£20 OTD\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":628,\"name\":\"fête accomplie presents: Sub Basics\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-14T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-15T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"36b8c69c5c7293465328a7b612684e03.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Fête Accomplie welcomes: Sub Basics, 14th August 2026. \\n\\nWe welcome you to an intimate session of hypnotic dub techno at The Grey Hound, with producer and DJ, Sub Basics. Support will be provided by Fête Accomplie residents. Founder of Temple of Sound and Maneuver, Sub Basics has become one of the defining voices in contemporary dub techno and UK bass music. His productions blend cavernous sub-bass, intricate percussion and spacious dub textures, drawing from soundsystem culture while pushing into techno, garage and broken-beat territories. With releases on his own imprints alongside labels such as Tar Hallow and ATW Records, and support from artists including Ben UFO, Laurent Garnier and Lena Willikens, his music has become a fixture in clubs, festivals and discerning record bags worldwide. \\n\\nTo warm up the room, FA. residents will continue to explore their beloved deep, dub infused techno with a focus on club intensity. \\n\\nFête Accomplie exists to create spaces of freedom, expression and connection through dance music. We operate a zero-tolerance policy towards harassment or discrimination of any kind, and any issues brought to our attention will be dealt with immediately.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2467231\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":866,\"name\":\"Collective Hysteria w/ RBI (live), ÇINTH, Jezebelle \\u0026 Lovelace\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-14T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-15T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2f8e6556ea981d5a2673084201fda385.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Miss us? We missed you! So we’re coming back to our London roots for summer. We’ve been inspired by our travels through the queer and psychedelic scenes in Europe and beyond, and dreaming about our community here at the intersection of these worlds.\\n\\nJoin us for a night of music from some of our favourite FLINTA* artists in London right now, a trip through deep and psychedelic sounds, channeling the wild energy of surreal natural landscapes into the heart of the city. These sonic delights will be accompanied by immersive visuals from an artist we are looking forward to working with for the first time.\\n\\nMUSIC\\n\\nÇINTH\\nRBI (live)\\nLovelace\\nJezebelle\\n\\nVISUALS\\nPorsha\\n\\nWe’re so excited to be hosting this event at Ormside Projects, an intimate community space with a great sound system. We want to make the space as accessible as possible, so please do get in touch if you have any questions or access requests.\\n\\nWe really want to emphasise that this is a queer space, created for those who identify as FLINTA* (femme, lesbian, intersex, nonbinary, transgender, agender) to dance, connect and express themselves freely. For this reason, we will be launching a FLINTA* ticket, to reduce additional barriers to entry often faced by gender minorities. If you do not identify as FLINTA* and are unable to afford the general release ticket, do drop us a message and we can help.\\n\\nSee you there x\\n\\n[Devon Armstrong is supported by the Early Career Promoter Fund which\\nis managed by PRS Foundation and funded by Arts Council England using Supporting\\nGrassroots Music funding from DCMS.]\\n\\nArtwork by Robin Timmis\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2462559\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":776,\"name\":\"West London Dub Club - Ital Power meets Entebbe\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-15T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8b92cd2e3e35fdf74c26cddadb2c9933.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"West London Dub Club presents Chapter VI:\\nITAL POWER meets ENTEBBE\\nALL TRIBES WELCOME!\\n5PM-12AM\\nSaturday 15th August 2026\\n\\nThe Dominion Centre\\n112 The Green, Southall UB2 4BQ\\n\\nFood - Music - Merchandise\\n\\nItal Power Sound System\\n-Outta West London\\n-M.Ital, Ital Shash, Benji Roots \\u0026 full crew\\n\\nEntebbe Sound System\\n-Outta North London\\n-Rasta Chanters\\n-Ras P, Gad Man \\u0026 Full Crew\\n\\nBoth playing on their own full sound systems\\nStrictly heavyweight business till done!\\n\\nInstagram \\u0026 Facebook - @WestLondonDubClub\\n\\nTravel\\nTube\\nSouthall (Elizabeth Line) 6 Min Walk\\n\\nCar\\nLarge car park next to venue\\n\\nTickets\\nAdvanced starting from £10 + booking fees\\nM.O.T.D (More On The Door)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2492231\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":780,\"name\":\"Impulse Control: Lebanon Fundraiser\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-16T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"13833f9bddf7c52ca47fd4d9097189fe.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Across two rooms, we're bringing together Lebanese artists alongside friends and supporters from London's underground music scene for a full programme of live performances and DJ sets spanning noise, industrial, experimental electronics, breaks, hardcore, techno, and beyond.\\n\\n100% of proceeds will go towards humanitarian relief efforts in Lebanon.\\n\\nEntry is by donation at the door. We suggest a donation of £10-£15, but please give whatever you can - every contribution makes a difference.\\n\\nFree tickets are available to help us estimate attendance, but are not required. Walk-ins are welcome throughout the day and night, subject to venue capacity. Please note that holding a free ticket does not guarantee entry if the venue is full.\\n\\nARDENT PAIN (live)\\n\\nPainful harsh noise.\\n\\nAVEL MISMO (live)\\n\\nAbstract electronics rooted in Lebanon.\\n\\nAVENTEX\\n\\nDeep, dark beats.\\n\\nBAYTEE BAYTAK\\n\\nBeirut rhythms meet UK bass and breaks.\\n\\nCHORONZON\\n\\nIndustrial excursions and razor-sharp sounds from across the globe.\\n\\nCOCKTAIL PARTY EFFECT\\n\\nBass-heavy mutations and leftfield club sounds.\\n\\niAMA B2B NEW FLESH\\n\\nMulti-genre resident DJs.\\n\\nMAXQUERADE\\n\\nBass-heavy bleeps and broken rhythms.\\n\\nMHAMAD SAFA\\n\\nExperimental electronics from Lebanon driven by intricate percussion.\\n\\nNAKEDAGGRESSIONDJ\\n\\nIndustrial techno at the edge of noise.\\n\\nNK47\\n\\nGenre-defiant club bangers from the Global South.\\n\\nPOWER FAILURE (live)\\n\\nRelentless hardcore with big breakdowns.\\n\\nSLYN (live)\\n\\nSound art via marine biology.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2485829\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":571,\"name\":\"Bengal to Bethnal Green\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-15T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ae76a7edc8a4078758f8f378241f060f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for a vibrant evening celebrating Bangladeshi heritage with:\\nHomemade food from 6pm from Oitij-jo Kitchen, a women-led project rooted in East London\\nPerformance 7pm - 9pm by global musicians from Grand Union Orchestra with post-concert Q\\u0026A \\n\\nDirected by renowned tabla master Yousuf Ali Khan, the performance blends traditional ragas, timeless classics, and fresh arrangements uniting top Bengali artists with global talent from East London’s celebrated Grand Union Orchestra.\\n\\nPraised by audiences as \\\"both resonant and sublime\\\" and \\\"truly amazing\\\".\\n\\nWe’re proud to be part of Backyard Biennial: East, a free, 8-week festival in collaboration with Whitechapel Gallery and 40+ local partners across East London (15 July - 6 September 2026), celebrating the histories, communities and creative practices that shape the East End.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":697,\"name\":\"Barzakh برزخ - Fundraiser for Lebanon\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-16T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"55694822047f5e2c94bfdd7c46a96aad.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Barzakh برزخ - Fundraiser for Lebanon: an evening of music and artist solidarity\\n\\nBarzakh is a café-library and cultural space in Hamra, one of Beirut's most loved neighbourhoods - and a place where many people displaced from southern Lebanon and Beirut's southern suburbs have recently taken refuge. \\n\\nWhen the war on Lebanon escalated at the end of September 2024, Barzakh transformed into a community kitchen, and its work remains as vital as ever amid the ongoing Israeli bombardment and occupation. Barzakh's small team works around the clock to distribute around 2,000 hot meals a day to people who have fled their homes, alongside other urgent community needs like medicine and cash support. Running the kitchen costs up to $1,000 a day.\\n\\nJoin us on 15 August at Jam in a Jar, Harringay, for a summer evening of artistic and musical solidarity, raising money to help Barzakh continue this crucial work.\\n\\nExpect:\\n\\n--- Art workshop and games led by Bosla Arts, a platform sharing the work and stories of artists worldwide facing grave challenges to their artistic freedom of expression.\\n\\n--- Live music by Bassel Hariri, a Syrian violinist from Aleppo who has dedicated his music career to exploring different avenues of expressing the sound of the Arab violin.\\n\\n--- Lebanese songs by Sura, a singer-songwriter originally from Lebanon and now based in London, whose music is shaped by both places. After training in opera in Lebanon, she found herself returning to Arabic music after moving to the UK. Her songs draw on the sounds she grew up with, exploring love, nostalgia and belonging.\\n\\n--- DJ set by Riwa, a poet, theatre-maker, sound designer, and puppeteer working in both creative and backstage capacities. Her art puts people and our relationships at the centre of the political narratives we inhabit, with recent explorations including the unpacking of generational baggage and the politics of pop princesses.\\n\\n--- Music from around the world on cassette, chosen by Sha3by Chic of London DJ collective Koshari.\\n\\n--- More TBC!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":842,\"name\":\"The Video Catalogue: Making and Re-making in Palestine, 2018-2026\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-15T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3b89fda76af20c2c0d952aa52fcb65dc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An evening of short films followed by a projection of living archival materials with live musical accompaniment, all centred around the genocide in Gaza.\\n\\nAttendees:\\n\\nZoom: Mahdi Atiya Karira, Puppeteer and writer\\n\\nLacking professional training or a local puppetry tradition in the Gaza Strip, Ativa Karira honed his skills by learning from Palestinian artists in Jerusalem and West Bank cultural centers, as well as from experienced Egyptian puppeteers. He takes pride in having been the first to \\\"introduce the art of string puppetry to the Gaza Strip.\\\" He founded the Khuyut Theatre (\\\"Theatre of Strings\\\") in Gaza City, where—prior to the war—he trained around fifteen young people, including twelve women, in the construction and manipulation of string puppets. The troupe created nearly eighty puppets and performed plays written by Mahdi, primarily for young audiences. In addition to his small home workshop, Mahdi worked in a larger space at Holst Park in Gaza City, a site dedicated to children's education and recreation. In early 2019, Khuyut Theatre garnered international media attention for its ingenuity in repurposing materials despite the blockade—such as extracting pigments from fishing gear to create paints. Over the past two years, his home, scripts, most of his puppets, his sets, and his workshop have been destroyed during repeated bombardments of Gaza.\\n\\nIn-person: Henry Plavidal, producer and editor.\\n\\nPlavidal’s work focuses on social issues, art, and conflict. He has worked in the field of socially engaged and journalistic cinema in numerous countries, addressing diverse subjects and causes, notably in Palestine. As part of a documentary filmmaking team, he has received awards from ARTE and Al Jazeera.\\n\\nThis screening is hosted by The Video Catalogue: an occasional screening series that seeks to bring together archival materials and surprising cinema. @thevideocatalogue\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":815,\"name\":\"Shedding Histories x Private Funktion: Nadia Ksaiba, Bena b2b Chameleonas \\u0026 Eman Pav\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T22:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-16T03:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c99c799b4d11f43503ca23f3ef179a22.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A dynamic rare groove party for those who love to dance. Shedding Histories combines forces with Private Funktion to bring you an intimate dusk till dawn party held at EartH Hackney in London.\\n\\nWe'll be joined by Nadia Ksaiba as well as sets from the Shedding Histories duo Bena \\u0026 Chameleonas alongside side Eman Pav of Private Funktion.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2484090\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":860,\"name\":\"ORMSIDE presents: Nkisi\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-16T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"66198cb4e190992231b108ac9578b539.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On Saturday 15th August, Ormside welcomes back a true pillar of our sonic identity. Nkisi returns for a defining, all-night-long session after nearly a decade of shared history within the space.\\n\\nInviting us into her expansive ethnographic research practice and distinctive sound world, she offers total immersion via rhythmic cycles and ceremonial sonics. Across the night, she will guide the room through five distinct chapters – a deliberate, unfolding procession exploring temporality, repetition, and trance-states\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2492439\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":800,\"name\":\"Body Hammer\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-15T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-16T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4c964c3aafaa003796e8619a07814f0d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dress to sweat\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2460814\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":165,\"name\":\"Zu\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-18T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-18T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"228a2b635d9a2d439c1d5da20ca39b90.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nZu\\nAn Italian jazz-punk-noise explosion, and you can dance to it. Shook the building to it's core last summer and back to do it all again, armed with a new album. \\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£17\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/zu-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":886,\"name\":\"LITF Presents: STRANGE(R) PAGES\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-18T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-18T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"91313ab96a3a422e1aa77003daf57523.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Lost in the Foxglove: Regular Poetry Club would love to welcome you to a brand new series fixture at Rhizomatic!. This time you're invited to STRANGE(R) PAGES. A combination poetry workshop, open mic event where guests are equipped with the tools to begin a brand new poem, and perform on the mic on the same night. Though, the twist is you won't be reading your own work aloud. \\n\\nThis event is perfect for anyone whose been wanting to work up the courage to perform, but has been too nervous to take the leap. You might be wondering what I could possibly mean by this… Seems like you'll just have to come and find out. Think queer, community, low-pressure, creativity, and play. \\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/37162/litf-presents-stranger-pages\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":887,\"name\":\"‘Flamboyance’ with Jack Parlett in conversation with Peter Scalpello\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-18T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-18T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"99cd1b97b12c6ed4e81c9a3dce715f4b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"JACK PARLETT AND CELEBRATED POET PETER SCALPELLO DISCUSS ‘FLAMBOYANCE’ AND HOW IT IGNITES EVERY ASPECT OF OUR LIVES, FROM ART AND ENTERTAINMENT TO RITUAL AND PROTEST.\\nFlamboyance is Jack Parlett’s follow up to his acclaimed Fire Island (A Housmans bestseller of 2022). This new book has all the qualities one has come to expect of Jack’s work; big hearted and erudite in equal measure.\\n\\nFlamboyance ignites every aspect of our lives, from art and entertainment to ritual and protest. The word conjures exuberance and unashamed passion; in thought, expression and dress. Yet historically the term ‘flamboyant’ has been reserved for the over-the-top and the outré, invoked at times as a pejorative innuendo or worse.\\n\\nIn his fascinating new book, Jack Parlett argues for its value as an empowering and creative force, illuminating the ways in which flamboyance is a fundamental aspect of human conduct that both marks and transcends difference.\\n\\nTaking in an eclectic array of examples, from Gothic architecture to the orange flowers of Dungeness, and populated by figures such as Oscar Wilde, James Baldwin, Elton John, Amy Winehouse, Lil Nas X and Chappell Roan, this is a book about flamboyant art and the art of flamboyance. And having both aspired to it and rejected it, Jack recounts his personal relationship to flamboyance while also finding new meanings of the word, exploring its surprises and contradictions, and reconnecting with its radical power.\\n\\nOUR SPEAKERS:\\n\\nJack Parlett is the author of three books: The Poetics of Cruising: Queer Visual Culture from Whitman to Grindr (a monograph with University of Minnesota Press), Same Blue, Different You (a poetry pamphlet with Broken Sleep Books), and Fire Island: A Queer History (Granta), which was named one of the Best Books of 2022 by the New Yorker and shortlisted for the Polari Book Prize 2023. His writing has appeared in the New Yorker, Document Journal, BBC Culture, Boston Review, Literary Hub and Poetry London.\\n\\nPeter Scalpello is a writer and psychotherapist from Glasgow, based in London. Their second book, Mirrorstage, was published this year with Cipher Press.\\n\\nAs always, tickets are priced on a sliding scale. If you are unable to pay for a ticket please do not hesitate to contact us at shop@housmans.com, and a free ticket will be made available.\\n\\nIf you choose ‘book + entry’ your copies of the book will be available to collect on the evening. If you would like to collect it earlier, or arrange for delivery, please contact us (postage is £2.95). Telephone 020 7837 4473 or email shop@housmans.com.\\n\\nDoors Open at 6:45pm, Event Starts 7:00.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/book-launch-flamboyance-with-jack-parlett/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":888,\"name\":\"HOUSMANS READING SERIES: Robert Glück\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-19T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-19T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a2ec0f59913a5b1ce4cfeb0f3f62e732.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Housmans are beyond honoured, and slightly delightedly flabbergasted, to welcome the legendary writer Robert Glück to the shop for a reading. Robert, or Bob, is one of the most important writers working in the world today, in a career that spans many decades, poetry and cutting edge fiction; his work has been of profound importance to the contemporary queer literary landscape.\\n\\nReading alongside Bob we’ve some of the most exciting younger writers working in London today: Oisín Roberts, JD Howse and Luke Roberts.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://housmans.com/event/housmans-reading-series-robert-gluck/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":832,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction Presents: Tasska, Psychoma, Speed Trials\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-19T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5c99c1683354923e5afca9f20c8709e6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Tasska - Targeting the social fractures emerging from a country on the brink, Tasska are a band emboldened by vulnerability and honesty. Drawing from the lyrical wryness of artists like Orange Juice and Jonathan Richman, and the bite of bands like Cola and Television, Tasska have forged the gut-punch and grace of their live performance in front of hometown Brighton audience. They're on the up, and not to be missed...\\n\\nPsychoma - A singular, unified vision: to resurrect the raw power of the grunge era and inject it with the modern intensity of hardcore and shoegaze. They aren't just playing alt-rock; they are building a wall of sound designed to envelop, disorient, and completely captivate the London underground.\\n\\nSpeed Trials - Speed Trials is a London based groovy grunge band. Within every dark cloud is a silver lining - they have arrived to part them all.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":669,\"name\":\"Zahn / Black Shape / Jawharp / Kunubu | Real Life Presents - New Cross Noise\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-20T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7fd496d68554b83c37b2728b83958c8c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nZAHN\\nNoise rock experiments from members of Eisturzende Neubauten, The Ocean and more...\\n\\n+ Support from\\nBlack Shape\\nNasty sludge grooves\\n\\nJawharp\\nHorrible Skronk madness\\n\\nKunubu\\nEvil space doom\\n\\nThursday 20th August\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£14\\nDoors 6pm\\n\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/zahn\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":732,\"name\":\"SCOBE 6: BJ Holy / leisure fm / flywheel / scobe collective\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"535f0f1d7760d7c8036b00ea1ceef28c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"the sixth scobe night - playful and friendly experimental music for freaks and sweethearts \\u003c3\\n\\nthis time with a dream lineup:\\n\\n***\\n\\nBJ Holy:\\n\\nBJ Holy plays flugelhorn and makes music and videos about city life, desire \\u0026 things in between\\n\\n***\\n\\nLeisure FM:\\n\\nleisure fm, a london-based polish twin duo, work with stretched-out beats and basslines, manipulated field recordings and distorted vocals to create murky soundscapes to dissociate to, moving through repetition, rumination, electroclash and broken dance music\\n(¬`‸´¬)♩𖦹 “moody in the club”\\n\\n꩜⋆.°⭑\\n\\nalso co-runners of Polish collective ‘złom’\\n\\n***\\n\\nFlywheel:\\n\\nUK artist flywheel is a musician and producer based in London who has released music with labels including YUKU, Accidental JNR label and Gimme A Break Records. His productions span leftfield techno, ambient and percussive club music. flywheel’s live show is a mess of extension leads and aggro drum machines. His latest EP, ‘Harbinger’ [YUKU] sees flywheel prioritise club-focused sound design, momentum and rhythmic interplay.\\n\\n***\\n\\nscobe collective:\\n\\nscobe resident earnest emo experimental music.\\n\\n\\n7pm onwards\\nno one turned away for lack of funds\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2486580\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":845,\"name\":\"FOOL Collective - First Showcase\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d1651cecf95a4cc00fe40740a9de5771.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"What is FOOL?: It started with song shares. Some of us had done School of Song workshops with Brian Eno, AG Cook, Oneohtrix Point Never and Arca, some did one, some did several, but we all ended up in the same room in London afterwards, talking.\\n\\nSome of us have years of experience. Some have never played a show. Some stepped back from the scene out of disillusionment, others are still finding their footing. And we decided to start something, not to fix a big problem, but to add to what others are already building. We need more.\\n\\nFOOL is founded on that premise. Our aim is to go for showcases where the stage is open to those in the collective, wherever we might be in the journey, not just where we’ve already arrived.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":705,\"name\":\"eyes down looking // BINGO @ THE IVY HOUSE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e2a80beb79e1eb67665c9aa3e82acaf6.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Feeling lucky? Eyes down looking ... \\n\\nThe Ivy House gives Blackpool a run for it's money for one night only. Two little ducks, all the fives, it's all to play for. \\n\\nThe night will comprise of 3x games of Bingo, with dazzling prizes to be won, and a bit of a knees up afterwards to dance off all the tension.\\n\\nDobbers and tickets will be provided on the door. \\n\\nTickets £7 / £5 unwaged. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":841,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction Presents: Highstone, Crimson Flame, Faestomp\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-20T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fcac7d2cbd05bd88705a8b206604e3e9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Highstone: Highstone are an exciting new band on the London gig circuit. The four-piece draws inspiration from the greats of the ’90s alternative scene - Jeff Buckley, Radiohead, and Nirvana - while also channeling the expansive influence of Pink Floyd and Led Zeppelin. The result is a refreshing, powerful, and almost cinematic sound, brought fully to life through their electrifying live performances.\\n\\nCrimson Flame: Crimson Flame are set to make headlines with their powerhouse singer and rhythm guitarist Chantelle Kimberley and driven by the gritty lead of guitarist Finley White, this duo is making waves in the blues rock scene, tearing up the rules and creating a new era of arena ready blues rock.\\n\\nFaestomp: Faestomp is an East-london singer, songwriter and producer making mellow shuffly rhythms with a stock/MIDI style sound, anchored in pop music.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":759,\"name\":\"VENT ⓥ DJ Spanish Fly, James Massiah, Nihal\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-20T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-20T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b5c62b1f91cc42f0b6d5ee24f8805dc4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"DJ Spanish Fly is universally known as the \\\"Godfather of Memphis rap.\\\" Originating in the South Memphis area, he pioneered the city's signature hip-hop sound by blending 808 drum machines, hypnotic baselines, and dark, lo-fi distortion, laying the early groundwork for modern trap and phonk.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2469486\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":844,\"name\":\"Form Affinity | Gil Shani Trio\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-21T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"09a0dd499e912f4a78ec81028d9afb9a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":648,\"name\":\"Repetitive Strain: Xanax + The Gall\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T01:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e4503bdf2f26f46436df72f7ac627072.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"REPETITIVE STRAIN EVENT:\\n\\nXANAX (LIVE – Penryn, Cornwall)\\n\\nLet's celebrate and vapourise: shredded electronic body music delivered in the most live and lithe sense, from minds behind GAMMA (Gob Nation) and FREAK GENES. \\n\\nTHE GALL (LIVE – Glasgow, Scotland)\\n\\nDeadly duo making London debut, pure rectangle music: metallic synth punk facilitated by new label SHUNNING GROUND. Members have been responsible for a huge amount of Scotland's finest digital detritus and wayward noise walls of the last decade including Unmaking, Time Binding Ensemble, Anxiety and Helena Celle's Mimetic Desire.\\n\\n+\\nREPETITIVE STRAIN DJs (Voices Radio)\\nThe most (un)wanted music, from MOTLASH \\u0026 VANITY CRYSTAL.\\n\\nat\\nSpanners, Brixton\\n20:00-01:00, 21.08.2026\\n£10.00, no-one turned away\\n18+, flat access, top bar\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":894,\"name\":\"Whole Danth Catalogue UK Edition\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"020a22a51c6fed82e245eb20051f9aa8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"WHOLE DANTH CATALOGUE UK edition\\n~ Access to Contemporary Bass Music ~\\n\\nDoor £15\\n\\nActs:\\nOssia Live Set (Young Echo)\\nYOKEL (Plaque)\\nStranger\\nWoofoot (HHBush)\\nMore TBA\\n\\u0026 Secret Guest\\nSupported by:\\nHood by Foot\\n\\nA party rooted in leftfield bass music, drawing from the spirit of hip-hop and the attitude of punk.\\n\\nIn recent years, it has been influenced by Bristol’s culture and the wider European underground scene, exploring the intersection of dance music’s functionality and experimentation, where spatial abstraction meets physical groove.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2512304\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":802,\"name\":\"family affair volume X: a party for palestine\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-21T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"16ba86df652afd594b45d84a1db8d0b5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Our last dance…. for now.\\n\\nFor our tenth edition, we’re welcoming two amazing artists to play for us, for the cause, for the very first time.\\n\\nAfter our sold out Palestine fundraiser party back in February, we return to the place where it all started for us: the small, sweaty loud basement of The Glove That Fits: a fitting place to hold the finale to our first run of parties.\\n\\nTickets have just gone live on RA - 100% of profits will be going to MSF UK as ever, raising urgent funds for medical aid in Gaza and beyond.\\n\\nTen parties in and over £10k raised - we’re going to take some time to take it all in, and go again on the other side.\\n\\nWe hope to see you there in a few weeks.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2493281\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":833,\"name\":\"The Hot Snakes Night Club\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-13T16:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a384f9caaf459ae6f43b068640e6546d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Hot Snakes Night Club is an immersive installation and  performance space by artist Chloe Langlois. Co-curated by TACO!  and Dinosaur Kilby, the club hosts a diverse programme of cabaret, live artist performance, workshops,  and experimental music from invited artists and guests.\\n\\nFor the duration of 4 weeks TACO! will be transformed into a multidisciplinary nightclub, complete with an artist-themed cocktail bar and an accompanying programme of cabaret, live performance and music. \\n\\nThe club launches on 22nd August with the event 24hr Gnosis - a 24 hr occult marathon of artist performances live-streamed on TACO!’s website and IRL in the gallery.     Artist contributors to the Hotsnakes Night Club include Chloe Langlois, Dinosaur Kilby, Kate Mahony, John Anthony Thadicaran,  Arianne Churchman,  Wayne Burrows, Qingqing Liu, Sister Punch, Friederike Steinert, OILS,  Frankie Roberts, Harun Morrison, Gusty Ferro, The Hundred CLub, Ugly Drugless,  Intimacy, The Electronic Audio Club, Mind Your Head Carbet, The Empty Void Orchestra, National Rails, Catherine Carter, R3YWYA, Kicho, Flying Carpets, Letti O’Burn \\u0026 Sunnyboy Tyson, Maryam Sandjari Hashemi, The Pipe Shoppe (Wojciech Rusin), Peter Groom, Sarah Doyle, Sparkes Thompson, The Receipt, and more….\\n\\nTACO!\\n2 Cygnet Square\\nLondon\\nSE2 9FA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":834,\"name\":\"The Hot Snakes Night Club Presents: 24 hr Gnosis \",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T10:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"00b52ea97278b9c847043c17dd5bca53.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\\"To inaugurate the Hotsnakes Night Club, please join us for 24hr Gnosis -  24hr’s of artist performances and live stream occult sleepover. Every hour for a whole day, Chloe Langlois has invited multiple artists to conjure and perform. Over the duration of 24hr hours, audiences can attend as a live studio audience, witnessing a range of participatory and passive performances. Access is free with a paid bar serving food and artist cocktails. \\n\\nAudiences wishing to take part in the gallery sleepover from  11pm til 9am can do so by booking. Places are limited. Please see the end of this web page for full details on how to take part in the sleepover.\\n\\n24hr Gnosis will be live-streamed on TACO!’s and the rtm websites.\\n\\nArtists participating in 24hr Gnosis include Chloe Langlois, John Anthony Thadicaran, Harun Morrison, Arianne Churchman, Kate Mahony, Wayne Burrows, Dinosaur Kilby, Qingqing Liu, Sister Punch, Friederike Steinert, OILS, Frankie Roberts, Dinosaur Kilby, Pil \\u0026 Galia Kollectiv, The Hundred Club,  and magical instruments from The Pipe Shoppe.\\\"\\n\\nTACO!\\n2 Cygnet Square\\nLondon\\nSE2 9FA\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":880,\"name\":\"BOHOMO PLACE - A Queer Community Day in Hackney Central\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"a426bf6003899bdcbdc804c0c403eedb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hate gentrification, expensive hipster cafes, and big corporates and chains? Love Hackney, local venues and you’re a raging homo (or dyke/trans/non-binary/queer…)? \\n\\nThen BOHOMO PLACE is for you! \\n\\nOn Saturday 22 August, we’re taking over Bohemia Place in Hackney Central to offer an LGBTQIA+ Community Day alongside our friends Queertopia and Paper Dress Vintage.\\n\\nFrom 1pm till 3am! \\nAll the activities are FREE!\\nBar open from 1pm. Come have a drink! \\nThis event is part of our SOFT launch series, whilst we raise the funds that’ll allow us to be completely functional for our BIG OPENING (coming soon!). Check out our crowdfunder HERE.\\n\\nAnother way to support us is to just come down and have a drink (or several!) at the Joiners Heart from 1pm. \\n \\n\\nSCHEDULE:\\n\\nThe Joiners Heart (18, Bohemia Place)\\n\\n1-5pm: queer market + badge making workshop with Queertopia\\n\\n6-7.30pm: Drag King makeup workshop by Richard Energy  \\n\\n7.30-9pm: Think pub vibes, mingling \\u0026 chilling\\n\\n9-10pm: pop-up performances by Prinx Silver \\u0026 CYRO\\n\\n10pm-00.30am: DJ set by Trojan-Tyne (expect lots of gay bangers!)\\n\\n \\n\\nCheck out our A JOINERS HISTORY photo exhibition at the venue! Celebrating and remembering the legacy of the old Joiners Arms.\\n\\nAll our activities are free- please reserve your free ticket below so we know how many people to expect.\\n\\n \\n\\nPaper Dress Vintage (352a Mare Street)\\n\\n2-8pm: all dayer in back garden, by Queer Open Decks Collective (Expect from funk to disco, soul, hip hop, and house),\\n\\n10.30pm-3am: Disco Dyke Club Night\\n\\n \\n\\nACCESSIBILITY:\\n\\nThe Joiners Heart is step-free and wheelchair accessible via a ramp. \\n\\nWe have a wheelchair accessible toilet and two ambulant toilets. All toilets are all genders.\\n\\nWe have an accessible bar to order from.\\n\\nIf you have any questions or access needs, please send us a message through here or email: friendsjoinersarms@gmail.com\\n\\n \\n\\nTRANSPORT:\\n\\nYou can get here by Bus:\\n\\nHackney Central Station (Stop H, K, J): routes 253, 254, 106, 236, 394, N253.\\nMare Street (Stop T, E, F): routes 30, 38, 48, 55, 106, 236, 242, 253, 254, 276, 394, D6, N38, N55.\\nAmhurst Road (Stop L, R): routes 30, 56, 236, 253, 276\\n\\n\\nor by Overground:\\n\\nHackney Central, Mildmay Line, 5mins walk;\\nHackney Downs, Weaver Line, 10 mins walk\\nIt may be possible to park on Bohemia Place outside our unit, with some spaces available after 4.30pm.\\n\\n \\n\\nThis event is supported with funding from Hackney Council.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38461/bohomo-place-a-queer-community-day-in-hackney-central\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":884,\"name\":\"Handsworth Songs\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T14:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"beef0def17786822e926dba2565f52fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An experimental documentary depicting protests around the UK, positioning the camera with the protesters rather than pointed at them.\\n\\n\\nHandsworth Songs (1986, 61 mins) is an experimental documentary depicting the lives of those in Handsworth, Brixton, and Tottenham during three different people’s uprisings in 1985, positioning the camera with the protesters rather than pointed at them.\\n\\nProduced by Black Audio Film Collective, Handsworth Songs interrogates the impact of colonialism and what it means to be Black-British at a time when these two terms were, and still are, at odds with each other.\\n\\nWhilst made for the television screen, Handsworth Songs has gone on to be screened in museums and art houses around the world. Following this screening we will hold a community conversation to mark the 15 year anniversary of Mark Duggan's death which caused uprisings across London and spread to other parts of England. We aim to consider how the riots of 1985 and 2011 are similar and different, understanding how they changed the course of history and also the way in which we, as an organisation in Haringey, interact with the history of the borough.\\n\\n\\n\\nThis is the third and final screening of HCC's Summer Programme: Making the Revolution Irresistible\\n\\nAbout the film \\u0026 filmmakers\\nTrailer\\n\\n\\nAWARDS:\\n\\nBritish Film Institute Grierson Award for Best Documentary in 1986.\\n\\nJOHN AKOMFRAH: Director\\n\\nFounder of Black Audio Film Collective, Akomfrah is a filmmaker who experiments with textures and sounds to create a landscape which explores the many outcomes of colonialism and immigration. Beginning with a career in television, via Chanel 4’s Workshop schemes, Akomfrah has more recently gone on to create installation pieces for art centres and museums internationally.\\n\\nOther works include:\\n\\nSeven Songs for Malcom X (1993)\\n\\nThe Stuart Hall Project (2013)\\n\\nThe Last Angel of History (1996)\\n\\n\\n\\nAbout our Guest Speaker\\n\\n\\nGuest Speaker: TBC\\n\\nBooking / Waiting List / Cancellation\\n\\n\\nPlease only book if you are confident you will be able to attend, as seating at this venue is limited. Due to safety regulations, walk-in entry cannot be guaranteed.\\n\\nThe registration form includes a small number of questions collected for reporting purposes. All data will be anonymised. Each attendee is required to complete the form. If you are booking on behalf of someone else and do not know an answer, please enter or select' N/A' where applicable.\\n\\nDue to the venue’s limited capacity, the event may sell out.If this happens, you can be added to the waiting list. When a ticket becomes available, you will receive an email to book it, and you will have 24 hours to complete your booking.\\n\\nIf you are unable to attend the event, please cancel your ticket(s) so that your place can be offered to someone else.\\n\\nWhy your donations are important?\\n\\nPlease read carefully! We’re introducing a Community Pricing to help cover the costs of our events. Choose the ticket tier that best reflects your current circumstances— considering income, housing, caring responsibilities, health, and day-to-day financial pressures. We trust you to choose what feels right. More on this system here.\\n\\nHCC is run by volunteers and does not receive any funding at the moment. Every donation you make will help us to support local venues and to organise other free screenings.\\n\\nIn a time of rising living costs and persistent barriers for marginalised communities in producing and accessing films that reflect their experiences and aspirations, we are committed to making our screenings free or pay-what-you-can.\\n\\nAbout the venue\\n\\nLordship Hub is a vibrant community centre and café at the heart of Lordship Rec, Tottenham’s largest park. The building is fully accessible, but located inside the park. If you need to be dropped off next to the building's main entrance (with the ramp), please contact us early so we can arrange the park's gate to be open. If you have any accessibility needs or questions, please contact us at haringeycommunitycinema@gmail.com.\\n\\nAbout HCC\\n\\nHaringey Community Cinema (HCC) was launched in April 2025 and is run by volunteers. Inspired by Brixton Community Cinema, HCC is aimed at bringing residents of Haringey together through film. Our mission is to showcase films that challenge, inspire, and spark critical reflection—films that make us think and act. Visit our website.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCovid Policy\\n\\nHCC does not currently have an official COVID-19 policy. However, we remain mindful that many people are still vulnerable to the virus. We kindly ask attendees to take the following precautions to help keep our events safe and accessible for everyone:\\n\\nIf possible, please take a lateral flow test before attending.\\nIf you test positive or are experiencing any COVID-19 symptoms, please do not attend, even if you feel well.\\nWe welcome and encourage the use of masks inside the venue for those who wish to wear them.\\nPlease be considerate of others' comfort levels and respect requests for physical distance.\\nThank you for helping us create a safer and more inclusive space.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/handsworth-songs-registration-1995292310011\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":859,\"name\":\"ORMSIDE presents: DJ Marcelle (in Conversation \\u0026 Extended Set) with sinny \\u0026 Marylou\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"88aa80f506809834f61605f5e26e9a50.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"DJ Marcelle returns to Ormside on August 22nd. This time, marking her fourth annual visit to Ormside, we invite the notorious DJ and collector to join us for a live discussion in the space ahead of her extended club set. This offering presents the rare opportunity to hear Marcelle talk through her fascinating life and practice, guided by a handful of records from her colossal collection.\\n\\nFollowing the discussion, Marcelle’s customary 3 hour set is framed by sets from two masters of open-format selection: London-based Sinny and French-born Wheel of Fortune member Marylou.\\n\\nNow a household name in certain circles, DJ Marcelle’s work is evidence of a lifelong dedication to sonic detail. A champion of tracks that shouldn’t exist – hidden within the grooves of custom dubplates – her sets lead with curiosity, asserting a refreshing and open approach to dancefloor curation. As always, she must be seen to be believed.\\n\\nOn closing duties, Marylou returns to Ormside for the first time this year. A Morphine Records associate and member of b4b supergroup Wheel of Fortune (CCL, Nonogigsta, rRoxymore), her psychedelic and multi-faceted DJ sets have earned her position as a deeply respected DJ and organiser on the international stage.\\n\\nsinny opens the night, supporting DJ Marcelle for the 3rd time at Ormside since the yearly event first began. Weaving together strands of historically and personally resonant musics that trace and collapse timelines, sinny’s sets are tactile, thoughtful and narrative held together with textured and immersive sonics.\\n\\nLimited tickets available for pre-show talk (40)\\n\\nTalk - DJ Marcelle in Conversation 21:00 - 23:00\\n\\nClub - 23:00 - 05:00\\n\\nSupport from Carhartt WIP\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2480889\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":808,\"name\":\"Saltings EP launch\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-23T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T19:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f480b9cdc21af296c023a205cb35d99a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join London-based folk duo Saltings for an intimate concert to mark the launch of their debut EP.\\n\\nSupport from Pearl Fish\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":809,\"name\":\"Saltings EP launch gig\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-23T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-23T19:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"97e61a2c8364bd47dee950f45e6ce563.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join London-based folk duo Saltings for an intimate concert to mark the launch of their debut EP. \\n\\nSaltings blend delicate guitar and mandolin with rich harmonies reminiscent of Gillian Welch and Dave Rawlings. \\n\\nSupport from contemporary folk singer and multi-instrumentalist Pearl Fish, who is featured on the EP.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":693,\"name\":\"The Hotel presents... Agnese Toniutti plays the music of Philip Corner + Miles Lukoszevieze\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-24T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-24T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"5f411260e63d6d364aa2d421a0fa94ad.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In anticipation of the release of Philip Corner’s ‘Passage Through: A Ritual’ LP, The Hotel proudly  presents its first recital. \\n\\nThe Hotel invites Philip Corner’s pianist of choice, Agnese Toniutti, to Cafe OTO to perform a  concert of Corner’s works on the grand piano. \\n\\nAs prelude, The Hotel will host a premiere of Miles Lukoszevieze’s new piece ‘Self-Shadowing  Prey’ for live electronics and playback ensemble, inspired by the writings of Ghérasim Luca.\\n\\n\\n\\nPassage Through: A Ritual LP by Philip Corner is released 14th September, with advance copies available for sale at the event, alongside other titles from The Hotel.\\n\\nThis evening in The Hotel is curated by Philip Corner and Henry Cyer.\\n\\nMiles Lukoszevieze’s ‘Self-Shadowing Prey’ is commissioned by The Hotel, with the support of Hinrichsen Foundation.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/the-hotel-presents-august-2026/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":889,\"name\":\"Everybody to Kenmure Street - Community Screening with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-25T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-25T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"104a0792fcafc92cfc51e8b13d4dca64.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In May 2021, a UK Home Office dawn raid triggers one of the most spontaneous and successful acts of civil resistance in recent memory. In Pollokshields, Scotland’s most diverse neighbourhood, hundreds of residents rush to the streets to stop the deportation of their neighbours. In today’s increasingly far-right political environment of immigration raids, deportation flights and border violence, Everybody to Kenmure Street is an empowering reminder of the importance of collective action.\\n\\n \\n\\nThe screening will be followed by a casual chat with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids @slantiraids on the organising they do in the area, and how you can get involved.\\n\\n \\n\\nAll are welcome, no matter your organising experience! The film is rated 12A.\\n\\n \\n\\nPay What You Can tickets are available from £1-8. This event is part of a series of community screenings around London with local anti raids groups, organised by april forrest lin 林森. All ticket revenue will be donated to Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids after event costs have been covered.\\n\\n \\n\\n18:30 - Doors open\\n\\n19:00 - Film screening\\n\\n20:45 - Chat with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids\\n\\n21:00 - Chat ends, space stays open\\n\\n21:30 - Event ends\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38273/everybody-to-kenmure-street-community-screening-with-southwark-and-lambeth-anti-raids\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":863,\"name\":\"Phrasing: Poetry and DJs\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0f2d00c312f161c784832704aeb654c0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"a lab of sonic curation and lyrical assembly.\\n\\npoets and disc jockeys perform in acoustic verse and electronic mix, in tandem and apart, held together in vibrational frequency by rhythm, by pause. \\n\\nsilence. suspension. drop. \\n\\nthe floor is open for poets who would like to experiment as part of the open jam. sign up on the night.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":881,\"name\":\"On Their Hearts They Walked - Gazan Photopoetry Book Event\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-27T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-27T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0826c5a4f751808001cd0e9e92da7c20.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us for an event presenting the collaboration photo poetry book ‘On Their Hearts They Walked’ by Gazan poet Jehad Jarbou and Gazan photographer Moayed Abu Ammouna. \\n\\nThe event will feature a presentation of and reading from the book, as well as music by Sara Masry and Paul on oud, Bint Mbareh, and a DJ set by Adan. The books will be available to purchase, as well as clothes by Shereen Abdelkareem and Amal Al Nakhala and limited Maqam Books selections. Food and drinks by Tigs Table. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":829,\"name\":\"Dub Sound Systems, Dhikr on Loudspeakers and the Politics of Amplification\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-27T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-27T20:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e7183acd7486366af611f6c8d17559ef.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Part screening, part listening session, part conversation, Dub Sound Systems, Dhikr on Loudspeakers and the Politics of Amplification is curated by Sarah El Miniawy in response to Joe Namy’s Cosmic Breath. \\n\\nThis event brings together artist GAIKA and artist-filmmaker Mahdy Abu Bahat in a conversation moderated by El Miniawy to trace the affinities between Moulid and Carnival through shared practices of amplification and temporary congregation.  \\n\\nMoulid endures as a counter-hegemonic practice, where Sufi transcendence becomes durational gathering and spectacle, sustained by the physical force of amplified sound. In these moments, dhikr, the act of remembrance in Islam, is felt differently by reciters, listeners and the urban landscape itself. Likewise, in London’s Carnival dub sound systems create an alternate environment within the city that gathers bodies around bass and volume, taking up space and amplifying communities that refuse to be erased.  \\n\\nRather than looking for a common genealogy, El Miniawy, GAIKA, and Abu Bahat will explore parallels across geographies when those on the margins temporarily occupy the centre through sound. Amplification and its technologies emerge as both sonic and social practice—from loudspeaker dhikr to dub bass—and the sound system as a temporary architecture for gathering. \\n\\nDoors open at 5.30pm; event starts at 6pm and ends at 8pm. \\n\\nImage credit: still from عـذر الوزة (The Goose's Excuse), 2023. A film by Mahdy Abo Bahat and Abdo Zin Eldin.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ibraaz.org/whats-on/dub-sound-systems-dhikr-on-loudspeakers-and-the-politics-of-amplification\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":867,\"name\":\"Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. \\u0026 feeo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-27T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bb5623d6a6a9d23b79385cc4eb6cb434.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nPresenting a double bill of vanguard techno producer Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. and vocalist and producer feeo at Ormside on Thursday 27th August. Ahead of carnival weekend celebrations and commemorations, we welcome two artists whose practices channel experiences of blackness via the collapsing and re-contextualisation of diasporic music idioms.\\n\\nWelcoming Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. to Ormside for his first UK show in a decade. A 90s veteran of UK techno, Alfa embodies resilience, having overcome serious health issues and systemic obstacles over the past few years. In response, his newest work ‘Infinite Black Inside’ (FO) tenderly serves fractured pulses and bass-heavy experiments, drawing on a full spectrum of radical Black music and a lifetime of experience. Free Jazz meets footwork, techno and dub – filtered through Alfa’s own lens to form a sonic imprint entirely his own, imbued with hope.\\n\\nfeeo is the solo project of London-based artist and vocalist Theodora Laird. Working across electronics, written word and performance – feeo investigates the feedback and tension between personal and political story. In her 2025 debut album ‘Goodness’ (AD93), feeo explores opposing forces of darkness and lightness, delivered via static hum, tape drones and whispers of dance music forms. On the 27th feeo presents a new solo performance at Ormside – her first London show since headlining ICA in February of this year.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":876,\"name\":\"Pre-launch • Ambient Sauna | Introspective Electronics x o.rbyss w/ Avsluta \\u0026 Luvandula\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-28T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4d7ccfc85b3b27a9a2a958b27c0fc560.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pre-launch • Join us for the first weekend in our new venue, just two doors down from the original space you know and love! With the main launch party on Monday 31st, come down early for an exclusive preview and be the first to try out the new setup.\\n\\nIntrospective Electronics \\u0026 o.rbyss are our two longest-running monthly residencies, soundtracking Ambient Sauna since its very beginnings. For this special occasion, their founders, Avsluta and Luvandula, join forces for the first edition of the series in our new space, digging deep into their ambient and downtempo collections.\\n\\n*Book your 70-minute sauna session, arrive early and stay late for 4 hours of music in the lounge*\\n\\nABOUT AMBIENT SAUNA\\nOur silent Treehouse sauna and the chatty Herbal sauna are both equipped with a sound system for deep listening. Our Bunker sauna, the Tea Loft listening lounge and yard offer a social setting, perfect for a catch up and meeting new friends.\\n\\nABOUT SAUNA SOCIAL CLUB\\nThe Sauna Social Club is London's first dedicated sauna and ambient listening space. We blend saunas and ice baths with ambient music, making the perfect place to relax and recharge. We've grown out of a need for more healthy spaces to listen to great music. Our goal is to create a space that's designed for comfort and wellbeing that doesn't centre around consumption.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tr.ee/Olqxg9oHjV\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":864,\"name\":\"Intimacy w/ Harry Smithson, Eleanor Arnold, Isabelle Pead and DJ Euro Kurd\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"74bee97cef6dc3aaff36d657448be280.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Intimacy, live at the Hot Snakes Night Club and on rtm.fm with an evening of experimental sound and performance art from friends and new faces. Existing as a monthly radio show on rtm since January 2024, Intimacy is a common ground for artists working with sound to test and develop new work through the live performance of radio.\\n\\nFREE\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":619,\"name\":\"Kiran Leonard / Jennifer Walton / Another Country $$$$\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-28T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"263f33e268a849f1c0f8aac0b64d3edb.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House presents a night of live music, featuring three incredible artists a week before they each head to Dorset to perform at End of the Road Festival.\\n\\nKiran Leonard's unique and ambitious body of work spans more than a decade of frenetic noise rock, ornate avant-folk, DIY no-fi, and everything in between. Renowned for the range and intensity of his live performances, his current live group features members of caroline and Shovel Dance Collective.\\n\\nJennifer Walton is a London-based musician whose debut album Daughters explores grief, memory and surreal Americana. She’s also known for her work with Cryalot, Microplastics, Iceboy Violet, BABii, and remixes for Metronomy.\\n\\nAnother Country $$$$ are a Manchester-based audio-visual duo, born through the city’s experimental dance underbelly- combining shape-shifting electronic production, live drums and visuals. They craft blistering hybrid sets that fuse dub, jungle, DnB, garage, noise and hyperpop with a haunting cinematic edge.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":798,\"name\":\"5 GATE TEMPLE @ CLUB CHEEK \",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9d69cd53336cd5df3f6ee9edece70d31.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"5gt\\nXXL  \\n\\nSons of Simeon \\nBlack Fondu (Live)\\nFat-lïp\\nBabe of the Abyss\\nXterea (live)\\nSister Marion X John T. Gast X Elheist\\nSolomon Garçon \\n\\n\\nPre Carnival weekend lift off\\n\\nGet down early for fullness. \\n\\n*PLEASE NOTE* ADVANCE TICKET GUARANTEES ENTRY UNTIL 1:30AM\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":610,\"name\":\"Ray Keith’s Dread Bank Holiday\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T21:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"276ad7205250655f2d49500f66060a25.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dread Recordings Bank Holiday Carnival Special\\n \\nRay Keith returns to the Fox \\u0026 Firkin with his legendary party for August Bank Holiday Friday, and it’s a Carnival Special!  Time for another knees up.  Those who know, know, those who don’t, come through.\\n \\nLineup:\\nGrooverider\\nRay Keith\\nNookie B3B Madcap (Jungle Set)\\nDJ Millz B2B V Dubz\\nHexa B2B Leaf B2B Agro\\nNooch B2B Tunstep B2B Konz B2B Ty\\nKL B2B Gwillz B2B El Metalix\\n \\nMCS\\nAya Marar\\nSammy Jo\\nJuiceman\\nFive Alive\\nIffy\\nBlacka\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/ray-keiths-dread-bank-holiday/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":801,\"name\":\"SUGAR 004 with Angel D'lite + Bethan - All Night Long\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T04:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"723cf7c88bda23c9102c00acd0c0861a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"SUGAR slides back into Spanners for another intimate steamy end-of-summer party.. Following 3 sold out, cosy editions of blissed-out euphoria SUGAR004 is also a special someone's birthday party...IYKYK (.....it's one of the djs.....) Dive into dreamy trance, plush breakbeats and sexy house grooves with a sweet n sticky centre, 10pm - 4am\\n\\nLondon selectors Angel D’lite and Bethan will be on decks all night long, as always.\\n\\nLow-income tickets available, as usual, message our instagram if this is for you :)\\n\\nEager Ravers get sweet treats by @Wyldgarlic as always — this time of the iced variety!\\n\\nLets send off summer off in style \\u003c3\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2487791\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":868,\"name\":\"Night Slugs \\u0026 Einhundert\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-28T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"158d2f369530ed21969c3f98fbdcd5ef.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"We’re back with our annual Carnival Weekend warmup and we’ve invited a few friends down!\\n\\nNIGHT SLUGS \\u0026 EINHUNDERT\\nORMSIDE PROJECTS\\nFriday, August 28th\\nDoors: 11:00PM\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2497682\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":850,\"name\":\"Critical Movement\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-29T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-30T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f1be0f8a4971d32af03da986cca976e8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"How can one transition from the stillness of meditation into a creative movement task? Is it possible to distinguish authentic impulses for movement from the starting moment of embodied habits?\\n\\nCritical Movement offers a practical exploration of performance training, specifically how intentional movement can emerge from states of deep attention and stillness. Drawing on the Pali concept of samadhi (meditative concentration) alongside personal phenomenological experience, participants will explore movement beyond habitual patterns and performative expectations. \\n\\nThe investigation of neutrality as equanimity sits at the core of this workshop — not passive, but a dynamic process of ego-softening, attentive witnessing, and embodied presence. It combines yoga-informed somatic awareness, meditation, micro-movement investigation, and ideas from Queer Phenomenology, particularly Sara Ahmed's writing on perception and orientation. Participants will examine how non-judgemental observation and subtle bodily sensations can become sources of creative action, resisting the speed and productivity-driven ethos that dominates much of contemporary artistic practice.\\n\\nDesigned as a conversational laboratory, the workshop fosters collective enquiry, reciprocal listening, and horizontal exchange, welcoming movers, performers, educators, choreographers, and artists interested in contemplative practice, movement research, critical pedagogy, and queer embodied methodologies.\\n\\nBoth sessions will be investigating the same questions, with different exercises and practices. Attending both sessions will foster a deeper understanding of the work, but each session offers a full individual experience.\\n\\nLuis Odriozola is a performer, movement director, and actor movement teacher. From an embodied queer movement perspective, his work researches methodologies and practices that seek a balance between the rigour of classic traditions and via negativa, versus the need for perspectives rooted in Black feminism and via positiva actor training.\\n\\nHe studied acting in Spain, then completed the Choreographic Creation, Dance Research and Training Program at Forum Dança in Lisbon, and the MFA Movement: Directing and Teaching at CSSD in London. He was a member of the ensemble 'Dynamika Metamorfozy' at the Grotowski Institute and neTTtheatre company in Poland, and as an actor, movement and yoga teacher he has worked in schools including LAMDA and CCSD in London, and with community and youth groups in Spain and Poland.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38557/critical-movement\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":730,\"name\":\"QUEER WAVE: Newquay Pride 2026 Afterparty\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-29T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-30T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f3ad49401ccaff880bd3a259c5626e6a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Free outdoor DJ set with Perrin from 6pm–9pm. The ticketed afterparty begins at 9pm.\\n\\nQUEER WAVE takes over The Pagan Arms for the Newquay Pride afterparty, bringing the energy of East London’s queer nightlife to Newquay.\\n\\nJoin us for an evening of outdoor music, live drag performance and late-night dancing with Perrin, Barbs and Jeon Q.\\n\\nPerrin is one of the people behind Happy Endings at Dalston Superstore and has been an integral part of East London’s queer scene for years. Connected with parties including Adonis, Perrin has played at well-known events across London, Berlin and beyond. Perrin opens the celebration with a three-hour outdoor DJ set from 6pm to 9pm, free to attend.\\n\\nBarbs is an East London-based drag performer and a much-loved figure within the queer nightlife scene. With a long-standing career performing across the UK, Barbs takes over the main performance area from 9pm to 10:30pm, bringing live vocals, high-energy drag and plenty of camp.\\n\\nJeon Q is now based in Newquay, where he is a resident DJ at The Pagan Arms, while remaining closely connected to East London’s queer club scene. He takes the party inside from 10:30pm to 2am, closing the night with a high-energy mix of house, trance, techno, breakbeat and garage.\\n\\nThe outdoor DJ set from 6pm to 9pm is free. The ticketed afterparty begins at 9pm.\\n\\nRunning order\\n\\nPerrin — Outdoor DJ set, 6pm–9pm — Free entry\\nBarbs — Drag performance, 9pm–10:30pm — Ticketed\\nJeon Q — Inside club set, 10:30pm–2am — Ticketed\\n\\nTickets\\n\\nEarly Bird — £6\\nAdvance — £8\\nOn the door — £10\\n\\nTickets are required from 9pm onwards.\\nLast entry is at 1am.\\n\\nThis is an inclusive LGBTQ+ event. Everyone is welcome, but discrimination, harassment and inappropriate behaviour will not be tolerated.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":878,\"name\":\"Pre-launch • Ambient Sauna | Guohan, Stella Z \\u0026 Voision Xi (Live) \",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-29T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"190ac732f1cbe47cf1a7b58896b0297a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pre-launch • Join us for the first weekend in our new venue, just two doors down from the original space you know and love! With the main launch party on Monday 31st, come down early for an exclusive preview and be the first to try out the new setup.\\n\\nOn Saturday we welcome Ambient Sauna regular Stella Z, Shanghai-based vocalist and composer Voision Xi, and London-based producer Guohan. Stella Z weaves together organic textures, object sounds, and nature-inspired atmospheres with psychedelic rhythms. Voision Xi brings a live performance rooted in warm, expressive vocals, jazz improvisation, and poetic songwriting, while Guohan rounds off the programme with deep grooves, organic rhythms, and beautifully imperfect electronic arrangements embracing human nuance.\\n\\n*Book your 70-minute sauna session, arrive early and stay late for 4 hours of music in the lounge*\\n\\nABOUT AMBIENT SAUNA\\nOur silent Treehouse sauna and the chatty Herbal sauna are both equipped with a sound system for deep listening. Our Bunker sauna, the Tea Loft listening lounge and yard offer a social setting, perfect for a catch up and meeting new friends.\\n\\nABOUT SAUNA SOCIAL CLUB\\nThe Sauna Social Club is London's first dedicated sauna and ambient listening space. We blend saunas and ice baths with ambient music, making the perfect place to relax and recharge. We've grown out of a need for more healthy spaces to listen to great music. Our goal is to create a space that's designed for comfort and wellbeing that doesn't centre around consumption.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tr.ee/otHCSeSGE6\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":856,\"name\":\"Friends of Mairi Ella\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-29T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"321385542e1013c8c25a8f4a88e8235f.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Charity gig supporting 999 club, a homeless charity working in South East London\\n\\nHello friends,\\n\\nIt would have been my dear friend Mairi Ella’s birthday this August, so i am throwing a fundraiser gig in her memory.\\n\\nThe lineup:\\n\\nSWEETCHEEKS\\n\\nLondon based hyper-pop numetal band daring to ask ‘what if Britney was in Slipknot?’ Setting girly pop melodies and anime synth lines against gnarly riffs, blast beats and harsh vocals, sweetcheeks is equal parts sugary and savage. Their wild and immersive live shows featuring K-pop style choreography have become the talk of the capital since their debut performance last year.\\n\\nVAUDEVILLES:\\n\\nthree-piece Garage Rock 'n' Roll band based in Manchester. Tearing through live shows with the energy of “a greyhound on meth”, the band play songs that combine infectious melodies with a strong dose of ripping riffs.\\n\\nTHE SPANISH INQUISITIONS\\n\\nLondon based saccharine goo rockers: covered in jam and surrounded by flies. Five members, each stickier than the last.\\n\\nSCOUT PARKS\\n\\nCanadian writer and musician living in London. He gained a love of folk music, playing around the campfires of his early years in Canada. Then an interlude studying classical music, singing opera in Reykjavik, before back to the singer songwriter world. Catch him round London frequenting open mics like Song Miners and Jamboree Poetry Mondays.\\n\\nall proceeds will go towards 999 club, a homeless charity working in south london. mairi ella always did everything in her power to help the homeless, wether that was emptying her wallet, giving the clothes off her back or sitting down and chatting with the people she would meet living on the streets. she was an incredible woman and friend and i miss her every day. if you aren’t able to attend the show, or would like to donate more than the ticket price, there is also a justgiving link in my bio.\\n\\nlooking forward to seeing you all there,\\n\\nBaby Niamh x\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/friends-of-mairi-ella-tickets-1996879934639?utm_experiment=test_share_listing\\u0026aff=ebdsshios\\u0026sg=b91ffa50f1b0f49a18e634cc1e3d0e28fad846847f8940f869e6dce21e0fc7cf2238b323066c4379b8c5797cb723252e525030c9837712280697e042ce4dde43fbd471edc7e2cc367174ab03ec\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":852,\"name\":\"Threshold Houseboys Choir: Form Grows Rampant\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-29T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"283b6a5f96330153f6b1882cdaad3f0e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A very rare screening of the now out of print DVD film of Peter Christopherson’s solo project ‘Threshold Houseboys Choir’ Form Grows Rampant.\\n\\n\\\"In 2003 I was invited to attend the Ginjae Festival in Krabi Town in the south of Thailand. Ginjae literally means vegetarian, though the connection is obscure. \\n\\nThe major celebrations of this festival take place on the nearby island of Phuket, but there, the atmosphere is one of spectacle, rather than purpose. I had been told about a very different celebration, based around a small chinese shrine or holy place, behind a Toyota dealership in Krabi Town, some 50 kilometres from Phuket island, on the mainland. The Ginjae Festival takes place on the 9th full moon of the year. Over the course of ten days (during which participants wear white and abstain from meat, alcohol and sex) a series of rituals are performed. intended to keep the world spinning on the correct axis. To bring merit and good luck to the village, and to scare away malign spirits that might otherwise bring misfortune to the neighbourhood; especially at busy intersections, accident black spots, etc... \\n\\nThe participants setting out from the shrine we visited were all young men, led by a young 'khatoey\\\" holy man. For the most part they were tattooed tearaways or troublemakers and not the kind of person you would expect to see the local shop-keepers on their knees praying to by the side of the road. In all cases that I witnessed, the rituals were carried out while the participants were in trance or possessed states; often lasting several hours. The boys were trained in, and induced into these states by their holy man, in whom they had complete trust. \\n\\nRemoved from immediate contact with the present by these mental states, the boys seemed not to feel pain. Though as their expressions show, this was not always the case when the trance weakened. Their trances also assisted their speedy recovery - along with the ice-water that their assistants poured on their wounds from kettles throughout the ritual. I saw most of these boys in the days that followed and they appeared to have suffered no ill-effects. and indeed to be almost completely scar free. Certainly emotionally they seemed buoyed by events, as did the worshippers in the neighbourhoods they passed through. \\n\\nBy contrast I was admitted to hospital for several days, suffering from some undiagnosed disorder, which I ascribe to temporarily becoming inadvertent host to one of the evil spirits that their rituals disturbed. \\n\\nIn this work my interpretation of the rituals - my focus and my music - ape entirely personal, and not directly connected to purpose of the Ginjae Festival. I simply believe I saw and filmed something profound, transcendent; the deity incarnate even; in the most unlikely of settings and want to share that with you. \\n\\nAs Jhonn said: \\\"We all get the gods we deserve...\\\"\\n\\n- Peter Christopherson Bangkok January 3rd 2007\\n\\nScreening starts at 8:30pm.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":869,\"name\":\"RALLY x Scenic Route x ORMSIDE : Jump Source / spirit blue / Thredd / anu \\u0026 404 eros\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-29T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-30T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e3c649ceae890d0a1bdf4714caf801a7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"anu \\u0026 404 eros\\nJump Source\\nspirit blue\\nThredd\\n\\nOrmside hosts RALLY x Scenic Route for the official RALLY 2026 Afterparty programme. DJ Sets from anu \\u0026 404 eros, Jump Source, spirit blue, and Thredd. Southwark Park was just the warm up.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2493603\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":728,\"name\":\"Club Yeke x Rozaly: Carnival Afterparty\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-30T10:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-31T04:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"422251602e4766bf64ed7d4545e8afb5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Yeke returns this Carnival Bank Holiday with another after party after last years sold-out madness.\\n\\nBringing international guests and local heroes under one roof for a celebration of Caribbean carnival from Martinique, Jamaica, Suriname, Dominica and beyond.\\n\\nSweat from the walls guaranteed...\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":862,\"name\":\"QUEER HEELS CLASS\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-30T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-30T18:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3ce3a551c90ac2d83476f6e6d964f420.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Monthly Queer Heels Class by Sula Castle\\n\\nOpen to All - No heels experience required !!\\n\\nAUGUST 30th 4-6pm \\n\\nClass Structure will be a mix of walking, improv and set tasks, and a cute routine at the end x will be chill and fun - not scary x i promise x\\n\\nAny questions or if financial barriers are an issue, DM @toughboysdanceco\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":879,\"name\":\"Pre-launch • Ambient Sauna | Danniella Dee\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-30T16:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-30T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8334b6687d1064400f19a8ba1d823006.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Pre-launch • Join us for the first weekend in our new venue, just two doors down from the original space you know and love! With the main launch party on Monday 31st, come down early for an exclusive preview and be the first to try out the new setup.\\n\\nFor our Sunday pre-launch matinee, we’re excited to welcome Coventry-born and based artist, selector and producer Danniella Dee for an extended dub \\u0026 reggae session. From singing as a chorister beneath Coventry Cathedral’s vaults to touring as her dad’s roadie with The Specials, she grew up between the worlds of sacred, strict rehearsals and bass-rattling rebellion. Today, alongside writing and producing her own music, she hosts The Baddis Sound on NTS Radio, exploring a deep love of reggae and the stories woven through it.\\n\\n*Book your 70-minute sauna session, arrive early and stay late for 4 hours of music in the lounge*\\n\\nABOUT AMBIENT SAUNA\\nOur silent Treehouse sauna and the chatty Herbal sauna are both equipped with a sound system for deep listening. Our Bunker sauna, the Tea Loft listening lounge and yard offer a social setting, perfect for a catch up and meeting new friends.\\n\\nABOUT SAUNA SOCIAL CLUB\\nThe Sauna Social Club is London's first dedicated sauna and ambient listening space. We blend saunas and ice baths with ambient music, making the perfect place to relax and recharge. We've grown out of a need for more healthy spaces to listen to great music. Our goal is to create a space that's designed for comfort and wellbeing that doesn't centre around consumption.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tr.ee/8hAwJm9s-B\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":545,\"name\":\"Fran \\u0026 Flora present a night of contemporary Yiddish music, feat. Merlin \\u0026 Polina Shepherd, Ilana Cravitz String Band and Fran \\u0026 Flora\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-30T19:15:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-30T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2e77bc561f41b4c089bd3ef65f5a2767.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Experimental-folk duo Fran \\u0026 Flora curate a special night at The Horse Hospital celebrating contemporary Yiddish culture, showcasing some of the UK’s most acclaimed klezmer artists.\\n\\nFran \\u0026 Flora present brand new material from their upcoming third album; Klezmer clarinet and piano-vocal duo Merlin \\u0026 Polina Shepherd perform a selection of original compositions; fiddler Ilana Cravitz + string band share a first public outing of selected tunes from Beregovsky's recently uncovered Tish Nign collection.\\n\\nABOUT THE ARTISTS\\n\\nFRAN \\u0026 FLORA\\n“time-travels brilliantly between solid folk origins and avant garde play with a surprise at every corner\\\" - Jude Rogers, The Guardian\\n\\nFran \\u0026 Flora's critically acclaimed releases and performances have led to their rise in prominence across folk and avant-garde musical landscapes alike. As leading women of their generation their sophomore album Precious Collection (Hidden Notes Records'24) was The Guardian’s ‘Top 10 Best Folk Albums of the Year’. Presenting uniquely reworked Yiddish music (collected from archival recordings \\u0026 manuscripts) and original compositions for strings, electronics and voice they create an unrivalled evocative and 'border-defying' (Mojo) aesthetic.\\nFar from recreating music from a bygone era their intricately sculpted contemporary sound remains 'as experimental as it is accessible' (The Guardian). Fran \\u0026 Flora perform and teach at festivals globally. \\n\\nMERLIN \\u0026 POLINA SHEPHERD\\n\\\"the Led Zeppelin of contemporary Yiddish music.\\\" – Seth Rogovoy, author, 'The Essential Klezmer'\\n\\nMerlin \\u0026 Polina Shepherd Duo (clarinets, voice, piano) perform together in a way that is rarely encountered. They play music from several linked cultures with improvisation, freedom and spontaneity. The Duo’s playful approach to their root traditions – klezmer, Slavic, East European and southern Medite­rranean – is full of knowledge and deference. It creates a unique sound that embraces the e­nduring spirit of folklore and takes the listener to new dimensions.\\n\\nThey have been performing as a duo since 2004. Apart from their own concerts, they collaborate internationally with performers of various disciplines: a baroque orchestra, a punk band, contemporary dancers, DJs, and theatre productions.\\n\\nILANA CRAVITZ is one of the world’s best-known klezmer fiddlers and is also in demand as a producer, editor, and Yiddish dance leader. Based in London, Ilana tours internationally and regularly helps to set up and run Yiddish culture festivals. She has introduced thousands of people to klezmer through her performances and teaching. Ilana was a co-founder of the London Klezmer Quartet and her book ‘Klezmer Fiddle – A How-To Guide’, is published by Oxford University Press.\\nIlana Cravitz’ Tish Nigumim String Band play a hand-picked selection of tunes from ‘Jewish Songs Without Words’ - an anthology of 215 tunes collected by Moshe Beregovski (1892-1961) that was prepared for publication in the late 1950s and then kept in the Vernadsky National Library, Kiev.\\nNigunim are tunes without words, composed to be sung, catchy and lift the spirits. \\nBeregovski’s book of nigunim was the fourth of five volumes of Jewish music painstakingly assembled by this dedicated Soviet Jewish ethnomusicologist. Tragically, he did not live to see them published. \\nIlana Cravitz is now working on an English edition of this volume, with its glimpses into a now-lost world.\\n\\n\\nThis event is open to the public, and is the closing event to the Jewish Music Institute’s Yiddish Cultural Weekend. \\nWith support from the JMI.\\n\\nDoors 7:15pm\\nMusic 7:45pm - 10:00pm\\nCurfew 11:00pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":875,\"name\":\"Ambient Launch Party • Marysia Osu, Millie McKee \\u0026 TBA\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-31T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-31T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b8c0dd9730c246ff97ab8c507cd80687.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Ambient Launch Party • Join us on Monday 31st August as we open the doors to our new space and celebrate two years of Sauna Social Club. Come early and stay late to fully experience our lovely saunas, large yard with ice baths, café, and Tea Loft listening lounge, with an extended programme of live and DJ performances soundtracking the day. Expect special treats throughout, including snacks and games ⋆˚꩜｡\\n\\n*Book your 70-minute sauna session, arrive early and stay late for 8 hours of music in the lounge*\\n\\nABOUT AMBIENT SAUNA\\nOur silent Treehouse sauna and the chatty Herbal sauna are both equipped with a sound system for deep listening. Our Bunker sauna, the Tea Loft listening lounge and yard offer a social setting, perfect for a catch up and meeting new friends.\\n\\nABOUT SAUNA SOCIAL CLUB\\nThe Sauna Social Club is London's first dedicated sauna and ambient listening space. We blend saunas and ice baths with ambient music, making the perfect place to relax and recharge. We've grown out of a need for more healthy spaces to listen to great music. Our goal is to create a space that's designed for comfort and wellbeing that doesn't centre around consumption.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://tr.ee/tsn2sCPBT-\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":820,\"name\":\"Hearing Tests, [Brick], Crapstallion, Second Skin | Real Life Presents - new London hardcore\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-01T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-01T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"26076f9037dab7d897239009f3c5f10d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nHearing Tests\\nAnti-fascist hardcore noise\\n\\nBrick\\nMurderous transfeminist hardcore\\n\\nCrapstallion\\nlo-fi hardcore punk with big fuzzy bass\\n\\nSecond Skin\\nNew London stompcore from some familiar faces\\n\\nTuesday 1st September\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\nDoors 6pm\\n£9\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/hearing-tests-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":760,\"name\":\"VENT ⓥ Valentina Magaletti \\u0026 YPY, Ben Vince\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-02T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-02T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f812ca6be6b6bc0972979613d7cd2be5.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Valentina Magaletti \\u0026 YPY (the solo moniker of Japanese musician Koshiro Hino) form an acclaimed experimental, electroacoustic duo. Their collaborative project blends Magaletti's highly percussive, avant-garde drumming with YPY's metallic, handcrafted electronics and polyrhythmic structures, highlighted by their acclaimed LP Kansai Bruises\\n\\nBen Vince is a striking composer and performer, known for his live improvised saxophone explorations and inventive techniques in creating new rhythms, textures and moods. Through live improvisation, sonic manipulation, reprocessing and looping, whether in the studio or on the stage, his spontaneous yet intuitive approach and collaborative nature surpasses the seeming limitations of his primary instrument.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2474351\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":892,\"name\":\" Britney issue no 1: Toxic by Taylor Le Melle launch event with MayDay and BOOKS\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-03T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-03T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"613b8f2445e1c0c3f0f3b9653c1a7837.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nHosted by MayDay in collaboration with BOOKS Peckham. A reading from Taylor Le Melle followed by in conversation with britney editors Kate Paul and Carle Gent. Plus refreshments. Plus karaoke.\\n\\nCome celebrate the launch of the hottest journal of art and new writing to launch this summer. britney is a journal of new art and writing, edited by Carle Gent and Kate Paul. A new artist/writer/clinician/mystic is commissioned for each issue, and each issue is named for a song by the inimitable Britney Spears. britney #1 is Toxic, by writer Taylor Le Melle. It is a science fiction that deals in architectures, bodily inheritances, bio hacking, academia, and double consciousness.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.maydayrooms.org/e/100/britney-issue-no-1-toxic-by-taylor-le-melle\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":677,\"name\":\"Roots On The Corner #44. Shere Khan Sound System meets Jah Messenjah Sound System\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-04T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-05T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"403421ce5c6f6af8c85402e4f574f7f7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Roots on the Corner No 44.\\nFriday 4th September 2026!\\n\\nJust when you thought your summer was dun, Roots on the Corner steps back with a deep and heavy start to our winter line up!\\n\\nJah MessenJah sound system (Swindon) “Playing JAH music inna king David style” meets resident sound Shere Khan sound system featuring The Jungle cat, Juno and Ras Terry Gad (London).\\n\\nExpect a deep and spiritually immersive session in Reggae, Dub-wise, Roots and Steppas (Dub Techno) with healing bass pressures, from two unique emerging sound systems.\\n\\nDoors open 10pm - 5am. Last Entry 3am. Nearest tube: Tottenham hale.\\nVenue: Distillery N17, Unit 25, Mill Mead Rd, London N17 9QU, UK\\nHome of Pirates Grog Rum.\\n\\nTickets: £5 / £8 / £11 / £15.\\n\\nExpect the usual giveaways and good vibes and we'll see you at the bar getting those Rum punches! Looking forward to skankin with ya!\\n\\nPlease bring ID, over 18\\\"s only.\\nCASH \\u0026 CARDS accepted.\\n(Online Ticket sales close 11am 4th September.)\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2442995\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":858,\"name\":\"Tufan ~ Closing Party ☆\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-05T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-06T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3eecd5307f3644a89795b96c79f17723.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To celebrate the ending of Tufan and Oitij-jo’s participation in Backyard Biennial: East, we are throwing the official big 12 hour closing party! \\n\\nFeaturing Art, Films, Zines, Workshop, DJs + Open Decks (BRING YOUR USB)!\\n\\nLineup: \\n\\nKhan-Ki featuring Alex Neon\\nMisbah\\nAmena Zaman\\nbkonsmoke (Ace.RGB B2B M4ria B2B frostfight000)\\n\\n3pm - 5pm ~ Film Screenings\\n\\n5pm - 7pm ~ T-Shirt Printing Workshop\\n\\n7pm - 8pm ~ Open Decks\\n\\n8pm - 3am ~ DJs\\n\\n9pm ~ Artwork Sales End\\n\\n+ More information about the programme to be announced…\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":861,\"name\":\"Portraiture + Roca + Texture Magazine\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-05T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-06T00:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"db8d31d2d5b8da042aea1c39f12343ac.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Texture Magazine + Roca host New York label Portraiture for a warm end to the summer, featuring friends from far and wide \\u003c3\\n\\nLive music all day from 3pm - late.\\n\\nWe'll have zines, merch, and more from Physical Interface and friends, and we also invite anyone attending to bring some food to share throughout the day :~)\\n\\nWe'll also be broadcasting all performances locally, so bring your own radio if you want to sit outside and catch some rays and still tune in 📡\\n\\nPlease let us know if you have any questions, accessibility requirements, or have any other barriers to attendance.\\n\\nSee you there!\\n\\n₊˚❀.ೃ࿔*:･\\n\\n~\\n\\nPoster by Tommy Brentnall\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":750,\"name\":\"London Radical Bookfair\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-06T11:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-06T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e50bf9dc3d8c15acd1aba2bc22e1700d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The London Radical Bookfair’s key aim is to create a welcoming space for readers and organisers to exchange ideas, discover new writing, and build connections across movements and communities.\\n\\nOrganised by BookLove and Housmans Bookshop on behalf of the Alliance of Radical Booksellers, the free event will run from 11am–5pm and is open to everyone.\\n\\nVisitors can expect a stimulating mix of stalls, books, pamphlets, magazines and zines covering subjects including politics, history, feminism, anti-racism, climate justice, queer liberation, trade unionism, internationalism and community organising. The fair will also provide opportunities to meet writers, campaigners and independent publishers working at the forefront of radical thought and activism.\\n\\nThe London Radical Bookfair is intended as a welcoming and inclusive event for the whole community. Alongside political and independent publishing, the fair will include children’s books, family-friendly materials and accessible spaces for people of all ages to browse, learn and take part. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":791,\"name\":\"WORMHOLE [day party]\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-06T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-06T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"c8e318dd71df926980aa20ca2552ada0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Holy hell, can you believe it's nearly been a year since the first WORMHOLE got cancelled? A year since Jerzy got lost and never made it to London with his tomatoes? Neither can we. So come celebrate it with us :)\\n\\nCome mourn one year since WORMHOLE began, at a brand new secret venue we're calling the WORM FACTORY, this time it's extra special because it's our birthday. Get those earholes and bumholes primed and grab a ticket for a Sunday day party on Sunday 6th September.\\n\\nLocation: top secret, somewhere in East London. Accessible via DLR. We'll drop the address a few days before (hopefully it's near you, but even if it isn't then its defintiely worth making the journey for. we promise!!\\n\\nAccessibility: there is a lift and accessible toilet!\\n\\nTickets live now via the link in bio, and on GEL (a new listings and ticketing platform built for a more equitable, transparent way into London's grassroots nightlife, arts and culture scene)\\n\\nCome fill your pieholes with us as we toast one year of cancelling ourselves x\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":757,\"name\":\"Animals on Psychedelics x Braintickle\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-06T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-06T23:59:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6a28dfef683fe80a6778fbfd30f6c1f7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"GNMR \\nKatya \\nNaone  b2b denial\\nCarl H b2b Richard Gregory\\n\\n\\nCelebrating 10 years of Animals on Psychedelics and the launch of Braintickle\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2484976\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":489,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents | Fool's Game / Last Wishes / Malignant Methods / Big Smoke\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-06T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-06T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6f938a8165cdc3548ace524591ee6fc8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nLast Wishes\\nDangerous UKHC on DAZE\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/lastwisheshardcore/\\n\\n+ support from\\nDetriment\\nRGHC back in the game\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/detrimentuk/\\n\\nBig Smoke\\nLondon hardcore ft. members of Renounced and Transcendence\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/bigsmoke.hc/\\n\\n\\u0026 more...\\n\\nSunday 6th September\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross and New Cross Gate\\nDoors 6pm\\n£13\\n14+, U16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/fools-game-last-wishes-malignant-methods\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":587,\"name\":\"A Global Grindcore Invasion - Rageous Intent, C.H.O.U., Mindcollapse, Vilmort \\u0026 Frakasø\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-08T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-08T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ef3e69ce170a021795af093e97228bc1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nA Global Grindcore Invasion. Filthy blastbeat chaos from Spain, China, Scotland, and the UK\\n\\nFeaturing:\\n\\nRageous Intent\\nC.H.O.U.\\nMindcollapse\\nVilmort\\nFrakasø\\n\\nTuesday 8th September\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\nDoors 6pm\\n£12\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/rageous-intent-chou\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":603,\"name\":\"New Lands \\u0026 SelOut present: Blood Wizard\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-08T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-08T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b79aff108acf6f76a3694fb98bf5b8b9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands and SelOut team up for a very special night at The Ivy House, with three of South London's finest bands gracing the stage to celebrate the 40th edition of the zine!\\nEmerging in 2021 with an album of home-recordings titled Western Spaghetti, the south London based project, fronted by songwriter Cai Burns quietly gained underground popularity. What began as a solo project with folkier leanings gradually evolved into a collaborative unit which became heavier, slower, and harder to pin down; blending ragged indie rock, dreamy synths,and glitched-out textures. Since then, Blood Wizard have built a devoted following across the UK and afar and have become a fixture of London's DIY scene.\\ntall child is a band of 5 queer friends based in London, also the alias for Zha Gandhi, a musician of Nigerian/Indian heritage. Zha takes inspiration from the likes of Mitski, Radiohead, Rachel Chinouriri and Arlo Parks, to create a beautifully intimate and authentic basis for their soundscape. They build on this with a brutally honest style of lyricism, that explores their experiences as a queer disabled POC, to develop a sonic space especially for those who feel their differences being used against them. Recently announced as the winner for Green Man Rising, they are paving the way for other black artists in the indie music scene. Their debut EP ‘Somehow You Grow' is out now via Sad Club Records!\\nlifepath99 is a noise pop and indie rock project originating from the ether.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":839,\"name\":\"flowers.ldn \\u0026 WSHWSH present: Intibint Album Release Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-10T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-11T00:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"11fb594f37b2c41ec6ceb61bd133bc3b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Head on over to Ormside Projects on Thursday 10th September for Intibint's Album Release party: presented by flowers.ldn and WSHWSH.\\n\\nIntibint’s debut album, titled ‘Half Moon Eyes’, is a self-produced project of electronic experimentation inspired by both Arabic and electronic sounds. The work is a progression into Intibint’s world through music, reflecting on the complexities of existing as someone connected to a war-torn homeland while navigating internal and external chaos across love, heartbreak and resistance.\\n\\nThe evening will include a live album performance by Intibint, alongside oud and DJ sets from Nihal, Salam Kitty, MAVEEN, candice a.m, and henna by HuqThat.\\n\\nGet your ticket now* and come celebrate with us!\\n\\n🩷🌙🐬🩷🌙🐬🩷🌙🐬\\n\\n*If you're on Universal Credit, an asylum seeker or can't afford a ticket, just email us for a free ticket (flowerssldn@gmail.com) - all are welcome and no one will be turned away for lack of funds.\\n\\nEvent Artwork: Intibint\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":536,\"name\":\"Up the Youth Club: Emma Warren in conversation with Jack Young\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-10T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-10T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"fee5846c2c2a358a70dc18a266c7a45e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us when we welcome Emma Warren to discuss her book Up the Youth Club with Jack Young \\n\\n'Youth clubs have always existed. They always will, because there will always be young people. How we care for our youth, and what we owe them, is a question for all of us.'\\n\\nIn Up the Youth Club, Emma Warren maps the shifting story of youth clubs in the UK and Northern Ireland, from factory workers in Victorian Boys' and Girls' clubs to renegade self-emancipatory spaces in the 1970s and the music-generating youth clubs of more recent decades. With a mixed lineage in church evangelism, the patronage of the upper classes, grassroots' DIY, and erratic state funding, the youth club has had a huge, yet almost invisible, effect on music, sport, culture and society.\\n\\nArguing that we cannot advocate for what we do not understand, Warren positions youth clubs as a kind of engine room - from the famous success stories to come out of their doors, such as The Specials or Stormzy, to the untold stories of young people finding shelter, sustenance and stimulation for over a century - and why their dwindling numbers, largely due to austerity and funding cuts, is of serious concern for us all.\\n\\nWith this impassioned history, Warren invites us to pick up the torch and play an active part in protecting and re-igniting this vital part of UK society.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://events.humanitix.com/up-the-youth-club-emma-warren-in-conversation-with-jack-young\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":582,\"name\":\"Sheila Maurice Grey\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-10T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-10T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b3162f4a0d1a60e8119bf3c2bd43c318.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"UK Jazz hero Sheila Maurice Grey is bringing her solo project to the Fox \\u0026 Firkin for the first time.\\n\\nSheila is a London based trumpet and flugelhorn player who leads the world renowned band Kokoroko and has featured on several projects such as Sampha, Little Simz, Yussef Dayes, Stormzy and others.\\n\\nSheila is also a visual artist who loves to paint. Her painting plays an important and central role in her solo music project where she aims to explore her musical voice as well as through her paintings provocatively question the of hyper sexualisation of black women throughout history.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://foxfirkin.com/event/sheila-maurice-grey/\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":588,\"name\":\"Locked Shut | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-11T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-11T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"66d43c3b8227e8097dea8818c5dcb519.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"TICKETS LIVE FROM 10AM ON 10/6/26\\n\\nReal Life Presents\\n\\nLocked Shut\\nMissouri hardcore mosh anthems\\n\\n+ Suitably massive supports coming soon\\n\\nFriday 11th September\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\n£12\\nDoors 6pm\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/locked-shut\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":851,\"name\":\"Hoxton Cabal 1st Birthday: Grace Sands, Benebe b2b Special Guest, Phil James, Fari Mond\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-11T21:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-12T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"9a36b728bf0ab6160dfdf325cef8d8db.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Hoxton Cabal turns one this September, and we are putting on a special line-up to celebrate!  \\n\\nFor a vinyl-only night it is only fitting that we invite the almighty Grace Sands to help us blow out our first candle. \\n\\nExpect those absolutely classic, deep and cheeky house cuts from Grace. Benebe will be joined for a special b2b by a surprise guest to close out the party with, well, you’ll find out!  \\n\\nFriends of the Cabal Phil James and Fari Mond will get us into the groove in true Cabal style. \\n\\nCapacity is limited to 80.  \\n\\nSee you down there…\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":870,\"name\":\"Expert Death x Untitled 909: Azu Tiwaline, ophélie, basic chanel + Sarjan\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-11T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-12T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"e937cf55acb7a18c8c41e88d074fbffd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Expert Death and Untitled 909 team up for an end-of-summer shindig.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2483969\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":891,\"name\":\"Materials: A Festival of Visual Culture and Politics\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-12T10:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-12T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d83591b9f7e02852d81f1eb77e613940.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Join us at Pelican House for the second Materials Festival, where we explore visual and spatial practices as a force for radical imagination and transformative social change. \\n​The theme for this year is embedded practice: what does it mean to develop a creative practice that is genuinely embedded in a place or community? How can we organise with our neighbours, colleagues and friends to respond to our shared material struggles? And what is our vision of the “good life” that we’re all building towards?\\n\\n​We’ll start the day at 10am, with free snacks and a pay-what-you-can lunch. Bookworkers and Beyond will be running a Publishing Fair, and we’ll be displaying London’s Ours, an exhibition of visual materials from the Greater London Council 1981–1986. After 6pm we’ll have a special performance by Circle Dance and a social with drinks and music.\\n\\n​Conversations\\n​Multitudes\\n\\n​Migrants in Culture\\n\\n​Common Knowledge\\n\\n​Lola Olufemi\\n\\n​Sarah Stein Lubrano\\n\\n​Unit 38\\n\\n​House of Annetta\\n\\n​Case studies\\n​Slow + Dirty Press\\n\\n​FAT Studio\\n\\n​Wards Corner Community Plan\\n\\n​Tottenham Family Fight Back\\n\\n​Workshops\\n​Artists \\u0026 Culture Workers\\n\\n​Autonomous Design Group\\n\\n​Cooperation Town\\n\\n​Section of Architectural Workers\\n\\n​The Department of Information \\u0026 Propaganda\\n\\n​The People’s Prop Department\\n\\n​workers.coop\\n\\n​Bookworkers \\u0026 Beyond Publishing Fair\\n​BOOKS\\n\\n​F.A.T. Studio\\n\\n​Migrants in Culture\\n\\n​PageMasters\\n\\n​Slow + Dirty Press\\n\\n​Sticky Fingers Publishing\\n\\n​and more to be confirmed!\\n\\n​Open studios with Pelican residents\\n​Common Knowledge\\n\\n​Migrants in Culture\\n\\n​Unit 38\\n\\n​Plus!\\n​Circle Dance presents: Neither Albion Nor Britannia\\n\\n​London's Ours! A GLC Exhibition\\n\\n​Collective art marking with the London School of Solarpunk\\n\\n​Bethnal Green walking tours\\n\\n​Free childcare for children over 5\\n\\n​Organised by Common Knowledge and Unit 38, with support from the Rosa Luxemburg Stiftung and Pelican House.\\n\\n​All profits from ticket sales will be distributed between our speakers. Email us if you're unwaged and would like come — no one turned away for lack of funds.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://luma.com/p8mapcri\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":874,\"name\":\"SLSA x The Horse Hospital present: FUTURE FREQUENCIES\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-12T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-12T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8bcf9ce085f4c2e4d3da8d739312e4ce.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"South London Space Agency and The Horse Hospital present FUTURE FREQUENCIES, a new event series bringing spoken word, grime, vocal improvisation together with experimental electronics. Come through for the open mic spoken word jam and stay for live sets from Pouya Ehsaei, GRANDMIXXER, Alya Al-Sultani, and Mez\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":836,\"name\":\"Small Car NRG\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-12T20:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-13T02:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3d5bb1e9dc1c02ab03dd2dbc03bf879a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Small Car NRG is pulling in for a pitstop at Avalon Cafe where it all began! Multiple laps around the Surrey Canal Speedway completed, fresh fluids, detailing, engine remapped to to the GTI version (Great Tunes Included).\\n\\nVery very excited to be inviting Memory Palace over from Barcelona for her first show in London! Operating at the intersection of IDM, bass, techno, and trance, her sets explore the idea of sonic spiralling, rhythms looping inward, melodies pulling the room tighter together until everyone is moving within the same pulse. A meditation in motion, drifting between introspection and release, always tinted with a dark, driving undercurrent.\\n\\nSpecial guests incoming :)\\n\\nAs always we will be starting the night off with Tweakers Welcome which is a supportive and low-pressure environment to practice DJing in a real club, on a real soundsystem!\\n\\nSign up form on our instagram @smallcarnrg\\n\\nLets have it 🙂\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":506,\"name\":\"Erode / Sinister Feeling / Bullet | Real Life x Tombstone\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-14T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-14T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"40496f589e4b81396e960cb4a259a4c2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life \\u0026 Tombstone Present\\nTrouble from Baltimore...\\n\\nErode\\nViolent death metal hardcore on DAZE\\n\\nSinister Feeling\\nGnarled stomping powerviolence\\n\\n+ Support from\\nBullet\\nAction from London\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/bullethxc/\\n\\nFlesh Prison\\nEvil from Brighton\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/fleshprisonuk/\\n\\nWasting Thirst\\nViolence from the South\\nhttps://www.instagram.com/wastingthirst/\\n\\n\\nAnd more...\\n\\nMonday 14th September\\n£11\\nDoors 7pm\\nOld Blue Last, nearest stations Old Street and Shoreditch High Street\\n38 Great Eastern St, London EC2A 3ES\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/erode-x-sinister-feeling-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":326,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents | Bulldoze / Kartel / Mindless / Ballkick / Paresthesia\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-15T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-15T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"335525e14f40c9e4ee0da82007645159.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nBulldoze\\nBack once again for a 3rd legendary lesson in beatdowns. Still here and strong.\\n\\n+ support from\\nKartel\\nReturning LBU heavyweights\\n\\nMindless\\nThe most dangerous men in Kent\\n\\nBallkick\\nHardcore punk rage\\n\\nParesthesia\\nDeath metal hardcore youth\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross and New Cross Gate\\n\\n£20\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/bulldoze-3\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":853,\"name\":\"Coby Sey / Miriam Adefris / Elliot Galvin / Tom Skinner (Quartet) | dove, Christine Kirubi\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-15T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-15T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7c74e517fcf77e2df6a0c50840114617.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Coby Sey is a songwriter, producer, vocalist, multi-instrumentalist, and DJ who, after years spent navigating the DIY artist scene in South East London, has developed a distinctive presence as an artist and performer.\\n\\nCoby’s recorded work spans live instrumentation, sample-based productions, and experimental music, blending recognizable motifs of hip hop, noise, jazz, and grime into a dubbed-out anaesthesia.\\n\\nHe employs an open-door approach to sharing and creating music, which is evident in his long-term collaborations with Mica Levi and Tirzah, as well as with peers such as Dean Blunt, TYSON, Laurel Halo, and Speakers Corner Quartet. He is also a founding member of London’s CURL collective (alongside Mica and Brother May) and hosts a long-running monthly show on NTS.\\n\\n-- \\n\\nMiriam Adefris is a harpist based in London. Rooted in both improvisation and composed structures, her solo sets amalgamate diverse musical influences from classical and experimental to jazz. She has recently released a debut album with her new band Flur to critical acclaim. Notable collaborations include performances with Floating Points, Shabaka Hutchings and singer Ganavya.\\n\\n--\\n\\nElliot Galvin is a long-time trailblazer in the UK jazz firmament with five solo albums that have seen him top album of the year lists at the likes of Downbeat and Jazzwise, as well as being a member of the Mercury nominated Dinosaur, and collaborating with Shabaka Hutchings, Emma-Jean Thackray, Norma Winstone, Marius Neset and Mark Lockheart.\\n\\nGalvin has also earned a fierce reputation as a borderless improvisor having released records with the likes of Mark Sanders and his now labelmate Binker Golding. In 2020 he released an entirely improvised piano album and was named The Guardian album of the month and BBC Music magazine’s album of the year. His latest album The Ruin features Shabaka Hutchings, Sebastian Rochford, Ruth Goller and the Ligeti Quartet, released on Gearbox Records, and was named Gilles Peterson's jazz album of the year 2025 and editor’s pick in Downbeat Magazine.\\n\\n--\\n\\nThe drummer, composer, and producer Tom Skinner has been a vital and central figure in London’s underground music scene. He was one of two drummers in Sons of Kemet, the ecstatically militant quartet that turned the fight against British colonial oppression into a brass-band party. And he remains one-third of The Smile, a trio with Thom Yorke and Jonny Greenwood. He has released solo music as Hello Skinny and under his own name.\\n\\n--\\n\\ndove, Christine Kirubi is a poet-artist based in London. She is the author of WILDPLASSEN published by the87press in 2024.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":849,\"name\":\"Algorave // decelerate\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-16T18:45:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-16T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b098ea6fc3a93e6b354df95e8b93c168.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"London? Live? Coding? is hosting OG live coder \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dIpzU71LAQQ\\\"\\u003eAlex McLean\\u003c/a\\u003e (who coined the term ‘algorave’) to collaborate on a new type of party. Depending on how it goes, it could be one of a kind! 🦙\\n\\nIt’s going to be a capital-a Algorave in the truest sense: Live coded dance music and visuals in a dark room with big speakers, with code projected for your pleasure. But in Algorave: decelerate we’re going to constrain the 22+ strong national/international lineup - the performers must play at a pre-specified BPM, with each performance slot decreasing in speed throughout the night. So we’ll start with hyper nosebleed techno from airhorn expert \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ttDQRBQEyBs\\\"\\u003etodepond\\u003c/a\\u003e, and finish locked in to something like tripped-out dubby trance from \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9iPRPIe_PbQ\\\"\\u003edigital selves\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\n\\nSomewhere in there we’ll also have an infiltration from the Sheffield Algorave scene, with \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.nts.live/shows/ashley-plenty-vibes/episodes/ashley-plenty-vibes-9th-august-2026\\\"\\u003eDJ MYNA\\u003c/a\\u003e and \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/live/414h7Vqk2r8?si=49J0K9efxjtFQdVk\\u0026t=22312\\\"\\u003eEpiploke\\u003c/a\\u003e (the latter being Alex’s from-scratch live code duo with Heavy Lifting) coming down from the North’s home of bleep and bassline… Along with \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rpJhDR8XnDo\\\"\\u003ehellocatfood\\u003c/a\\u003e down from Birmingham, \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rFuzW8Qw1oQ\\\"\\u003ePondskater\\u003c/a\\u003e coming from Germany and a whole host of talent from the insurgent London scene. The packed lineup will be kept perfectly to time by a friendly but fair robot. 🤖👍\\n\\nWith techbro accelerationism destroying the world, algorave is one example of humans using handmade code creatively and collectively, with this decelerationist algorave creating a brief opportunity to imagine a different future for ourselves.\\n\\n\\u003cem\\u003e\\\"The scene at an algorave is often what you'd expect from any good techno night - a dark room, engaging visuals. a decent, bass-heavy speaker set-up, and lots of people ready to dance. .. performers at algoraves respond to each other and the audience in real time, often projecting the lines of code onto the walls as they type. lt’s coding as improvisation and experiment..\\\" — The Wire magazine\\u003c/em\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cem\\u003eLive coders write computer programs live, while the programs generate their music, but the focus is on people dancing and seriously enjoying themselves\\\" — Dazed and Confused\\u003c/em\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cem\\u003e\\\".. not so much a revolution as a de-volution, a rolling back to the backend of music production, where the possibilities of the encoded information inside computer software is open and endless\\\" — Mixmag\\u003c/em\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cem\\u003e\\\"... loud, disorientating and brilliant\\\" — The Guardian\\u003c/em\\u003e\\n\\nA collaboration between London? Live? Coding? and the Pattern Clubs of Sheffield and London.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":865,\"name\":\"Klust Music Launch Party: Tomos, Tokomololo, IFAND, SHINOBii + Ani Glass\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-17T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-17T23:55:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4b9866d1f7d4ba96969c827d2f1af0f2.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Klust Music Launch Party featuring live performances from Tokomololo and SHINOBii, alongside DJ sets from Welsh producers Tomos, IFAND and Ani Glass.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://link.dice.fm/r0b8d6173ad0\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":855,\"name\":\"Deptford Junction Presents: The Herons, Tomboy Grandpa, Neighbour Club\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-17T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-17T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f398c8de5c3ddf98ccad09b3f1235d11.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Herons - Franco-Anglo-Uzbek punk trio based in East London. Fresh from European support dates with Witch Post of Partisan Records, they perform in both French and English, bringing a bilingual edge to London’s indie scene.\\n\\nTomboy Grandpa - Scrappy symphonies about gender, romance, \\u0026 being bent in a straight world. They sound a bit like: Tiger Trap, Heavenly, Rilo Kiley, Go Sailor, Talulah Gosh, early MBV, Dressy Bessy, The Spook School, Henry's Dress.\\n\\nNeighbour Club - They are a four piece indie rock band with dual girl / boy vocals. Heavily inspired by Pavement, The Beths and the movie 10 Things I Hate About You.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":873,\"name\":\"The Ivy House Birthday Bash 2026\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-18T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-18T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"93f8db187ac9a765beaaae0b1ff03142.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House is turning 13! To celebrate, we are hosting two very special days of music. On Friday, we will be joined by musical wizards Glass Eel, Sidney Jones and the Murmuration, with special guests Preen headlining the night. It's sure to be a wonderful one. See you there.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":714,\"name\":\"People Drift with RRRKRTA\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-18T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-19T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"eaeb58a2db703dcf19fc667598082b18.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"On September 18th 2026, People Drift is delighted to invite RRRKRTA (clinging vine, hard wax) to Spanners for an all-night session along with DJJJ (people drift).\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2484575\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":872,\"name\":\"The Ivy House Birthday Bash 2026\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-19T17:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Ivy House celebrates 13 years of community ownership with a mega Saturday party!\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":766,\"name\":\"HAKEEM (+ Q\\u0026A and Acoustic Set)\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-19T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"2e75f1c70b49ea91f8ea5e006985a807.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Doc’n Roll is delighted to be part of The Music is Black Festival from East Bank and to bring a special event to the Rio Cinema celebrating one of London’s most distinctive contemporary musicians, Hak Baker. \\n\\nThe evening will include a special screening of Hakeem, live Q\\u0026A, and an intimate acoustic performance by Hak Baker, offering audiences a unique opportunity to hear directly from Hak about his journey, creative process, and the experiences that have shaped his career. \\n\\nHak’s story is one of resilience, creativity, and community, making him an inspiring figure for a new generation of artists and music fans alike. \\n\\nSynopsis \\nAn unconventional music documentary for a very unconventional musician, this film follows British singer and rapper Hak Baker over five years. Directed by the filmmaking duo of DEADHORSES (James Topley and Ivo Beckett), Hakeem balances profundity and profanity as Baker confronts the traumas of class and masculinity in the wake of his sudden stardom. An anarchic yet sincere portrait of British lad culture, full of arresting aesthetics and savage honesty, this is more than a chronicle of a musician's life – it’s a fascinating and intimate portrait of existential angst, brotherhood and hope in the face of the taboos that surround male mental health.\\n\\nThe Music is Black Festival from East Bank at Queen Elizabeth Olympic Park is a celebration of Black British music across a full programme of events including four live festival weekends. Led by the artists, creators and collectives who built its legacy and shape what’s next, this is where sound lives and culture moves.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://riocinema.org.uk/Rio.dll/WhatsOn?f=2652932\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":746,\"name\":\"Sullow \\u0026 Resonant Bodies | David Sappa\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-19T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-19T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1ed6f4e73226f8d37e825b0ee49ec2c4.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sullow are an improvising trio featuring Jacken Elswyth, Daniel S. Evans, and Joshua Barfoot of Shovel Dance Collective. Inflected and informed by the traditional music they mutate within the larger group, they negotiate an improvisation that has been variably described as ‘farmyard’ and ‘rodeo’. By turns scrabbling and sweeping, passing motifs rise and fall in quick attacks, short decays and dense bursts of momentary composition.\\n\\nResonant Bodies is a duo comprising Rob Bentall (nyckelharpa) and Zebedee Budworth (hammered dulcimer), who met playing in processional folk-horror ensemble Slug Milk sometime in 2017. They also now also help to coordinate the minimalist free-folk project Emergence Collective. As a duo they seek routes into a free-flowing, improvised folk music via the raw, tonal harmonies of their ancient instruments.\\n\\nLast autumn Resonant Bodies, Jacken, and Josh played a mini-tour together and spent a day recording an album soon to be released as part of the Unfiter series. For this micro-tour a full-strength Sullow and Resonant Bodies will perform together, to explore the tensions and affinities between their contrasting approaches to free-folk. \\n\\n--\\n\\nDavid Sappa is an experimental musician working through kinetic sound objects \\u0026 improvisational environments, field recording + extended listening practices\\n\\nThey’re interested in sound for its tactile, textural and somatic qualities, and as modes for interrelatedness and interplay that can explore dynamics between our social, psychological and material entanglements within different environments.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":717,\"name\":\"free movements ~ equinox \",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-20T14:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"b19d41161a33a1868076374fcd17b20b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"more info soon \\u003c3\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":785,\"name\":\"Dave Bixby, live in London\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-20T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"8a84a011f16933297cee0556b933e908.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"life is beautiful records presents the final EU/UK tour for the legendary US folk artist Dave Bixby, known for his acclaimed 1969 album 'Ode to Quetzalcoatl', which garnered him a cult following amongst vinyl collectors and outsider folk aficionados. \\n\\nthe London date of this tour will be the final concert of this tour, Live at St Giles, Camberwell on the 20th September 2026.\\n\\npreluding Bixby's performance will be 'orchestra379', a collective improvisation project, with a fluctuating lineup for each occasion, curated by artist \\u0026 founder of life is beautiful, aloisius. this iteration of orchestra379 shall be specifically curated in honour fittingly for the opening for Dave Bixby's final London show.\\n\\nsoundtracking before \\u0026 between the live performances, will be Zakia Sewell, known for their NTS \\u0026 BBC Radio 6 shows, such as 'Questing' \\u0026 'Dream Time'.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":890,\"name\":\"Everybody to Kenmure Street - Community Screening with Lewisham Anti Raids\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-21T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-21T21:26:00Z\",\"poster\":\"22a11b48a4885b45675a09396fdfd67c.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In May 2021, a UK Home Office dawn raid triggers one of the most spontaneous and successful acts of civil resistance in recent memory. In Pollokshields, Scotland’s most diverse neighbourhood, hundreds of residents rush to the streets to stop the deportation of their neighbours. In today’s increasingly far-right political environment of immigration raids, deportation flights and border violence, Everybody to Kenmure Street is an empowering reminder of the importance of collective action.\\n\\n \\n\\nThe screening will be followed by a casual chat with Lewisham Anti Raids @lewisham_anti_raids on the organising they do in the area, and how you can get involved.\\n\\n \\n\\nAll are welcome, no matter your organising experience! The film is rated 12A.\\n\\n \\n\\nPay What You Can tickets are available from £1-8. This event is part of a series of community screenings around London with local anti raids groups, organised by april forrest lin 林森. All ticket revenue will be donated to Lewisham Anti Raids after event costs have been covered.\\n\\n \\n\\n18:30 - Doors open\\n\\n19:00 - Film screening\\n\\n20:45 - Chat with Lewisham Anti Raids\\n\\n21:00 - Chat ends, space stays open\\n\\n21:30 - Event ends\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38278/everybody-to-kenmure-street-community-screening-with-lewisham-anti-raids\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":846,\"name\":\"The PGs + Gem Stark\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-22T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-22T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0a29434e4cac0b36dcb54ab15b16cc7b.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands is back. New music at your favourite community owned pub. This week from The PGs and Gem Stark.\\n\\nThe PGs are local singers Mary Currie and Alison Craig and musicians Marcus Holdaway, Nick Haeffner. Together they will be playing a selection from Mary, and Gareth Williams’ ( “This Heat”) iconic album from the eighties “Flaming Tunes.” Along with some of their own kickin’songs.\\n\\nGem Stark is a folksinger from the North-West of England now situated in South-East London influenced by Only Connect questions and other such nonsense she doesn’t quite understand. With an antsy fingerstyle guitar and quivering voice, too restless for the country but too lackadaisical for the city, her sincere sensibilities are especially meaningful to anyone that has cried to the hum of a PAT-failed lamp in a second-hand bookshop within a 30-mile radius of the Peak District.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":885,\"name\":\"Ray Laurél - 'Neptune Rising' Private Listening Party\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-25T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-25T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f518178c1a542748280a1e1effc2f2bd.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A night hosted by Ray Laurél — a first play-through of his upcoming record, Neptune Rising, on Shai Space's custom hi-fi Soundsystem. Herbal teas provided, BYOB.\\n\\nDoors at 7pm\\nMusic for Lovers - Playback at 8:15pm\\nNeptune Rising - Playback at 9:15pm\\nEnds 10pm\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":788,\"name\":\"Curbside Lambsear | Stamp Rack | C.Y Charisse\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-25T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-25T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ac566a3ae97948823b07d8059acbe3f9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Curbside Lambsear explore rough textures and soft intentions, weaving together elements of pop, folk, and improvisation with influences of drone, dub, and post-punk. With a set from Stamp Rack (Daniel S. Evans and Mike O’Malley) and a DJ set from C.Y Charisse.\\n\\n-- \\n\\nCurbside Lambsear is Annabelle Mödlinger and Magdalena McLean. The collaboration explores rough textures and soft intentions, weaving together elements of pop, folk, and improvisation with influences of drone, dub, and post-punk. \\n\\nThe project began as a way for Magdalena and Annabelle to experiment with writing music together, using early sessions to learn new instruments, the process of recording and writing on DAWs. \\n\\nTheir musical output is the result of time spent together in the studio fusing disparate influences into collage; phone notes, little poems written on public transport, field recordings, sample loops, rehearsal voice memos and string melodies merge, realign, and sometimes coalesce into songs.\\n\\n-- \\n\\nStamp Rack is a duo of Mike O’Malley and Daniel S. Evans. \\n\\nMike O’Malley is a guitarist and producer based in London, best known for his work as part of the band caroline.\\n\\nDaniel S. Evans is a multi-instrumentalist and producer based in London. He plays as part of the experimental folk groups Shovel Dance Collective, Sullow, and The Greater London Banjo Trio, and as Meanders in a duo with Jasper Llewellyn.\\n\\n-- \\n\\nC.Y CHARISSE is a London-based music archivist. Working with forgotten records, field recordings, and damaged media, her hybrid DJ sets excavate musical histories, reconstructing fractured identities through the sonic languages of dub, drone, and noise.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":700,\"name\":\"FANTASY STATE\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-25T22:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-26T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"4f770787b2566fea95ad9a0ad0045257.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"FANTASY STATE is a queer club for euphoric dance music.\\n\\nFor one night only ;)\\n\\nExpect a sweaty \\u0026 sexy dance floor xxx\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":871,\"name\":\"FLOORJAM 008 with MoMA Ready, LORA S, Ellaweez, Ki Pharaoh \\u0026 Damsel\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-25T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-26T05:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"7998a06d2240f03dc72f09dc48c276e3.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"FLOORJAM is back with a blazing line up featuring some of the most exciting names in electronic music.\\n\\nOur eight party in the series sees NY-based stalwart MoMA Ready joins us bringing his brilliant take all facets of Black electronic music to the Bermondsey hub that is Ormside Projects.\\n\\nEllaweez joins hot off the back of supporting DJ Bone on his EU tour, alongside London favourite Ki Pharaoh of WA.dgtl and FLOORJAM residents Lora S and Damsel.\\n\\nWe're excited to reconvene with our growing community of dancers.\\n\\n\\\"For the dancers, for the shakers, for the groovers, for the 4am crew. Euphoric cuts on the dancefloor for yours truly.\\\"\\n\\nBY US, FOR US ALL\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://ra.co/events/2499928\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":581,\"name\":\"Silhouettes Project\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-27T13:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-27T21:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1d81eeed1af011e974e83afbd5cfaab9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Silhouettes Project is landing at the Fox \\u0026 Firkin.\\n\\nDisrupting the norms of traditional genre and collaborative music-making processes, The Silhouettes Project is a musical collective in the heart of East London’s thriving cultural scene. Masterminded by Jaden Osei-Bonsu (Eerf Evil) and Asher Korner (Asher Kosher), the collective’s Hackney studio and creative hub has become a vital space for artists to connect and create, creating a new blueprint for community, alternative industry structures, and developing top-level talent across the creative arts.  Established through Root 73, a non-profit arts organisation that has quickly morphed into a recording studio, record label and an apprenticeship scheme for young people searching for experience in the industry, The Silhouettes Project’s testament to community, youth and the empowerment of rising voices remains as steady as the rhythms coursing through the music.  Their pioneering, self-sustaining ecosystem has become a notable success story, birthing the beautiful, innovative material that made up their debut album The Silhouettes Project Vol. I. Championing some of the most exciting talents across the UK including ENNY, Bel Cobain, Nix Northwest, Lex Amor and 30 more artists, rappers and producers, the collective earned well over 50M+ streams, critical acclaim across the likes of  The Guardian, Highsnobriety and Clash, and went on to perform Glastonbury and other festivals across Europe.\\n\\nSupported by a grassroots music grant from Arts Council England, helping us continue to champion emerging artists and live music in the community.  All events support Lewisham Donation Hub, a local charity providing vital support to those facing acute hardship across South East London.  The largest pub garden in SE London will have street food, drinks, and a laid-back summer atmosphere. Families are welcome, with free entry for children, market stalls, and activities to keep little ones entertained.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":767,\"name\":\"perspectives•\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-27T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ede9e432a7584508a6d6f6e3c6f95a14.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"𝚘𝚗 𝚜𝚞𝚗𝚍𝚊𝚢 𝟸𝟽𝚝𝚑 𝚜𝚎𝚙𝚝𝚎𝚖𝚋𝚎𝚛, 𝚙𝚎𝚛𝚜𝚙𝚎𝚌𝚝𝚒𝚟𝚎𝚜• 𝚙𝚛𝚎𝚜𝚎𝚗𝚝𝚜 𝚊 𝚍𝚊𝚢𝚝𝚒𝚖𝚎 𝚊𝚞𝚍𝚒𝚘-𝚟𝚒𝚜𝚞𝚊𝚕 𝚎𝚡𝚙𝚎𝚛𝚒𝚎𝚗𝚌𝚎 𝚊𝚝 𝚌𝚕𝚞𝚋 𝚌𝚑𝚎𝚎𝚔, 𝚋𝚛𝚒𝚡𝚝𝚘𝚗.\\n\\n𝚙𝚎𝚛𝚜𝚙𝚎𝚌𝚝𝚒𝚟𝚎𝚜• 𝚖𝚘𝚟𝚎𝚜 𝚋𝚎𝚢𝚘𝚗𝚍 𝚝𝚑𝚎 𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚟𝚎𝚗𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚊𝚕 𝚍𝚊𝚗𝚌𝚎𝚏𝚕𝚘𝚘𝚛, 𝚌𝚘𝚖𝚋𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚒𝚖𝚖𝚎𝚛𝚜𝚒𝚟𝚎 𝚜𝚙𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚊𝚕 𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚒𝚐𝚗 𝚠𝚒𝚝𝚑 𝚏𝚘𝚛𝚠𝚊𝚛𝚍-𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚔𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚜𝚘𝚞𝚗𝚍 𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚒𝚐𝚗𝚜 𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚕𝚒𝚟𝚎 𝚎𝚡𝚙𝚎𝚛𝚒𝚎𝚗𝚌𝚎𝚜, 𝚏𝚎𝚊𝚝𝚞𝚛𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚍𝚎𝚋𝚞𝚝 𝚙𝚎𝚛𝚏𝚘𝚛𝚖𝚊𝚗𝚌𝚎𝚜 𝚏𝚛𝚘𝚖 𝚒𝚗𝚝𝚎𝚛𝚗𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚊𝚕 𝚕𝚒𝚟𝚎 𝚊𝚛𝚝𝚒𝚜𝚝𝚜 𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚊 𝚌𝚞𝚜𝚝𝚘𝚖 𝚕𝚒𝚐𝚑𝚝𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚒𝚗𝚜𝚝𝚊𝚕𝚕𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗.\\n\\n𝚠𝚎 𝚠𝚒𝚕𝚕 𝚋𝚎 𝚓𝚘𝚒𝚗𝚎𝚍 𝚋𝚢 𝚝𝚑𝚎 𝚏𝚘𝚕𝚕𝚘𝚠𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚊𝚛𝚝𝚒𝚜𝚝𝚜:\\n\\n• 𝚝𝚎𝚖𝚙𝚕𝚎 𝚛𝚊𝚝 [𝚕𝚒𝚟𝚎]\\n• 𝚏𝚘𝚛𝚎𝚜𝚝\\n• 𝚊𝚕𝚒𝚌𝚒𝚊\\n• 𝚎𝚗𝚊 𝚋. [𝚕𝚒𝚟𝚎]\\n• 𝙰𝙽𝙽𝚇 \\n\\n𝚠𝚒𝚝𝚑 𝚕𝚒𝚐𝚑𝚝𝚒𝚗𝚐 \\u0026 𝚜𝚙𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚊𝚕 𝚍𝚎𝚜𝚒𝚐𝚗 𝚋𝚢 𝚖𝚎𝚝𝚊𝚕 𝚞𝚙𝚊, 𝚗𝚒𝚌𝚘𝚕𝚎 𝚐𝚘𝚛𝚍𝚘𝚗 + 𝚜𝚎𝚊 𝚑𝚘\\n\\n𝚊𝚛𝚝𝚠𝚘𝚛𝚔 𝚋𝚢 @𝚍𝚎𝚎𝚋_𝚊𝚑 •\\n\\n𝚙𝚎𝚛𝚜𝚙𝚎𝚌𝚝𝚒𝚟𝚎𝚜• 𝚒𝚜 𝚜𝚞𝚙𝚙𝚘𝚛𝚝𝚎𝚍 𝚋𝚢 𝚝𝚑𝚎 𝚎𝚊𝚛𝚕𝚢 𝚌𝚊𝚛𝚎𝚎𝚛 𝚙𝚛𝚘𝚖𝚘𝚝𝚎𝚛 𝚏𝚞𝚗𝚍 𝚠𝚑𝚒𝚌𝚑 𝚒𝚜 𝚖𝚊𝚗𝚊𝚐𝚎𝚍 𝚋𝚢 𝚙𝚛𝚜 𝚏𝚘𝚞𝚗𝚍𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗 𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚏𝚞𝚗𝚍𝚎𝚍 𝚋𝚢 𝚊𝚛𝚝𝚜 𝚌𝚘𝚞𝚗𝚌𝚒𝚕 𝚎𝚗𝚐𝚕𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚞𝚜𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚜𝚞𝚙𝚙𝚘𝚛𝚝𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚐𝚛𝚊𝚜𝚜𝚛𝚘𝚘𝚝𝚜 𝚖𝚞𝚜𝚒𝚌 𝚏𝚞𝚗𝚍𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚏𝚛𝚘𝚖 𝚍𝚌𝚖𝚜.\\n\\n𝚌𝚞𝚛𝚊𝚝𝚎𝚍 𝚋𝚢 𝚊𝚗𝚗𝚡 𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚗𝚒𝚌𝚘𝚕𝚎 𝚐𝚘𝚛𝚍𝚘𝚗.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":715,\"name\":\"People Drift\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-03T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-04T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":893,\"name\":\"Out Of Body Pop 10\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-04T12:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-04T20:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"014fdb46115745d154d6232613ab5481.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Our 10th party is here!\\n\\nWe ran oobp1 on 13.09.2020 - a time when we couldn't dance, but we could still paint and be together. \\n\\nWe have kept working to make a day party that gives our people what they want. Gathering a wide variety of feedback, bringing elements in and out, finessing an event format that we call ‘neuro-inclusive’.\\n\\nAt oobp10 you will have the freedom to move between distinct spaces, with distinct activities. \\nBetween loudness and quietness. \\nBetween dark walls covered in projections and bright walls that you decorate with our free art materials.\\nDrink drinks.\\nEat pizza. \\nLet your creativity flow with our paintbrushes, or follow the meditative process of knotting paracord. \\nExist between the space, the street, and the canal (we allow re-entry).\\n\\nThe dancefloor will host DJs who have kept oobp alive over the years, not least Don Sinini, our resident wavey emo dancehall don, and Will Soer aka dj dyspraxic/ \\\"dis swag’s sick!\\\", our founder (he did the first oobp radio show on 18.10.2016). \\n\\nWe will also have 2 x dj+dj pairs coming over from 2 other events that we love...\\n...from The Surfers Club we've got PrettyBoyRio+Raidaa, bringing neo soul, uptempo r’n’b, hip hop, inviting us to ride the wave...\\n...from Bodyswap we have Harietta+Eli La Nuit, bringing Dancey Synths’n’more from Dalston Superstore, where they play futurist music (and oobp pillars) from Frank Ocean to Sophie.\\n\\nCome and find your flow.\\n\\n...\\n\\n\\nWHAT YOU CAN EXPECT\\n\\n(the link for our venue map and Instagram account is at the bottom of this page)\\n\\n1. a low-lit indoor Dancefloor with DJ sets, projected visuals and no flashing lights. Each set has a distinct sonic theme, see set times above!\\n\\n2. a covered, outdoor Painting + Social Area paints and art tools provided for everyone, plus the guided, meditative sensory activity of knotting\\n\\n3. a bar with alcohol and non-alc options, plus pizza on sale inside the venue (inc vegan options) until 18:00\\n\\n4. from 15:00 onwards we will have a Quiet area in the HWK cafe space, where you can paint or use one of our colouring-in books without conversation\\n\\n5. re-entry is allowed all day\\nHWK is 5 mins walk from the canal, if you want to literally touch grass then walk past Barge East\\nwe're also 10 mins walk from the V\\u0026A storehouse which is free and very cool\\n\\n6. genderless toilets and no-tolerance of harassment - we ask that you respect each other's space and think about those around you, especially if you’re a big guy with a loud voice like our founder Will!\\n\\n7. any profits from the event will go to Arts Emergency, a charity that helps young people from underprivileged backgrounds get into the arts\\n\\n…\\n\\nWe want to actively include people, and build a more ideal space for everyone, together.\\n\\nBeing neuro-inclusive doesn't mean that we're only focused on serving neurodivergent people or that we are fully accessible for everyone, but we will always work to improve the accessibility of OOBP in attainable ways as we develop. For a more deeply accessible, differentiated experience, we'd recommend checking out Disco Neurotico (for example, they run events with silent disco technology to avoid sensory overwhelm on the dancefloor)\\n\\nIf you have any questions for us in the runnup to the event, please message our @outofbodypop instagram account.\\n\\nOur music policy is wide but specific; we want to look forwards, exploring experimental but accessible sounds, music that’s fun and interesting, which you don’t tend to hear in clubs. Syncopated rhythms and big chords in all sorts of different forms.\\n\\nWe will be offering free paints and art tools for everyone to use, including a mix of white and pastel-coloured paper.\\n\\nWe are happy for you to take photos or videos, there will be lots of cute visual things to look at! We just ask that you keep it within reason (especially on the dancefloor) and the OOBP team will do the same; we have team members who we know are happy to be filmed, we won’t stand around at the side of the dancefloor filming everyone else or get up in their face with a DSLR when they’re dancing.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":882,\"name\":\"Sienna Melella + antematterz\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-06T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-06T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"eac2156ed30293d347886ae6300050d7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Lands returns to The Ivy House with Sienna Mellella + antematterz.\\nSienna Melella, singer-songwriter, London.\\nantematterz is the solo project of Lucas Souza, who began releasing music under this name in November 2020. Since then, the artist has been building a solid and coherent career, which also involved co-creating the band roadkill, a project that allowed him to explore new creative dynamics and mature as a musician.\\nOver the past six years, antematterz has dedicated his time to developing his second album, Giving up The Blade, a work that reflects this artistic evolution and where the influences that shape his sound identity are clearly audible, from Bright Eyes to Death Cab for Cutie, passing through the vocal melodies of Big Thief. The result is a sound that crosses the intimacy of Indie Folk with electronic elements, transporting us to an introspective and emotional universe, built with time and intention.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":883,\"name\":\"LOAM 002\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-08T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-08T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"LOAM 002\\nDATE: 08.10.2026\\nTIME: 18:30 - 23:30\\nLOCATION: Autumn Three, 39 Autumn Street, E3 2TT, London\\n\\nLOAM is an intimate listening space for dense, organic, and experimental sound. Practice over status. Raw collaboration.\\n\\nThe name comes from fertile soil - richness through mixture, not purity.\\n\\nThe ground held. This is what grows from it - five artists move through one continuous evening: dense and organic ambient, downtempo, experimental, IDM, deconstructed club, (and a live cello performance???).\\n\\nLow lighting. Floor cushions and seating alongside standing space close to the sound. No correct place to be.\\n\\nLineup (A-Z): \\n\\nTickets Info:\\nEarly Bird: £10 \\nGeneral Admission: £15\\nOnline only\\nAll proceedings are equally split between the invited artists\\n\\nSnacks and drinks available at the bar.\\n\\nCome early, stay close to the sound.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":821,\"name\":\"DEAFKIDS, KOMBI \\u0026 Brava | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-20T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-20T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"40fa064f491d9acbeae4b5fe7b8bcec7.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"New Cross Live Presents\\n\\nDeaf Kids\\nBrazilian legends blending the raw spirit of noise punk, global rhythms and experimental electronics into a sonic assault since 2010. Armed with a brand new album 'Cicatrizes Do Futuro' they're here to shake London to the ground.\\n\\nKombi\\nAmbient drones by Joao of TEST\\n\\nBrava\\nOutsider house music with a hardcore MC, LDN via San Sebastian\\n\\nTuesday 20th October\\nNew Cross Inn, Nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\nDoors 6pm\\n£17\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/deaf-kids\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":847,\"name\":\"The TEJ Quartet + arps \\u0026 Big Oil\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-20T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-20T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"71b995c7e8d869e23928bcf0c5ec977a.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An entirely instrumental special edition of New Lands! \\n\\nThe TEJ Quartet is built around the idiosyncratic and hypnozting guitar work of Toby Evans-Jesra (Lobby, Leather.head, Piglet). He is joined by three incredible guitarists who symphonise and explore every sonic space between quiet and loud, between jarring and joy. \\n\\nAlso performing will be arps \\u0026 Big Oil, who will be debuting a very special live collaboration, merging arps' lush, ambient, amphibian-infused dreamscapes and Big Oil's primitive-inspired fingerpicked guitar.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":737,\"name\":\"Nerorgasmo - Italian Legends in London | Real Life X Cryptic Growth\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-23T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-23T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"ba14d750ba261a48f91d00cb7f7f90a0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life, Cryptic Growth and Backstage Hand Clinic Present\\n\\nNerorgasmo\\nLegendary Italian hardcore punk, in London for the first time.\\n\\n+ supports coming soon\\n\\nFriday 23rd October\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate \\u0026 New Cross\\nDoors 6pm\\n£15\\n14+, u18s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/nerorgasmo\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":895,\"name\":\"Chunt1685\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-24T23:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-25T06:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f40ae44dab9ec3a3e740057a901aa3e1.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Choat\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":854,\"name\":\"Kaleidoscopic\",\"start_time\":\"2026-10-29T07:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-10-29T11:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"69cbcdf7e4c7862fef6edb8cd121d670.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Each distinctive, creative, and unique, Afromerm, Lara Aisha, and Phoebe Massey will bless your ears with their experimental electronic sounds. \",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":837,\"name\":\"Sheer Terror \\u0026 The Drowns | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-02T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-02T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"d93c0cd356df23db905f9ff3f27a0e69.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Sheer Terror\\nNew York Hardcore legends bringing their first new music in 10 years to South-East London! Mosh it up.\\n\\nThe Drowns\\nSeattle street punks\\n\\n+ Support coming soon\\n\\nMonday 2nd November\\n£23\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\nDoors 6pm\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/sheer-terror-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":848,\"name\":\"Dead Slow Hoot + On? \",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-03T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-03T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"136521ca09900f206bbc823f7945a9d9.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Dead Slow Hoot and On? take the stage for another special New Lands night.\\n\\nDead Slow Hoot is a left of the dial indie rock quartet taking influence from bands like Wilco, Built To Spill and Big Thief - tender songs that take unexpected turns, tight but loose.\\n\\nThey're joined by On?, feauring members of Duds, Humint and Plastic Gift, drawing on inspiration by way of The Cars, Thin Lizzy and Weezer.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":640,\"name\":\"lagrimas | Real Life x South London Scum\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-09T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-09T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"f41a4b1549adf300f87438aaf7bba2db.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life \\u0026 South London Scum Present\\n\\nLagrimas\\nIn the UK for the first time, SoCal screamo punks taking filthy crust from basements to the world.\\n\\n+ Support from\\nCassus\\nUK skramz legends\\n\\nHemiptera\\nMelodic crust with strings\\n\\nSevy Verna\\nThe new wave of UK screamo\\n\\nMonday 9th November\\n£14\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n\\nDoors 6pm, 14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/lagrimas\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":877,\"name\":\"Poison Ruin | Real Life Presents - Grim winter punks\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-11T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-11T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6d9ef84d524fc1185a2930922d2fc789.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nPoison Ruin\\nGrim and wintery Philadelphia punks, returning with new album 'Hymns From The Hills'\\n\\n+ Supports coming soon...\\n\\nWednesday 11th November\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\nDoors 6pm\\n£17\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/poison-ruin\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":586,\"name\":\"Babe Haven \\u0026 Latter | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-15T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-15T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3f91523e1b1f0aec4db9931c08ed98e0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nBabe Haven\\nNew icons of thrashy queer-punk nu-metal anthems\\n\\nLatter\\nHeavy-hearted Chicago noise punk\\n\\n+ support coming soon\\n\\nSunday 15th November\\nNew Cross Inn\\n£15\\nDoors 6pm\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/babe-haven-latter\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":507,\"name\":\"The S.E.T. | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-16T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-16T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"274a7650c8d3015cdfb2544064b7dde0.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nThe S.E.T.\\nBaltimore heavy hardcore ft. Che of Flatspot Records and Ryan from End It!, righteous fury from hardcore for the truth. Putting words into action and mobilising our community.\\n\\n+ UKHC support tba\\n\\n\\nMonday 16th November\\nNew Cross Inn\\nDoors 6pm\\n£16\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/the-set\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":477,\"name\":\"Real Life Presents - Moral Law | Straightedge Metalcore\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-23T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-23T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"97b43a46a58461d312057a8d767c076d.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nMoral Law\\nStraight edge mosh warriors on New Age Records\\n\\n+ support from\\nRebel\\nKent hardcore\\n\\n\\u0026 more UKHC coming soon...\\n\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\nDoors 6pm\\n£11\\n\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/moral-law\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":739,\"name\":\"Sunday Best | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-27T19:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"80f7e68070c0d8e887369401b447afe8.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nSunday Best\\nUnderground London Emo-punks. \\\"Cleopatra, In A Past Life\\\" out now.\\n\\nA very special headline set from some of our closest friends. More news (including some incredible supports) coming soon...\\n\\nFriday November 27th\\nSebright Arms, nearest stations Bethnal Green and Cambridge Heath\\n£10\\nDoors 7pm\\n18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/sunday-best-2\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":738,\"name\":\"Restraining Order | Real Life Presents\",\"start_time\":\"2026-11-30T18:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-11-30T22:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"780df81d385ce882f2214064450d0609.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"Real Life Presents\\n\\nRestraining Order\\nFast-stomping, side-to-side, Massachusetts hardcore. \\n\\nClobber\\nLondon's most massive\\n\\nAku\\nBN1 side-to-side crew\\n\\nBullet\\nNew New Wave Of UKHC\\n\\nMonday 30th November\\nNew Cross Inn, nearest stations New Cross Gate and New Cross\\n£15\\nDoors 6pm\\n14+, u16s with an adult 18+\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://pit.live/events/restraining-order-1\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":770,\"name\":\"Discus Music Residency January 2027 - RIGHT HERE RIGHT NOW\",\"start_time\":\"2027-01-17T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2027-01-17T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"0cfc0499abf3846d15c2ce4e1aa72787.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Discus Music residency at the Horse Hospital, Colonnade WC1N 1JD, takes place on the third Sunday of each month throughout 2027, and rotates between three artists on the label:  Hi Res Heart, Right Here Right Now and The Martin Pyne Ensemble.\\n\\nThe venue is fully seated.\\n\\nSUNDAY 17th JANUARY 2027 – DOORS 7.30 PM\\nRIGHT HERE RIGHT NOW \\n\\nCharlotte Keeffe – trumpet\\nAshley John Long - double bass\\nBen Handysides – drums \\nMoss Freed – guitar\\n\\nDescribed by Jazzwise as \\\"avant-garde for all,\\\" Charlotte Keeffe’s Music-making is a vibrant tapestry of textures and gestures, inspired by everything, everywhere, and everyone. Keeffe’s passionate approach to free improvisation invites listeners into a raw, expressive world where anything is possible… \\n\\nHer trumpets are Sound Brushes - painting bold sonic landscapes alongside her musical brothers, Ashley John Long on double bass, Ben Handysides on drums and Moss Freed on guitar, forging a rich breeding ground for Musical liberation.\\n\\n\\\"The radical spirit of offhand precarity frequently bubbles over into an effervescent sense of the imperative to explore. In a word? Fearless.\\\" - PRESTO MUSIC\\n\\n\\\"A messy emporium of raw, raucous realness. Alive.” Keeffe and her quartet nailed it.\\\" - Sammy Stein, FREE JAZZ BLOG\\n\\n\\\"Charlotte Keeffe is rapidly developing a reputation as one of UK’s finest improvisers.\\\" - Tony Dudley-Evans\\n\\nDiscus Music: discusmusic.bandcamp.com / discus-music.org\\nWe are a large Sheffield based independent label for creative music with over 200 CD/DL releases, curated by Martin Archer. As well as the residency group leaders Martin Archer, Charlotte Keeffe and Martin Pyne, artists on the label include Keith Tippett, Julie Tippetts, Paul Dunmall, Cecil Taylor, Tony Oxley, Pat Thomas, Laura Cole, Let Spin, Das Rad, Orchestra Of The Upper Atmosphere, Uroboro, Stephen Grew, Guy Segers, Corey Mwamba, Robert Mitchell, Alya Al-Sultani, Inclusion Principle, Johnny Hunter, Mick Beck, Billy Marrows, Jan Todd / frostlake, Faith Brackenbury, Tony Bianco, The Exu, Faradena Afifi, Steve Beresford, Paul Khimasia Morgan, Laura Jurd, Keir Cooper, Ron Caines, Matthew Bourne, Chris Sharkey, Carla Diratz, Theo May, Paul Taylor, This Celestial Engine, Fjall, Walt Shaw, Steve Tromans, Rachel Musson, Mark Sanders, James Mainwaring, Ricard Scott, Army Of Briars, Nick Robonson, Michael Bardon, Bo Meson, Juxtavoices, Alex Ward and many more.\\n\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":771,\"name\":\"Discus Music Residency February 2027 – MARTIN PYNE TRIO\",\"start_time\":\"2027-02-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2027-02-21T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"1b7b1209a04fd72599f38a8073cd2884.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Discus Music residency at the Horse Hospital, Colonnade WC1N 1JD, takes place on the third Sunday of each month throughout 2027, and rotates between three artists on the label:  Hi Res Heart, Right Here Right Now and The Martin Pyne Ensemble.\\n\\nThe venue is fully seated.\\n\\nSUNDAY 21st FEBRUARY 2027 – DOORS 7.30 PM\\nMARTIN PYNE'S CHALK HORSES TRIO\\n\\nMartin Pyne – vibraphone / balafon\\nDavid Beebee – electric piano\\nAngus Bishop - drums\\n\\n+ SUPPORT\\nJosephine Davies – solo saxophone \\n\\nCHALK HORSES TRIO came together to record music which featured on half of Martin Pyne’s new double album TRIOS (Discus). This represents the latest stage in a journey exploring the intersecting sonorities of vibraphone and rhodes piano, which began on Pyne and Beebee’s duo album Ripples, and continued on The Act Of Noticing where they were joined by saxophonist Josephine Davies to form the trio Espial.\\n\\nTonight Josephine will open the evening with a short solo set before joining the trio for the second part of their performance. \\n\\nExpect lush impressionism, dark atmospheres, lyrical melodies, intricate textures and intoxicating grooves. \\n\\n“Just gorgeous, pure music. Softly, as in a morning sunrise.” – Darren Bergstein, Downtown Music Gallery NYC\\nReviewing Ripples\\n\\n“Debussy was creating elements of modern jazz decades before it emerged and if he were alive today, one could imagine this is the kind of combo he might put together.” – Dominic Rivron, INTERNATIONAL TIMES”\\nReviewing The Act Of Noticing\\n\\n\\nDiscus Music: discusmusic.bandcamp.com / discus-music.org\\n\\nWe are a large Sheffield based independent label for creative music with over 200 CD/DL releases, curated by Martin Archer. As well as the residency group leaders Martin Archer, Charlotte Keeffe and Martin Pyne, artists on the label include Keith Tippett, Julie Tippetts, Paul Dunmall, Cecil Taylor, Tony Oxley, Pat Thomas, Laura Cole, Let Spin, Das Rad, Orchestra Of The Upper Atmosphere, Uroboro, Stephen Grew, Guy Segers, Corey Mwamba, Robert Mitchell, Alya Al-Sultani, Inclusion Principle, Johnny Hunter, Mick Beck, Billy Marrows, Jan Todd / frostlake, Faith Brackenbury, Tony Bianco, The Exu, Faradena Afifi, Steve Beresford, Paul Khimasia Morgan, Laura Jurd, Keir Cooper, Ron Caines, Matthew Bourne, Chris Sharkey, Carla Diratz, Theo May, Paul Taylor, This Celestial Engine, Fjall, Walt Shaw, Steve Tromans, Rachel Musson, Mark Sanders, James Mainwaring, Ricard Scott, Army Of Briars, Nick Robinson, Michael Bardon, Bo Meson, Juxtavoices, Alex Ward and many more.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":731,\"name\":\"Discus Music Residency March 2027 - HI RES HEART\",\"start_time\":\"2027-03-21T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2027-03-21T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"6430a3e5d75c60319297da2dbd32acdc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"The Discus Music residency at the Horse Hospital, Colonnade WC1N 1JD takes place on the third Sunday of each month throughout 2027, and rotates between three artists on the label:  Hi Res Heart, Right Here Right Now and The Martin Pyne Ensemble. The venue is fully seated.\\n\\nSUNDAY 21st MARCH 2027 – DOORS 7.30 PM\\nHI RES HEART\\nMartin Archer – saxophones\\nCharlotte Keeffe – trumpet\\nGraham Clark – violin\\nMichael Bardon – double bass\\nMartin Pyne – drums, vibraphone\\nMelanie Little – dance\\n\\nHi Res Heart is an improvising group where spaciousness and fire co-exist. Even when the music is at its most abstract, the spirit of the blues is never too far away. The music is often direct and melodic in an open ended flow which reacts to the moment, while the unusual percussion set up of drum set, hand percussion and vibraphone provides an ever changing textural and rhythmic counterpoint. For this performance we are joined, as we are whenever space and budget permit, by the creative dance of Melanie Little.\\n\\n\\\"This is resolutely experimental jazz inventiveness, with room left for each musician's creativity.\\\" - Guy Stuckens RADIO AIR LIBRE\\n\\n\\\"There are too many highlights to mention. It may have its roots in the music of 70s Chicago, but it’s superfluous to know this: Hi Res Heart transcend them to create a music of their own that is very much of the 2020s. I could listen to this music all day.\\\" - Dominic Rivron, INTERNATIONAL TIMES\\n\\n\\\"Will have all your senses on full alert.\\\" - PAULA MCADAM\\n\\n\\\"Superb examples of what the group can do without charts in front of them. Fans of free jazz and free improvisation will find plenty to get excited about.\\\" - Peter Thelen, EXPOSÉ\\n\\n\\\"Wild, florid and fantastic in its scope; a must for all those seeking adventure.\\\" - Mr Olivetti, FREQ\\n\\n\\\"Seven meticulously crafted plays, each as captivating as the last, each with its own unique character.\\\" - Marie Mesmer, HIGHLANDS\\n\\n+ SUPPORT\\n\\nDiscus Music: discusmusic.bandcamp.com / discus-music.org\\n\\nWe are a large Sheffield based independent label for creative music with over 200 CD/DL releases, curated by Martin Archer. As well as the residency group leaders Martin Archer, Charlotte Keeffe and Martin Pyne, artists on the label include Keith Tippett, Julie Tippetts, Paul Dunmall, Cecil Taylor, Tony Oxley, Pat Thomas, Laura Cole, Let Spin, Das Rad, Orchestra Of The Upper Atmosphere, Uroboro, Stephen Grew, Guy Segers, Corey Mwamba, Robert Mitchell, Alya Al-Sultani, Inclusion Principle, Johnny Hunter, Mick Beck, Billy Marrows, Jan Todd / frostlake, Faith Brackenbury, Tony Bianco, The Exu, Faradena Afifi, Steve Beresford, Paul Khimasia Morgan, Laura Jurd, Keir Cooper, Ron Caines, Matthew Bourne, Chris Sharkey, Carla Diratz, Theo May, Paul Taylor, This Celestial Engine, Fjall, Walt Shaw, Steve Tromans, Rachel Musson, Mark Sanders, James Mainwaring, Ricard Scott, Army Of Briars, Nick Robonson, Michael Bardon, Bo Meson, Juxtavoices, Alex Ward and many more.\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":206,\"name\":\"test\",\"start_time\":\"2027-07-09T09:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2028-06-07T09:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":331,\"name\":\"test event - resale queue\",\"start_time\":\"9999-01-01T09:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"9999-10-10T09:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"gel admins only\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":false,\"is_on_listings_site\":false,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":true,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}]",
