/74c79cf7e27bfef8b2935bb159b46c45.webp\" alt=\"Awaiting Home: Opening Night and exhibition\" class=\"w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover\"> </div> <!-- Event header -->  <div class=\"flex items-start gap-2 mb-2\"> <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-surface-900\">Awaiting Home: Opening Night and exhibition</h1>  </div> <p class=\"text-surface-600 mb-4\"> Friday, July 24, 2026 · 6:00 PM – Friday, July 31, 2026 11:00 PM </p> <div class=\"mb-6\"> <a href=\"/venues/67\" class=\"text-surface-900 hover:text-surface-600 hover:underline\"> Palestine House </a> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">113 high Holborn</p> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">London</p> </div>  <!-- Tickets section --> <div class=\"mb-8\"> <a href=\"https://www.tickettailor.com/events/palestinehouse/2300971\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-block px-6 py-3 font-medium transition-colors\" style=\"background-color: var(--theme-fg); color: var(--theme-bg);\" onmouseenter=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg-800)'\" onmouseleave=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg)'\">\nGet Tickets\n</a> </div> <div class=\"mt-6 text-surface-700\">6:30pm- Doors Open <br /><br />7pm- Welcoming <br /><br />7:45 – 8:45pm Collective Counter-Mapping — Brittle Projects<br /><br />Join curator duo brittle who will be activating Awaiting Home through a participatory counter-mapping exercise. Drawing from Jamaica Kincaid’s writing on gardens, inheritance and diasporic memory, the session invites participants to consider how we hold places in memory and imagination.<br /><br />9:00 – 9:30pm Live Performance — Saurabh Shivakumar<br /><br />9:45 – 10:25pm Live Performance — Aley Baracat<br /><br />Curatorial Note: <br /><br />From one to another we move. We move internally to places of home within, we move externally to places of safety and belonging. We sit with the temporality and fleeting moments of flight in the air. Grasping for the familiar; within space. We hold on to kin. She (the earth) offers safety to nest, to root and build. Connection to earth is connection to the grains of soil our ancestors walked. The wind moves… always, across borders and seas, we move alongside the wind, with our feet planted deep to the core of the earth. <br /><br />She (the earth) is a witness. The ways land is turned into assets, boundaries, or battlegrounds. She witnesses the changes to temporalities. She resists, heals, and remembers.<br /><br />Awaiting Home, brings together artists working with moving image, photography, digital and analog storytelling, opening portals that explore stories of people and the lands that hold them, revealing the complex relationships between landscapes and people. The artists weave together the intermediary between bodies and the ground they inhabit. <br /><br />Who has the right to stay? Who is pushed to move? What does it mean to own, to borrow, to inherit, or simply to care for this temporary place we call home?<br /><br />Curated by Culture Shock | @cultureshockcuration<br /><br />Palestine House, London | Exhibition running from Friday 24th – 31st July 2026</div> <p class=\"mt-6 text-sm text-surface-600\">\nBy   <a href=\"/promoters/373\" class=\"text-surface-600 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Culture Shock </a>  </p>  </div> </div> </div>  </main> <footer class=\"mt-auto max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 text-sm text-surface-600 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-500\" data-footer> <a href=\"/about\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">&copy; 2026 gel</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/subscribe\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">subscribe</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/privacy-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">privacy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/purchase-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">purchase policy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"mailto:hello@gel.now\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">contact us\n</a> </footer> <script type=\"module\">const e=document.querySelector(\"[d