23,25.97-6.18-17.41-55.03,15.44-55.03,26.53,0,33.69,48.29,33.69,83.8,0,41.69-6.74,86.61,4.21,96.86,7.44,6.46,22.46,6.88,22.46,15.72,0,11.93-29.9,14.18-46.18,8.98-27.93-8.98-3.65-60.5-22.46-74.82-15.58-11.79-32,5.19-66.96,5.47-42.53.28-50.53-10.53-81.98-10.53-24.56,0-38.88,12.07-38.88,26.25,0,24.14,25.41,42.11,57.41,42.11,46.74,0,64.71-21.9,85.63-21.9,8.42,0,14.04,3.09,14.04,8.98,0,16.84-37.2,32.99-104.58,32.99-73.13,0-89.14-41.55-118.19-39.02-19.09,1.68-11.93,27.79-23.3,43.09-11.65,15.58-34.25,23.44-72.99,23.3-38.18-.14-73.41-3.93-73.41-20.63,0-6.74,6.88-10.81,17.13-10.81,15.72,0,30.46,13.76,57.83,13.76,34.67,0,30.46-35.09.7-36.92-13.34-.98-29.34,4.21-42.53,2.11C13.48,184.03,0,154.55,0,113.56Z\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></svg> </a> <nav class=\"site-header__nav flex gap-6 items-end\" data-astro-cid-sckkx6r4 style=\"--themeBackground: #f0f0f0;--themeForeground: #2b2b2b;--themeAccent: #4c6ef5;\"> <a href=\"/about\" class=\"text-surface-600 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\" data-astro-cid-sckkx6r4 style=\"--themeBackground: #f0f0f0;--themeForeground: #2b2b2b;--themeAccent: #4c6ef5;\">about</a> <a href=\"/account\" class=\"text-surface-600 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\" data-astro-cid-sckkx6r4 style=\"--themeBackground: #f0f0f0;--themeForeground: #2b2b2b;--themeAccent: #4c6ef5;\">account</a> </nav> </div> </header>  <main class=\"flex-1\" data-astro-cid-sckkx6r4 style=\"--themeBackground: #f0f0f0;--themeForeground: #2b2b2b;--themeAccent: #4c6ef5;\">  <div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-6\"> <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8\"> <!-- Left: Image only on desktop --> <div class=\"hidden lg:block\"> <img src=\"https://api.gel.now/api/events/754/images/poster/1ecdd09ef5493fc16a5bf598fd3c4789.webp\" alt=\"Race Rhythm Revolution | Session 2: Organic Music Society: A cosmos of being otherwise\" class=\"w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover\"> </div> <!-- Right panel (desktop) / Main content (mobile) --> <div> <!-- Image on mobile only --> <div class=\"lg:hidden mb-6\"> <img src=\"https://api.gel.now/api/events/754/images/poster/1ecdd09ef5493fc16a5bf598fd3c4789.webp\" alt=\"Race Rhythm Revolution | Session 2: Organic Music Society: A cosmos of being otherwise\" class=\"w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover\"> </div> <!-- Event header -->  <div class=\"flex items-start gap-2 mb-2\"> <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-surface-900\">Race Rhythm Revolution | Session 2: Organic Music Society: A cosmos of being otherwise</h1>  </div> <p class=\"text-surface-600 mb-4\"> Wednesday, July 29, 2026 · 7:00 PM – 9:00 PM </p> <div class=\"mb-6\"> <a href=\"/venues/45\" class=\"text-surface-900 hover:text-surface-600 hover:underline\"> Mosaic Rooms </a> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">226 Cromwell Road</p> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">London</p> </div> <div class=\"mb-4\"> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600 mb-1\">Artists</p> <div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-2\">  <a href=\"/artists/1940\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Aditi Jaganathan </a>  </div> </div> <!-- Tickets section --> <div class=\"mb-8\"> <a href=\"https://tzkrti.com/en/events/4124\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-block px-6 py-3 font-medium transition-colors\" style=\"background-color: var(--theme-fg); color: var(--theme-bg);\" onmouseenter=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg-800)'\" onmouseleave=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg)'\">\nGet Tickets\n</a> </div> <div class=\"mt-6 text-surface-700\">Rhythm Race Revolution is an 8-week course with Aditi Jaganathan that uses music and its attendant cultural texts, as a site of deep study, through which ideas of race, gender, colonialism, healing and transformative justice are collectively explored. It is a radical learning space tracing the sonic(s) of resistance. <br /><br />Session 2:<br /><br />Organic Music Society: A cosmos of being otherwise<br /><br />Using the life and practice of Don Cherry, we will move with the ways in which he created a mirror, for life to reflect the radical impulse of music. Through improvisation and a deep study of global music, we will witness the power of his learnings through the music he wove with others. <br /><br />Reading lists will be provided to those who book. Places are limited.<br /><br />Bio <br /><br />Dr Aditi Jaganathan is a thinker and creator, writer and dreamer. Having worked at the intersections of law, culture and politics in various capacities, Aditi is motivated by a politics of refusal, living in rupture as rapture; turning away from hegemonic worlds of oppression and tuning into something different, beyond the world we live in and moving to the rhythms of an elsewhere. It is this compulsion which guides her pedagogy in the education work she does. Riffing off education for liberation, she creates spaces of (un)learning as a site of radical praxis, using tools of music, film and visual culture, to unpack the ways in which ideologies of oppression and liberation travel through cultural production.<br /><br />Reading lists will be provided to those who book. Places are limited.</div>   </div> </div> </div>  </main> <footer class=\"mt-auto max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 text-sm text-surface-600 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-500\" data-footer> <a href=\"/about\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">&copy; 2026 gel</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/subscribe\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">subscribe</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/privacy-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">privacy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/purchase-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">purchase policy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"mailto:hello@gel.now\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">contact us\n</a> </footer> <script type=\"module\">const e=document.querySelector(\"[data-footer]\");e&&new IntersectionObserver(([o])=>{o.isIntersecting&&(e.classList.remove(\"opacity-0\"),e.classList.add(\"opacity-100\"))},{threshold:.1}