//api.gel.now/api/events/718/images/poster/67e2f316f2546e73c1119fa5c2ff761c.webp\" alt=\"Folk Critique + Cambridge Companion to Folk Music – launch event\" class=\"w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover\"> </div> <!-- Event header -->  <div class=\"flex items-start gap-2 mb-2\"> <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-surface-900\">Folk Critique + Cambridge Companion to Folk Music – launch event</h1>  </div> <p class=\"text-surface-600 mb-4\"> Friday, July 31, 2026 · 7:30 PM – 11:00 PM </p> <div class=\"mb-6\"> <a href=\"/venues/10\" class=\"text-surface-900 hover:text-surface-600 hover:underline\"> Cafe Oto </a> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">18-22 Ashwin St</p> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">London</p> </div> <div class=\"mb-4\"> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600 mb-1\">Artists</p> <div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-2\">  <a href=\"/artists/1867\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Mataio Austin-Dean </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1868\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Ula Taylor-Reilly </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1869\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> The Black British Folk Collective </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1870\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Ross Cole </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1871\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Grace Connolly Linden </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1872\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Jacken Elswyth </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1873\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Aisha Farr </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1874\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Angeline Morrison </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1875\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Marcus MacDonald </a> <span> · </span> <a href=\"/artists/1876\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Bianca Wilson </a>  </div> </div> <!-- Tickets section --> <div class=\"mb-8\"> <a href=\"https://www.cafeoto.co.uk/events/folk-critique/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-block px-6 py-3 font-medium transition-colors\" style=\"background-color: var(--theme-fg); color: var(--theme-bg);\" onmouseenter=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg-800)'\" onmouseleave=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg)'\">\nGet Tickets\n</a> </div> <div class=\"mt-6 text-surface-700\">‘These things were on the walls in Tudor times: some of them are really old, some not so old. But that tradition of discussing song, which I would love to find traces of – there must be some traces but, like with a lot of vernacular culture, they evaporate.’<br /><br />Please join us for a double launch, celebrating the publication of Folk Critique, a new pamphlet from Ross Cole and the Fair Organ collective; and the Cambridge Companion to Folk Music (edited by Ross Cole), a groundbreaking new collection of essays on traditional culture and its continuing power in today’s world.<br /><br />The evening will include a discussion of folk revivalism, nationalism, resistance and what it means to take an attitude of ‘folk critique’; performances from Angeline Morrison, the Black British Folk Collective, Mataio Austin-Dean and Jacken Elswyth; and readings from Aisha Farr and Grace Connolly Linden.<br /><br />We hope attendees will stay to have a drink and a chat afterwards.<br /><br />Generously supported by The Leverhulme Trust.</div> <p class=\"mt-6 text-sm text-surface-600\">\nBy   <a href=\"/promoters/353\" class=\"text-surface-600 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> The Fair Organ </a>  </p>  </div> </div> </div>  </main> <footer class=\"mt-auto max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 text-sm text-surface-600 opacity-0 transition-opacity duratio