t;]}],[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,8],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;experimental&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,37],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;noise&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,102],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;improvisation&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,142],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;Acoustic&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,163],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;Free improvisation&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,261],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;experimental music&quot;]}]]]}],&quot;user&quot;:[0]}\" ssr client=\"load\" opts=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;TicketForm&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}\" await-children><section class=\"relative\"><div class=\"border border-surface-300 rounded\"><div class=\"text-[color:var(--theme-fg)] text-[1.1rem] font-semibold text-center p-2.5 flex h-full\">Loading ticket options...</div></div></section><!--astro:end--></astro-island> </div> <div class=\"mt-6 text-surface-700\">GRAIN is a concert series and archiving project for experimental and improvised music,  programmed / produced by Caius Williams & Theodora Laird.<br /><br />Brandon Lopez & Caius Williams (duo)<br />Theodora Laird, Mica Levi, Angharad Davies (trio)<br /><br />Doors 7:30, Music 8PM (2 sets with an interval)<br />NO ADMISSION DURING THE SETS<br /><br /><br />BRANDON LOPEZ:<br />is a bassist and composer living in New York City. His work deals with improvisation, finding new sonic possibilities on the double bass.<br /><br />Collaborations with the likes Fred Moten, Gerald Cleaver, John Zorn, The Mat Maneri Quartet, Nate Wooley’s “knknighgh”, Satoko Fuji, Zeena Parkins, Ingrid Laubrock and Tom Rainey, Standing On The Corner, Cecilia Lopez, Ash Fure, Joe Morris, Tyshawn Sorey, and many others.<br /><br />Playing with the New York Philharmonic 2019 season as a featured soloist with the New York Philharmonic in the premier of Ashley Fure’s “Filament” under the baton of Jaap Van Zweden. His solo work has been featured at the Met Museum in a live collaboration with silent films by directors Stan Brakhage and Germaine Dulac. His collaborative work with Fred Moten and Gerald Cleaver was critically acclaimed by publications of note and won Best of Jazz 2022 in the NYTimes. His most recent solo recording won best of 2023 in the NYC Jazz record. He’s been awarded the Van Lier Fellowship (2018) and Jerome Artist in Residence (2020) at Roulette Intermedium, The Artist in Residence at Issue Project Room (2018), commissions from the Robert D. Bielecki Foundation for the recording of SUN BURNS OUT YOUR EYES (2022), 2023 NYSCA grant for the multimedia piece NADA SAGRADA premiered at the Vision Festival, and an award in 2020 from the Doris Duke Charitable Trust.<br /><br />He is currently a instructor of improvisation and double bass at the New School for Jazz.<br /><br />CAIUS WILLIAMS:<br />is a musician from London who plays the double bass, guitar, and bass guitar. He works in collaboration with others, alongside various solo projects, often working with improvisation and explorations of resonance, and perception. https://caiuswilliams.bandcamp.com/<br /><br />THEODORA LAIRD<br />is a vocalist and multidisciplinary artist. Releases under her solo project ‘feeo’ have received critical acclaim. Theodora's practice has involved in tandem with an interest in situating narratives within freely improvised music, specifically through frequent involvement in the GRAIN residency.<br /><br />ANGHARAD DAVIES<br />is a Welsh violinist based in London working with free-improvisation, compositions and performance. Her approach to sound involves attentive listening and exploring beyond the sonic confines of her instrument, her classical training and performance expectation.<br /><br />MICA LEVI<br />is a musician and composer born in Guildford and living in South East London.They use programming software, written notation and improvisation to produce music. </div> <p class=\"mt-6 text-sm text-surface-600\">\nBy   <a href=\"/promoters/19\" class=\"text-surface-600 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> GRAIN </a>  </p>  </div> </div> </div>  </main> <footer class=\"mt-auto max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 text-sm text-surface-600 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-500\" data-footer> <a href=\"/about\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">&copy; 2026 gel</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/subscribe\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">subscribe</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/privacy-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">privacy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/purchase-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">purchase policy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"mailto:hello@gel.now\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">contact us\n</a> </footer> <script type=\"module\">const e=document.querySelector(\"[data-footer]\");e&&new IntersectionObserver(([o])=>{o.isIntersecting&&(e.classList.remove(\"opacity-0\"),e.classList.add(\"opacity-100\"))},{threshold:.1}).observe(e);</script> <!-- Pass user data to client-side via data attribute --> <script>(function(){const userData = undefined;\n\n      if (userData) {\n        document.documentElement.dataset.user = JSON.stringify(userData);\n      }\n    })();</script> <!-- Initialize auth and theme stores --> <script type=\"module\" src=\"/_astro/Layout.astro_astro_type_script_index_0_lang.Cig_QlfO.js\"></script> <astro-island uid=\"194iIp\" prefix=\"r5\" component-url=\"/_astro/FloatingThemeSwitcher.D_12sDBb.js\" component-export=\"default\" renderer-url=\"/_astro/client.DYKcjN1Z.js\" props=\"{&quot;data-astro-cid-sckkx6r4&quot;:[0,true]}\" ssr client=\"load\" opts=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FloatingThemeSwitcher&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}\" await-children><div class=\"\n        fixed bottom-4 right-4 sm:bottom-6 sm:right-6 z-40\n        transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out\n        w-15 sm:w-16\n      \" style=\"transform-origin:bottom right\"><button class=\"\n            w-15 h-15 sm:w-16 sm:h-16\n            rounded-full\n            shadow-2xl\n            backdrop-blur-md\n            