/891/images/poster/d83591b9f7e02852d81f1eb77e613940.webp\" alt=\"Materials: A Festival of Visual Culture and Politics\" class=\"w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover\"> </div> <!-- Event header -->  <div class=\"flex items-start gap-2 mb-2\"> <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-surface-900\">Materials: A Festival of Visual Culture and Politics</h1>  </div> <p class=\"text-surface-600 mb-4\"> Saturday, September 12, 2026 · 10:00 AM – 9:00 PM </p> <div class=\"mb-6\"> <a href=\"/venues/34\" class=\"text-surface-900 hover:text-surface-600 hover:underline\"> Pelican House </a> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">144 Cambridge Heath Road</p> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">London</p> </div>  <!-- Tickets section --> <div class=\"mb-8\"> <a href=\"https://luma.com/p8mapcri\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-block px-6 py-3 font-medium transition-colors\" style=\"background-color: var(--theme-fg); color: var(--theme-bg);\" onmouseenter=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg-800)'\" onmouseleave=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg)'\">\nGet Tickets\n</a> </div> <div class=\"mt-6 text-surface-700\">Join us at Pelican House for the second Materials Festival, where we explore visual and spatial practices as a force for radical imagination and transformative social change. <br />​The theme for this year is embedded practice: what does it mean to develop a creative practice that is genuinely embedded in a place or community? How can we organise with our neighbours, colleagues and friends to respond to our shared material struggles? And what is our vision of the “good life” that we’re all building towards?<br /><br />​We’ll start the day at 10am, with free snacks and a pay-what-you-can lunch. Bookworkers and Beyond will be running a Publishing Fair, and we’ll be displaying London’s Ours, an exhibition of visual materials from the Greater London Council 1981–1986. After 6pm we’ll have a special performance by Circle Dance and a social with drinks and music.<br /><br />​Conversations<br />​Multitudes<br /><br />​Migrants in Culture<br /><br />​Common Knowledge<br /><br />​Lola Olufemi<br /><br />​Sarah Stein Lubrano<br /><br />​Unit 38<br /><br />​House of Annetta<br /><br />​Case studies<br />​Slow + Dirty Press<br /><br />​FAT Studio<br /><br />​Wards Corner Community Plan<br /><br />​Tottenham Family Fight Back<br /><br />​Workshops<br />​Artists & Culture Workers<br /><br />​Autonomous Design Group<br /><br />​Cooperation Town<br /><br />​Section of Architectural Workers<br /><br />​The Department of Information & Propaganda<br /><br />​The People’s Prop Department<br /><br />​workers.coop<br /><br />​Bookworkers & Beyond Publishing Fair<br />​BOOKS<br /><br />​F.A.T. Studio<br /><br />​Migrants in Culture<br /><br />​PageMasters<br /><br />​Slow + Dirty Press<br /><br />​Sticky Fingers Publishing<br /><br />​and more to be confirmed!<br /><br />​Open studios with Pelican residents<br />​Common Knowledge<br /><br />​Migrants in Culture<br /><br />​Unit 38<br /><br />​Plus!<br />​Circle Dance presents: Neither Albion Nor Britannia<br /><br />​London's Ours! A GLC Exhibition<br /><br />​Collective art marking with the London School of Solarpunk<br /><br />​Bethnal Green walking tours<br /><br />​Free childcare for children over 5<br /><br />​Organised by Common Knowledge and Unit 38, with support from the Rosa Luxemburg Stiftung and Pelican House.<br /><br />​All profits from ticket sales will be distributed between our speakers. Email us if you're unwaged and would like come — no one turned away for lack of funds.</div> <p class=\"mt-6 text-sm text-surface-600\">\nBy   <a href=\"/promoters/403\" class=\"text-surface-600 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Materials </a>  </p>  </div> </div> </div>  </main> <footer class=\"mt-auto max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 text-sm text-surface-600 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-500\" data-footer> <a href=\"/about\" class=\"hover:underline hover:te