1f8ea5e006985a807.webp\" alt=\"HAKEEM (+ Q&#38;A and Acoustic Set)\" class=\"w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover\"> </div> <!-- Event header -->  <div class=\"flex items-start gap-2 mb-2\"> <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-surface-900\">HAKEEM (+ Q&amp;A and Acoustic Set)</h1>  </div> <p class=\"text-surface-600 mb-4\"> Saturday, September 19, 2026 · 6:30 PM – 11:00 PM </p> <div class=\"mb-6\"> <a href=\"/venues/37\" class=\"text-surface-900 hover:text-surface-600 hover:underline\"> Rio Cinema </a> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">107 Kingsland High Street</p> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600\">London</p> </div> <div class=\"mb-4\"> <p class=\"text-sm text-surface-600 mb-1\">Artists</p> <div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-2\">  <a href=\"/artists/1969\" class=\"text-surface-700 hover:text-surface-900 hover:underline\"> Hakeem </a>  </div> </div> <!-- Tickets section --> <div class=\"mb-8\"> <a href=\"https://riocinema.org.uk/Rio.dll/WhatsOn?f=2652932\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"inline-block px-6 py-3 font-medium transition-colors\" style=\"background-color: var(--theme-fg); color: var(--theme-bg);\" onmouseenter=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg-800)'\" onmouseleave=\"this.style.backgroundColor='var(--theme-fg)'\">\nGet Tickets\n</a> </div> <div class=\"mt-6 text-surface-700\">Doc’n Roll is delighted to be part of The Music is Black Festival from East Bank and to bring a special event to the Rio Cinema celebrating one of London’s most distinctive contemporary musicians, Hak Baker. <br /><br />The evening will include a special screening of Hakeem, live Q&A, and an intimate acoustic performance by Hak Baker, offering audiences a unique opportunity to hear directly from Hak about his journey, creative process, and the experiences that have shaped his career. <br /><br />Hak’s story is one of resilience, creativity, and community, making him an inspiring figure for a new generation of artists and music fans alike. <br /><br />Synopsis <br />An unconventional music documentary for a very unconventional musician, this film follows British singer and rapper Hak Baker over five years. Directed by the filmmaking duo of DEADHORSES (James Topley and Ivo Beckett), Hakeem balances profundity and profanity as Baker confronts the traumas of class and masculinity in the wake of his sudden stardom. An anarchic yet sincere portrait of British lad culture, full of arresting aesthetics and savage honesty, this is more than a chronicle of a musician's life – it’s a fascinating and intimate portrait of existential angst, brotherhood and hope in the face of the taboos that surround male mental health.<br /><br />The Music is Black Festival from East Bank at Queen Elizabeth Olympic Park is a celebration of Black British music across a full programme of events including four live festival weekends. Led by the artists, creators and collectives who built its legacy and shape what’s next, this is where sound lives and culture moves.</div>   </div> </div> </div>  </main> <footer class=\"mt-auto max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 text-sm text-surface-600 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-500\" data-footer> <a href=\"/about\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">&copy; 2026 gel</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/subscribe\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">subscribe</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/privacy-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">privacy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"/purchase-policy\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">purchase policy</a> ⋅ <a href=\"mailto:hello@gel.now\" class=\"hover:underline hover:text-surface-900\">contact us\n</a> </footer> <script type=\"module\">const e=document.querySelector(\"[data-footer]\");e&&new IntersectionObserver(([o])=>{o.isIntersecting&&(e.classList.remove(\"opacity-0\"),e.classList.add(\"opacity-100\"))},{threshold:.1}).observe(e);</script> <!-- Pass user data to client-side via data attribute --> <script>(function(){const userData = undefined;\n\n   