are Sound Brushes - painting bold sonic landscapes alongside her musical brothers, Ashley John Long on double bass, Ben Handysides on drums and Moss Freed on guitar, forging a rich breeding ground for Musical liberation.\\n\\n\\&quot;The radical spirit of offhand precarity frequently bubbles over into an effervescent sense of the imperative to explore. In a word? Fearless.\\&quot; - PRESTO MUSIC\\n\\n\\&quot;A messy emporium of raw, raucous realness. Alive.” Keeffe and her quartet nailed it.\\&quot; - Sammy Stein, FREE JAZZ BLOG\\n\\n\\&quot;Charlotte Keeffe is rapidly developing a reputation as one of UK’s finest improvisers.\\&quot; - Tony Dudley-Evans\\n\\nDiscus Music: discusmusic.bandcamp.com / discus-music.org\\nWe are a large Sheffield based independent label for creative music with over 200 CD/DL releases, curated by Martin Archer. As well as the residency group leaders Martin Archer, Charlotte Keeffe and Martin Pyne, artists on the label include Keith Tippett, Julie Tippetts, Paul Dunmall, Cecil Taylor, Tony Oxley, Pat Thomas, Laura Cole, Let Spin, Das Rad, Orchestra Of The Upper Atmosphere, Uroboro, Stephen Grew, Guy Segers, Corey Mwamba, Robert Mitchell, Alya Al-Sultani, Inclusion Principle, Johnny Hunter, Mick Beck, Billy Marrows, Jan Todd / frostlake, Faith Brackenbury, Tony Bianco, The Exu, Faradena Afifi, Steve Beresford, Paul Khimasia Morgan, Laura Jurd, Keir Cooper, Ron Caines, Matthew Bourne, Chris Sharkey, Carla Diratz, Theo May, Paul Taylor, This Celestial Engine, Fjall, Walt Shaw, Steve Tromans, Rachel Musson, Mark Sanders, James Mainwaring, Ricard Scott, Army Of Briars, Nick Robonson, Michael Bardon, Bo Meson, Juxtavoices, Alex Ward and many more.\\n\\n&quot;],&quot;is_featured&quot;:[0,false],&quot;poster_small&quot;:[0,&quot;&quot;],&quot;is_preview&quot;:[0,false],&quot;external_url&quot;:[0,&quot;&quot;],&quot;is_announced&quot;:[0,true],&quot;is_on_listings_site&quot;:[0,true],&quot;resale_queue_enabled&quot;:[0,true],&quot;is_test_event&quot;:[0,false],&quot;is_cancelled&quot;:[0,false],&quot;categories&quot;:[1,[[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,2],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;gig&quot;]}]]],&quot;is_free&quot;:[0,false],&quot;date_created&quot;:[0,&quot;0001-01-01T00:00:00Z&quot;],&quot;date_updated&quot;:[0,&quot;0001-01-01T00:00:00Z&quot;],&quot;venues&quot;:[1,[[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,17],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;The Horse Hospital&quot;],&quot;address&quot;:[0,&quot;Colonnade&quot;],&quot;city&quot;:[0,&quot;London&quot;],&quot;country&quot;:[0,&quot;&quot;],&quot;postcode&quot;:[0,&quot;WC1N 1JD&quot;],&quot;capacity&quot;:[0,120],&quot;description&quot;:[0,&quot;The Horse Hospital is an artist-led, not-for-profit independent arts venue in central London.\\n\\nEstablished in 1993 by Roger K. Burton, THH has uplifted countercultural and experimental art across music, performance, film, fashion, and visual art. It has also served as a living archive of countercultural activity and ‘outsider art.’ \\n\\nAs of 2025, The Horse Hospital is run by The Horse Hospital Collective. This collective has been entrusted with the responsibility of continuing, expanding upon and reaffirming The Horse Hospital’s originating vision, with a renewed focus on providing a home for DIY cultural practices. \\n\\nThe THH Collective’s internally-directed programme runs concurrently with usage of the space by wider communities through our Open Access scheme, as well as provision through direct hire. &quot;],&quot;contact_email&quot;:[0,&quot;&quot;],&quot;on_listings_site&quot;:[0,false],&quot;wheelchair_accessible&quot;:[0,false],&quot;accessible_bathrooms&quot;:[0,false],&quot;hearing_loop&quot;:[0,false],&quot;accessible_parking&quot;:[0,false],&quot;lift_access&quot;:[0,false],&quot;date_created&quot;:[0,&quot;0001-01-01T00:00:00Z&quot;],&quot;date_updated&quot;:[0,&quot;0001-01-01T00:00:00Z&quot;]}]]],&quot;promoters&quot;:[1,[[0,{&quot;id&quot;:[0,331],&quot;name&quot;:[0,&quot;Discus Music&quot;],&quot;contact_email&quot;:[0,&qu